COLLDATA("sh22804","en",[[1,"Water is not rendered impure by anything."],[2,"Regarding ablution with seawater, he said: “They are two seas; it does not harm you whichever of them you begin with.”"],[4,"When she performed Hajj she would pass by Umm Salamah ؓ [and] she said: I said to her: “Show me the vessel in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution!” She said: So she brought it out, and I said: “This is the makkūk of the muftī.” Then I said: “Show me the vessel in which he used to perform ghusl.” She brought it out, and I said: “This is the qafīz of the muftī; it is the cup of the generous.”"],[5,"I entered upon Umm Salamah ؓ and said: “Show me—” and he mentioned it, and in it she said regarding the ghusl vessel: “This is a makhtūm,” meaning the ṣāʿ, and she said regarding the ablution vessel: “This is a quarter of the muftī.”"],[6,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution with a kūz.”"],[7,"“He performed ablution with half a mudd.”"],[9,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were on a journey and they came to a pool in a corner of which was a carcass. They refrained from it until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to them. They said: “O Messenger of Allah, this pool has a carcass in one corner of it.” He ﷺ said: “Water [it] and draw [from it], for water is lawful and is not forbidden.”"],[10,"Ibn Abī Shaybah said: ʿAlī b. Hāshim narrated to us."],[11,"“We used to prefer to take water from the pool to wash with in a corner because of the prohibition against urinating in stagnant water.”"],[12,"“We used to travel with Maymūnah and she would stop at pools containing beetles and dung, and we would draw water for her from them; she saw no harm in that.”"],[14,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought water and there was only a little water. He performed ablution in the middle of the vessel, then he ordered it to be sprinkled on the people, and we considered ourselves fortunate, those whom that water reached. He said: I think it reached all the people, then he stood and led them in the morning prayer."],[15,"“My hand and the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ alternated in a single vessel.”"],[17,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in my house, Husayn ؓ came, and he was a young boy, until he sat on the belly of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he placed his penis on his navel, so I got up to him, and he said: \"Bring me water.\" I brought him water and he poured it on him. Then he said: \"The urine of a girl is washed, and water is poured on that of a boy.\""],[18,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in my house, and Husayn ؓ was with me when he began to walk, and I was heedless of him, so he entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sat on his belly and urinated. I went to take him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up and said: \"Leave him.\" So I left him until he finished. Then he called for water and said: \"Indeed water is poured on the urine of a boy, and the urine of a girl is washed, so pour it generously.\" Then he performed ablution, then he stood to pray. When he stood, he embraced him to himself. When he bowed or sat, he put him down. Then he sat supplicating and wept. Then he stretched out his hand. When he finished the prayer, I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I saw you today do something I have not seen you do.\" He ﷺ said: \"Jibril ﷺ came to me and informed me that my son here will be killed by my community. I said: 'Show me his soil.' He showed me his red soil.\""],[19,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was lying on his back playing with a child on his chest, the child urinated. She (the mother) stood to take him and hit him, but he ﷺ said: \"Leave him. Bring me a jug of water.\" He sprinkled the water on the urine until the water overflowed onto the urine. Then he ﷺ said: \"This is how it is done with urine: it is sprinkled for a male, and washed for a female.\""],[20,"\"Water is poured on the urine of a boy, and the urine of a girl is washed.\""],[21,"He added: \"whether she has eaten food or not,\" but he did not trace it back to the Prophet."],[22,"A bedouin came and urinated in the mosque. \"So the Prophet ﷺ ordered that the place be dug up, and a bucket of water was poured on it.\""],[23,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and he came upon two graves whose occupants were being punished. He said: \"They are not being punished for something major.\" Then he said: \"Yes, indeed. One of them used to backbite people, and the other used not to protect himself from his urine.\" Then he ﷺ took a fresh palm branch or two, broke them, and planted each piece on a grave, saying: \"It will be lightened for them as long as these remain fresh,\" or he said: \"as long as they do not dry.\""],[24,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about dry dung that a man steps on. He said: \"That clean place purifies him.\""],[26,"\"I was with Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ ؓ, when a dish containing bread and meat was gifted to her. She stood for prayer and we stood to pray. A cat got to the food and ate from it. When we finished, Umm Salamah ؓ took the bowl and turned it around until the place where the cat had eaten was facing her, and she ate from it.\""],[27,"\"There is no harm in the leftover water of a cat.\""],[28,"Ali ؓ was asked: \"A cat drinks from a vessel?\" He said: \"There is no harm in the leftover water of a cat.\""],[30,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"would take musk and wipe his head and beard with it.\""],[32,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was watering a she-camel of mine in front of me, so I spat, and my sputum fell on my garment. So I began to wash my garment from the water-skin that was in front of me. He said, 'O Ammar, your sputum and the tears of your eyes are only like the water in your water-skin. Only that is washed from urine, excrement, semen from the greatest water, blood, and vomit.'"],[34,"I entered upon Anas b. Malik ؓ and saw a wooden cup with him. He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to drink from it and perform ablution.'"],[35,"I was walking with the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'O my son, ask for water for ablution for me from this house.' I said, 'The Messenger of Allah is requesting water for ablution.' They said, 'Tell him that his bucket is made of the skin of a dead animal.' He ﷺ said, 'Ask them: Did they tan it?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'For its tanning is its purification.'"],[36,"A sheep of ours that we used to milk died, so we asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it. He said, 'What happened to your sheep, O Umm Salamah?' She said: I said, 'It died, so we threw it away.' He ﷺ said, 'Would you not have benefitted from its hide?' She said: It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, it is a dead animal.' He ﷺ said, 'Its tanning makes it lawful just as vinegar makes wine lawful.'"],[37,"We used to obtain from the spoils of the polytheists with the Prophet ﷺ water-skins and vessels, and we would divide them all even if they were from dead animals."],[38,"He used to like the vessel that had a lid."],[39,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I was in a tent. He said, 'What an excellent tent, if there is no dead animal in it.'"],[40,"Ibn Mas'ud ؓ was in the mosque with some people whom he was teaching the Qur'an. He called for a drink and said, 'Indeed, this drink was in the water-skin of a sheep given to us for milking that died.'"],[41,"Indeed, the one who drinks from vessels of gold and silver only causes the fire of Hell to gurgle in his belly."],[43,"A man called Abu Humayd brought the Prophet ﷺ a vessel containing milk from al-Naqi' during the day. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Why did you not cover it, even by placing a stick across it?'"],[44,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked for water while he was circumambulating the House. A man among them said, 'Shall I bring you a drink that we make?' He said, 'Yes.' He said: A vessel containing nabidh was brought. He ﷺ said, 'Why did you not turn a vessel over it and place a stick across it?' He said: He ﷺ drank from it and frowned. Then he called for water and poured it over it, then he drank and gave others to drink."],[46,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go to relieve himself at al-Mughammas."],[47,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to relieve himself, he would go far away until no one could see him."],[48,"The Prophet ﷺ would choose a place to urinate just as he would choose a place to settle."],[49,"He was"],[50,"When he wanted to urinate and came upon hard ground, he would take a stick and scratch the earth with it until he loosened the soil, then he would urinate on it."],[51,"The veil between the eyes of the jinn and the private parts of the children of Adam when a man removes his garment is to say: In the name of Allah."],[52,"A Bedouin met the Prophet ﷺ asking him about defecation, so he said: \"Do not face the qiblah, nor turn your back to it when you clean yourself.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what should I do?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Position yourself with two stones and keep the third.\""],[53,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinated standing more than once on a sand dune that he liked."],[54,"He forbade facing the qiblah with defecation or urination."],[56,"He saw Abu Hurayrah ؓ urinating standing while wearing two rose-colored garments, so he called for water and washed what was there."],[57,"I saw 'Ali ؓ urinating standing in the courtyard, then he performed ablution and wiped over his sandals, then entered the mosque."],[58,"That he came to the mortar and urinated standing. Then he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. Then he headed to the mosque. I said to him: 'You have done something disliked?' He replied: 'I served the Messenger of God ﷺ for nine years, and he used to do that.'"],[59,"That he saw Sahl b. Sa'd ؓ urinate the urine of an old man while standing, almost preceding him [i.e., unable to control it]. Then he performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks. I said: 'Would you not remove the leather socks?' He said: 'No, I saw one better than me and you wipe over them' – meaning the Prophet ﷺ."],[60,"While Sa'd b. 'Ubadah ؓ was standing urinating, he died; the jinn killed him. They [the jinn] said: 'We killed the chief of the Khazraj, Sa'd b. 'Ubadah. We shot him with two arrows and did not miss his heart.'"],[61,"I accompanied Abu Dharr ؓ, and all of his character pleased me, except that when he entered the privy, he would sprinkle water [on his private parts and garment]."],[62,"Suraqah b. Malik ؓ came and began to say: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ taught us such and such.' Someone among the people said to him: 'How did he teach you to defecate?' He said: 'Yes, he commanded us to lean on the right [side] and raise the left.'"],[63,"He commanded us to lean on the left [side] and raise the right."],[64,"Most of the punishment of the grave is from urine, so cleanse yourselves from urine."],[65,"Three stones suffice for istinja' (cleaning oneself after relieving oneself)."],[66,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the night of the jinn, and I heard him while they were asking him for legal rulings about istinja'. I heard him say: 'Three stones.' They said: 'What about water?' He said: 'It is purer and purer.'"],[67,"'Three stones.' They said: 'What about water?' He said: 'It is purer and purer.'"],[68,"The delegations of the jinn from the island came to the Prophet ﷺ and stayed with him. Then it occurred to them, and they wanted to return to their lands. They asked him to give them provision. He said: 'I have nothing to provide you with, but come close: every bone you pass by will be for you abundant meat, and every dung you pass by will be for you fruit.' Therefore, he forbade wiping oneself with dung and bones."],[69,"God is One (witr) and loves the odd number, so when you perform istijmar (using stones to clean), do so an odd number of times."],[70,"You must clean the anus thoroughly, for it removes hemorrhoids."],[72,"He used to wash his hands three times, rinse his mouth three times, and sniff water into his nostrils three times, three times, and wash his face three times, and his forearms three times, three times."],[73,"He performed ablution, washing his hands three times, rinsing his mouth three times, and sniffing water into his nostrils three times."],[74,"Uthman ؓ called for water for ablution, while Ali and Talhah ؓ were with him. He performed ablution three times, three times, then said: 'I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution as I have performed ablution?' They said: 'Yes.'"],[75,"Abu Ya'la said: Kamil b. Talhah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, similar to the hadith of Bishr:"],[76,"Uthman ؓ called for water for ablution, while Ali and Talhah ؓ were with him. He performed ablution three times, three times, then said: 'I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution as I have performed ablution?' They said: 'Yes.'"],[77,"Uthman ؓ called for water for ablution, while Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd, and Ali ؓ were with him. Then he performed ablution while they were watching, and he mentioned the ablution three times, three times. Then he said to those present: 'I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution as I have performed ablution now?' They said: 'Yes.' 'And that was because of something that reached him about the ablution of some men.'"],[78,"I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution as I have performed ablution now? They said: 'Yes.' 'And that was because of something that reached him about the ablution of some men.'"],[79,"While we were sitting with Ali ؓ, a man said to him: 'Show me the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!' He called Qanbar and said: 'Bring me a jug of water.' He washed his hands and face three times, and inserted some of his fingers into his mouth. Then he mentioned the hadith, in which is: 'The outside of the ears is part of the head and their inside is part of the face.' Then he sipped water after the ablution, then said: 'Thus was the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[80,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and wiped his head once."],[81,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and wipe his head like this, and Hafs passed his hand over his head until he wiped the back of his neck."],[82,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution, and he placed his hand on top of his head, then brought it back to the back of his neck, then brought it out from under his chin."],[84,"Allah does not accept a prayer without purification, nor charity from stolen property."],[85,"And from Hammad, from Humayd and others, from al-Hasan ؓ from the Prophet ﷺ — the like of it."],[87,"He used to use the siwak during the night many times."],[88,"When he woke up during the night, he would call a servant girl named Barirah for the siwak."],[89,"He used to use the siwak when he lay down on his bed, when he got up during the night, and when he went out to pray. He said: I said to him: You have made things hard on yourself with this siwak! He said: Indeed Usamah ؓ"],[90,"Were it not that I would place a burden on my community, I would have made the siwak obligatory."],[91,"Were it not that I would place a burden on my community, I would have commanded them to use the siwak at every prayer."],[92,"Ibn Abi Shaybah said: Muhammad b. Hayyan narrated to us: Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Habib — with it."],[93,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to tie their siwaks to the tassels of their swords, and the women to their head covers."],[94,"He used to use the siwak with the leftover water of his ablution."],[95,"The Prophet ﷺ used to use the siwak with the leftover water of his ablution."],[96,"The siwak is a means of purification for the mouth and a means of pleasing the Lord."],[97,"Abd al-A'la b. Hammad narrated to us, saying: Hammad b. Salama narrated to us — with this. Abd al-A'la said: It is a mistake, and the correct version is: from Ibn Abi 'Atiq, from 'A'ishah ؓ."],[98,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited using a basil twig as a siwak, and he said: \"It stirs up the vein of leprosy.\""],[100,"I came to Abu Ayyub al-Azdi and shook hands with him. He saw that my nails were long, and he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking him, and he said: \"One of you asks me about the news of the heavens while he leaves his nails like the claws of birds, in which impurity and dirt gather.\""],[101,"I saw Shaqiq take from his hair, then enter the mosque and pray Zuhr and 'Asr without touching water."],[102,"We wipe it with water."],[103,"Whatever iron has touched of nail or hair, then touch it with water."],[104,"\"It only increased him in purity,\" meaning the trimming of hair and nails."],[105,"I heard Ibn 'Umar ؓ say to the barber: \"O boy, reach the two bones.\" He said: When he shaved him, he gave him his forearms and chest, and he shaved the hair on them while people were watching. Salim said to him: \"O father, people think it is a sunnah?\" He said: \"Inform the people that it is not a sunnah, but Ibn 'Umar's hair was bothering him, so he wanted to lighten it from him.\""],[106,"Ibrahim ﷺ was commanded and he circumcised himself with an adze, and it was hard on him, so Allah Almighty revealed to him: \"You hastened before We commanded you with its tool.\" He said: \"O Lord, I disliked delaying Your command.\""],[107,"He is only called a carpenter because he circumcised himself with an adze."],[108,"The purifying acts are four: trimming the mustache, shaving the pubic hair, clipping the nails, and using the siwak."],[110,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “O ‘Ali, when you perform wudu, say: Bismillah. O God, I ask You for the completeness of wudu, the completeness of prayer, the completeness of Your pleasure, and the completeness of Your forgiveness. For this is the zakat of wudu.”"],[112,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ would get up for wudu, the vessel would be enough, and he would name God Almighty, then he would perform wudu thoroughly.”"],[114,"“Performing wudu thoroughly in difficult circumstances, walking to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer—these wash away sins.”"],[115,"‘Abd b. Humayd narrated it from Safwan."],[116,"Abu Ya‘la narrated it from Ahmad b. Ibrahim al-Dawraqi, from Safwan. Al-Darawardi and Abu Damra narrated it from al-Harith, from Abu al-‘Ayyas—spelled with a dotted ya’ and an unpointed letter—from Sa‘id b. al-Musayyab, from ‘Ali ؓ. It has a corroborating report in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayra ؓ, and another in the Sunan from the hadith of Abu Sa‘id ؓ."],[117,"I was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the mosque of al-Khayf when two men came to him, an Ansari and a Thaqafi, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then the Thaqafi said…"],[118,"It was said: “O Messenger of God, how will you recognize your community on the Day of Resurrection?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “By the radiant marks on their faces and limbs from the traces of wudu.”"],[119,"“A righteous trait may be in a man, and through it God Almighty sets right all his deeds. A man’s purification for his prayer—God, Mighty and Majestic, expiates his sins through his purification, and his prayer remains as a supererogatory act.”"],[120,"105 82/2 – Al-Bazzar said: Sahl b. Bahr narrated to us, Mu‘alla b. Asad narrated to us, Bashshar b. al-Hakam Abu Badr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us—with it."],[121,"“The likeness of a person is the likeness of a river in which he bathes five times. What dirt could remain on him? He gets up for wudu and washes his hands, and every sin his hands committed falls away. He rinses his mouth, and every sin his tongue uttered falls away. Then he washes his face, and every sin his eyes looked at falls away. Then he wipes his head, and every sin his ears heard falls away. Then he washes his feet, and every sin his feet walked toward falls away.”"],[122,"“And you are the radiant ones with bright marks.”"],[123,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “O my son, keep to performing wudu thoroughly, and your guardian angels will love you, and your lifespan will be increased. O Anas, exaggerate in sniffing water into the nose after major impurity, for you will come out of your bath with no sin or error upon you.” He said: I said: “How is the exaggeration, O Messenger of God?” He ﷺ said: “Wet the roots of the hair and cleanse the skin. O my son, if you can remain in a state of wudu, then do so, for whoever death comes to while he is in a state of wudu will be granted martyrdom.”"],[124,"Ahmad b. Mani' said: Yazid b. Harun narrated to us: Al-'Ala Abu Muhammad al-Thaqafi narrated to us: Anas ؓ narrated to us."],[126,"A man greeted the Prophet ﷺ, but he did not respond until he had wiped (with dry earth). Then he said: “Nothing prevented me from responding to you except that I was not in a state of wudu.” Or he said: He did not respond until he had wiped and then responded."],[127,"I saw 'Uthman b. 'Affan ؓ sitting at the maqa'id performing wudu. A man passed by and greeted him, but he did not respond until he finished his wudu. Then he entered the mosque, stood before the man, and said: Nothing prevented me from responding to you except that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever performs wudu and then does not speak until he says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger—his sins between the two wudus are forgiven.'"],[129,"He urinated, then recited verses of the Qur'an before touching water."],[131,"In the letter that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to 'Amr b. Hazm when he sent him to Najran: 'No one should touch the Qur'an except one who is pure; no man should pray with his hair tied up; and no one should sit with his knees drawn up while there is nothing between his private part and the sky.'"],[133,"'Blessed are those who clean between (their fingers).' He said: They asked: 'O Messenger of Allah, who are those who clean between?' He said: 'Cleaning between in wudu is to clean between your fingers and nails, and cleaning between after eating, for there is nothing more burdensome to the angel who is with a servant than to smell food odor from one of you.'"],[134,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed wudu and cleaned his beard with his fingers, then said: 'Thus my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me to clean between.'"],[135,"Ibn 'Umar ؓ saw people performing wudu and said: 'Clean between,' meaning between the fingers."],[136,"'Uthman ؓ performed wudu and cleaned between the toes of his feet, then said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do that.'"],[138,"He used to rinse his mouth three times after drinking milk."],[140,"And I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entrust his charity to anyone other than himself until he placed it in the hand of the beggar, and I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entrust his wudu to anyone other than himself until he prepared his wudu for himself when he got up at night."],[141,"I saw 'Ali ؓ drawing water for his wudu, so I hastened to draw it for him. He said: 'Stop, O Abu al-Janub, for I saw 'Umar ؓ drawing water for his wudu, and I hastened to draw it for him. He said: Stop, O Abu al-Hasan, for I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drawing water for his wudu, and I hastened to draw it for him. He said: Stop, O 'Umar, for I dislike that anyone should share in my purification.'"],[143,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man performing ablution while he was washing his khuffs. He ﷺ said with his hand like this: \"You were only commanded to wipe,\" and he spread the fingers of his two palms over his khuffs."],[144,"I asked Ibn 'Abbas ؓ about wiping over the khuffs. He said: \"Three days and their nights for the traveler, and one day and night for the resident.\""],[145,"He used to command wiping, but he himself used to wash his feet. He said: It was said to him about that: How is it that you command wiping? He said: \"How bad it would be for me if its benefit were for you and its sin upon me! I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it and command it, but ablution has been made beloved to me.\""],[146,"A man from the people of Sham asked his father Abu Umamah about wiping over the khuffs. He said: \"Yes, wipe over them.\" The Shami said: Then where is the statement of 'Ali ؓ? My father said to me: \"O my son, go to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and inform him of what you said!\" He said: So I went to him and said: \"My father sends you greetings of peace and asks you about wiping over the khuffs.\" He said: \"If you put them on while your feet were pure, then wipe over them until you take them off.\""],[147,"I saw 'Amr ibn Hazm wiping over the khuffs, and he said: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over his khuffs.\""],[148,"I saw Qays ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah ؓ, who had served the Prophet ﷺ for ten years. He said: \"Then he came to the Tigris wearing two dyed khuffs, performed ablution, and wiped over his khuffs once, and he said like this with his palm, with his fingers on the top of his khuffs.\""],[149,"\"I saw Qays ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah ؓ urinate, then he came to the Tigris, performed ablution, and wiped over his khuffs once, and he said: like this with his palm, with his fingers on the top of his khuffs.\""],[150,"I went out with 'Abdullah ؓ to Madinah, and he used to wipe over the khuff three times."],[151,"We went out with Abu Musa ؓ to some gardens, and I felt the need to relieve myself, so I went for my need, then returned and sat by a stream. Abu Musa came upon me while I was about to take off my khuffs. He said: \"Keep them on, and wipe until you remove them when you sleep.\""],[152,"\"We used to wipe over the khuffs and were commanded to do so.\" A man said to him: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: \"Do not get angry.\""],[153,"\"We used to wipe over our khuffs.\" A man said to him: Did you hear it from the Prophet ﷺ? He said: \"No, but we heard it from one of our companions who is not accused, saying: Wipe over the khuffs and do such and such, except that he did not mention (the Prophet) by name.\""],[154,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. He got up in the darkness before dawn and said: \"O Anas, is there water in your water-skin?\" I said: Yes. He said: Then he went aside and urinated, and I poured water for him and he performed ablution. When he wanted to wipe, I lowered my back to see what he would do. He said: \"It is as you see,\" and he wiped over his khuffs."],[155,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and we did not remove our leather socks for three days and their nights for a need, so we fulfilled it. And we were with him in residence for a day and a night, wiping over our leather socks."],[157,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinate, then he came and performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. He placed his right hand on his right leather sock and his left hand on his left leather sock, then wiped their tops with a single wipe. It was as if I were looking at the traces of the fingers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the leather socks."],[158,"Wiping over the leather socks is done by drawing lines with the fingers."],[160,"The first person I saw wearing leather socks in Islam was al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah ؓ. He came to us while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he had on two black leather socks. He began looking at them and was amazed by them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, they will become abundant for you, meaning the leather socks.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how should we proceed?\" He ﷺ said: \"You wipe over them and pray.\""],[162,"She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, should a man remove his leather socks every hour?\" He ﷺ said: \"No, but he may wipe over them as long as he wishes.\""],[164,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left the two mawaqi' on his feet during the expedition of Tabuk for three [days]."],[166,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"What is complete ablution?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent until the prayer time arrived. He called for water and described the manner of ablution, then he sprinkled water under his garment and said: \"This is complete ablution.\""],[167,"When one of you performs ablution, let him take a handful of water and sprinkle it on his private part. Then if anything affects him, let him say: 'It is from that.'"],[169,"He disliked it, meaning wiping the face with a towel."],[171,"There is no Muslim servant who performs ablution and does it well, then says three times: 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger' – except that eight gates of Paradise are opened for him, and he may enter from whichever he wishes."],[173,"When he prayed and then remained in the mosque until the next prayer time arrived, he would perform a light ablution inside the mosque."],[175,"One of you performs ablution from food, but does not perform ablution from an indecent word he utters."],[176,"Umar ؓ led the people in prayer, and something passed from a person. Umar ؓ said: \"I adjure the one who passed this wind to perform ablution and repeat his prayer.\" Jarir ؓ said: \"Will you adjure everyone who heard it to perform ablution and repeat the prayer?\" He said: \"What a good thing you have said, may God reward you well.\" So he ordered them to do that."],[177,"He saw Abu Hurayrah ؓ insert his finger into his nose, and it came out smeared with blood or with blood on it, then he prayed."],[178,"Touching is anything short of intercourse."],[180,"He was praying with his companions behind him, and a blind man came and stepped on a mat covering the head of a well, and he fell into the well. The people laughed, so the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered those who laughed to repeat the ablution."],[181,"Whoever laughs in prayer does not have to perform ablution."],[182,"He was asked about a man who laughs in prayer; he said: \"He repeats the prayer, but does not repeat the ablution.\""],[184,"Anas b. Malik ؓ used to perform ablution after eating what fire had touched, and he reported that Abu Talhah ؓ performed ablution after eating what fire had touched."],[185,"He used to rinse his mouth three times after drinking milk."],[186,"I came to Anas ؓ but did not find him, so I sat until he came. He came angry, and I spoke to him. He said: \"We were with this one—meaning al-Hajjaj—and food was brought, and they ate, then they stood and prayed without performing ablution. I said: 'Did you not used to do this?' He said: 'No, we did not do it.'\""],[187,"I saw Anas b. Malik ؓ in a bad mood, and I said: \"I see you are in a bad mood?\" He said: \"Why should I not be in a bad mood when I have just come from those people? They ate bread and meat, then prayed without performing ablution.\""],[188,"Perform ablution, for ablution is required after eating what fire has touched, and after what comes out from between dung and blood."],[189,"Zayd b. Thabit ؓ used to perform ablution after eating what fire had touched."],[190,"He ate from a sheep's shoulder, then prayed without performing ablution."],[191,"If I ate meat and drank the milk of milch-camels, then prayed without performing ablution, I would not care if I did not rinse my mouth and wash my hands from the residue of the food."],[192,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon his daughter Fatimah ؓ , and she brought him some meat and he ate. When he got up, she ؓ took hold of his cloak ﷺ and said: Will you not perform ablution? He ﷺ said: \"From what, my little daughter?\" She ؓ said: From that which the fire has changed. He ﷺ said: \"Is not the purest of our food that which the fire has changed?\""],[193,"The Prophet ﷺ took a bite from a shoulder, then prayed without performing ablution."],[194,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and I brought him a cold shoulder, and I would scrape it, and he ate it, then he ﷺ stood and prayed."],[195,"I pulled out for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a shoulder from the pot of al-Abbas ؓ and he ate it, then stood and prayed without performing ablution."],[196,"And al-Bazzar said: Ahmad b. Aban narrated to us."],[198,"He used to rinse his mouth three times after drinking milk."],[200,"When one of you touches his penis, let him perform ablution."],[201,"When one of you touches his penis, let him perform ablution."],[202,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman touching her private part. He said: \"She should perform ablution.\""],[203,"Whoever touches his penis must perform ablution."],[204,"I asked Sa'id—meaning Ibn al-Musayyib—about touching the penis, and he said, \"It is like any other part of your body.\""],[205,"About touching the penis, he said, \"I do not care if I touch it or my nose or my ear.\" Yahya said: \"Or one of them.\""],[206,"Hudhayfah ؓ was asked about touching the penis."],[207,"I and some men with me entered upon 'A'ishah ؓ, and we asked her about a man touching his private part and a woman touching her private part. She said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'I do not care if I touch it or my nose.'\""],[209,"\"If one of you sleeps lying down, let him perform ablution.\" It was said to him, \"The Prophet ﷺ used to sleep lying down and not perform ablution?\" He said, \"You are not like the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and if there was anything from the Messenger of Allah, he knew it.\""],[210,"\"When he lays on his side, he performs ablution.\""],[211,"I asked Zayd b. Thabit for a ruling about sleeping sitting up, and he saw no harm in it. I said, \"What do you think if I lay on my side?\" He said, \"Perform ablution.\""],[212,"\"Whoever sleeps in any state and loses consciousness, ablution is required of him.\""],[213,"I saw Abu Hurayrah ؓ sleeping sitting up until I could hear his snoring, then he would stand and pray without performing ablution."],[214,"I mentioned to 'Ata'—meaning the sleep of the Prophet ﷺ until he snored and then prayed—so he said, \"The Prophet ﷺ was not like others.\""],[215,"They used to lay on their sides."],[216,"\"We used to come to the Prophet's mosque ﷺ to pray, and we would wait for the prayer. Some of us would doze or sleep, and he would not renew ablution.\""],[218,"He used to perform ablution after (consuming) camel milk and camel meat, and he would not pray in camel resting places."],[219,"Ishaq said: Al-Mu'tamir mentioned it to someone other than me, from his father, from his grandfather, meaning from Layth, from Musa, from his father, from his grandfather."],[220,"I perform ablution after (eating) camel meat, and I do not pray in camel resting places."],[221,"He would not pray in camel resting places."],[222,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution after (consuming) camel milk and camel meat, and he would not pray in their resting places. He would not perform ablution after (consuming) sheep milk or sheep meat, and he would pray in their enclosures."],[223,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to drink milk and not perform ablution after it; and if some of it dripped on his garment, he would not wash it."],[224,"A Bedouin intercepted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while traveling and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, prayer overtakes us while we are in camel resting places; should we pray?' He ﷺ said: 'No.' He said: 'Should we perform ablution after (eating) their meat?' He ﷺ said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Should we pray in sheep enclosures?' He ﷺ said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Should we perform ablution after (eating) their meat?' He ﷺ said: 'No.'"],[225,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat meat, then stand for prayer without touching a drop of water."],[226,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat some milk (or a milk product), then pray without performing ablution."],[227,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to eat tharid and drink milk, then pray without performing ablution."],[228,"He used to pass by the cooking pot and take a bone from it, eat from it, then pray without performing ablution."],[230,"When the verse of tayammum was revealed, I did not know how to perform it. So I went to the Prophet ﷺ to ask him, but I did not find him. I set out looking for him and met him coming toward me. When he saw me, he knew what I had come for. He struck his hands on the ground and wiped his face."],[231,"Some men came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “We are people who stay in the sandy desert, and we are affected by major ritual impurity, and among us are menstruating women and women in postpartum bleeding, and we do not find water for four months.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Use the earth.”"],[232,"The Prophet ﷺ was on a journey. When the time for prayer came, the people dismounted. A shepherd saw them and came down. He struck the ground with his hand and performed tayammum, then gave the call to prayer."],[233,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ urinate and then wipe himself with dust. I said to him, “Water is near you!” He ﷺ said, “And what makes me know? Perhaps I would not reach it.”"],[234,"Tayammum is for every prayer."],[235,"The purest earth is cultivated land."],[238,"I stood with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a night of Ramadan. He got up to perform ghusl while I screened him. Some water remained in the vessel, and he said: “If you wish, pour it out, or if you wish, pour it over yourself.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, this leftover water is dearer to me than what I would pour over myself.” He said: “So I performed ghusl with it, and he ﷺ screened me. I said: “Do not screen me!” He ﷺ said: “Rather, I screened you just as you screened me.”"],[239,"Al-Harith said: Umar b. Sa'id b. Masruq narrated to us, from his father, from Makhul, from Muhammad b. Suwayd al-Fihri, from Hudhayfah ؓ, from the Prophet ﷺ, and he mentioned it at length."],[240,"While Umar ؓ was performing ghusl beside a camel—meaning while he was in ihram—and I was screening him with a garment, he said to me: “O Ya'la, pour water on my head!” I said: “The Commander of the Faithful knows best.” He said: “By Allah, I do not think water increases the hair except in dishevelment.” He said: “In the name of Allah,” and he poured water over his head."],[242,"That he did not see any harm in a man performing ghusl from major ritual impurity and then warming himself with his wife before she performs ghusl, or the woman performing ghusl before the man and then warming herself with him."],[243,"“What do you say about one who performs ghusl from major ritual impurity and then warms himself with his wife?” He said: “I do not know.” He said: “Shall I not inform you about your friend Alqamah, that he did not see any harm in it?”"],[244,"That he did not see any harm in that."],[246,"That when he performed ghusl, he sprinkled water on his eyes and inserted his finger into his navel."],[247,"Ibn Abbas ؓ, when he performed ghusl from janabah, poured with his right hand over his left seven times."],[248,"As for me, I scoop three scoops onto my head."],[249,"A man asked him about ghusl from janabah, and he said: \"Three times.\" The man said: \"I have a lot of hair.\" He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had more hair than you and was better.\""],[250,"The delegation of Thaqif said: \"O Messenger of Allah, our land is a cold land, so what suffices us for ghusl from janabah?\" He ﷺ said: \"As for me, I pour over my head three times.\""],[251,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about a man who performs ghusl from janabah and misses some part of his body with water, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He washes that place, then prays.\""],[252,"I asked Umm Salamah about the ghusl of a man, and she said: \"He cleans the hair and makes the skin thoroughly wet.\" And I asked her about the ghusl of a woman, and she said: \"She cleans her scalp and does not undo her hair.\""],[253,"What a good house the bathhouse is: it removes dirt and reminds of the Fire."],[254,"What a good house the bathhouse is: a Muslim man enters it because when he enters it, he asks Allah Almighty for Paradise and seeks refuge in Him from the Fire. And what a bad house the wedding is: a Muslim man enters it because when he enters it, it makes him desire this world and forgets the Hereafter."],[255,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper, and whoever of the females of my ummah believes in Allah and the Last Day, let her not enter the bathhouse."],[256,"I asked Muhammad b. Sirin about entering the bathhouse, and he said: \"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ used to dislike it.\""],[257,"Ibn Umar ؓ did not enter the bathhouse, and he said: \"It is among the luxuries that they invented.\""],[258,"That the two of them would not enter the bathhouse."],[259,"That he used to enter the bathhouse, and the bathhouse attendant would apply depilatory paste to him. When it reached his waist, he would say to the attendant: 'Leave.'"],[260,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade entering the water except with a waist-wrapper."],[261,"“Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent. And whoever of your women believes in Allah and the Last Day should not enter the bathhouse.” He said: I reported it to Umar b. Abd al-Aziz ؓ during his caliphate, and he wrote to Abu Bakr b. Muhammad b. Amr b. Hazm: 'Ask Muhammad b. Thabit about his hadith, for he is approved.' So he asked him, and he wrote to Umar ؓ, and he forbade women from the bathhouse."],[262,"When one of you has intercourse with his wife and then wishes to return, let him wash his private part."],[263,"Abu Ya'la said: Ubaid Allah, that is al-Qawariri, narrated to us."],[265,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the courtyard of the mosque and called out at the top of his voice: “Indeed, this mosque is not permissible for a junub or a menstruating woman, except for the Prophet ﷺ, his wives, Ali, and Fatimah ؓ. Have I not made the names clear to you so that you may not go astray?”"],[267,"Sa'd ؓ would become junub, then perform ablution and go out."],[269,"That he used to scrape semen from his garment."],[270,"About a man who had a wet dream in a garment and then could not locate it: He said, 'Wash the entire garment.'"],[272,"Umar ؓ gave a ruling regarding Rifa'ah, saying: 'Would you do that? When one of you has intercourse with a woman and then fails to ejaculate, he does not perform ghusl?' He said: 'We used to do that in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and no prohibition from Allah Almighty came to us about it, and there was no prohibition from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[273,"I was with Umar ؓ when it was said to him: 'Zayd b. Thabit ؓ is giving legal opinions to the people in the mosque—Zuhair said in his hadith: to the people according to his own opinion—concerning one who has intercourse without ejaculating.' He said: 'Bring him quickly.' So he was brought. Umar said: 'O enemy of yourself! Have you reached the point of giving legal opinions to the people in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ according to your own opinion?' He said: 'I did not do that. My paternal uncles narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'Which of your paternal uncles?' He said: 'Ubayy b. Ka'b.' Zuhair said: 'And Abu Ayyub and Rifa'ah b. Rafi'.' Umar ؓ turned to me and said: 'What does this young man say?' I said: 'We used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'Did you ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it?' He said: 'We used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: So he gathered the people, and they agreed that water is only required from water, except for two men: Ali b. Abi Talib and Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ, who said: 'When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part, ghusl becomes obligatory.' He said: Ali ؓ then said: 'O Commander of the Believers, the most knowledgeable of people about this are the wives of the Prophet ﷺ.' So he sent to Hafsah ؓ, and she said: 'I have no knowledge.' Then he sent to Aishah ؓ, and she said: 'When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part, ghusl becomes obligatory.' Then Umar ؓ became enraged and said: 'Let it not reach me that anyone did it without performing ghusl, or I will punish him severely.'"],[274,"«When the two circumcised parts meet, ghusl becomes obligatory.» He said: Then ‘Ali ؓ said: O Commander of the Faithful, the most knowledgeable people about this are the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. So he sent for Hafsah ؓ, and she said: I have no knowledge. Then he sent for ‘A’ishah ؓ, and she said: «When the two circumcised parts meet, ghusl becomes obligatory.» So ‘Umar ؓ relented, then said: Let it not reach me that anyone does it and does not perform ghusl, except that I will exhaust him with punishment."],[275,"That he used to tell stories, and in his stories he would say: «Indeed, when a man has intercourse with a woman but does not ejaculate, no ghusl is required of him.» A man arose from Zayd’s presence, went to ‘Umar ؓ, and informed him. ‘Umar ؓ said to the man: Go to him and bring him to me, so that you may be a witness against him! When he came, ‘Umar ؓ said to him: O enemy of God, are you the one who misleads people without knowledge? Zayd ؓ said: By God, O Commander of the Faithful, I did not invent it on my own; rather,"],[277,"A man said to him: A man has intercourse with his wife but does not ejaculate? He said: «Even if he shakes her until her saddle parts shake, no ghusl is required of him.»"],[278,"«Even if he shakes her until her saddle parts shake, no ghusl is required of him.»"],[279,"«Even if I reached that with her, I would perform ghusl.»"],[280,"«Even if she reached that from him, she would perform ghusl.»"],[281,"«Water is from water, and there is no harm in a dirham or two dirhams.»"],[282,"«Water is from water.»"],[283,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for a man from the Ansar, but he was delayed. He said: «What kept you?» He said: When your messenger came to me, I was with my wife, so I got up and performed ghusl. He said: «What is upon you that you should not perform ghusl as long as you have not ejaculated?» He said: So the Ansar used to do that."],[284,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went in search of a man from the Ansar and called him. The Ansari came out with his head dripping water. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: «What made you delay?» He said: You called me while I was with my wife, and I feared I would keep you waiting, so I hastened, got up, poured water over myself, and came out. He ﷺ said: «Did you ejaculate?» He said: No. He ﷺ said: «If you do that, do not perform ghusl; wash what of you touched the woman, and perform wudu as for prayer, for water is from water.»"],[286,"A woman called Busrah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, one of us sees herself with her husband in a dream? He ﷺ said: «If you find wetness, then perform ghusl, O Busrah.» He said: Then ‘A’ishah ؓ said to her: You have disgraced women! He ﷺ said: «Let her ask about what seems appropriate to her; may your forehead be dusty, or may your right hand be dusty.»"],[287,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, one of us sees in her dream what a man sees? He ﷺ said: «Do you find desire?» She said: Perhaps. He ﷺ said: «Do you find water?» She said: Perhaps. He ﷺ said: «Then let her perform ghusl.»"],[288,"Umm Sulaym ؓ asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he mentioned the like of it and said: “Dampness” instead of “water.” And at the end of it he said: “He said: When she sees that, let her perform ghusl.” Then some women met her and said to her: “You have disgraced us before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!” She said: “I would not stop until I know whether I am in a lawful state or an unlawful state!”"],[289,"A woman came to Umm Sulaym and said: “I saw in a dream as if so-and-so was having intercourse with me.” Umm Salamah mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “If she sees moisture, let her perform ghusl.”"],[291,"“Ghusl is from five things: cupping, the bathhouse, janabah, the dead, and Friday.” He said: That was mentioned to Ibrahim, and he said: They did not consider any ghusl obligatory except janabah, and they used to recommend the Friday ghusl."],[292,"“When one of you is junub, let him not sleep; for he does not know—perhaps his soul may be taken in his sleep.”"],[294,"“Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said to Adam: ‘O Adam, what led you to eat from the tree I forbade you?’” He said: “Adam made an excuse and said: ‘O Lord, Hawwa’ made it appealing to me.’ He said: ‘Then I have punished her by making her not carry except with discomfort, and not give birth except with discomfort, and I have made her bleed twice every month.’” He said: “Hawwa’ wailed at that, and it was said to her: ‘Upon you is the wailing, and upon your daughters.’”"],[296,"He said: “Hand me the khumrah.” It was said: Who? He said: The Prophet ﷺ. She said: “I am menstruating.” He said: “Your menstruation is not in your hand.”"],[298,"“Aishah ؓ used to forbid women from looking at themselves at night during menstruation, and she would say: ‘There may be yellowness or duskiness.’”"],[299,"“Asma’ and her brother’s daughters used to narrate to us. One of us would perform ghusl after the end of menstruation, then menstruation again—its flow leading to yellowness and duskiness—and she would command us to abstain from prayer until we saw nothing but pure whiteness.”"],[300,"“One of us would perform ghusl, and her yellowness would remain.”"],[302,"Fatimah bint Qays ؓ asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the woman with istihadah, and he said: “Count the days of your menstrual periods.” And he ordered her to use a cloth and pray and perform ghusl for every purification."],[303,"“Let her consider five, seven, eight, nine, ten. When ten have passed, then she is a mustahadah.”"],[304,"“The Prophet ﷺ ordered Umm Habibah to perform ghusl for every prayer, and she had been suffering from istihadah.”"],[306,"She asked 'A'ishah ؓ saying: 'One of us menstruates while she and her husband have only one bed and one blanket; what should she do?' She said: 'She should tie her waist-wrapper tightly, then sleep with him, and he may have what is above that.'"],[307,"Hudhayfah ؓ would leave after the dawn prayer in Ramadan and enter with her under his blanket, turning his back to her and not facing her, meaning while she was menstruating."],[308,"He had a wife who disliked men. Whenever he wanted her, she would claim to be menstruating. He thought she was lying, so he went to her and found her truthful. He came to the Prophet ﷺ, who ordered him to give charity of one-fifth of a dinar."],[309,"'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ had a wife."],[310,"'Umar ؓ came to a slave-girl of his, and she said, 'I am menstruating.' He had intercourse with her and found her menstruating. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, so he said: 'May Allah forgive you, O Abu Hafs. Give charity of half a dinar.'"],[313,"'Umar ؓ came to Mu'adh ؓ while he was among some of his companions and said: 'O Mu'adh, what is the foundation of this matter?' He said: 'Sincerity, which is the natural disposition; prayer, which is the religion; and obedience.'"],[314,"Abu Dharr ؓ sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he mentioned a hadith similar to the one before it. He said: 'I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is prayer?' He ﷺ said: 'A good placed before you; whoever wishes may do less of it, and whoever wishes may do more.'"],[315,"The first thing for which a servant will be brought to account is his purification. If he perfects his purification, then his prayer will be similar to his purification. Then he will be brought to account for his prayer. If his prayer is good, then the rest of his deeds will be similar to his prayer."],[316,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'What do you think of a man who recites at the beginning of the night and then steals at its end?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When he recites at its beginning, its end prevents him from stealing in the dark.'"],[318,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out for the funeral of a man from the Ansar, and he mentioned the hadith, in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O 'Umar, you will not be asked about the deeds of people, but you will be asked about prayer.'"],[319,"A man died during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[320,"The first thing for which a servant will be brought to account is his prayer. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says to the angels: 'Look at My servant's prayer. If you find it complete, it will be recorded as complete. If you find something missing from it, He says: Look and see if My servant has any voluntary prayers, so that his prayer may be completed from his voluntary prayers. Then the rest of his deeds will be taken according to that measure.'"],[321,"The first thing Allah Almighty made obligatory upon people in their religion is prayer, and the last thing that remains is prayer, and the first thing they are held accountable for is prayer. He says: 'Look at My servant's prayer.' Then he mentioned it until he said: 'If any voluntary prayer is found for him, the obligatory prayer is completed from the voluntary.' Then he said: 'Look: is his zakat complete? If his zakat is found complete, it is recorded as complete, and if it is found deficient...' He said: 'Look: does he have any charity? If he has, his zakat is completed from the charity.'"],[322,"We came to Abu Dharr ؓ – we were six people, our sixth a man from Juhaynah and we from Aslam – and found him preparing to leave Madinah. He said: 'Welcome to you. What brings you?' They said: 'We came to greet you and to benefit from you.' He ؓ said: 'Yes. I heard Abu al-Qasim ﷺ say: \"The five prayers – whoever meets Allah Almighty with them, not having neglected anything of them, Allah will forgive his sins even if they were as much as the fill of the earth.\"' We said: 'What about what came before in the pre-Islamic era?' He said: 'Piety wipes it out' – twice. The Juhani said to him: 'Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'Glory be to Allah! Is it permissible for a man to lie about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?'"],[323,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'O Anas, if you can always be praying, then do so, for the angels pray for you as long as you pray.'"],[324,"\"Be steadfast, and you will not be able to fully do so. Know that the best of your deeds is prayer, and no one maintains ablution except a believer.\""],[325,"Jibril, peace and blessings be upon him, said to me: 'Prayer has been made beloved to you, so take from it as much as you wish.'"],[326,"Jibril, peace and blessings be upon him, said to me: 'Prayer has been made beloved to you, so take from it as much as you wish.'"],[327,"The five prayers, and Jumu'ah to Jumu'ah, are expiations for what is between them as long as major sins are avoided."],[328,"The example of the five prayers is like a sweet flowing river, or an abundant river, at the door of one of you; he bathes in it five times a day. What dirt would remain on him?"],[329,"Whoever prays the morning prayer and then his protection is violated, the sanctuary of Allah Almighty has been violated and his covenant has been broken, and I will seek retribution for his covenant."],[330,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said to him: 'May Allah place you in the highest company of Paradise, and me with you.' He ﷺ said: 'Amin.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, teach me a righteous deed to do.' He ﷺ said: 'Establish prayer, for it is the best of jihad, and abandon sins, for that is the best of emigration, and remember Allah much, for the most beloved of deeds to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is that you meet Him with it.'"],[332,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was concerned about the call to prayer, and he disliked using a bell as the people of Makkah did. He ﷺ used to send men when prayer time came, and they would be busy with that instead of prayer. Abdullah b. Zayd al-Ansari ؓ returned, concerned with the Messenger's ﷺ concern, and he was visited in a dream. It was said to him: 'Why are you concerned?' He said: 'Because of the Messenger's ﷺ concern.' The one who came to him said: 'Go to the Prophet ﷺ and tell him to call for prayer: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, twice; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, twice; Hayya 'ala al-salah, twice; Hayya 'ala al-falah, twice; Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; La ilaha illa Allah.' Then he said to him: 'Make between the adhan and the iqamah something like that.' He said: Abdullah ؓ went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Teach it to Bilal.' Then Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ came and said: 'I saw the like of what Abdullah b. Zayd saw, but Abdullah preceded me.'"],[333,"Abu Mahdhurah ؓ gave the call for the noon prayer while Umar ؓ was in Makkah, and he raised his voice when the sun had passed its zenith. Umar ؓ said: 'O Abu Mahdhurah, do you not fear that your windpipe will split?' He ؓ said: 'I wanted to make you hear.' Umar ؓ said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Delay the prayer until it is cooler when the heat is intense, for the heat is from the blast of Hell. Hell complained until parts of it consumed other parts, and it asked permission of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, for two breaths, and He permitted it. So the intensity of heat is from the blast of Hell, and the intensity of extreme cold is from its cold.\"'"],[334,"\"Delay the prayer until it is cooler when the heat is intense, for the heat is from the blast of Hell. Hell complained until parts of it consumed other parts, and it asked permission of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, for two breaths, and He permitted it. So the intensity of heat is from the blast of Hell, and the intensity of extreme cold is from its cold.\" (Marfu')"],[335,"\"The first to give the adhan in the heaven was Jibril ﷺ .\" Umar and Bilal ؓ heard him. Umar ؓ came and informed the Prophet ﷺ of what he had heard. Then Bilal ؓ came and informed the Prophet ﷺ of what he had heard. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Umar beat you to it, O Bilal. Give the adhan as you heard.\" He said: Then the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to place his fingers in his ears to help with the sound."],[337,"The Prophet ﷺ had two mu'adhdhins: one of them was Bilal, and the other was Abd al-Aziz b. al-Asamm ؓ."],[338,"Abu Nu'aym said: Abu Bakr b. Khallad narrated to us, al-Harith narrated to us with it. [3] Abu Qurrah al-Zubaydi narrated it in his Sunan through the path of Musa b. Ubaydah with it exactly, and he added: \"And Bilal ؓ used to give the adhan at night, waking the sleeper, while Ibn Umm Maktum ؓ used to aim for dawn and would not miss it. And it is as if Abd al-Aziz b. al-Asamm ؓ, according to this, is Ibn Umm Maktum, and Allah knows best.\" :"],[339,"Abu Nu'aym said: Abu Bakr b. Khallad narrated to us, al-Harith narrated to us with it. [3] Abu Qurrah al-Zubaydi narrated it in his Sunan through the path of Musa b. Ubaydah with it exactly, and he added: \"And Bilal ؓ used to give the adhan at night, waking the sleeper, while Ibn Umm Maktum ؓ used to aim for dawn and would not miss it. And it is as if Abd al-Aziz b. al-Asamm ؓ, according to this, is Ibn Umm Maktum, and Allah knows best.\" :"],[341,"He used to give the adhan two by two, and make the iqamah odd."],[342,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered Bilal ؓ to give the adhan on top of the Ka'bah."],[344,"I gave the adhan at night, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"You have prevented the people from food and drink. Go up and call out: 'Behold, the servant has slept.'\" So I went, saying: \"Would that Bilal's mother had not given birth to him, and his forehead became wet from the splash of blood.\" Then I called out three times: \"Behold, the servant has slept.\""],[345,"\"Do not rely on the adhan of Ibn Umm Maktum, but rather on the adhan of Bilal.\" He said: Ibn Umm Maktum was blind."],[347,"\"If I were able to give the adhan along with the khilafah, I would give the adhan.\""],[348,"Umar ؓ said to his sitting companions: \"Who is your mu'adhdhin?\" They said: \"Our slaves and freedmen.\" He said: \"Our freedmen and our slaves. That is a great deficiency for you.\""],[350,"\"The most beloved of Allah's servants to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, are those who watch the sun and the moon.\""],[351,"\"The mu'adhdhin's virtue over those who attend the prayer with his adhan is one hundred and twenty; if he gives the iqamah, then two hundred and forty good deeds—except for one who says the like of what he says.\""],[352,"\"The mu'adhdhins will have the longest necks of people on the Day of Resurrection, and they will be the first to be permitted to speak on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[354,"Verily, the inhabitants of the heavens hear nothing from the inhabitants of the earth except the adhan."],[355,"I was admitted into Paradise, and I saw therein domes of pearls. I said, 'For whom are these, O Jibril?' He said, 'For the mu'adhdhins and the imams of your Ummah.'"],[356,"It has reached us that the first people to be clothed on the Day of Resurrection from the garments of Paradise will be the mu'adhdhins."],[358,"When ʿUthmān ؓ heard the adhan, he would say, 'Welcome to those who proclaim justice, and to the prayer—welcome and greetings.'"],[359,"When ʿAlī ؓ heard the adhan, he would say, 'I call every witness to testify to it, and I bear it on behalf of every denier.'"],[360,"When the caller calls to prayer, the gates of heaven are opened and supplication is answered. So whoever is afflicted by distress or hardship, let him wait for the caller. When he says 'Allāhu akbar,' he says 'Allāhu akbar.' When he bears witness, he bears witness. When he says 'Hayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh,' he says 'Hayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh.' When he says 'Hayya ʿalā al-falāḥ,' he says 'Hayya ʿalā al-falāḥ.' Then he says: 'O Allah, Lord of this perfect call, the call of truth that is answered—the call of truth and the word of piety—make us live upon it, cause us to die upon it, and resurrect us upon it. Make us among the best of its people in our living and our dying.' Then he asks Allah for his need."],[363,"And supplication is answered—and he did not mention what comes after it."],[364,"When he heard the mu'adhdhin say 'Allāhu akbar, Allāhu akbar,' he would say the like of what he said. When he said 'Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh,' he said the like of that. When he said 'Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan rasūlu Allāh,' he said the like of what he said. When he said 'Hayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh, hayya ʿalā al-falāḥ,' he said, 'There is no might and no power except with Allah.'"],[365,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ halted to rest one night, and Bilāl ؓ gave the adhan. He said, 'Whoever says the like of his words and bears witness with the like of his testimony will have Paradise.'"],[367,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us and said: 'Whoever undertakes the adhan of one of the mosques of Allah, Exalted be He, seeking thereby the Face of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, Allah, Exalted be He, will grant him the reward of forty thousand thousand prophets, forty thousand thousand truthful ones, and forty thousand thousand martyrs. Forty thousand thousand nations will enter into his intercession, in every nation forty thousand thousand men. He will have in every part of the gardens forty thousand thousand dwellings, in every dwelling forty thousand thousand houses, in every house forty thousand thousand couches, upon every couch a wife from the houris with wide eyes. The expanse of every house among them is the expanse of the world forty thousand thousand times. Before every wife are forty thousand thousand serving girls. In every house are forty thousand thousand tables, upon every table forty thousand thousand large bowls, in every large bowl forty thousand thousand kinds of food. If the two heavy ones (jinn and mankind) were to descend upon it, He would accommodate them in the least house of its houses with whatever they wished of food, drink, clothing, perfume, fruits, and various gifts, curiosities, ornaments and garments. Every house among them is self-sufficient with what it contains of these things, without need of another house. When the mu'adhdhin says, \"Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh,\" seventy thousand thousand angels surround him, all of them sending blessings upon him and seeking forgiveness for him. He is under the shade of the mercy of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, until he finishes, and forty thousand thousand angels record his reward. Then they ascend with it to Allah, Exalted be He.'"],[369,"Ask Allah, Exalted be He, for the Wasilah for me. No believer asks it for me in this world except that I will be a witness for him or an intercessor on the Day of Resurrection."],[370,"Aḥmad b. Manīʿ said: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us: Mūsā b. ʿUbaydah narrated to us with this. [It is followed by] al-Walīd b. ʿAbd al-Malik, from Mūsā b. Aʿyun. Al-Ṭabarānī transmitted it in al-Awsaṭ."],[371,"Aḥmad b. Manīʿ said: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us: Mūsā b. ʿUbaydah narrated to us with this. [It is followed by] al-Walīd b. ʿAbd al-Malik, from Mūsā b. Aʿyun. Al-Ṭabarānī transmitted it in al-Awsaṭ."],[373,"Bilal ؓ was late one day with the adhan, so a man gave the adhan. Then Bilal ؓ came and wanted to give the iqamah, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The one who gives the adhan gives the iqamah.”"],[375,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw a man praying two rak'ahs after the iqamah had been called, so he said: “Two prayers together?”"],[377,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked him about the prayers. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer in the dark, then he prayed the afternoon prayer in daylight. The next day, he waited for the dawn prayer until it was said: “What is keeping him?” Then he prayed. Then he waited for the afternoon prayer until it was said: “What is keeping him?” Then he prayed. Then he ﷺ said: “Where is the questioner?” He said: “Here I am.” He ﷺ said: “Did you witness us yesterday?” He said: “Yes.” He ﷺ said: “And did you witness us today?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Whichever of these you choose is a time, and what is between them is a time.”"],[378,"A man asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about the time of the morning prayer. He ﷺ said: “Pray it with me today and tomorrow.” When he was at the plain of Namirah near al-Juhfah, he prayed it when dawn broke. Then when we were at Dhu Tuwa, he delayed it until the people said: “Has the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away?” They said: “If only we had prayed it.” Then he came out and prayed it before the sun. Then he turned to the people and said: “What did you say?” They said: “We said: If only we had prayed.” He ﷺ said: “If you had done that, punishment would have befallen you.” Then he called the questioner and said ﷺ: “The prayer is between these two times.”"],[379,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ wrote to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari ؓ: I am writing about the prayer, and the most worthy thing for Muslims to attend to is the matter of their religion. I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying; I retained from that what I have retained, and I forgot from it what I have forgotten. So pray the noon prayer in the midday heat, the afternoon prayer while the sun is alive, the sunset prayer at the breaking of the fast of the fasting person, the evening prayer as long as you do not fear people's sleeping, and the morning prayer in darkness, and lengthen the recitation in it."],[380,"Gabriel ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: [Arise] and pray, and that was at the sun's decline when it had passed the meridian. So the Messenger of God ﷺ stood and prayed the noon prayer, four rak'ahs."],[382,"The Prophet ﷺ"],[383,"(Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ wrote to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari ؓ: Pray the noon prayer when the sun declines, the afternoon prayer while the sun is alive, white and clear, pray the sunset prayer when the sun sets – or when the sun has set – and pray the evening prayer when the twilight disappears until the first half of the night, for that is the Sunnah. And stand in darkness or in the dark, and lengthen the recitation.)"],[384,"Gabriel ﷺ came and prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ prayed with the people when the sun had declined. Then he prayed the afternoon prayer when his shadow was equal to him. Then he prayed the sunset prayer when the sun had set. Then he prayed the evening prayer after that, as if he intended the disappearance of the twilight. Then he prayed the dawn prayer in darkness when dawn broke. Then Gabriel ﷺ came the next day and prayed the noon prayer with the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ prayed the noon prayer with the people when his shadow was equal to him. Then he prayed the afternoon prayer when his shadow became twice his length. Then he prayed the sunset prayer when the sun had set, at the same time. Then he prayed the evening prayer after a portion of the night had passed. Then he prayed the dawn prayer and made it bright."],[385,"I asked Anas b. Malik ؓ, saying: Tell me about the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ that he used to persist in, for it has reached me that he delayed and advanced, but the prayer that he used to persist in is as if I were looking at it. He said: (The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray the noon prayer when the sun had declined; if it was summer he would cool it down. He used to pray the afternoon prayer while the sun was white and clear. He used to pray the sunset prayer when the disk of the sun had disappeared, and he would leave while the light of the star could not be seen. He used to delay the last evening prayer until, if he feared sleeping, he said: “O Bilal, give the adhan.” And I heard him ﷺ say: “Were it not that my community would sleep through it, it would please me to place it in the third of the night or half the night.” We used to leave the dawn prayer while we could see the light of the stars.)"],[386,"“I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say about the prayer: ‘Do not advance it for leisure, and do not delay it for need.’”"],[387,"We complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ about the intense heat, but he did not relieve us, and he said: “Seek help with ‘There is no power and no strength except with God,’ for it repels ninety-nine doors of harm, the least of which is anxiety.”"],[388,"Bilal announced the dawn prayer with enough light for the people to see the places where their arrows fell."],[389,"Pray the dawn prayer at daybreak, for whenever you pray it at daybreak, the reward is greater."],[390,"Sulayman b. Ubayd Allah narrated to us: Abu Amir narrated to us: Fulayh narrated from Asim b. Umar, from his father, from his grandfather, and he mentioned something similar. He said: We do not know of anyone who corroborated Fulayh."],[391,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Maghrib, then people would return to their families while they could still see the places where arrows fell when they shot them."],[392,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left Makkah at sunset and did not pray until he reached Sarif, which is nine miles from Makkah."],[393,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Fajr with us when dawn had broken and the stars were intertwined in the sky, so that we could hardly recognize one another, and men could hardly recognize one another."],[394,"A prayer is not missed until the time of the next prayer enters."],[395,"We used to pray Fajr with Ibn al-Zubayr ؓ, then go to Ji'ad, relieve ourselves, and return. Ibn al-Zubayr ؓ said: We used to pray with Umar ؓ while it was still dark, and one of us would leave without recognizing his companion."],[396,"Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah ؓ said to the Ansari who reminded him of the time of Asr prayer: Yes, bear witness that we used to pray Asr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while the sun was white and clear, then we would go to Banu Amr b. Awf, which is two miles from Madinah, and the sun had not yet disappeared."],[397,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ asking him about the prayer times. He prayed early and late, and said: \"The time is what is between these two.\""],[398,"When the shadow is one and a half cubits to two cubits, pray Zuhr."],[399,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Fajr when the dawn was bright."],[400,"\"Perform the morning prayer at dawn, for it is greater in reward.\""],[401,"\"Indeed, one of you may pray a prayer, and what he misses of its time is more severe upon him than [the loss of] his family and wealth.\""],[402,"\"Indeed, a man may pray a prayer, and what he misses of its time is better than his family and wealth.\""],[403,"I said to my father: \"O my father, what do you think about the saying of the Exalted: 'Those who are heedless of their prayer'—which of us does not become heedless? [Which of us] does not talk to himself?\" He said: \"It is not that; it is only wasting the time. He occupies himself until the time passes.\""],[404,"I asked my father and said: \"O father, 'those who are heedless of their prayer'—is it the heedlessness of one of us in his prayer, talking to himself?\" Sa'd said: \"Do we not all do that? But the heedless one...\""],[405,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about: \"Those who are heedless of their prayer.\" He said: \"They are those who take the prayer out of its time.\""],[406,"\"Indeed, after me there will be sinful leaders who pray the prayer at other than its time. So when they do that, pray the prayer at its time, and make your prayer with them a supererogatory prayer.\""],[408,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to like the white rooster and would command keeping it, and he would say: \"Indeed, it calls to prayer, wakes the sleeping, and drives away the jinn with its crowing.\""],[409,"\"A'ishah ؓ used to keep a rooster for the time of her prayer and for the time of her pre-dawn meal.\""],[411,"\"Indeed, the delegation of Thaqif came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and gave him a gift. They asked him, and they kept asking him until they did not pray Dhuhr except together with Asr.\""],[413,"I entered upon Anas b. Malik ؓ and he mentioned the hadith. He said: \"Then a slave girl came to him and said: 'Prayer, may Allah keep you well!' He said: 'Which prayer?' She said: 'Asr prayer.' He said: 'Have you already prayed it?' She said: 'I prayed it before I entered upon you.' He said: 'Move away from me; Asr has not yet come.' Then she repeated, and he said to her the like of his first statement. Then she repeated and spoke to him, and he said: 'I have heard what you said. Hand me water for ablution, for the people pray this prayer before its time.' Then he prayed.\""],[414,"I entered upon A'ishah ؓ, and she prayed Asr at the hour that you call between the two prayers. Then she said ؓ: \"Indeed, we, the family of Muhammad, do not pray the little yellow [prayer (i.e., Asr too early)].\""],[416,"Delay the Zuhr prayer in intense heat."],[417,"Abu Ya'la said: 'Abd al-A'la b. Hammad narrated to us, 'Abdullah b. Dawud narrated to us, with this. Abu Ya'la said: Thus."],[418,"Indeed, the intense heat is from the scorching breath of Hell, so delay the prayer."],[420,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to his Companions one night while they were waiting for the 'Isha' prayer, and said: \"The people have prayed and slept, while you are waiting for it? Verily, you are in prayer as long as you are waiting for it.\" Then he ﷺ said: \"Were it not for the weakness of the weak and the old age of the elderly, I would have delayed this prayer until the middle of the night.\""],[422,"Do not let the Bedouins overcome you regarding the name of [your prayer], for in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, it is called 'Isha'. Allah, the Exalted, said: 'And after the 'Isha' prayer, there are three times of privacy for you.' The Bedouins call it 'Atamah' only because of their camels and their milking."],[423,"342 282 / 2 - Abu Ya'la said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, 'Uthman b. 'Umar narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, with this:"],[425,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade sleeping before it and engaging in conversation after it – meaning the 'Isha' prayer."],[426,"I used to sleep before the 'Atamah, and when I heard the iqamah, I would get up and pray. It reached me that it is disliked, so I asked Anas b. Malik ؓ, and he disliked it and said: \"Do not sleep before it.\""],[428,"'A'ishah, the Mother of the Believers ؓ heard my speech after the 'Isha' prayer, which the Bedouins call 'Atamah. He said: We were in a room between her and him separated by palm branches. She said: \"O 'Urayyah – or O 'Urwah – what is this late-night conversation? I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sleeping before this prayer, nor conversing after it; either he slept and was safe, or he prayed and gained reward.\""],[429,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sleeping before the 'Isha' prayer, nor engaging in idle talk after it; either he remembered Allah and gained reward, or he slept and was safe."],[430,"Late-night conversation is for three: a newlywed, a traveler, or one performing night prayer."],[431,"Whoever sleeps before the 'Isha' prayer, may he not sleep."],[433,"Ask your needs from Allah Almighty in the morning prayer."],[435,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'Amr b. 'Abasa ؓ came to him, and he had pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon Islam. He said: \"Inform me, O Muhammad, of what you know and I am ignorant of.\" He asked him about the times of prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"When you have prayed Maghrib, prayer is accepted and witnessed until you pray Fajr. Then avoid prayer until the sun rises and becomes white, for the sun rises between the two horns of a devil. When it has become white and risen, prayer is accepted and witnessed until midday, when the sun is at its zenith and every thing stands in its shadow—that is the hour in which Hell is stoked. When the sun declines, prayer is accepted and witnessed until the sun turns yellow, for the sun sets between the two horns of a devil.\""],[436,"\"Except on Friday, for there is no harm in praying then at midday, because Hell is not stoked on that day.\""],[437,"We returned from the funeral of Rafi' b. Khadij ؓ after the morning prayer, and al-Walid b. 'Utbah was in charge of the people. He wanted to pray over it, so Ibn 'Umar ؓ stood and shouted at the top of his voice: \"Do not pray over your deceased until the sun has risen.\" So the commander and the people sat down."],[438,"I used to travel with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I never saw him pray after 'Asr or after Fajr."],[439,"And Abu Bakr said: Yahya b. Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us with this chain. This chain is good (hasan)."],[440,"A man saw Abu al-Darda' ؓ praying when the sun had turned yellow, and he said: \"O companions of Muhammad, you forbid prayer after Fajr and after 'Asr?\" He said: \"Yes, except that this house is not like others.\""],[441,"We were at a funeral in which Budayl was present, and he said—while the sun was yellow on the edges of the walls—\"Do not pray at this hour.\" Abu Umamah ؓ said: \"I prayed with Abu Hurayrah ؓ over a funeral at this hour.\""],[442,"\"There is no prayer after Fajr except two rak'ahs.\""],[443,"And Ibn Abi 'Umar said: Al-Muqri' narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman b. Ziyad narrated to us with this chain."],[444,"And 'Abd b. Humayd said: Ya'la narrated to us, al-Ifriqi narrated to us with this chain."],[445,"He used to pray after 'Asr, and Ibn 'Abbas ؓ forbade him. Tawus said: \"It was only forbidden lest it be taken as a ladder.\" Ibn 'Abbas ؓ said: \"It is not for any believing man or believing woman, when Allah and His Messenger have decided a matter, to have any choice in their affair\"—the verse—\"and I do not know whether you will be punished for it or rewarded.\""],[446,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade praying after the dawn prayer until the sun rises, for it rises on the horn — or two horns — of Satan."],[447,"Umar ؓ used to strike for the two rakʿahs after ʿAsr."],[448,"Indeed, what is the matter with people who pray a prayer that I accompanied the Messenger of God ﷺ and never saw him pray, and we heard him forbid it — meaning the two rakʿahs after ʿAsr."],[449,"Umar ؓ saw Tamim al-Dari ؓ praying after ʿAsr and struck him with the whip. Tamim said, 'Why, O Umar, do you strike me for a prayer I prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ?' Umar ؓ said, 'O Tamim, not all people know what you know.'"],[450,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade prayer at midday except on Friday."],[451,"He saw a man praying after ʿAsr and rebuked him, saying: Do not pray after ʿAsr, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'There is no prayer after ʿAsr.'"],[452,"I performed tawaf with Umar ؓ after the dawn prayer. He mounted and did not stop until he reached Dhu Tuwa, then he prayed two rakʿahs."],[453,"Abu Hubayrah al-Ansari, the companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, saw me praying Fajr when the sun had risen, and he criticized that and forbade me. Then he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Do not pray until the sun has risen, for it rises between the horns of a devil.'"],[454,"Do not pray at sunrise or sunset, for it rises and sets on the horn of a devil. Pray between those times as you wish."],[456,"I was sitting in a gathering in which Ubada ؓ was present. He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Gabriel ﷺ came to me from God Almighty and said: O Muhammad, God Almighty says: I have enjoined upon your community five prayers. Whoever fulfills them with their ablution, their times, their bowing, and their prostration, he has with Me a covenant that I will admit him by them into Paradise."],[457,"Prayer was made obligatory on the Messenger of God ﷺ on the night of the Isra as fifty prayers, then it was reduced until it was made five. God, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'You have in the five the reward of fifty; a good deed is multiplied tenfold.'"],[458,"A Bedouin came to him and said: O Ibn Abbas, we are people among the Muslims, and here are people among the Muhajirun who claim that we are not upon anything. Ibn Abbas ؓ said: The Prophet of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever establishes the prayer, gives the zakat, performs the pilgrimage to the House, fasts Ramadan, and honors the guest — will enter Paradise.'"],[460,"He had prayed toward both qiblahs. He said: I was in my house when a caller called at the door: The Prophet ﷺ has turned toward the Kaaba. I bear witness that our imam, the men, the women, and the boys prayed toward here – meaning Jerusalem – and toward here – meaning the Kaaba."],[461,"“Face the qiblah closely.”"],[462,"375 309/2 – Harun b. Ma‘ruf narrated to us, Bishr b. al-Sari narrated to us, with it."],[463,"“I do not know anything of people’s affairs except the qiblah.”"],[464,"“The noblest gatherings are those that face the qiblah.”"],[465,"I saw ‘Abdullah b. ‘Amr ؓ in the Sacred Mosque opposite the waterspout, saying: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said to His Prophet ﷺ: “We will surely turn you to a qiblah that pleases you.” So this is the qiblah, this is the qiblah."],[466,"‘Umar ؓ saw a man praying far from the qiblah and said: Come forward, do not ruin your prayer. I only told you what I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say."],[467,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enter the mosque from the gate of Banu Shaybah until he came to the front of the Kaaba. He faced the qiblah and drew a line in front of him widthwise, then said the takbir and prayed while people were circumambulating between the line and the Kaaba."],[468,"“A woman and a dog cut off the prayer.” I said: What can screen me? He ﷺ said: “An arrow, a saddle, or a stone.”"],[469,"“If there is between you and the one passing in front of you the like of the back of a saddle, then it screens you.”"],[470,"“If there is between you and the one passing in front of you the like of the back of a saddle, then it screens you.”"],[472,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey – or an expedition – when clouds covered us. We tried to determine the qiblah and differed, so each of us prayed and drew a line in front of him to mark our places. When morning came, we looked and found that we had prayed toward other than the qiblah. We mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not order us to repeat, saying: “Your prayer is sufficient.”"],[473,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over his son Ibrahim and said the takbir over him four times."],[476,"He used to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ. One day he entered upon him while he had uncovered his thighs. He said: “O son of Abū Ṭālib, do not uncover your thigh, for it is ʿawrah, and do not look at the thigh of a living person or a dead one, for you wash the dead.”"],[477,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me while I had uncovered my thigh. He said: “O ʿAlī, cover your thigh, for it is part of the ʿawrah.”"],[478,"A woman should not pray in fewer than three garments if she is able."],[479,"How does the [slave woman] pray? He said: “As she goes out.”"],[480,"A woman prays in three garments."],[481,"I saw my father praying in a single garment while his other clothes were set aside. He said: “O my daughter, the last prayer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed was in a single garment.”"],[482,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū Bakr narrated to us with this. :, : :"],[483,"I saw Maymūnah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, praying in a full, tight chemise and a head cover, without a waist wrapper."],[484,"I asked ʿAṭāʾ about people who are drowning and come out naked: how do they pray? He said: “If they find grass, they cover themselves with it; otherwise they pray sitting, with their imam among them—or he said: in their midst.”"],[485,"Most of those who prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were the people of knots.” I said: “And who are the people of knots?” He said: “One of them had only a single garment which he tied at his neck.”"],[487,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in a single garment, wrapping it around himself."],[488,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer in a single garment, wrapping it around himself."],[489,"And Abu Ya'la said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Ya'la b. al-Harith narrated to us, with it. [ ] : , : , : :"],[490,"And Musa b. Muhammad narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated to us, with it. :"],[491,"(I visited my sister Umm Habiba ؓ, and I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying in a single garment, having wrapped its two ends over opposite shoulders)"],[492,"And Abu Ya'la said: Ishaq b. Yahya narrated to us, Isma'il b. 'Ayyash narrated to us, with it. :"],[493,"Ibrahim b. al-Husayn narrated to us, [Mubashshir] - meaning Ibn Isma'il - and al-Harith b. 'Atiyya, and Muhammad b. Kathir, from al-Awza'i, from [Ya'ish] b. al-Walid, from Mu'awiya ؓ, something similar to it."],[494,"I came to 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ and said: We go out every year, and I have a [building] in which there is a small space. [If] I pray in it, the woman would be parallel to me, and if I go out, I become cold. He said: Place a garment between the two of you as a barrier, then pray however you wish."],[495,"\"It does not harm any of you to pray in his garment, wrapped up, but let him tie it so that it does not distract him from his prayer.\""],[496,"(Indeed 'Ali ؓ did not see any harm in a man praying in a single garment, and he used to pray in a single garment, having wrapped its two ends over opposite shoulders)"],[497,"(I saw Khalid b. al-Walid ؓ leading the people in prayer in the army in a single garment)"],[498,"(Indeed the Messenger of God ﷺ came out leaning on Usama b. Zayd ؓ, wearing a Qitri garment, with no other garment on him)"],[499,"(Prayer in a single garment is good; we did it with the Messenger of God ﷺ)"],[500,"He asked 'A'isha ؓ: Did the Messenger of God ﷺ pray on a straw mat? For I heard in the Book of God, Mighty and Majestic: \"And We have made Hell a mat for the disbelievers\"? 'A'isha ؓ said: No, the Messenger of God ﷺ did not pray on it."],[501,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[502,"(I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating on his garment."],[503,"(I entered upon Zayd b. Thabit ؓ and saw him praying on a mat, and he prostrated on it."],[504,"(I saw al-Nu'man b. Bashir ؓ praying on a plank."],[505,"(I do not like to pray in this locked house of theirs."],[507,"(I was praying toward a grave, and 'Umar ؓ saw me and began saying: \"The grave, the grave.\" I did not understand what he meant, so I raised my head toward the sky, and he said: \"The grave is in front of you.\""],[508,"They both said: And Hushaym narrated to us: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, from 'Umar ؓ, the like of that. This is a sound report that al-Bukhari cited in suspended form."],[509,"\"The prayer is cut off by a dog, a donkey, and a woman.\""],[510,"(I was praying when a man passed in front of me, so I prevented him. Then I asked 'Uthman b. 'Affan ؓ, and he said: \"O son of my brother, it does not harm you.\""],[511,"(Abu Sa'id ؓ was praying when al-Harith passed in front of him – or wanted to pass in front of him – until he was about to grab his hair. Al-Harith complained to Marwan, so Abu Sa'id came to Marwan, and Marwan said: \"If you obey this man and his companions, they will surely turn you into Jews.\" Abu Sa'id ؓ said: \"[You] have lied, by Allah. If you and your father became Jews, we would not become Jews with you.\") Ayyub said: Muhammad said: \"He spoke the truth. Judaism was offered to them in pre-Islamic times and they refused it.\""],[513,"Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayyihan came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him for a servant, so the Prophet ﷺ promised him one if he obtained captives. Then he met 'Umar ؓ, who said: \"O Abu al-Haytham, the Prophet ﷺ has obtained captives. So go to him, for he will fulfill his promise to you.\" Abu al-Haytham and 'Umar ؓ went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and 'Umar ؓ said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu al-Haytham has come to you to claim your promise.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"We have obtained two black slave boys. Choose whichever of them you wish.\" He said: \"I consult you.\" He ﷺ said: \"Take this one, for he has prayed with us, and do not beat him, for we have been forbidden from striking those who pray.\""],[514,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade striking those who pray."],[515,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us, then he mentioned it."],[516,"'Amr b. al-Dahhak b. Makhlad narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Musa narrated to us, with it. [And] Musa is weak."],[518,"We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the prayer of children. He said: \"When one of them knows his right hand from his left, then command him to pray.\""],[519,"\"Command them to pray at seven, and strike them for it at thirteen.\""],[521,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us while we were building the mosque, and he said: \"Make it spacious [so that you may fill it].\""],[522,"\"Had I not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'I intend to extend our qiblah,' I would not have added to it.\""],[523,"\"I intend to extend our qiblah,\" I would not have added to it. So he extended what was between the minbar and the place of the maqsurah."],[524,"\"Mosques are the houses of Allah on earth.\""],[525,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which places are [the worst]?\" He said: \"I do not know,\" or he remained silent. Then he said to him: \"Which places are the best?\" He said: \"I do not know,\" or he remained silent. Then Gabriel ﷺ came to him and asked him, and he said: \"I do not know.\" He said: \"Ask your Lord.\" So he said: \"We do not ask Him about anything,\" and he trembled a trembling by which the soul of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ almost ascended. When Gabriel ﷺ ascended, Allah (Mighty and Majestic) said: \"Muhammad asked you: Which places are the best? And you said: I do not know?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Tell him that the best of places are the mosques, and the worst of places are the markets.\""],[527,"\"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, even like the nest of a qata, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\""],[528,"[Ishaq said:] Jarir and Abu Mu'awiyah—meaning from al-A'mash—informed us with this chain of narration likewise."],[529,"\"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah like the nest of a qata, a house will be built for him in Paradise and a good deed will be recorded for him.\""],[530,"Whoever builds a mosque"],[531,"Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah said: Yahya b. Adam narrated to us, Qutbah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, with it, raised. :"],[532,"I heard it from al-A'mash when he was a young man. :"],[533,"Al-Bazzar said: Salm b. Junadah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us - in his house - from Sufyan al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, raised. Al-Bazzar said: We do not know anyone who followed Salm b. Junadah in this; it is only known from the hadith of Ahmad b. Yunus, from Abu Bakr b. 'Ayyash. :"],[534,"Abu Ya'la narrated it in his Musnad: Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. 'Ar'arah narrated to us, Yahya b. Adam narrated to us, [Qutbah b. al-'Ala' narrated to us, from al-A'mash], with it, raised [also]. 351/9 - And Muhammad b. Harb al-Nasha'i narrated it, from Muhammad b. 'Ubayd, from his brother Ya'la b. 'Ubayd, from al-A'mash, with it, raised also. :"],[535,"Abu Ya'la narrated it in his Musnad: Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. 'Ar'arah narrated to us, Yahya b. Adam narrated to us, [Qutbah b. al-'Ala' narrated to us, from al-A'mash], with it, raised [also]. 351/9 - And Muhammad b. Harb al-Nasha'i narrated it, from Muhammad b. 'Ubayd, from his brother Ya'la b. 'Ubayd, from al-A'mash, with it, raised also. :"],[536,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us - and he mentioned a long hadith - in which there is: \"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will grant him for every span - or he said: for every cubit - forty thousand thousand cities of gold, silver, pearls, rubies, and gems. In every city there are forty thousand palaces, in every palace seventy thousand houses, in every house a thousand rooms, in every room forty thousand beds, on every bed a wife from the houris of Paradise, and in every house forty thousand serving girls, and in every house forty thousand tables, on every table forty thousand bowls, in every bowl forty thousand kinds of food. And Allah, the Exalted, will give His friend such strength that he will be able to have intercourse with all those wives and consume all that food and drink in a single day.\""],[537,"\"Whoever builds a mosque, even if it is like the nest of a sandgrouse for its eggs, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\""],[538,"\"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\""],[539,"\"Whoever builds a mosque, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\" She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and these mosques on the road to Makkah? He said: \"And those.\""],[540,"\"Even if only the size of the nest of a sandgrouse.\""],[541,"\"Whoever builds a house in which Allah is worshipped from lawful [wealth], Allah will build for him a house in Paradise of pearls and rubies.\""],[543,"Anas b. Malik ؓ passed by before the sweeping plague, and he would pass by a mosque that had been newly built and ask about it. He would be told: This is a mosque built by the tribe of so-and-so. He said: It used to be said: (A time will come upon people when they will build mosques [to boast with them], then they will not frequent them except a little). Ayyub said: Then the sweeping flood came and swept them away."],[545,"Keep your children, the insane, the execution of your legal punishments, the drawing of your swords, your buying and selling, and your disputes away from your mosques. Perfume them on your Fridays, and place purification facilities at their doors."],[546,"A man took a louse from his garment and threw it in the mosque, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Put it back in your garment.\""],[547,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man who had taken a louse."],[548,"He forbade that legal punishments be carried out in mosques, or that poetry be recited in them, or that weapons be drawn in them."],[549,"Legal punishments are not to be carried out in mosques."],[550,"I heard Ibn 'Abbas ؓ delivering a sermon on a rainy day, and he said: \"Pray in your dwellings, and do not carry this filth on your feet to the mosque, for not all the neighbors of the mosque can perform purification for you.\""],[551,"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and burying it is a good deed."],[552,"If you see an elder reciting poetry in the mosque on Friday and mentioning the days of ignorance, strike his head with a staff."],[553,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a dream, and I said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about this hadith that is narrated from you: 'The angels are harmed by what the children of Adam are harmed by'?\" He ﷺ said: \"It is true.\""],[554,"I heard Jabir ؓ when he was asked about garlic, and he said: \"There was no garlic in our land at that time. What was prohibited was only onion and leek.\""],[555,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to eat garlic, and he said: \"Were it not that the angel descends upon me, I would eat it.\""],[557,"The best form of ribat (keeping guard) is awaiting the prayer and keeping to the gatherings of remembrance. No servant prays and then remains seated in his place of prayer but that the angels continue to send blessings upon him until he breaks his ablution or gets up."],[558,"Whoever sits in his prayer place or enters a mosque for prayer, the angels do not cease to pray for him as long as he remains in his sitting place, so long as he does not invalidate his ablution: 'O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him.'"],[559,"We entered upon 'Abdullah b. Habib – he is Abu 'Abd al-Rahman – while he was dying in his mosque. I said, 'Would you move to your bed?' He said..."],[560,"Do you not see His saying: 'The servant does not cease to be in prayer as long as he is in his prayer place.' He said: I said, 'His sitting place where he prays?' He said: 'Rather, the entire mosque.'"],[561,"There is no man who makes the mosques his home, and then an illness or ailment keeps him away from them, but when he returns, Allah welcomes him with joy."],[562,"Indeed, Allah, Exalted is He, will call out on the Day of Resurrection: 'Where are My neighbors?' The angels will say: 'Our Lord, who deserves to be Your neighbor?' He will say: 'Where are those who frequent the mosques?'"],[563,"Those who frequent the mosques of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, are the people of Allah."],[564,"'Abd b. Humayd said: Yunus b. Muhammad narrated to us, Salih narrated to us, with this same hadith."],[565,"Abu Ya'la said: Ibrahim b. al-Hajjaj al-Nili narrated to us."],[566,"Al-Bazzar said: 'Abd al-Wahid b. Ghiyath narrated to us. Both of them said: Salih narrated to us, with this same hadith. Al-Bazzar said: We do not know anyone who narrated it from Thabit except Salih. And so said al-Tabarani in al-Awsat."],[567,"Indeed, Abu al-Darda' ؓ said to his son: 'O my son, let your house be the mosque, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The mosque is the house of the pious. Whoever makes the mosques his home, Allah will guarantee for him comfort, mercy, and safe passage over the Sirat to Paradise.\""],[568,"There are six gatherings in which a Muslim is not present except that he is under the protection of Allah, Exalted is He: in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic; in a congregational mosque; with a sick person; following a funeral procession; in his own home; or with a just ruler, honoring and respecting him."],[569,"'Abd b. Humayd said: 'Abdullah b. Yazid al-Muqri' narrated to us, with this same hadith."],[570,"Al-Bazzar said: Muslim narrated to us, 'Abdullah b. Yazid narrated to us, with it."],[572,"Indeed I say when I enter the mosque: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah."],[573,"When he went out to the mosque, he would say: 'O Allah, protect me from the accursed Satan.'"],[574,"That when he entered the mosque, he would greet the Prophet ﷺ, then say: 'O Allah, open for me the gates of Your mercy,' and when he left, he would send blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ and seek refuge from Satan."],[575,"When he entered the mosque, he would say: 'O Allah, open for me the gates of Your mercy,' and when he left, he would say: 'O Allah, open for me the gates of Your bounty.'"],[577,"That he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about praying with a bow. He said: 'Pray with the bow, and cast aside the bowstring.'"],[578,"'Pray with the bow and cast aside the bowstring' - raised attribution."],[579,"'Pray with the bow and cast aside the bowstring' - raised attribution."],[580,"'Pray with the bow and cast aside the bowstring' - raised attribution."],[581,"When we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the military camp and the prayer was called, we would rush to our bows and swords and pray with them, as if they were a cloak."],[582,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me to pray with my hair plaited, and to smooth the pebbles during prayer."],[583,"Whoever buys a garment for ten dirhams and one of them is unlawful, Allah will not accept his prayer as long as he wears it. Then he inserted his fingers into his ears and said: May they be deaf if I did not hear the Prophet ﷺ say it."],[584,"The Prophet ﷺ removed his sandals while praying, so those behind him removed theirs. He ﷺ said: 'What made you remove your sandals?' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we saw you remove yours, so we removed ours.' He ﷺ said: 'Jibril"],[585,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed and removed his sandals, so the people removed their sandals. He said to them: '[Why] did you remove your sandals?' They said: 'You removed yours, so we removed ours.' He said: 'Jibril ﷺ"],[586,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying while wearing two sandals made of camel hide. He said: He spat to his left, then rubbed with his sandal where he had spat."],[587,"Abdullah came to Abu Musa at his home. When the prayer time arrived, Abu Musa said: 'Go forward, O Abu Abd al-Rahman, for you are older than me and more learned.' He said: 'No, you go forward, for we came to you in your home and your mosque, so you are more entitled.' Abu Musa ؓ went forward and removed his sandals. When he said the salam, Abdullah said to him: 'What did you intend by removing them? Are you in the sacred valley of Tuwa?'"],[588,"He used to pray in his leather socks."],[589,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to pray with his head tied back."],[591,"Were it not that you would be overburdened, I would have commanded you to use the siwak at every prayer."],[593,"If they are three, one of them should go forward and the other two should line up behind him. He said: And I came once and stood at his left, so he moved me to his right."],[594,"The women of the Children of Israel used to pray with the men in the same row. They took wooden clogs to make themselves taller, so that one of them could look at her friend. Menstruation was imposed upon them, and they were moved back. Abdullah said: So move them back from where Allah, Mighty and Majestic, moved them back."],[595,"I entered with Umar for the voluntary prayer of Zuhr, and he placed me at his right. Then Yarfa came, so I and he stood behind him."],[596,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed with him and with Jabir—or Jabbar—b. Sakhr, and he placed them behind him."],[597,"Press together in the rows, for the devils pass through you like small lambs."],[598,"And Abu Ya'la said: 'Abdullah b. 'Umar b. Aban narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, with it."],[599,"«The best of the rows of men are the first ones, and the worst are the last ones; and the best of the rows of women are the last ones and the worst are the first ones.»"],[600,"(Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon the one who keeps the first row straight.)"],[601,"(Umm Salamah ؓ led us in the afternoon prayer, and she stood in the middle of us.)"],[602,"(Bilal ؓ used to straighten our shoulders and strike our feet to establish the row.)"],[604,"(I entered the mosque of Hims, and there was a young man with people around him, with short curly hair. When he spoke, it was as if light and pearls came out of his mouth. I said: Who is this?) They said: Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ. I heard him say: Whoever is pleased to meet Allah Almighty safely, let him come to these five prayers where the call is made for them, for they are among the ways of guidance and among what your Prophet ﷺ instituted for you. Let him not say: I have a prayer place in my house so I will pray there. If you do that, you will abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, and if you abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet, you will go astray. By the One in whose hand is my soul, I have seen us in the time of the Prophet ﷺ when none would stay away from it except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was evident, to the point that a sick man would be supported between two men until he was placed in the row."],[605,"And Abu Ya'la said: 'Abd al-A'la b. Hammad narrated to us."],[606,"«I was about to order a caller for prayer, then go after men who stay away from prayer and burn their houses down upon them.»"],[607,"(I entered upon Zayd b. Thabit to visit him while he was sick, and his two sons were with him. The prayer was called, so he said: Go to the prayer, for a man's prayer in congregation is twenty-five degrees more excellent than his prayer alone.)"],[608,"«A man's prayer alone in the way of Allah Almighty is [worth] twenty-five prayers, and his prayer with his traveling companions is [worth] nine hundred prayers, and his prayer in congregation is [worth] forty-nine thousand prayers.»"],[609,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: «Whoever keeps to the congregation wherever he is and with whomever he is will pass over the bridge like flashing lightning in the first group with the foremost, and his face will be brighter than the moon on the night of the full moon. For every day and night he keeps to it, he will have the reward of a martyr. And whoever keeps to the front row and catches the first takbir without harming a believer, Allah Almighty will give him the reward of the muezzin on the Day of Resurrection.»"],[610,"(Whoever hears the call to prayer and then does not come to the prayer without an excuse, there is no prayer for him.)"],[611,"He disliked that a man leave the mosque after hearing the iqamah."],[612,"Whoever hears the call to the congregation and does not come, three times, then hears and does not come, three times, a seal is placed upon his heart and his heart is made the heart of a hypocrite."],[613,"The excellence of a man's prayer in congregation over his prayer alone is twenty-four parts."],[614,"Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His angels send blessings upon those who join the rows, and between the prayer of an individual and the congregation there are twenty-five degrees."],[616,"A man came as a delegate, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Is there not a man who will give charity to this one and pray with him?' He said: A man stood and prayed with him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'This is the congregation, and these are a congregation.'"],[618,"I witnessed Abdullah b. Umar ؓ in Makkah while al-Hajjaj was besieging Ibn al-Zubayr ؓ, and Ibn Umar ؓ was between the two. Sometimes he attended the prayer with these, and sometimes he attended the prayer with those."],[619,"A hypocrite does not maintain the later isha prayer for forty nights."],[621,"When the imam prays sitting, then pray sitting."],[622,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ while he was leading the people in prayer, Abd al-Rahman wanted to move back, but the Prophet ﷺ gestured to him: 'Stay in your place.' So he prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed following the prayer of Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ."],[623,"I entered upon Jabir b. Abdullah ؓ and found him sitting while leading his companions in the afternoon prayer, and they were sitting. He said: I watched until he said the salam, then I said: May Allah forgive you, you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and you lead them in prayer while sitting? He said: I am ill, so I sat and ordered them to sit. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The imam is a shield; if he prays standing, then pray standing, and if he prays sitting, then pray sitting.'"],[624,"He used to lead the people in prayer here, and some people would place their heads before he placed his head, and raise their heads before he raised his head. When he finished, he turned to them and said: 'O people, why do you sin and cause others to sin? I prayed for you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I did not deviate from it.'"],[625,"I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, and a man raised his head before the Prophet ﷺ. When he finished, he said: 'Whoever raises his head before the imam or places it before him, there is no prayer for him.'"],[626,"Verily, the one who raises his head and lowers it before the imam, his forelock is in the hand of a devil."],[628,"When we raised our heads from bowing behind the Prophet ﷺ, we would remain standing until we saw the Prophet ﷺ had prostrated and placed his face on the ground, then we would prostrate after that."],[630,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us, and he mentioned a long hadith in which he said: \"Whoever leads a people and they are pleased with him, and he is moderate with them in his presence, his recitation, his bowing, his prostration, and his sitting, then he will have the like of their rewards. And whoever is not moderate with them in that, his prayer will be returned to him and will not go beyond his collarbones, and he will be in the position of a tyrannical, transgressing ruler who did not act rightly toward his subjects and did not establish among them the command of Allah, Exalted is He.\" Then Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ said: \"O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, what is the position of the tyrannical, transgressing ruler who did not act rightly toward his subjects and did not establish among them the command of Allah, Exalted is He?\" He ﷺ said: \"He is the fourth of four, and he is the most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection: Iblis, Pharaoh, Qabil the killer of a soul, and the tyrannical ruler is their fourth.\""],[632,"Be concise in the prayer, for behind you are the weak, the elderly, and the one with a need."],[633,"Al-A'mash said: And Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Harith b. Suwayd, from Abdullah, something similar."],[634,"And Ibrahim al-Nakha'i narrated to us from Abdullah something similar."],[635,"And Habib b. Abi Thabit narrated to us, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas ؓ, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. I said: The hadith of Abu Hurayrah ؓ they reported."],[636,"He and his father entered upon Anas b. Malik ؓ during the time of Umar b. Abd al-Aziz ؓ, when he was governor, and he prayed a light prayer as if it were the prayer of a traveler or close to it. When he said the salam, he said: \"May Allah have mercy on you, did you consider this prayer; is it the obligatory prayer or something you offered voluntarily?\" He said: \"It is the obligatory prayer, and it is indeed the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; I did not miss anything from it except something I forgot. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: 'Do not be harsh on yourselves, lest harshness be imposed on you. For a people were harsh on themselves, so harshness was imposed on them. Those are their remnants in the monasteries and hermitages and monasticism which they innovated; We did not prescribe it for them.'\""],[637,"Mu'adh ؓ led his people in the dawn prayer and recited Surat al-Baqarah, and behind him was a Bedouin man who had a water-carrying camel of his. When it was the second rak'ah, the Bedouin prayed and left Mu'adh ؓ. So they informed the Prophet ﷺ about him, and he said: \"I feared for my camel, and I have dependents whom I earn for.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Pray with them the prayer of the weakest of them, for among them are the young, the elderly, and the one with a need. Do not be a tempter.\""],[639,"It is from the Sunnah that the imam be prompted when he asks you [to do so]."],[640,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ hesitated in a verse during the dawn prayer. When he finished the prayer, he looked at the faces of the people and said: \"Did not Ubayy b. Ka'b pray with you?\" They said: \"No.\" He said: The people thought that he only sought him to prompt him."],[642,"Anas b. Malik ؓ passed by us in the mosque of Banu Tha'labah and said: \"Have you prayed?\" We said: \"Yes,\" and that was during the morning prayer. So he ordered a man who called the adhan and the iqamah, then he prayed with his companions."],[644,"“The prayer was commenced, and the people pushed one another regarding the leadership. He kept saying to this one and that one: ‘Go forward,’ until the earth swallowed them up.”"],[646,"(The Messenger of God ﷺ recited in the evening prayer during travel “By the Fig and the Olive.”)"],[647,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite in the first two units the Opening of the Book and a surah, and in the last two the Opening of the Book.”"],[648,"(They both prayed with ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ [the dawn prayer], and he recited: “When the sky is split apart,” and he prostrated in it.)"],[649,"(I prayed with ʿUmar ؓ the dawn prayer, and he recited in it the surah of the Pilgrimage and prostrated twice in it.) I said: “The dawn prayer?” He said: “(The dawn prayer.)”"],[650,"The Prophet ﷺ recited in the dawn prayer: “Blessed is He in whose hand is the dominion.”"],[651,"(The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to recite in the dawn prayer “By the night when it covers” and “By the sun and its brightness.”)"],[652,"The Prophet ﷺ recited in the dawn prayer “Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of daybreak” and “Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind,” and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The daybreak is Hell.”"],[654,"I entered upon Jābir b. ʿAbd Allāh ؓ in Makkah and found him sitting and praying with his companions… the hadith, and in it: “We used to call to prayer in our houses and gather our families.”"],[656,"“The imam of a people is their delegate to God, Mighty and Majestic, so put forward the best of you.”"],[657,"Muʿādh ؓ used to pray the dawn prayer with the Prophet ﷺ, then return and lead his companions."],[658,"Salmān ؓ was put forward by his people to lead them in prayer, but he refused until they compelled him. When he led them, he said: “Are all of you satisfied?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “Praise be to God. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘Three people’s prayer is not accepted: a woman who leaves her house without her husband’s permission; a runaway slave; and a man who leads people in prayer while they dislike him.’”"],[659,"Indeed, 'Ali ؓ used to dislike that the one who had performed tayammum should lead those who had performed wudu'."],[660,"Indeed, Mu'awiyah ؓ led them in prayer wearing a single shirt."],[661,"O Abu 'Ubaydah, let no one after me lead the prayer while sitting."],[663,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer while a man was praying alone behind the row of people, so he said: \"O you who pray alone, could you not have joined a row and entered with them, or pulled a man to yourself if the space was tight for you? Repeat your prayer, for there is no prayer for you.\""],[665,"Regarding the one who forgets a prayer, he said: \"He should pray it when he remembers it.\""],[666,"During the journey in which they slept until the sun rose upon them, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"You were dead, and Allah, the Exalted, returned your souls to you. Whoever sleeps through a prayer should pray it when he wakes up, and whoever forgets a prayer should pray it when he remembers it.\""],[667,"\"You were dead, and Allah, the Exalted, returned your souls to you. Whoever sleeps through a prayer should pray it when he wakes up, and whoever forgets a prayer should pray it when he remembers it.\" [Marfu']"],[668,"Hudhayfah ؓ appointed me as his successor, so we prayed Zuhr. Then we came upon a group of people praying Zuhr, and we prayed with them. Then we prayed 'Asr, and we came upon a group of people praying 'Asr, and we prayed with them. Then we prayed Maghrib, and we came upon a group of people praying Maghrib, and we prayed with them. But when I stood for the third time, he detained me."],[669,"Al-Walid b. 'Uqbah ؓ led the people in prayer, and 'Abdullah made the people repeat the prayer, and he repeated the prayer."],[670,"Whoever forgets a prayer and does not remember it except while he is with the imam should pray with the imam. Then when he finishes his prayer, he should repeat the prayer he forgot, then he should repeat the prayer he prayed with the imam."],[671,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and camped during the latter part of the night, and he did not wake up until the sun had risen. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Bilal ؓ to give the adhan, then he prayed two rak'ahs. Ibn 'Abbas ؓ said: \"By it, the world and all that is in it would not please me.\""],[674,"Indeed, he heard Rifa'ah b. Rafi'—a man from the people of Badr—say: \"He said takbir in his prayer, and said: 'Allahu akbar, O Allah, to You belongs all praise, and to You belongs all sovereignty, and to You returns the whole affair. I ask You of all good, and I seek refuge in You from all evil.'\""],[675,"He heard a man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ called Rifa'ah b. Rafi' say: When he entered the prayer, he said the takbir."],[676,"I was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the mosque of al-Khayf, and two men came to him: an Ansari and a Thaqafi. Then he mentioned the hadith. He said: The Thaqafi said: Tell me, O Messenger of God, about what I have come to ask you. He ﷺ said: 'You have come to ask me about the prayer.' Then he mentioned the hadith. He ﷺ said: 'Then when you stand for prayer, recite what is easy of the Quran. Then when you bow, place your hands firmly on your knees and spread your fingers until you are at rest bowing. Then when you prostrate, place your face firmly in prostration until you are at rest prostrating. And pray at the beginning of the night and at its end.' He said: What do you think if I pray the entire night? He ﷺ said: 'Then indeed you will...'"],[677,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pause briefly before the recitation, asking God of His bounty."],[678,"The opening of prayer is purification, its prohibition is the takbir, and its release is the taslim."],[680,"When Bilal ؓ said: 'The prayer is established,' the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up."],[681,"Al-Hasan ؓ disliked saying the takbir until the mu'adhdhin had finished the iqamah."],[683,"Regarding a man who enters the mosque while the people are bowing: should he say the takbir? He said: No, not until you take your place in the row."],[684,"He entered while the Prophet ﷺ was bowing, so he bowed before reaching the row. They mentioned his action to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Hudhayfah did well and beautifully.'"],[685,"Everything has a best part, and the best part of prayer is the first takbir, so guard it."],[686,"When he began the prayer, he would say: 'O God, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan, from his madness, his poetry, and his pride.' It was said: What is his madness? He said: His madness is the seizure that afflicts the children of Adam, his poetry is verse, and his pride is arrogance."],[687,"I prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar ؓ, and they did not raise their hands except at the opening of prayer. And he said: They did not raise their hands after the first takbir."],[688,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ raise his hands when he began the prayer, when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing."],[689,"What I saw and forgot, I have not forgotten that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ, when he stood in prayer, stood like this, and he placed his right palm on his left forearm, adhering to the wrist."],[690,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ begin the prayer: he raised his hands until they passed beyond his ears."],[691,"Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad b. Mani' narrated to us with this."],[692,"Whatever I forget, I have not forgotten that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placing his right hand on his left hand, meaning in the prayer."],[693,"A man came while the Prophet ﷺ was in prayer. When he reached the row, he said: Allah is the greatest, a great (greatness); and praise be to Allah in abundance; and glory be to Allah morning and evening. When the Prophet ﷺ finished his prayer, he said: Who is the one who uttered these words? The man said: I, O Messenger of Allah, and I intended by them only good. He said: I saw the gates of heaven opened for them. Ibn 'Umar ؓ said: I have not abandoned them since I heard them."],[694,"A man stood behind the Prophet ﷺ while he was in prayer and said: Praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed in it. When the Prophet ﷺ finished his prayer, he said: Who is the one who spoke? A man from the group said: I. He ﷺ said: I saw twelve angels rushing to it, which of them would write it down?"],[696,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he missed a man... then he mentioned the hadith. He said: The man said: I passed by you, O Messenger of Allah, while you were praying Maghrib, so I prayed with you, and you were reciting this surah: Al-Qari'ah."],[697,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set for me to recite with 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' and its like from the Quran."],[698,"He used to recite in the four (rak'ahs) of Zuhr and 'Asr."],[699,"I said to 'Ikrimah: I sometimes recite in Maghrib: 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak' and 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind', and some people criticize me for that!? He said: Glory be to Allah! Recite with them, for they are from the Quran."],[700,"It was said to Ibn 'Umar ؓ, or a man said to him: I pray behind so-and-so, and he prolongs the prayer. He said: Two rak'ahs of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were lighter than one rak'ah of the prayer of so-and-so, or were like the prayer of so-and-so, or like one rak'ah of the prayer of so-and-so."],[701,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer with them, and recited to them the two shortest surahs of the Qur'an, or the most concise. He said: When he finished the prayer, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, or Mu'adh ؓ, said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, I saw you pray a prayer the like of which I have never seen you pray before.' He ﷺ said: 'Did you not hear the crying of the child behind me in the women's row? I wanted to free his mother for him.'"],[702,"He led us in prayer."],[703,"I came to Anas ؓ and said: 'Tell me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He led his household in prayer and prayed the noon and afternoon prayers with us, reciting in a low voice. He recited al-Mursalat, al-Nazi'at, 'Amma yatasa'alun, and similar surahs."],[704,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited in the sunset prayer: 'Ha Mim,' the surah in which the smoke is mentioned."],[705,"The Prophet ﷺ recited in the sunset prayer: 'At-Tin wa az-Zaytun' (The Fig and the Olive)."],[706,"Abd b. Humayd said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us with it."],[707,"A Jew passed by the people of a mosque while they were saying 'Amin.' The Jew said: 'By the One who taught you Amin, you are indeed upon the truth.'"],[708,"I was given three traits: prayer in rows, I was given the greeting of peace, which is the greeting of the people of Paradise, and I was given Amin, which no one before you was given, unless Allah, Blessed and Exalted, gave it to Aaron, for Moses ﷺ used to supplicate and Aaron ﷺ would say Amin."],[709,"She prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ and heard him saying: 'Maliki yawmi ad-din' (Master of the Day of Judgment). When he recited 'wa la ad-dallin' (nor of those who go astray), he said: 'Amin,' so loudly that she heard him while she was in the women's row."],[710,"Whoever catches the people in bowing: that rak'ah is not counted."],[711,"A man entered the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard the sound of his sandals. When he said the salutation, he said: 'How did you catch us?' He said: 'In prostration, so I prostrated.' He said: 'Do that, but do not count the prostration unless you catch the rak'ah. If you see the imam standing, then stand; if bowing, then bow; if prostrating, then prostrate; if sitting, then sit.'"],[712,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform qunut in the dawn prayer before the bowing, and he said: 'I only perform qunut with you so that you may supplicate your Lord and ask Him for your needs.'"],[713,"He stayed overnight with the Prophet ﷺ, and he performed qunut before the rak'ah. Then my mother was sent the following night, and she informed me of the same."],[714,"I stayed overnight with the Prophet ﷺ to see how he performs qunut in his witr. He performed qunut before bowing. Then I sent my mother, Umm 'Abd, saying: 'Stay overnight with his wives ﷺ and observe how he performs qunut in his witr.' She informed me that he ﷺ performed qunut before bowing."],[715,"The Prophet ﷺ did not perform qunut except for one month: he did not perform qunut before it, nor after it."],[716,"He ﷺ performed qunut for a month, supplicating against 'Usayyah and Dhakwan. When he ﷺ prevailed over them, he abandoned the qunut."],[717,"Qunut in the morning prayer was mentioned to Abu Mijlaz, and he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man to the tribe of so-and-so and said: \"Look, if they give permission, then pass them by to the tribe of so-and-so.\" When he came to them asking them, a man entered, donned his armor—meaning his weapon—then went out to the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and stabbed him, throwing him down. The messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Allah, I am the messenger of Your Messenger: convey my greetings to him.\" He said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \"And peace be upon you all.\" The people said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we did not see anyone!\" He ﷺ said: \"So-and-so was killed, and he sent me greetings.\" Then he stood with them for a month at the end of the dawn prayer, saying: \"O Allah, take the Banu 'Usayyah: they disobeyed their Lord, and take the Banu Dhakwan.\" He said: Then he abandoned it, and there was nothing besides that.'"],[718,"I said to Ibn 'Umar and Ibn 'Abbas ؓ: 'Does old age prevent you two from qunut?' They said: 'We did not take it from our companions.'"],[720,"We, the company of prophets, have been commanded to hasten our breaking of the fast, to delay our pre-dawn meal, and to place our right hands over our left hands in prayer."],[721,"We, the company of prophets, have been commanded to delay our pre-dawn meal and to hold our hands over our left hands in prayer."],[722,"My grandfather narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from 'Amr b. al-Harith, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas ؓ, mentioning it. He erred in his saying 'from 'Amr b. al-Harith'—it is actually Talhah b. 'Amr. And Ahmad b. Tahir: al-Daraqutni and others declared him a liar. Al-Tabarani narrated it in al-Awsat from Ahmad b. Tahir."],[723,"Allah, the Exalted, continues to turn toward the servant in his prayer as long as he does not turn away. That was the man who..."],[724,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man moving pebbles while he was in prayer. When he finished, he said to the man: 'That is your share of your prayer.'"],[725,"The Prophet ﷺ would sometimes touch his beard during the prayer."],[726,"He would touch his head and his beard during the prayer."],[727,"Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Layth b. Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas ؓ with this, and he did not mention his beard."],[728,"When one of you finds a sound or something in his stomach while he is in prayer, he should place his hand over his nose and leave."],[730,"While the Prophet ﷺ was praying Asr during the Battle of Badr, he smiled during the prayer. When he completed the prayer, they said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you smiled while you were in prayer?!' He ﷺ said, 'Indeed, Mikail (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by me while returning from pursuing the people, and there was dust on his wing. He smiled at me, so I smiled back at him.'"],[731,"And Abu Ya'la said: 'Amr b. Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, 'Ali b. Thabit narrated to us similarly."],[732,"When you are engaged in a matter of this world, proceed with it, and when you are engaged in a matter of the Hereafter, take your time as much as you can. If you intend to do good, do not delay it. If Satan comes to you while you are praying and says, 'You are showing off,' then prolong it."],[734,"A man came to Abdullah and said, 'So-and-so recites while bowing.' He said, 'Indeed, men recite the Quran but it does not go beyond their throats. When it becomes firmly rooted in the heart, then it has effect.'"],[735,"He prohibited a man from reciting the Quran while bowing or prostrating."],[737,"I prayed next to Abu Hurayrah ؓ and I stood on the tips of my toes and knees, so he struck my thigh until I settled down."],[739,"I saw Wahb b. Kaysan prostrating on the hairline. He said: I asked him about that, and he said..."],[740,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating on the top of his forehead, at the hairline."],[741,"He used to prostrate on his forehead, at the hairline."],[742,"The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complained to him about leaning on the hands in prostration, and he permitted them to support themselves on their knees with their elbows."],[743,"Abdullah b. Mas'ud ؓ commanded us, when we prostrated, to place our elbows and forearms on the ground. I mentioned that to Tawus, and he said: \"That is a lie.\""],[745,"Indeed Allah, Exalted is He, does not look at the prayer of a servant who does not raise his lower garment above his heels, and who touches the ground with his palms."],[746,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man who did not complete his bowing or his prostration. He said: \"If this man were to die in the state he is in, he would die upon other than the religion of Muhammad ﷺ.\" As for bowing along with prostration, the likeness of one who prays but does not complete his bowing or prostration is that of a hungry man who eats only one or two dates, which do not satisfy him at all."],[747,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man: \"When you bow, place your hands on your knees and spread your fingers apart.\""],[748,"I heard Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ delivering a sermon, saying: \"O people, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ built this mosque while we were with him, the Muhajirun and the Ansar. When it becomes very crowded, a man among you may prostrate on the back of his brother.\" He saw people praying in the road and said to them: \"Pray in the mosque.\""],[749,"On the back of his brother."],[750,"When he prostrated, the whiteness of his armpits would be seen."],[751,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a rainy day, and when he prostrated he would protect himself with a cloak on which there was mud."],[752,"He saw a man prostrating without bowing, and said: \"You have lied; there is no prostration except with bowing.\""],[753,"We used to supplicate while standing and sitting, and we used to glorify while bowing and prostrating."],[754,"Al-Hasan ؓ led us in one of the two evening prayers and lengthened it. I saw his beard quivering. When he finished, I said to him: 'Were you reciting?' He said: 'Most of it was glorification and supplication.'"],[755,"It was my night with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he slipped away. I thought he had gone to one of his other wives, so I went out feeling jealous. Then I found him ﷺ prostrating like a garment thrown on the ground. I heard him saying: 'My physical form and my inner self have prostrated to You, and my heart has believed in You. This is my hand and what I have committed against myself. O Great One, from whom every great thing is hoped, forgive the great sin.' Then he ﷺ raised his head and said: 'What brought you out?' I said: 'I had a thought.' He ﷺ said: 'Some thoughts are sinful. Seek forgiveness from God Almighty. Gabriel ﷺ came to me and ordered me to say these words that you heard. Say them in your prostration, for whoever says them will not raise his head before he is forgiven.'"],[756,"When a servant prostrates, he prostrates on seven parts: his face, his two palms, his two knees, and his two feet. Whatever he does not do, he has fallen short."],[757,"Abd b. Humayd said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us with this."],[758,"I say: Muhammad b. Umar is al-Waqidi: very weak, but he is not alone in narrating it. Abu Ya'la said: Musa b. Muhammad b. Hayyan narrated to us, Muhammad b. Abi al-Wazir Abu al-Mutarraf narrated to us, from Abdullah b. Ja'far: something similar. Abdullah b. Ja'far alone narrated it - and he is the father of Ali b. al-Madini - and he is weak, and he erred in its chain. Rather, Amir b. Sa'd narrated it from al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib ؓ . This is how Muslim and the authors of the Sunan reported it."],[760,"He would say the takbir when he bowed and when he lowered himself."],[761,"The first person to reduce the takbir was al-Walid b. Uqbah, so Abdullah said: 'They reduced it, may God reduce them. I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ say the takbir every time he bowed, every time he prostrated, and every time he raised his head.'"],[763,"She did not see any harm in a man moving his ring to another finger to keep it safe during prayer."],[764,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was praying in my house, and Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ came and stood beside him on his right. A scorpion approached the Prophet ﷺ, but when it drew near to him, it was turned away. Then it approached Ali, so he took a sandal and killed it while he was praying. When he finished his prayer, he said ؓ: 'May God fight it! It approached the Prophet ﷺ and was turned away from him, then it came toward me.' The Messenger of God ﷺ did not see any harm in killing it during prayer."],[765,"Al-Husayn ؓ came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was prostrating and climbed onto his back. He ﷺ took him by the hand and stood up while he was on his back, then he bowed, then he let him go, and he ؓ left."],[767,"Your raising of hands in prayer is an innovation. By God, the Messenger of God ﷺ did not do more than this - meaning with his finger."],[768,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying. He (the narrator) said: He raised his head from bowing and raised his palms until they were level with or reached the tops of his ears, as if they were two fans."],[770,"I met al-Aswad and said to him: Abu al-Ahwas narrates from Abd Allah—regarding the tashahhud—the blessed words. He said: Go to him and forbid him from this, and tell him: Abd Allah taught Alqamah the tashahhud and counted them on his hand."],[771,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud as a teacher teaches children writing."],[772,"On the pulpit."],[773,"Abu Bakr ؓ used to teach us the tashahhud on the pulpit, as children are taught in school."],[774,"I was given the openings of speech, its comprehensive words, and its conclusions. We said: Teach us from what Allah Almighty taught you. So he taught us the tashahhud."],[775,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a dream, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, the tashahhud has been reported to us differently! So-and-so said such-and-such, and so-and-so said such-and-such, and Ibn Masud ؓ said such-and-such. The Prophet ﷺ said: How excellent is the tashahhud of Ibn Masud."],[776,"He did not add anything in the two rak'ahs beyond the tashahhud."],[778,"I entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying, placing his right hand on his right thigh and pointing with his index finger, saying: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion."],[780,"The opening of prayer is purification, its prohibition is the takbir, and its release is the taslim."],[781,"The Prophet ﷺ gave one taslim to his right side."],[782,"He gave one taslim facing the qiblah."],[783,"I saw Qabisa b. Dhu'ayb: when he performed the taslim, he would give one salam facing the qibla. Al-Zuhri said: I mentioned that to 'Abd Allah b. Mawhab, and he said: I asked Qabisa about that, and he said: I saw Zayd b. Thabit give one salam facing the qibla."],[784,"I prayed behind 'Umar, behind 'Ali, and behind Abu Dharr ؓ, and I saw all of them give salam to his right and to his left."],[785,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ give salam to his right and to his left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.'"],[786,"He gave salam to his right and to his left, then he stood up."],[787,"He would give salam to his right and to his left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,' until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."],[788,"'Ammar ؓ was our commander for a year, and he did not lead us in any prayer except that he gave salam to his right and to his left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.'"],[790,"I heard Ibn 'Umar ؓ say at the end of the prayer: 'O Allah, You are Peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.' Then I prayed beside 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr ؓ and heard him say them, so I said to him: 'I heard Ibn 'Umar ؓ say the same as you say!' 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr ؓ said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say them at the end of his prayer.'"],[791,"A man prayed beside 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar ؓ, and when he finished his prayer, he sat supplicating... and he mentioned it. He said: Then he prayed beside 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr ؓ and said the same. The man said to him: 'This is a supplication I heard from your brother 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar ؓ.'"],[792,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pointing with his finger during the prayer, and when he gave salam, I heard him say: 'O Allah, I ask You for all good, what I know of it and what I do not know, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, what I know of it and what I do not know.'"],[793,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave salam from the prayer, he would say: 'Glory be to your Lord, the Lord of Might, above what they describe.'"],[794,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more than once say at the end of his prayer, when he was about to leave."],[795,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say at the end of every prayer - I do not know whether after the taslim or before the taslim."],[796,"And al-Harith said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, or al-Ashja'i, from Sufyan, with it."],[797,"And Abu Ya'la said: Ishaq—he is Ibn Abi Isra'il—narrated to us, Hammad—he is Ibn Zayd—narrated to us, from Abu Harun, and he mentioned it similar to the hadith of Ali ibn Asim. Abu Harun alone narrated it, and he is weak."],[798,"She came with a small skin of ghee to the Messenger of God ﷺ ... and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then he taught her to say after every prayer ten times: 'Glory be to God' ten times, 'Praise be to God' ten times, and 'God is greatest' ten times."],[799,"Whoever seeks forgiveness from God Almighty after every prayer three times, saying: 'I seek forgiveness from God, besides whom there is no god, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer, and I turn to Him in repentance,' his sins will be forgiven, even if he fled from the battlefield."],[800,"Anas ibn Malik ؓ prayed in the mosque of Banu Rifa'ah over here, and he ordered a man from his companions to give the call to prayer, and he led them in the dawn prayer. When he finished his prayer, he turned to the people and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he prayed with his companions, would turn to the people and say: 'O God, I seek refuge with You from a deed that disgraces me. O God, I seek refuge with You from wealth that makes me arrogant. O God, I seek refuge with You from a companion who destroys me. O God, I seek refuge with You from a hope that distracts me. O God, I seek refuge with You from poverty that makes me forget.'"],[801,"We do not know anyone who narrated it from Anas except al-Ja'd, nor from him except Abu 'Imran, nor did anyone relate it except Bakr, and he is not strong. Thus he said, and 'Uqbah followed him as you see."],[802,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say after the two rak'ahs of dawn: 'O God, Lord of Gabriel.'"],[803,"The poor among the Muslims complained about the superiority the rich had over them. They said: O Messenger of God, these are our brothers: they believed as we believed, prayed as we prayed, fasted as we fasted, but they have an advantage over us in wealth: they give charity and maintain family ties, while we are poor and cannot do that. He ﷺ said: Shall I not tell you something that, if you do it, you will catch up with their virtue? Say after every prayer: 'God is greatest' eleven times, 'Praise be to God' eleven times, 'Glory be to God' eleven times, and 'There is no god but God alone, no partner with Him' eleven times: you will attain the like of their virtue. The rich heard of that and said the same as the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded them. They came to him and said: O Messenger of God, our brothers say the same as we say. He ﷺ said: That is the grace of God, which He gives to whom He wills. Shall I give you glad tidings, O company of the poor? The poor believers will enter Paradise before their rich ones by half a day, which is five hundred years."],[804,"We do not know it except from this route, and its defect is Musa ibn 'Ubaydah. Ibn Majah included part of it in the book of asceticism."],[805,"Three things: whoever comes with them with faith will enter from whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes and will be married to as many of the wide-eyed houris as he wishes: whoever pardons his killer, pays a hidden debt, and recites after every obligatory prayer: 'Say: He is God, the One.' Abu Bakr ؓ said: Or one of them, O Messenger of God? He ﷺ said: Or one of them."],[806,"Al-Hasan ibn Ali ؓ married a woman from among us and settled among us. A man from the tribe made food and invited the tribe and invited al-Hasan ؓ. He said: I did not see al-Hasan ؓ accept his invitation. He said: I saw al-Hasan ؓ gesture to a servant of his. When al-Hasan ؓ stood and left, I came to ask his servant about what delayed him from the invitation and what he was gesturing about. He said: I met al-Hasan ؓ and greeted him, and he returned my greeting and welcomed me, saying: What brings you, O so-and-so? Do you have a need? I said: O son of the Messenger of God, I came to ask your servant about what delayed you from the invitation and what you were gesturing about. Al-Hasan ؓ said: I will tell you that. As for what delayed me from it, I was fasting. As for what I was gesturing about, I was asking him: Has the sun risen or not? Then al-Hasan ؓ narrated, saying: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever prays the dawn prayer then sits remembering God Almighty until the sun rises, it will be for him a screen or a veil from the Fire."],[807,"That I pray the dawn prayer and then sit in my place remembering God Almighty until the sun rises is more beloved to me than charging on excellent horses in the path of God Almighty from the time I pray the dawn prayer until it rises."],[809,"We came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I saw him turning away to his right and to his left."],[810,"His uncle Wāsiʿ b. Ḥabbān was standing praying in the mosque while Ibn ʿUmar ؓ was leaning his back against the qiblah wall of the mosque. When Wāsiʿ finished, he turned to his left toward Ibn ʿUmar ؓ and sat with him. Ibn ʿUmar ؓ said to him: 'What prevents you from turning to your right?' He said: 'I saw you, so I turned toward you.' Ibn ʿUmar ؓ said: 'You have done well. Some people say: When you are praying and you finish, turn to your right.' Ibn ʿUmar ؓ said: 'When you are praying and you finish, turn to your right if you wish, or to your left if you wish.'"],[811,"About a surah whose end contains a prostration, he used to say: 'Recite and prostrate, then stand and recite and bow. If you wish, bow in [the surahs] al-Aʿrāf, al-Najm, Iqraʾ bi-smi Rabbik, and the like of them.'"],[812,"One of them prostrated in [the recitation of] 'When the sky is split asunder' or in 'Iqraʾ bi-smi Rabbik,' while the other did not prostrate. The one who prostrated was better than the one who did not prostrate. If it was not ʿUmar ؓ, then he [the one who prostrated] is better than ʿUmar ؓ."],[813,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ recited [Sūrat] al-Najm and prostrated, then stood and recited another surah."],[814,"The prostration [of recitation] is only upon the one who sits for it [i.e., who attends the recitation]."],[815,"The Prophet ﷺ prostrated in [the recitation of] 'When the sky is split asunder' ten times."],[816,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū Bakr narrated to us… and he mentioned it. : :"],[817,"There is no prostration in the Mufaṣṣal [surahs]."],[818,"Ḥammād narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, the like of it :"],[819,"Khuzaymah saw in a dream that he prostrated on the forehead of the Prophet ﷺ, so he [the Prophet] lay down for him ﷺ and said: 'Fulfill your vision,' and he prostrated on his forehead."],[820,"I saw in a dream as if I were under a tree, and as if the tree were reciting [Sūrat] Ṣād. When it reached the prostration, it prostrated and said in its prostration: 'O God, forgive me thereby a sin; O God, remove from me thereby a burden; grant me thereby gratitude; and accept it from me as You accepted from Your servant David his prostration.' So I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him. He said: 'Did you prostrate, O Abū Saʿīd?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'You are more deserving of prostration than the tree.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ recited Sūrat Ṣād, and when he came to the prostration, he said in his prostration what the tree had said in its prostration."],[822,"Whoever is able to prostrate, let him prostrate. Whoever is not able, let him not raise anything to his face. Let his prostration be bowing, and let his bowing be to gesture with his head."],[823,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a sick person while I was with him. He saw him praying and prostrating on a cushion, so he forbade him and said: 'If you are able to prostrate on the ground, prostrate; otherwise gesture, and make the prostration lower than the bowing.'"],[824,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed on the ground in the obligatory prayer while seated, and in the glorification prayer he sat on the ground and gestured."],[826,"When one of you intends a matter, let him say: 'O Allah, I seek Your guidance by Your knowledge, and I seek Your power by Your might, and I ask You of Your immense bounty. For You have power and I have none, and You know and I do not, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if this matter—whatever it is that I intend—is good for me in my religion, my livelihood, and my ultimate end, then decree it for me and facilitate it for me and bless me in it. But if it is bad for me in my religion, my livelihood, and my ultimate end, then turn it away from me and turn me away from it, and decree for me good wherever it may be, and make me content with it.' There is no might nor power except with Allah, the Most High, the Most Great."],[827,"691 558 / 2 - Ibn Hibban said: Abu Khalifah narrated to us, 'Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Ya'qub narrated to us with it."],[829,"If you are able not to pray any prayer except that you prostrate after it two prostrations, then do so."],[831,"Glorification (saying subhan Allah) is for men, and clapping is for women."],[832,"'Abidah ibn Humayd narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ؓ something similar."],[833,"I used to ask permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ. If he was in prayer, he would say subhan Allah, and if he was not in prayer, he would permit me."],[835,"Whoever walks in the darkness of the night to the mosque will meet Allah Almighty with light on the Day of Resurrection."],[836,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a sermon and mentioned a long hadith, in which he said: 'Whoever walks to any mosque, for every step he takes he gets ten good deeds, ten evil deeds are erased from him, and he is raised by ten degrees.'"],[837,"There is no Muslim who performs ablution and does it well, then walks to one of the houses of Allah to pray an obligatory prayer in it, except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, writes for him a good deed for every step."],[838,"The prayer was established, so the Messenger of God ﷺ went out to the mosque walking, and I was with him, taking short steps. He said: 'I only did this so that the number of our steps in seeking the prayer would increase.'"],[839,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. I say: al-Dahhak has weak memory, and what is preserved in this matter is mawquf from Zayd b. Thabit ؓ ."],[840,"I went out intending to go to the mosque, and there was Zayd b. Thabit ؓ , so he placed his hand on my shoulder, leaning on me. He said: I kept taking long strides, out of youthfulness, so Zayd ؓ said to me: 'Shorten your stride, for the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever walks to the mosque will have ten good deeds for every step.\"'"],[841,"Your walking to the mosque and your returning to your family are equal in reward."],[842,"There is no man who performs ablution, then comes to one of the mosques and takes a step, except that God, Mighty and Majestic, writes for him a good deed, erases by it a sin, and raises him by it a degree."],[845,"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, God Almighty will forbid his flesh from the Fire. He said: I have not left them since."],[846,"I came to Abu al-Darda' ؓ during the illness in which he died, and he said: 'O son of my brother, what brought you to these lands, and what concerned you about them?' I said: 'Nothing concerned me except maintaining the connection between you and my father.' Abu al-Darda' ؓ said: 'What a bad time for a lie this is. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever performs ablution, then stands and prays two rak'ahs or four rak'ahs, obligatory or non-obligatory, performing bowing and prostration completely in them, then asks God for forgiveness, except that He will forgive him.\"'"],[847,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: 'Do you have a need?' until one day he said: 'O Messenger of God, my need.' He ﷺ said: 'What is your need?' He said: 'My need is that you intercede for me on the Day of Resurrection.' He ﷺ said: 'Who guided you to this?' He said: 'My Lord.' He ﷺ said: 'Then help me by performing many prostrations.'"],[848,"Whoever harms a friend of Mine has declared war on Me. My servant does not draw near to Me with anything I love more than performing what I have made obligatory upon him. And My servant continues to draw near to Me with supererogatory deeds until I love him. When I love him, I am his leg with which he walks, his hand with which he strikes, his tongue with which he speaks, and his heart with which he reasons. If he asks Me, I will give him, and if he seeks My refuge, I will grant him refuge. I have never hesitated about anything I am going to do as I hesitate about taking his soul, because he hates it and I hate to displease him."],[850,"Abdullah ؓ held that it is the morning prayer – meaning the middle prayer."],[852,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ performed the night prayer, he prostrated between every two rak'ahs."],[853,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to use the tooth-stick during the night two or three times. When he stood up at night, he would pray four rak'ahs without speaking anything, without commanding anything, and he would say the taslim after every two rak'ahs."],[854,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night to pray as he prayed. He began the prayer and recited a recitation that was neither light nor loud: a beautiful recitation, in which he recited distinctly and made us hear. He said: Then he bowed for about the length of a surah. Then he raised his head and said: 'Allah hears the one who praises Him: Possessor of might, dominion, pride, and greatness.' He said: Then his standing was about the length of a surah. He said: And he prostrated for about that long until he finished the lengthy recitation, while the darkness of night was still upon him."],[855,"They mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a freedwoman of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, and they said: 'She stands in prayer at night and fasts during the day.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'But I sleep and pray, and I fast and break my fast.'"],[856,"Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ja'dah, who said: It was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ... and he mentioned it."],[857,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the night prayer, and his eyes overflowed until his tears streamed down, and he said: 'Their sides forsake their beds.'"],[858,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided Surah al-Baqarah into two rak'ahs."],[859,"I saw 'Uthman ؓ at the Maqam one night, having completed the recitation of the Quran in a single rak'ah, then he departed."],[860,"He used to perform witr at the time of the adhan."],[861,"The first adhan:"],[862,"I said to 'A'ishah ؓ: 'There are people among us who recite the Quran two or three times in a night.' She said: 'Those are people who recited but did not recite. I saw myself standing with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the entire night, and he would not pass by a verse of hope except that he asked his Lord and supplicated, nor a verse of fear except that he supplicated to his Lord and sought refuge.'"],[863,"He would stand for the entire night reciting al-Baqarah, Al 'Imran, al-Nisa', and the rest similar to that."],[864,"I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after the night prayer, and I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, permit me to worship as you worship.'... He mentioned the hadith and said: He faced the qiblah and placed me on his right. Then he recited the Opening of the Book, then he began Surah al-Baqarah, not passing by a verse of mercy except that he asked, nor a verse of fear except that he sought refuge, nor a parable except that he reflected, until he completed it. Then he said the takbir, and I heard him say in his bowing: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Almighty,' until I thought he was saying: 'and with His praise.' He remained in his bowing for nearly as long as his standing. Then he raised his head, said the takbir, and prostrated, and I heard him say in his prostration: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.' And I think he was saying: 'and with His praise.' He remained in his prostration for nearly as long as his bowing. Then he rose until he finished his two prostrations, and he recited the Opening of the Book, then he began Al 'Imran in the same way. Then I heard the call to dawn. Hudhayfah ؓ said: 'I have never performed a worship more difficult for me than that.'"],[865,"When a man prays during the night and wakes his wife, and they pray two rak'ahs, they are recorded among the men who remember Allah much and the women who remember."],[866,"I mentioned the night prayer, and some of them said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Half of it, a quarter of it, or the interval between two milkings of a camel.\""],[867,"When one of you goes to sleep while intending to pray during the night, let him place a handful of dirt near him. Then when he wakes, let him take a handful with his right hand and throw it to his left."],[868,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to pray during the night, whether little or much, and to make that an odd number."],[869,"Counting the verses (for the number of prostrations or length) applies to voluntary prayers, not the obligatory."],[870,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to use the toothstick at night two or three times. Whenever he slept and woke, he would use the toothstick, perform ablution, and pray two rak'ahs or a few rak'ahs."],[871,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from raising his voice in recitation before the 'atamah (nightfall) prayer and after it, as it would confuse his companions in their prayer."],[872,"Abu Bakr said: Malik b. Isma'il narrated to us, Khalid b. 'Abdullah narrated to us, with this."],[873,"He would confuse his companions while the people were praying."],[874,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in prayer until his feet or his legs became swollen. It was said to him: \"Has not Allah forgiven you your past and future sins?\" He ﷺ replied: \"Should I not be a grateful servant?\""],[875,"Al-Bazzar said: Al-Hasan b. Muhammad al-Umawi narrated to us, Muhammad b. Bishr narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us with it. I say: It is defective, and the well-known version is from Ziyad b. 'Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah ؓ."],[876,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt some pain. When morning came, it was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the traces of pain are evident on you!\" He ﷺ said: \"Despite what you see, last night I recited the seven long surahs.\""],[877,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his gaze to the sky, then lowered it. We said, “O Messenger of Allah, why did you do that?” He said, “I was amazed at two angels who descended to the earth seeking a servant in his prayer place, but they did not find him. Then they ascended to their Lord and said, ‘Our Lord, we used to record for Your believing servant such-and-such deeds in his day and night, but we found that You had detained him in Your snare, so we did not record anything for him.’ So He, Blessed and Exalted, said, ‘Record for My servant his deeds of his day and night, and do not diminish anything from them. Upon Me is his reward, for I detained him, and he shall have the reward of what he used to do.’”"],[878,"Whoever among you becomes drowsy in the mosque, let him move to his bed, so that he may know what he is saying."],[880,"Umar ؓ faced the people after the night prayer and said, “What remains of the night is better than what has passed of it.”"],[881,"He used to pray twenty rak‘ahs in Ramadan plus the witr."],[882,"And ‘Abd b. Humayd said: Abu Nu‘aym narrated to us, Abu Shaybah—that is Ibrahim—narrated to us with this."],[884,"Pray in your homes, and do not make them graves, and do not take my house as a place of festivity. Send prayers upon me and greet me, for your prayers and greetings reach me wherever you are."],[885,"They asked Umar ؓ about praying in the mosque, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The obligatory prayer is in the mosque, and the voluntary prayer is in the home.”"],[887,"I arrived with al-Zuhri in Syria from the Battle of Yarmuk, and I saw him praying on his mount whichever direction it faced."],[889,"Ziyad came to Anas ؓ and said to him, “Recite.” So he recited and raised his voice, and Anas ؓ lifted the cloth from his face upward and said, “Is this what you do?!”"],[890,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us on a night of Ramadan—while the people were praying—and said, “Let not some of you raise their voices over others, for that harms the one praying.”"],[892,"The most beloved of deeds to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was that which a servant persists in, even if it is little."],[893,"A young man devoted himself to worship during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, so his father went to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “My son has exhausted himself in worship.” He ﷺ said, “Command him to be moderate with himself.”"],[894,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ learned that a man in the mosque was prolonging the prayer, so he came to him, then took hold of his shoulder and said ﷺ: “Indeed Allah, Most High, is pleased with ease for this community and dislikes hardship for it,” he said this three times, “and this man has adopted hardship and abandoned ease.” Then he pulled him away forcefully, and after that he was not seen (doing that)."],[895,"The wife of 'Uthman b. Maz'un ؓ came to the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, and they saw that she was in a bad state, so they said to her: “There is no man in Quraysh richer than your husband!” She said: “We get nothing from him. As for his day, he fasts; as for his night, he stands in prayer.” He said: Then the Prophet ﷺ entered, and they mentioned that to him. He said: Then the Prophet ﷺ met him and said: “O 'Uthman, is there not for you an example in me?” He said: “And what is that, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ? May my father and mother be your ransom.” He ﷺ said: “As for you, you fast during the day and stand in prayer at night, but your family has a right over you, and your body has a right over you. So pray and sleep, and break the fast and fast.” He said: Then the woman came to them after that perfumed as if she were a bride, and they said to her: “What happened?” She said: “What happened to people has happened to us.”"],[896,"When one of you stands at night and the Qur'an becomes difficult for him, let him sleep."],[898,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached Badr the next morning, he spent that entire night in worship, while he was traveling."],[900,"Ibn 'Abbas ؓ said: “O Abu Yahya, did you not see that I slept last night and missed the Witr! Ibn Makhramah came to me and another with him, and they occupied me from the Witr, so I slept until morning. Then a slave girl woke me, and I said to her: 'See if the sun has risen.' She said: 'No.' So I prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr, then I said: 'See if the sun has risen.' She said: 'No.' So I prayed the Fajr prayer.”"],[901,"You must observe the two rak'ahs of Fajr, for in them are great merits."],[902,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited quietly in the two rak'ahs before Fajr, and he used to recite in them: “Say, O disbelievers” and “Say, He is Allah, the One.”"],[903,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to stand in them for as long as it takes to recite the Opening of the Book."],[904,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the two rak'ahs of Fajr: in the first rak'ah, “The Messenger has believed” until he completed it, and in the second, from Al 'Imran: “Say, O People of the Scripture, come to a word that is equitable between us and you,” the verse."],[905,"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day..."],[906,"Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr, it is like the reward of freeing a slave from the descendants of Isma'il."],[907,"Ibn Abi 'Umar said: Waki' narrated to us: Bashir b. Salman – he is Abu Isma'il – narrated to us from al-Qasim b. Safwan al-Ansari, from his father ؓ, something similar."],[908,"They did not persist in any voluntary prayer as they persisted in a prayer before Zuhr."],[909,"He used to pray four (rak’ahs) before Zuhr."],[910,"761 618 / 2 - And Abu Ya’la said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Bakr narrated to us with this. :"],[911,"I saw ‘Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ when the sun declined pray four long (rak’ahs). I asked him, and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying them, and I asked him, and he said: “The gates of heaven are opened when the sun declines, and they are not closed until Zuhr is prayed. So I love that a deed be raised for me to Allah, Mighty and Majestic.”"],[912,"Whoever consistently prays four rak’ahs before ‘Asr, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."],[913,"I invited a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ to my home. When the mu’adhdhin called the Maghrib adhan, he prayed, and I asked about that, and he said: Ubayy b. Ka’b ؓ used to pray them."],[914,"I bear witness concerning five of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, among those who gave allegiance under the tree, that they used to pray two rak’ahs before Maghrib."],[915,"Abu Bakr, ‘Umar, and ‘Uthman did not pray the two rak’ahs before Maghrib."],[916,"‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf ؓ used to pray two rak’ahs in his house after Maghrib."],[917,"He was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ command prayer after the obligatory? He said: Between Maghrib and ‘Isha."],[918,"Whoever prays two rak’ahs after the two rak’ahs of Maghrib, reciting in each rak’ah the Opening of the Book and “Say: He is Allah, One” fifteen times, will come on the Day of Resurrection and it will be said to him: “This one is of the truthful.” Then he will pass them. Then it will be said: “This one is of the martyrs.” Then he will pass them. Then it will be said: “This one is of the prophets.” Then he will pass them. Then it will be said: “This one is of the angels.” Then he will pass them, and he will not be veiled until he reaches the Throne of the Most Merciful."],[919,"It used to be said: The Witr is upon the people of the Qur’an. I said: What do you command your daughter? He said: I command her to pray two rak’ahs after ‘Isha, and she was a girl of five or six years."],[920,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying between Maghrib and Isha, and he continued praying until he prayed Isha."],[922,"Ali ؓ came out to us when the muezzin called the adhan and said: Your Prophet ﷺ commanded the witr and set this hour for it. Give the adhan, O Ibn al-Nabbah."],[923,"I entered upon Jabir b. Abdullah ؓ in Makkah and found him praying sitting down, and he mentioned the hadith: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: No man prays the Isha prayer in congregation, then prays after it as much as he wishes, then prays witr before sleeping, except that on that night he is as if he encountered Laylat al-Qadr."],[924,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, morning came upon me and I had not prayed witr. He ﷺ said: Witr is only at night. He said that three times, then said the third time: Go and pray witr."],[925,"The clever ones are those who pray witr at the beginning of the night, and the strong ones are those who pray witr at the end of the night."],[926,"I was commanded to pray witr and to offer the sacrifice, and it was not made obligatory."],[927,"She saw Aisha ؓ praying behind the Maqam, and she prayed witr with one rak'ah in which she recited Surah Ibrahim."],[928,"When you hear the scream, then pray witr with one rak'ah."],[929,"He used to pray witr with three rak'ahs, reciting in the first with Sabbih, in the second with Qul ya ayyuha al-kafirun, and in the third with Qul huwa Allahu ahad."],[930,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the witr in the first rak'ah: Sabbih isma rabbika al-a'la, in the second: Qul ya ayyuha al-kafirun, and in the third: Qul huwa Allahu ahad."],[931,"I said to Miqsam: I pray witr with three, then the adhan is called, then I go out. He said: It is not proper except with five or seven. Al-Hakam said: I told Mujahid and Yahya b. al-Jazzar about it, and they said: Ask him from whom this is. He said: From the trustworthy ones, Aisha and Maymunah."],[932,"And Abu Bakr said: Ghandar narrated to us, from Shu'bah likewise, and he did not mention his revisiting Mujahid and Yahya."],[933,"I said to Miqsam: 'I perform witr with three [rak'ahs], then I go out to the prayer.' He said: 'There is no witr except with seven or five.' Then I met Mujahid and Yahya b. al-Jazzar and mentioned that to them. They said: 'Ask him: from whom?' He said: 'From the trustworthy one, from the trustworthy one, from 'A'ishah and Maymunah, from the Prophet ﷺ.'"],[934,"And Muhammad b. Ja'far informed us: Shu'bah narrated to us with this chain of transmission, the like of it:"],[935,"Abu Musa ؓ, when he led us in the morning prayer, would make us recite. Then 'Ali ؓ came, and a man beside me asked him about witr. He said: 'Three is more beloved to me than one, and five is more beloved to me than three, and seven is more beloved to me than five.'"],[936,"A man's voluntary prayer where no one sees him is equal to twenty-five times his prayer in the sight of the people."],[937,"The Prophet ﷺ performed witr on his donkey, while he was heading toward Khaybar."],[938,"I spent the night with the Prophet ﷺ to observe how he performed qunut in his witr. He performed qunut before the ruku'. Then I sent my mother, Umm 'Abd ؓ, and said to her: 'Stay overnight with his wives ﷺ and observe how he performs qunut in his witr.' She came to me and informed me that he ﷺ performed qunut before the ruku'."],[940,"He used to pray the duha prayer, and he said: 'Whoever prays it, a house will be built for him in Paradise, and his sins during the hours of the day will be forgiven.'"],[941,"I saw 'Abd Allah b. Abi Awfa ؓ pray two rak'ahs. His wife said to him: 'You only prayed two rak'ahs!' He said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray the duha prayer as two rak'ahs when he was given the good news of the conquest and of the head of Abu Jahl.'"],[942,"There is no person who comes to an open space of land and prays the duha prayer as two rak'ahs, then says: 'O Allah, to You belongs praise. I have become Your servant upon Your covenant and Your promise. You created me and I was nothing. I ask Your forgiveness for my sin, for my sins have indeed burdened me and surrounded me, unless You forgive them for me. So forgive them, O Most Merciful of the merciful,' except that Allah forgives his sin in that sitting place, even if it were like the foam of the sea."],[943,"Whoever prays the fajr prayer, then sits until the sun rises, then prays two rak'ahs, Allah forbids the Fire to consume him or scorch him."],[944,"Abu Dharr ؓ sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat with him, and he said: 'O Abu Dharr, have you prayed the duha?' He said: 'No.' He ﷺ said: 'Get up and pray the duha.' He said: So he prayed, then he came back."],[945,"And al-Harith said: Yunus b. Muhammad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Ma'bad b. Hilal al-'Anbari: A man narrated to me in the mosque of Damascus, from 'Awf b. Malik, something similar. :"],[946,"\"O Abu Dharr.\" I said: \"At your service, and at your pleasure.\" He said: \"Have you prayed any rak'ahs today?\" I said: \"No.\" He ﷺ said: \"Get up and pray.\" So I got up and prayed as much as Allah, the Exalted, willed. Then I returned and sat down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent for a long time, not speaking to me. I said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has disliked my company.\" Then he ﷺ turned to me and said: \"O Abu Dharr.\" I said: \"At your service, and at your pleasure.\" He ﷺ said: \"Seek refuge in Allah from the evil of the devils among mankind and jinn.\" I said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom, do humans have devils?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Does not Allah, Mighty and Majestic, say: 'Devils among mankind and jinn, inspiring one another'—the verse.\" Then he ﷺ turned to me and said: \"O Abu Dharr.\" I said: \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah.\" He ﷺ said: \"Shall I not teach you a word that is a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?\" I said: \"Yes, may my father and mother be your ransom.\" He ﷺ said: \"Say: 'There is no might and no power except with Allah.'\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent and did not speak until that lasted a long time. So I began the conversation and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you commanded me to pray. What is prayer?\" He ﷺ said: \"A good thing established; whoever wishes may do little, and whoever wishes may do much.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is fasting?\" He ﷺ said: \"An obligatory duty that suffices.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is charity?\" He ﷺ said: \"Multiplied many times over, and with Allah is more.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best?\" He ﷺ said: \"Faith in Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and striving in the path of Allah, the Exalted.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which martyrs are best?\" He ﷺ said: \"The one whose blood is shed and his horse is hamstrung.\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which slaves are best [to free]?\" He ﷺ said: \"The most expensive in price and the most precious to their owners.\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best?\" He ﷺ said: \"Effort from one of little means, and a secret given to the poor.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what if I find nothing to give in charity?\" He ﷺ said: \"You help a weak person or make something for someone unskilled.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what if I cannot?\" He ﷺ said: \"Then refrain from this,\" and he ﷺ pointed to his tongue, \"for it is a good charity that a person gives on behalf of himself.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which verse of the Qur'an revealed to you is greatest?\" He ﷺ said: \"The Verse of the Throne. And do you know what the likeness of the heavens and the earth is in relation to the Throne?\" I said: \"No, unless you teach me from what Allah, the Exalted, has taught you.\" He ﷺ said: \"The likeness of the heavens and the earth in relation to the Throne is only like a ring thrown in a vast desert. And the superiority of the Throne over the heavens and the earth is like the superiority of the desert over that ring.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how many were the prophets, peace be upon them?\" He ﷺ said: \"They were one hundred and twenty-four thousand.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, were all of them messengers?\" He ﷺ said: \"No, the messengers among them were three hundred and fifteen men.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which of them was first?\" He ﷺ said: \"Adam, ﷺ .\" I said: \"Was Adam a prophet?\" He ﷺ said: \"Yes, Allah formed his dust and created him with His hand and breathed into him of His spirit and spoke to him directly. Then the people around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became many.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Shall I not inform you of the most miserly of people?\" I said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He ﷺ said: \"The one in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not send blessings upon me ﷺ.\""],[947,"The Prophet ﷺ went out to the Harrah of Banu Mu‘awiyah, and I followed his tracks until he appeared upon it. Then he prayed the Duha prayer, eight rak‘ahs, making them long. He ﷺ said: “O Hudhayfah, did I make it long for you?” I said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He ﷺ said: “I asked Allah, Mighty and Majestic, three things concerning it, and He granted me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to let any other nation prevail over my Ummah, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to destroy it by years of drought, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to make its might (war) among themselves, and He withheld it from me.”"],[948,"She used to pray the Duha prayer eight rak‘ahs while seated. It was said to her: “Aishah ؓ prays it four!” She said: “Aishah ؓ is a young woman, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘The prayer of one seated is half of the prayer of one standing.’”"],[949,"The Prophet ﷺ sent out an expedition. They obtained great spoils and returned quickly. A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, we have not seen an expedition quicker in return nor greater in spoils than this expedition.” He ﷺ said: “Shall I inform you of one quicker in return and greater in spoils than it? A man who performs ablution in his house and perfects his ablution, then heads to the mosque and prays the morning prayer in it, then follows it with the Duha prayer. He has been quicker in return and greater in spoils.”"],[950,"Abu Ya‘la narrated it in his Musnad, from Abu Bakr."],[951,"And Ibn Hibban, from Abu Ya‘la, and al-Bazzar also transmitted it from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah ؓ. He—that is Abu Hurayrah—said: Abu Bakr ؓ said: “O Messenger of Allah…”"],[952,"I saw Aishah ؓ pray the Duha prayer eight rak‘ahs. I said to her: “Is this something I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do, or something he commanded you to do?” She said: “I will not tell you anything about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding them, but if my father were raised from the grave for me on condition that I abandon them, I would not abandon them.”"],[953,"Aishah ؓ used to pray the Duha prayer and prolong it."],[954,"No one consistently maintains the Duha prayer except the oft-returning (awwab)."],[955,"The Prophet ﷺ arrived when I was nine or ten years old. He said: “O Anas, increase in purification and your lifespan will be increased. And pray the Duha prayer, for it is the prayer of the oft-returning (awwabin).”"],[956,"He said to Abu Dharr ؓ: “O uncle, grant me some good.” He said: “Yes, son of my brother. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: ‘O Abu Dharr, if you pray the Duha prayer two rak‘ahs, you will not be recorded among the heedless. If you pray it four, you will be recorded among the doers of good. If you pray it six, no sin will follow you. If you pray it ten… [missing]. If you pray it twelve, a house will be built for you in Paradise.’”"],[957,"Whoever prays the morning prayer and then remains seated in his place, not engaging in any worldly talk, and remembers Allah Almighty until he prays the Duha prayer four rak‘ahs, he will emerge from his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him, with no sin upon him."],[958,"Whoever prays the Fajr prayer in congregation, then remains sitting in his place until he prays the supererogatory (subhah) of the Duha, will have the reward of a complete Hajj and Umrah—his Hajj and his Umrah."],[959,"The prayer of the penitent is when the young camels feel the heat of the sun."],[960,"The Prophet ﷺ came to them in the mosque of Quba' and saw them praying the Duha prayer, so he said: 'This is the prayer of the penitent.' He said: 'They used to pray it when the young camels felt the heat of the sun.'"],[961,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray the Duha prayer at all. 'Umar b. al-Hakam said: I mentioned this to Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas ؓ, and he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to leave off an action out of dislike that people would see him and then do it, so he would do it privately. And I do pray it.'"],[962,"He used to pray the Duha prayer until it would not be thought that he had abandoned it, and he would leave it until it would not be thought that he would pray it."],[963,"Ibn 'Abbas said, when he came to this verse: 'They extol His glory in the evening and at sunrise,' he said: 'This is the Ishraq prayer.'"],[965,"Whoever abandons the prayer deliberately has been absolved of the protection of Allah, the Exalted."],[966,"Whoever is absolved of the protection of Allah, the Exalted, has disbelieved."],[967,"Regarding one who says: 'The prayer is from Allah, the Exalted, and I will not pray it,' and 'The zakat is from Allah and I will not pay it,' he said: 'He is asked to repent. If he repents, [it is accepted]; otherwise, he is killed.'"],[968,"Regarding one who says: 'The prayer is from Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and I will not pray it': his neck is struck from here—and Ishaq pointed to the back of his neck—there is no disagreement among the imams about it."],[970,"'Abdullah b. Shaqiq led us in the 'Asr prayer and prostrated with us twice, and we did not notice any mistake. When he said the salam, they mentioned that to him. They said: 'We did not notice any mistake!' He said: 'I was talking to myself.'"],[971,"'Amr b. al-'As ؓ led the people in prayer and stood up from his tashahhud. The people shouted at him, saying: 'Glory be to Allah, glory be to Allah,' but he continued praying as he was. When he completed his prayer, he prostrated twice, then said: 'O people, what you intended was not hidden from me, and nothing prevented me from sitting except that what I did was according to the Sunnah.'"],[972,"'Uqbah b. 'Amir ؓ stood up in his prayer."],[973,"He rose after the first two rak'ahs (in a four-rak'ah prayer), and the people glorified Allah (tasbih) to alert him. He completed standing, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness (sajdatay al-sahw) until he concluded. He said: 'You thought I would sit; I did as I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.'"],[974,"Abu Ya'la said: 'Amr b. Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us. Amr said: I have not heard anyone attribute it [to the Prophet] except Abu Mu'awiyah.'"],[975,"And Waki' narrated to us, from Isma'il, and he mentioned it as a statement of a Companion (mawquf). And al-Mughirah b. Shubayl narrated it, from Qays, from al-Mughirah."],[976,"I entered upon Abu Hurayrah and 'Abd Allah b. Hanzalah ؓ while they were sitting in the mosque when the sun had declined [from its zenith]. 'Abd Allah b. Hanzalah ؓ said: 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ led us in the Maghrib prayer, and he did not recite in the first rak'ah; he forgot. When he stood for the second rak'ah, he recited the Opening of the Book (Umm al-Qur'an) and a surah, then he returned and recited the Opening of the Book and a surah, then he continued until he completed his prayer, then he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness.'"],[977,"Whoever prays a prayer in which he does not remember anything of worldly affairs will not ask Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for anything in it except that Allah will grant it to him."],[978,"Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan ؓ led us in the Maghrib prayer, which is three [rak'ahs], and he stood up after two [rak'ahs]. The people glorified Allah to alert him, but he gestured to them [to remain silent]. When he completed his prayer and said the salam, he turned around and addressed them, saying: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do as you saw me do, and had I not seen him do it, I would not have done it.'"],[979,"The two prostrations of forgetfulness suffice for every addition and deficiency [in prayer]."],[980,"826 672 / 2 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Hafs b. Bishr al-Asadi narrated to us; Hakim b. Nafi' narrated to us, and he mentioned it. Hakim is weak."],[983,"Gabriel ﷺ came to me with a white mirror in which there was a black spot. I said: 'What is this?' He said: 'This is Friday, in it there is an hour.'"],[984,"The days were shown to me, and among them Friday was shown to me. It was like a beautiful mirror, and in its middle there was a black spot. I said: 'What is this blackness?' He said: 'This is the hour [in which supplication is answered].'"],[985,"Gabriel ﷺ came to me with [the knowledge of] Friday, and it is like a white mirror in which there is something like a black spot. I said: 'O Gabriel, what is this?' He said: 'This is Friday.' I said: 'And what is Friday?' He said: 'You have in it good.' I said: 'And what do we have in it?' He said: 'It will be a festival ('id) for you and for your people after you, and the Jews and Christians will be subordinate to you.' I said: 'And what do we have in it?' He said: 'You have in it an hour in which no Muslim servant coincides with it asking Allah, Exalted is He, for anything of the affairs of this world or the Hereafter except that Allah will grant it to him—if he has a share [destined] in it; otherwise He will store for him with Himself what is better than it—if he has no share [destined]; or he seeks refuge in Him from an evil that is written for him except that He will avert from him a calamity greater than it.' I said: 'And why is that?' He said: 'Because your Lord, Blessed and Exalted, has taken in Paradise a valley of white musk. When the Day of Resurrection comes, He will descend from 'Illiyyun upon His Throne, then the Throne will be surrounded by pulpits of gold adorned with jewels, then the prophets will be brought and they will sit upon them, then the pulpits will be surrounded by chairs of light, then the martyrs will come until they sit upon them, and the people of the upper chambers (ahl al-ghuraf) will descend and sit upon the sandhill. Then their Lord will manifest Himself to them and will say: \"Ask Me and I will give you.\" They will ask Him for His pleasure, and He will say: \"My pleasure: I will make you dwell in My abode and grant you My honor, so ask Me and I will give you.\" They will ask Him for His pleasure, and He will bear witness to them that He is pleased with them. It was said: Then there will be opened for them what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined. He said: And that is the extent of your departure from Friday [prayer]. He said: Then the prophets, the truthful, and the martyrs will ascend with Him, and the people of the upper chambers will return to their chambers, which are of white pearl, or red ruby, or green chrysolite. From them are their chambers and their doors, with rivers flowing through them, their fruits lofty and hanging down. There is no grief or worry in them. He said: Thus they are not in greater need of anything than the Day of Friday, in order to increase in looking at their Lord and to increase in honor from Him.'"],[986,"We call it 'the Day of Increase' (yawm al-mazid). I said: 'What is al-mazid?' He said: 'Allah, Exalted is He, has made in Paradise a wide valley and has placed in it sandhills of musk. When it is Friday, He descends into it and says: \"Clothe My servants, feed My servants, give drink to My servants, perfume My servants.\" Then He says: \"What do you desire?\" They say: \"We desire Your good pleasure, our Lord.\" He says: \"I am pleased with you.\" Then they depart, and the houris with wide lovely eyes ascend to the chambers of green chrysolite or red ruby.'"],[987,"The five prayers, and Friday to Friday, are expiations for what is between them, as long as major sins are avoided. A man said, 'O Messenger of God, does Friday expiate until [the next] Friday?' He said, 'Yes, and an additional three days. And in it there is an hour in which no Muslim servant asks God, Exalted is He, for something good except that He grants it to him. The days were presented to me, and I saw Friday among them as if it were a mirror in splendor and light, and it pleased me. Then I saw in it a black spot, and I asked Gabriel ﷺ , and he said, \"It is the hour in which the Resurrection will occur.\"'"],[988,"Indeed, Friday day and Friday night are twenty-four hours. There is no hour in them except that God, Exalted is He, has in it six hundred freed from the Fire."],[989,"Six hundred thousand freed, and he said at the end: one of them said: 'All of them had deserved the Fire.'"],[990,"Indeed, in Friday there is an hour in which no Muslim who supplicates for good coincides with it except that it is answered. Fatimah said, 'O Messenger of God, which hour is it?' He said, 'When the sun begins to set.' Fatimah used to say to a servant called Arbad Arbid, 'Climb the hill, and when you see the sun beginning to set, inform me.' He would inform her, and she would go to her place of prayer and keep supplicating until the sun set, then she would pray."],[991,"Indeed, a Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'It has reached me that you say: Friday to Friday and the five prayers are expiations for what is between them for whoever avoids major sins?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Yes.' Then he added, 'The bath on Friday is an expiation, and walking to Friday is an expiation: every step of it is for the work of twenty years. When he finishes the Friday prayer, he is rewarded with the work of two hundred years.'"],[992,"Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, his sins and misdeeds are expiated for him. When he starts walking, for every step he has the work of twenty years. When he finishes Friday, he is rewarded with the work of two hundred years."],[993,"He used to prefer not to nullify his ablution between the Friday ghusl and the prayer, and he would say: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'When one of you comes to Friday, let him perform ghusl.'"],[994,"He was asked about the hour on Friday, and he said, 'God knows best. Indeed, God, Exalted is He, created Adam ﷺ on Friday after 'Asr. He created him from a handful He took from the entire surface of the earth. Do you not see that among his descendants are the red, the black, the evil, and the good? Then He made a covenant with him, but he forgot, and from that he is called insan (human). By God, the sun did not set on that day until he was sent down to the world.'"],[996,"Anas ؓ used to be in his palace, and sometimes he would hold Friday prayer, and sometimes he would not."],[997,"We wrote to 'Umar ؓ asking him about Friday in Bahrain, and he wrote to us: 'Hold Friday prayer wherever you are.'"],[998,"I passed by 'Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah ؓ while he was sitting at his door on Friday, and he said, 'What is the sermon of your leader?' We said, 'Did you not hear?' He said, 'No, this mud kept us.'"],[999,"The blind man, if he does not find a guide, then there is no Friday prayer upon him."],[1000,"Abū al-Mulayḥ was in charge of al-Ubulla, and among al-Ḥajjāj's governors there was none more God-fearing than Abū al-Mulayḥ. On Fridays he would come and lead the Friday prayer in al-Baṣra, then return."],[1001,"Attend the Friday prayer and draw near to the imam, for a man may stay away from the Friday prayer even though he is one of those required to attend."],[1002,"I saw Ibn Masʿūd ؓ turning the women out of the mosque on Friday."],[1004,"We were commanded to perform the ritual bath on Friday. I said, 'You, the first Emigrants, or all the people in general?' He said, 'I do not know.'"],[1005,"I never thought that anyone would neglect the ritual bath on Friday."],[1006,"Whoever performs the ritual bath on Friday, it is as if he fasted a day in the path of God, Mighty and Majestic, and the day is like seven hundred."],[1007,"Whoever purifies himself and does so well, then comes to the Friday prayer and does not engage in idle talk or act foolishly, it will be an expiation for what is between it and the next Friday, and the five prayers are an expiation for what is between them. And on Friday there is an hour during which no Muslim servant asks God Almighty for any good but He grants it to him."],[1008,"My close friend ﷺ enjoined me to perform the ritual bath on Friday."],[1009,"Part of the Sunnah is the ritual bath on Friday."],[1010,"852 691 / 2 - And al-Ḥārith said: Al-Muqrīʾ narrated to us, al-Masʿūdī narrated to us with it. : :"],[1011,"Whoever performs ablution on Friday, it is acceptable and good, but whoever performs the ritual bath, the bath is better."],[1012,"A man asked ʿAlī ؓ about the ritual bath. He said, 'Bathe every day if you wish.' He said, 'No, rather the bath that is recommended.' He said, 'Bathe every Friday, on the day of Fiṭr, on the day of Sacrifice, and on the day of ʿArafa.'"],[1013,"They used to love to have intercourse on Friday so as to make the ritual bath obligatory."],[1014,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said in one of the Fridays: 'This is a day of Eid which God has appointed for the Muslims, so bathe, and whoever has perfume, it does not harm him to touch some of it, and you should use the toothstick.'"],[1015,"It is a duty upon every Muslim to bathe on Friday, to use the toothstick, and to touch some perfume if he has any."],[1017,"He used to pray Friday when the sun had passed its zenith."],[1018,"A man delayed the prayer on Friday, and an old man said to him: 'By God, I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying, and I did not see him do as you do!' He said: 'When I saw him, he mentioned the Messenger of God ﷺ – I said to him: How did you see him act? He said: I saw him ﷺ come out when the sun had passed its zenith – and the man was Abu Juhayfah ؓ.'"],[1019,"He went to Friday prayer, and when the sun had passed its zenith, Umar ؓ came out to them and sat on the pulpit. The mu'adhdhin began his call to prayer, and when he finished, he stood up, praised God Almighty, and extolled Him."],[1020,"Sa'd ؓ used to take a midday nap after Friday."],[1021,"Our men used to attend Friday prayer with Umar ؓ, then return with their cloaks over their heads, following the shade of the walls, and take a midday nap afterwards."],[1023,"The Messenger of God ﷺ delivered a sermon to us until he made the young women in their chambers hear it."],[1024,"He used to give the Friday sermon standing, then sit, then stand and give the sermon."],[1025,"He sat a light sitting."],[1026,"Al-Harith said: Muhammad b. Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, Sulayman b. al-Harith al-Ansari narrated to us, from Abbas b. Sahl, from his father."],[1027,"And 'Abd Allah b. Yazid al-Bahili narrated from Iyas b. Salama from his father."],[1028,"He used to deliver two sermons and sit twice: first when he ascended, and between the two sermons."],[1029,"The Prophet ﷺ recited in his sermon [surah] al-Ma'idah and Surat al-Tawbah."],[1031,"If I take a pulpit, my father Ibrahim ﷺ took one; and if I take a staff, my father Ibrahim ﷺ took one."],[1032,"The wooden piece in the enclosure: the Prophet ﷺ used to lean on it when he stood. When he ﷺ passed away, it was stolen. It was sought and found in the mosque of Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf. Termites had eaten it out. Two pieces of wood were carved and hollowed for it, then they were fitted over it, then the two pieces were joined together upon it. So when you see it, you see the joint in it."],[1033,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver the Friday sermon standing by the trunk of a palm tree. It was said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, the people have become numerous and they would love to see you. If only you would take a pulpit to stand on so the people can see you.' He said: 'Yes. Who will make this pulpit for us?' A man stood up and said: 'I will.' He said: 'Will you make it?' He said: 'Yes' - and he did not say: 'If Allah wills.' He said: 'What is your name?' He said: 'So-and-so.' He said: 'Sit down.' So he sat down. Then he returned and said: 'Who will make this pulpit for us?' A man stood up and said: 'I will.' He said: 'Will you make it?' He said: 'Yes,' and he did not say: 'If Allah wills.' He said: 'What is your name?' He said: 'So-and-so.' He said: 'Sit down.' So he sat down. Then he returned and said: 'Who will make this pulpit for us?' A man stood up and said: 'I will.' He said: 'Will you make it?' He said: 'Yes, if Allah wills.' He said: 'What is your name?' He said: 'Ibrahim.' He said: 'Make it.' When Friday came, the people gathered. When he ascended the pulpit and stood upright on it, facing the people, the palm trunk moaned until it made me hear it while I was at the far end of the mosque. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended from the pulpit and embraced it, and he did not stop until it became still. Then he returned to the pulpit, praised Allah Almighty and extolled Him, then said: 'This palm trunk only moaned out of longing for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he left it. By Allah, had I not descended to it and embraced it, it would not have become still until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[1034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver the sermon by a trunk. A Byzantine man came to him and said: 'I will make you a pulpit to deliver the sermon on.' So he made for him this one you see. When he stood on it to deliver the sermon, the trunk moaned like a she-camel moaning for her young. He descended to it and hugged it, and it became still. He ordered that a hole be dug for it and that it be buried."],[1035,"The next day I saw that it had been moved. I said: 'What is this?' They said: 'The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar ؓ came and moved it.'"],[1036,"And through him from Ibn Abi Za'idah, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id b. Abi Karib, from Jabir ؓ, he mentioned something similar with the addition."],[1038,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at the people on Friday, their appearance being shabby, and said: 'What harm would it do a man to take two garments for this day?' The next Friday had not come before some coarse clothes arrived from Bahrain, [and he saw] the one with two garments and the striped cloak."],[1039,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had two garments that he would wear on Friday. When he finished, he would fold them and put them away."],[1040,"He used to wear his red cloak on the two Eids and on Friday."],[1042,"We used to pray in the time of Umar ؓ on Friday, and when Umar ؓ came out and sat on the pulpit, we would cut off the prayer. We used to talk and he would talk to us, and perhaps a man would ask the one next to him about their market and their servants. When the muezzin became silent, he delivered the sermon, and we did not speak until he finished his sermon."],[1043,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas ؓ said to a man on Friday: 'There is no Jumu'ah for you.' The man mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Sa'd said to me: There is no Jumu'ah for you.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Why, O Sa'd?' He said: 'He spoke while you were delivering the sermon.' He ﷺ said: 'Sa'd has spoken the truth.'"],[1044,"Abdullah b. Mas'ud ؓ entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon, and he sat next to Ubayy b. Ka'b ؓ and asked him about something, but he did not answer him. He thought it was anger, so he mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ. Ubayy ؓ said: 'O Abdullah, you did not attend Jumu'ah with us.' He said: 'Why?' He said: 'You spoke while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon.' He ﷺ said: 'Ubayy has spoken the truth.'"],[1046,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us and mentioned the hadith in its length - and in it: Then he delivered a sermon and said: 'Praise be to Allah, we praise Him, seek His help, seek His forgiveness, believe in Him, and rely upon Him. We bear witness that there is no god but Allah, alone without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. We seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our souls and the misdeeds of our actions. Whomever Allah guides, none can lead astray, and whomever He leads astray, none can guide.'"],[1048,"I saw al-Hasan b. Abi al-Hasan ؓ enter the mosque of Wasit on Friday while Ibn Hubayrah was delivering the sermon on the pulpit. He prayed two rak'ahs, then sat down."],[1050,"Whoever abandons Jumu'ah three times, a seal is placed on his heart, and his heart is made like the heart of a hypocrite."],[1051,"Whoever abandons the Friday prayer three times consecutively has thrown Islam behind his back."],[1052,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood as a preacher on Friday and said: 'Perhaps a man who has Jumu'ah, while he is within a mile of Madinah, does not attend it.' Then he said the second time: 'While he is within two miles of Madinah, he does not attend it.' Then he said the third time: 'While he is within three miles of Madinah, he does not attend Jumu'ah, and Allah seals his heart.'"],[1054,"A man came while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon on Friday, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'One of you amuses himself until Jumu'ah is about to pass him by, then he comes stepping over people's necks, harming them.' He said: 'I did not do that, O Prophet of Allah, but I was sleeping, then I woke up, got up, performed ablution, and then came.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Is this a day of ablution?!'"],[1056,"Whoever catches one rak'ah of Jumu'ah should add another to it."],[1057,"Whoever catches one rak'ah of Jumu'ah should add another to it, and whoever misses the two rak'ahs should pray four, or Zuhr, or the first."],[1058,"Whoever catches one rak'ah of Jumu'ah has caught it; he should add another one to it."],[1061,"I saw 'Imran b. Husayn ؓ pray Jumu'ah, then he prayed two rak'ahs after it. They said, 'He completed it... he completed it.' I mentioned that to 'Imran ؓ, and he said, 'That spears should pierce my insides is dearer to me than that I should do that deliberately.' I watched him on the next Jumu'ah, and he prayed, then sat with his legs drawn up and did not pray until he stood for 'Asr."],[1062,"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, tell us about Friday: what good is in it?' He said, 'In it there are five qualities: in it Allah created Adam, in it Allah sent Adam down, in it Allah took Adam's soul, in it there is an hour in which no Muslim supplicates except that Allah gives him what he asks, as long as he does not ask for a sin or severing ties of kinship, and in it the Hour will be established. There is no angel brought near, no earth, no mountains, and no wind but that it is apprehensive of Friday.'"],[1064,"'Ali ؓ prayed 'Asr during travel [as two rak'ahs], then he entered his tent and prayed two rak'ahs while I was looking."],[1065,"We prayed with the Prophet ﷺ the prayer of travel, two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, except Maghrib, three."],[1066,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to complete the prayer and shorten it."],[1067,"I came to Abu Dharr ؓ at al-Baldah, which is Mina, and it was said to him, 'Uthman ؓ prayed four [rak'ahs].' He said, 'I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar ؓ, and they prayed two rak'ahs.' Then he stood and prayed four."],[1068,"We set out on a journey, and we were twelve riders, all of whom had accompanied Muhammad ﷺ except me. The time for prayer came, and a man from the group went forward and prayed four [rak'ahs]. Salman ؓ said, 'What do we have to do with four? Half of four is enough for us. We are more in need of lightening.'"],[1069,"The Prophet ﷺ was on a journey, and he delayed Zuhr, hastened 'Asr, and combined them, and he delayed Maghrib, hastened 'Isha', and combined them."],[1070,"I witnessed al-Nu'man b. Bashir combining Maghrib and 'Isha'."],[1071,"'Umar ؓ wrote to Abu Musa ؓ that combining two prayers without a valid excuse is one of the major sins."],[1072,"The prayer was originally prescribed as two prostrations [i.e., two rak'ahs]... [two rak'ahs each], for Zuhr and 'Asr. They used to pray two rak'ahs after Zuhr and two rak'ahs after 'Asr. Then Zuhr was made four for them and 'Asr four, so they abandoned that when it was made obligatory upon them. The prayer of travel was kept as it was, and the prayer of residence was made four. He affirmed it and said: Yes."],[1073,"Whoever prays four [rak'ahs] while traveling is like one who prays two [rak'ahs] while resident."],[1074,"When he left Madinah and traveled a farsakh, he would shorten the prayer."],[1075,"And Ahmad b. Mani' said: Hushaym narrated to us, [with it]."],[1076,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he passed beyond a farsakh he would shorten the prayer."],[1077,"Ibn 'Umar ؓ was asked about prayer during travel, and he said: Two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs. Whoever contradicts the Sunnah has disbelieved."],[1078,"I asked 'Abdullah b. 'Umar ؓ about prayer during travel, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, except Maghrib."],[1079,"He used to go out to al-Ghabah and would not break his fast or shorten the prayer."],[1080,"A man asked Ibn 'Abbas ؓ: 'Should I shorten the prayer up to 'Arafah?' He said: 'Do not shorten the prayer except for a full day's journey.'"],[1081,"We were with Ibn 'Abbas ؓ on a journey. The sun set, and it was said to him: 'O Abu al-'Abbas, the prayer?' He said: 'We are a traveling people.' Then he traveled on until he reached Marr al-Zahran and dismounted. Between where he was when it was said to him 'the prayer' at sunset and Marr al-Zahran was two farsakhs."],[1083,"I prayed the fear prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, two rak'ahs, except Maghrib, which was three."],[1084,"Abu Musa ؓ was at al-Dar in Isfahan, and there was no great fear there that day, but he wanted to teach them their religion and the Sunnah of their Prophet ﷺ. He arranged them in two rows: one group with weapons facing their enemy, and another group in front of him. He prayed one rak'ah with those next to him, then they moved backwards walking on their heels until they stood in the place of the others, passing through them, until they stood behind him. He then prayed another rak'ah with them and said the salam. Then those who had been next to him and the others stood up and prayed one rak'ah each, then some of them said salam to the others. Thus the imam completed two rak'ahs in congregation, and the people completed one rak'ah each."],[1085,"The fear prayer is two rak'ahs and four prostrations. If a matter hastens him, fighting [and speaking] has become permissible."],[1087,"The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. When you see that, hasten to prayer."],[1088,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Pray as the most recent prescribed prayer you have prayed.'"],[1089,"I prayed the eclipse prayer behind the Prophet ﷺ, and I did not hear a single letter from him during it."],[1091,"People wake up in a barren land, and Allah, Exalted is He, brings them provision from Himself, yet they wake up as polytheists, saying: 'We were given rain by such-and-such a star.'"],[1092,"He used to expose himself to the first rain, taking off his clothes except for the waist-wrapper."],[1093,"Three things I fear for my ummah: seeking rain by the stars, injustice of rulers, and denial of divine decree."],[1094,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Madinah. He turned toward it and said: 'Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, has purified this island from polytheism, but I fear for them that the stars may lead them astray.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, how can the stars lead them astray?' He ﷺ said: 'Rain falls and they say: We were given rain by such-and-such a star.'"],[1096,"Ali ؓ went out on the day of Eid and saw some people praying. He said: O people, we were present with the Prophet of Allah ﷺ on a day like this, and no one prayed before the Eid prayer, or before the Prophet ﷺ. A man said: O Commander of the Believers, will you not forbid them to pray before the imam comes out? He said: I do not want to forbid a servant when he prays, but we tell them what we witnessed from the Prophet ﷺ, or as he said."],[1097,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to the Eid prayer walking."],[1098,"How did Ibn Umar ؓ pray on the day of Eid? He said: He would attend the Fajr prayer with the imam, then return to his house and perform ghusl [his ghusl] for janabah, and wear his best clothes, and apply the best perfume he had, then go out until he came to the musalla, and sit there until the imam arrived. When the imam came, he prayed with him, then returned and entered the mosque of the Prophet ﷺ and prayed two rak'ahs in it, then went to his house."],[1099,"On the day of departure from Mina, Ibn Abbas ؓ used to say the takbir and command those around him to say the takbir, acting upon the words of the Exalted: 'When you have completed your rites, remember Allah.'"],[1100,"Ibn Umar ؓ used to go early to the Eid prayer from the mosque, raising his voice with the takbir until he reached the musalla, and he would say the takbir until the imam arrived."],[1101,"It was said to Ali ؓ: There are people who cannot come out; some of them have an illness, and some of them live far from the mosque. He ؓ said: Pray here and in the mosque, and pray four [rak'ahs]: two for the Sunnah and two for going out."],[1102,"He used to say the takbir from the morning of Arafah until the end of the days of Tashriq, and he would not say the takbir in the Maghrib prayer. His takbir was: Allahu akbar kabira, Allahu akbar kabira, Allahu akbar kabira, wal-hamdu lillah, [Allahu] akbar, or he said: Allahu akbar 'ala ma hadana."],[1103,"He used to wear his red burdah on the two Eids and on Friday."],[1104,"Ibn Umar ؓ would not eat on the day of Fitr until he returned from the musalla."],[1105,"He distributed dates among his companions before going early to the Eid prayer, and said: Eat before you go out. He did."],[1106,"Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ used to pray the Eid prayer before the sermon."],[1107,"that he saw the Prophet ﷺ praying on the day of Eid al-Fitr between the two stones"],[1108,"the prayer on the two Eids used to be before the sermon"],[1109,"the takbir in Eid al-Fitr is one takbir with which the prayer is opened, then he says takbir five times, then he recites, then he says takbir and bows, then he stands and says takbir five times, then he recites, then he says takbir and bows"],[1110,"he used to say takbir in Eid seven takbirs in the first, and five in the last"],[1111,"We were with Thabit al-Bunani, and an old man was with him, and we mentioned what is recited in the two Eids, and the old man said: I accompanied Anas b. Malik ؓ to al-Zawiya on the day of an Eid, and a client of theirs was leading them in prayer, and he recited: Sabbih isma Rabbika al-A'la, and Wa al-layli idha yaghsha. Anas ؓ said: He recited the two surahs which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited"],[1112,"I went out with Ka'b b. 'Ujra ؓ on the day of Eid, and he did not pray before it. When we prayed, he saw the people as one neck going to the mosque, and he said: This is indeed an innovation and an abandonment of the Sunnah"],[1113,"Maysara used to pray before the imam on the day of Eid, so I said: Did not 'Ali ؓ used to dislike prayer before it? He said: Yes"],[1114,"I saw Anas b. Malik and al-Hasan ؓ praying on the day of Eid before the imam came out. He said: And I saw Muhammad b. Sirin come and sit and not pray"],[1117,"that he bequeathed: When I am near death, sit by me one who will prompt me with La ilaha illa Allah, and hasten with me to my grave, and do not announce my death to the people, for I fear that would be an announcement like the announcement of the Jahiliyyah"],[1118,"Abu Bakr ؓ entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and he was gloomy, so he said: Why do I see you gloomy? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I was with a cousin of mine last night, so-and-so, and he was in the throes of death. He ﷺ said: Did you not prompt him with La ilaha illa Allah? He said: I did, O Messenger of Allah. He ﷺ said: And did he say it? He said: Yes. He ﷺ said: Paradise is guaranteed for him. Abu Bakr ؓ said: O Messenger of Allah, how is it for the living? He ﷺ said: It is more destructive of their sins, it is more destructive of their sins"],[1119,"Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ fell ill, and his companions came to visit him. He said: Sit me up. So they sat him up. Then he said: A word I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"Whoever's last words at death are 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner,' it demolishes the sins and errors that came before it. So prompt your dying ones with it.\" They said: O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, how is it for the living? He said: It demolishes even more, even more."],[1120,"I entered upon Abu Bakr ؓ and saw death upon him. I said: \"Hayj, hayj: one whose tears are ever prepared will one day be poured out.\" He ؓ said: Do not say that, but say: \"And the agony of death comes with the truth—that is what you used to flee from.\""],[1121,"'Abd narrated it, from Abu Bakr."],[1122,"Report about the Children of Israel, and there is no sin, for among them were wonders."],[1123,"Salman ؓ visited a sick man and saw that he was in the throes of death. He said: O Angel of Death, be gentle with him, for he is a believer. The man said: He says, 'I am gentle with every believer.'"],[1124,"The pain of the Angel of Death is more severe than a thousand strikes with a sword. There is no believer who dies but every vein of his aches separately. Al-Harith said: I think he said: And give him glad tidings of Paradise, for the distress is great and the terror is severe, and the closest the enemy of God is to him is at that hour."],[1125,"He raided Khurasan and stayed two years praying two rak'ahs and not combining. A cousin of his was dying, so he went to visit him and said..."],[1126,"The death of the believer is with the sweat of the forehead."],[1127,"The death of the believer is the sweat of the forehead: the believer still has some sins for which he is recompensed at death, and his forehead sweats from that."],[1128,"The death of the believer is with the sweat of the forehead."],[1129,"The gift of the believer is death."],[1130,"There is no deceased person who dies and Surah Yasin is recited at his side except that Allah, the Exalted, makes it easy for him."],[1132,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[1134,"Whoever expects recompense for three of his children who died before reaching the age of accountability, Allah, the Exalted, will admit him to Paradise by the virtue of His mercy to them."],[1135,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[1136,"Whoever sends ahead three of his children, being patient and expecting recompense, they will screen him from the Fire by the permission of Allah, the Exalted."],[1137,"The Prophet ﷺ said to the Ansar ؓ: \"What is the meaning of 'raqūb' among you?\" They said: \"The one who has no child.\" He said: \"That is not the raqūb. The raqūb is the one who comes to his Lord - Mighty and Glorious - and has not sent ahead any of his children.\""],[1138,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[1139,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[1140,"And Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us with it."],[1141,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ with a sick son of hers, and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah Almighty to heal this son of mine. He ﷺ said: Do you have a child who has died? She said: Yes, in Islam. He ﷺ said: A strong shield, a strong shield."],[1142,"Indeed, he has taken refuge in a strong shield, the one for whom three children have died in Islam."],[1143,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to look after the Ansar, visit them, and ask about them. We were informed that a woman from the Ansar had a son who died and she was greatly distressed over him. He ﷺ came to her and ordered her to fear Allah Almighty and be patient. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a childless woman who does not give birth, and I had no child other than him. He ﷺ said: The truly childless is the one whose child remains alive. Then he ﷺ said: There is no Muslim man or Muslim woman for whom three children die but that Allah will admit them both to Paradise. Umar ؓ said: May my father be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, and two? He ﷺ said: And two."],[1144,"There was a man from the Ansar who used to sit with the Prophet ﷺ, and with him was a son of his who was five years old. The boy died, and he was greatly distressed over him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Would it please you that you would not come to any gate of the gates of Paradise except that you would find him calling you to it? He said: Yes. He ﷺ said: It is as I tell you."],[1146,"Whoever dies on Friday is protected from the punishment of the grave."],[1148,"Whoever washes a dead person and conceals his faults, Allah Almighty will purify him from his sins. And if he shrouds him, Allah - Mighty and Majestic - will clothe him from fine silk."],[1149,"I asked Ibn Abbas ؓ about performing ghusl after washing a dead body? He said: You have then made your companion impure."],[1150,"Al-Hasan did not consider that the one who washes a dead person needs to perform ghusl."],[1151,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave us a sermon and mentioned the hadith, and in it: \"Whoever washes a deceased person and fulfills the trust in it, for every hair of it he will have the freeing of a slave, and a hundred degrees will be raised for him by it.\" Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: \"How does he fulfill the trust in it, O Messenger of God?\" He ﷺ said: \"He covers his private parts and conceals his blemishes. If he does not conceal his blemishes and does not cover his private parts, God Almighty will expose his private parts before all creatures.\""],[1152,"\"When I die, wash me, shroud me, embalm me, perfume me with incense, and do not scatter embalming spices on my shroud, and do not follow me with a censer.\""],[1154,"The best shroud is a full suit (hulla)."],[1155,"On the day of Uhud, Hamzah ؓ was shrouded in a striped cloak; when his head was covered, his feet showed, and when his feet were covered, his head showed."],[1156,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was shrouded in two white Suhuli garments."],[1157,"I came when my father was dying, and he said: \"Do not shroud me in a sewn shirt.\" They said: \"It is necessary.\" So I sent to the fuller, and my father had a shirt at the fuller's. It was brought, and he was dressed in it, and it was taken away. I locked my door and followed it, then returned to my house and found the shirt in the house. I sent to those who washed my father and said: \"Did you shroud him in his shirt?\" They said: \"Yes.\" I said: \"Is it this one?\" They said: \"Yes.\""],[1159,"Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said to Ali ؓ: \"Tell us, O Abu al-Hasan, about walking with the funeral procession. Which is best?\" Ali ؓ said: \"By God, the superiority of walking behind it over walking in front of it is like the superiority of the obligatory prayer over the voluntary prayer.\" Abu Sa'id ؓ said: \"By God, I have not sat since I attended a funeral procession attended by Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ, and I saw Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ walking in front of it.\" He said: \"May God forgive them. The best of this nation after its Prophet ﷺ are Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ, then God knows best where the good is. If you saw them do that, they did it while knowing that the superiority of walking behind it over walking in front of it is like the superiority of the obligatory prayer over the voluntary prayer, just as we know that after tomorrow there is a night. But they liked the people to spread out and disliked them being cramped, and they knew that they would be followed as examples.\" He said: \"O Abu al-Hasan, tell me about carrying the funeral bier: is it obligatory on those who attend it?\" He ؓ said: \"No, but it is good. Whoever wishes takes it, and whoever wishes leaves it. When you are with a funeral procession, put it before you and make it a focus between your eyes, for it is an admonition, a reminder, and a lesson. If you decide to carry it, look at the rear left side of the bier and place it on your right shoulder. When you reach the graveyard, stand and do not sit, for you will see a great matter. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Your brother, your brother; he competed with you in the world and contended with you in it, and was constrained in the spaciousness of the earth with palaces. He has been placed in a grave under the interior of a grave, turned on his side. So stand and do not sit until you pour the dust upon him. If the people do not let you, and they will not let you, and they say: \"By God, this is nothing,\" then stand and do not sit until he is lowered into his pit, even if they fight you fiercely.'\""],[1160,"Amr b. Hurayth visited al-Hasan while Ali ؓ was with him... the hadith. Amr said to him: \"What do you say about walking in front of the funeral procession?\" He said: \"The superiority of walking behind it over walking in front of it is like the superiority of the obligatory prayer over the voluntary prayer.\" He said: \"But I saw Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ walking in front of it.\" He said: \"They disliked causing hardship to the people.\""],[1161,"Whoever's fasting coincides with Friday, and he visits a sick person, and attends a funeral, and frees a slave, Paradise becomes due for him."],[1162,"The first thing a believing servant is rewarded with after his death is that forgiveness is granted to all who followed his funeral procession."],[1163,"Whoever prays over a funeral is as if he fasted a day in the path of Allah – Mighty and Majestic – and the day is as seven hundred days. And whoever attends the funeral of a Muslim man is as if he fasted a day in the path of Allah – Mighty and Majestic – and the day is as seven hundred days."],[1164,"Whoever prays over a funeral gets a qirat, and whoever walks with it until it is buried gets two qirats."],[1165,"No Muslim attends the funeral of a Muslim man without receiving a qirat of reward. If he sits until they pray over it, he receives two qirats of reward, each qirat like Uhud."],[1166,"Whoever follows a funeral and takes hold of the four sides of the bier, forty sins are forgiven for him, all of them major."],[1167,"I saw Sa‘d b. Abī Waqqāṣ ؓ at the funeral of ‘Abd al-Raḥmān b. ‘Awf ؓ standing between the two front poles, placing the bier on his shoulder."],[1168,"Indeed Allah, Exalted is He, loves silence at three times: during recitation of the Qur’an, during battle, and during a funeral."],[1169,"He saw Ibn ‘Umar and ‘Ubayd b. ‘Umayr walking in front of the funeral in upper Makkah, going ahead, then sitting down; when it passed them, they stood up."],[1170,"Abū Hurayrah ؓ bequeathed: When I die, do not set up a tent over me, do not follow me with fire, and hasten with me."],[1171,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a funeral, and he saw some women and said: 'Will you carry him?' They said: 'No.' He said: 'Will you lower him?' They said: 'No.' He said: 'Then go back, burdened with sin, not rewarded.'"],[1172,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: 'Whoever follows a funeral gets for every step he takes until he returns one hundred thousand good deeds, the erasing of one hundred thousand bad deeds, and the raising of one hundred thousand degrees. If he prays over it, seventy thousand angels are appointed for him seeking forgiveness for him until he returns. And if he witnesses its burial, they seek forgiveness for him until he is raised from his grave.'"],[1174,"Ibn ‘Umar ؓ, when he saw a funeral, would stand until it passed him. And Ibn ‘Umar ؓ, when he went out in a funeral, would turn his back to the graves."],[1176,"None of you should pray over your funerals except me, as long as I am among you."],[1178,"He forbade that a voice or a fire should follow the deceased."],[1180,"There was a man circumambulating the House, saying: 'Oh... oh,' in his supplication. He said: 'I went out one night and found the Messenger of God ﷺ burying that man at night by the light of a lamp.'"],[1181,"The Prophet ﷺ attended a deceased person of ours who was being buried and said: 'Do not make it heavy on your companion.'"],[1182,"Umar ؓ bequeathed to me, saying: 'When you place me in my grave niche, press my cheek to the earth, so that there is nothing between my skin and the earth.'"],[1183,"When the plague of al-Jarif occurred, Bushayr b. Ka'b dug a grave for himself and recited the Quran in it until he completed it. When he died ؓ, he was buried in it."],[1184,"Qays b. Asim ؓ bequeathed to his sons, saying: 'Bury me where Bakr b. Wa'il will not see me, for I used to raid them in the pre-Islamic era.'"],[1185,"When Maymunah ؓ died, who was his maternal aunt, I took my cloak and spread it in her grave niche, but Ibn Abbas ؓ took it and threw it away."],[1186,"Make a niche in the side of the grave, and do not dig a trench."],[1187,"Whenever Anas ؓ placed the deceased in the grave, he would say: 'O God, keep the earth away from his sides and widen his grave for him.'"],[1188,"A son of Samurah who had run died, and he heard weeping. He said: 'What is this weeping?' They said: 'For so-and-so.' He forbade them from that, then called for a basin or a large cup and washed him before him, then shrouded him before him. Then he said to a servant of his: 'O so-and-so, go to his grave, and when you place him down, say: In the name of God and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then untie the knots of his head and the knots of his feet, and say: O God, do not deprive us of his reward and do not test us after him.'"],[1190,"Two men from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ were killed at the gate of Banu Salim. This was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered that they be buried where they were killed. So they were carried from where they had been struck, and that coincided with the cemetery of Banu Hilal, so they were buried there."],[1192,"No believer ever consoles another believer in a calamity except that on the Day of Resurrection he will be clothed with a garment in which he will be made joyful."],[1194,"I used to hear Umar ؓ say: 'No one from Quraysh enters a door except that people enter with him.' I did not know the interpretation of his statement until Umar ؓ was stabbed. He ordered Suhayb ؓ to lead the people in prayer for three days, and he ordered that food be prepared for the people. When they returned from the funeral, they came and the tables had been laid, but the people refrained from them because of the grief they were in. Al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib ؓ came and said: 'O people, indeed ... has died.' The hadith continues."],[1195,"The dead are tested in their graves for seven days, so they used to recommend that food be given on their behalf during those days."],[1197,"I had forbidden you from three things, and now I permit them to you: I had forbidden you from making nabidh, so now make nabidh, and every intoxicant is haram; I had forbidden you from storing the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, so now eat and store it; and I had forbidden you from visiting graves, so now visit them, but do not say anything indecent."],[1198,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Abtah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up cheerfully and went toward the graveyard. He sat by one of the graves, then he sat with us looking sorrowful. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you left us a while ago cheerful, and you have returned sorrowful?' He ﷺ said: 'I asked my Lord for permission to visit my mother's grave, and He permitted me—or he said: He gave me a dispensation—so I went to intercede for her, but I was prevented.'"],[1199,"For me to sit on a burning coal until it burns through to my flesh and reaches me would be dearer to me than sitting on a grave. Uthman b. Hakim said: 'I saw Kharija b. Zayd in the graveyard, and I mentioned that to him. He made me sit on a grave and said: \"That only applies to someone who uses it as a toilet.\"'"],[1200,"Whoever sits on a grave to defecate or urinate, it is as if he sat on a burning coal."],[1201,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade sitting on graves or praying on them."],[1203,"My father and my uncle were killed on the day of Uhud, and they were buried in a single grave. I did not find anything of their inheritance; the allies took it."],[1205,"A man was with the Prophet ﷺ and then he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was informed that he had died. He ﷺ said: 'The one who was with us just now?' They said: 'Yes.' He ﷺ said: 'It is as if it were a seizure of anger.'"],[1207,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is more protective of the blood of His believing servant than any of you is of the most precious of his wealth, until He takes him while on his bed."],[1209,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew up his knees that day. An angel entered but found no place to sit. He said: So I made room for him. And Umm Sa'd—meaning Ibn Mu'adh—was weeping over him, saying: 'Woe to the mother of Sa'd, Sa'd, in excellence and glory, after his many favors and glory, he puts forward his youth as a barrier.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'All the weeping women lie except Umm Sa'd.'"],[1210,"Abu Ya'la said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Ahmad b. Yunus narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Rahman, who is Ibn Abi Layla, and he mentioned it in full. Ibn Abi Layla has poor memory, and the confusion in it is from him, and Allah knows best."],[1211,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said... and he mentioned the hadith on the permissibility of weeping over the deceased and on the ruling of wailing. (33) And its completion will come, if Allah Almighty wills, in the Book of Asceticism."],[1212,"The Prophet ﷺ said on the day Ibrahim died: 'Whatever sorrow is in the heart or the eye is only mercy. But whatever is in the voice or in loud lamentation is from Satan.'"],[1213,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a man from Banu Mu'awiyah and found him in his death throes, with his women around him weeping over him. Some men went to restrain the women, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Leave them. But when death is certain, let me not hear the voice of any wailing woman.'"],[1214,"Abu Hurayrah ؓ said to a man from among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Should a man go out fighting in the path of Allah, the Exalted, and be killed as a martyr in a region of the earth, and then a foolish, ignorant woman weep over him—would he be punished because of her weeping over him?' The man replied to Abu Hurayrah ؓ: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke the truth, and Abu Hurayrah has erred.'"],[1215,"I entered with al-Hakam b. al-A'raj upon Bakr b. 'Abdullah, and they discussed the deceased being punished by the weeping of the living. Bakr narrated to us, saying:"],[1216,"When 'Abdullah b. Abi Bakr ؓ died, he was wept over. Abu Bakr ؓ went out to the men and said: 'I apologize to you regarding these women. They are recently out of the era of ignorance. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The deceased is showered with burning coals because of the weeping of the living.\"'"],[1218,"When Abu Bakr ؓ died, he was wept over. 'Umar ؓ said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The deceased is punished because of the weeping of the living.\"' But they refused to stop weeping. 'Umar ؓ said to Hisham b. al-Walid: 'Stand up and expel the women.' 'A'ishah ؓ said: 'I adjure you!' 'Umar ؓ said: 'Enter, for I have permitted you.' He entered, and 'A'ishah ؓ said: 'Will you expel me, O my son?' He said: 'As for you, I have permitted you.' He began expelling them one by one, striking them with the whip. Umm Farwah came out, and he separated them, or he said: 'He separated the wailing women.'"],[1219,"Three things will persist in my community until the Hour begins: wailing, belief in stars, and boasting about lineage."],[1220,"I asked al-Hasan: 'Did the women of the Muhajirun do what is done today?' He said: 'No. Here: scratching faces, tearing garments, plucking hair, and the flutes of Satan—two ugly, obscene sounds: one at this blessing. Allah, the Exalted, mentioned the believers, saying: \"In their wealth is a known right for the beggar and the deprived.\" But you have made in your wealth a known right for the songstress at this blessing and for the wailing woman at a calamity. A man dies with debts and trusts, and leaves a will. Satan comes to his family and says: \"By Allah, you will not carry out his estate, return his trust, pay his debt, or execute his will until you give me my right first.\" So they buy new clothes, then tear them deliberately; they bring white cloth and dye it; then a pavilion is set up in his house; they bring a hired slave-girl who weeps with a sorrowful eye and seeks her tears for their dirhams. Whoever calls her, she weeps for him for a fixed fee. She entertains their living in their homes and harms their dead in their graves, depriving them of their reward by what they pay her. What can the wailing woman say? She says: \"O people, I command you to what Allah forbade you. Allah, the Exalted, commanded you to be patient, and I forbid you to be patient. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, forbade you from despair, and I command you to despair.\" So it is said: \"Acknowledge her right.\" Then cool drink is prepared for her, she is clothed, and she is mounted on animals. Indeed, to Allah we belong and to Him we return. I never thought I would be in a community where such things happen.'"],[1221,"He is not one of us who shaves, wails, or tears his clothes."],[1222,"Wailing women will have upon them garments of tar."],[1223,"Any wailing woman who dies before repenting, Allah will clothe her in a garment of fire and make her stand before the people on the Day of Resurrection."],[1224,"I was at a funeral where there was a woman wailing. He kept repelling her, but she paid no attention. Ibn 'Umar ؓ said: 'O Mujahid, we seek the reward, while she seeks the sin.'"],[1226,"When the deceased was brought and placed before him, he would face them and say: 'You have come as intercessors, so intercede for him, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A hundred men are an ummah, and an ummah will not gather sincerely supplicating for their deceased but that Allah grants them his sins and forgives them.'"],[1227,"Ibn Abbas ؓ stood to pray over a funeral. He said the takbir, then began the Opening of the Book (al-Fatihah), raising his voice with it. Then he prayed upon the Prophet ﷺ and said the takbir, and sincerely supplicated for the deceased. Then he said the takbir and supplicated for the believing men and women. Then he turned to the people and said: 'O people, by Allah, I did not raise my voice with the recitation except so that you may know that it is a sunnah.'"],[1228,"He would say in the prayer over the deceased: 'O Allah, forgive him, bless him, and bring him to the cistern of Your Messenger.'"],[1229,"We used to say in the prayer over the deceased: 'O Allah, You are our Lord and his Lord. You created him and provided for him. You gave him life and sufficed him. Forgive us and him, and do not deprive us of his reward, and do not lead us astray after him.'"],[1230,"Yahya narrated to us, from Yahya b. Sa'id, from Sa'id b. Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah."],[1231,"When he prayed over a funeral he would say: 'O Allah, Your servant and the son of Your servant, he used to testify that there is no god but You...' and he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[1233,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a sermon... and he mentioned the hadith, in which there is: 'Whoever prays over a deceased, Jibril (peace and blessings be upon him) prays over him, and with him are seventy thousand angels, and his past sins are forgiven. If he remains until he is buried and casts dust upon him, he returns with a qirat of reward for every step until he returns to his home, and the qirat is like Uhud. Whoever digs a grave for a Muslim, Allah Almighty forbids him from the Fire and grants him a house in Paradise which, if placed between Sana'a and Abyssinia, would contain them.'"],[1235,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit the poor of Madinah... and he mentioned the hadith, in which there is: 'So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked to her grave, prayed over her, and said the takbir four times.'"],[1236,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over his son Ibrahim and said the takbir over him four times."],[1237,"The last takbir the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said over funerals was four. Abu Bakr ؓ said the takbir over Fatimah ؓ four times. Al-Hasan said the takbir over Ali ؓ four times. Al-Husayn said the takbir over Al-Hasan ؓ four times. Ali ؓ said the takbir over Yazid al-Mukaffaf four times. Abdullah b. Umar said the takbir over his father ؓ four times. The angels said the takbir over Adam (peace be upon them) four times. Ibn al-Hanafiyyah said the takbir over Ibn Abbas ؓ in Ta'if four times."],[1238,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbir over a funeral five times."],[1240,"I prayed with Uthman ؓ at the funeral of men and women, and he placed the men next to him and the women next to the qiblah, and he said four takbirs."],[1241,"He used to place the men behind the women, and the women next to him."],[1242,"When the funeral is present and the ruler is present, the ruler has more right to pray over it."],[1243,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over the mother of so-and-so who died in childbirth, and he stood at her middle."],[1246,"Ibn Umar ؓ prayed over a newborn in the house, then it was taken and buried. I said to Nafi': Had it cried? He said: I do not know."],[1247,"He witnessed Ibn Umar ؓ at a funeral, and people began whispering: He is the son of adultery. So-and-so said: It is said: He is the worst of the three. That reached Ibn Umar ؓ, and he said: No, he is the best of the three."],[1248,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over a woman who died in childbirth from adultery, and over her child."],[1250,"Al-Bara' b. Ma'rur ؓ died before the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah. When he arrived, he prayed over him."],[1251,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a new grave and said: What is this grave? They said: The grave of so-and-so. He ﷺ said: Why did you not inform me? They said: You were sleeping, and we disliked waking you. He ﷺ said: Do not do that; call me for your funerals. Then he arranged a row over her."],[1252,"A woman used to pick up reeds and dirt from the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by her grave and prayed over her."],[1253,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit the poor of Madinah and attend their funerals when they died. He said: A woman from the people of al-Awali died. He ﷺ said: When she is present, inform me. He said: They came to him to inform him of her, but found him sleeping and the night had gone, so they disliked waking him and feared for him the darkness of the night and the creatures of the earth, so they buried her. When morning came, he ﷺ asked about her, and they told him that. He ﷺ walked to her grave, prayed over her, and said four takbirs."],[1255,"The likeness of one who reviles the dead is like one who stands on the brink of destruction, and the likeness of one who sits on the bed of a woman whose husband is absent is like one whose anus lets out wind on the Day of Resurrection."],[1256,"A funeral of a man from the Anṣār was brought past the Prophet ﷺ, and he was praised with good, so he said: “It has become due.” Then another funeral was brought past him and it was praised with less than that, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It has become due.” It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, what has become due?” He ﷺ said: “The angels are the witnesses of Allah in the heaven, and you are the witnesses of Allah on the earth.”"],[1257,"There is no Muslim who dies and four people from the households of his closest neighbors testify that they know nothing but good from him, except that Allah, Exalted be He, says: “I have accepted your knowledge, and I have forgiven him for what you do not know.”"],[1259,"I met men from among those who met the Prophet ﷺ and Abū Bakr ؓ. When they came and found no place except to pray in the mosque, they turned back and did not pray."],[1261,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over the Najāshī."],[1262,"Your brother the Najāshī has died. Stand up and pray over him, or stand up and supplicate for him."],[1264,"When he professes Islam and then dies and funeral prayer has not been offered over him, funeral prayer should be offered over him."],[1265,"A young Jewish boy used to serve the Prophet ﷺ, and he fell ill, so he visited him. He said: “Do you testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?” The boy looked at his father, who said to him: “Say as Muḥammad says.” He said: So he accepted. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: “Pray over your companion.”"],[1266,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out for the funeral of a man from the Ansar. When he was placed, Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: O Messenger of God, do not pray over him, for he is a wicked man. The Messenger of God ﷺ turned and said: Did any of you see him doing any act of Islam? A man said: Yes, O Messenger of God, he stood guard with us one night in the way of God Almighty. So he prayed over him and threw soil upon him, and said: Your companions think that you are from the people of the Fire, and I bear witness that you are from the people of Paradise. Then he ﷺ said: O Umar, you will not be asked about people's deeds, but you will be asked about the prayer."],[1267,"A man died in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and some of them said: O Messenger of God, do not pray over him..."],[1269,"\"O Abu Dharr,\" and I said: \"At your service and gladly.\" He said: \"Have you prayed today?\" I said: \"No.\" He ﷺ said: \"Rise and pray,\" so I rose and prayed as long as Allah, the Exalted, willed, then I returned and sat. He ﷺ remained silent for a long time without speaking to me, so I said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has disliked my company.\" Then he ﷺ turned to me and said: \"O Abu Dharr.\" I said: \"At your service and gladly.\" He ﷺ said: \"Seek refuge in Allah from the evil of the devils of mankind and jinn.\" I said: \"May my father and mother be sacrificed for you; do humans have devils?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Does not Allah, Mighty and Majestic, say: 'Devils of mankind and jinn, inspiring one another'—the verse?\" Then he ﷺ turned to me and said: \"O Abu Dharr.\" I said: \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah.\" He ﷺ said: \"Shall I not teach you a phrase that is a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?\" I said: \"Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you.\" He ﷺ said: \"Say: 'There is no might nor power except with Allah.'\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ persisted in not speaking until that lasted long from him. So I initiated the speech and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you commanded me to pray; what is prayer?\" He ﷺ said: \"It is a good that is placed; whoever wishes takes little, and whoever wishes takes much.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is fasting?\" He ﷺ said: \"An obligatory duty that suffices.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is charity?\" He ﷺ said: \"Multiplied manifold, and with Allah is more.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best?\" He ﷺ said: \"Faith in Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and Jihad in the path of Allah, the Exalted.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which martyrs are best?\" He ﷺ said: \"One whose blood is spilled and whose horse is hamstrung.\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which slaves are best?\" He ﷺ said: \"The most expensive in price and the most precious to their owners.\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best?\" He ﷺ said: \"An effort from one of little means, and a secret to a poor person.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what if I do not find anything to give in charity?\" He ﷺ said: \"You help a weak person or you make something for an unskilled person.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what if I cannot?\" He ﷺ said: \"Then you restrain this—and he ﷺ pointed to his tongue—for it is a good charity a person gives on behalf of himself.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which verse revealed to you of the Quran is greatest?\" He ﷺ said: \"The Verse of the Throne. And do you know what the likeness of the heavens and the earth is in relation to the Throne?\" I said: \"No, unless you teach me from what Allah, the Exalted, has taught you.\" He ﷺ said: \"The likeness of the heavens and the earth in the Throne is but like a ring cast in a desert, and the excellence of the Throne over the heavens and the earth is like the excellence of the desert over that ring.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how many were the prophets (peace be upon them)?\" He ﷺ said: \"They were one hundred twenty-four thousand.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, were all of them messengers?\" He ﷺ said: \"No, the messengers among them were three hundred fifteen men.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which of them was first?\" He ﷺ said: \"Adam ﷺ .\" I said: \"Was Adam a prophet?\" He ﷺ said: \"Yes; Allah formed his clay, created him with His hand, breathed into him of His spirit, and spoke to him directly.\" Then the people became many around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Shall I not inform you of the most miserly of people?\" I said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He ﷺ said: \"One in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not send blessings upon me ﷺ.\""],[1271,"This is a document that the Messenger of God ﷺ wrote for Amr b. Hazm regarding the obligatory dues of camels and sheep: For sheep, when they reach forty, one sheep; until they reach one hundred and twenty. If they exceed one hundred and twenty, then two sheep; until they reach two hundred. If they exceed two hundred, then three sheep; until they reach three hundred. If they exceed three hundred and are more than that, one sheep is counted for every hundred. For camels: in twenty-five, a bint makhad (a one-year-old female camel); if not found, then an ibn labun (a two-year-old male camel). When they reach thirty-six, then a bint labun (a two-year-old female camel). When they reach forty-six, then a hiqqah (a three-year-old female camel); until they reach sixty. Then a jadha'ah (a four-year-old female camel); until they reach seventy-five. Then two bint labun; until they reach ninety. If they exceed, then two hiqqah; up to one hundred and twenty. Then it returns to being counted from the first obligatory due of camels, a sheep; until they reach one hundred and twenty. If they are numerous, then in every fifty a hiqqah."],[1272,"He read the document of Umar ؓ: There is nothing on less than five camels...."],[1274,"There is nothing on less than five camels, nothing on less than forty sheep, nothing on less than thirty cattle, nothing on less than twenty mithqals, nothing on less than two hundred dirhams, nothing on less than five awsuq. The tenth is on dates, raisins, wheat, and barley. Whatever is irrigated by flowing water, on it is the tenth; and whatever is irrigated by bucket, on it is half the tenth."],[1275,"He imposed zakat on gold, silver, camels, cattle, sheep, wheat, barley, sult (a kind of barley), and raisins."],[1276,"He took from every ten cattle one sheep."],[1278,"He gave Jabir ؓ a sum that was owed to him by the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: And I give you more: there is no zakat on it until a year has passed over it."],[1279,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ, when he gave a man a grant, would say: Do you have wealth? If he said yes, he would say: Pay its zakat. If he had no wealth, he would say: Do not pay zakat on it—meaning the grant—until a year has passed over it."],[1281,"The people of Syria said to Umar ؓ: The best of our wealth is horses and slaves. So Umar ؓ took ten for every horse and ten for every head, and he provided for their sustenance. For he used to give them more than he took from them. Then these—meaning the officials of the Umayyads—took ten per head and ten per horse, and did not provide sustenance."],[1282,"I asked Sa'id b. al-Musayyab about draft horses: Is there charity on them? Sa'id said: There is no charity on any horses."],[1284,"There is no zakat on one who lends money."],[1285,"This is the month of your zakat. Whoever has a debt, let him repay it, then leave what remains."],[1287,"By Allah, if they withheld from me even a hobble that the Prophet ﷺ used to take from them, I would fight them over it. He used to take a hobble along with the camel. Then he recited: 'Muhammad is but a messenger; messengers have passed away before him.'"],[1288,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ consulted Ali ؓ about the apostates. He said: 'Allah, exalted is He, has joined prayer and zakat, and I do not think they should be separated.' At that, Abu Bakr ؓ said..."],[1290,"Umar ؓ passed by a flock of zakat sheep, among them a ewe with a large udder. He said: 'I do not think the owners gave this willingly. Do not take the best of the Muslims' wealth. Do not tempt people. Avoid taking food (as zakat).'"],[1291,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a fine she-camel among the zakat camels and said: 'May Allah fight him!' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I redeemed it with two camels from the fringes of the herd.' He said: 'Yes, then.'"],[1292,"He sat with me while I was in the mosque of Basra in the time of al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf al-Thaqafi, holding a staff and a document in his hand. He said: 'O Abdullah, do you think this document will benefit me with this governor of yours?' I said: 'What is this document?' He said: 'A document that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote for us.' I said: 'How did he write it for you?' He said: 'I entered Madinah with my father...' and he mentioned the hadith... 'My father said to Talha: Get us a document from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stating that we will not be transgressed against in our zakat. He said: That is for every Muslim. We said: Even so. So he walked with us and said: O Messenger of Allah, these two have chosen that you write for them that they will not be transgressed against in their zakat. He said: That is for every Muslim. He said: O Messenger of Allah, they have chosen to have a document from you. So he wrote this document for us. Do you think it will benefit me with this governor of yours? For by Allah, we have been transgressed against in our zakat.' He said: 'I said: I do not think so, by Allah.'"],[1294,"A despised caravan will come to you. When they come, welcome them and leave them to what they seek. If they act justly, it is for themselves; if they wrong, it is upon them. Satisfy them, for the completion of your zakat is their satisfaction, and let them pray for you."],[1295,"A man from Banu Tamim came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is Allah sufficient for me if I pay the zakat to your messenger, and I am absolved of it before Allah, exalted is He, and His Messenger?' He ﷺ said: 'If you pay it to my messenger, you are absolved of it, and you have its reward, and its sin is upon the one who changes it.'"],[1296,"I said to Abu Hurayrah ؓ: 'Should I pay the best of my wealth as zakat?' He said: 'No. If they come, do not disobey them; if they turn away, do not greet them, lest you be disobedient without being wronged. Say: below the right, take the right, and leave falsehood. If he takes that, then that is it; if he goes beyond to other than it, be patient. Allah, exalted is He, will gather for you on the Day of Resurrection in the balance.'"],[1298,"He used to pay in advance the zakat of al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib for two years."],[1300,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Muadh ؓ to Yemen, and he used to take garments as zakat for wheat and barley."],[1302,"I said to al-Abbas ؓ: 'Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to appoint you over the zakat.' He asked him, and he ﷺ said: 'We would not appoint you over the washing of people's sins.'"],[1303,"The Banu Abdul-Muttalib walked to al-Abbas ؓ and said: Speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for us, so that he may assign to us what he assigns to the people of this si'aya and other than it. While they were thus conferring, Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ came, and al-Abbas ؓ called him and said: Your people and the sons of your uncle have gathered, would you speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for them so that he may assign them the si'aya? Ali ؓ said: Allah, Most High, has refused for you, O Banu Abdul-Muttalib, to feed you the filth of people's hands. Rabi'a b. al-Harith said: Leave this one, for you will have no good from him."],[1304,"Nawfal b. al-Harith sent his two sons to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and said to them: Go to your uncle, perhaps he will appoint you over the sadaqat, so that you may obtain something and get married. They met Ali ؓ and he said: Where are you heading? They told him of their need. He said to them: Go back. So they went back. When evening came, their father ordered them to go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When they were shown to the door, they asked permission, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Aisha ؓ: Let down your curtain; admit to me the two sons of my uncle. They told the Prophet of Allah ﷺ of their need, and the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to them: Nothing of the sadaqat is lawful for you, O Ahl al-Bayt. It is the washing of hands. You have a fifth (khums), and in the fifth is what suffices you, or enriches you."],[1305,"Rushayd narrated to me. Ibn Mandah and Ibn al-Sakan both narrated it from al-Barudi with it. Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Tarikh from Abu Nu'aym with it."],[1306,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Arqam b. Abi Arqam over some sadaqa. He passed by Abu Rafi' and asked him to follow him, so he came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He ﷺ said: O Abu Rafi', indeed sadaqa is forbidden for Muhammad and the family of Muhammad. And the mawla of a people is from them, or from themselves."],[1307,"I came to Umm Kulthum, meaning the daughter of Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, and entered upon her. In the house there was a bed woven with palm fiber, a cushion, and a hanging water-skin. I began to look, and she said: What are you looking at? Indeed, we are in good from Allah. If we had nothing but the sadaqa of the Prophet ﷺ or of Ali ؓ, we would have sufficiency in that. He said: I said: Are there dirhams that Salman ؓ bequeathed to a mawla of his called Ruqayya? She said: I do not know her. I said to her: Take it. She said: I fear it may be sadaqa, and sadaqa is not lawful for us. But go and give it as sadaqa yourself. I said to her: Rather, you give it as sadaqa. She refused, then said: Last night a purse came from Iraq and I returned it, refusing to accept it."],[1309,"Indeed, when Abu Musa and Mu'adh ؓ were sent to Yemen to teach the people their religion, they did not take sadaqa except from these four: wheat, barley, dates, and raisins."],[1310,"Whatever is ba'l (rain-fed), or sayl (flood-irrigated), or 'athari (naturally irrigated), then for every ten one; and whatever is by nadh (artificial irrigation), then for every twenty one."],[1312,"Umar ؓ said to me: Pay zakat on your wealth. I said: It is only hides and quivers. He said: Assess its value, then pay its sadaqa."],[1314,"From Asma', that she used not to pay zakat on jewelry."],[1315,"The wife of Ibn Mas'ud said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have jewelry, and in my care are orphans. Should I not assign the zakat of my jewelry to them?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[1317,"A camel from the charity passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he took a hair from the back of a camel and said: 'I am no more entitled to this hair than any man among the Muslims.'"],[1319,"Umar ؓ sent him to estimate the dates, and he said: 'When you come upon a land, estimate it, and leave for them the amount they eat.'"],[1320,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man to a people and he estimated their palm trees, so they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'So-and-so came to us and estimated our palm trees.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I sent him, and in my soul he is trustworthy. If you wish, take what he estimated for you, and if you wish, we will take it and return it to you.' They said: 'This is the truth, and by the truth the heavens and the earth stand.'"],[1322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade harvesting at night and cutting palm dates at night."],[1324,"When Allah Almighty gives you good, then begin with those you support, and give from the surplus, and you will not be blamed for sufficiency, and do not fail yourself."],[1325,"I saw Abu Hurayrah ؓ circumambulating this House, calling out: 'No charity except from the surplus of one's family.'"],[1327,"There is nothing that brings you closer to Paradise and distances you from the Fire except that I have commanded you with it, and there is nothing that distances you from Paradise and brings you closer to the Fire except that I have forbidden you from it. And the Trustworthy Spirit breathed into my heart that no soul dies except that Allah Almighty has written its provision, so fear Allah and be moderate in seeking provision, and let not the delay of provision drive you to seek it by disobedience, for what is with Allah Almighty is only attained through obedience to Him."],[1328,"A man from among you comes to me and asks me, and I give him, so he departs carrying nothing in his lap but fire."],[1329,"God sends down provision according to the need, and He sends down patience according to the trial."],[1330,"God, exalted be He, gives His servant what He has decreed for him of provision, so be moderate in seeking. Take what is lawful and leave what is forbidden."],[1332,"He advised his sons at his death: I enjoin you to fear God ... and he mentioned the hadith, in which: And beware of begging, for it is the last earning of a man."],[1333,"Charity never mixes with wealth except that it destroys it."],[1335,"He came seeking permission to enter upon Uthman ؓ, so Uthman ؓ said: Do not give him permission. He sought permission, so Kab said: Give him permission, may God rectify you. So he gave him permission, and in his hand was a staff. Uthman ؓ said: O Kab, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Awf ؓ, has died and left wealth. What do you think? He said: He used to fulfill the right of God in it, so there is no harm upon him. Abu Dharr ؓ raised his staff and struck Kab, and said: You have lied. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: I would not love to have this mountain as gold, spending it and having it accepted from me, leaving nothing of it behind me. And I adjure you by God, O Uthman, did you hear? Three times. He said: Yes. He said: O Kab, enough. He said: I find in the Torah what I told you; God, Mighty and Majestic, said: God erases what He wills ... to the end of the verse. He said: Indeed God, Mighty and Majestic, erased it. He said: I seek forgiveness from God, exalted be He."],[1337,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave Hakim b. Hizam less than what he gave his companions, so Hakim said: O Messenger of God, I did not think I would be given less than anyone among the people. So he increased him, then he asked for more, so he increased him until he was satisfied. He said: O Messenger of God, which of your gifts is best? He said ﷺ: The first ... and he mentioned the hadith."],[1338,"For one of you to take his ropes, go to the mountain, gather a bundle of firewood, place it on his back, bring it to the market and sell it, and eat from its price is better for him than coming to a man and asking him, whether he gives him or refuses him ... the hadith."],[1339,"A man from Judham narrated to me, from a man among them called 'Adi, that there was a dispute between him and two wives of his. He threw a stone at one of them and killed her. He rode to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was in Tabuk and asked him about the affair of the slain woman. He said: \"Pay her blood money to her heir.\" 'Adi ؓ said: \"It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of God ﷺ on a red, crop-eared she-camel of his. He said: 'O people, know that there are three hands: the hand of God Most High is the highest, the hand of the giver is the middle, and the hand of the one given is the lowest. So abstain (from asking), even by bundles of firewood.' Then he raised his hands and said: 'O God, have I conveyed?'\""],[1340,"Charity is not lawful for a rich person, nor for one who is strong and able-bodied."],[1341,"Indeed, one of you comes to me and asks me, and I give him, then he departs carrying nothing in his lap but fire."],[1342,"Charity is not lawful for one who possesses fifty dirhams or its equivalent in gold."],[1343,"Whoever asks without being poor, it is as if he is gnawing on live coals."],[1344,"She said to her daughters: \"Give charity and do not wait for surplus, for if you wait for surplus you will not find it, but if you give charity you will not miss its loss.\""],[1346,"Their sa' on that day was a mudd and a third of a mudd."],[1347,"We used to pay zakat al-fitr during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ with the mudd by which they used to trade."],[1348,"The uqiyyah is forty, the nashsh is twenty, and the nawah is five."],[1350,"Umar ؓ came to al-Jabiyah, the Jabiyah of Damascus, and stood as a preacher. He mentioned the hadith until he said: \"Indeed, when I leave this place of mine, no one who has a right in charity should remain except that he comes to me.\" Only two men of those present came to him, so he ordered that they be given. A man stood and said: \"May God keep the Commander of the Believers righteous. This rich man who checks on others is not more entitled to charity than this poor man who abstains.\" Umar ؓ said: \"Woe to you! How can we reach those?\""],[1352,"A man asked Umar ؓ about his camels, and he mentioned their leanness and sores. Umar ؓ said: \"I think they are big and fat.\" Then Umar ؓ passed by him while he was among his camels, driving them, and he was saying: \"Abu Hafs Umar swore by God, that there is no scab or sore on them. So forgive, O God, if he has acted wickedly.\" He said: Umar ؓ said: \"What is this?\" He said: \"The Commander of the Believers asked me about my camels, and I told him about them, and he claimed that he thinks they are big and fat, while they are as you see.\" He said: \"I am the Commander of the Believers, Umar. Come to me in such-and-such a place.\" So he came to him, and he ordered that they be seized, and he gave him in their place from the camels of charity."],[1354,"No servant is honored by God Most High except that trial increases upon him in severity. No servant gives charity from his wealth but it decreases, nor withholds it but it increases his wealth. No thief steals except that it is counted against his provision."],[1357,"She used to give zakat al-fitr on behalf of those of her family who died: the young, the old, the present, and the absent."],[1359,"He stood and delivered a sermon—as if he meant the Prophet ﷺ—and said: \"The owners of the purses have perished, and I do not grieve for them, but for those upon whom you pray.\" He had hardly descended when they were afraid to ask him, so they said: \"Who do you think he meant?\" They said: \"We think he meant a people who will come after us, who hoard these wealth and shed blood over them.\""],[1360,"No people ever withheld zakat but Allah, Exalted is He, withheld rain from them."],[1361,"Whoever leaves behind a treasure, it will be made into a bald male serpent on the Day of Resurrection with two venom glands, following him and saying: \"Who are you?\" He says: \"I am your treasure that you left behind.\" It will not cease following him until it makes him swallow his hand, and it will bite it off, then it will follow the rest of his body."],[1363,"It was mentioned to me that deeds will boast to one another, and charity will say: \"I am the best of you.\" And Umar ؓ said: \"No Muslim gives a pair of anything from his wealth as charity except that the gatekeepers of Paradise rush to receive him.\""],[1364,"Abu Dharr ؓ sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ... and he mentioned the hadith similar to the previous hadith, in which: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is charity?\" He said: \"Multiplied many times over, and with Allah is more.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which is best?\" He ﷺ said: \"The effort of one with little, or a secret given to the poor.\""],[1365,"The charity of a Muslim increases one's lifespan, prevents an evil death, and Allah removes from him through it arrogance and pride."],[1366,"Charity and maintaining family ties—Allah, Exalted is He, increases one's lifespan through them, averts an evil death, and Allah repels through them what is disliked and feared."],[1367,"Whoever spends a pair of anything from his wealth in the way of Allah, Exalted is He, the gatekeepers of Paradise will call him from whichever of its gates he wishes."],[1368,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when I drew near him I heard him say: \"This is the chief of the desert dwellers.\" I greeted him, then sat down and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what wealth is there for which I will not be held accountable, from a guest who visits me or dependents if they become many?\" He ﷺ said: \"Excellent wealth is forty camels, and the most is sixty, and woe to the owners of hundreds, except one who gives in their milk, and their aid, and lends their backs for riding, and lends their stallion for breeding, and slaughters their fat ones, and feeds the contented beggar and the destitute.\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how noble and excellent are these traits! Is it not permissible in the valley where I am, because of the abundance of my camels?\" He said: \"How do you deal with the milch camel given as a gift?\" I said: \"I give a hundred as gifts every year.\" He said: \"How do you deal with lending?\" I said: \"The camels go out and the people go out, and whoever takes hold of a camel's head goes away with it.\" He said: \"How do you deal with lending camels for riding?\" I said: \"I lend young she-camels in milk and old ones past breeding.\" He said: \"Is that dearer to you, or the wealth of your master?\" I said: \"Rather my own wealth.\" He said: \"You have of your wealth only what you eat and consume, or wear and wear out, or give and spend; and what remains is for your master.\" I said: \"For my master?\" He said: \"Yes.\" I said: \"By Allah, if I remain, I will leave their number small.\" Al-Hasan said: \"And he did so.\""],[1369,"There is no morning except that a caller calls out from the sky: 'O Allah, give every spender a replacement, and every withholder ruin. O seeker of good, come forward; O seeker of evil, refrain.'"],[1370,"In the son of Adam there are three hundred and sixty joints, or bones, or joints—upon each one of them every day is a charity. He said: 'A good word a man speaks is charity, helping a man his brother with something is charity, a drink of water you give is charity, and removing harm from the road is charity.'"],[1371,"A man from Banu Tamim came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have abundant wealth and family and a town presence, so tell me how I should spend and what I should do.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Bring out the zakat from your wealth, for it is a purification that purifies you, and maintain ties with your relatives, and recognize the right of the beggar, the neighbor, and the poor, and give the near of kin his due...' the verse."],[1372,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: 'O 'A'ishah, spend and do not withhold, lest it be withheld from you.'"],[1373,"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date."],[1374,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the pulpit: 'Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date, for it straightens what is crooked, wards off an evil death, and falls from the hungry in the place it would from the full.'"],[1375,"That I give this ring of mine in charity to a poor person is more beloved to me than a thousand dirhams I gift to the House."],[1376,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'Something I heard from you, I doubted it.' He said: 'When one of you doubts a matter, let him ask me about it.' He said: 'Your saying about your wives: I hope for them after me the truthful ones.' He said: 'Whom do you mean by the truthful ones?' He said: 'We said: Our children who die young.' He said: 'No, but the truthful ones are the charitable ones.'"],[1377,"Indeed, a biting time will come upon you, when the believer clings to what is in his hand fearing to spend, and Allah Almighty says: 'And whatever you spend of anything, He will replace it, and He is the Best of Providers.'"],[1379,"O Messenger of Allah, command me with a charity. He ﷺ said: 'Give water to drink,' meaning water. Al-Hasan said: 'So he set up two drinking places between which I used to run while I was a boy.'"],[1380,"Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr ؓ died, so Aisha ؓ gave charity on his behalf with slaves that belonged to her."],[1381,"The Prophet ﷺ had nine wives, and one day he said: 'The best of you is the one with the longest hand.' So each one of them stood up and placed her hand on the wall. Then he ﷺ said: 'I do not mean this; rather, I mean the one among you who is most generous with her hand.'"],[1382,"The best charity is that given to a hostile relative."],[1383,"I was supporting the Prophet ﷺ against my chest when he said: 'Whoever gives charity seeking the pleasure of Allah, the Exalted, and is sealed with it, will enter Paradise.'"],[1384,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us and mentioned the hadith, in which there is: 'Whoever gives charity, Allah, the Exalted, will give him for the weight of every atom of it the like of Mount Uhud from the bliss of Paradise. And whoever carries it to a needy person will have the like of that. Even if forty thousand people pass it from hand to hand until it reaches the needy person, each one of them will have the like of that reward in full. And what is with Allah is better and more lasting for those who fear Allah and do good.'"],[1385,"No Muslim spends a pair of anything in the path of Allah, the Exalted, except that the angels come with sweet basil, vying with each other at the gates of Paradise, saying: 'O servant of Allah, O Muslim, this is better.'"],[1387,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we were as you know, and we have become in-laws with you, and Allah has placed good for us in our relationship by marriage with you. My mother has died. Will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf?' He said: 'If you were to give charity on her behalf with even the foot of a sheep, it would benefit her.'"],[1389,"Every good deed that one of you does for a rich or poor person is charity."],[1390,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: 'Which of people is the best?' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, a man who gives his wealth and his life.' He ﷺ said: 'What a good man this is, but it is not him. Rather, the best of people is a man who gives his utmost effort.'"],[1391,"All creation are the dependents of Allah, the Exalted, so the most beloved of them to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is the one who is most beneficial to His dependents."],[1392,"Whoever walks to fulfill the need of his Muslim brother, Allah Almighty records for him for every step he takes a good deed until he returns from where he left him. If his need is fulfilled, he comes out of his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him, and if he dies in the meantime, he enters Paradise without reckoning."],[1393,"Whoever helps his brother in his need and is kind to him, it is incumbent upon Allah Almighty to serve him from the servants of Paradise."],[1394,"Whoever relieves a distressed person, Allah Almighty records for him seventy-three good deeds, one of which Allah Almighty uses to set right for him his affairs of this world and the Hereafter, and seventy-two are in degrees [of reward]."],[1395,"The one who guides to good is like the doer of it, and Allah Almighty loves relieving the distressed."],[1396,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'Who is the best of people?' He ﷺ said: 'The most beneficial of them to people.'"],[1397,"Allah Almighty remains in the servant's need as long as the servant is in his brother's need."],[1399,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has a palm tree in my garden. Order him to sell it to me or give it to me.' He said: The man came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said: 'Do so, and you will have a palm tree in Paradise for it.' But he refused. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: 'This is the most miserly of people.'"],[1401,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for something which was not easy [to give], so she said: 'O Messenger of Allah, promise me.' He ﷺ said: 'A promise is a gift.'"],[1403,"I went with a companion of mine to Salman ؓ. He brought bread and salt. My companion said: 'If only there were thyme in our salt.' So Salman ؓ sent his water-skin [as collateral] and brought thyme. When we had eaten, my companion said: 'Praise be to Allah who has made us content with what He has provided us.' Salman ؓ said: 'If you had been content, my water-skin would not have been pawned.'"],[1406,"The month is twenty-nine [days]."],[1408,"Abd Allah b. Yazid addressed the people at the pilgrimage season and said: 'O people, we have witnessed the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ and heard from them, and they narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Fast at the sighting of the new moon, and break your fast at its sighting. If it is obscured from you, then complete the number as thirty days. If two just witnesses testify, then fast at their sighting and break your fast for it, and refrain [from eating] for it.'"],[1409,"They said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'Will you not go forward and add a day or two?' The Prophet ﷺ became angry."],[1410,"The sunnah is that on the night when the crescent of Ramadan is looked for, for the fasting or for the breaking of the fast, the adhan for the Maghrib prayer is called at its time, then the iqamah is delayed until the crescent is seen or it is despaired of, and some stars appear."],[1411,"Two months do not complete sixty days."],[1412,"The month is thirty, and the month is twenty-nine."],[1413,"The month is twenty-nine."],[1414,"I informed 'A'ishah ؓ that Ibn 'Umar ؓ says: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The month is twenty-nine.' She denied that and said: 'May Allah forgive Abu 'Abd al-Rahman. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not say that, but he said: The month may be twenty-nine.'"],[1415,"If the crescent sets before the twilight, then it is for its night; and if it sets after the twilight, then it is for two nights."],[1416,"When the Prophet ﷺ saw the crescent, he would say: 'I believe in Allah who created you' - three times."],[1417,"Two Bedouins testified before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that they had seen the crescent yesterday for breaking the fast, or for the sacrifice, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted their testimony."],[1418,"I was supporting the Prophet ﷺ against my chest, and he said: 'Whoever fasts a day seeking the Face of Allah, the Exalted, and it is sealed for him with it, he will enter Paradise.'"],[1419,"Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah will be distanced from the Fire by a distance of one hundred years' journey."],[1420,"Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, Allah will place between him and the Fire a trench whose width is like that between the heaven and the earth."],[1421,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ, when he turned to Usama b. Zayd ؓ, say: \"O Usama, upon you is the path to Paradise, and beware of being diverted from it.\" He said: \"O Messenger of God, what is the quickest way to traverse that path?\" He ﷺ said: \"Thirst in the midday heat, and restraining the self from the pleasure of women. O Usama, upon you is fasting, for it draws one near to God, Mighty and Majestic. Nothing is more loved by God Most High than the breath of a fasting person, who has left food and drink for the sake of God Most High. If you are able for death to come to you while your belly is hungry and your liver is thirsty, then do so; for by that you will attain the nobility of the station in the Hereafter, and you will dwell with the prophets, and your spirit will rejoice at coming upon them, and the Compeller will bless you.\" [Then he mentioned the rest of the hadith, and in it:] \"And know, O Usama, that the closest of people to God Most High on the Day of Resurrection is the one whose grief, thirst, and hunger in this world are most prolonged.\""],[1422,"If a man fasts one day voluntarily and then is given the earth's fill of gold, he would not receive the full reward of that fast until the Day of Reckoning."],[1423,"Whoever fasts one day seeking the face of God Most High, God will distance him from Hell as far as a crow flies from when it is a fledgling until it dies of old age."],[1424,"Whoever fasts one day in the way of God Most High voluntarily outside Ramadan will be distanced from the Fire by a hundred years' journey of a well-trained, swift horse."],[1425,"Everything has a door, and the door of worship is fasting."],[1427,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us on the last day of Sha'ban and said: \"O people, a blessed month has overshadowed you, in which there is a night better than a thousand months. God has made its fasting obligatory and its night prayer voluntary. Whoever performs a virtuous act voluntarily in it is like one who performs an obligatory act in other months, and whoever performs an obligatory act in it is like one who performs seventy obligatory acts. It is the month of patience, and the reward of patience is Paradise. It is the month of consolation. It is a month in which the believer's provision is increased. Whoever provides iftar to a fasting person in it will have the reward of freeing a slave and forgiveness of his sins.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of God, not all of us find what we can provide to break a fast.\" He ﷺ said: \"God Most High gives this reward to whoever provides iftar to a fasting person with a sip of milk, a date, or a drink of water. And whoever satiates a fasting person will have forgiveness of his sins, and God, Mighty and Majestic, will give him a drink from my basin such that he will never thirst until he enters Paradise. He will have the like of the fasting person's reward without diminishing the fasting person's reward in any way. It is a month whose beginning is mercy, its middle forgiveness, and its end liberation from the Fire. And whoever lightens the burden of his servant in it, God will liberate him from the Fire.\""],[1428,"This month of Ramadan has come; the gates of heaven are opened in it, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained. Whoever reaches Ramadan and is not forgiven in it, then when will he be forgiven?"],[1429,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said when Ramadan approached: \"Glory be to God! What are you about to face?\" or \"What is the person about to face?\" three times. Umar ؓ said: \"O Messenger of God, has revelation come down?\" He ﷺ said: \"No.\" He ؓ said: \"Has an enemy appeared?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Then what is it?\" He ﷺ said: \"God Most High forgives all the people of the Qibla on the first night of the month of Ramadan.\" Then he looked at a man sitting before him who was shaking his head and saying: \"Excellent! Excellent!\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"It is as if your chest is troubled.\" He said: \"No, but I remembered the hypocrites.\" He ﷺ said: \"The hypocrite is the disbeliever, and the disbeliever has no share of that.\""],[1430,"My community has been given five characteristics in Ramadan that were not given to any community before them: the bad breath of a fasting person is more fragrant to God than the scent of musk; the angels seek forgiveness for them until they break their fast; God beautifies His Paradise every day and then says: \"My fasting servants are about to cast off their burden and harm and come to you\"; the rebellious devils are chained in it so they cannot reach what they reach in other months; and they are forgiven on the last night. It was said: \"O Messenger of God, is it the Night of Decree?\" He ﷺ said: \"No, but the worker is only given his full wage when he finishes his work.\""],[1431,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say when the month of Ramadan had begun: \"If the servants knew what is in Ramadan, my community would wish that the whole year were Ramadan.\" A man from Khuza'ah said: \"Tell us about it.\" He ﷺ said: \"Paradise is adorned for Ramadan from the beginning of the year to the beginning of the year, until when the first day of Ramadan comes, a wind blows from beneath the Throne and rustles the leaves of Paradise. The houris with large eyes look at that and say: 'O Lord, grant us husbands from Your servants in this noble month who will be a delight to our eyes and whose eyes will be delighted by us.' There is no servant who fasts Ramadan except that he is married to a wife from the houris with large eyes in a tent of hollow pearl, as God Most High described: 'Houris, restrained in pavilions.' Each of them has seventy garments, no garment the same color as another, and she is given seventy kinds of perfume, no kind with the scent of another. Each of them has seventy couches of red ruby adorned with pearls, on each couch seventy beds with linings of brocade, and above the seventy beds seventy canopied couches. Each woman has a thousand maidservants for her needs and a thousand manservants, with each manservant a platter of gold containing a kind of food, the last morsel of which gives a pleasure not found in the first. Her husband is given the like of that on a couch of red ruby, upon him two bracelets of gold adorned with red ruby. This is for each day of Ramadan, besides the good deeds he has done.\""],[1432,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us, and he mentioned the hadith, and in it: \"Whoever fasts Ramadan and refrains from backbiting, talebearing, lying, and engaging in falsehood, and holds his tongue except for the remembrance of God Most High, and restrains his hearing, sight, and all his limbs from the prohibitions of God Most High and from harming Muslims, he will have such nearness to God Most High that his knee will touch the knee of Abraham, the Friend.\""],[1434,"Whoever resolves to fast during the night should fast, and whoever enters the morning without having resolved to fast should not fast."],[1435,"The Prophet ﷺ would come and ask for food but not find any, so he would make the fast obligatory. She said: Sometimes he came while fasting and I had something special, so we would say: O Messenger of God, if only you were not fasting we would feed you. Then he would ask for it and eat ﷺ."],[1436,"I heard a man ask Anas b. Malik ؓ: I ate the pre-dawn meal, then it occurred to me to break my fast? He said: Break your fast. Then he said: Abu Talhah ؓ used to come to his family and say: Do you have anything? If they said no, he would say: Then I am fasting."],[1437,"Abu al-Darda' ؓ used to come to them after dawn and ask them for breakfast, and would not find it, so he would say: Then I am fasting."],[1438,"Keep fasting pure, for fasting is not from food or drink, but fasting is from sins."],[1439,"Abu Hurayrah ؓ, when he fasted, would sit in the mosque and say: We keep our fasting pure."],[1440,"The easiest fasting is abandoning food and drink."],[1441,"If vomiting overcomes him, he has not broken his fast; if he vomits intentionally, he has broken his fast."],[1442,"The sky rained hail, and Abu Talhah ؓ said to us while we were boys: Hand me some of that hail, O Anas. So I handed it to him, and he began eating while fasting. I said: Are you not fasting? He said: Yes, but this is not food or drink; it is only a blessing from the sky with which we cleanse our stomachs. Anas ؓ said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him, and he said: Take from your uncle."],[1443,"And 'Abd al-Warith b. 'Abd al-Samad b. 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us: My father narrated to us with it."],[1444,"And al-Bazzar said: Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, and he mentioned it. :"],[1445,"Al-Bazzar narrated it from Hilal b. Yahya, from Abu 'Awanah, from Qatadah, from Anas ؓ, who said: I saw Abu Talhah ؓ, and he mentioned it as mawquf."],[1446,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to fast in summer. When fasting in summer, he would not pray Maghrib until I brought him fresh dates, and he would eat and drink, then stand and pray. In winter, I brought him dried dates, and he would eat and drink, then stand and pray."],[1447,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to like to break his fast on three dates, or on something that fire had not touched."],[1448,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when there were fresh dates, would not break his fast except on fresh dates; and when there were no fresh dates, he would not break his fast except on dry dates."],[1449,"He used to forbid continuous fasting and command hastening the breaking of the fast and delaying the pre-dawn meal."],[1450,"Hasten the breaking of the fast and delay the pre-dawn meal."],[1451,"There is no continuous fasting in the fast."],[1452,"And al-Yamān Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us, from Abū ʿAtīq, from Jābir ؓ, with it."],[1453,"The Prophet ﷺ used to fast continuously."],[1454,"There is no silence of a day until night, no continuous fasting in the fast, no adopting bedouin ways after the emigration, and no emigration after the conquest... the rest of the hadith."],[1455,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade continuous fasting, and this sister of mine fasts continuously, but I forbid her."],[1456,"A man asked ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ about making up Ramadan in the ten days of Dhū al-Ḥijjah. He said: I do not know what the exchange was between them, but he commanded him to make up Ramadan in the ten days of Dhū al-Ḥijjah. He said: Do not say that your father heard that from ʿUmar ؓ."],[1457,"Rāfiʿ b. Khadīj ؓ commanded her to make up Ramadan separately."],[1458,"The fast of the fasting person [is not broken by kohl]. 1267 1032 - Al-Harith said: Yahya b. Ishaq narrated to us, Sa'id b. Zayd narrated to us, from 'Amr b. Khalid, from Muhammad b. 'Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, from 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ."],[1459,"I waited for the Prophet ﷺ to come out to us in Ramadan, and he came out from the house of Umm Salamah ؓ having applied kohl, and his eyes ﷺ were filled with kohl."],[1461,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I am ruined.' He ﷺ said: 'What has ruined you?' He said: 'I had intercourse with my wife in Ramadan.' He said: 'A donkey carrying dates was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ordered that some of it be given to him, saying: 'Take this and give it in charity.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, there is no household between its two lava tracts poorer than mine.' He said: 'He ﷺ laughed until his molars showed, then said: 'Feed it to your family, and a day in place of a day, and seek forgiveness from Allah Almighty.' He said: 'I do not know whether in both of their hadiths or the hadith of one of them: a day in place of a day, and seek forgiveness from Allah Almighty.'"],[1462,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I broke the fast on a day in Ramadan.' He said: 'Give charity for what you have done, fast a day in its place, and seek forgiveness from Allah Almighty.'"],[1463,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I broke the fast on a day in Ramadan.' He said: 'Without excuse or travel?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What an evil thing you have done.' He said: 'What do you command me?' He said: 'Free a slave.' He said: 'By the One who sent you with the truth, I have never owned a slave.' He said: 'Then fast two consecutive months.' He said: 'I am not able to do that.' He said: 'Then feed sixty poor people.' He said: 'By the One who sent you with the truth, I cannot even satisfy my own family.' He said: 'A basket of dates was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Give this in charity to sixty poor people.' He said: 'To whom should I give it?' He said: 'To the poorest person you know.' He said: 'By the One who sent you with the truth, there is no household between its two lava fields more needy than us.' So he ﷺ said: 'Give it in charity to your dependents.'"],[1464,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled in Ramadan, and he fasted and broke his fast."],[1465,"I returned with a companion of mine from 'Umrah, and we arrived at the new moon, the crescent of Ramadan, so we stopped in the land of Abu Hurayrah ؓ on a severely hot day, and we woke up not fasting except for one man among us. Abu Hurayrah ؓ entered upon us in the middle of the day and found our companion seeking the shade of the palm trees, so he said: 'What is the matter with your companion?' They said: 'He is fasting.' He said: 'What prevented him from breaking his fast? Allah has granted him a concession. If he had died, I would not have prayed over him.'"],[1466,"Breaking the fast while traveling is a duty."],[1467,"He used to fast while traveling and break his fast."],[1468,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent two men on an errand in Ramadan, and he instructed one of them not to fast, and was silent about the other, so he fasted. When they returned, he said: 'What did you do?' One of them said: 'I fasted,' and the other said: 'I did not fast.' He ﷺ said: 'Both of you have done right.'"],[1469,"We besieged Tustar with Abu Musa ؓ over us, and he fasted and we fasted."],[1470,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ came to a people besieging a fortress and ordered them to break the fast."],[1471,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of the conquest of Makkah, 'Break your fast; it is a day of fighting.'"],[1472,"Ibn Umar ؓ went out hurrying to avoid the turmoil that might occur in Madinah during Ramadan, so he broke the fast. Then, on the night he was to enter Makkah, the next morning he was fasting."],[1473,"Anas ؓ became too weak to fast, so he made a large bowl of tharid and invited thirty poor people and fed them."],[1474,"The pregnant and the nursing woman, if they fear [for themselves or their children], break the fast and feed [the poor], and they do not have to make up the fast."],[1475,"I never saw Abdullah fasting except for the month of Ramadan and two days."],[1476,"I asked Ata about a man who deliberately chooses a day to fast. He said: Ibn Abbas ؓ disliked singling out a month or a day to fast, and he used to say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever fasts perpetually, he has not fasted.'"],[1477,"He disliked fixing a specific day to fast."],[1478,"And he disliked fasting on Mondays and Thursdays."],[1479,"I entered upon al-Ashari ؓ on Friday while he was having lunch, and he invited me. I said, 'I am fasting.' He said, 'Do not fast on a day you make its fast obligatory upon yourself.'"],[1480,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from singling out Friday for fasting and from cupping while fasting... the rest of the hadith."],[1481,"Partake of the pre-dawn meal; for indeed in the suhur there is blessing."],[1482,"Partake of the pre-dawn meal, even if with a grain of sand from the earth."],[1483,"You must take the pre-dawn meal, for it is the blessed meal; and delay it as much as you can, and make the pre-dawn meal even if with a gulp of water."],[1484,"Sometimes the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say to me: 'Bring your blessed pre-dawn meal,' and sometimes it would be nothing but two dates."],[1485,"The congregation is a blessing, tharid is a blessing, and the pre-dawn meal is a blessing; take the pre-dawn meal, for it increases strength and it is from the Sunnah. Take the pre-dawn meal even if with a gulp of water—or upon a gulp of water— take the pre-dawn meal; may Allah's blessings be upon those who take the pre-dawn meal."],[1486,"Alqamah b. Ulathah was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Bilal ؓ came to call him to prayer. He ﷺ said: 'Gently, O Bilal, Alqamah is taking his pre-dawn meal.' He said: 'And he was taking his pre-dawn meal with a head.'"],[1487,"While the Prophet ﷺ was taking his pre-dawn meal, and when he finished his suhur, Alqamah b. Ulathah came, and the Prophet ﷺ called for a head. While he was eating, Bilal ؓ came."],[1488,"I came to the mosque and entered, and I leaned my back against the chamber of the Prophet ﷺ, and there was the Prophet ﷺ taking his pre-dawn meal. I cleared my throat, and he ﷺ said: 'Abu Yahya, come to the meal.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I intend to fast.' He ﷺ said: 'And I intend to fast, but this mu'adhdhin of ours has poor eyesight, or something in his eyesight, for he gave the call to prayer before dawn rose.'"],[1489,"Al-Hasan b. Sufyan said in his Musnad, and Mutayyan: Abu al-Sha'tha' Ali b. al-Hasan narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, with it. [3]:"],[1490,"1299 1058/3 - And al-Hasan also said, and al-Baghawi: Dawud b. Rushayd narrated to us, with it.:"],[1491,"Ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated it from Asim b. Ali, from Qays b. al-Rabi', from Ash'ath with it. And he named Abu Hubayrah Yahya b. Abbad."],[1492,"And Ibn Mandah said: Al-Hasan b. Mansur al-Imam informed us. 1058/6 - And Ibn al-Sakan said: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Ta'i informed us, they both said: Al-Walid b. Marwan informed us, my uncle Junadah b. Marwan narrated to us, from his father, from Ash'ath b. Sawwar, from Yahya b. Abbad b. Shayban, from his father, from his grandfather, with it. 1058/7 - Ibn Mandah said: And Abd al-Rahman b. Sharik concurred with him, from his father, from Ash'ath, meaning in his saying: from his father, from his grandfather. I say: The first is more likely correct."],[1493,"And Ibn Mandah said: Al-Hasan b. Mansur al-Imam informed us. 1058/6 - And Ibn al-Sakan said: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Ta'i informed us, they both said: Al-Walid b. Marwan informed us, my uncle Junadah b. Marwan narrated to us, from his father, from Ash'ath b. Sawwar, from Yahya b. Abbad b. Shayban, from his father, from his grandfather, with it. 1058/7 - Ibn Mandah said: And Abd al-Rahman b. Sharik concurred with him, from his father, from Ash'ath, meaning in his saying: from his father, from his grandfather. I say: The first is more likely correct."],[1494,"And Ibn Mandah said: Al-Hasan b. Mansur al-Imam informed us. 1058/6 - And Ibn al-Sakan said: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Ta'i informed us, they both said: Al-Walid b. Marwan informed us, my uncle Junadah b. Marwan narrated to us, from his father, from Ash'ath b. Sawwar, from Yahya b. Abbad b. Shayban, from his father, from his grandfather, with it. 1058/7 - Ibn Mandah said: And Abd al-Rahman b. Sharik concurred with him, from his father, from Ash'ath, meaning in his saying: from his father, from his grandfather. I say: The first is more likely correct."],[1495,"We came to Ali ؓ while he was at the camp of Abu Musa, and I found him eating. He said: “Come close and eat.” I said: “I intend to fast.” He said: “And I intend to fast.” Then he ate until when he finished, he said to his muezzin Ibn al-Nabbah: “Give the iqamah.”"],[1496,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Look who is in the mosque and invite him.” So there were Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ, and I invited them, and they ate, then they left, and he led them in the morning prayer."],[1497,"We, the company of prophets, have been commanded to hasten our breaking of the fast and to delay our pre-dawn meal. [The hadith.]"],[1498,"We, the company of prophets, have been commanded to hasten our breaking of the fast and to delay our pre-dawn meal. [The hadith.]"],[1499,"We, the company of prophets, have been commanded to hasten our breaking of the fast and to delay our pre-dawn meal. [The hadith.]"],[1500,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ in a dream, and I saw him not looking at me. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the matter with me?” He said: “Are you not the one who kisses while fasting?” He said: “By the One who sent you with the truth as a prophet, I will never kiss after this while I am fasting.” He affirmed it and said: “Yes.”"],[1501,"And Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, the like of it. : :"],[1502,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and said: “O Aisha, is there any piece of bread?” I brought him a round loaf, and he put it on his mouth and said: “O Aisha, has anything of it entered my stomach? Likewise is the kiss of the fasting person. Breaking the fast is only from what enters, not from what comes out.”"],[1503,"And Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad b. Mani' narrated to us, with this. : :"],[1504,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us from the house of Hafsa ؓ, and he had applied kohl with ithmid in Ramadan."],[1505,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to apply kohl while fasting."],[1506,"The Prophet ﷺ used the toothstick while fasting."],[1507,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the kiss of the fasting person. He said: “It is a fragrant herb that he smells.”"],[1508,"A man asked Abu Hurayra ؓ: “May I kiss my wife while I am fasting?” He said: “No harm.” He said: “May I kiss a woman other than her?” He said: “Uff.” He said: “And I asked Sa'd b. Malik, and he said: ‘No harm.’”"],[1509,"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."],[1510,"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."],[1511,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped while fasting."],[1512,"Everything from your wife is lawful for you when you are fasting except what is between the legs."],[1513,"The fasting person has at the time of breaking his fast a supplication that is answered. Whenever 'Abdullah b. 'Amr ؓ broke his fast, he would call his family and children and supplicate."],[1514,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: O 'Ali, when you are fasting in the month of Ramadan, say after breaking your fast: 'O Allah, for You I fasted, and upon You I relied, and with Your provision I break my fast.' It will be written for you like the reward of one who fasts without diminishing anything from their rewards."],[1515,"A man asked Abu Hurayrah ؓ, saying: 'I ate while fasting.' He said: 'There is nothing upon you.' He said: 'I drank while fasting.' He said: 'There is nothing upon you.' He said: 'Then I ate such and such while fasting.' He said: 'O my son, you have not been accustomed to fasting.'"],[1516,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and bread and meat were brought. She said: I desired to eat from the food of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: 'Come, O Umm Ishaq, and eat.' She said: So I ate, then he handed me a bone with meat on it. I raised it to my mouth, then I remembered that I was fasting. My hand remained unable to raise it to my mouth and unable to put it down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is the matter with you, O Umm Ishaq?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I was fasting.' He said: 'Complete your fast.' Dhu al-Yadayn said: 'Now, when you are full?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'It is only provision that Allah, Exalted is He, drove to her.'"],[1517,"I have not seen anyone more insistent on fasting Ashura than 'Ali b. Abi Talib and Abu Musa ؓ."],[1518,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them to fast Ashura, the tenth day."],[1519,"He asked 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Qasim about fasting Ashura, and he said: 'Ibn 'Umar ؓ did not fast it.'"],[1520,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to fast Ashura, so fast it."],[1521,"He used to fast on the day of Ashura."],[1522,"Fast on the day of Ashura, a day the prophets used to fast, so fast it."],[1523,"Whoever among you has not eaten, let him fast; and whoever has eaten, let him complete the rest of his day."],[1524,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded fasting on Ashura, but he would not fast it."],[1525,"And al-Harith said: Abd al-Aziz b. Aban narrated to us, from Ulaylah bt. so-and-so al-Azdiyyah: My mother narrated to me, from Amat Allah, from Razinah the maidservant of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[1526,"That she heard the Messenger of God ﷺ mention the fast of Ashura? She said: Yes, he used to venerate it so much that he would call for his suckling infants and the suckling infants of his daughter Fatimah ؓ , and he would put saliva in their mouths and say: Do not breastfeed them until night."],[1527,"A bedouin asked the Prophet ﷺ about fasting the day of Arafah and the day of Ashura. He ﷺ said: The day of Ashura expiates the year before it and the year after it, and the fast of Arafah expiates the year before it."],[1528,"Your Lord looks upon His creation on the night of the middle of Sha'ban and forgives all of them, except one who is a polytheist or one who severs ties. They said: The Messenger of God ﷺ used to fast Sha'ban, and Ramadan would enter while he was fasting, out of reverence for Ramadan."],[1529,"When he broke his fast, he would begin the next day fasting from Shawwal until he completed it to its end."],[1530,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would sometimes join Sha'ban with Ramadan."],[1531,"Whoever fasts the day of Arafah will be forgiven for two consecutive years."],[1533,"Abu Bakr narrated to us:"],[1534,"Whoever fasts the Day of Arafah will be forgiven for two years: a year before it and a year after it."],[1535,"Whoever accompanies me, male or female, should not fast the Day of Arafah, for it is a day of eating, drinking, and remembrance of Allah Almighty."],[1536,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ passed by tents at Arafat and asked, \"To whom do these tents belong?\" We said, \"To Abd al-Qays.\" He spoke well of them and forbade them from fasting the Day of Arafah."],[1537,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting the Day of Arafah at Arafah."],[1538,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on the day of Eid al-Fitr and the day of Eid al-Adha."],[1539,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: \"Stand up and proclaim among the people that the days of Tashriq are days of eating and drinking; no fasting is to be done in them.\""],[1540,"Al-Nadr b. Shumayl informed us: Abu Ibrahim al-Madani narrated to us, from Ismail, the like of it."],[1541,"Ahmad b. Mani and al-Harith both said: Rawh b. Ubada narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abi Humayd narrated to us, with this chain. Muhammad is weak, and he is Abu Ibrahim al-Madani whom al-Nadr referred to by his kunya."],[1542,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting six days of the year: three days of Tashriq, the day of Fitr, the day of Adha, and Friday singled out among the days."],[1543,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting the three days of Tashriq after the day of sacrifice."],[1544,"1348 1097/3 - Abu Ya'la said: Abu Khaythama narrated to us: Rawh narrated to us, with this chain."],[1545,"Musa b. Muhammad narrated to us: Kahmas b. al-Minhal narrated to us: Sa'id b. Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqqashi, and he mentioned the like of the hadith of al-Tayalisi."],[1546,"Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad b. Khalid al-Tahhan narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah, from Anas ؓ , and he mentioned it. I say: Muhammad b. Khalid erred in it; it is Yazid al-Raqashi, not Qatadah."],[1547,"Al-Harith said: Abdullah b. Awn narrated to us: Abu Ubaydah narrated to us: Abu Abdullah narrated to us: from Yazid al-Raqashi, and he mentioned the like of the narration of al-Tayalisi."],[1548,"The Prophet ﷺ sent Ali ؓ during the days of Tashriq to announce: O people, these are days of eating and drinking, and of marital relations."],[1549,"The Prophet ﷺ sent Ali ؓ during the days of Tashriq to announce: O people, these are days of eating and drinking, and of marital relations."],[1550,"The Prophet ﷺ sent Ali ؓ during the days of Tashriq to announce: O people, these are days of eating and drinking, and of marital relations."],[1551,"The Prophet ﷺ sent Ali ؓ during the days of Tashriq to announce: O people, these are days of eating and drinking, and of marital relations."],[1552,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. Musa is weak."],[1553,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a man to announce during the days of Tashriq: These are days of eating, drinking, and marital relations."],[1554,"Some people from the companions of Abdullah came to Abu al-Darda ؓ on Friday while they were fasting. He said: This is a day of Eid, so I adjure you to break your fast."],[1555,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never seen not fasting on Friday."],[1556,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about fasting, but he was distracted from him. Ibn Mas'ud ؓ said to him: Fast Ramadan and three days of every month. The man said: I seek refuge in Allah from you, O Abdullah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: What more do you want? Fast Ramadan and three days of every month."],[1557,"We do not know that Ibrahim narrated in musnad form from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ؓ , except this."],[1558,"Fasting Ramadan and three days of every month removes the rancor of the chest. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the rancor of the chest? He ﷺ said: Its pain and its malice."],[1559,"A man asked Ibn Abbas ؓ about fasting. He said: If you want the fasting of the best of mankind, the Prophet ﷺ , the unlettered, the Arab, the Qurayshi, Abu al-Qasim ﷺ , he used to fast three days of every month and say: It is the fasting of a lifetime."],[1560,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ was asked about the rabbit. He said: Who among you witnessed the Prophet ﷺ when the Bedouin man came to him? A man from the people said: The Bedouin brought it, and he had perfumed it and prepared it and gifted it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . He said: I saw it menstruating. Then he ﷺ said to the people: Eat. The Bedouin did not eat. He ﷺ said: What prevented you from eating? He said: I am fasting. He said: Then why not the white days?"],[1563,"I asked Ibn 'Abbas ؓ about fasting the three white days. He said: 'Umar ؓ used to fast them."],[1564,"Fasting the month of patience and three days of every month is fasting the whole time, and it removes the rancor of the heart."],[1565,"And al-Bazzar said: 'Abd al-Wahid b. Ghiyath narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us with it. And Hajjaj has weakness in it. 1107/3 - However, Yunus b. Abi Ishaq corroborated him. Al-Bazzar also transmitted it."],[1566,"And al-Bazzar said: 'Abd al-Wahid b. Ghiyath narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us with it. And Hajjaj has weakness in it. 1107/3 - However, Yunus b. Abi Ishaq corroborated him. Al-Bazzar also transmitted it."],[1567,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him of my Islam. Then I was absent from him for a year, then I came to him and said: 'O Messenger of God, it is as though you recognize me?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, I have not broken my fast since I parted from you.' He ﷺ said: 'Who commanded you to torment yourself? Fast one day of the month.' I said: 'Give me more.' He said: 'Fast two days.' I said: 'Give me more.' He said: 'Fast three days of every month.'"],[1568,"Whoever fasts Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday, God Almighty will build for him a house in Paradise whose exterior is seen from its interior and whose interior is seen from its exterior."],[1569,"And Abu Ya'la said: Suwayd narrated to us, Baqiyya narrated to us, from Abu Bakr, Muhammad b. Zayd narrated to me, from Hanash al-San'ani, from Ibn 'Abbas ؓ, similarly. And the hadith of Ibn 'Abbas and Ibn 'Umar will come later."],[1570,"And from Baqiyya, from Abu Bakr, from Zayd b. Aslam, from Ibn 'Umar ؓ, with it."],[1571,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: 'Should I fast the whole time?' He forbade him, and he repeated it, and he forbade him, three times: 'But the fast of Dawud - fast one day and break the fast one day; for that is the fast of Dawud ﷺ .' And that man did not cease fasting one day and breaking the fast one day until he died."],[1572,"The best fast is the fast of my brother Dawud. He used to fast half the time, fasting one day and breaking the fast one day."],[1573,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he came upon a man, and they said: 'He has not broken his fast since such and such.' He said: 'He has neither fasted nor broken his fast.' When 'Umar ؓ saw his anger, he said: 'O Messenger of God, fasting two days and breaking the fast one day?' He said: 'Can anyone bear that?' He said: 'O Messenger of God, fasting one day and breaking the fast one day?' He ﷺ said: 'That is the fast of my brother Dawud.' He said: 'O Messenger of God, fasting one day and breaking the fast two days?' He ﷺ said: 'And who can bear that?' He said: 'O Messenger of God, fasting Monday?' He ﷺ said: 'That is the day I was born and the day prophethood was sent down upon me.' He said: 'O Messenger of God, fasting the day of 'Arafa and the day of 'Ashura'?' He ﷺ said: 'One of them expiates a year, and the other expiates what is before it and what is after it.'"],[1575,"We were sitting waiting for the Prophet ﷺ, and he came to us with anger on his face until he sat down. Then we saw his face brighten, and he ﷺ said: 'The Night of Decree and the Messiah of Misguidance were made clear to me, so I came out to make them clear to you. Then I met at the entrance of the mosque two men arguing, or he said: fighting, with Satan accompanying them, so I came between them, and I was made to forget them. I will tell you something of them. As for the Night of Decree, seek it in the last ten nights on odd nights. As for the Messiah of Misguidance, he is a man with a bright forehead, a defective eye, a broad neck, as though he were so-and-so b. 'Abd al-'Uzza, or 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Qatan.'"],[1576,"I saw the Night of Decree, then I was made to forget it, and I saw the Messiah of Misguidance, and I saw two men arguing, so I came between them, and I was made to forget them. So as for the Night of Decree, seek it in the last ten nights. As for the Messiah of Misguidance, he is a man with a bright forehead, a defective left eye, a broad neck, with some blood on him, as though he were so-and-so b. 'Abd al-'Uzza, or 'Abd al-'Uzza b. so-and-so."],[1577,"Whoever among you seeks the Night of Decree, let him seek it in the last ten nights."],[1578,"So I narrated that to Ibn 'Abbas ؓ, who said: 'What amazed you about that? 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ, when the elders among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ were summoned, used to summon me with them, and he said: Do not speak until they speak. One day, or one night, he summoned us and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning the Night of Decree what you already know: Seek it in the last ten nights, on odd nights. Which odd night is it? A man said, expressing his own opinion: The ninth, the seventh, the fifth, the third. Then he said to me: What is wrong with you that you do not speak, O Ibn 'Abbas? I said: O Commander of the Faithful, if you wish, I will speak. He said: I only called you so that you would speak. He said: I only say what I think. He said: It is your opinion that I am asking about. I said: I have heard that Allah, exalted is He, often mentions seven. He mentioned the heavens as seven, and the earths as seven, until He said, among other things: And what the earth produces as seven. He said: Everything you have said I recognize except this: what do you mean by your saying, 'And what the earth produces as seven'? He said: Allah, exalted is He, says: Then We split the earth in fissures, and caused to grow within it grain and grapes and green fodder and olives and palm trees and gardens of dense foliage and fruits and grass, as provision for you. So the gardens are every dense garden, and the grass is what the earth produces that people do not eat. 'Umar ؓ said: Are you unable to say something like what this young man said, whose head has not yet fully grown? Then he said to me: I had forbidden you to speak with them; but when I call you, speak with them."],[1579,"I was with Abu Dharr ؓ, and he was asked about the Night of Decree, and he mentioned something similar up to his saying: the last ten."],[1580,"I was with Abu Dharr ؓ, and he mentioned it, adding: I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you inform us of it? He ﷺ said: If I were permitted concerning it, I would inform you of it."],[1581,"I asked Abu Dharr ؓ, and he mentioned something similar."],[1582,"I stayed in the mosque of Madinah with a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, from Banu Bayadah, during the last ten nights of Ramadan, in a dome of his whose door was covered with a piece of matting. He said: While we were in the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a dome of his, he lifted the matting from the door and signaled to those in the mosque to gather. We gathered, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us an admonition, the like of which I have never heard from any preacher. He said: When one of you stands to pray, he is conversing privately with his Lord, blessed and exalted is He, so let him consider with what he converses. And let not some of you raise their voices over others with the Qur'an. Then he lowered the matting, and each of us returned to his place. Some of us said to others: This night has great significance, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ admonished us during it. And indeed it was the night of the twenty-third."],[1585,"The Night of Decree is the night of the twenty-seventh."],[1586,"The Night of Decree is the night of the seventeenth: the day of the Criterion, the day the two hosts met. I do not doubt, and no exception was made."],[1587,"It is the night on the day of which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met the people of Badr. He said: Allah, mighty and majestic is He, says: And what We sent down upon Our servant on the day of the Criterion, the day the two hosts met."],[1588,"I saw the moon on the Night of Decree as if it were a piece of a bowl."],[1589,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out one night, intending to inform us of the Night of Decree, and ..."],[1590,"Al-Juhani said: O Messenger of God, we are far away, as you know, and we are not able to attend this month. So tell us (the date of) the Night of Decree. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, this is the night of the twenty-third, and it is when eight remain? He said: No, this month decreases, and it is when seven remain."],[1591,"A man asked Shurayh about a woman who vowed to perform i'tikaf during Rajab of that year in the mosque. He said: And Ziyad or Ibn Ziyad had forbidden women from performing i'tikaf in the mosque. Shurayh said: I do not say that it is in a revealed book, nor in a past Sunnah; it is only an opinion. She should fast Rajab of that year, and when she breaks her fast, a poor person should break his fast with her every day, or she should feed a poor person every night—two acts of worship for one. God does whatever He wills."],[1592,"Safiyyah performed i'tikaf, and some of her family fell ill, so she asked permission from the Messenger of God ﷺ to visit him. He said: Take hold of the two doorposts and do not enter."],[1595,"When Ibrahim ﷺ finished building the House, He said to him: 'Proclaim the pilgrimage among the people.' He said: 'But how far will my voice reach?' It was said: 'Proclaim, and upon Me is the conveying.' So Ibrahim called out: 'O people, the pilgrimage to the Ancient House has been prescribed for you.' And it was heard by all between heaven and earth. Do you not see that people come for pilgrimage from all corners of the earth, reciting the talbiyah?"],[1598,"Make pilgrimage, for it is as if I am looking at an Ethiopian with a small ear, holding a pickaxe, demolishing it stone by stone. We said to Ali ؓ: Is this your own opinion? He said: No, by the One who split the grain and created the soul, but I heard it from your Prophet ﷺ."],[1599,"There is no one who refrains from Hajj in Islam."],[1600,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us and mentioned the hadith, in which (he said): 'Whoever looks after the family of a pilgrim or one performing Umrah with goodness, he will have the like of his reward completely, without diminishing anything from the pilgrim's reward.'"],[1602,"I was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the mosque of al-Khayf, when a man from the Ansar and a man from Thaqif came to him. When they had greeted him, they said: 'We have come to you, O Messenger of God, to ask you.' He ﷺ said: 'If you wish, I will tell you what you are asking me about, and if you wish I will remain silent and you ask me.' They said: 'Tell us, O Messenger of God, so that we may increase in faith or increase in certainty—Ismail was unsure. The Ansari said to the Thaqafi: 'Ask.' He said: 'No, you ask him, for I acknowledge your right, so ask him.' The Ansari said: 'Tell us, O Messenger of God.' He ﷺ said: 'You have come to ask me about your departure from your house heading for the Sacred House, and what you will have for it; about your circumambulation of the House, and what you will have for it; about your two rak'ahs after the circumambulation, and what you will have for them; about your going between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and what you will have for it; about your standing at Arafah, and what you will have for it; about your stoning of the Jamarat, and what you will have for it; about your sacrifice, and what you will have for it; about shaving your head, and what you will have for it; and about your circumambulation after that, and what you will have for it.' He said: 'By the One who sent you with the truth, it was about this that I came to ask you.' He ﷺ said: 'When you leave your house heading for the Sacred House, your camel does not place a foot nor lift it except that God Almighty writes for you a good deed, wipes out a sin, and raises you a degree. As for your circumambulation of the House, and your two rak'ahs after the circumambulation, they are like freeing a slave from the descendants of Ishmael. As for your going between al-Safa and al-Marwah, it is like freeing seventy slaves. As for your standing on the evening of Arafah, God Almighty descends to the lowest heaven and boasts of you to the angels, saying: 'These are My servants who have come to Me with disheveled hair and covered in dust from every deep valley, hoping for My mercy and forgiveness. If your sins were as numerous as the grains of sand or the foam of the sea, I would forgive them. Depart, My servants, forgiven, and for those you intercede for.' As for your stoning of the Jamarat, for every pebble you throw, a major sin from the destructive, obligatory sins is removed. As for your sacrifice, it is stored for you with your Lord. As for shaving your head, for every hair you shave, a good deed is recorded and a sin is wiped out.' He said: 'O Messenger of God, what if the sins are fewer than that?' He said: 'Then it will be stored for you among your good deeds. As for your circumambulation of the House after that, you will circumambulate while you have no sin. An angel will come and place his hand between your shoulders, then say: 'Work for what is to come, for what has passed has been forgiven you.'"],[1603,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us and mentioned a long hadith, in which (he said): 'Whoever goes out for Hajj or Umrah, for every step until he returns, he will have a million good deeds, a million sins erased, and a million degrees raised. With his Lord, for every dirham he spends, he will have a million dirhams, and for every dinar, a million dinars. For every good deed he performs, he will have a million good deeds until he returns, and he is in the protection of God Almighty. If He causes him to die, He will admit him to Paradise, and if He returns him, He will return him forgiven and with his supplications answered. So seize his supplication when he arrives, before he falls into sins, for he will intercede for a hundred thousand men on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[1604,"He stood at a gate inside which led to the mosque, the mosque of Mina, and praised God Almighty and extolled Him, then said: 'These are none but the servants of the disbelieving, wicked people. They have made it difficult to come every year, so they steal our wealth and take our slaves captive. God Almighty has made their blood and wealth lawful because of what they have made lawful of our blood and wealth,' meaning Najdah the Kharijite and his companions. 'I sent to them, and they were given what they asked for. Here are the slaves and the saddlebags—separate them, and whatever you recognize, take it. But I do not think it is right to shed blood in the sanctuary of God Almighty. The Messenger of God ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: 'Which land is most sacred?' It was said: 'Makkah.' He said: 'Which month is most sacred?' It was said: 'Dhu al-Hijjah.' He said: 'Which day is most sacred?' It was said: 'The Day of the Great Pilgrimage.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Your blood and your wealth are sacred to you until you meet your Lord, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this land of yours, in this month of yours.'"],[1605,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave a sermon and mentioned the hadith. He said: 'O people, time has come full circle, and today it is as it was on the day God created the heavens and the earth. The number of months with God is twelve months in the Book of God, Mighty and Majestic, from the day He created the heavens and the earth. Of them, four are sacred: Rajab of Mudar, between Jumada and Sha'ban, Dhu al-Qa'dah, Dhu al-Hijjah, and al-Muharram. The postponement (al-nasi') is an increase in disbelief, by which those who disbelieve are led astray, making it lawful one year and sacred another, to correspond with the number that God has made sacred, thus making lawful what God has forbidden. That is the postponement from Satan—the hadith... And in it: 'What day is this?' They said: 'A sacred day.' He said: 'What month is this?' They said: 'A sacred month.' He said: 'What land is this?' They said: 'A sacred land.' He said: 'God Almighty has made your blood, your wealth, and your honor sacred to you, like the sanctity of this day, in this month, in this land. Indeed, there is no prophet after me, and no nation after you. Let those present convey to those absent.' Then he raised his hands and said: 'O God, bear witness. O God, bear witness.' Three times."],[1606,"And Abd b. Humayd said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and he mentioned it in full. 1134/3 - Abu Ya'la also narrated it from another route, from Musa."],[1607,"And Abd b. Humayd said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and he mentioned it in full. 1134/3 - Abu Ya'la also narrated it from another route, from Musa."],[1609,"He said to his sons: 'Go out from Makkah willingly on foot, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"For the pilgrim who rides, for every step his mount takes there are seventy good deeds, and for the one who walks, for every step he takes there are seven hundred good deeds from the good deeds of the Haram.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what are the good deeds of the Haram?\" He ﷺ said: \"A good deed is multiplied by a hundred thousand.\"'\""],[1612,"Perform Hajj and `Umrah consecutively, for by the One in Whose hand is my soul, they remove poverty and sins just as the bellows removes the dross of iron."],[1613,"Perform Hajj and `Umrah consecutively."],[1614,"No one travels by sea except a warrior, a pilgrim performing Hajj, or a pilgrim performing `Umrah."],[1616,"Any servant whose body I have made healthy and whose livelihood I have made ample, if five years pass and he does not come to Me as a delegate, he is indeed deprived."],[1617,"And Abu Yala said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. 1139/3 - And Abd al-Razzaq said: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, from al-Ala' b. al-Musayyib with it. I say: There is disagreement about it from al-Ala'. : :"],[1618,"And Abu Yala said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. 1139/3 - And Abd al-Razzaq said: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, from al-Ala' b. al-Musayyib with it. I say: There is disagreement about it from al-Ala'. : :"],[1619,"Any servant whose body I have made healthy and whose provision I have made ample, if five Hajj seasons come upon him and he does not come to Me in any of them, he is indeed deprived."],[1621,"Perform Hajj on behalf of the children, do not consume their provisions and leave their sins upon your necks."],[1622,"Regarding the Hajj of a child, he said: 'I narrated it to Ibn al-Munkadir, and he performed Hajj with all his family.'"],[1623,"It was said to him: 'Do you perform Hajj with children?' He said: 'Yes, I present them to Allah Almighty.'"],[1624,"If a slave performs Hajj ten times, he still owes a Hajj if he can find a way to it. If a Bedouin performs Hajj ten times, he still owes a Hajj when he emigrates, if he can find a way to it. If a minor performs Hajj ten times, he still owes the Hajj of Islam when he reaches the age of discernment, if he can find a way to it."],[1626,"Umar ؓ came to Makkah and was informed that a freed slave of Amr b. al-As had camels that ate filth. He sent for them and drove them out of Makkah, and said: 'Camels used for carrying firewood and transporting water.' Umar ؓ said: 'Neither Hajj nor `Umrah is to be performed on them.'"],[1627,"It was forbidden to ride a jallalah (a camel that eats impurities)."],[1629,"His mother came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, Abu Ma‘qil had promised me that he would not perform Hajj unless I was with him. He performed Hajj on his riding camel, but I was not able to walk. I asked him for the trimmings of a palm tree, and he said, ‘It is the sustenance of his dependents.’ I asked him for a young camel he had, and he said, ‘It is in the path of Allah; I will not give it to you.’” The Prophet said, “O Abu Ma‘qil, what does Umm Ma‘qil say?” He said, “She has spoken the truth.” The Prophet said, “Give her your young camel, for Hajj is part of the path of Allah Almighty.” So he gave her his young camel."],[1630,"His wife said to him, while he had a male camel and a she-camel, “Give me your male camel to perform Hajj on it.” He said, “It is a charitable endowment in the path of Allah Almighty.” She said, “It is indeed in the path of Allah for me to perform Hajj on it,” but he refused. She said, “Then give me the she-camel, and you perform Hajj on your male camel.” He said, “I do not prefer anyone over myself.” She said, “Then give me some of your provisions.” He said, “I have no surplus beyond what I take out myself, and if I had any, I would give it to you.” She said, “When you do what you have said, convey my greetings of peace to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ when you meet him, and tell him what I said to you.” When he met the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, he conveyed her greetings and told him what she had said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Umm Taliq has spoken the truth. If you had given her your male camel, it would have been in the path of Allah, and if you had given her your she-camel, it would have been in the path of Allah, and if you had given her some of your provisions, Allah would have replaced it for you.” I said, “O Prophet of Allah, what equals Hajj?” He ﷺ said, “An ‘umrah in Ramadan.”"],[1631,"A man asked Ibn ‘Abbas ؓ, “I hire myself out to these people and perform the rites with them; do I have a reward?” He said, “Yes: ‘Those will have a share of what they have earned’ (Qur’an 2:202).”"],[1632,"I said to Ibn ‘Umar ؓ, “I have riding camels that I rent out for Hajj, and I work to support my family. Some people claim that I have no Hajj because they are rented out.” He said, “They have lied. You have a reward for your Hajj and a reward for your effort in supporting your family, so you have two rewards.”"],[1633,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a man reciting the talbiyah on behalf of Shubrumah. He asked, “Who is Shubrumah?” The man mentioned a relative of his. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Have you performed Hajj for yourself?” He said, “No.” He said, “Then perform Hajj for yourself, and then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah.”"],[1634,"Musaddad said: ‘Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Muhammad ibn ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from ‘Ata’, and he mentioned it as mursal. The preserved version of this hadith is from Ibn ‘Abbas ؓ."],[1635,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ, “My father cannot perform Hajj unless he is carried crosswise (on a mount); shall I perform Hajj on his behalf?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “My mother died without making a will; shall I give charity on her behalf?” He said, “Yes.”"],[1636,"Allah Almighty will admit three people to Paradise for a single Hajj: the deceased, the one performing Hajj, and the one who carried it out (i.e., financed it)."],[1637,"Al-Harith said: Isma‘il ibn Abi Isma‘il narrated to us, Isma‘il ibn ‘Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Shu‘ayb al-Madani, who raised it (to the Prophet) in a similar manner."],[1638,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ designated Dhat ‘Irq as the miqat for the people of Iraq."],[1639,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered ihram from the mosque of Dhu al-Hulayfah."],[1640,"He performed Hajj with Anas b. Malik ؓ, and he narrated to him that he entered ihram from al-'Aqiq."],[1641,"'Imran b. Husayn ؓ, he (the narrator) thought he said: meaning, he entered ihram from Basra. When he came to 'Umar ؓ, and that had reached him, he spoke harshly to him and said: 'People are saying that a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ entered ihram from a city among the cities.'"],[1642,"It is from the Sunnah that one does not enter ihram for Hajj except in the months of Hajj."],[1643,"There is no man who removes his garment while he is in ihram, and the sun touches him until it sets, except that it sets with his sins."],[1644,"Whoever fulfills his rites and the Muslims are safe from his tongue and his hand, his past and future sins will be forgiven."],[1645,"'Abd b. Humayd said: 'Abdullah b. Musa narrated to us, Musa b. 'Ubayda narrated to us with it, and he did not say: 'and his future [sins]'."],[1646,"The delegations of Allah, the Exalted, are three: the pilgrim, the one performing 'umrah, and the warrior."],[1647,"Muhammad b. Abi Humayd is alone in narrating it, and he has hadiths that are not corroborated."],[1648,"I entered upon 'Abdullah b. 'Amr ؓ, and he narrated to us, saying: 'There is no one, or no man, who raises his voice with the talbiyah except that Allah, the Exalted, says: Rejoice!' The uncle of Mirdas said: 'O Abu Muhammad, by Allah, Allah does not give glad tidings except of Paradise.' He said: 'Who are you, O son of my brother?' He said: 'I am Mirdas b. Shaddad al-Junadi.' He said: 'O son of my brother, our best ones used to follow one another upon that.'"],[1649,"It was said to Ibn al-Munkadir: 'Will you perform Hajj while you have a debt?' He said: 'Hajj is more effective in fulfilling the debt.'"],[1650,"My father, when we set out for Makkah, would travel with us for a month from his place, and when he returned, he would travel with us for two months. That was mentioned to him, and he said: 'It has reached me that a man remains in the way of Hajj until he enters upon his family.'"],[1651,"This House is the pillar of Islam. Whoever sets out aiming for this House, as a pilgrim, a performer of 'umrah, or a visitor, is guaranteed by Allah: if He takes his soul, He will admit him to Paradise, and if He returns him, He returns him with spoils and reward."],[1652,"Whoever dies on the road to Makkah, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will not present him on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He call him to account."],[1653,"Whoever sets out from this direction for Hajj or Umrah and dies during it, he will not be presented nor called to account, and it will be said to him: 'Enter Paradise.'"],[1654,"Whoever sets out as a pilgrim and dies, the reward of the pilgrim will be written for him until the Day of Resurrection. Whoever sets out for Umrah and dies, the reward of the one performing Umrah will be written for him until the Day of Resurrection. Whoever sets out as a warrior in the path of Allah and dies, the reward of the warrior will be written for him until the Day of Resurrection."],[1655,"Umar ؓ came seeking permission for Umrah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O my brother, supplicate, and do not forget us in your righteous supplication.'"],[1656,"He was asked about tamattu' in Hajj, and he said: 'It was for us, not for you.'"],[1657,"I performed Hajj with the Prophet ﷺ, and he found Aisha ؓ taking off her clothes. He said: 'What is the matter with you?' She said: 'I was informed that you made your family exit ihram.' He ﷺ said: 'Yes, for those who do not have a sacrificial animal. As for us, we have not exited ihram because we have sacrificial animals, until we reach 'Arafat.'"],[1658,"Imran b. Husayn ؓ arrived with companions of his who had combined Hajj and Umrah. It was said to Uthman b. Affan ؓ: 'Imran has arrived with companions of his performing Hajj and Umrah.' So he sent to him: 'Choose one of them.' Imran said: 'The Commander of the Believers forbade us, and he gave us a choice, so I choose Hajj.'"],[1659,"We set out with Ali ؓ until when we were at Dhul-Hulayfah, he said: 'I intend to combine Hajj and Umrah. Whoever among you wishes that, let him say as I say.' Then he began the talbiyah, saying: 'For Umrah and Hajj together.'"],[1660,"The Prophet ﷺ stood on al-Marwah with an arrowhead in his hand, trimming his hair with it, and he was saying: 'Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[1661,"The Prophet ﷺ and his companions did not perform tawaf except one tawaf for their Hajj and Umrah."],[1662,"And Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah said: Yahya b. Ya'la narrated to us, with it.:"],[1663,"And Abu Ya'la also said: Abu Bakr narrated to us, with it. I say: Layth is weak. And the hadith of Jabir is in Muslim from another route. And the hadith of Ibn Umar ؓ is in the Sunan:"],[1664,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ resolved to prohibit tamattu' in Hajj. Ubayy b. Ka'b stood up to him and said, \"That is not for you to do. The Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, was revealed for it, and we performed 'umrah with it along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So Umar ؓ abandoned that."],[1665,"My father and Abu Musa went to Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ and said, \"Will you not teach the people the matter of this tamattu'?\" He said, \"Is there anyone left who has not performed it? As for me, I will do it.\""],[1666,"I heard Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ say, \"If I performed 'umrah, then performed 'umrah, then performed Hajj, I would be doing tamattu'.\""],[1667,"If they separate Hajj and 'umrah, the 'umrah being outside the months of Hajj, it is more complete for the Hajj of one of you and for his 'umrah."],[1668,"Ibn Umar ؓ, when he entered ihram from Makkah, did not perform sa'i until he returned from Mina."],[1669,"We entered ihram for 'umrah in Ramadan and arrived in Makkah in Shawwal, while people were then numerous. We asked, and everyone we asked said, \"It is tamattu'.\""],[1670,"Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr ؓ said, \"Perform Hajj ifrad, and leave this statement of your blind ones.\" Abd Allah b. Abbas ؓ said, \"You are the one whose heart Allah has blinded. Ask your mother about this.\""],[1671,"He performed tamattu' with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the tamattu' of Hajj."],[1673,"He performed Hajj with his masters. He said: I met Umm Salamah, the Mother of the Believers, and said to her, \"I have never performed Hajj. So which of the two should I begin with, Hajj or 'umrah?\" She said, \"Begin with whichever you wish.\" I said to her, \"People say that if someone has never performed Hajj, he should begin with Hajj.\" She said to me, \"Begin with whichever you wish.\" Then I went to Safiyyah and asked her, and she said to me the same as Umm Salamah said: \"Begin with whichever you wish.\" Then I came back to Umm Salamah and informed her of Safiyyah's statement. Umm Salamah said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'O family of Muhammad, whoever of you performs Hajj, let him make an 'umrah with his Hajj, or with a Hajj.'\""],[1674,"Umar b. al-Khattab saw upon Talhah two dyed garments while he was in ihram and said, \"What is this?\" He said, \"O Commander of the Believers, there is no harm in it; it is only red dye.\" He said, \"You all, this group, are leaders whom people imitate. Perhaps an ignorant person, if he saw you, would say, 'I saw upon Talhah two dyed garments,' and thus wear dyed garments in ihram. Let me not find any of you wearing a dyed garment in ihram.\""],[1675,"Umar ؓ noticed upon Abd Allah b. Ja'far ؓ two dyed garments while he was in ihram, and said, \"What is this?\" Ali said, \"I do not think anyone teaches us the Sunnah.\""],[1676,"A woman asked Ibn Umar ؓ, \"Should I wash my clothes while I am in ihram?\" He said, \"Indeed, Allah, Exalted is He, does nothing with your dirt.\""],[1677,"The one in ihram may perform ghusl and wash his clothes if he wishes."],[1678,"Abu 'Awana narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas ؓ, something similar. :"],[1679,"A woman in ihram must not wear perfumed garments, but she may wear saffron-dyed ones, and I do not consider yellow dye to be perfume."],[1680,"She saw 'A'ishah ؓ on the evening of Tarwiyah wearing a rose-colored shift and a black khimar while she was in ihram."],[1681,"The two of them entered upon 'A'ishah ؓ while she was wearing a rose-colored shift and a black khimar. She was asked, \"Does a woman in ihram cover her face?\" She raised her khimar like this from her chest to her head and said, \"There is no harm in this.\""],[1682,"She used to grant a concession to a woman in ihram regarding wearing gloves."],[1683,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing a jubba and showing traces of khaluq. He said, \"What should I do in my 'umrah?\" Then revelation descended and he was covered with a cloth. Umayyah liked to see him ﷺ while revelation was coming down to him. The hadith."],[1684,"Any man who marries while in ihram, we take his wife away from him, and his marriage is not valid."],[1685,"I was with Sa'id b. Jubayr, and he saw a man putting his head between the curtain and the House. He forbade him and said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas ؓ say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a person in ihram from putting his head between the curtain and the wall, or between the curtain and the House."],[1686,"Maymunah shaved her head."],[1689,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left for Madinah, walking, then he turned toward the House and said: \"By Allah, I do not know of any house that Allah the Exalted has placed on earth more beloved to me than you, nor any land more beloved to me than you. I did not leave you out of dislike, but those who disbelieved drove me out.\" Then he called out: \"O Banu 'Abd Manaf, it is not lawful for any servant to prevent a servant from circumambulating this House at any hour he wishes, night or day.\""],[1690,"The hands are raised in seven places: at the beginning of prayer, when seeing the House, on al-Safa and al-Marwah, on the evening of 'Arafah, at Muzdalifah, at the two jamarat, and over the deceased."],[1692,"O people of Makkah, do not put doors on your houses so that the desert-dweller may alight wherever he wishes."],[1694,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf on his mount on the day of the conquest of Makkah, touching the corners with a staff that he had with him."],[1696,"Indeed Ibrahim the Prophet ﷺ was the first to erect the boundary markers of the Sacred Precinct; Gabriel indicated to him their locations."],[1697,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded Tamim b. Asid, the grandfather of 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Muttalib b. Tamim, on the day of the conquest of Makkah, and he demarcated them."],[1698,"Quraysh found a stone in the pre-Islamic era from the Maqam of Ibrahim containing writing, and they began to bring it out to those who came to them from the People of the Book, but they did not know what was in it, until a rabbi from Yemen came to them and read it to them. Therein was: 'I am Allah, Lord of Bakkah; I made it when I made the sun and the moon, and I blessed its people in meat and milk.' And on the other side: 'I am Allah, Lord of Bakkah; I created the womb and derived for it a name from My own name; whoever maintains it, I maintain him, and whoever severs it, I sever him.' And on the other side: 'I am Allah, Lord of Bakkah; I created good and evil, so blessed is he through whose hands good comes, and woe to him through whose hands evil comes.'"],[1699,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Tamim b. Asid al-Khuza'i to renew the boundary markers of the Sacred Precinct, which Ibrahim ﷺ had placed, with Gabriel showing them to him."],[1700,"Whoever deems lawful anything of the boundaries of Makkah, upon him is the curse of Allah."],[1702,"Indeed the one who consumes the rent of the houses of Makkah consumes only fire into his belly."],[1703,"It has been forbidden to take rent for the houses of Makkah and to sell its properties."],[1705,"While I was performing tawaf with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he stopped and smiled. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I saw you stop and smile.' He ﷺ said, 'Isa met me performing tawaf with two angels, and he greeted me, so I greeted him.'"],[1706,"I saw 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf ؓ performing tawaf around the House while singing camel-driver songs, wearing two khuffs. 'Umar ؓ said to him, 'I do not know which of the two is more astonishing: your singing around the House, or your tawaf in your shoes.' He said, 'I did this at the time of one better than you, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not find fault with me for it.'"],[1707,"1481 1212 / 2 - Suwayd b. Sa'id narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, and he mentioned it."],[1709,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ during tawaf, and his sandal broke. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, hand it to me so I can fix it.' He ﷺ said, 'This is a selfish privilege, and I do not like selfish privilege.'"],[1710,"The Prophet ﷺ was performing tawaf around the House, and his sandal strap broke. A man took out a strap from his own sandal and went to fasten it to the Prophet's ﷺ sandal, but he snatched it away and said, 'This is a selfish privilege, and I do not like selfish privilege.'"],[1712,"I saw Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ performing tawaf around the House, saying between the door and the corner, or between the Station and the door, 'Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.'"],[1714,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded his wife to perform tawaf riding in her howdah behind the worshippers in the middle of the mosque. I asked, 'At night or during the day?' He said, 'I do not know.' I asked, 'In which seven [circuits]?' He said, 'I do not know.'"],[1716,"Indeed, Allah the Exalted boasts to [the angels] about those performing tawaf."],[1717,"Whoever performs seven circuits around the House and prays two rak'ahs behind the Station, it is like freeing a slave."],[1719,"Aisha ؓ used to perform tawaf three weeks, combining them, then she would pray two rak'ahs for each week."],[1720,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf before dawn, then he prayed six rak'ahs, turning to the right and left in each pair of rak'ahs. He said, 'We thought that it was two rak'ahs for each week, but he did not say the taslim.'"],[1722,"He used to crowd to reach the corner, and when people saw him, they would make way for him. Nafi' said, 'One day I ended up in the crowd of people, and a man placed his elbow behind me. The man in front of him fell, and I fell from behind him. I did not think I would get out until they killed me, but he insisted on advancing.'"],[1723,"When he passed by the Black Stone and saw a crowd around it, he would face it, say 'Allahu akbar,' and say, 'O Allah, out of faith in You and following the Sunnah of Your Prophet.'"],[1724,"Were it not for what the impurities of the Age of Ignorance touched, no one with an ailment would touch it except that he would be healed, and there is nothing on earth from Paradise except it."],[1725,"Indeed, this corner is the right hand of Allah on earth, with which He shakes the hands of His servants as a man shakes the hand of his brother."],[1726,"An angel descended upon the Black Stone."],[1727,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: \"How did you do in touching the Black Stone?\" He said: I said: \"I touched it and left it.\" He said: \"You did right.\""],[1728,"I was with A'ishah ؓ when a female servant of hers came and said: \"I touched the Black Stone three times in seven circumambulations.\" She said: \"May Allah not reward you—two or three times? Why did you not say takbir, turn away, and pass by? You wanted to push against the men.\""],[1730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited in the two rak'ahs of tawaf: \"Say: O disbelievers\" and \"Say: He is Allah, the One.\""],[1731,"Umar ؓ used to kiss the Black Stone, then prostrate upon it, then kiss it, then prostrate upon it three times."],[1732,"I saw Muhammad b. Abbad b. Ja'far kiss the Black Stone and prostrate upon it, and he said: \"I saw my maternal uncle Ibn Abbas ؓ kiss it and prostrate upon it,\" and he said: \"I saw Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ kiss the Black Stone and prostrate upon it.\""],[1733,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ stand at the Black Stone and say: \"Indeed I know that you are a stone that can neither harm nor benefit,\" then he kissed it. Then Abu Bakr ؓ performed Hajj and stood at the Black Stone, then said: \"Indeed I know that you are a stone that can neither harm nor benefit, and had I not seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kiss you, I would not have kissed you.\""],[1735,"A'ishah ؓ used to circumambulate the House veiled."],[1737,"Hajj is Arafah, and Umrah is the tawaf."],[1738,"Whoever catches Arafah has caught the Hajj, and whoever misses Arafah has missed the Hajj."],[1739,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing in the pre-Islamic era at Arafat with the polytheists, and I saw him standing in Islam at that same standing place, so I knew that Allah—Blessed and Exalted—had appointed him for that."],[1740,"The Prophet ﷺ used to descend at the valley of Namirah."],[1741,"Gabriel came to Ibrahim (peace and blessings be upon them both) and took him to Mina, and prayed with him all the prayers. Then he prayed Fajr with him, then he went with him to Arafah and alighted with him where the people alight. Then he prayed the two prayers with him together. Then he brought him to the standing place, until when it was about the earliest time anyone from the people prays Maghrib, he departed and brought him to Muzdalifah, and prayed the two night prayers with him together. Then he stayed the night, until when it was about the earliest time anyone from the people prays Fajr, he prayed Fajr with him. Then he stood with him, until when it was about the latest time anyone from the people prays, he departed with him to Mina, and he threw the Jamrah, then he slaughtered and shaved, then he departed with him. Then Allah, Exalted be He, later revealed to His Prophet ﷺ: 'Follow the religion of Ibrahim, inclining toward truth.'"],[1742,"A man from Quraysh said to Abdullah b. Amr ؓ: 'I am weak in family and riding beasts. Our only riding beasts are these slow-moving donkeys. Should I not depart from Muzdalifah at night?' He said: 'As for Ibrahim, he spent the night at Mina, until when morning came and the sun's edge rose, he traveled to Arafah until he descended at a place there. Then he went forth and stood at his standing place there, until when the sun set, he departed. When he came to Muzdalifah, he descended at his place there. When it was the time of the early Fajr prayer, he stood, until when it was bright morning, he departed. That is the religion of Ibrahim ﷺ , and your Prophet ﷺ was commanded to follow him.'"],[1743,"Abu Ya'la said: Zuhayr b. Harb narrated to us: Ismail narrated to us with this."],[1744,"Gabriel (peace and blessings be upon him) departed with the Prophet ﷺ until he came to Muzdalifah, and he descended there and spent the night. Then he prayed Fajr at the earliest time any Muslim prays, then he stood with him until the latest time any Muslim prays, then he pushed on to Mina, climbed up, and slaughtered. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted be He, revealed to Muhammad ﷺ: 'Then We revealed to you: Follow the religion of Ibrahim, inclining toward truth' – the verse."],[1745,"Arafah is the day when people are known."],[1746,"Arafah is entirely a standing place, except the interior of Urana. And Muzdalifah is entirely a standing place, except the interior of Muhassir."],[1748,"The most frequent supplication of mine and of the prophets before me at Arafah was: 'There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner. His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O Allah, place light in my hearing, light in my sight, and light in my heart. O Allah, expand my chest and ease my affair. I seek refuge in You from the whisperings of the chests and the scattering of affairs. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what enters the night, from the evil of what enters the day, from the evil of what the winds blow, and from the evil of the calamities of time.'"],[1749,"There are no days better in the sight of Allah, Exalted be He, than the ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah. A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, are they better or their equivalent in jihad in the path of Allah, Exalted be He?' He said: 'They are better than their equivalent in jihad in the path of Allah, except a man who goes out with his life and wealth and returns with none of that.' And there is no day better in the sight of Allah, Exalted be He, than the Day of Arafah. Allah, Exalted be He, descends to the lowest heaven and says: 'Look at My servants, disheveled and dusty, performing Hajj, coming from every deep valley. They have not seen My mercy or My punishment.' No day is seen in which more are freed from the Fire than the Day of Arafah."],[1750,"Whoever says on the night of Arafah these ten words one thousand times, he will not ask Allah, Exalted be He, for anything except that He gives it to him, except for cutting ties of kinship or a sin: 'Glory be to the One whose throne is in the heaven. Glory be to the One whose footstool is on the earth. Glory be to the One whose way is in the sea. Glory be to the One whose authority is in the Fire. Glory be to the One whose mercy is in Paradise. Glory be to the One whose decree is in the graves. Glory be to the One whose favor is in the air. Glory be to the One who raised the heaven. Glory be to the One who spread the earth. Glory be to the One from whom there is no escape except to Him.'"],[1751,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the evening of Arafah raising his hands, so that what was under his armpit could be seen."],[1752,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at Arafah and began supplicating like this, and he placed the backs of his hands facing his chest."],[1753,"He stood at Arafat and said like this... and he raised his hands toward his chest."],[1754,"Indeed, Allah – Mighty and Majestic – boasts to the angels about the people of Arafah."],[1755,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded Bilal ؓ on the morning of Jam' to call out among the people: 'Be silent, or hush,' and he did so. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, Allah, Exalted is He, has been gracious to you in this gathering of yours: He has given your wrongdoers to your righteous, and He has given your righteous what they asked. Move on in the name of Allah.'"],[1756,"Indeed, Allah, Exalted is He, looked upon this gathering and accepted from their righteous, and made their righteous intercede for their wrongdoers, and overlooked all of them."],[1757,"No one remains on the Day of Arafah with an atom's weight of faith in his heart except that Allah, Exalted is He, forgives him. He said: A man said, 'For the people at the place of standing, O Messenger of Allah, or for all people?' He ﷺ said: 'Rather, for all people.'"],[1758,"Indeed, Allah, Exalted is He, boasts to the angels about the people of Arafat, saying: 'O My angels, look at My servants: they have come to Me from every deep valley, disheveled and dusty. Bear witness that I have answered their supplications, given their wrongdoers to their righteous, and given their righteous what they asked, except for the offenses between them.' When they departed and came to Jam', they returned to Allah, Exalted is He, in asking. Allah, Exalted is He, says: 'O My angels, My servants have returned to Me in asking. Bear witness that I have answered their supplications, given their wrongdoers to their righteous, given their righteous what they asked Me, and I have taken upon Myself the offenses between them.'"],[1759,"And I have given their righteous all that they asked Me, except for the offenses between them. And in it: 'O My angels, My servants stood and returned to desire and request, so I call you to witness that I have answered their supplications.'"],[1761,"Ibn al-Zubayr ؓ delayed the departure until it became light, so Ibn Umar ؓ said, 'The rising of the sun – are they waiting for the practice of the people of Jahiliyyah? So Ibn Umar ؓ departed, and the people departed with him, and Ibn al-Zubayr departed.'"],[1762,"The people of Jahiliyyah used to stand at Arafat until when the sun was on the tops of the mountains like turbans on the heads of men, they would depart. Then they would stand at Muzdalifah until when the sun was on the tops of the mountains, they would push on. When Islam came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the departure from Arafat until the sun set, and he hastened the departure from Jam', and he departed from it when everything became light in the last part of the night, and he prayed the dawn prayer there in the dark."],[1763,"I departed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the two departures, and he would depart with tranquility upon him."],[1765,"When we arrive, if Allah, Exalted is He, wills, we will alight at al-Khayf, and al-Khayf is the mosque of Mina."],[1767,"I was looking at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was slaughtering his camels standing, and I heard him ﷺ say – after he had shaved his head, then he entered a red tent of his, and I saw him bring his head out of his tent, saying: 'May Allah have mercy on those who shave their heads' – three times, then he said: 'And those who shorten.'"],[1769,"Permission was not given to anyone to spend the night away from Mina except to al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib because of his duty of providing water."],[1771,"When we reached the valley of Muhassir, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Take the pebbles for the jamarat from the valley of Muhassir.'"],[1772,"We looked at Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ on the first day of nafr, and he came out to us with water dripping from his beard, pebbles in his hand and pebbles in his lap, walking and saying takbir on his way until he reached the first jamrah, and he threw at it until he ran out of pebbles for fear that the pebbles of others who threw might hit him. Then he supplicated for a while, then went to the middle jamrah, then the other one."],[1773,"For the pebbles of the jamarat, whatever is accepted from them is raised up, and whatever is rejected is left. Were it not for that, it would be taller than a span."],[1774,"That there is no harm in what a man throws at the jamarat, whether it is pebbles or anything else. Abdullah b. Amr b. Uthman said: This was mentioned to Abdullah b. Umar ؓ, and he said: He spoke the truth. And Abu Habba ؓ was a Badri."],[1775,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught the people their rites. He said: Allah Almighty opened our hearing, and we could hear while we were in our saddles. Among what he taught us: 'When you throw the jamrah, throw it with pebbles like those used for khazf.'"],[1776,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession to the shepherds to throw the jamarat at night."],[1778,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ driving his sacrificial camel barefoot. He said: 'Ride it!' So he rode it."],[1779,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ included the Muslims as partners in their sacrificial animals: a cow for seven people."],[1780,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to send the hadi, and he would instruct the one he sent with it that if any of it became disabled, he should slaughter it, dip its sandal in its blood, then strike its side with it, and let those after you eat from it, but you should not eat any of it, nor anyone from your traveling companions."],[1781,"Regarding a man who sends a hadi while he is resident, he said: He sets a day for it; when it reaches that day, he abstains from what the pilgrim in ihram abstains from."],[1782,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions ؓ used to slaughter the budn with the left foreleg tied, standing on the remaining legs."],[1783,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding voluntary budn: 'If one becomes disabled before entering the Haram, then slaughter it, then dip your hand in its blood, then strike its side, and do not eat from it. If you eat from it, you will be liable for it.'"],[1784,"A man said: 'O Messenger of God, a sacrificial camel has become obligatory upon me, and the sacrificial camels have already been slaughtered, so what do you think?' He ﷺ said: 'Slaughter in its place seven sheep.'"],[1785,"The Prophet ﷺ drove one hundred sacrificial camels in his Hajj."],[1787,"When Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ entered Jerusalem, he said: 'Labbayk, O God, labbayk.'"],[1788,"I only heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ these words: 'Labbayk, O God, labbayk; labbayk, no partner is Yours; indeed praise and blessing are Yours.' And I did not hear him mention Hajj or 'Umrah. Mujahid said: And Umar b. al-Khattab said in it: 'And dominion, no partner is Yours.'"],[1789,"He performed Hajj with Anas b. Malik ؓ, and he used to say in his talbiyah: 'Labbayk, a true Hajj, worship and servitude.'"],[1790,"He departed from Arafah, and his talbiyah was: 'Labbayk, O God, labbayk.'"],[1791,"The best Hajj is al-'ajj and al-thajj. Al-'ajj is raising the voice in talbiyah, and al-thajj is slaughtering."],[1792,"As for al-'ajj, it is the talbiyah, and as for al-thajj, it is the slaughtering of camels."],[1793,"He used to say: 'Labbayk, O God, labbayk; labbayk, no partner is Yours, labbayk; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; no partner is Yours!'"],[1795,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ during the Farewell Hajj saying: 'Do you know which day this is?' They said: 'God and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'This is the middle of the days of Tashriq.' He said: 'Do you know which land this is?' They said: 'God and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'This is al-Mash'ar al-Haram.' He said: 'I do not know, perhaps I will not meet you after this year of mine. Indeed your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred among you, some of you over others, like the sanctity of this day of yours in this land of yours, until you meet God—Mighty and Majestic—and He asks you about your deeds. Indeed, let the nearest of you convey to the farthest.' He said: 'Then he followed it with: O God, have I conveyed? O God, have I conveyed?' And he passed away when he reached Madinah."],[1796,"Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. 'Ar'arah and Ya'qub narrated to us, they separated it, they said: Abu 'Asim narrated to us, with it. Abu Dawud extracted it in abbreviated form from the hadith of Abu 'Asim, with this chain. : , :"],[1798,"I set out with Mu'adh b. Jabal and Ka'b ؓ in a state of ihram for 'Umrah from Jerusalem, and our leader was Mu'adh ؓ and our affair was entrusted to him, and he led us in prayer. When we were on part of the road, Mu'adh ؓ went aside to relieve himself, and a man brought him a wild donkey that he had hamstrung, and Ka'b took it and gave it as a gift to the traveling companions. He said: Mu'adh did not return except when the people's pots were boiling with it. He asked and was informed, and he said: 'Let no one obey me except that he overturns his pot!' He said: So Ka'b and the people overturned their pots. Then when we were on part of the road, and Ka'b was praying by a fire, a swarm of locusts passed by him, and he took two locusts and killed them, forgetting his ihram. Then he remembered his ihram and threw them away. When we reached Madinah, the people entered upon Umar ؓ and I entered with them. Ka'b said: 'What do you think, O Commander of the Faithful?'—and he related to him the story of the two locusts. He said: 'No harm in that, O Ka'b.' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Himyar loves locusts. What did you impose upon yourself?' He said: 'Two dirhams.' He said: 'Two dirhams are better than a hundred locusts. Impose what you imposed upon yourself.'"],[1799,"He performed Hajj with Ka'b. Locusts came, and Ka'b began striking them with his whip. I said, 'O Abu Ishaq! Are you not in ihram?' He said, 'Yes, but it is from the game of the sea, and it first came out of the nostril of a fish.'"],[1800,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ at Sifah al-Rawha' when we came across a hamstrung wild donkey. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'The owner of this donkey is about to come.' It was not long before its owner came and said, 'Take it.' The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded Abu Bakr ؓ to distribute it among the traveling companions. Then we departed until we were at al-Uthaya near al-Arj, where there was a gazelle with an arrow deeply embedded in it, and it was bending its neck. The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded Abu Bakr ؓ to stand by it and keep people away from it."],[1801,"Al-Zubayr ؓ used to travel with dried strips of wild game meat and eat it while in ihram."],[1802,"I accompanied al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam ؓ from Madinah to Makkah while he was in ihram, and he used to eat the meat of land game. I said to him about that, and he said, 'A non-muhrim hunted it, and I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he did not see any harm in it.'"],[1803,"Umar ؓ ruled regarding the jerboa a young she-goat, regarding the hyena a ram, regarding the gazelle a ewe, and regarding the rabbit a young she-goat (less than a year old)."],[1804,"Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us with this. 1281/3 - And Ahmad b. Mani' said: Sufyan narrated to us with this, limited to the jerboa: : :"],[1805,"Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us with this. 1281/3 - And Ahmad b. Mani' said: Sufyan narrated to us with this, limited to the jerboa: : :"],[1806,"Abu Ya'la: Abu Ubaydah b. al-Fudayl b. Iyad narrated to us: Malik b. Su'ayr narrated to us from al-Ajlah from Abu al-Zubayr, and he mentioned it, but he added: 'And I do not think but that he raised it.' : :"],[1807,"Regarding ostrich eggs that a muhrim breaks: 'Make your male camel mount your she-camels, and when their pregnancy becomes clear to you, designate the number of eggs you broke, and say: This is a sacrificial animal, and you are not responsible for its guarantee. Whatever of that turns out good is good, and whatever is spoiled, you are not liable for it, just like eggs: some of them turn out good and some spoil.' He said: Muawiyah ؓ marveled at Ali's ؓ ruling, and Ibn Abbas ؓ said: Muawiyah was not impressed with what it was, except with what the eggs would be sold for in the market and given in charity."],[1808,"The Prophet ﷺ ruled regarding the hyena a ram and considered it game."],[1809,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled regarding a hunting dog: if it is killed, forty dirhams; regarding a livestock dog, a ewe from the sheep; regarding a farm dog, a faraq of grain; regarding a house dog, a faraq of dust. It is incumbent upon the owner of the killer to pay it, and incumbent upon the owner of the house to accept it."],[1811,"She wanted to perform Hajj with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said to her, 'Perform Umrah in Ramadan, for it is equal to a Hajj for you.'"],[1812,"And Ahmad b. Mani' said: Ismail narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us from Sa'id b. Jubayr with its meaning. : :"],[1814,"Urwah said to Ibn Abbas: Woe to you! Have you gone astray? You command Umrah in the ten days (of Dhu al-Hijjah) while there is no Umrah in them?! He replied: O little Urwah, ask your mother! He said: Abu Bakr and Umar did not say that, and they were more knowledgeable about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and more obedient to him than you. He replied: From here you are struck; we bring you the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and you bring us Abu Bakr and Umar!"],[1816,"I approached with Muadh b. Jabal and Kab ؓ in a state of ihram for Umrah from Bayt al-Maqdis."],[1818,"Whoever performs Hajj to this House, let his last covenant be the tawaf of the House, and he granted a dispensation for women."],[1819,"I have not seen anyone oppose Ibn Abbas but that he remained silent until... Jabir b. Abdullah opposed him regarding a menstruating woman after she performs tawaf on the Day of Sacrifice. Ibn Abbas said: She may depart. They sent to a woman who had experienced that during the time of the Prophet ﷺ and she agreed with Ibn Abbas."],[1821,"Forgiveness is granted to the pilgrim and to those for whom the pilgrim seeks forgiveness for the remainder of Dhu al-Hijjah, Muharram, Safar, and ten days of Rabi al-Awwal."],[1822,"I saw Abu Hurayrah ؓ lead the people in prayer in Madinah in the evening on the last day of departure, then he said: Indeed Muhammad Aba al-Qasim ﷺ has preceded in good deeds, and Dhakwan, the freedman of Marwan, has preceded the pilgrims and reported about the people's safety."],[1824,"Umar ؓ intended to take the treasure of the Kaaba and spend it in the cause of Allah Almighty. Ubayy b. Kab ؓ said to him: Your two companions preceded you and did not do it; if it were good they would have done it. So he left it."],[1825,"The Throne is over the Sacred Precinct."],[1826,"Allah Almighty sends down every day one hundred mercies: sixty of them for those performing tawaf, twenty for the people of Makkah, and twenty for the rest of the people."],[1827,"I indeed know the most beloved spot on earth to Allah Almighty: it is the House and its surroundings."],[1828,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, chose speech and chose the Quran; He chose the lands and chose the Sacred Precinct; He chose the Sacred Precinct and chose the Mosque; He chose the Mosque and chose the site of the House."],[1830,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade cursing Asad al-Himyari and said: He was the first to clothe the House."],[1831,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ covered the House during his Hajj with striped Yemeni cloths."],[1833,"Ali b. al-Husayn ؓ was asked about praying inside the Ka'bah, and he said: I prayed with my father al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ inside the Ka'bah."],[1834,"Mu'awiyah ؓ came to Makkah and entered the Ka'bah. He sent for Ibn 'Umar ؓ and said: Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray? He replied: Between the two pillars. Then 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr ؓ came and shook the door violently, so it was opened for him. He said: O Mu'awiyah, by Allah, you knew that I knew the same as Ibn 'Umar knew, but you envied me and so you sent for him instead of me."],[1836,"The Prophet ﷺ came to me one day and said: Today I did something I wish I had not done. I entered the House, and I fear that a man from one of the horizons may come and not be able to enter it, and so he will turn back with something in his heart about it."],[1838,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reach al-Safa and begin with it in the daytime. He stood at it, then he kept walking until he reached the bottom of the valley, where he hastened, and the people hastened with him, until he passed beyond the valley, then he walked."],[1839,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ performing sa'i between al-Safa and al-Marwah, saying: The wide watercourse is not to be crossed except at a run."],[1840,"He performed tawaf with the Prophet ﷺ between al-Safa and al-Marwah. He descended and Ibn Umm Maktum hastened, then stopped until the Prophet ﷺ caught up with him. He said: How beloved is Makkah, a valley where my family and visitors are; there I walk without a guide; there my tent pegs are firmly set. The Prophet ﷺ said: And how beloved it is."],[1841,"I was in a small doorway of mine, and I saw the Prophet ﷺ performing sa'i between al-Safa and al-Marwah. I saw him when he came to the bottom of the valley hastening until his knees appeared."],[1842,"She saw the Prophet ﷺ from a small doorway of hers while he was hastening in the bottom of the watercourse, and he was saying..."],[1843,"She looked out from a small doorway of hers and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: Allah the Exalted has prescribed sa'i for you, so perform sa'i. And she heard him ﷺ say while he was hastening: 'My Lord, forgive and have mercy, for You are the Most Mighty, the Most Generous!'"],[1844,"O people of Makkah, your tawaf between al-Safa and al-Marwah is only when you return from Mina."],[1846,"I said to al-Abbas ؓ: Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the guardianship of the Ka'bah for us. He said: He said: I will give you what is better than that: the siqayah. It will provide for you and you will not have to provide for it. I then said to Qabisah: Did he ask the Prophet ﷺ? He said: He did not add to this, and it could only be that he had asked him as much."],[1847,"And Abu Ya'la said: 'Ubaydullah - he is al-Qawariri - narrated to us, Muhammad b. 'Abdullah b. al-Zubayr - he is Abu Ahmad - narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, with it something similar, and he did not say: \"from his father.\""],[1848,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us at the siqayah, and he went to drink from the cistern from which the people drink. We said to him: \"Should we bring out for you, for the people have stirred this with their hands?\" He ﷺ said: \"No, rather give me to drink from this which the people have drunk from.\" He said: So he ﷺ drank from that which the people drank from."],[1849,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the Jamrah, he walked until he came to the House, and circumambulated it seven times, then came to Zamzam. A bucket of water was brought, so he performed ablution, then said: \"Draw water for your siqayah, O Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, for were it not that the people would overcome you over it, I would draw.\""],[1851,"Zamzam is food of nourishment and a healing of sickness."],[1852,"A healing of sickness."],[1854,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas ؓ found a disobedient woman cutting from the hima, so he took her axe and her cloak. She complained about him to 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ, who said: \"Return to her her axe and her cloak!\" He said: \"By Allah, I will not return them; it is booty that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted me!\" He said: Sa'd ؓ made from that axe a shovel and continued to work with it until he died."],[1855,"Whoever you find has cut anything from the hima, then beat him and strip him."],[1856,"When we returned from the expedition of Tabuk, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"This is Taybah; my Lord settled me in it. It expels the filth of its people as the bellows expel the dross of iron. So whoever of you meets anyone of the laggards, let him not speak to him nor sit with him!\""],[1857,"The cities were conquered by the sword, and Madinah was conquered by the Quran."],[1858,"Whoever is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for no one dies in it except that I will be an intercessor or a witness for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[1859,"There were people in Kufah, and he mentioned a hadith, in which: They came to Madinah, and 'Umar ؓ said: \"Indeed Allah, exalted is He, chose for His Prophet Madinah, and it is the least of the earth in food and the saltiest in water, except for this date, for the Dajjal will not enter it nor the plague, if Allah, exalted is He, wills.\""],[1861,"When he returned from the expedition of Tabuk, he looked out over the mountain pass of al-Mabrak, Uhud appeared to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"This is a mountain that loves us and we love it.\""],[1863,"Indeed Ibn ʿUmar ؓ, when he arrived from a journey, would pray two rakʿahs in the Prophet's ﷺ mosque, then he would come to the grave and say: 'Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah. Peace be upon you, O Abu Bakr. Peace be upon you, O my father!'"],[1864,"Indeed, when he arrived from a journey, he would begin with the mosque and pray two rakʿahs in it, then he would come to the grave."],[1865,"Do not make my grave an idol."],[1866,"Whoever visits my grave—or he said: 'Whoever visits me'—I will be a witness for him or an intercessor. And whoever dies in one of the two sacred cities, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will raise him among the secure on the Day of Resurrection."],[1867,"Whoever performs Hajj and then visits me after my death is like the one who visited me during my lifetime."],[1868,"He saw a man coming to a small door that was near the grave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, entering through it and supplicating. He called him and said: 'Shall I not tell you a hadith I heard from my father, from my grandfather ؓ, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: \"Do not take my grave as a place of festivity, and do not make your houses graves. Send blessings upon me, for your blessings and greetings reach me wherever you are.\""],[1869,"And Abu Yaʿla said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[1871,"Whoever performs ablution and perfects his ablution, then comes to the mosque of Quba and prays four rakʿahs in it, that is equal to an ʿUmrah."],[1872,"He used to come to Quba riding and walking."],[1873,"ʿUmar ؓ came to the mosque of Quba and ordered Abu Layla, saying to him: 'Avoid the uncovered places, and sweep the mosque with a palm branch.' He said: 'If this mosque were in one of the horizons or one of the cities, it would be incumbent upon us to come to it.'"],[1875,"A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the Sacred Mosque."],[1876,"A prayer in the Sacred Mosque is more excellent than a hundred thousand prayers in any other mosque."],[1878,"Wajj is sanctified; from it the Lord—Blessed and Exalted—ascended to the lowest heaven on the day He completed the creation of the earth."],[1880,"Seventy prophets prayed in the Mosque of al-Khayf, and between Hira' and Thabir [lie] seventy prophets."],[1881,"The Mosque of al-Khayf is the burial place of seventy prophets."],[1883,"Whoever prays the obligatory prayer in the Mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis in congregation, it is for him as twenty-five thousand prayers; and whoever prays it alone, it is for him as a thousand prayers."],[1884,"O Messenger of God, give us a ruling about Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: It is the land of gathering and dispersal; go to it and pray in it, for a prayer in it is like a thousand prayers elsewhere. She said: O Messenger of God, what if we cannot bear the journey to it? He said: Then let him send oil to be lit in it; whoever sends something to it is like one who prays to God in it."],[1887,"Uthman b. Affan ؓ bought a garden from a man, and he bargained with him until the price was settled. Then he said: Give me your hand. He said: They would not conclude a sale except by a hand-clasp. When the seller saw that, he said: No, by God, I will not sell it until you increase me ten thousand. Uthman turned to Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ and said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: God, Exalted, will admit into Paradise a man who is easy-going when selling, buying, judging, and collecting. Then he said: Take the ten thousand so that I may deserve this word which I heard from the Prophet."],[1888,"Uthman b. Affan ؓ came as a pilgrim, and when he finished his hajj, he came to some land at al-Ta'if, and there was a piece of land adjacent to his land which he sought to buy. The difference between them in price was ten thousand. When Uthman ؓ placed his foot in the stirrup, he said to a man among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ: Did you hear the Prophet ﷺ say: May God have mercy on a servant who is easy-going in selling, easy-going in buying, easy-going in settling, easy-going in collecting? The man said: Yes. So Uthman ؓ said: Bring the man back to me. Then he gave him the ten thousand and took the land."],[1889,"He bargained with a man over some land until the sale was concluded, or nearly concluded. The man said: By God, I will not give it to you until you increase me ten thousand. Uthman ؓ turned to a man and said: Do you know that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: May God have mercy on a man who is easy-going in collecting, easy-going in demanding? They said: Yes. So he increased him ten thousand and took the land."],[1890,"I set out to Madinah and stopped at the valley. There were two men between whom was a single goat, and the buyer was saying to the seller: Be fair in my purchase. Then a man of good physique appeared, and the buyer said: O Messenger of God, tell him to be fair in my purchase. The Messenger of God ﷺ stretched out his hand and said: You own your wealth. I hope to meet God Almighty on the Day of Resurrection with no one seeking anything from me, that I wronged him in wealth, blood, or honor except by his right. May God have mercy on a man who is easy in selling, easy in buying, easy in taking, easy in giving, easy in collecting."],[1892,"I left the mosque and found a man calling behind me: Raise your lower garment, for it is more reverent to your Lord and purer for your garment, and trim your hair if you are a Muslim. So I walked behind him while he wore a lower garment and a cloak and carried a whip. I said: Who is this? It was said: Ali, the Commander of the Faithful... Then he mentioned the hadith, and in it: Then he came to a cloth merchant's house and said: O sheikh, be fair in my purchase of a shirt for three dirhams. When he recognized him, he did not sell him anything. Then he came to another, and when he recognized him, he did not sell him anything. Then he came to a young boy and bought from him a shirt for three dirhams, and he wore it between the wrists and the ankles. The owner of the garment came, and it was said: Your son sold a shirt to the Commander of the Faithful for three dirhams. He said: Why didn't you take two dirhams from him? So he took the dirham, then brought it to Ali ؓ while he was sitting with the Muslims, and said: Keep this dirham. He said: What is its matter? He said: The shirt was worth two dirhams—meaning my son sold it to you for three dirhams. He ؓ said: He sold me with my consent, and he took with his consent."],[1893,"Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Ammar narrated to us, Mu'afa b. Imran narrated to us, Mukhtar al-Tammar narrated to us, with it the hadith of Tariq b. Abdullah al-Muharibi, indicating the validity of hand-to-hand transaction. It will come, God willing, soon in the chapter on measuring for one who receives full measure and the validity of hand-to-hand transaction."],[1895,"The one who is cheated is neither praiseworthy nor rewarded."],[1897,"The Prophet ﷺ gave his maternal aunt a slave boy, and said: \"Do not make him a butcher, nor a cupper, nor a goldsmith.\""],[1898,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped on the two jugular veins and between the shoulders, and he gave the cupper his wage; had it been unlawful he would not have given it to him."],[1899,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade female singers and wailing women, and their purchase, their sale, and trade in them. He said: \"Their earnings are unlawful.\""],[1900,"Indeed, Allah — Blessed and Exalted — loves, when one of you does a deed, that he perfects it."],[1902,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us... and he mentioned a long hadith, in which he said: \"Whoever earns unlawful wealth, Allah will not accept from him any charity, nor manumission, nor Hajj, nor ‘Umrah, and Allah — Mighty and Majestic — will record for him sins in proportion to that, and whatever remains of it at his death will be his provision to the Fire. And whoever buys stolen property, knowing it is stolen, is like the one who stole it in its shame and sin. And whoever buys stolen goods knowing they are stolen, is like the one who stole them in their shame and sin.\""],[1903,"Whoever buys stolen goods knowing they are stolen has shared in their sin and shame."],[1904,"Whoever buys stolen goods knowing they are stolen has shared in their sin and shame."],[1905,"Any man who earns wealth lawfully and feeds himself, or clothes someone beneath him among the creatures of Allah Most High, there is purification for him in that."],[1907,"Do not be impressed by a man with broad forearms who sheds blood, for he has with Allah Most High a killer who does not die. And do not be impressed by a man who earns wealth unlawfully, for if he spends it or gives it in charity it will not be accepted from him, and if he leaves it, it will not be blessed for him, and if anything remains of it, it will be his provision to the Fire."],[1908,"Wealth is not from abundance of goods, but wealth is self-contentment."],[1910,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the mosque of al-Khayf, and his companions said to me: \"Come here, O Wathilah — that is, move away from his face.\" But he ﷺ said: \"Leave him, for he has only come to ask.\" So I drew near and said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about a matter we will take from you after you are gone.\" He ﷺ said: \"Consult your own self.\" I said: \"How can I do that?\" He ﷺ said: \"Leave what makes you doubtful for what does not make you doubtful, even if the muftis give you fatwas.\" I said: \"How can I know that?\" He ﷺ said: \"Put your hand on your heart, for the heart is at peace with the lawful and is not at peace with the unlawful. Indeed, the piety of a Muslim is to leave the minor for fear of falling into the major.\" I said: \"Then who is the covetous?\" He ﷺ said: \"The one who seeks earnings from unlawful sources.\" I said: \"Then who is the scrupulous?\" He ﷺ said: \"The one who stops at the doubtful.\" I said: \"Then who is the believer?\" He ﷺ said: \"The one whom people trust with their wealth and their lives.\" I said: \"Then who is the Muslim?\" He ﷺ said: \"The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.\" I said: \"Then which jihad is best?\" He ﷺ said: \"A word of truth in the presence of a tyrannical ruler.\""],[1912,"I and some women from the Ansar entered upon Asma’ bint Makhrabah, the mother of Abu Jahl. Her son ‘Abdullah b. Abi Rabi’ah used to send her perfume from Yemen, and she would sell it until the time of the soldiers' stipend. She said: So I bought from her, and she weighed for me, and I put it in bottles like others did. Then she said to me: \"Write down my right against you.\" So I said — meaning to the scribe — \"Write it against al-Rubayyi‘ bint Mu‘awwidh b. ‘Afra’.\" She said: \"You are like the daughter of the killer of his master.\" I said: \"By Allah, I am not the daughter of the killer of his master; rather I am the daughter of the killer of his slave.\" She said: \"By Allah, I will never sell you anything ever.\" I said: \"And by Allah, I will never buy from you anything ever.\" And by Allah, it was not perfume or fragrance there. Then she said: \"By Allah, O my son, I have never smelled a perfume more fragrant than it. But when she said what she said, I got angry and I said what I said.\""],[1914,"The people of Paradise do not buy and sell; if they did buy and sell, they would trade only in cloth."],[1916,"O Allah, bless my Ummah in its early morning."],[1917,"O Allah, bless my Ummah in its early morning."],[1918,"Wealth is not from abundance of worldly goods, but wealth is self-sufficiency. Allah, the Exalted, gives His servant what He has decreed for him of provision, so be moderate in seeking. Take what is lawful and leave what is forbidden."],[1919,"Allah, the Exalted, sends down provision according to the need, and sends down patience according to the affliction."],[1921,"I asked Abu Ja'far—meaning Muhammad b. Ali b. al-Husayn ؓ—what is mukhabarah? He said: It is sharecropping for a portion of the produce."],[1922,"A man had land, and another man said to him: Would you like me to sharecrop with you, so that whatever Allah brings forth is divided between me and you? He said: Yes, until I ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He went to Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ, and they said: Ask the Prophet ﷺ. He asked him, and he did not reply to him at all. He said to them: He ﷺ did not reply to me at all! They said to him: Go ahead, for if it were forbidden he would have prohibited you from it. So he sharecropped with him until his crop swayed or turned green, and it was on the way of the Prophet ﷺ. He passed by it one day and said: Whose land is this? They said: It belongs to so-and-so; so-and-so sharecropped it. He ﷺ said: Summon them both! They both came, and he said to the owner of the land: Return to this man what he spent on your land, and you may keep what your land produced!"],[1923,"My paternal uncle sent me with a servant of his to Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, and he said: What do you say about sharecropping? He said: Ibn Umar ؓ did not see any harm in it, until he was told a hadith from Rafi' b. Khadij ؓ about it: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Banu Harithah and saw a crop on the land of Zuhayr, and said: How good is the land of Zuhayr? They said: It is not Zuhayr's. He said: Is it not the land of Zuhayr? They said: Yes, but he sharecropped it to so-and-so. He said: Return to him his expenses, and take your crop. Rafi' ؓ said: So we took our crop and returned to him his expenses."],[1924,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade renting out land for a portion of its produce and leasing it, unless a man buys land or it is lent to him. He said: My father lent some land, and the borrower cultivated it and built a house on it. One day my father rode by and saw the building, and said: What is this? He was told: The one you lent your land to built it. He said: As compensation for what I lent him? So he ordered the building to be demolished."],[1925,"Seek provision in the hidden treasures of the earth."],[1926,"A man took land from Ibn Umar ؓ and stipulated that he would not put manure on it. He said: Nothing improves it except that. He said: If nothing improves it except that, then leave it."],[1928,"He sat with me while I was in the mosque of Basra in the time of al-Hajjaj b. Yusuf, and in his hand was a staff and a scroll he was carrying. He mentioned a hadith in which: I entered Madinah with my father when I was a young boy, with camels we had brought to Madinah to sell. He said: Talhah b. Ubaydillah ؓ was a friend of my father, so we stayed with him. My father said: O Abu Muhammad, come out with us and sell our camels for us, for we have no knowledge of this market. He said: As for me selling for you, no; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a townsman from selling for a bedouin. But I will go out with you both to the market, and if I approve of a man to trade with you, I will instruct you to sell to him. He said: He came out with us and sat in a corner of the market, and men bargained with us for our camels. When a man offered us what satisfied us, we went to him and sought his advice about selling. He said: Sell to him, for I am satisfied with his trustworthiness and his prayer. He said: So we sold to him and took what was ours."],[1930,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a gathering of the Ansar on Thursday night in Ramadan—and he did not fast Ramadan after that—saying: Barley for barley, qafiz for qafiz, hand to hand, and any excess is usury."],[1931,"Gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, salt for salt, dates for dates, like for like, measure for measure. Whoever increases or asks for increase has engaged in usury."],[1932,"I asked Jabir b. Abd Allah ؓ about wheat for dates with excess, hand to hand. He said: \"During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ we used to buy a sa' of wheat for six sa's of dates, hand to hand. If it is a single type, then there is no good in it except like for like.\""],[1933,"Ibn Abbas ؓ used to sell dates from his slaves for one, two, or three years. Jabir ؓ said to him about that, and he said: \"Do you not know that there is no usury between a slave and his master?\""],[1934,"Ibn Abbas ؓ used to sell fruit from his slaves before it was edible, and he did not consider usury between himself and his slave."],[1935,"We were in need, so I took my wife's two anklets in the year in which Abu Bakr ؓ was appointed caliph. Abu Bakr ؓ met me and said: \"What is this?\" I said: \"The tribe is in need of spending money.\" He said: \"I have silver coins with which I want silver.\" He called for a scale and placed the two anklets in one pan and the silver coins in the other. The two anklets outweighed by about a daniq, so he cut it off. I said: \"O Caliph of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, it is lawful for you!\" He said: \"O Abu Rafi', if you make it lawful, Allah Almighty will not make it lawful. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Gold for gold, weight for weight, and silver for silver, weight for weight; the one who gives extra and the one who takes extra are in the Fire.'\""],[1936,"And al-Nadr b. Muhammad informed us, from Muhammad b. al-Sa'ib, from Ibn al-Sa'ib, from Usamah b. Zayd, from Abu Rafi' ؓ with this hadith, similarly."],[1937,"And Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah said: Ya'la b. Ubayd narrated to us, and he mentioned it."],[1938,"And al-Harith said: Abd al-Wahhab b. Ata' narrated to us, Muhammad b. al-Sa'ib al-Kalbi narrated to us, and he mentioned it."],[1939,"Abu Ya'la said: al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, al-Kalbi informed us, with it."],[1940,"He wrote to the commanders of the armies in Syria: \"You have descended upon a land of usury. Do not buy gold for gold except weight for weight, nor silver for silver except weight for weight, nor food for food except measure for measure.\""],[1941,"Ikrimah, the freedman of Ibn Abbas ؓ, came to Basra and we sat with him in the congregational mosque. He said: \"Will you not forbid this old man of yours—meaning al-Hasan b. Abi al-Hasan—who claims that what people exchange hand to hand, silver for silver and gold for gold, is forbidden, while I testify that Ibn Abbas ؓ permitted it?\" Abu Sa'id said: I said to him: \"Woe to you! Do you not know that I was sitting at his head and you at his feet when a man came and stood before you. I said: 'What do you need?' He said: 'I want to ask Ibn Abbas ؓ about gold for gold.' I said: 'Go, for he claims there is no harm in it.' He uncovered his turban from his face, then Ibn Abbas ؓ sat up and said: 'I seek forgiveness from Allah. By Allah, I used to think that whatever Muslims exchange hand to hand is lawful, until I heard Abd Allah b. Umar and Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ preserve from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what I did not preserve. I seek forgiveness from Allah.'\""],[1942,"I heard Ibn Abbas ؓ three days before his death saying: \"I seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him regarding currency exchange.\""],[1943,"Some ten and odd of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ came to Ibn ʿAbbās ؓ and said: We are older than you and know more about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than you. What do you think about when you permit money-changing? We heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding it."],[1944,"I asked Saʿīd b. al-Musayyab about a sheep for two sheep on credit. He said: A man asked ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ, and ʿUmar ؓ said: The last thing Allah revealed was the verse on usury, and the Prophet ﷺ was taken before he explained it, so leave usury and doubtful matters."],[1945,"I had low-quality dates, so I bought from the market better dates than them for half their measure. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him what I had done. He ﷺ said: Go and take back your dates and return these! So I did. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Dates for dates, like for like; wheat for wheat, like for like; barley for barley, like for like; salt for salt, like for like; gold for gold, weight for weight; silver for silver, weight for weight. Whatever is extra is usury!"],[1946,"1665 1375 / 2 - Abu Yaʿlā narrated it: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarīr narrated to us, with it."],[1947,"The Prophet ﷺ had dates with me, and I found better ones, two ṣāʿs for one ṣāʿ, so I bought them. I brought them to the Prophet ﷺ and he said: Where did you get this, O Bilāl? I said: I bought it, one ṣāʿ for two ṣāʿs. He ﷺ said: Return it – or give back – to us our dates."],[1948,"A dirham for a dirham, and whatever is extra between them is usury."],[1949,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and mentioned a long hadith – in which he said: Whoever consumes usury, Allah will fill his belly with fire according to how much he consumed. And if he earns wealth from it, Allah will not accept anything of his deeds, and he will remain under the curse of Allah and His angels as long as he has a carat of it."],[1950,"Bilāl ؓ had worm-eaten dates, so he sold two ṣāʿs for one ṣāʿ."],[1951,"And I asked him – meaning Abū Hurayrah ؓ – about buying a sheep for two sheep on credit. He said: No, except hand to hand."],[1952,"If he cannot separate the gold from the silver, there is no harm in selling it for gold or silver."],[1953,"ʿAlī and ʿUthmān ؓ forbade money-changing."],[1954,"The Prophet ﷺ and Abū Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ forbade money-changing."],[1955,"I saw thirty of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, all of them forbidding money exchange (sarf); among them was Mu'adh b. Jabal."],[1956,"He met Ibn 'Abbas ؓ and asked him about money exchange (sarf), and he said: There is no harm in it. Then it reached him that he retracted that statement."],[1957,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a portion of a slaughtered camel being sold for its offspring, and he forbade them from that."],[1958,"He was asked about one camel for two camels on credit, so he said: The increase is permissible when some of it is balanced by some; but as for meat set aside, there is no harm in it."],[1959,"Indeed 'Ali ؓ sold one camel for two camels together, deferred to a term."],[1960,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of animals for animals."],[1961,"Silver for silver, gold for gold, dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, salt for salt, like for like, in hand-to-hand exchange, or weight for weight."],[1962,"I slaughtered a camel during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and divided it into portions. A man said: Give me a portion of the portions for a sheep. The Prophet ﷺ said: This is not permissible."],[1963,"Dates for dates: it is more deserving to be riba than silver for silver."],[1965,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ twice... And he mentioned the hadith. He said: We came in a caravan from al-Rabadhah until we disembarked near Madinah, and with us was our lady companion. He said: While we were sitting, a man came to us wearing two white garments. He greeted us and we returned his greeting. He said: From where have the people come? We said: From al-Rabadhah, and south of al-Rabadhah. He said: And with us was a red camel. He said: Will you sell me the camel? We said: Yes. He said: For how much? We said: For such-and-such sa's of dates. He said: He did not reduce anything for us, and said: I have taken it. Then he took hold of the camel's head until he entered Madinah and disappeared from us. We blamed each other, saying: You gave your camel to a man you do not know! The lady companion said: Do not blame yourselves, for I have seen a face that would never betray you. I have never seen a man whose face more resembled the full moon on the night of Badr than his face. When the evening came, a man came and said: Peace be upon you. Indeed I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to you, and he commands you to eat until you are full, and to take full measure until you receive your due. So we ate until we were full, and took full measure until we received our due. When the next day came, we entered Madinah, and behold the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing on the pulpit delivering a sermon to the people."],[1966,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ twice. Once I saw him in the market of Dhu'l-Majaz while he was on a mount and its hocks had been bloodied... And he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then we came after that and disembarked at Madinah, and a man came out to us and said: From where have you come? We said: From al-Rabadhah, or from its vicinity. He said: Do you have anything you would sell? We said: Yes, this camel. He said: For how much? We said: For such-and-such wasqs of dates. He took hold of its halter and pulled it, and then entered Madinah with it. I said: What have we done? We sold our camel to a man we do not know! He said: And with us was a lady companion in the side of the tent, and she said: I guarantee the price of the camel. I have seen the face of a man like the full moon on the night of Badr; he will not cheat you. When morning came, a man came with dates and said: I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to you, that you eat from these dates until you are full, and that you take full measure until you receive your due. He said: And we did so."],[1968,"About the man who buys a slave girl on condition that she not be sold or given away? She said: I disliked that, and I disliked the condition."],[1969,"Umar ؓ gave me a servant, and Abdullah said, 'Will you sell her?' She said, 'I would not sell you a servant that the Commander of the Faithful gave me.' He kept at her until he bought her from her, and stipulated for her her service until she buys a servant. A spy informed Umar ؓ of that, so he went to him in the evening or morning. Umar ؓ said to him, 'I have heard that you bought the slave girl of Zaynab!' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then do not approach her, and no one has any right in her.'"],[1971,"Hudhayfah ؓ bought a she-camel from two men of al-Nakha', and stipulated for them their satisfaction with the payment, so he brought them to his house and took out for them a purse. They fought over it, then he took out for them another purse, and they fought over it. Hudhayfah ؓ said, 'I seek refuge with Allah from you two.'"],[1972,"Hudhayfah ؓ bought a she-camel from a man for four hundred dirhams, and stipulated for him his satisfaction with the payment. He brought a man from Isfahan who was more knowledgeable about weighing than him, and Hudhayfah ؓ took out a purse for him, and he accepted most of it. Then he took out another purse for him, and he accepted most of it. Then he took out a third purse for him, and he accepted most of it. He said, 'I seek refuge with Allah from you two.'"],[1974,"Ibn Umar ؓ sent to Rafi' b. Khadij ؓ asking him about the statement of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the land of the Persians, its purchase, and its renting. Rafi' b. Khadij ؓ said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of the land of the Persians, its purchase, and its renting.'"],[1975,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him, he forbade him from a loan and a sale, a condition and a sale, and selling what you do not have."],[1976,"The price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the price of wine are forbidden."],[1977,"He asked Abu Hurayrah ؓ about buying milk in the udders of sheep. He said, 'There is no good in it.'"],[1978,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of unborn offspring—meaning the purchase of what is in the wombs."],[1979,"He prohibited selling fruit until its ripeness is apparent."],[1980,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited that deferred for deferred be sold, debt for debt. In the wording of Waki', the other said: 'That deferred for deferred be sold, which is debt for debt.'"],[1981,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited that deferred for deferred be sold, debt for debt. In the wording of Waki', the other said: 'That deferred for deferred be sold, which is debt for debt.'"],[1982,"Whoever buys a sheep that has been kept unmilked, he has the choice for three days. If he approves of it, he keeps it; and if he returns it, he returns with it a saa' of dates."],[1983,"Do not practice touch-selling, do not bid against each other, do not sell uncertainty, and a townsperson must not sell for a desert dweller. Whoever buys a sheep that has been kept unmilked, let him milk it for three days. If he returns it, let him return with it a saa' of dates."],[1984,"The stray (animal) is to be returned."],[1985,"Fruit is not to be sold until its ripeness appears. Ibn ʿAbbās ؓ used to say: Until it is edible."],[1986,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the qafīz of the miller."],[1987,"I was a goat-herder, and al-Barāʾ b. ʿĀzib ؓ forbade me, saying: This is not lawful."],[1989,"ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān ؓ used to forbid hoarding. My father said: They did not consider hoarding except in food and condiments."],[1990,"ʿUthmān ؓ used to forbid hoarding, then al-Zubayr ؓ spoke to him about a client of his or a person, and he left him."],[1991,"I used to buy leaves and date-stones for Saʿīd b. al-Musayyab, and he would hoard them."],[1992,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that food be hoarded."],[1993,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade hoarding in the town."],[1995,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her the harvest of forty wasqs of dates and twenty wasqs of barley in Khaybar. ʿĀṣim b. ʿAdī came to her and said: If you wish, I will pay you here and receive it from you in Khaybar. She said: Until I ask the Commander of the Believers. She mentioned that to him, and he disliked it, saying: How about the guarantee?"],[1997,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ paid in advance to a Jewish man called Yāmīn for dates to a named term. The Jew said: From the dates of the garden of the Banū so-and-so? The Prophet ﷺ said: As for the dates of the garden of the Banū so-and-so, then no."],[1999,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade muzābanah and muḥāqalah."],[2000,"Indeed his father used to dislike that (fodder) be sold in its place of growth."],[2001,"That he disliked selling ripe dates except (in) an entire cutting at a time."],[2002,"That he was asked about selling ripe dates, and he said: 'One cutting, not two cuttings.'"],[2003,"Whoever withholds surplus water, Allah - Blessed and Exalted - will withhold His surplus from him on the Day of Resurrection."],[2005,"The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters. Whoever avoids them is more pious for his religion, and whoever falls into them is on the verge of falling into major sins, like a shepherd grazing near a sanctuary is on the verge of entering it. Indeed, every king has a sanctuary, and Allah's sanctuary is His limits."],[2006,"And Abu Ya'la narrated it: Muhammad b. al-Faraj narrated to us, Muhammad b. al-Zibriqan narrated to us, Musa b. 'Ubaydah narrated to us, Sa'd b. Ibrahim informed me, from someone who informed him, from 'Ammar b. Yasir ؓ something similar."],[2007,"I came at night, I and Sa'd ؓ, to a garden with palm trees, and we looked for the owner of the garden but did not find him. Sa'd ؓ said to me: 'If it pleases you to be a true Muslim, then do not eat anything from it.' He said: 'So we remained hungry.'"],[2009,"Indeed, this time of yours is a time of hardship, in which the believer clings to what is in his hand out of fear of spending. Allah - Mighty and Majestic - said: 'And whatever you spend of anything, He will replace it; and He is the best of providers.' He said: 'And the worst of people will be witnessed selling to every distressed person. Indeed, selling to the distressed is unlawful; indeed, selling to the distressed is unlawful. The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim; he does not wrong him nor forsake him. If you have any kindness, then bestow it upon your brother; otherwise, do not add destruction to his destruction.'"],[2010,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ at the mosque of al-Khayf, and his companions said to me: 'Move aside, O Wathilah,' meaning, 'Move away from the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Leave him; he has only come to ask.' He said: 'So I drew near and said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about a matter we will take from you after you are gone?' He ﷺ said: 'Let your own self give you a ruling.' I said: 'How can I do that?' He ﷺ said: 'Leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt, even if the muftis give you rulings.' I said: 'How can I do that?' He ﷺ said: 'Place your hand on your heart, for the heart finds tranquility in the lawful and does not find tranquility in the unlawful. Indeed, the piety of a Muslim is to leave the small (sin) for fear of falling into the large (sin).' I said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom, who is the greedy?' He ﷺ said: 'The one who seeks gain from other than its lawful means.' I said: 'Who is the pious?' He ﷺ said: 'The one who stops at the doubtful.' I said: 'Who is the believer?' He ﷺ said: 'The one whom people trust with their blood.' I said: 'Who is the Muslim?' He ﷺ said: 'The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.' I said: 'Which jihad is best?' He ﷺ said: 'A word of truth in the presence of a tyrannical ruler.'"],[2012,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by wheat that had been rained on, while its top was dry wheat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What made you do that? Why did you not leave it so that your brothers could buy what they recognize?'"],[2013,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a sermon and mentioned the hadith in full, and in it: 'Whoever deceives a Muslim in a sale or purchase is not from us, and he will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection with the Jews, because they are the most deceitful of people towards the Muslims.'"],[2014,"Whoever deceives is not from us."],[2015,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man selling food. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O owner of the food, is the bottom of the food like its top?\" He said, \"Yes.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever cheats the Muslims is not one of them!\""],[2016,"I went out of the mosque, and there was a man calling behind me: \"Raise your lower garment...\" Then he mentioned the hadith: That it was Ali ؓ. He said: Then he ended up at the camel market and said, \"Sell and do not swear, for an oath sells the goods but wipes out the blessing.\" Then he came to a date seller, and there was a servant girl crying. He said, \"What is the matter with you?\" She said, \"This man sold me dates for a dirham, but my master refused to accept them.\" He said, \"Take it and give her her dirham, for she has no authority.\" It was as if he refused, so I said, \"Do you not know who this is?\" He said, \"No.\" I said, \"This is Ali, the Commander of the Faithful!\" So he poured back his dates and gave her her dirham. Then he ؓ passed by the date sellers and said, \"Feed the poor and your earnings will increase.\""],[2017,"For I would love for you to be pleased with me, O Commander of the Faithful. He ؓ said, \"I will only be pleased with you when you give them their full due.\" And he added after that his saying: \"Your earnings will increase.\" Then he passed by, accompanied by the Muslims, until he reached the fish sellers. He said, \"No floating fish is to be sold in our market.\" Then he came to the cloth merchant's shop—which is the market of fine linen—and came to an old man and said, \"O old man, be good in selling me a shirt.\""],[2018,"Indeed, God does not love the obscene and foul-mouthed, nor the loud-mouthed in the markets!"],[2019,"Ibn Umar ؓ passed by a man selling some small sheep of his. He said, \"For how much are you selling these sheep of yours?\" He said, \"For such and such.\" Ibn Umar ؓ said, \"I will take them for such and such.\" So he swore not to sell them. Ibn Umar ؓ went off to relieve himself, then passed by him again. He said, \"O Abu Abd al-Rahman, take them for what you offered me.\" He said, \"You swore an oath, so I will not help Satan against you by accepting.\""],[2020,"None of you should buy against the purchase of his brother, nor propose against the proposal of his brother."],[2021,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"O assembly of merchants, I am throwing between your shoulders: Do not go out to meet the caravans, and no settled person should sell for a bedouin.\""],[2022,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was at a funeral and said, \"Which of you will go to Madinah and leave no idol there but break it, no image but deface it, and no grave but level it?\" A man from the group stood up and said, \"I will, O Messenger of God.\" The man went, but it was as if he feared the city and returned. Ali ؓ went and then returned, saying, \"I did not come to you, O Messenger of God, until I had left no idol there but I broke it, no grave but I leveled it, and no image but I defaced it.\" He said, \"Whoever returns to making any of these...\" and he spoke harshly about it. And he said to Ali: \"O Ali, do not be a seducer, nor arrogant, nor a merchant—except a merchant of good—for those are the ones outstripped in deeds!\""],[2023,"Nine-tenths of provision is in trade."],[2024,"The merchant is a sinner, except one who takes the truth and gives it."],[2026,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave us a sermon... and he mentioned a long hadith, in which [he said]: \"Whoever makes things difficult for his Muslim brother, God will strip away his provision from him, ruin his livelihood, and leave him to his own self. Whoever harms a Muslim is not of me, and I am not of him in this world and the Hereafter. Whoever delays payment to his creditor while able to pay, upon him is the sin of a tax collector.\" Awf b. Malik al-Ashja'i stood up to him and said, \"What is the sin of a tax collector?\" He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The sin of a tax collector is that upon him every day is the curse of God, the angels, and all people. And whoever God curses, you will never find a helper for him.\""],[2027,"Whoever lends people a debt, and God Almighty knows that he intends to repay it, but his term comes before that, God Almighty will make this person pleased with his right and overlook him. And whoever lends people a debt, and God Almighty knows that he does not intend to repay it, God will exact retribution from him, saying: 'You thought that I would not exact retribution for him from you.'"],[2028,"A man said: 'O Messenger of God, I owe the Hajj of Islam and I owe a debt?' He ﷺ said: 'Pay off your debt.'"],[2029,"Al-Aswad b. Yazid used to borrow from a client of al-Nakha', a merchant, and when his stipend came he would pay him back. When his stipend came he said to him: 'If you wish, postpone it for us, for we have obligations in this stipend.' The merchant said: 'I will not do that.' So al-Aswad paid him five hundred dirhams, until when the merchant took them he said to him: 'Take it; here you are.' Al-Aswad said: 'I asked you this and you refused?' The merchant said to him: 'I heard you narrate to us from 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud ؓ that the Prophet ﷺ used to say: Whoever lends twice, he will have the like of the reward of one of them as if he had given it in charity.'"],[2031,"Every loan that brings benefit is usury."],[2033,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered the Jews to be expelled, they said: 'We have debts owed to us!' He said: 'Take and deduct.'"],[2035,"No one should be left in distress in Islam — or he said: left with no way out."],[2036,"Negligence is in three things — and he mentioned them. And a man's negligence about himself regarding debt until it overwhelms him."],[2037,"He mentioned that a man died during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ and left behind two dinars as a debt, and he had no means to pay it. The Messenger of God ﷺ refused to pray over him and said: 'Pray over your companion!' Abu Qatadah ؓ stood up and said: 'I will pay it on his behalf.' So the Messenger of God ﷺ stood and prayed over him."],[2038,"Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad b. 'Isa narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah, and he did not name Abu Qatadah:"],[2039,"I attended a funeral in which the Prophet ﷺ was present. When it was placed, the Prophet ﷺ asked: 'Does he owe a debt?' They said: 'Yes.' So he turned away from it and said ﷺ: 'Pray over your companion!' When 'Ali ؓ saw him turn away, he said: 'O Prophet of God, he is free of his debt; I am guarantor for what he owes.' So the Prophet ﷺ came and prayed over him, then he left and said: 'O 'Ali, may God and Islam reward you well. May God release your pledge on the Day of Resurrection as you released the pledge of your Muslim brother. There is no servant who pays off his brother's debt except that God releases his pledge on the Day of Resurrection.' A man from the Ansar stood and said: 'O Messenger of God, is this for 'Ali specifically?' He ﷺ said: 'No, rather for all Muslims.'"],[2040,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a man to pray over him, and he said: 'Does he owe a debt?' They said: 'Yes.' He ﷺ said: 'If you guarantee his debt, I will pray over him.'"],[2041,"Whoever of you is able to die with no debt upon him, let him do so, for I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ when a man's funeral was brought to him and he had a debt, and he said: 'I will not pray over him until you guarantee his debt, for my prayer over him benefits him.' They did not guarantee his debt, and he did not pray over him, and he said: 'He is held in pledge in his grave.'"],[2042,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a funeral to pray over it. He said: 'Does he owe a debt?' They said: 'Yes.' He ﷺ said: 'Gabriel — peace and blessings be upon him — forbade me from praying over anyone who owes a debt.' Then he ﷺ said: 'The debtor is held in pledge in his grave until it is paid off for him.'"],[2043,"The Messenger of God ﷺ delivered a sermon to us... and he mentioned a long hadith, and in it: 'Whoever lends to one in distress and is gracious in requesting repayment, let him begin his deeds anew, and for him with God Almighty is, for every dirham, a thousand qintars in Paradise. Whoever lends to his Muslim brother, for him for every dirham is the weight of Mount Uhud, Hira', and Mount Sinai in good deeds. If he is gentle with him in requesting repayment after its due date, charity is recorded for him every day, and he will pass over the Sirat like flashing lightning, with no reckoning and no punishment. And whoever's Muslim brother is in need of a loan, and he does not lend to him while he has it, God will forbid Paradise to him on the Day when He will recompense the doers of good.'"],[2044,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas ؓ came to demand a debt owed to him by a man, and they said: 'He has gone out.' He said: 'I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: If a man were killed in the path of God Almighty, then brought to life, then killed, then brought to life, then killed, he would not enter Paradise until his debt is settled.'"],[2045,"Whoever loves to be shaded, or for God to shade him from the heat of Hell or from the scorching wind of Hell? All the people said: 'We do, O Messenger of God!' He said: 'Whoever grants respite to one in difficulty or forgives his debtor.'"],[2047,"The Messenger of God ﷺ bought from a Bedouin a camel or a she-camel for a wasq of 'ajwah dates, but he did not have them with him. The Bedouin came to him to demand payment, and he postponed him. The Bedouin shouted: 'What treachery! What treachery!' The companions of Muhammad scolded him, but he ﷺ said: 'Leave him, for the one who has a right has a say.' That happened two or three times. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Take him to Khawlah bt. Hakim—she was among the first of the female emigrants—and ask her for a loan, for she collects 'ajwah dates.' They went to her, and she paid him in full. He returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'You have paid in full and have been generous.' He ﷺ said: 'Are not those among you the best of you with God? Indeed, the best of creation with God are those who fulfill and are generous.'"],[2048,"The Messenger of God ﷺ borrowed a camel from a Bedouin, and he mentioned something similar, and in it he said: 'So the companions of Muhammad ﷺ scolded him.'"],[2049,"Whoever grants respite to one in difficulty, for him is a charity for every day. Then after that he said: 'Whoever grants respite to one in difficulty, for him for every day is the like of what he granted respite for.' Buraydah ؓ said: 'I said: O Messenger of God, what is this?' He said: 'A charity is brought for him every day before the term, and after the term a charity is brought for him every day equal to what he granted respite for.'"],[2050,"Whoever loves his supplication to be answered, let him relieve one in difficulty."],[2051,"A man was taken to the gate of Paradise. He raised his head and saw written on the gate of Paradise: 'Charity is multiplied ten times, and a single loan is multiplied eighteen times, because the one seeking a loan does not come to you except while he is in need, whereas charity may fall into the hand of the rich.'"],[2052,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he was detaining a man for two uqiyyahs, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Thus (it is done).'"],[2054,"Whoever sells a slave who has property, his property belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates it. And whoever sells palm trees that have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates it. The Messenger of God ﷺ judged accordingly."],[2056,"The borrowed item is to be returned, and the gift of a milch animal is to be returned."],[2058,"Al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib ؓ, when he gave money as a speculative partnership, stipulated upon his partner that he should not travel by land or by sea, nor descend into a valley with it, nor buy with it an animal with a wet liver (i.e., livestock). If he did that, he would be liable. His condition was brought to the Prophet ﷺ and he approved it."],[2060,"The Prophet ﷺ judged concerning a man who was found to have no means to pay, and some of his creditors found their goods intact with him, so he ruled that he should take back his goods if he found them."],[2061,"Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ was a generous, young, handsome man, one of the finest youths of his people. He would not hold onto anything, and he kept borrowing until he had consumed all his wealth in debt. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him to request his creditors to reduce the debt for him, but they refused. If they would have left anything for anyone on account of anyone, they would have left it for Mu'adh ؓ on account of the Prophet ﷺ. So the Prophet ﷺ sold all his property to pay off his debt, until Mu'adh ؓ stood with nothing. Then, in the year of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet ﷺ sent him as a governor over a group of the people of Yemen, to compensate him. Mu'adh ؓ remained in Yemen as a governor—and he was the first to trade with the wealth of Allah, the Exalted—and he remained until he acquired wealth, and until the Prophet ﷺ passed away. When he returned, 'Umar said to Abu Bakr ؓ: 'Send for this man and leave him what is enough for his living, and take the rest.' Abu Bakr ؓ said: 'The Prophet ﷺ sent him only to compensate him, and I will not take anything from him unless he gives it to me.' So 'Umar ؓ went to him, when Abu Bakr ؓ did not comply with him, and 'Umar mentioned that to Mu'adh ؓ. Mu'adh ؓ said: 'The Prophet ﷺ sent me to compensate me, and I will not do it.' Then Mu'adh met 'Umar ؓ and said: 'I have obeyed you, and I will do what you commanded me. I saw in a dream that I was in a pool of water and feared drowning, and you saved me from it, O 'Umar.' So Mu'adh came to Abu Bakr ؓ and mentioned that to him, and he swore that he had not hidden anything from him, until his whip was made clear to him. Abu Bakr ؓ said: 'By Allah, I will not take it from you; I have given it to you as a gift.' 'Umar ؓ said: 'Now it is good and lawful.' Then Mu'adh ؓ went out to Syria."],[2062,"Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ was a generous young man, the finest of the youths of his people. He continued until he drowned his wealth in debt. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke to his creditors, and if anyone would have been left for the sake of anyone, Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ would have been left for the sake of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: So Mu'adh ؓ remained with no wealth."],[2064,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: 'O Abu Ayyub, shall I not guide you to a charity that Allah and His Messenger love? Reconcile between people when they hate each other and have become corrupt!'"],[2065,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us... and he mentioned the hadith, in which: 'Whoever walks in making peace between two people, the angels pray for him until he returns, and he is given the reward of the Night of Decree.' And in it: 'Whoever wrongs his neighbor by a span of land, it will be made a collar of fire around his neck on the Day of Resurrection reaching seven earths, until he enters Hell.'"],[2066,"The protected area of the old well's shaft is fifty cubits, and the protected area of the newly dug well's shaft is twenty-five cubits."],[2068,"Delay in payment by a rich man is injustice, and whoever is transferred to a wealthy man for collection should accept it."],[2070,"O people, whoever has a trust with him should return it to the one who entrusted him with it."],[2071,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us... and he mentioned a long hadith, in which: 'Whoever betrays his trust in this world and does not return it to its owners dies upon other than the religion of Islam, and he meets Allah while He is angry with him. Then it will be commanded to take him to the Fire, and he will fall from its edge forever and ever.'"],[2072,"Abu Bakr ؓ was brought a trust that had been lost, and he did not make him liable for it."],[2073,"'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ did not hold anyone liable for a trust."],[2075,"The greatest embezzlement in the sight of Allah, the Exalted, on the Day of Resurrection is a cubit of land that two men or two neighbors steal, which is between them, and one of them steals from his companion, so it will be made a collar of seven earths around his neck."],[2076,"It is not lawful to take any part of a man’s property except what he gives willingly."],[2077,"Cursed is anyone who diminishes anything from the boundary markers of the land without right."],[2078,"He witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in his sermon, and he said: ‘Your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you [i.e., inviolable].’"],[2079,"Whoever takes a handspan of the Muslims’ road will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying it from seven earths. He said: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in seven expeditions, the last of which was Hunayn. I was riding in the vanguard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and my mount became restive, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was beating it. He said: ‘Gently,’ and he rebuked it, and it stood still."],[2080,"Cursed is one who slaughters for other than Allah, cursed is one whom Allah curses, and cursed is anyone who diminishes anything from the boundary markers of the land without right."],[2082,"I met him and spoke with him. I said: O Prophet of Allah, what about silver found near an inhabited village or a frequented road? He ﷺ said: Announce it for a year. If its owner comes, give it to him. Otherwise, preserve its container, its tie, and its count, then make use of it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about silver found in ancient land? He said: On it and on buried treasure is one fifth. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about a sheep found in a desert land? He said: Eat it, for it is for you or for your brother or for the wolf. I said: O Prophet of Allah, what about a camel, male or female, found in a desert land with its saddlebag and waterskin on it? He said: Leave it; what do you have to do with it?"],[2083,"I went out and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar ؓ sitting, and a small boy was crying. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Umar ؓ: ‘Take the boy to you, for he is lost.’ Umar ؓ took him to himself … the hadith."],[2084,"He found a dinar, cut two qirats from it, then went to Fatimah ؓ and said: ‘Prepare food for us.’ Then he went to the Prophet ﷺ and invited him. He came with those with him, and he brought them a handful. When the Prophet ﷺ saw it, he did not recognize it, so he said: ‘What is this?’ He informed him, and he said: ‘Pick it up, pick it up; the two qirats are on me. Put your hands in the name of Allah.’"],[2085,"Ali ؓ brought him a dinar he found in the market, and he ﷺ said: ‘Announce it for three days.’ He announced it, but found no one who recognized it. He returned to the Prophet ﷺ and told him, and he said: ‘Eat it, or do as you wish with it.’ So he bought with it barley for three dirhams, dates for three dirhams, meat for one dirham, and oil for one dirham, and one dirham remained with him—the exchange rate was eleven dirhams per dinar. Later its owner came and recognized it. Ali ؓ said to him: ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me,’ and he mentioned that to him. The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘If anything comes to us, we will pay it to you.’"],[2087,"I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he found a date-pod containing two dates. He took one date and gave me the other."],[2088,"I heard Ibn Umar ؓ say concerning lost property: ‘Hand it over to the ruler.’"],[2089,"He said to Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ: ‘I found a dinar and picked it up, until I reached one hundred dinars.’ He said: ‘Announce it for a year.’ He announced it for a year, then came to him. He said: ‘Announce it for a year.’ Then he came to him the third time, and he said: ‘Announce it, then do as you wish with it.’"],[2090,"I said: O Messenger of God, we come upon camels that have milk, and they are kept from being milked, while we are in need. He ﷺ said: Call out for the owner of the camels three times. If he comes, then (leave them); otherwise, untie their udder straps, then drink, then tie them again, and leave for the milk its natural channels. I said: O Messenger of God, stray animals come to us; do we have reward if we give them water? He ﷺ said: Yes, in every living being with a warm liver there is reward."],[2092,"Breaking the dinar and the dirham is among the corruption in the land."],[2094,"Give the hired worker his wage before his sweat dries."],[2096,"Whoever is given a gift while there are people with him, they are his partners in it."],[2097,"Whoever receives a gift while there are people sitting with him, they are his partners in it."],[2098,"I had twenty dirhams owed to me by a non-Arab. He sent me a gift, so I asked Ibn Abbas ؓ, and he said: Calculate the value of the gift and take the remainder."],[2099,"Visit one another and exchange gifts, for visiting increases affection, and a gift removes ill will."],[2100,"Exchange gifts, for it increases love and removes hidden grudges."],[2101,"I do not accept a gift from a bedouin."],[2102,"Whoever gives a gift to maintain ties of kinship or as charity, it is valid. But whoever gives a gift expecting something in return, he is more entitled to it if he is not satisfied with what he receives."],[2103,"About a man who gave a lamb as a gift, and it gave birth, then he wanted to take it back; he said: He may take back its value."],[2104,"About a man who gave a young slave girl as a gift, and she grew up, then he wanted to take her back; he said: He may take back the value openly."],[2105,"When a gift is destroyed, its owner has no right to revoke it."],[2106,"A man was nicknamed Ḥimār. He used to give the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a small skin of clarified butter and a small skin of honey. When its owner would come to demand payment, he would bring him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and say, 'O Messenger of Allah, give this man the price of his goods.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would do no more than smile and order that he be paid."],[2108,"Treat your children equally in gifts. If I were to prefer anyone, I would prefer females."],[2110,"A guest came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he sent me to a Jew and said, 'Tell him: The Messenger of Allah says, \"Sell to me or lend me until Rajab.\"' I went to him and said that. He said, 'By Allah, I will neither sell to him nor lend him except with a pledge!' I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. He said, 'By Allah, if he had sold to me or lent to me, I would have paid him. I am trustworthy in heaven and trustworthy on earth. Take my iron coat of mail to him.' He said: Then it was revealed, consoling him about this world: 'Do not extend your eyes toward what We have given some groups of them to enjoy—the splendor of worldly life.'"],[2111,"Abū Bakr said: Wakīʿ narrated to us with this. 1498/3 – And Isḥāq said: Rawḥ b. ʿUbādah informed us – meaning from Mūsā – with this chain, the like of it."],[2112,"Abū Bakr said: Wakīʿ narrated to us with this. 1498/3 – And Isḥāq said: Rawḥ b. ʿUbādah informed us – meaning from Mūsā – with this chain, the like of it."],[2113,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū Bakr narrated to us, then he mentioned it."],[2114,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to borrow dates from a Jewish man, and the Jew said, 'No, by Allah, except with a pledge.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I am trustworthy in heaven and trustworthy on earth.'"],[2115,"Whoever mortgages land for a debt owed by him, he may pay from its produce what is surplus over its expenses, and then he may pay from that his debt that he owes, after accounting for what remains for him for his work and expenses, justly."],[2117,"There is no orphanhood after puberty."],[2118,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man: 'You and your wealth belong to your father.'"],[2120,"On the day Saʿd ؓ judged Banū Qurayẓah, I was a young boy. They were uncertain about me and did not find that the razor had passed over me, so I was spared."],[2122,"He would not bargain in three things: hire to Makkah, a slave, and a sacrificial animal."],[2124,"Whoever revives dead land that is not the right of any Muslim, it belongs to him, and there is no right for an unjust root."],[2125,"The servants are the servants of Allah, and the lands are the lands of Allah, and there is no right for an unjust root."],[2126,"Whoever revives dead land, it belongs to him."],[2128,"He was asked about a man who dedicated something in the path of Allah, most high; may he divert it to something else? He said: Discharge it where its owner placed it. He said: By Allah, no; the path of Allah is not that some of you strike the necks of others."],[2130,"I brought Ibn Mas'ud ؓ some runaway slaves from 'Ayn al-Tamr - or he said: from al-'Ayn - and he said: Rejoice in the reward and the spoils! He said: I said: This is the reward, so what is the spoils? He said: Forty dirhams. And he was in Kufa."],[2131,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and mentioned a hadith, and in it: Whoever wrongs a hired worker in his wages, his deeds are nullified and the fragrance of Paradise is forbidden to him; its fragrance can be found from a distance of five hundred years' journey."],[2132,"The Prophet ﷺ set the reward for a runaway slave, if taken outside the city, at ten dirhams."],[2134,"There is no manumission before ownership."],[2135,"A woman freed a slave of hers, and 'A'ishah ؓ said to her: Now, if you have freed him and did not stipulate his property, then his property belongs to him."],[2136,"A slave was jointly owned by two men, and one of them freed his share, so the Prophet ﷺ detained him until he sold some sheep."],[2137,"A slave was jointly owned by two men, and one of them freed his half, so his partner went to 'Umar ؓ, and he wrote that he should be valued at the highest price."],[2138,"Regarding a slave owned by two men when one of them frees his share, he said: He guarantees a third of its value to his companion at a fair valuation on the day he freed him."],[2139,"Indeed Abu Hurayrah ؓ said to a servant of his: \"O so-and-so, were it not that you are a child of fornication, I would have freed you.\""],[2140,"Among the worst of your slaves are the black people: if they are hungry, they steal; and if they are full, they commit fornication."],[2141,"Indeed ʿĀʾishah ؓ was asked, and it was said to her: \"Abu Hurayrah ؓ says: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'To give in charity a shoe-lace of my sandal is more beloved to me than to manumit a child of fornication.'\" Then ʿĀʾishah ؓ said: \"He misheard, and thus he erred in his response. The Messenger of God ﷺ only said: 'To give in charity a shoe-lace of my sandal is more beloved to me than to command my slave-girl to fornicate and then manumit her child.'\""],[2142,"I saw the slave who was to be freed after his master's death whom the Messenger of God sold."],[2143,"Whatever a man manumits of his slaves during his illness, that is a bequest; if he wishes, he may revoke it."],[2144,"Indeed he saw no harm in a man revoking his manumission."],[2145,"When a slave who has a contract of manumission becomes bankrupt, the debt is to be given priority."],[2146,"Indeed a slave of his with a contract of manumission became unable to fulfill it, so he returned him to slavery and retained what he had taken from him."],[2147,"They are entitled to what they took from him - meaning: if he did not complete it and was returned to slavery - then whatever was taken is theirs."],[2148,"If two installments are missed, and he does not pay his installments, he is returned to slavery."],[2149,"Indeed he ruled regarding the mother of the child that she is not to be sold, nor given as a gift, nor inherited; her owner may enjoy her as long as he lives, and when he dies, she is free."],[2151,"Indeed the Messenger of God ﷺ gave her a slave-girl, and that slave-girl gave birth as a result of fornication, and she wanted to manumit her child, so she consulted the Messenger of God ﷺ about that. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"To give charity with some charity is better for you than to manumit her, but you may employ her.\""],[2153,"Indeed Abu Bakr ؓ made clear that Allah, the Exalted, gave you charity in the form of one-third of your wealth at the time of your death."],[2154,"Indeed Abu Bakr ؓ bequeathed the fifth, and said: 'I take from my wealth what Allah has permitted from the fay' of the Muslims.'"],[2155,"Indeed the Prophet ﷺ sent a crier who announced on the day of the conquest of Makkah: 'There is no bequest to an heir, the child belongs to the bed, and a woman's gift is not permissible except with her husband's permission.'"],[2156,"There is no bequest to an heir."],[2158,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the grandfather one-sixth of the wealth along with a male child, and along with one brother half, and along with two or more one-third, and when there was no heir other than him, he gave him all the wealth."],[2159,"We used to give him inheritance in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, meaning the grandfather."],[2160,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[2161,"Al-Bazzar said: Ibn Umar b. Hayyaj narrated to us, Qabisa narrated to us. Al-Bazzar said: We do not know it with this wording from Abu Sa'id ؓ except from this route, and I think that Qabisa erred in his wording, and he only had: 'We used to give it' - meaning the fitrah - and Qabisa was not followed in this."],[2163,"Bring the people in to me, and do not bring in except Quraysh. So they entered slipping in until the house was filled, so he said: 'Is there anyone among you who is not from you?' They said: 'The son of a sister, the client, and the ally.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The son of their sister is from them, their ally is from them, and their client is from them.'"],[2165,"He gave charity to his mother with a slave girl of his whom he had contracted to pay for her freedom, so the mother died while she owed a remainder of her contract. He said: I asked Imran b. Husayn ؓ, and he said: 'You inherit your mother, and to divide her among her relatives is more beloved to me.'"],[2167,"Regarding a group of people who drowned in a ship, Ali ؓ made some of them inherit from others."],[2169,"Umar ؓ asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'How do we give inheritance in the case of kalalah?' He ﷺ said: 'Has not Allah, the Exalted, already explained that?' Then he recited: 'And if a man is inherited by kalalah...' to the end. As if Umar ؓ did not understand, so Allah, the Exalted, revealed: 'They ask you for a ruling. Say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning kalalah...' to the end of the verse. As if Umar ؓ did not understand, so he said to Hafsa ؓ: 'When you see that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is in a good mood, ask him about it.' She saw him in a good mood and asked him about it, so he ﷺ said: 'Did your father write this for you? I do not think your father will ever know it.' So Umar ؓ used to say: 'I do not think I will ever know it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said what he said.'"],[2170,"“There is nothing in the Book of Allah, nor in the decree of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They will all find it, and they will say: ‘What is it?’ He will say: ‘The inheritance of the sister along with the daughter is half.’ And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has said: ‘If a man dies having no child but has a sister...’ the verse.”"],[2171,"“A man inherits from his full brother, to the exclusion of his paternal brothers.”"],[2172,"He heard Murrah say concerning kalālah. I said to Murrah: “Who doubts about kalālah? It is those other than the child and the parent.” He said: “They doubt about the child.”"],[2174,"ʿAlī and al-Zubayr brought a dispute before ʿUmar ؓ concerning the mawālī of Ṣafiyyah ؓ. ʿAlī ؓ said: “She is my paternal aunt, and I pay blood money on her behalf and inherit from her.” Al-Zubayr ؓ said: “She is my mother, and I inherit from her.” ʿUmar said to ʿAlī ؓ: “Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made walāʾ subordinate to inheritance?”"],[2175,"“If a man accepts Islam at a man’s hands, he is his mawlā; he inherits from him and pays blood money on his behalf.”"],[2176,"“Whoever accepts Islam at a man’s hands, he is his mawlā.”"],[2177,"I asked Ibrāhīm about a Nabataean who accepts Islam and forms an alliance with a man. He said: “He inherits from him and pays blood money on his behalf.”"],[2179,"Muʿādh b. Jabal ؓ used to allow a Muslim to inherit from a disbeliever, but he did not allow a disbeliever to inherit from a Muslim."],[2180,"Two brothers brought a dispute before Yaḥyā b. Yaʿmar: a Jew and a Muslim. He made the Muslim inherit from them. It was said to him: “Why did you make the Muslim inherit?” He said: “Abū al-Aswad told me that a man told him that two brothers brought a dispute before Muʿādh ؓ: a Jew and a Muslim. The Muslim said: ‘My father was a Jew, and he had wealth and land. My Islam did not harm me with him; rather, he entrusted his wealth to me and land that I cultivated and managed. I used to give charity, host guests, do good, and free slaves. He did not criticize that about me. Then he died, and they came between me and his wealth and said: “You have no right.” So Muʿādh made the Muslim inherit.’”"],[2181,"“A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever, except if he has a slave.”"],[2182,"In the pommel of the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a document was found in which was: “The believers’ blood is equal; the lowest of them is entitled to give protection. A Muslim is not killed for a disbeliever, nor one with a covenant while his covenant lasts. The people of two religions do not inherit from one another.”"],[2184,"The Prophet ﷺ is not inherited from."],[2186,"When the apostate from Islam is killed, his children inherit from him."],[2188,"He asked 'Asim b. 'Adiyy about Thabit b. al-Dahdah: \"Do you know of any lineage for him among you?\" They said: \"No, he is only an outsider among us.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that his inheritance be given to his sister's son."],[2190,"Blood-money is inherited by the heirs according to the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[2192,"There was a quarrel between him and two wives of his, so he threw a stone at one of them and killed her. He rode to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at Tabuk, and asked him about the matter of the killed woman. He ﷺ said: \"You pay her blood-money, but you do not inherit from her.\""],[2195,"'Ali ؓ took Ka'b b. 'Ujrah ؓ by the hand and stood him between the two rows, then said to him: \"Narrate what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!\" He ؓ said: \"I heard him say: 'The daughter of a brother and the daughter of a sister through breastfeeding are not lawful (to marry).'\""],[2196,"It was found on the hilt of the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ... She mentioned the hadith and said: \"And in the last part: 'A woman is not married in addition to her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt, and a woman does not travel three nights except with a mahram.'\""],[2197,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade marrying a slave woman in addition to a free woman."],[2198,"Marrying a free woman in addition to a slave woman is a divorce of the slave woman."],[2199,"Any man who marries while he is in ihram, we take his wife away from him and we do not approve his marriage."],[2200,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote a document in which: \"No jalab, no janab, no wirat, and no shighar in Islam. Every intoxicant is forbidden. Whoever practices ijba' has practiced riba.\""],[2201,"The muhrim does not marry, nor does he propose for himself or for anyone else."],[2203,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us ... and he mentioned the hadith, in which [he said]: \"Whoever walks in arranging the marriage of a man lawfully until he brings them together, God Almighty will provide him with a thousand women from the houris of paradise, each woman in a palace of pearl and ruby, and for every step he takes or word he speaks in that matter he will have the worship of a year: standing in prayer its nights and fasting its days. And whoever walks in reconciling a woman and her husband will have the reward of a thousand martyrs truly slain in the path of God, and for every step he will have the worship of a year, its fasting and its standing in prayer.\""],[2205,"\"The best of you are the easiest of you in dowry.\""],[2206,"And I met him and spoke to him. He said: I said, \"O Messenger of God, I went out with an uncle of mine on a journey, and he suffered sore feet. He said, 'Lend me your sandals.' I said, 'I will not lend them to you unless you marry me to your daughter.' He said, 'I have married you to my daughter.'\" He said: \"When we came to our family, he sent me back my sandals and said, 'You have no wife with me.'\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Leave her; there is no good for you in her.\""],[2207,"\"Two matters never come together except that the more beloved of them to God Almighty is the easier of them.\""],[2208,"\"Whoever arranges a marriage for a servant of God Almighty, arranging it only for His sake, God, Mighty and Majestic, will crown him in Paradise with a crown by which he will be known.\""],[2209,"Umar ؓ mounted the pulpit, the pulpit of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and said: \"I shall not acknowledge any increase in dowry above four hundred dirhams.\" Then he descended. A woman of Quraysh confronted him and said, \"O Commander of the Believers, have you forbidden people to increase their women's dowries above four hundred dirhams?\" He said, \"Yes.\" She said, \"Have you not heard God Almighty say in the Qur'an: 'And you have given one of them a qintar' ... the verse?\" He said, \"O God, forgiveness! All the people are more knowledgeable than Umar.\" Then he returned, mounted, and said, \"O people, I had forbidden you to increase their dowries above four hundred dirhams. Whoever wishes to give from his wealth whatever he likes, or whoever is pleased in himself, let him do so.\""],[2210,"\"There is no blame on a man to marry with whatever he wishes of his wealth, little or much, when he has witnesses.\""],[2211,"He used to divide the sheep among his companions from the charity, and a sheep would fall between two men, and one of them would say, \"Leave me your share that I may marry with it!\""],[2212,"\"Whoever makes lawful [a woman] for a dirham has made lawful [what is unlawful].\""],[2213,"While my father was on a raid in the pre-Islamic era, they suffered from the heat. A man said, \"Who will give me his sandals, and I will marry him to the first daughter born to me?\" My father took off his sandals and threw them to him. A girl was born to the man and reached maturity. My father said, \"Gather my family to me,\" and then said, \"Bring the dowry.\" He said, \"By God, I will not give you more than what I gave you: the sandals.\" My father said, \"By God, I will not give her to you except with a dowry.\" So my father came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked him about that. He said, \"Shall I not inform you of what is better than that? Leave her, so you will not break your oath, and you will not cause your companion to break his.\" So my father left her."],[2215,"About a man who married a woman and she had insanity, leprosy, or vitiligo, he said: \"She is his wife; if he wishes, he divorces, and if he wishes, he keeps her.\""],[2217,"Your wives indeed boast over me. They say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not marry you; you are only a possession of the right hand! So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Did I not make your dowry substantial? Did I not free forty of your people?\""],[2218,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made her manumission her dowry; he gave her herself as her dowry.\""],[2220,"\"A man married a woman, and the Prophet ﷺ outfitted her, but he did not give anything.\""],[2222,"\"Whoever witnesses the marriage contract of a Muslim man, it is as if he fasted a day in the path of Allah, the Exalted, and the day is equivalent to seven hundred.\""],[2224,"It was said to ʿĀʾishah ؓ : 'Indeed Abū Hurayrah ؓ says: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Ill omen is in three things: in the house, the woman, and the horse.\"' Then ʿĀʾishah ؓ said: 'Abū Hurayrah ؓ did not memorize it well; because he entered while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was saying: \"May Allah fight the Jews! They say: Ill omen is in three things: in the house, the woman, and the horse.\" He heard the end of the hadith but did not hear its beginning.'"],[2226,"He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her while he was in a state of iḥrām,\" meaning Maymūnah. And Ibn ʿUmar and Saʿīd b. al-Musayyib used to reject that."],[2228,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us, and he mentioned the hadith, in which is: \"Whoever wrongs a woman by withholding her dowry, then he is, in the sight of Allah, the Exalted, an adulterer. And Allah, the Exalted, will say to him on the Day of Resurrection: 'My servant, I gave you in marriage upon My covenant, yet you did not honor My covenant?' Then Allah, the Exalted, will take charge of seeking her right, and He will exhaust all his good deeds, and whatever remains of them, it will be commanded that he be taken to the Fire. And whoever has two wives and does not treat them justly in the division of his self and his wealth, he will come on the Day of Resurrection fettered, with his side leaning, until he enters the Fire.\""],[2229,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be carried to his wives while he was ill, and he would divide justly among them."],[2230,"He used to draw lots between his wives when he intended to travel. And the lot fell to ʿĀʾishah ؓ in the expedition of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq."],[2232,"ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar ؓ said to ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ : \"Seek for me the daughter of Ṣāliḥ in marriage.\" He said: \"He has orphans, and he would not prefer us over them.\" So ʿAbd Allah went to his paternal uncle Zayd b. al-Khaṭṭāb to seek her hand for him. He took him to Ṣāliḥ and said: \"ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar sent me to you to ask for your daughter's hand.\" He said: \"I have orphans, and I would not let my own flesh suffer while raising yours in status. I call you to witness that I have married her to so-and-so.\" Her mother's inclination was towards ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar ؓ , so she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ , ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar proposed to my daughter, but her father married her to an orphan under his care without consulting her.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Ṣāliḥ and said: \"You married off your daughter without consulting her?\" He said: \"Yes.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Consult women about themselves,\" twice. Then Ṣāliḥ said: \"I only did this because of what Ibn ʿUmar would give her as a dowry, for she has from my wealth the like of what he would give her.\""],[2233,"Whenever he wanted to give one of his women in marriage, he would say: \"Indeed so-and-so son of so-and-so mentions so-and-so daughter of so-and-so.\""],[2234,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ separated a virgin girl from her husband; her father had given her in marriage while she was unwilling. He said: And whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave one of his daughters in marriage, he would come to her curtain and say: \"Indeed so-and-so mentions so-and-so.\""],[2236,"\"O Bedouin, lust and hunger?\" He said: That is it. He ﷺ said: \"Go, and the first woman you meet who has no husband, she is your wife.\" The Bedouin said: I entered the palm grove of Banu al-Najjar, and there was a young woman picking dates into a basket. I said to her: O owner of the basket, do you have a husband? She said: No. He said: Come down, for the Messenger of God ﷺ has married you to me. He said: She came down, and I went with her to her house. She said to her father: This Bedouin came to me while I was picking dates into the basket, and he asked me: Do you have a husband? I said: No. He said: Come down, for the Messenger of God ﷺ has married you to me. The girl's father came out to the Bedouin, and the Bedouin said: What is the owner of the basket to you? He said: My daughter. He said: Does she have a husband? He said: No. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ has married her to me. The girl and her father went to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he informed him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Does she have a husband?\" He said: No. He ﷺ said: \"Go, prepare her trousseau well, then send her to him.\" The girl's father went and prepared his daughter, and took good care of her, then sent with her dates and milk. She brought them to the Bedouin's house, and the Bedouin returned to his house. He saw a well-adorned young woman, and he saw dates and milk, so he stood up to pray. When dawn broke, he went early to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the girl's father went early to his daughter. She said: By God, he did not approach us, nor did he approach our dates or our milk! He said: The girl's father went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and informed him. He called the Bedouin and said: \"O Bedouin, what prevented you from being intimate with your wife?\" He said: O Messenger of God, I left you and entered the house, and there was a well-adorned young woman, and I saw dates and milk, so it was incumbent upon me to spend my night until morning in prayer—meaning out of gratitude. He ﷺ said: \"O Bedouin, go and be intimate with your wife.\""],[2237,"Julaybib was a man from the Ansar, and he used to enter upon women and converse with them. Abu Barzah ؓ said: I said to my wife: Beware, let not Julaybib enter upon you! He said: The companions of the Prophet ﷺ, when one of them had an unmarried woman, they would not marry her off until they knew whether the Messenger of God ﷺ had a need for her or not. One day the Messenger of God ﷺ said to a man from the Ansar: \"O so-and-so, marry your daughter to me!\" He said: Yes, and a delight to the eye! He ﷺ said: \"I do not want her for myself.\" He said: Then for whom? He ﷺ said: \"For Julaybib.\" He said: O Messenger of God, let me consult her mother. He went and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ is proposing to your daughter. She said: Yes, and a delight to the eye! You are marrying the Messenger of God ﷺ! He said: He does not want her for himself. She said: Then for whom? He said: For Julaybib. She said: Woe to me! For Julaybib? No, by the life of God, I will not raise Julaybib. When her father got up to go to the Prophet ﷺ, the young woman said from her chamber to her parents: Who proposed to me to you? They said: The Messenger of God ﷺ. She said: Would you reject the command of the Messenger of God ﷺ? Give me to the Messenger of God ﷺ, for he will never waste me. Her father went to the Prophet ﷺ and said: She is yours to deal with. So he married her to Julaybib. Hammad said: Ishaq b. Abdullah b. Abi Talhah said to me: I said to Thabit: Do you know what he ﷺ supplicated for her? He said: O God, pour abundant good upon them, and do not make their livelihood a constant struggle! Thabit said: So he married her to him."],[2239,"I followed the Messenger of God ﷺ among women, and he said to us: \"As much as you are able.\" We said: O Messenger of God, accept our pledge! He ﷺ said: \"I do not shake hands with you; I only take from you what God, Mighty and Majestic, has taken.\""],[2241,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas ؓ said: \"While I was circumambulating the House, I saw a woman and she pleased me.\" And it was said: The beauty of a woman you do not know does not harm you."],[2242,"\"The fornication of the two eyes is looking.\""],[2243,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us, and he mentioned a hadith, and in it: \"Whoever casts an unlawful glance at a woman, God will fill his eyes with fire, then order him to the Fire. But if he lowers his gaze from her, God will put love and mercy into his heart, and order him to Paradise. And whoever shakes hands with a woman unlawfully will come on the Day of Resurrection with his hands chained to his neck, then be ordered to the Fire. And if he jokes with her, he will be detained for every word in this world for a thousand years.\" And in the hadith: \"God's anger intensifies against a married woman who fills her eyes with someone other than her husband or a close relative. If she does that, God will nullify every deed she has done. And if she lets someone else lie in his bed, it is incumbent upon God, Exalted is He, to make her swallow fire from the day she dies in her grave.\""],[2244,"\"Sin is what stirs in the hearts, and any glance, the devil has an appetite in it.\""],[2245,"\"Three eyes will not see the Fire on the Day of Resurrection: an eye that wept from fear of God, Exalted is He; an eye that kept watch in the path of God, Mighty and Majestic; and an eye that lowered its gaze from what God, Blessed and Exalted, has forbidden.\""],[2246,"\"Cover your forelocks from us, O Umm Ayman.\""],[2247,"\"I was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ, and there was a Bedouin with a beautiful daughter of his. The Bedouin began to present her to the Messenger of God ﷺ hoping that he would marry her.\""],[2249,"The best of you are those who are best to their families."],[2251,"Aishah ؓ married the daughter of Abd al-Rahman to al-Mundhir b. al-Zubayr. Abd al-Rahman said, \"You marry a man's daughter without his command?\" Aishah ؓ became angry and said to al-Mundhir, \"Let her own her affair.\" He did so, and they did not consider it anything."],[2253,"Hafsah became husbandless after her husband, and Uthman became wifeless after Ruqayyah. Umar passed by Uthman and said, \"Would you like Hafsah? Her waiting period has ended.\" He did not respond to him at all. So he came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said, \"I will marry Hafsah, and I will marry Uthman to her sister Umm Kulthum.\" Umar said, \"Excellent.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Hafsah and married Uthman to Umm Kulthum."],[2255,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and we camped one night. Then we went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the morning. He began asking one man after another: \"Did you marry, O so-and-so? Did you marry, O so-and-so?\" Then he said, \"Did you marry, O Ka'b?\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He ﷺ said, \"A virgin or a previously married woman?\" I said, \"A previously married woman.\" He said, \"Why not a virgin, so that you could play with her and she could play with you?\""],[2256,"Al-Hasan ؓ disliked marrying off an orphan boy or girl until they reached puberty."],[2258,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he brought his wives ؓ with him. She said: My baggage was light, so it was on a swift camel. The baggage of Safiyyah bt. Huyayy ؓ was heavy, so it was on a slow, heavy camel that held back the caravan. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Transfer Aishah's baggage onto Safiyyah's camel, and transfer Safiyyah's baggage onto Aishah's camel, so that the caravan can proceed.\" When I saw that, Aishah ؓ said: I said, \"O refuge with Allah! Has this Jewess prevailed over the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Umm Abd Allah, your baggage was light, and Safiyyah's baggage was heavy, so the caravan was delayed. We transferred her baggage onto your camel and your baggage onto her camel.\" She said: I said, \"Do you not claim that you are the Messenger of Allah?\" She said: The Prophet ﷺ smiled and said, \"Are you in doubt about me, O Umm Abd Allah?\" She said: I said, \"Do you not claim that you are the Messenger of Allah? Then why did you not act justly?\" Abu Bakr ؓ heard me, and he had sharpness, that is, a temper. He came to me and slapped my face. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Gently, O Abu Bakr.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, did you not hear?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A jealous woman cannot see the bottom of the valley from its top.\""],[2259,"A woman from Jurash came to the Prophet ﷺ on a camel and called out, \"O Aishah, help me with a supplication from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to calm me or comfort me.\" He said to her, \"Place your right hand on your heart and wipe it, and say: In the name of Allah; O Allah, heal me with Your healing, cure me with Your cure, enrich me with Your richness and Your bounty from all besides You, and avert from me Your harm.\""],[2261,"I rented out Abd Allah b. Jarir for the Hajj. He came to Umar ؓ, and Umar asked him about things. Among what he asked was: \"How did you find your wives?\" He said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, I cannot kiss any of them on a day that is not her day without her accusing me, and I do not go out for an errand without her saying, 'You were with so-and-so, you were with so-and-so.'\" Umar ؓ said, \"Many of them do not believe in Allah and do not trust the believers. Perhaps one of them is in need, or goes to the market to buy something for one of them, and she accuses him.\" Ibn Mas'ud ؓ said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, did you not know that Ibrahim, the Friend of the Merciful, complained to Allah Almighty about sharpness in Sarah's character, and He said to him, 'The woman is like a rib; if you leave her, she remains crooked, and if you straighten her, she breaks. So enjoy her despite her faults.'\" Umar ؓ struck Ibn Mas'ud ؓ between his shoulders and said, \"Allah has placed in your heart, O Ibn Mas'ud, no small amount of knowledge.\""],[2262,"O people, women among you are like captives. You have taken them as a trust from Allah, and you have made their private parts lawful by the word of Allah. You have rights over them, and they have rights over you. Among your rights is that they should not allow anyone you dislike to tread on your beds, and that they should not disobey you in what is right. If they do that, then they are entitled to their provision and clothing with kindness. And if you strike them, strike in a way that is not severe."],[2263,"Safiyyah said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and there was no one among the people more hateful to me than him. He began to say: 'Your people did such and such, and they did such and such.' I did not rise from that seat of mine until no one was dearer to me than him."],[2264,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: 'Whoever marries a woman and has intercourse with her in her anus, or with a man, or a boy—he will come on the Day of Resurrection more foul-smelling than a carcass.' ... the hadith. And its remainder will come, Allah willing, in the hadith, and in it: 'Any woman who harms her husband—her prayer will not be accepted, nor any good deed of her work, until she helps him and pleases him. Even if she fasts all time, stands in prayer, frees slaves, and carries provisions for jihad in the way of Allah, she would be the first to enter the Fire if she does not please him and help him.' And he said: 'And the man bears the like of that punishment and burden if he is harmful and unjust to her. Whoever harms a woman until she ransoms herself from him—Allah will not be satisfied with any punishment for him short of the Fire, because Allah becomes angry for the woman as He becomes angry for the orphan. And any woman who obtains khul' from her husband remains in the curse of Allah, the curse of the angels and His messengers, and all people. When the Angel of Death descends upon her, he says to her: Enter the Fire with those who enter. Indeed, Allah and His Messenger are free from the one who harms a woman until she obtains khul' from him. And whoever is patient with the bad character of his wife and seeks reward from Allah—Allah will give him of reward the like of what He gave Ayyub for his trial, and she will bear each day and night a burden like the sand of 'Alij. If she dies before helping him and pleasing him, she will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection upside down with the hypocrites in the lowest level of the Fire. And whoever has a wife who does not suit him, does not show patience with what Allah has provided, makes things difficult for him, and burdens him with what he cannot bear—no good deed will be accepted from her. If she dies upon that, she will be gathered with those upon whom is wrath.'"],[2266,"Allah cursed the procrastinating women. It was asked: Who are the procrastinating women? He said: 'The man calls the woman to his bed, and she says: Later, later, until sleep overcomes his eyes.'"],[2267,"It is not lawful for a woman to sleep until she presents herself to her husband. He was asked: How does she present herself to her husband? He said: 'She removes her clothes and enters with him under his blanket, pressing her skin to his skin. If she does that, she has presented herself.'"],[2268,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the procrastinating woman and the excusing woman. The procrastinating woman is the one who, when her husband wants her, says: 'Later, now.' The excusing woman is the one who, when her husband wants her, says: 'I am menstruating,' while she is not menstruating."],[2269,"When one of you has intercourse with his wife, let him be truthful to her. If he finishes before her, let him not rush her."],[2271,"The first people to practice coitus interruptus were a group of the Ansar. They came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'A group of the Ansar are practicing coitus interruptus.' He became alarmed and said: 'The soul that is to be created will surely come into being.' He neither commanded nor forbade."],[2272,"If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said anything about it, it is as he said—meaning coitus interruptus. And I see no harm in it. Your field: if you wish, you can withhold water, and if you wish, you can water it."],[2273,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have not been able to reach you from the polytheists except by a young girl, and I practice coitus interruptus with her, intending to sell her in the market?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is decreed will come to her.'"],[2274,"I practiced coitus interruptus with a slave-girl of mine, yet she gave birth to the most beloved of people to me: this boy."],[2275,"A man came to Ibn Umar ؓ and asked him about coitus interruptus. He struck his hand toward what was next to him, so the man turned away, and he threw pebbles at him and said, 'Uff!' Abdulaziz said: I mentioned that to Anas ؓ, and he said, 'We did not consider it problematic.'"],[2276,"There is no harm in coitus interruptus."],[2278,"Part of it was mentioned previously in the chapter on living with women. 1929 1615 - Al-Harith said: Al-Khalil b. Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr b. Ubayd narrated to us, Al-Hasan b. Abi al-Hasan narrated to us, from Imran b. Husayn ؓ."],[2279,"The private parts of women are forbidden to you."],[2280,"Be shy before Allah, the Exalted, for Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, is not shy of the truth. Do not approach women in their anuses."],[2282,"When he married Fatimah ؓ, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Make the majority of the dowry in perfume.'"],[2284,"Umm Salamah sent me to the Prophet ﷺ ... and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then he took my hand and we went out, and he had recently married Zaynab bt. Jahsh ؓ. He passed by his wives and they congratulated him, and the people congratulated him, saying: 'Praise be to Allah; may Allah cool your eyes, O Messenger of Allah!'"],[2286,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have a daughter who is such and such...' and she mentioned her beauty and attractiveness, and said, 'I prefer you for her.' He ﷺ said: 'I have accepted her.' She continued praising her until she mentioned that she had never had a headache or complained of anything. He ﷺ said: 'I have no need of your daughter.'"],[2288,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her with Abu Bakr ؓ and said to her: 'O Aishah, feed us.' She said: 'By Allah, we have no food.' He ﷺ said: 'Feed us.' She said: 'By Allah, we have no food.' He said: 'Feed us.' She said: 'By Allah, we have no food.' Abu Bakr ؓ said: 'O Messenger of Allah, a believing woman does not swear about something that it is not with her when it is with her.' He ﷺ said: 'And what makes you know whether she is a believer or not? The example of a believing woman among women is like a white-legged crow among crows. The Fire was created for the foolish, and women are among the foolish, except the woman who has the comb and the lamp.'"],[2290,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'O Ali, do not have intercourse with your wife in the middle of the month, nor at the first appearance of the new moon. Have you not seen that the insane are often struck down during those times?'"],[2291,"Uthman b. Maz'un ؓ came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, I do not like to look at my wife's private parts, nor for her to see that from me.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"And why is that? God Most High has made you a garment for her, and I see that from my family and they see it from me.\" He said: \"Then who can be compared to you, O Messenger of God?\" Then he turned away, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed Ibn Maz'un is truly modest and veiling.\""],[2292,"When one of you goes to his wife, let him cover himself, and they should not strip completely like two donkeys."],[2294,"A woman is married for four things: for her beauty, her wealth, her lineage, and her religion. So win the one with religion and character, may your hands be rubbed with dust."],[2295,"The best benefit a Muslim gains after Islam is a wife who delights him when he looks at her, obeys him when he commands her, and protects him in his wealth and herself when he is absent."],[2296,"Three things break the back: poverty that enters and its owner finds no enjoyment, a wife whom her husband trusts but she betrays him, and a leader who angers God Most High and pleases people. And the righteousness of a believing woman is like seventy truthful women, and the immorality of an immoral woman is like the immorality of a thousand immoral women."],[2297,"Women are but playthings; whoever takes a plaything, let him improve it or choose it well."],[2299,"When Fatimah was given to Ali, the Messenger of God ﷺ sent to Ali: 'Do not approach your wife until I come to you.' She said: The Prophet ﷺ came and called for water. He said in it what God willed him to say, then he sprinkled the water on Ali's chest and face. Then he called Fatimah, and she stood up stumbling in her garment from shyness, and he sprinkled on her as well. Then he looked and saw darkness behind the house and said: 'Who is this?' Asma said: 'I am.' He said: 'Asma bt. Umays?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Did you come with the daughter of the Messenger of God as an honor to the Messenger of God?' I said: 'Yes.' He supplicated for me with a supplication that is the most deserving of my deeds to me. Then he said: 'O Fatimah, I have not failed to marry you to the most beloved of my family to me.' Then he went out and said to Ali: 'Take your wife.' Then he turned to a chamber and kept supplicating for them until he entered his chamber."],[2300,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'A woman has pleased me but she does not bear children; should I marry her?' He ﷺ said: 'No.' So he turned away from her. Then his soul followed her, and he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, this woman and her like have pleased me; her charm and her like have pleased me; should I marry her?' He said: 'No. A black woman who bears children is more beloved to me than her. Do you not realize that I will vie with other nations through you on the Day of Resurrection? The offspring of Muslims will come holding the waists of their fathers, and it will be said to them: Enter Paradise, until I see the miscarried fetus bloated and sluggish, and it is said to him: Enter Paradise! He says: O Lord, and my parents? God, Mighty and Majestic, says: Enter Paradise, you and your parents.'"],[2301,"Leave the beautiful barren woman, and hold to the black woman who bears children, for I will vie with other nations through you, even the miscarried fetus will remain bloated at the gate of Paradise, and it will be said to him: Enter Paradise! He says: Not until my parents enter with me."],[2302,"Shall I not tell you about your women among the people of Paradise? The loving, the childbearing, who when she wrongs or is wronged says: I will not taste sleep until you are pleased."],[2303,"Whoever marries has been given double the worship."],[2304,"«Whoever is able to marry, but does not marry, is not one of us.»"],[2305,"«Whoever loves my natural disposition, let him follow my Sunnah. And part of my Sunnah is marriage.»"],[2306,"«A young man's devotion is not complete until he marries.»"],[2307,"«O youth of Quraysh, do not commit fornication. Whoever preserves his youth will enter Paradise.»"],[2308,"ʿAṭṭāf b. Wadāʿa al-Hilālī came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"O ʿAṭṭāf, do you have a wife?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Nor a slave girl?\" He said, \"No.\" He ﷺ said, \"And you are healthy and wealthy?\" He said, \"Yes, praise be to God.\" He ﷺ said, \"Then you are one of the brothers of the devils. Either you are of the monasticism of the Christians, in which case you are one of them, or you are one of us, so do as we do. For part of our Sunnah is marriage. The worst of you are your unmarried, and the most wretched of your dead are your unmarried. Truly, the devil has no weapon more effective against the righteous among men than women, except for the married. Those are the purified, the innocent of indecency. Woe to you, O ʿAṭṭāf! They are the companions of Dāwūd, the companions of Ayyūb, the companions of Yūsuf, and the companions of Kursuf...\" and he mentioned the rest of the hadith. \"Woe to you, O ʿAṭṭāf! Marry, for you will be among those increased.\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, I will not marry until you marry me to whomever you wish.\" So the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I have married you, in the name of God Almighty and by His blessing, to Karīma bt. Kulthūm al-Ḥimyarī.\""],[2310,"ʿUtba b. Farqad offered his son marriage, but he refused. He mentioned that to ʿUthmān ؓ, and ʿUthmān ؓ said to him, \"Did not the Prophet ﷺ marry, and Abū Bakr ؓ married, and ʿUmar ؓ married, and we have from them what we have?\" He said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, who has deeds like the deeds of the Prophet ﷺ, and Abū Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ, or like your deeds?\" When he said \"like your deeds,\" he said, \"Enough! If you wish, marry; and if you wish, do not.\""],[2311,"Ibn ʿAbbās ؓ said to me—and that was before my beard had grown—\"Have you married, O Ibn Jubayr?\" I said, \"No, and I do not intend to do so today.\" He said, \"What is in your loins of the deposited ones will surely come out.\""],[2312,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned things for which a man is rewarded, even in having intercourse with his wife. It was said, \"O Messenger of God, how can he be rewarded for fulfilling his desire?\" He ﷺ said, \"Do you not see that if he had done it unlawfully, he would have been sinful?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"So likewise he is rewarded.\""],[2313,"A group of people gathered and said, \"If only we could send to the wives of the Prophet ﷺ and ask them about his character ﷺ.\" So they sent to them, and they said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ prays and sleeps, fasts and breaks his fast, and marries women.\" They said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ has been forgiven his past and future sins.\" Some of them said, \"I will pray all night and not sleep.\" Others said, \"I will fast every day and not break my fast.\" Others said, \"I will abstain from women and not approach them, for they are a distraction.\" The Prophet ﷺ learned of that and said, \"What is the matter with men who spy on the affairs of their Prophet, and when they are informed of it, they turn away from it, so one of them says such and such, and another says such and such?\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"But I sleep and pray, break my fast and fast, and marry women. Whoever turns away from my Sunnah is not of me.\""],[2314,"«Any young man who marries in his youth, his devil cries out, 'Woe to him! Woe to him! He has protected his religion from me.'»"],[2315,"If only one day of my life remained, I would meet God Almighty with a wife. For I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"The worst of you are your unmarried.\""],[2317,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to us during the Farewell Pilgrimage, \"This is the pilgrimage, then staying at home on the mats in the houses.\""],[2318,"When the Prophet ﷺ performed Hajj with his wives, he said: \"It is only this, then upon you is [to travel on] the backs of mats.\""],[2320,"I was with Umar ؓ, and while we were sitting with him, a woman came and sat near him. She said: 'O Commander of the Faithful, my husband's evil has increased and his good has decreased.' He said to her: 'Who is your husband?' She said: 'Abu Salamah.' He said: 'That is a man who has companionship [with the Prophet], and he is indeed a truthful man.' Then Umar ؓ said to a man sitting with him: 'Is it not so?' The man said: 'O Commander of the Faithful, we know him only as you have said.' He said to another man: 'Stand and summon him for me.' The woman stood when he sent for her husband and sat behind Umar ؓ. It was not long before the two came together until he sat before Umar ؓ. Umar ؓ said: 'What does this woman sitting behind me say?' He said: 'Who is this, O Commander of the Faithful?' He said: 'This is your wife.' He said: 'And what does she say?' He said: 'She claims that your good has decreased and your evil has increased.' He said: 'Evil is what she said, O Commander of the Faithful! She is among the righteous of her women, the most clothed of them and the most comfortable in household, but her stallion is unproductive.' Umar ؓ said to the woman: 'What do you say?' She said: 'He has spoken the truth.' Umar ؓ stood with a whip and struck her with it, then said: 'O enemy of herself, you consumed his wealth and exhausted his youth, then you began to report what is not in him?' She said: 'O Commander of the Faithful, do not hasten; by Allah, I shall never sit in this gathering again!' He ordered for her three garments and said: 'Take this for what I did to you, and beware of complaining about this old man.' He said: 'It is as if I see her standing with the garments. Then he ؓ turned to her husband and said: 'Let not what you saw me do to her cause you to mistreat her.' He said: 'I would never do that.' He said: 'Go away, both of you.'"],[2321,"A woman from the tribe of Tayy, from Banu Sinbis, called Umm Ba'l, came to Ali ؓ with her husband. She said that her husband does not have intercourse with her, and she is a woman who wants children. The man said: 'Do you not see what blessings are upon her?' He said: 'And she is in a good appearance.' He said to him: 'No, nor from the magic where it moves from the old man?' He said: 'Nor from magic.' He said: 'You are ruined and you cause ruin.' Then he turned to her and said: 'Be patient until relief comes to him.'"],[2323,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that his daughter Fatimah ؓ should serve inside the house, and Ali ؓ [should handle] what is outside the house."],[2324,"The women said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the men have taken the virtue of jihad. Is there anything from our deeds by which we can attain the virtue of jihad?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Yes, the service of one of you in her house attains for her the virtue of jihad.'"],[2326,"No marriage is valid without a guardian, or the authority (sultan)."],[2327,"No marriage is valid without a guardian."],[2328,"Women should not be married except to suitable matches (kuf'), and only guardians may marry them off, and there is no dowry less than ten dirhams."],[2330,"A man said to Umar ؓ: 'I have a daughter whom I buried alive in the Jahiliyyah, and I brought her out and she became Muslim. Then she committed a sin punishable by a hadd, so she took a knife and slaughtered herself. I reached her after she had cut some of her jugular veins, so I treated her and she recovered. Then she became devout and devoted herself to the Quran. Now she is being proposed to, but what happened to her prevents me [from mentioning it].' Umar ؓ said: 'Would you intend to uncover a cover that Allah Almighty has concealed? If I learn that you mention anything of her affair, I will make you an example for the people of the cities. Rather, marry her off as a chaste Muslim woman.'"],[2333,"Uthman b. Abi al-As was invited to a circumcision, but he refused to attend. He was asked about that, and he said: 'During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we did not attend circumcisions, nor were we invited to them.'"],[2334,"He was invited to a meal, and when he came he said: “What is this?” They said: “The circumcision of a girl.” So he stood up and did not eat, and said: “This is something we were not invited to in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[2336,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave me some measures of dates and barley, and said: “When the women of the Ansar come to you, feed them from it.”"],[2337,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ made the wedding feast three days.”"],[2338,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ was asked about wedding feast food, and it was said: “O Commander of the Believers, what food is more fragrant than the aroma of our food?” He said: “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘In wedding feast food there is a measure of the fragrance of Paradise.’” Umar ؓ said: “Ibrahim the Friend ﷺ and Muhammad ﷺ prayed for it to be blessed and made pleasant.”"],[2340,"A man invited Abdullah b. Masud ؓ to a wedding feast. When he came he heard entertainment, so he did not enter. He said: “What is wrong with you?” He said: “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘Whoever swells the ranks of a people is one of them, and whoever approves of the action of a people is a partner of the one who did it.’”"],[2342,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ: “Is it disliked to refuse a kindness?” He said: “How ugly that would be! If a trotter were gifted to me I would accept it, and if I were invited to it I would respond.”"],[2343,"“Respond to your brother, for you are in a good position with him: either it is a truth you witness, or otherwise you forbid him from it and enjoin good upon him.”"],[2345,"“Whoever enters upon a meal without being invited to it enters as a sinner and eats what is unlawful.”"],[2347,"A woman came to him and said: “What is the husband’s right over his wife?” He ﷺ said: “She should not deny him herself even if she is on the back of a camel saddle, and she should not give anything from his house except with his permission, and if she does that the reward is his and the sin is hers. She should not fast a voluntary day except with his permission, and if she does that she sins and is not rewarded. She should not go out of his house except with his permission, and if she does the angels curse her—the angels of wrath and the angels of mercy—until she repents or returns.” It was said: “Even if he is unjust?” He said: “Even if he is unjust.”"],[2348,"\"I will never marry.\""],[2349,"When Muʿādh ؓ came from Yemen, he said: \"O Messenger of God ﷺ, I saw people prostrating to one another. Should we not prostrate to you?\" He ﷺ said: \"If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command women to prostrate to their husbands.\""],[2350,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by some women and said: \"Peace be upon you, O ungrateful deniers of kindness!\" They said: \"We seek refuge in God from denying God's blessings!\" He ﷺ said: \"One of you says when she is angry with her husband: 'I have never seen any good from you.'\""],[2351,"A man brought his daughter to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, this is my daughter, and she refuses to marry.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: \"Obey your father.\" She kept rejecting his words. She said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not marry until you tell me: what is the husband's right over his wife?\" He ﷺ said: \"If he had a wound, or his nostrils gushed blood and pus, and you licked it with your tongue, you would not have fulfilled his right.\" She said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never marry.\" He ﷺ said: \"Do not marry them off except with their permission.\""],[2352,"A man went on a military expedition while his wife was upstairs and her father was downstairs. He ordered her not to leave her house, and her father fell ill."],[2353,"She asked ʿĀʾishah ؓ, the Mother of the Believers, saying: \"One of our husbands desires her, and she withholds herself from him, either because she is angry or because she is not eager for him. Is there any sin upon her in that?\" She said: \"Yes. His right over you is that if he desired you while you were on a camel saddle, you should not refuse him.\""],[2354,"Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr came to her father complaining about al-Zubayr. He said to her: \"Return, my little daughter. If you are patient and treat him well, then he dies, and you do not marry after him, and you both enter Paradise, you will be his wife.\""],[2355,"\"It is not lawful for a woman to take from her husband's house except with her husband's permission. It is not lawful for her to take it while he is unwilling, nor to go out while he is unwilling without his permission, nor to make anyone covet him as long as they are together, nor to be harsh toward him, nor to keep away from his bed. She should not harm him, even if he is more unjust than her, until she comes to him and pleases him. If he accepts from her, then it is good and excellent; God accepts her excuse, and her argument prevails, and there is no sin upon her. If the husband refuses to be pleased, she has presented her excuse to him. If she does none of that, and she is content with separation until three nights pass for her. If she permits without his permission, or comes without his permission to visit a parent or someone else, and she breaks an oath for him, and obeys a parent or child in that, or keeps away from his bed, or is harsh toward him—then three major sins are written against them as long as they do that: the greatest of major sins: associating partners with God, killing a believer deliberately, and the third: consuming usury. It is a sufficient sin for a woman that every time her husband is angry with her, three major sins come, the devil takes control of her, and she becomes one of the people of the Fire.\" He said: \"And Muʿādh ؓ narrated to us that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The angels continue to curse her, and God Almighty curses her, and the keepers of the abode of mercy and the abode of punishment curse her because of what she has violated of disobedience to God, Mighty and Majestic.'\""],[2356,"We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among a group of women from the Ansar, and he took from us: 'That you will not deceive your husbands.' She said: When we left, we said: 'Did we ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what deceiving our husbands means?' So we returned to him and she asked him, and he said: 'That you betray him and gift his wealth to other than him.'"],[2358,"O people, indeed women are captives with you. You have taken them by Allah's trust, and made their private parts lawful by Allah's word. You have rights over them, and they have rights over you. Among your rights is that they not allow anyone you dislike to tread on your beds, and that they not disobey you in what is good. If they do that, then they are entitled to their provision and clothing with kindness. And if you strike them, strike with a blow that is not severe...\""],[2359,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade striking women, so they complained. Then he permitted them to strike them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Last night, seventy women went around the family of Muhammad, all of whom had been struck.' And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I do not like to see a man with his vein throbbing, the muscles of his neck bulging over his wife, killing her.'"],[2360,"The Prophet ﷺ stood among the people, praised Allah Almighty, extolled Him, then said: 'Indeed Allah Almighty enjoins you to treat women well! Indeed Allah enjoins you to treat women well! Indeed Allah enjoins you to treat women well! Indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your mothers, your fathers, your brothers, your paternal aunts, and your maternal aunts. Indeed a man from the People of the Two Books marries a woman and does not know what good he has in her, and neither of them desires to part from the other until they die of old age.'"],[2361,"Jibril ﷺ kept enjoining me to treat women well, until I thought that he would forbid divorcing them."],[2363,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'My wife does not prevent the hand of a toucher?' He said: 'Divorce her.' He said: 'She is a beautiful woman, and I love her.' He ﷺ said: 'Enjoy her.'"],[2365,"'Umar ؓ, when he heard a sound, would be alarmed; then if it was said: 'A circumcision or a wedding,' he would calm down."],[2366,"Muhammad b. Sirin used to be pleased with the beating of the tambourine at the wedding procession."],[2367,"I attended Thabit b. Wadi'ah and Qarazah b. Ka'b al-Ansari at a wedding, and there was singing. He spoke to them about that, and he said: 'Permission was granted for singing at weddings and for weeping over the dead without wailing.'"],[2368,"I entered upon 'Uqbah b. 'Amr, Thabit b. Yazid, and Qarazah b. Ka'b, and with them were slave girls singing and fragrant herbs. I said: 'You do this?!' They said: 'Permission was granted to us for singing at weddings and weeping over the dead without wailing.'"],[2369,"He used to love making marriage public."],[2371,"He passed by the people of al-dirakla (a kind of game) and said: \"Take hold, O Banu Arfida, so that the Jews and Christians may know that in our religion there is ample room (for permitted amusement).\" He said: While they were thus engaged, Umar ؓ came, and when they saw him they scattered."],[2373,"A man from the desert married his cousin, and she bore him a girl, then he died leaving her. A man from the Ansar married her (the widow). Her guardians said: We will not leave our daughter with them. They brought the dispute to the Prophet ﷺ. The mother said: I am the one who carried her, the one who is entitled to custody, and the one who breastfeeds. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: \"Whom do you choose?\" She said: I choose God and His Messenger and the abode of faith, and the Muhajirun and the Ansar. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not take her away as long as my eye watches over her, and if I remain, I will place her in a position that will delight her eye.\" He said: Then they brought the dispute to Abu Bakr ؓ, and he said to her: \"Whom do you choose?\" She said the same as the first statement. Abu Bakr ؓ ruled in favor of the guardians. Bilal ؓ stood up and said: \"O Abu Bakr...\" Then Abu Bakr ؓ ruled as the Messenger of God ﷺ had ruled."],[2374,"Umar ؓ divorced Umm Asim, and she died, and Asim remained in the care of his maternal grandmother. She disputed with him before Abu Bakr ؓ, and he ruled that the child should be with his grandmother, and the maintenance was upon Umar ؓ. He said: \"She has more right to him.\""],[2375,"Zayd b. Haritha ؓ went out to Makkah, and the daughter of Hamza b. Abd al-Muttalib ؓ arrived. Ja'far b. Abi Talib ؓ said: I will take her and I have more right to her; she is my cousin, and her maternal aunt is with me, and the maternal aunt is like a mother and has more right. Ali ؓ said: Rather I have more right to her; she is my cousin, and with me is the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and she has more right to her. And I raise my voice so that the Messenger of God ﷺ may hear my argument before he comes out. Zayd ؓ said: Rather I have more right to her; I went to her, traveled, and brought her. The Messenger of God ﷺ came out and said: \"What is the matter with you?\" Ali ؓ said: She is my cousin, and I have more right to her, and with me is the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ; she will be with her, and she has more right to her than anyone else. Ja'far ؓ said: I have more right to her, O Messenger of God; she is my cousin, and her maternal aunt is with me, and the maternal aunt is like a mother, and she has more right to her than anyone else. Zayd ؓ said: Rather I have more right to her; I went to her, undertook the journey and spent, so I have more right to her. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I will judge between you in this and in other matters.\" Ali ؓ said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ said \"and in other matters,\" I said: The Qur'an was revealed regarding our raising our voices. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"As for you, O Zayd, you are my mawla and their mawla.\" He ؓ said: I am content, O Messenger of God. He ﷺ said: \"As for you, O Ja'far, you resemble my creation and my character, and you are from my tree from which I was created.\" He ؓ said: I am content, O Messenger of God. He ﷺ said: \"As for you, O Ali, you are my chosen friend and my trustee.\" Yazid b. al-Had said: I mentioned that to Abdullah b. Hasan, and he said: Indeed he ﷺ said: \"You are from me and I am from you.\" He ؓ said: I am content, O Messenger of God. He ﷺ said: \"As for the girl, I have ruled that she goes to Ja'far, to be with her maternal aunt, and the maternal aunt is like a mother.\" They said: We submit, O Messenger of God."],[2377,"\"The example of a righteous woman among women is like the example of the crow with a white-marked foot (al-ghurab al-a'sam).\" It was said: O Messenger of God, what is al-ghurab al-a'sam? He ﷺ said: \"The one with one of its legs white.\""],[2379,"\"The woman is entrusted with her private part.\""],[2380,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Fatimah ؓ: \"Move to Umm Sharik, and do not cause us to miss you.\""],[2382,"I asked Sa'id b. al-Musayyib about a woman divorced three times: Where should she observe her waiting period? He said: In her husband's house. I said to him: Then what about the hadith of Fatimah bt. Qays? He said: That woman caused trouble for the people; she was foul-tongued. Or he said: She was a woman with evil in her tongue towards her in-laws."],[2384,"I came to Ibrahim al-Nakha'i and said: A man disputed with me - he was called Sa'id - ... and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then Ibrahim said: That came to me once, and he claimed that he said to his wife: Every wife of his is divorced three times except you. I said: Shurayh used to say: If he begins with divorce, it takes effect on her. It reached me that when he went out, he said: Is this anything but the opinion of men? Then it reached me that he became wary regarding her and left her. Jarir said: I met Sa'id al-Zubaydi and asked him about this. He said: Indeed I asked Sa'id b. Jubayr and he said: She is not divorced. Then al-Zubaydi said: Indeed, if I had been in the state I am today back then, I would not have divorced her."],[2385,"\"O Mu'adh, God has not created anything on the face of the earth more beloved to Him than emancipation, and God has not created anything on the face of the earth more hateful to Him than divorce. So if a man says to his slave: You are free, if God wills - he is free, and there is no exception for him. And if he says to his wife: You are divorced, if God wills - then he has his exception, and no divorce occurs.\""],[2387,"The divorce of the intoxicated person is not valid."],[2389,"I heard Ibn 'Umar ؓ say about the man who marries a woman to make her lawful (for her previous husband): 'They are both adulterers, even if they remain together for ten years or twenty years, since he married her for that.'"],[2391,"News reached Abu Musa ؓ that the Prophet ﷺ was displeased with them, so he came to him and mentioned that. He said: 'One of you says, \"I married, I divorced,\" but that is not the way of the Muslims. Divorce the woman in the beginning of her waiting period.'"],[2392,"A man never divorces according to the Sunnah and then regrets it forever."],[2394,"A man proposed to a woman, and they said: 'We will not marry you until you divorce three times.' He said: 'Bear witness that I have divorced three times.' When he consummated the marriage with the woman, they claimed the divorce. He said to them: 'How did I say it?' He said: 'We said, \"We will not marry you until you divorce three times,\" and you divorced three times.' He said: 'Do you not know that I married so-and-so daughter of so-and-so and divorced her, and so-and-so was under me and I divorced her,' until he counted three. They said: 'That is not what we meant.' So Shaqiq b. Thawr went to 'Uthman ؓ, and they instructed him to ask 'Uthman about that. When he arrived, he asked him, and he reported that he asked 'Uthman ؓ, and he said: 'He has his intention.'"],[2395,"If he says: 'Your affair is in your hand,' 'Take care of your own affair,' or 'I have directed you to your family if they accept her' - it is one irrevocable divorce."],[2396,"Ibn Abi 'Atiq came to Zayd b. Thabit ؓ while weeping. He said: 'What makes you weep?' He said: 'I gave my wife authority over her affair, and she separated from me.' He said: 'What made you do that?' He said: 'Destiny.' He said: 'It is one divorce; if you wish, take her back, and if you wish, leave her.'"],[2397,"Regarding (saying) 'haram': 'If he intended divorce, then it is divorce, and if he did not intend divorce, then it is an oath that you expiate.'"],[2398,"Kinana b. Thawr had a wife who had borne him children in the pre-Islamic era. He said to her: 'What is above your belt is forbidden.' She took her case to al-Ash'ari, who said: 'What did you intend?' He said: 'Divorce.' He said: 'It has separated her from you.'"],[2400,"We were with Ibn Mas'ud ؓ, and a man came to him and said: 'A man said to his wife, \"She is divorced eight times.\"' He said: 'Did you say it in one go?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Do you want your wife to be separated from you?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'It is as you said.' Then another came and said: 'A man said to his wife, \"Tonight she is divorced as many times as the stars.\"' He said: 'Did you say it in one go?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Do you want your wife to be separated from you?' He said: 'Yes.' Ibn Mas'ud ؓ then mentioned the women of the people of the earth with something I do not remember, then he said: 'Allah has made clear to you how divorce is. Whoever divorces as Allah Almighty commanded him, it will be made clear to him, and whoever is confused about it, we will make his confusion apply to him. By Allah, you will not confuse yourselves and we will bear it. It is as you say.'"],[2401,"He said: \"The one with whom consummation has not occurred, when the triple [divorce] is combined upon her, it takes effect.\" He said: I mentioned that to Tawus, and he said: I bear witness that I heard Ibn Abbas make it one. He said: And Amr said: One, even if he combines them."],[2402,"\"The one with whom consummation has not occurred, and the one with whom consummation has occurred - in the triple [divorce] they are the same.\""],[2403,"A man among my forefathers divorced his wife a thousand times, so his sons came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Indeed your father did not fear Allah, so as to make for him a way out. She is irrevocably separated from him by three [divorces]. And the rest of them are an act of aggression; he took the signs of Allah in mockery.\""],[2405,"\"Jesting is not permissible in three things: divorce, marriage, and manumission. So whoever utters them, they become binding.\""],[2406,"A man in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would divorce his wife and say: I was joking, and he would free his slave and say: I was joking, and he would give his daughter in marriage and say: I was joking. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Three things - whoever says them in jest, they are valid upon him: divorce, manumission, and marriage.\" So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed concerning that: 'And do not take the signs of Allah in mockery.'"],[2408,"Al-Ghumaysa' or al-Rumaysa' came complaining about her husband, and she said: He does not reach her. He said: She lied, O Messenger of Allah! Indeed I do it, but she wants to return to her first husband. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"She is not lawful for him until she tastes his honey.\""],[2409,"\"She is not lawful for him until she tastes the honey.\""],[2410,"\"The honey is intercourse.\""],[2411,"He only meant by the honey marriage."],[2413,"\"There is no divorce before marriage.\""],[2414,"Ibn Jurayj said: And Amr b. Shu'ayb said, from Tawus, from Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ - the like of it."],[2415,"\"There is no divorce before marriage.\""],[2416,"There is no divorce before marriage, and no manumission before ownership."],[2417,"“There is no divorce for one who has not married, and no manumission for one who has not owned, and no vow in disobedience to Allah, Exalted is He.”"],[2419,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking his permission to marry, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have married three. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Marry, and do not divorce; for Allah, Exalted is He, hates the tasters—men and women who frequently marry and divorce.”"],[2420,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I heard Allah, Exalted is He, say: “Divorce is twice.” So where is the third? He said: “Then either retain [her] in kindness or release [her] with excellence.”"],[2422,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, who am I? He ﷺ said: “You are Sa'd b. Malik b. Wahb b. 'Abd Manaf b. Zuhrah. Whoever says otherwise, upon him is the curse of Allah, Exalted is He.”"],[2424,"Mu'awiyah proposed to Umm al-Darda' ؓ , but she refused to marry him. She said: I heard Abu al-Darda' ؓ say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The woman belongs to her last husband,” and I do not want a replacement for Abu al-Darda'."],[2426,"Umar ؓ sent for a man from Banu Zuhrah while he was in al-Hijr. He said: I went with him to him, and he had reached [the time of] the Jahiliyyah. He asked him about a child born in the Jahiliyyah. Sufyan said: The people of the Jahiliyyah had no waiting period for their women. When a man died, the woman would go and be married without observing a waiting period. He said: He asked him about the sperm-drop. He said: As for the sperm-drop, it is from so-and-so; but the child belongs to the bed of so-and-so. Umar ؓ said: “He has spoken the truth, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the child belongs to the bed.” When the man turned away, he said..."],[2427,"Nasr b. al-Hajjaj claimed 'Abd Allah b. Rabah, the freedman of Khalid b. al-Walid. Then 'Abd al-Rahman b. Khalid b. al-Walid stood up and said: 'My freedman; he was born on my father's bed.' Nasr said: 'My brother; he and my daughters are in the same position.' He said: Their dispute grew long, so they entered upon Mu'awiyah while Fihr was under his head, and they both claimed him. Mu'awiyah ؓ said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The child belongs to the bed, and the fornicator gets the stone.\"' Nasr said: 'Where is this judgment of yours, O Mu'awiyah, regarding Ziyad?' Mu'awiyah said: 'The judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is better than the judgment of Mu'awiyah.' He said: 'Abd Allah b. Rabah would not respond to Nasr's claim. So Nasr said: 'O Abu Khalid, there is no wealth like one you inherit, so take me as a brother at the bed as a witness. O Abu Khalid, my wealth is abundant and my standing is something, and my roots will make you rise ever higher. O Abu Khalid, do not make our daughters slaves to Makhzum, and be generous. O Abu Khalid, if you fear Ibn Khalid, al-Hajjaj did not fear Khalid. O Abu Khalid, we are not fire nor are they gardens where eyes graze, calm.'"],[2429,"I heard Ibn 'Abbas ؓ while I was standing at his head saying, and a man said to him: 'Mu'awiyah ؓ forbade temporary marriage.' Ibn 'Abbas ؓ said: 'Look: if it is in the Book of Allah Almighty, then he has lied against the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and if it is not in the Book of Allah Almighty, then it is as he said.'"],[2430,"'A'ishah ؓ, when asked about temporary marriage, would say: 'Between me and you is the Book of Allah Almighty.' Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'And those who guard their private parts, except from their spouses...' the verse. She said: 'So whoever seeks other than what Allah Almighty has married him to or given him ownership of has transgressed.'"],[2431,"\"Marriage, divorce, and inheritance abolished temporary marriage.\""],[2432,"We were on the expedition of Tabuk, and we stopped at Thaniyyat al-Wada'. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw lamps and women weeping, and said: 'What is this?' It was said: 'Women who were taken in temporary marriage, so they are weeping.' He ﷺ said: 'It is forbidden.' Or he said: 'Marriage, divorce, waiting period, and inheritance abolished temporary marriage.'"],[2433,"\"If I had gotten ahead regarding temporary marriage with women, I would have stoned.\""],[2435,"\"If he buys her as a virgin, he may, if he wishes, not seek clearance of her womb.\""],[2436,"He forbade on the day of Khaybar that pregnant women be penetrated until they give birth."],[2437,"\"Hold to the concubines, for they have blessed wombs.\""],[2438,"He forbade on the day of Khaybar that pregnant women be penetrated, and said: 'Would you water another's crop?!'"],[2439,"He forbade that pregnant captive women be penetrated."],[2440,"The Prophet ﷺ sought to ascertain the womb status of Safiyyah ؓ, so it was said to him: \"Is she from the Mothers of the Believers or from the Mothers of the Children?\" He said: \"From the Mothers of the Believers.\""],[2442,"'A'ishah took her sister Umm Kulthum, the wife of Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah ؓ, and performed Hajj with her during her waiting period."],[2444,"Umm Kulthum bt. 'Uqbah was married to al-Zubayr b. al-'Awwam. He went out for prayer while she was in labor. She concealed it from him, and said to him: \"Put my heart at ease with a divorce.\" So he divorced her. When he returned, she had already given birth. He went to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him, and he said: \"The term has reached its appointed time. Propose to her.\" He said: \"She deceived me, may Allah Almighty deceive her.\""],[2446,"Ibn al-Kawwa' asked 'Ali ؓ about two slave-girls who were sisters. He said: \"One verse permitted them and another verse forbade them. Neither I nor anyone from my household would do it, nor would I declare it lawful or unlawful.\""],[2447,"'Umar ؓ was asked about a woman and her daughter from right hand possession. He said: \"I would not like to permit both of them together, and I forbid both together.\""],[2448,"Mu'adh b. 'Ubayd Allah b. Ma'mar asked 'A'ishah ؓ, saying: \"I have a slave-girl whom I have had relations with, and she has a daughter who has reached puberty. May I have relations with her?\" She forbade him from that. He said: \"No, unless you say it is forbidden.\" She said: \"No one from my family does that, nor anyone who obeys me.\""],[2449,"Ibn 'Umar ؓ was asked about it and he forbade it."],[2451,"I attended the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came to him and said: \"If I find a man on the belly of my wife, should I strike him with the sword?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What evidence is clearer than the sword?\" Then he recanted and said: \"The Book of Allah Almighty and a witness.\" Sa'd b. 'Ubadah ؓ said: \"What evidence is clearer than the sword?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Book of Allah Almighty and a witness.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O assembly of the Ansar, this Sa'd has been provoked by jealousy until he contradicted the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic!\" A man from the Ansar said: \"Sa'd is jealous; he never married a previously married woman, and none of us could marry a woman he had divorced.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Sa'd is jealous, and I am more jealous than him, and Allah is more jealous than me.\" A man from the Ansar said: \"Over what does Allah Almighty become jealous?\" He said: \"Over a man who strives in the path of Allah Almighty while his family is violated.\""],[2452,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to enter upon his wives every morning and greet them. Among them was a woman who had honey. Whenever he ﷺ entered upon her, she would bring him some of it, and he would stay with her. 'A'ishah and Hafsah ؓ noticed that. When he ﷺ entered upon them, they said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we smell the scent of maghafir from you!\" He said: \"So he ﷺ abandoned that honey.\""],[2453,"He said: \"O Zayd b. Thabit, do you not know that we used to recite among what we recited: 'Do not disown your fathers, for that is disbelief on your part'?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[2454,"When the affair of the two who engaged in li'an came before the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'I would not like to be the first of the four.'"],[2455,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ conducted li'an between the 'Ajlani and his wife, who was 'Uwaymir b. al-Harith, and he conducted li'an between them regarding a pregnancy."],[2457,"Ka'b b. Malik ؓ wanted to marry a Jewish woman, so he asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he forbade him, saying: 'She will not protect you (i.e., preserve your chastity).'"],[2459,"Ghaylan embraced Islam while he had ten wives, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to choose four of them and separate from the rest. And Safwan ؓ embraced Islam while he had eight wives, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to keep four of them and separate from the rest."],[2461,"'The ila' of the Jahiliyyah was for a year, two years, or more than that. Allah the Exalted set a time limit for them of four months, so whoever's ila' is less than four months is not ila'.' And 'Ata' said: 'If he makes ila' from her while she is in her family's house before she is brought to him, it is not ila'.'"],[2463,"I asked al-Qasim b. Muhammad about a man who said: 'If I marry so-and-so, she is divorced.' He said: 'A man came to 'Umar ؓ and said: I said: If I marry so-and-so, she is zihar. He said: If you marry her and want to keep her, you must offer expiation.'"],[2464,"A man made zihar from his wife until Ramadan ended, or he said: He made zihar from her for Ramadan, then he came to his family at night..."],[2465,"A woman from Banu Bayadah sent to the Prophet ﷺ a wasq of barley, or he said: half a wasq of barley - Ayyub was uncertain. The Prophet ﷺ gave it to the one who had made zihar from his wife, and said: 'Give this as charity, for a sa' of barley suffices in place of half a sa' of wheat.'"],[2466,"A man made zihar from his wife, then he saw her in the moonlight and she pleased him, so he had intercourse with her. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him, and he said: 'Has Allah the Exalted not said: before they touch each other?' He said: 'I saw her and she pleased me!' He said: 'Refrain until you offer expiation.'"],[2468,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'What removes from me the reproach of breastfeeding?' He ﷺ said: 'The slave,' meaning a male or female slave."],[2469,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'Why do you not marry the daughter of Hamzah ؓ?' He ﷺ said: 'She is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding, and breastfeeding makes unlawful what is unlawful through lineage.'"],[2470,"There is no breastfeeding after weaning, and no orphanhood after a wet dream."],[2471,"He forbade that a foolish woman be used as a wet-nurse, and said: \"Indeed, milk causes resemblance.\""],[2472,"The 'ayfa does not make [marriage] prohibited. We said: What is the 'ayfa? He said: A woman who gives birth and her milk becomes restricted in her breast, so her slave-girl suckles from her once or twice."],[2473,"Seek wet-nurses among Muzaynah, for they are people of trustworthiness."],[2475,"'Amr b. Umayyah went out to the market, and while he was bargaining over a cloak, 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ appeared before him and said: What is this, O 'Amr? He said: I want to buy it and then give it as charity. He ؓ said: You then, you. So 'Umar paid, and 'Amr ؓ bought it. Then he entered upon his wife and said: I have given it to you as charity. Then he went out to the market and sat in his sitting place. 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ met him and said: What happened with the cloak? He informed him, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whatever you give them of anything is charity for you.\" So 'Umar ؓ said: Do not lie about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ! He said: Then he called from the door: O mother! She said: Come in, O 'Amr, what is the matter with you? He said: 'Umar ؓ says: Do not lie about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ! He said: I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whatever you give them of anything is charity for you\"? She said: O Allah, yes."],[2476,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ advising some of his family, saying: \"Spend on your family from your means, and do not raise your stick from them, and make them fear Allah, Mighty and Majestic.\""],[2477,"Whoever has two daughters, or two sisters, or two female relatives, and spends on them until they become self-sufficient, or until Allah, the Exalted, enriches them from His bounty, they will be a shield for him from the Fire."],[2478,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched a military expedition, and a young man asked his permission to go out with it. He said: \"Have you left behind anyone in your family who is complete?\" He said: \"I do not know, and they are young children.\" He said: \"Return to them, for in them there is a good struggle.\""],[2479,"\"Whatever a man spends on his family, his children, and his wealth, it is recorded for him as charity. And whatever a person uses to protect his honor is recorded for him as charity.\" He said: \"And every expenditure of a believer in other than disobedience is guaranteed by Allah, the Exalted, to be replaced, except an expenditure on building.\" So we said to Jabir ؓ: O Abu 'Abd Allah, what did he mean by his saying: \"whatever a person uses to protect his honor\"? He said: He gives to the poet and the one with a tongue. He said: It is as if he is saying: the one whose tongue is feared."],[2481,"Indeed, for a woman during her pregnancy until her delivery, until her weaning, there is reward like the one who wallows in the path of Allah. If she perishes during that, she has the reward of a martyr."],[2482,"\"Out of ninety-nine women, one is in Paradise, and the rest are in the Fire.\" This weighed heavily on those present from the Emigrants, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, when a Muslim woman becomes pregnant, she has the reward of one who fasts, stands in prayer, is in a state of ihram, and strives in the path of Allah, the Exalted. When she gives birth, then for her in the first breastfeeding is the reward of giving life to a soul.\""],[2484,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed to slaughter a number of camels at an idol from the idols of the pre-Islamic era? He ﷺ said: \"Fulfill your vow, and do not disobey your Lord.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience to Allah, the Exalted, nor in severing ties of kinship, nor in what one does not own.\""],[2485,"\"Three in which there is no oath: no oath for a child against his father, no oath for a woman against her husband, and no oath for a slave against his master.\""],[2486,"\"There is no vow in disobedience to Allah, the Exalted, and no oath in severing ties of kinship, and no oath for a slave against his master, and no oath for a wife with her husband, and no oath for a child with his father.\""],[2487,"He performed Hajj with a relative of his who was performing qiran with him, and the Prophet ﷺ saw him, and said: \"What is this?\" He said: It is a vow. \"Then he ordered that the qiran be cut off.\""],[2488,"Whoever swears by the Quran, then upon him for every verse is an oath."],[2489,"A man said in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"By the trust!\" So he said: \"Did I say: 'By the trust'?\" \"Did I say: 'By the trust'?\" ... He kept repeating it until we said: Would that he had kept silent!"],[2490,"From a woman, she said: If she wears a garment from her husband, it is a gift. He said: \"She gives it as a gift.\" And I asked al-Hasan, and he said: She expiates for her oath."],[2491,"Whoever swears an oath, then he is as he said. If he says, 'I am a Jew,' then he is a Jew; if he says, 'I am a Christian,' then he is a Christian; if he says, 'I am a Magian,' then he is a Magian."],[2492,"Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do that which is better and expiate for his oath."],[2493,"Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do that which is better, and no expiation is upon him."],[2494,"Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, its expiation is to abandon it."],[2495,"Whoever swears concerning his slave that he will beat him, its expiation is to leave him, and with expiation there is a good deed."],[2496,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man, 'O so-and-so, did you do such-and-such?' He said, 'No, by Allah, besides whom there is no god, I did not do it,' while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ knew that he had done it. So he said to him, 'Allah has expiated your lie by your affirmation of \"There is no god but Allah.\"'"],[2497,"Allah granted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some camels as spoils, and he displayed them. Abu Musa al-Ash'ari ؓ said, 'O Messenger of Allah, give me some!' He ﷺ said, 'No.' He asked him three times, then the Prophet ﷺ said, 'By Allah, I will not do it,' until there remained four with prominent humps. He said, 'Take them, O Abu Musa.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I asked you and you refused me, and you swore, so I feared that some doubt might have occurred to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He ﷺ said, 'When I swear an oath and then see that something else is better, I expiate for my oath and do that which is better.'"],[2498,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a group of people asking him for mounts. He said, 'I have nothing to mount you on, and by Allah, I will not mount you.' So he left us for some days, then some camels from the zakah camels were brought to him. He sent for me and ordered for us three camels with white humps. We departed with them, and I said to my companions, 'By Allah, I think there will be no blessing for us in them, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ swore that he would not mount us, so perhaps he forgot. Let us return to him and remind him of his oath.' So we returned to him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, your oath that you swore not to mount us?' He ﷺ said, 'I know my oath. Whoever among you swears an oath and then sees something better, let him do that which is better and expiate for his oath.'"],[2499,"There is no one who swears a false oath to thereby seize the property of a Muslim man, except that he will meet Allah Almighty while He is angry with him."],[2500,"We used to count among the sins for which there is no expiation the false oath (al-yamin al-ghamus). He said: It was asked, 'What is it?' He said: 'Seizing a man's property by his oath.'"],[2501,"A mudd of wheat for each poor person suffices for the expiation of an oath."],[2503,"A vow is an oath."],[2504,"And Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Yazid Abu Khalid, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir ؓ – the like of it. :"],[2505,"A man vowed to slaughter some camels at Buwana. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Did you swear an oath to that, and did you say that while there was in your soul something of the affairs of the pre-Islamic ignorance?” He said: No. He ﷺ said: “Then slaughter them.”"],[2506,"The sister of 'Uqbah b. 'Amir vowed to perform Hajj walking with her hair uncovered. He asked the Prophet ﷺ about that, and he ﷺ said: “Order her to veil herself, to ride, and to fast three days.”"],[2507,"His paternal aunt al-Furay'ah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has died and she had a vow that she did not fulfill. Will it suffice if I fulfill it on her behalf? He ﷺ said: “Tell me, if your mother had a debt and you paid it – would it not be accepted from you?” She said: Yes. He ﷺ said: “Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is more deserving of that!” She said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother died and she had to walk to the Ka'bah? He ﷺ said: “Are you able to walk on her behalf?” She said: Yes. He ﷺ said: “Then walk on behalf of your mother.”"],[2508,"There is no vow in disobedience to Allah."],[2509,"The Prophet ﷺ sent out an army and said: “If good news comes to me from them, I will surely praise Allah, the Exalted, with the praise He fully deserves.” When good news from them came to him ﷺ, he said: “O Allah, to You belongs praise as gratitude, and to You belongs favor as grace.” 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said to him: O Messenger of Allah, you said: “If good news comes to me from them, I will surely praise Allah with the praise He fully deserves”? He ﷺ said: I said: “O Allah, to You belongs praise as gratitude, and to You belongs favor as grace.”"],[2512,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: “Which day is this?” We said: The day of sacrifice. He said: “Which month is this?” We said: Dhu al-Hijjah, a sacred month. He said: “Which land is this?” We said: A sacred land. He ﷺ said: “Indeed your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to you like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours! Let the one present convey to the one absent.”"],[2513,"The Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon during the Farewell Hajj and said: “O people, which land is this?” Then he mentioned something similar and added: “Do not revert after me to disbelief, striking one another's necks.”"],[2514,"He witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during his Hajj in his sermon, and he said: “Indeed your wealth and your blood are sacred to you like the sanctity of this land on this day. Let no one make you revert after me to disbelief, striking one another's necks. Let the one present convey to the one absent.” He said: I do not know whether I will ever meet you here after today. O Allah, bear witness against them. Have I conveyed?"],[2515,"This surah was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the middle of the days of Tashriq at Mina, while he was on the Farewell Hajj: “When the victory of Allah and the conquest comes…” until he finished it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ knew that it was the farewell, so he ordered his mount al-Qaswa' to be saddled, and it was saddled for him. He ﷺ stood for the people at al-'Aqabah, and the people gathered to him. He praised Allah, the Exalted, and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: O people, every blood that was shed in the pre-Islamic ignorance is now null and void, and the first blood I abolish is the blood of Iyas b. Rabi'ah b. al-Harith, who was being nursed among Banu Layth and was killed by Hudhayl. And the first usury I abolish is the usury of al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib ؓ . You shall have your capital sums, so you do not wrong and you are not wronged."],[2516,"I found on the blade of the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a writing: “Among the people most severe in transgression is one who strikes someone other than the one who struck him, a man who kills someone other than his killer, and a man who gives allegiance to someone other than the people who have shown him favor. Whoever does that has disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger, and Allah will accept from him neither ransom nor recompense. And in the other: The believers’ blood is equal in value and their wealth is equal in protection; the lowest of them may grant protection on their behalf; a Muslim is not to be killed for a disbeliever, nor one who has a covenant while his covenant remains; the people of two different religions do not inherit from one another; a woman is not to be married to her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt; there is no prayer after ‘Asr until the sun sets; and a woman is not to travel three nights without a mahram.”"],[2517,"He used to stand before the people on the day of Adha or the day of Fitr and say: “I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage saying: ‘What day is this?’ They said, ‘The day of sacrifice.’ He said, ‘What month is this?’ They said, ‘A sacred month.’ He said, ‘What land is this?’ They said, ‘The sacred city.’ He ﷺ said: ‘Indeed your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to you like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours, until the day you meet Him. O Allah, have I conveyed? Let the one present convey to the one absent.’” Wabisah said: “So we testify against you as it was testified against us.”"],[2519,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prescribe a fixed punishment for wine until Abu Bakr ؓ prescribed forty lashes.” Ibn Shihab said: Al-Sa'ib b. Yazid said: “Then Umar ؓ prescribed eighty. Then Uthman ؓ lashed both eighty and forty: when a man was brought to him full of drink, he lashed him eighty, and when a man was brought to him who had slipped a slip, he lashed him forty.”"],[2520,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ advising one of his family, saying: “Beware of wine, for it is the key to every evil …”"],[2521,"“It has reached me that Umar, Ibn Umar, and Uthman ؓ used to lash forty for wine.”"],[2522,"“A man drank wine or cooked grape juice—Hushaym was unsure—so he came to Umar ؓ and said: ‘He drank only what is lawful.’ His words were more severe to him than what he had done, so he consulted about him, and they advised him to strike him eighty lashes, and it became a sunnah after him.”"],[2523,"“Whoever drinks wine, lash him eighty.”"],[2524,"“Ibn al-Nu‘ayman was brought to the Prophet ﷺ having drunk wine, so he ordered those in the house and they stood up and struck him with their hands, palm branches, and sandals.”"],[2525,"“Whoever drinks wine, lash him. If he repeats it a fourth time, kill him.”"],[2527,"“A man gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a leather waterskin of wine as a gift, so he ordered it to be sold. When he turned away, he ﷺ said: ‘The One who forbade drinking it forbade selling it,’ so he ﷺ ordered its stopper to be untied and it was opened.”"],[2528,"“There was a man who transported wine from Khaybar and sold it to the Muslims. He brought some with the money and arrived with it in Madinah, where a Muslim met him and said: ‘O so-and-so, wine has been forbidden.’ So he put it down where he reached, on a hill, and covered it with cloths. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, I have heard that wine has been forbidden.’ He ﷺ said: ‘Yes.’ He said: ‘Should I return it to the one I bought it from?’ He ﷺ said: ‘It is not proper to return it.’ He said: ‘Should I give it as a gift to someone who may repay me for it?’ He ﷺ said: ‘No.’ He said: ‘There is wealth in it belonging to orphans under my care.’ He ﷺ said: ‘When the wealth of Bahrain comes to us, we will compensate your orphans from their wealth.’ Then he called out: ‘O people of Madinah!’ The man said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, what about the containers, we can make use of them.’ He ﷺ said: ‘Then untie their stoppers.’ So they poured out until it settled in the belly of the valley.”"],[2530,"Three verses were revealed concerning wine. The first thing that was revealed was: 'They ask you about wine and gambling...' the verse. It was said: 'Has wine been forbidden?' They said: 'O Messenger of God, let us benefit from it as God, Mighty and Majestic, has said!' He ﷺ remained silent about them. Then this verse was revealed: 'Do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated...' the verse. It was said: 'Has wine been forbidden?' They said: 'O Messenger of God, we do not drink it near prayer time,' and he ﷺ remained silent about them. Then it was revealed: 'O you who believe, indeed wine, gambling, sacrificing on stone altars, and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan, so avoid it.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Wine has been forbidden.' A skin of wine from Syria – or skins – was brought to a man, so the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar ؓ stood up."],[2531,"He used to gift the Messenger of God ﷺ a skin of wine every year. When God Almighty sent down the prohibition of wine, he came with it. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw it, he laughed and said: 'It has been forbidden after you!' He said: 'O Messenger of God, shall I sell it and benefit from its price?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'May God curse the Jews; He forbade them the fat of cattle and sheep, so they melted it and sold it. Indeed God Almighty has forbidden wine and its price.'"],[2532,"A man used to gift the Prophet ﷺ a skin of wine every year. He gifted it to him one year after it had been forbidden. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'It has been forbidden!' The man said: 'Shall I not sell it?' He said: 'The One who forbade drinking it has forbidden selling it.' He said: 'Shall I not use it to honor the Jews?' He ﷺ said: 'The One who forbade it has forbidden using it to honor the Jews!' He said: 'Then what shall I do with it?' He ﷺ said: 'Pour it out in the stony valley.'"],[2533,"A man met the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, I have brought my merchandise.' He ﷺ said: 'What is your merchandise?' He said: 'Wine.' He ﷺ said: 'Take it to the stony valley, untie its mouths, and pour it out.' He said: 'He went out with it, but his soul refused, so he returned to him and said: 'O Messenger of God, what is wrong with me and my family; there is nothing that can provide for me, near or far, other than it!' The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'Take it out to the stony valley, untie its mouths, and pour it out.' He said: 'So he did.' Then he returned to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I have done it, O Messenger of God!' The Messenger of God ﷺ raised his hands until the whiteness of his armpits was seen, and said: 'O God, enrich so-and-so and the family of so-and-so from Your bounty!' Indeed, if a man from that household died, he would leave as inheritance a thousand camels."],[2535,"The drinker of wine is like the worshiper of the idol, and the drinker of wine is like the worshiper of al-Lat and al-Uzza."],[2536,"Whoever drinks wine, little or much, God Almighty will give him to drink from the boiling water of Hell on the Day of Resurrection."],[2537,"God does not accept the prayer of a wine drinker as long as any of it remains in his body."],[2538,"Whoever drinks wine, his prayer is not accepted for forty days; if he dies, he goes to the Fire; if he repents, God, Mighty and Majestic, accepts his repentance. If he drinks it a second time, his prayer is not accepted for forty days; if he dies, he goes to the Fire; if he repents, God Almighty accepts his repentance. If he drinks it a third or fourth time, it is a right upon God Almighty to give him to drink from the mud of khabal. It was said: 'O Messenger of God, what is the mud of khabal?' He said: 'The pus of the people of the Fire.'"],[2539,"Muhammad b. Abi Bakr narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, Fudayl b. Maysarah narrated to us, from Abu Hariz, from Shahr b. Hawshab, from Ibn Abbas ؓ, and he mentioned something similar:"],[2540,"The child of adultery will not enter Paradise, nor one who is disobedient to his parents, nor one addicted to wine. It was said: 'O Messenger of God, what is one addicted to wine?' He ﷺ said: 'Three years, once in each year.'"],[2541,"Whoever departs this world while intoxicated will be placed in the grave intoxicated, will be raised from his grave intoxicated, and will be ordered to the Fire intoxicated, to a mountain called Sakran, in which there is a spring through which pus and blood flow; that is their food and drink as long as the heavens and the earth endure."],[2543,"I was with Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ in Syria. The people of the covenant said: 'You have burdened us—or imposed upon us—that we supply the Muslims with honey, and we cannot find it.' Umar ؓ said: 'Indeed, when the Muslims enter a land and are not settled there, it is hard for them to drink plain water, so they must have something to make it palatable.' They said: 'We have a drink we make from grapes, something resembling honey.' He said: 'Then bring it.' They brought it, and he ؓ began lifting it with his finger and stretching it like honey. He said: 'This is like the tar of camels.' Then he ؓ called for water and poured it over it, then he lowered it and drank from it, and his companions drank. He said: 'How good this is! So supply the Muslims with it.' They supplied them with it. It remained as long as Allah willed, then a man became numb from it. The Muslims rose and beat him with their sandals, saying: 'A drunkard!' The man said: 'Do not kill me, for by Allah I drank nothing but what Umar ؓ supplied us.' Umar ؓ stood among the people and said: 'O people, I am only a human being; I do not make lawful what is lawful, nor make unlawful what is unlawful. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken, and revelation was lifted.' Then Umar ؓ took hold of his garment and said: 'I declare my innocence before Allah, the Exalted, of making unlawful things lawful for you, so leave it, for I fear that people will enter into it deeply. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Every intoxicant is unlawful.\" So leave it.' Then Uthman ؓ used to make it, then Mu'awiyah ؓ used to drink the sweet (unfermented) kind."],[2544,"I forbid you from a small amount of that whose large amount intoxicates."],[2545,"Al-Ash'ari ؓ addressed us on the pulpit of Basrah and said: 'Indeed, the wine that was forbidden in Madinah is the mixture of unripe dates and dried dates.'"],[2546,"There is no jalab, no janab, no wirat, and no shighar in Islam, and every intoxicant is unlawful."],[2547,"He forbade combining fresh dates and raisins (in making drink)."],[2548,"I used to boil tila' for Abu al-Darda' ؓ until two-thirds of it went and one-third remained."],[2549,"Abu al-Darda' ؓ used to drink tila' from the pitch-lined jar."],[2550,"Intoxication is one of the major sins."],[2551,"Whoever drinks a drink until his mind goes has come to a door of the doors of major sins."],[2552,"Every intoxicant is unlawful."],[2553,"Abdullah used to swear that what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade when wine was forbidden—and he ordered its jars to be broken and poured out—is dates and raisins."],[2554,"The first thing Islam is poured out as a vessel is poured out is a drink called tila'."],[2555,"I entered upon 'A'ishah ؓ in her chamber among women from the Ansar, and they began asking her about vessels. She said: 'O believing women, you are asking about vessels, many of which did not exist at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Whatever drink intoxicates any of you, let her avoid it; and if the water of her beloved intoxicates her, let her avoid it. For every intoxicant is forbidden.'"],[2556,"I do not deem lawful any intoxication, even if it be from bread or water."],[2557,"Every intoxicant is forbidden."],[2559,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when the delegation of 'Abd al-Qays came. He said: 'What is the matter with you that your complexions have turned yellow, your bellies have grown large, and your veins have become prominent?' They said: 'Our leader came to you and asked you about a drink that suited us, and you forbade him from it, and we are in a land that is unhealthy and feverish.' He ﷺ said: 'Then drink whatever is good for you.'"],[2560,"I went on a military campaign with 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ to Syria. We halted at a place, and a dihqan (village chief) came seeking the Commander of the Faithful until he reached him. When the dihqan saw 'Umar ؓ, he prostrated. 'Umar ؓ said: 'What is this prostration?' He said: 'This is what we do to kings.' 'Umar ؓ said: 'Prostrate to your Lord who created you!' Then he said: 'O Commander of the Faithful, I have prepared food for you; come to me.' 'Umar ؓ said: 'Is there anything in your house of Persian images?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'We have no need of your house, but go and send us a type of food, and do not add anything to it.' He said: 'So the dihqan left and sent him the food, and he ate from it. Then 'Umar ؓ said to his servant: 'Is there any of that nabidh in your water-skin?' He said: 'Yes.' He brought it to him, and he poured it into a vessel, then smelled it and found its odor objectionable. He poured water over it three times, then drank, and said: 'If you find anything objectionable in your drink, do this with it.'"],[2562,"He forbade (the use of) al-naqir and al-muqayyar – one of them or both – and al-dubba' and al-hantamah."],[2563,"He used to forbid (the use of) al-hantamah. He (the sub-narrator) said: I said: 'What is al-hantamah?' He said: 'The green jar.' And (he forbade) al-dubba', al-muqayyar, and al-muzafat. He said: I said: 'But we make jars of lead and soak (nabidh) in them at night and drink it in the morning.' He said: 'That, by Allah, is wine!' He said: I said: 'Then what?' He said: 'A water-skin in which you soak (nabidh) in the morning and drink it in the evening.'"],[2564,"I waited for the time when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would break his fast, and I brought him nabidh in a jar. When he brought it close to his mouth, it bubbled, so he said: 'Throw it against this wall, for this is the drink of one who does not believe in Allah and the Last Day.'"],[2565,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ with nabidh in a jar, and he said to him the like of that."],[2566,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[2567,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[2568,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[2569,"I asked Anas ؓ, and someone else also asked him: 'Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid nabidh in jars?' He said: 'How could he forbid it? By Allah, he never saw it at all!'"],[2570,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I am a man often sick, so permit me to use a jar in which I soak nabidh.' So he permitted it to me."],[2571,"And I heard him, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, forbidding nabidh in jars, and I heard him when he ordered the drinking of nabidh in jars."],[2573,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[2575,"'Amr b. al-'As ؓ wrote to 'Umar ؓ asking him about a man who embraced Islam, then disbelieved, then embraced Islam, then disbelieved, after that several times. Should Islam be accepted from him? 'Umar ؓ wrote to him: 'Accept from them what Allah accepted from them. Offer him Islam; if he accepts, then leave him, otherwise strike his neck.'"],[2576,"Abu Hurayrah ؓ said to me: Do you know al-Rajjāl? I said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'His molar tooth in the Fire is bigger than Mount Uhud.' He had embraced Islam, then apostatized and joined Musaylimah, and said: 'Two rams butted each other; the one I love most to win is my ram.'"],[2577,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[2579,"When al-Ḥajjāj encamped against Ibn al-Zubayr ؓ, he seized a man and handed him over to Sālim b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar ؓ to execute him. Sālim said to him: 'Are you a Muslim?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Have you prayed the dawn prayer?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Go, I have no way against you.' What he did reached al-Ḥajjāj, who said to him: 'What did the man do?' He said: 'I asked him: Are you a Muslim? He said: Yes. I asked him: Have you prayed the dawn prayer? He said: Yes. My father told me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that: Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under the protection of Allah Almighty until morning or evening.' He said: 'He is one of the killers of ʿUthmān ؓ.' He said: 'I am not the avenger of ʿUthmān, so I will not kill his killers.' This reached his father ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar ؓ, who rushed out dragging his lower garment and met him about what he had done, and said: 'I named you Sālim so that you would be safe; I named you Sālim so that you would be safe.'"],[2580,"A man passed by a mosque of the mosques of Banū Ḥanīfah, and their imam was reciting according to the recitation of Musaylimah: 'By the grinders, grinding; by the kneaders, kneading; by the bread-soakers, soaking; by the morsel-eaters, eating.' ʿAbd Allāh sent for them, and they were brought: seventy men reciting according to the recitation of Musaylimah. ʿAbd Allāh ؓ said: 'We cannot restrain Satan from these people. Send them off to Syria, perhaps Allah Almighty will destroy them by spear thrusts and plague.'"],[2582,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[2584,"Gabriel ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Muhammad, what an excellent people your community is, were it not that among them are remnants of the deeds of the people of Lot.'"],[2585,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say from the pulpit: 'Whoever does the deed of the people of Lot, kill him.'"],[2587,"A woman came to him and said: 'I have committed adultery.' He said: 'Perhaps you were approached while asleep in your bed, or were you coerced?' She said: 'I was approached willingly, not coerced.' He said: 'Perhaps you were overpowered?' She said: 'I was not forced.' He detained her, and when she gave birth and her son grew up, he had her flogged."],[2588,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[2589,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the youths of Quraysh: 'Do not commit adultery, for whoever Allah Almighty preserves his youth for him will enter Paradise.'"],[2590,"A woman confessed to adultery before ʿUmar ؓ. ʿUmar ؓ sent Abū Wāqid and said: 'If she retracts, we will leave her.' She refused, so he had her stoned."],[2592,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us ... and he mentioned the hadith, in which [he said]: \"Whoever walks in arranging the marriage of a man lawfully until he brings them together, God Almighty will provide him with a thousand women from the houris of paradise, each woman in a palace of pearl and ruby, and for every step he takes or word he speaks in that matter he will have the worship of a year: standing in prayer its nights and fasting its days. And whoever walks in reconciling a woman and her husband will have the reward of a thousand martyrs truly slain in the path of God, and for every step he will have the worship of a year, its fasting and its standing in prayer.\""],[2593,"No cuckold will enter Paradise."],[2596,"Avert the prescribed punishments from the servants of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[2599,"A servant girl belonging to the family of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ committed fornication. He said: “O ‘Ali, impose the prescribed punishment on her.” He said: He left her until she had given birth to what was in her womb, then he flogged her fifty times. Then he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said: “You have acted correctly.”"],[2600,"‘Umar ؓ carried out the prescribed punishment on a man while he was sick, and he said: “I fear that he may die before the prescribed punishment is carried out on him.”"],[2602,"Lesbianism among women is fornication on their part."],[2604,"A man came to ‘Ali ؓ and said: “I have committed an offense deserving a prescribed punishment.” ‘Ali ؓ said: “Ask him what it is.” But he did not inform them. So ‘Ali ؓ said: “Beat him until he tells you to stop.”"],[2606,"He and his father entered upon Anas ؓ, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then they went out the next morning and said: “Let us ride out to look and take a lesson.” He said: “Yes.” So they all rode out, and behold, they came upon deserted dwellings whose inhabitants had perished and vanished, leaving them empty and roofless. They said: “Do you know these dwellings?” He said: “How well I know them and their people! These were the people of dwellings whom transgression and envy destroyed. Envy extinguishes the light of good deeds, and transgression confirms or denies that. The eye commits adultery, and so does the palm, the foot, the hand, and the tongue; the private part confirms that or denies it.”"],[2608,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned, and Abu Bakr and ‘Umar ؓ stoned, and their practice is a sunnah."],[2610,"If I had previously decreed anything regarding temporary marriage, I would have stoned."],[2612,"A slave was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and it was said: “This one has stolen,” and evidence was established against him, and his stolen property was found with him. The Prophet ﷺ said: “This is a slave belonging to orphans who have no one else besides him,” so he let him go. Then he was brought a second time, and a third, and a fourth, and he let him go four times. Then he was brought a fifth time, and he cut off his hand. Then he was brought a sixth time, and he cut off his foot. Then a seventh time, and he cut off his hand. Then an eighth time, and he cut off his foot. Then al-Harith said: “Four for four; he pardoned him four times and punished him four times.”"],[2613,"He brought a slave of his to Umar ؓ who had stolen. He said: This one stole a mirror belonging to my family, and it is worth more than sixty dirhams. He said: Your servant took your goods."],[2614,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a man who had stolen a cloak. He said: Did you steal? I do not think you would steal. He said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Take him and cut off his hand, then cauterize it, then bring him to me. So they cut it off, then cauterized it, then brought him. He said: Repent to God. He said: I repent to God. He ﷺ said: O God, turn to him in mercy."],[2615,"A man brought to the Prophet ﷺ another man, leading him, and he had stolen a cloak. He ordered that his hand be cut off. The man said: O Messenger of God, I did not know that my cloak would reach the value for which a Muslim man's hand is cut off. He ﷺ said: Would that this had been before."],[2616,"Ibn al-Zubayr ؓ was brought a young servant of Umar b. Abdullah b. Abi Rabi'ah who had stolen. He ordered him to be measured by the span. He was found to be six spans, so he cut off his hand."],[2617,"Umar ؓ was brought a slave who had stolen. He ordered him to be measured by the span. He was found to be six spans less a finger joint, so he left him, and he was called Numaylah."],[2618,"I do not cut off more than a hand and a foot."],[2619,"Whoever steals, cut off his hand. Then if he steals, cut off his foot. Then if he steals, cut off his hand. Then if he steals, cut off his foot."],[2620,"I saw Ali ؓ when a man was brought to him. They said: He has stolen a camel. He said: I do not think you stole. He said: Yes. He said: Perhaps it was made to seem so to you? He said: Yes, I did steal. He said: Take him, Qanbar, tie his finger, light the fire, and call the butcher to cut. Then wait until I come. When he came, he said to him: Did you steal? He said: No, so he left him. They said: O Commander of the Faithful, why did you leave him when he had confessed to you? He said: I take him by his word and leave him by his word. Then Ali ؓ said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a man who had stolen. He ordered his hand to be cut off, then he wept. We said: O Messenger of God, why do you weep? He ﷺ said: How can I not weep when my community has its hands cut off before your eyes? They said: O Messenger of God, could you not have pardoned him? He ﷺ said: That is an evil ruler who pardons the prescribed punishments. But pardon one another for the prescribed punishments among yourselves."],[2621,"The likeness of one who sits on the bed of a woman whose husband is absent is like one whom lions bite on the Day of Resurrection."],[2622,"A man from those branches came to Umar. He spread out his quiver, and a sheet fell out, and in it was: 'Convey to Abu Hafs a message: May you be ransomed by a trusted brother of my loincloth. Our camels, may God guide you, we were distracted from you during the time of the siege. Camels of Banu Sa'd b. Bakr and Aslam, or Juhaynah, or Ghifar. Ja'dah of Sulaym hobbles them, seeking the tithe of the pregnant ones. What young camels were found hobbled behind Sal' at the gathering of the carpenters?' Umar ؓ said: Call Ja'dah b. Sulaym. He called him and spoke with him, and ordered him to be flogged a hundred lashes while hobbled, and forbade him to enter upon a woman whose husband is absent."],[2624,"Some people were at Aishah's ؓ tent—I think that was in Makkah—and Uthman ؓ passed by them. Abu Said ؓ said: There remained none of the group but cursed or reviled him except me. Among those who cursed or reviled him was a man from Kufah. Uthman ؓ was harsher toward the Kufan than toward others. He said: O Kufan, do you revile me? As if threatening him. He said: Then he went to Madinah, and it was said to him—meaning to the Kufan—: Go to Talhah. Talhah ؓ went with him until he came to Uthman ؓ. Uthman ؓ said: By God, I will flog you a hundred lashes. Talhah said: By God, you will not flog him unless he is an adulterer. He said: I will deprive you of your stipend. Talhah ؓ said: O Kufan, God will provide for you."],[2626,"There was some matter between Uthman and Aishah ؓ, and each of them spoke against the other. Aishah ؓ went to speak, but Uthman ؓ said the takbir, and the people said the takbir with him. He did that to her twice so that her words would not be heard. When she saw that, she fell silent."],[2628,"It is not permissible for anyone who believes in Allah and the Last Day to flog more than ten lashes except in the case of a prescribed punishment."],[2629,"He narrated to him — and he had slave boys in a village among the villages of the Romans — they fought each other, so he struck each of them three lashes."],[2631,"He proposed to a woman in Makkah while he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"If only I had someone to see her and tell me about her.\" A man called Hīt said: \"I will describe her for you: when she approaches, you would say she walks on six; when she turns away, you would say she walks on four.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"I consider this man to be objectionable; I think he knows about women.\" He used to enter upon her — meaning upon Sawdah ؓ. When he came to Madinah, he banished him. This remained so until the time of ʿUmar's rule, and he permitted him to enter Madinah on Friday and beg for charity."],[2633,"The Prophet ﷺ imprisoned someone on suspicion, as a precaution and for investigation, for a day and a night."],[2635,"A man said to another man: \"You do not approach your wife except in fornication or unlawfully.\" He brought him to ʿUmar ؓ, and ʿUmar ؓ said: \"He has accused you of something that is lawful for you.\""],[2638,"A man threw a stone at another man and killed him. He was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he exacted retaliation from him."],[2640,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called a young slave girl of his, and she was slow. He ﷺ said: \"Were it not for the fear of retaliation on the Day of Resurrection, I would have caused you pain with this toothstick.\""],[2642,"Ibn al-Zubayr ؓ exacted retaliation for a slap."],[2643,"A man stabbed another man with a horn in his knee. He came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking retaliation. It was said to him: \"Wait until you recover.\" He refused, hastened, and took retaliation. He said: His leg became defective, while the leg of the one from whom retaliation was taken healed. He came to the Prophet ﷺ, and it was said to him: \"You have nothing; you refused.\""],[2644,"Umar ؓ used to say about someone from whom retaliation was taken and then he died: His killing is justified, no blood money is due."],[2646,"Ibn Mas'ud ؓ used to say about it: The amount of his wound is deducted, and then he is liable for the remainder."],[2648,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding mutilation."],[2650,"I heard Umar ؓ while he was standing on this pulpit teaching the people the sunnahs, and among what he taught them, he said: For the collarbone a camel, for the molar a camel, and for the rib a camel."],[2651,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ used to assign for the thumb and the one next to it half the blood money of the hand, and he assigned for the thumb fifteen, for the one next to it ten, for the middle finger ten, for the one next to it nine, and for the last one six. Then Uthman b. Affan ؓ found a document that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote for Amr b. Hazm, in which was: And for the fingers ten, ten. So Uthman ؓ made them ten, ten."],[2652,"A man asked Ibn Umar ؓ about a one-eyed man whose healthy eye was gouged out. Abdullah b. Safwan said: Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ ruled for it the full blood money. He said: I am asking you. He said: You ask me while this one tells you that Umar ؓ ruled that?"],[2653,"I met Umar ؓ while he was at the season of pilgrimage, and I called from behind the tent: Indeed I am so-and-so son of so-and-so al-Jarmi, and a nephew of ours has a brother who is a captive among Banu so-and-so. We presented to him the obligatory compensation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but he refused. So Umar ؓ raised the side of the tent and said: Do you recognize your companion? I said: Yes. He said: There he is. Take him away so that we may carry out for you the judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: And we used to say that it was four camels."],[2654,"Umar ؓ used not to give inheritance from the blood money to brothers from the mother."],[2655,"Brothers from the mother do not inherit the blood money of their brother through their mother when he is killed."],[2656,"Indeed, 'Amr b. Ma'di Karib struck a man from Banu Kinanah with a ma'mumah (a head wound reaching the brain membrane). 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ wanted to exact retaliation from him, but al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: There is no retaliation for a ma'mumah."],[2657,"While I was with 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ, a Bedouin came to him seeking [retaliation for] a head wound. 'Umar ؓ said: We, the people of the towns, do not pay blood money among ourselves for [mere] flesh wounds (mudagh)."],[2658,"In our pre-Islamic ignorance (Jahiliyyah), we only paid blood money from the 'aql for what reached a third of the full diyah, and it was taken immediately. If it was not available with us, it was considered a debt to be paid later. When Islam came, among what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prescribed regarding the 'aqilah from Quraysh and the Ansar was a third of the diyah."],[2659,"He said regarding quasi-intentional killing (shibh al-'amd): the strike with a stick or a heavy stone [is compensated] in thirds: one third of jadha'ah (four-year-old camels), one third of hiqqah (three-year-old camels), and one third of thaniyyah (five-year-old camels) up to bazil of its year (six-year-old camels)."],[2660,"Two women from Hudhayl, one of them killed the other. He mentioned the hadith, and said: She was pregnant. The 'aqilah (male relatives) of the killed woman said: She was pregnant and miscarried a fetus. The 'aqilah of the killer feared that they would be made liable, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, it did not drink, nor eat, nor cry out at birth (istahalla). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: This is the rhymed prose of Jahiliyyah. He ruled for the fetus a ghurrah: a male or female slave."],[2661,"Hamal b. al-Nabighah had two wives: Mulaykah and Umm 'Afif. One of them threw a stone at the other and struck her in the heart, and she miscarried a dead fetus. That was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ruled that the diyah is upon the people of the 'aqilah of the killer, and for the fetus a ghurrah: a male or female slave, or ten camels, or one hundred sheep. Her guardian - or her father - said: O Messenger of Allah, it did not eat, nor drink, nor cry out at birth, so such a thing is void. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: We have nothing to do with the rhymed prose of Jahiliyyah."],[2662,"I found inscribed on the pommel of the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a writing: Among the most insolent of people is one who strikes someone other than the one who struck him, and a man who kills someone other than his killer, and a man who gives allegiance to other than his benefactor. Whoever does that has disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger; no optional or obligatory deed will be accepted from him. And regarding blood money: The believers' blood and property are equal in sanctity, and the lowest of them may strive to protect their blood. A Muslim is not killed for a disbeliever, nor one with a covenant while his covenant is in effect. The people of two different religions do not inherit from each other. A woman is not married in addition to her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt. There is no prayer after 'Asr until the sun sets. A woman does not travel for three nights except with a mahram."],[2664,"Some people from Juhaynah brought a captive to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Take him and warm him (adfi'uhu).\" He said: In their dialect, 'warmth' meant killing. So they took him and killed him. The Prophet ﷺ asked them, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, you commanded us to kill him, so we killed him. He ﷺ said: \"How did I say to you?\" They said: You said to us: Take him and warm him. He ﷺ said: I have shared with you; therefore pay his blood money, and I am your partner in it."],[2665,"The Muslims mistakenly struck Abu Hudhayfah ؓ on the day of Uhud, and he kept saying: 'My father, my father,' until they killed him. He said: 'May Allah forgive you, and He is the Most Merciful of those who show mercy.' This reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it increased him in goodness in his sight, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ paid his blood money from his own resources."],[2666,"So he commanded concerning it, and it was paid as blood money. I say: This story is in al-Bukhari from 'Urwah, and I did not see in it his statement: 'So it was paid as blood money.'"],[2667,"A man was crowded on Friday and died, so 'Ali ؓ paid his blood money from the public treasury."],[2668,"A man smashed the mouth of another man during the time of Mu'awiyah ؓ, and he offered him the blood money, but he refused. They increased it until they gave him three blood monies. He said: Then a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever gives charity of blood or of what is less than that, it will be an expiation for his past sins, from the day his mother gave birth to him until the day he gives charity of it.' He said: So the man pardoned."],[2670,"The blood money during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was of four ages: twenty-five hiqqah, twenty-five jadha'ah, twenty-five bint labun, and twenty-five bint makhad. This was until 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ established the garrison cities. 'Umar ؓ said: 'Not all people find camels, so value the camels at one uqiyyah each.' Thus it was four thousand. Then camels became expensive, so 'Umar ؓ said: 'Value the camels,' and they were valued at one and a half uqiyyah. He said: Thus it was six thousand. Then camels became expensive, so 'Umar ؓ said: 'Value the camels,' and they were valued at two uqiyyahs. Thus it was eight thousand. Then camels became expensive, so 'Umar ؓ said: 'Value the camels,' and they were valued at two and a half uqiyyahs. Thus it was ten thousand. Then camels became expensive, so 'Umar ؓ said: 'Value the camels,' and the camels were valued at three uqiyyahs. Thus it was twelve thousand. 'Umar ؓ then imposed upon the people of silver twelve thousand [dirhams], upon the people of gold one thousand dinars, upon the people of camels one hundred camels, upon the people of garments two hundred garments, the value of each garment being five dinars, upon the people of sheep one thousand ewes, upon the people of goats two thousand goats, and upon the people of cattle two hundred cows."],[2672,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of someone who encounters me wanting to take from my wealth?' He ﷺ said: 'Adjure him by Allah, the Exalted—three times. If he refuses, then fight him. If he kills you, you will enter Paradise, and if you kill him, he will enter the Fire.'"],[2675,"We were with one of the companions of Muhammad ﷺ one day during an illness he had, and he was unconscious. The Prophet ﷺ came to him and said: 'What were you discussing just now?' He said: 'We were mentioning the martyrs of this Ummah; we only consider one who goes out with his wealth until he is killed.' He ﷺ said: 'The martyrs of my Ummah would then be few. They are martyred by killing, plague, drowning, abdominal disease, a woman dying in childbirth, and her dying in her postpartum period.'"],[2676,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas ؓ disputed with Talhah b. 'Ubaydillah ؓ over some property of his. Talhah ؓ came to him one day while Sa'd ؓ was sitting with his sword drawn, placing it on his thighs. Talhah ؓ said to him: 'For whom have you prepared this, O Sa'd?' He said: 'For you.' He said: 'Would you really do it?' He said: 'By the One who sent Muhammad with the truth, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever fights over his wealth or wealth of his and is killed, he is a martyr.\"'"],[2677,"Rafi' b. Khadij ؓ was struck on the day of Uhud in his chest with an arrow. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'Remove the arrow.' He said: 'If you wish, I will remove the arrow and the cotton, and if you wish, I will remove the arrow and leave the cotton, and I will testify for you on the Day of Resurrection that you are a martyr.' I said: 'Remove the arrow and leave the cotton, and testify for me on the Day of Resurrection that I am a martyr.' He said: 'Yes.' So he removed the arrow and left the cotton, and he lived through the life of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr and 'Umar and 'Uthman ؓ. When it was the time of Mu'awiyah ؓ or after him, he died after 'Asr. They wanted to take him out [for burial], but Ibn 'Umar ؓ said: 'A man like Rafi' b. Khadij should not be taken out until the people of the surrounding villages are informed.' So he sat [unburied] until the next day. When the next day came, he was taken out. A female client of his wept at the edge of the grave, so Ibn 'Umar ؓ said: 'The old man cannot bear the punishment of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, from this foolish woman,' or words to that effect."],[2678,"Whoever is killed defending his property wrongfully is a martyr, and whoever is killed defending his own life is a martyr, and whoever is killed defending his family is a martyr, and whoever is killed defending his neighbor is a martyr, and whoever is killed in the cause of Allah Almighty is a martyr."],[2679,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."],[2680,"Whoever is thrown from his riding animal in the path of Allah Almighty and dies is a martyr."],[2681,"The destruction of my nation is by stabbing and plague. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this stabbing we have known, but what is the plague?' He ﷺ said: 'A poke from your enemies among the jinn, and in each of them are martyrs.'"],[2682,"The one stabbed, the one with a stomach ailment, the woman in childbirth, and the one who dies of a stomach disease are martyrdom."],[2683,"They will be martyred by killing, stabbing, drowning, stomach disease, the death of a woman while pregnant, and her death in childbirth."],[2684,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ in the cave, and he said: 'O Allah, stabbing and plague.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I know that you have asked for the deaths of your nation, so this stabbing we have known, but what is the plague?' He said: 'A sore like boils; if you live long, you will see it.'"],[2685,"The plague was mentioned, so I recalled that the Prophet ﷺ said: 'A poke that afflicts my nation from their enemies among the jinn, a gland like the gland of the stomach. Whoever remains in it is like a stationed soldier, and whoever is afflicted by it is a martyr, and whoever flees from it is like one who flees from battle.'"],[2686,"The martyrs were mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'They are those who, when they meet the enemy, do not turn their faces until they are killed. Those are the ones who will recline in the lofty chambers of Paradise, and their Lord will smile at them. And when your Lord smiles at a servant in a situation, there is no reckoning upon him.'"],[2687,"Indeed, Allah Almighty takes the souls of the martyrs of the sea with His own hand and does not entrust them to the Angel of Death. The parable of his soul when it departs from his chest is like milk when it enters his chest."],[2688,"The martyrs are three: A man who goes out with his own self and his wealth, patient and seeking reward, not wanting to kill or be killed. If he dies or is killed, all his sins will be forgiven, and he will be saved from the punishment of the grave, and he will be secure from the greatest terror, and he will be married to the houris with wide lovely eyes, and the garment of honor will be placed upon him, and the crown of eternity will be placed upon his head. The second: He goes out with his own self and his wealth, seeking reward, wanting to kill but not be killed. If he dies or is killed, his knee will be with the knee of Abraham, the close friend of the Most Merciful, before Allah, in a seat of truth. The third: A man who goes out with his own self and his wealth, seeking reward, wanting to kill and be killed. If he dies or is killed, he will come on the Day of Resurrection brandishing his sword, placing it on his shoulder, while the people are kneeling on their knees, saying: 'Make way for us, for we have offered our blood for Allah, Mighty and Majestic.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, if he said that to Abraham or to any prophet among the prophets, he would move aside for him from the path because of the right he sees. He will not ask Allah Almighty for anything except that He gives it to him, and he will not intercede for anyone except that his intercession is accepted, and he will be given in Paradise whatever he loves, and no prophet or anyone else will surpass him in station in Paradise. He will have in the Garden of Firdaws a thousand thousand cities of silver, a thousand thousand cities of gold, a thousand thousand cities of pearl, a thousand thousand cities of ruby, a thousand thousand cities of large pearls, a thousand thousand cities of chrysolite, and a thousand thousand cities of light. In each city among the cities are a thousand thousand palaces, in each palace a thousand thousand houses, in each house a thousand thousand couches. Each couch is a thousand years' journey in length and a thousand years' journey in width, and its height in the sky is five hundred years' journey. Upon it is a wife whose sleeve protrudes from the sides of the couch twenty miles from each corner; it has four corners. The lashes of her eyes are like the wings of eagles or like the primary feathers of eagles, and her eyebrows are like the crescent moon. Upon her are garments that grow in the gardens of Eden, watered from Tasnim, and their blossoms dazzle the eyes besides her. If she appeared to the people of this world, no sent prophet and no angel brought near would see her without being tempted by her beauty. Before each woman among them are a hundred thousand virgin female servants, besides the servants of her husband. Before each couch are chairs made of a substance other than the substance of the couch, each couch a hundred thousand cubits long. On each couch are a hundred thousand mattresses, the thickness of each mattress is as between heaven and earth, and between them is a distance of five hundred years' journey. They will enter Paradise five hundred years before the truthful and the believers. They will deflower the virgins. When he draws near to the couch, the mattresses will lower themselves for him until he mounts it, reclining wherever he wishes. He will recline with the houris with wide lovely eyes for seventy years, and one more splendid and more beautiful than her will call to him: 'O servant of Allah, is there not for us a turn with you?' He will turn to her and say: 'Who are you?' She will say: 'I am of those about whom Allah Almighty said: \"And with Us is more.\" Then one even more splendid and more beautiful will call to him: 'O servant of Allah, do you have no need of us?' He will say: 'I did not know your place.' She will say: 'Did you not know that Allah Almighty said: \"No soul knows what has been hidden for them of comfort for eyes\"?' He will say: 'Yes, by my Lord.'\" He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Perhaps he will be occupied with her after that for a year, occupied only with the bliss and pleasure he is in. When the people of Paradise enter, the martyrs of the sea will ride boats of pearls on a river of light. Their oars are rods of pearl, coral, and ruby. With them is a wind called al-Zahra' on waves like mountains. It is only shimmering light. Those waves are lighter in their eyes and sweeter to them than cold drink in a white glass to the people of this world on a summer day. Their days, which they had in the vanguard of their companions who were in this world, their boats will be advanced before their companions by a thousand thousand years and fifty thousand years. Their right flank behind them is at half the proximity of those to their companions, and their left flank is likewise. Their rearguard are those who were behind them in those boats of pearl. While they are thus traveling in that river, those waves will raise them to a throne before the Throne of the Lord of Might. While they are thus, the angels will appear to them, being multiplied in beauty, splendor, comeliness, and light over the servants of the people of Paradise, just as they are multiplied over the people of Paradise by their stations with Allah. One of them will be about to fall prostrate to some of their servants among the angels, but he will say: 'O friend of Allah, I am a servant to you. We are a hundred thousand stewards in the gardens of Eden, a hundred thousand stewards in the gardens of Firdaws, a hundred thousand stewards in the gardens of Bliss, a hundred thousand stewards in the gardens of Refuge, a hundred thousand stewards in the gardens of Eternity, a hundred thousand stewards in the gardens of the Permitted, and a hundred thousand stewards in the gardens of Peace. Each steward among them is at the gate of a city. In each city are a hundred thousand palaces, in each palace a hundred thousand houses of gold, silver, large pearls, rubies, chrysolite, pearls, and light. In them are his wives, his couches, and his servants. If the lowest of them were to host the jinn and mankind, and their like with them a thousand thousand times, the lowest palace among his palaces would be spacious enough for them, all they wish of hospitality, servants, fruits, produce, food, and drink. Each palace is sufficient with what it contains of these things for all their capacity, not needing the other palace in any of that. The lowest of them in station is the one who enters upon Allah morning and evening, and He commands all honor. He will not be occupied until he looks upon His beautiful face, Blessed and Exalted is He.\""],[2689,"The first blood shed from a martyr, all his sins are forgiven for him, except debt."],[2691,"Some people were in Kufa with Ibn al-Mukhtar (meaning the father of al-Mukhtar b. Abi 'Ubayd) when he was killed at the bridge of Abu 'Ubayd. He said: They were all killed except two men who charged the enemy with their swords, and they made way for them, so they escaped, or three. They came to Madinah, and 'Umar ؓ came out while they were sitting and mentioning them. 'Umar ؓ said: What did you say about them? They said: We sought forgiveness for them and prayed for them. He ؓ said: You must tell me what you said about them, or you will face severe consequences from me. They said: We said that they are martyrs. He said: By the One besides whom there is no god, and by the One who sent Muhammad with the truth, and by the One without whose permission the Hour will not come, no living soul knows what God has for a dead soul, except the Prophet of God, for God Almighty has forgiven him his past and future sins. By the One besides whom there is no god, and by the One who sent Muhammad with the truth, and by the One without whose permission the Hour will not come, a man fights for show, fights out of zeal, fights seeking this world, and fights seeking wealth. And those who fight will have nothing with God except that which is in their hearts."],[2693,"He said to me: O Hanan, begin with yourself and strive against it. O servant of God, begin with yourself and raid it; for if you are killed while fleeing, God will resurrect you as a fleer; if you are killed while showing off, God, Mighty and Majestic, will resurrect you as a show-off; and if you are killed patiently seeking reward, God, Blessed and Exalted, will resurrect you as patient and seeking reward."],[2694,"The combatants on the Day of Resurrection will only be resurrected according to their intentions."],[2696,"The Messenger of God ﷺ one day brought out a piece of a black khamisah, tied it to a spear, then shook it and said: Who will take it with its due right? The Muslims were afraid of it because of the condition. A man stood up to him and said: O Messenger of God, I will take it with its due right. He ﷺ said: Do not fight a Muslim with it, and do not flee with it from an unbeliever."],[2698,"Two men from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ were killed at the gate of Banu Salim. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered that they be buried where they were killed. So they were carried from where they were struck, and it happened to be a graveyard near Banu Hilal, so they were buried there."],[2700,"Whoever fights and remains patient until he is killed or prevails will be protected from the trial of the grave."],[2701,"A man came to the prayer while the Messenger of God ﷺ was praying. When he reached the row, he said: O God, give me the best of what You give Your righteous servants. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished, he said: Who spoke just now? The man said: I, O Messenger of God. He ﷺ said: Then your horse will be hamstrung and you will be martyred."],[2702,"Bilal ؓ gave the call to prayer during the life of the Messenger of God ﷺ, then gave the call for Abu Bakr ؓ during his life, and he did not give the call during the time of 'Umar ؓ. 'Umar ؓ said to him: What prevents you from giving the call? He said: I gave the call for the Messenger of God ﷺ until he passed away, and I gave the call for Abu Bakr ؓ until he passed away, because he was my patron. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: O Bilal, there is nothing better than your deed except jihad in the path of God. So he went out to Syria and fought."],[2703,"'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ sent out an army, among them Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ. When it departed, he saw Mu'adh ؓ and said: What held you back? He said: I wanted to pray the Friday prayer and then leave. 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: A morning or evening spent in the path of God Almighty is better than the world and all it contains."],[2704,"Standing for an hour in the path of God Almighty is better than witnessing the Night of Decree at the Black Stone."],[2705,"Whoever's head is cracked in the path of Allah, the Exalted, Allah forgives him his past sins."],[2706,"Abu Bakr ؓ sent Yazid b. Abi Sufyan to Sham, and he walked with them about two miles. It was said to him: 'O Caliph of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, would you turn back?' Abu Bakr ؓ said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever's feet become dusty in the path of Allah, the Exalted, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, forbids them to the Fire.'"],[2707,"Standing for an hour in the path of Allah is better than a man's worship of sixty hours."],[2708,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he had a crowd of people with him. A man came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is best in station with Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection after His prophets and His chosen ones?' He ﷺ said: 'The one who strives in the path of Allah, the Exalted, with his soul and his wealth until the call of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, comes to him while he is on the back of his horse, holding its reins.' He said: 'Then who?' He ﷺ said: 'A man in a remote area who worships his Lord well and leaves the people safe from his evil.'"],[2709,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us ... and he mentioned the hadith, in which [he said]: \"Whoever walks in arranging the marriage of a man lawfully until he brings them together, God Almighty will provide him with a thousand women from the houris of paradise, each woman in a palace of pearl and ruby, and for every step he takes or word he speaks in that matter he will have the worship of a year: standing in prayer its nights and fasting its days. And whoever walks in reconciling a woman and her husband will have the reward of a thousand martyrs truly slain in the path of God, and for every step he will have the worship of a year, its fasting and its standing in prayer.\""],[2710,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ urged us to jihad and said: 'The example of the mujahidun of my nation is like the example of Jibril and Mikail, and they are the messengers of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and His treasurers.'"],[2711,"Whoever says 'Allahu Akbar' once in the path of Allah, the Exalted, will have for it a rock in his scale on the Day of Resurrection heavier than the seven heavens and the seven earths and what is in them, what is between them, and what is beneath them. Whoever says in the path of Allah: 'There is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest' and raises his voice with it, Allah, the Exalted, writes for him His greatest pleasure. Whoever Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, writes for him His greatest pleasure, He will gather him with Ibrahim and Muhammad, may prayers and peace be upon them, in the Abode of Majesty. It was said: 'And what is the Abode of Majesty?' He said: 'The abode of Allah, the Exalted, by which He named Himself, where He will look at the Possessor of Majesty and Honor morning and evening. That has been forbidden to the killer of a believing soul, the one who disobeys his parents, and they are innocent of me and I am innocent of them.'"],[2712,"Yazid b. Shajara stood among his companions and said: 'It has come upon you morning and evening from among red, green, and yellow, and in the graves is what is in them. When you meet the enemy tomorrow, advance, advance! For I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A man does not advance a step but the houris of Paradise advance toward him. If he retreats, they retreat. If he is martyred, the first splash of blood is an expiation for his sins, and two houris descend to him, shake off the dust from him, and say: Welcome, your time has come. And he says: Welcome, your time has come.'"],[2713,"Make purchases on Allah's account and take loans on Allah's account. It was said: Who would take a loan on Allah's account, O Messenger of Allah? He ﷺ said: Your saying: 'Lend us until we get our livelihood, and sell to us until Allah opens for us.' You will continue to be in good as long as your jihad continues. And there will be in the last of time a people who doubt jihad, so wage jihad in their time and raid, for raiding on that day is better."],[2714,"Whoever goes out as a pilgrim and dies, the reward of a pilgrim will be written for him until the Day of Resurrection. And whoever goes out as a warrior in the path of Allah, Exalted is He, and dies, the reward of a warrior will be written for him until the Day of Resurrection. And whoever goes out for 'umrah and dies, the reward of one performing 'umrah will be written for him until the Day of Resurrection."],[2715,"An hour in the path of Allah, Exalted is He, is better than fifty Hajjs."],[2716,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day he addressed the people: There is none among the people like a man who takes hold of the head of his horse and wages jihad in the path of Allah, and avoids the evils of people, and like a man who is remote with his livestock, hosting his guest and giving its due right."],[2717,"Whoever is killed, it is an expiation for every sin except shirk (associating partners with Allah)."],[2718,"A morning or an evening spent in the path of Allah is better than the world and what it contains."],[2720,"The Prophet ﷺ was on a journey, and he missed a man from his companions. Then the man was brought to him, and he said: 'I wanted to be alone with the worship of my Lord, and to withdraw from people.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do not do that, and let none of you do it' - he ﷺ said it three times - 'for enduring an hour in some of the places of the Muslims is better than worship for forty years.'"],[2721,"Ribat (guarding the frontier) for a day in the path of Allah equals the worship of a month or a year, its fasting and its standing (in prayer). And whoever dies as a murabit (one stationed at the frontier) in the path of Allah, Exalted is He, Allah, Exalted is He, will protect him from the punishment of the grave, and will continue to record for him the reward of his ribat as long as the world lasts."],[2723,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us while we were at Khaybar: that we should not kill a child or a woman."],[2724,"A man came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and knelt on his knees, then praised Allah Almighty and repeated the praise three times. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'May Allah Almighty fight him! What a word Satan cast upon him! If I were to kill a delegate from among the Arabs, I would kill him.'"],[2725,"We did not kill the traders of the polytheists during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[2726,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched a military expedition, he would say: In the name of Allah, in the path of Allah, and upon the creed of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Do not pilfer, do not act treacherously, do not mutilate, and do not kill children."],[2728,"Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah Almighty has indeed fought, and whoever looks after a warrior's family in his absence with goodness has indeed fought."],[2730,"Whoever sees off warriors in the path of Allah Almighty until they alight at their first stop, and spends the night with them until they depart heading for jihad, and then returns to his family, he will have the reward of seventy pilgrimages with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, besides sharing with them in the good they were engaged in."],[2731,"It is as if he performed twenty-five pilgrimages."],[2732,"Abu Bakr ؓ dispatched Yazid b. Abi Sufyan to Syria, and he walked with them for about two miles. It was said to him, 'O Caliph of the Messenger of Allah, would you not turn back?' Abu Bakr ؓ said, 'No, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever's feet become dusty in the path of Allah Almighty, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will forbid them to the Fire.'"],[2734,"The banner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was black, and his standard was white."],[2735,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has honored my community with the banners."],[2737,"The Prophet ﷺ bade farewell to a man and said: May Allah provide you with piety, forgive your sin, and facilitate good for you wherever you are."],[2738,"He used to prefer, when he intended to travel, to set out on Thursday."],[2739,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he stopped at a place, would not depart from it until he bade it farewell with two rak'ahs."],[2740,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to be considerate among the people, and in one of those traveling groups there was a man whom his companions were praising. They said: \"O Messenger of God, when we stop he prays, and when we travel he recites.\" He ﷺ said: \"Then who takes care of feeding his camel?\" They said: \"We do.\" He ﷺ said: \"All of you are better than him.\""],[2741,"When a man wanted to accompany him on his journey, he would stipulate that he should not accompany us on an unlawful camel, nor dispute with us over the call to prayer, nor fast except with our permission. Nafi' said: There was a man who accompanied him on a journey, and he would order us to wake him and prepare his pre-dawn meal."],[2742,"Whoever serves twelve men in the path of God Most High, his sins depart from him as on the day his mother gave birth to him. And whoever gives water to a man in the path of God, Mighty and Majestic, he will come to the Prophet's ﷺ basin on the Day of Resurrection. He said: And when the Prophet ﷺ traveled, he would stipulate service upon the best of them; and whoever missed that, he would stipulate the call to prayer. He said: A group came to the Prophet ﷺ from an expedition, and he saw among them people whom worship had exhausted. He said: \"Who serves them?\" Some of them said: \"We do, O Messenger of God.\" He ﷺ said: \"You are better than them.\""],[2743,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: \"O Aktham b. al-Jawn, go on campaign with people other than your own tribe; your character will improve and you will be honored among your companions.\""],[2744,"The best of traveling companions are four."],[2745,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Zayd b. Harithah, or to 'Amr b. al-'As ؓ: \"When you dispatch a raiding party, do not corrupt them, and keep them in low ground; for God Most High grants victory to the people through their weakest.\""],[2746,"We went on a campaign with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he saw a place where there was congestion, and the people crowded and cut off the road. His caller announced: \"Whoever blocks a place or cuts off a road, there is no jihad for him.\""],[2748,"Three things are part of a person's happiness: a righteous wife, a good mount, and a spacious dwelling. And part of a person's misery is: a bad wife, a bad mount, and a cramped home."],[2749,"Three things are among the comforts of this world, even if it has no comfort: a smooth mount, a righteous wife, and a spacious dwelling."],[2752,"A woman should not travel more than three [days] except with a husband or a mahram."],[2754,"Honor the goats, wipe the mucus from them, and pray in their resting places, for they are among the animals of Paradise."],[2755,"Abu al-Darda' ؓ passed by a people who had made a camel kneel and loaded two sacks on it, then placed another on top of that, and the camel was unable to rise, so Abu al-Darda' ؓ removed that sack and helped it rise. Then Abu al-Darda' ؓ said: \"If Allah forgives you for what you do to the beasts, He will surely forgive a great deal. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Allah, Blessed and Exalted, enjoins you to treat these mute animals well: to let them alight at their resting places, and if a drought afflicts you, to leave their marrow.'\""],[2756,"Upon the back of every camel is a devil, so when you ride them, mention Allah, and let them be of service; for indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is the One who carries."],[2757,"Do not leave camels untethered; tie their udders, for the devil suckles them."],[2758,"When the land is fertile, dismount from your mounts and give them their due of pasture; and when the land is barren, travel quickly on them with their marrow."],[2759,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Farewell Hajj, and he took his wives with him. She said: \"My baggage was light, and it was on a swift camel, while the baggage of Safiyyah bt. Huyayy was heavy...\" (the rest of the hadith)."],[2761,"He was seen wiping the cheek of his horse, and he was asked about that, and he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Jibril ﷺ reproached me concerning the horse.'\""],[2762,"The Prophet ﷺ woke up while he was wiping the sweat of his horse, and he was asked about it, and he said: \"I was reproached tonight concerning horses.\""],[2763,"Whoever keeps a horse in the cause of Allah, Exalted be He, it will be his shield from the Fire."],[2764,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ wiping the face of his horse with his sleeve."],[2765,"A man came to him and said: \"Have you heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say anything about horses?\" He said: \"Yes, I heard him ﷺ say: 'Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[2766,"The horses have goodness tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection, and their owners are assisted because of them."],[2768,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted for the horse two shares and for its rider one share."],[2770,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned for him on the Day of Badr two shares for his horse and one share for himself."],[2771,"That he was present at Hunayn with the Prophet ﷺ, and he allotted for his horse two shares and for him one share."],[2772,"For the horse there is one share; the Arabian and the non-Arabian are equal."],[2773,"I asked Ikrimah ؓ about that, and he said: They are equal."],[2775,"They are equal in the two shares."],[2776,"That they were two horsemen on the Day of Hunayn, and they were given six shares: four for their two horses and two for themselves; then they sold the two shares for two young camels."],[2777,"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave on the Day of Badr the horse two shares and the man one share."],[2779,"He is not from us who shouts to urge horses on the day of racing, and he is not from us who incites a slave against his master, and he is not from us who corrupts a woman against her husband."],[2780,"The Prophet ﷺ scanned the people and saw a man with an Arabic bow in his hand, so he said: 'Keep to this and its like, and the lances of qana (a type of spear); for by means of this, Allah Most High will enable you to gain control in the lands and will support you in victory.'"],[2781,"The Prophet ﷺ held a race between horses and camels."],[2782,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by some people who were shooting arrows. He said: 'Take (i.e., shoot), and I am with Ibn al-Adra'.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, should we take (shoot) while you are with some of us and not others?' He ﷺ said: 'Take (shoot), and I am with all of you, O Banu Isma'il.'"],[2783,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by some people of Aslam who were competing in archery. He ﷺ said: 'Shoot, Banu Isma'il, for your father was an archer, and I am with Ibn al-Akwa'.' The people held back their hands, so he ﷺ said: 'What is the matter with you that you do not shoot?' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, should we shoot when you have said: \"I am with Ibn al-Akwa'\"? We know that your side cannot be defeated.' He ﷺ said: 'Shoot, and I am with all of you.'"],[2784,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Badr: 'Fight the people of disbelief, for whoever reaches (the enemy) with an arrow will have a degree.' It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, what is the degree?' He said: 'What is between the heaven and the earth.'"],[2785,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: 'Every Muslim has three (blessings): There is no man among the Muslims who shoots an arrow in the path of Allah Most High at the enemy, whether he hits or misses, but the reward of that arrow will be for him like the equivalent of a living soul (i.e., freeing a slave). And there is no man among the Muslims from whom a hair turns white in the path of Allah Most High but it will be for him a light that runs before him on the Day of Resurrection. And there is no man among the Muslims who frees a slave, young or old, but it becomes a right upon Allah Most High to reward him for every limb of that (slave) with multiple, multiplied (rewards).'"],[2786,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from shooting with a small pebble (mirmah) except a pebble that he can see."],[2787,"He (the Prophet's companion) used to see no harm in two men betting on a race, but he disliked that they should separate (disagree) over that."],[2788,"There is no harm in betting on horses when there is among them a horse that is not below the others; if it wins, it gets the prize, and if it does not win, nothing is due from it."],[2790,"I came to a gathering like the wind, and I passed by a small group of the Ansar with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the like of whom I had never seen before or after, wearing swords on their shoulders, nearly thirty in number. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I have indeed seen fear (i.e., something startling).'"],[2791,"Some people complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about walking (fatigue). He called them and said: 'You should adopt the nasalan (a swift, light gait).' So we walked with nasalan and found it lighter for us."],[2792,"The feet of a servant never become dusty in the path of Allah, the Exalted, except that Allah forbids the Fire upon him. I never saw more people walking than on that day, while we were behind the mountain pass."],[2794,"Leave your nails long in the land of the enemy, for they are a weapon."],[2796,"Umar b. Abd al-Aziz wrote: 'Any man from the people of the army register who makes a donkey mount an Arabian mare, deduct ten dinars from his stipend.'"],[2797,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a donkey called Ufayr."],[2799,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met the enemy, he would say: 'O Allah, You are my support and my helper; by You I move, and by You I assail, and by You I fight.'"],[2800,"Indeed, Allah, the Exalted, loves silence in three situations: during the recitation of the Qur'an, during the advance against the enemy, and during the funeral."],[2802,"The battle cry of the Prophet ﷺ was: 'O All Good!'"],[2804,"Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ sent him on an expedition, then said to a man: 'Catch up with him and do not startle him from behind, and say to him: The Prophet ﷺ commands you to wait for him, and say to him: Do not fight a people until you have invited them.'"],[2805,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent out a military expedition, he would say: 'Win the hearts of the people, and be patient with them, and do not raid them until you have invited them. There is no household on earth, whether of settled folk or of Bedouins, except that your bringing them to me as Muslims is more beloved to me than that you kill their men and bring me their women.'"],[2806,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out an expedition to al-Lat and al-Uzza, and they raided a tribe of the Arabs, capturing their fighters and their children. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, they raided us without inviting us.' So he asked the members of the raiding party, and they confirmed that. He said: 'Return them to their place of safety, then invite them.'"],[2808,"Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ wrote to Bakr b. Wa'il: 'From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, to Bakr b. Wa'il: Submit and you will be safe.' They said: 'We found no one to read it except a man from Banu Dubay'ah, so they were called Banu al-Katib.'"],[2811,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ advising some of his family, saying: 'And do not flee on the day of battle.'"],[2813,"I find for him in this world and the Hereafter nothing from his military expedition except these dinars that were given to him."],[2815,"Emigration remains as long as the polytheists are fought."],[2817,"There is no silence of a day until night, no continuous fasting in the fast, no adopting bedouin ways after the emigration, and no emigration after the conquest... the rest of the hadith."],[2819,"The Prophet ﷺ was on one of his military expeditions and passed by some people of Muzaynah. A slave belonging to a woman among them followed him. When he was on part of the road, he greeted him, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'So-and-so?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What is your matter?' He said: 'I want to fight alongside you.' He said: 'Did your mistress permit you?' He said: 'No.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Return to her and convey my greeting of peace to her.' So he returned to her and conveyed the greeting, and told her. She said: 'By Allah, did he command you to convey greeting to me?' He said: 'Yes.' She said: 'Return and fight alongside him.'"],[2821,"Umm Kabshah, a woman from 'Uraynah — 'Uraynah of Quda'ah — said: 'O Messenger of Allah, permit me to go out with such-and-such army?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'No.' She said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I do not intend to fight; I only intend to treat the wounded and the sick — or: to give water to the sick.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Were it not that it would become a sunnah, and that so-and-so went out, I would have permitted you, but sit down.'"],[2823,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah, Juhaynah came to him and said: 'You have settled among us, so make a pact with us so that we feel secure from you and you feel secure from us.' He made a pact with them, and they did not embrace Islam."],[2824,"The Prophet ﷺ made a treaty with Banu Taghlib on the condition that they remain on their religion, and not make their children Christians. They have broken the treaty, and if the matter is completed for me, I will kill their fighters and take their offspring captive."],[2827,"A blind Muslim man used to take refuge with a Jewish woman who treated him well, but she used to insult the Prophet ﷺ whenever she mentioned him. He forbade her, but she refused. So he killed her. The matter was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he questioned him. The man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, she was among the best people to me in treatment, but she used to insult you whenever she mentioned you. I forbade her, but she refused, so I killed her.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ declared her blood to be of no consequence."],[2828,"A monk was brought to Ibn 'Umar ؓ and it was said to him: 'This one insults the Prophet ﷺ.' He said: 'If I had heard him, I would have killed him. We did not grant them protection so that they could insult our Prophet ﷺ.'"],[2829,"He passed by a man who used to wear a different garment every day—or he said: a robe unlike the other—he would wear three hundred and sixty garments a year, and he had a treaty. He invited him to Islam, but he became angry and insulted the Prophet ﷺ, so Gharafa killed him. Amr b. al-As said to him: They only feel secure with us because of the treaty. He said: We did not make a treaty with them on condition that they harm us regarding Allah Almighty and His Messenger."],[2831,"No people ever break a covenant except that killing occurs among them, and immorality never appears among a people except that death is imposed upon them."],[2833,"A man from the people of the dhimma goaded the donkey of a Muslim woman, then seized her, but Awf b. Malik ؓ intervened between him and her, and struck him. He came to Umar ؓ and mentioned that to him. He summoned the woman and asked her, and she confirmed Awf ؓ. So he ordered that he be crucified. Then Umar ؓ said: O people, fear Allah regarding the protection of Muhammad ﷺ, so do not wrong them. Whoever among them does something like this, then there is no protection for him."],[2835,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on a military expedition and appointed Khalid b. al-Walid over the vanguard. He saw a slain woman and said: Who killed this one? They said: Khalid b. al-Walid killed her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man: Catch up with Khalid b. al-Walid and say to him: Do not kill a woman, or a child, or a hired servant."],[2836,"I forbade you from killing children and the elderly. A man said: May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, what is upon us from killing the children of the polytheists? He said: And what do you know of what they used to do?"],[2837,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a slain woman on the day of Khaybar and said: Who killed this one? A man said: I did, O Messenger of Allah; I had her ride behind me, and she wanted to kill me, so I pushed her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that she be buried."],[2839,"Religion is sincere advice. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He ﷺ said: To Allah's Book, His Prophet, and the leaders of the Muslims."],[2841,"A man from among them may give protection on behalf of the Muslims."],[2843,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was at al-Ji'rana, and I kept not passing by any group of the Ansar's cavalry except that they said: Away with you, away with you. When I reached him—meaning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—I raised the letter and said: It is I, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He ﷺ had written for me a guarantee of safety on a piece of paper—meaning when he migrated. He said: The Prophet ﷺ said: Yes, today is a day of loyalty, kindness, and truthfulness."],[2845,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mutilation."],[2846,"He forbade his armies from mutilating any of the disbelievers."],[2848,"A shaykh who was stationed at the coast told me: I went out on the night of my guard duty; no one else among those assigned to guard went out except me. I came to the structure and climbed upon it—the structure was the guard post. It appeared to me that the sea was rising until it was level with the mountaintops. This happened several times while I was awake. Then I slept and saw in a dream as though I had a banner, and the people of the city were walking behind me while I was in front of them. When morning came, I returned to the city and met the commander of the army and Abu Salih, the freedman of Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ. They were the first to leave the city. They said to me: 'Where are the people?' I said: 'They returned before me.' They said: 'Why don't you tell us the truth? We are the first to leave the city.' He said: So I informed them that no one had gone out except me. Abu Salih said: 'What did you see?' I said: 'By Allah, it appeared to me in what I saw that the sea was rising until it was level with the mountaintops.' Abu Salih said: 'You have spoken the truth. Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ narrated to us from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who said: \"There is no night except that the sea rises three times over the people of the earth, seeking permission from Allah Almighty to overwhelm them—meaning to flood—and Allah Almighty restrains it.\"' I said: 'I also saw in the dream as though I had the banner, and that the people of the city were walking with me while I was in front of them.' Abu Salih said: 'If your dream is true, you will surely attain the reward of this city tonight.' He said: Abu Salih had been keeping his distance from me before that, but then he seemed to trust me and began to talk to me. He said: 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ advised us that we should form a partnership of three: a man who sells on our behalf, a man who goes on military expeditions, and a man who brings us provisions. This is my turn, so I am now returning to the city.'"],[2849,"Two eyes the Fire will not touch: an eye that overflowed from fear of Allah, and an eye that spent the night guarding in the path of Allah."],[2850,"Two eyes the Fire will never touch: an eye that spent the night keeping watch over the Muslims in the path of Allah Almighty, and an eye that wept from fear of Allah Almighty."],[2851,"The Fire is forbidden to touch two eyes: an eye that wept from fear of Allah, and an eye that spent the night guarding Islam from the people of disbelief."],[2852,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Which people have the best standing with Allah?' He said: 'A man on the back of his horse, frightening the enemy and being frightened by them.'"],[2854,"Whoever the polytheists grant land to, he has no land."],[2856,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Khaybar: 'Eat and feed your animals, but do not carry away.'"],[2858,"Beware of misappropriating spoils of war: a man who has intercourse with a woman before the distribution, then returns her to the division; or who wears a garment until it becomes worn out, then returns it to the division."],[2860,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ, when he prayed a prayer, would sit for the people for whoever had a need. If no one had a need, he would rise and enter. He (the narrator) said: He prayed prayers in which he did not sit for the people. Ibn Abbas ؓ said: I came to the door and said: O Yarfa, is there a complaint from the Commander of the Believers? He said: There is no complaint from the Commander of the Believers. So I sat, and Uthman b. Affan ؓ came and sat. Yarfa came out and said: Rise, O Ibn Affan; rise, O Ibn Abbas. They entered upon Umar ؓ, and behold, before him were heaps of wealth, upon each heap a shoulder (of meat). Umar ؓ said: I looked into the people of Madinah and found you two among the most numerous of its people in kinsfolk. Take this wealth and divide it; whatever is surplus, return it. He said: As for Uthman ؓ, he scooped, but as for me, I knelt on my knees and said: And if there is a deficit, will you return to us? He said: A chip from a rough stone, meaning a stone from a mountain. Was this not with Allah when Muhammad ﷺ and his companions used to eat the leather? I said: Yes, by Allah, this was with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, while Muhammad ﷺ was alive; and if it had been opened to him, he would have done with it other than what you are doing. So Umar ؓ became angry and said..."],[2862,"Al-Abbas came to Umar ؓ and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted me al-Bahrayn as a fief. He said: Who testifies for you? He said: Al-Mughirah b. Shubah."],[2863,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to Qays b. Malik al-Arhabi: In Your name, O Allah. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Qays b. Malik: Peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah, His blessings, and His forgiveness. To proceed: I have appointed you over your people, their Arabs and non-Arabs, their clients, their common folk, and their outskirts. And I grant you as a fief from the grain of Yasar two hundred sa's, and from the raisins of Khaywan two hundred sa's, permitted for you and your descendants after you forever, forever, forever. Qays said: The saying of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"forever, forever, forever\" is dearer to me; indeed I hope that my descendants will remain forever."],[2864,"When Islam appeared, we had a well, and I feared that those around us would overpower us over it. So I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he wrote for me a document: From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah. To proceed: They shall have their well if he is truthful, and they shall have their home if he is truthful. He said: We never brought it to any of the judges of Madinah except that he ruled in our favor by it. He said: And in the document there was a misspelling: \"kana\" was written \"kawuna.\""],[2865,"Uyaynah b. Hisn and al-Aqra' b. Habis came to Abu Bakr ؓ and said: O Caliph of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we have a salt marsh land in which there is no pasture nor benefit. If you see fit to grant it to us as a fief? He said: So he granted it to the two of them and wrote for them a document for it."],[2866,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ appointed Hudhayfah ؓ as a judge. He wrote to Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman ؓ ten characteristics; I remembered six and forgot four: Do not grant as a fief except the wealth of Kisra or the people of his household, or one who was killed in battle, or the houses of the postal stations, or the place of prisons, and the drainage of water and the thickets."],[2868,"Whoever embraces Islam upon something, it is his."],[2869,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled concerning a slave: if he embraces Islam and then his master comes and embraces Islam, he (the master) is more entitled to him."],[2871,"The people of idols are fought for prayer, and the People of the Book are fought for the jizya."],[2872,"Umar ؓ stipulated upon the people of the dhimmah the hospitality of a day and a night, and that they should not neglect the bridges. If a man from the Muslims is killed in their land, then upon them is his blood money."],[2873,"Umar ؓ wrote to the amirs of the jizya not to impose the jizya upon women and children, and Umar ؓ used to seal the necks of the people of the jizya."],[2874,"The Messenger of God ﷺ wrote to the Magians of Hajar, offering them Islam: whoever accepted Islam, it would be accepted from him, and whoever refused, the jizya would be imposed upon him, on condition that no woman of theirs be married and no animal slaughtered by them be eaten."],[2875,"On what basis is the jizya taken from the Magians when they are not People of the Book? Al-Mustawrid ؓ stood up to him, seized him by the collar, and said: O enemy of God, do you criticize Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ? He took him to the palace, and Ali ؓ came out to them and said: Al-bada' — Sufyan said: he means, 'Sit down.' So they sat in the shade of the palace. He told him what he had said, and Ali ؓ said: I am the most knowledgeable of people about the Magians. They had knowledge which they taught and a book which they studied. Their king became drunk one day and fell upon his daughter or his sister. Some of the people of his kingdom observed him, and when he sobered up they came to impose the prescribed punishment on him, but he refused them and summoned the people of his kingdom and said: Do you know of a religion better than the religion of Adam? He used to marry his sons to his daughters, and I am upon the religion of Adam, so what would make you averse to his religion? So they pledged allegiance to him and fought those who opposed them until they were killed. When morning came, their book had been taken up by night and removed from among them, and the knowledge that was in their breasts was gone. Thus they are People of the Book, and the Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar ؓ took the jizya from them."],[2877,"By the One besides whom there is no god, God Almighty divided this fay' through the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ before Persia and Rome were conquered."],[2878,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was passing through Wadi al-Qura and said: O Muhammad, to what do you call us? He said: To God alone. He said: Then this wealth, is anyone more entitled to it than another? He said: One fifth is for God Almighty, and four fifths are for these, and even if you take an arrow from your pocket, you are no more entitled to it than your brother. He said: Then who are these—meaning those upon whom is wrath? He said: The Jews. He said: And who are these—meaning those who are astray? He said ﷺ: The Christians."],[2879,"Fatimah ؓ came to Abu Bakr ؓ to ask him for the share of the near of kin, and Abu Bakr ؓ said to her: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: The share of the near of kin is for them during my lifetime, but they have none after my death."],[2881,"Some people want to make me renounce my religion, and by God, I hope never to cease upon it until I die. There is nothing sold for gold or silver but that in it is the fifth of God and the shares of the Muslims."],[2883,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ came to Madinah, he sent us out and commanded us to raid a tribe of Kinanah. The fay' at that time was: whoever took something, it was his."],[2885,"I witnessed Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ at al-Jabiyah. He praised God and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: To proceed: God has granted you this fay', in which the high and the low are equal; no one is more entitled to it than another, except for these two tribes: Lakhm and Judham, for I am not distributing anything to them. A man from Lakhm stood up and said: O son of al-Khattab, I adjure you by God regarding justice. He said: The son of al-Khattab only wants justice and equality. By God, I know that if the migration had been to San'a', only a few from Lakhm and Judham would have gone out to it. I will not make those who endured the journey and purchased mounts equal to a people who only fought in their own lands. Abu Hudayrij stood up and said: O Commander of the Faithful, if God Almighty brought the migration to us in our own lands, and we supported it and believed in it, does that remove our right in Islam? Umar ؓ said: By God, I will distribute it three times. Then he distributed among the people, and each man received half a dinar. If his wife was with him, he gave him a dinar, and if his grandfather was with him, he gave him half a dinar."],[2887,"I was with some camels of mine that I was tending in the pre-Islamic era, and the cavalry of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or the cavalry of his companions, raided them. I gathered my camels and mounted the stallion, and it spread its forelegs and sped away. I dismounted from it and mounted a she-camel of theirs, and I escaped on it while they drove the camels away. I then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he returned them to me, as he had not yet divided them."],[2888,"A slave woman fled and joined the enemy, and the Muslims took her as booty. The Muradis recognized her, so they came to Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah ؓ and said: 'Our slave woman fled from us.' He said: 'I have no knowledge about this matter, but I will write to the Commander of the Faithful, so wait for his letter.' The Muradis remained silent for a while, then he said: 'Umar's ؓ letter has come to me regarding your slave woman: if she has been divided into fifths and distributed, then that is the proper course; otherwise, return her to her owners.' They asked: 'By Allah, did Umar really write that?' He replied: 'By Allah, it is not lawful for me to lie.'"],[2890,"The Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr ؓ used to take one-fifth of the salab."],[2892,"Extra spoils granted as reward are a right; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted extra spoils."],[2894,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and accepted Islam on the condition that he would pray two prayers, and he accepted that from him."],[2895,"A casket was brought to Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ, and his companions looked at it but did not recognize its value. He said: 'Do you permit me to send it to A'ishah ؓ because of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ love for her?' They said: 'Yes.' So it was brought to A'ishah ؓ, and she opened it. It was said: 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ sent this to you.' She ؓ said: 'What has Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ opened for me after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? O Allah, do not keep me alive for a future gift.'"],[2897,"The Muhajirun obtained a leather tent after Hunayn, or on the day of Hunayn. The Muhajirun said: 'O Prophet of Allah, we are happy to give it to you, so take it to shade yourself, and some of us will shade ourselves with you.' He ﷺ said: 'Would you like your Prophet to be in a tent of fire?'"],[2899,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from one of his expeditions having captured some slaves. She and her sister went until they entered upon Fatimah ؓ, so they went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and she asked him to speak to them, and they complained to him of their need. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The orphans of the people of Badr have preceded you.'"],[2901,"If my Ummah does not misappropriate spoils, no enemy will ever approach them. Abu Dharr said to Habib b. Maslamah: \"Did the enemy ever stand firm against you for even the milking of a sheep?\" He said: \"Yes, and for three tough sheep.\" Abu Dharr ؓ said: \"You have misappropriated, by the Lord of the Ka'bah.\""],[2902,"Nothing from the spoils of the Muslims is lawful for anyone, whether little or much—not a thread or a needle—for a taker or a giver, except by right."],[2903,"I am holding you by your belts away from the Fire. Come away from the Fire! But you overcome me and plunge into it like moths and locusts. I am about to let go of your belts, and I will meet you at the Cistern. You will come to me together and in scattered groups, and I will recognize you by your marks and your names, just as a man recognizes a stray camel among his camels. But you will be taken away to the left. I appeal to the Lord of the Worlds concerning you, saying: 'O Lord, my people! O Lord, my Ummah!' He will say: 'O Muhammad, you do not know what they innovated after you; they kept walking backwards on their heels after you left.' Let me not find any of you on the Day of Resurrection carrying a bleating sheep and calling, 'O Muhammad, O Muhammad!' for I will say, 'I cannot avail you anything; I conveyed to you.' Let me not find any of you on the Day of Resurrection carrying a neighing horse and calling, 'O Muhammad, O Muhammad!' for I will say, 'I cannot avail you anything; I conveyed to you.' And let me not find any of you on the Day of Resurrection carrying a leather water-skin and calling, 'O Muhammad, O Muhammad!' for I will say, 'I cannot avail you anything; I conveyed to you.'"],[2905,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of Khaybar that shares be sold until they are divided."],[2907,"We came to Umar ؓ while he was in his tent, and I called out: \"I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so, al-Jarmi. A nephew of ours is a captive among the captives of so-and-so, and I presented to them the ruling of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We used to say that the ruling is four.\""],[2908,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ ruled regarding captives taken among the Arabs that the ransom is four hundred."],[2909,"There is no ownership over an Arab, and we will not take from a man's hand a captive who has embraced Islam under him; but we will value him at five camels."],[2910,"Umar ؓ said to me when he was stabbed: \"Know that every captive among the believers in the hands of the polytheists—his ransom is from the treasury of the Muslims.\""],[2911,"We raided with Salman b. Rabi'ah to Balanjar and besieged its people. While we were doing so, Salman was struck by a stone that hit his head. He said: \"If I die, bury me at the base of this city wall.\" He died, so we buried him where he said. We besieged its people and conquered the city, taking many captives and much wealth. One of our men got a thousand dirhams or more. When we set out to return, we reached a place called al-Sadd, and we could not pass through it until we went inland via the sea. We came out at Muqan, Jilan, and al-Daylam. We did not pass by any people except that they asked us for peace and gave us hostages, until the people despaired of us here—meaning in Kufah—and wept for us, and poets composed verses about us. Abdullah b. Salam ؓ bought a Jewish woman for seven hundred dirhams. When he passed by the Exilarch, he stopped at his place. Abdullah said: \"O Exilarch, would you like an old woman from your people? Buy her from me.\" He said: \"Yes.\" Abdullah said: \"I took her for seven hundred dirhams.\" He said: \"You may have a profit of seven hundred dirhams.\" He (Abdullah) said: \"I said: No.\" The Exilarch said: \"Then I have no need of her.\" I said: \"By Allah, you will take her for what she cost, or you will disbelieve in the religion you follow.\" He said: \"By Allah, I will never buy her from you for anything.\" Abdullah b. Salam ؓ said to him: \"Come close.\" He came close, and Abdullah recited to him what is in the Torah: \"You will not find a slave from the Children of Israel except that you buy him for what he cost and set him free.\" And: \"If they come to you as captives, you ransom them, though expelling them is forbidden to you. Do you believe in part of the Book and disbelieve in part?\"—the verse. He said: \"By Allah, I will buy her from you for what she cost.\" Abdullah said: \"I swear not to reduce her below four thousand dirhams.\" He brought him four thousand dirhams, and Abdullah returned two thousand dirhams to him and took two thousand."],[2913,"Ali ؓ was brought people from the Zutt. He said: \"I think he killed them.\" Then he looked at the sky, then at the earth, and said: \"Allahu Akbar, Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. Dig this spot—no, this spot.\" Then he looked at the sky, then at the earth, and said: \"Allahu Akbar, Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. Dig this spot.\" They dug, and he threw them into it. Then he entered, and I entered upon him and said: \"What do you think about what you were doing just now? Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ give any instruction concerning them?\" He said: \"To fall from the sky to the earth would be dearer to me than to say about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what he did not say. I am only employing a stratagem. Do you think that if I said 'Allahu Akbar, Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth, dig this spot,' what would it be?\""],[2914,"We entered upon al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"War is deception.\""],[2915,"War is deception."],[2917,"It was said to ‘Ali ؓ: Will you not appoint a successor? He said: No, but I will leave you to what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left you to."],[2918,"Then ‘Umar ؓ lay down in one of the gardens of Madinah... Then he mentioned a story, and ‘Umar ؓ said: Whom will you appoint as successor after me? A man from the people said to him: Al-Zubayr b. al-‘Awwam ؓ. He said: Then you will appoint as successor a stingy, ill-tempered man—meaning bad in character. Another man said: We will appoint Talhah b. ‘Ubayd Allah ؓ. He said: How can you appoint as successor a man whose first possession, which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him, was land that he gave as a dowry to a Jewish woman? A man from the people said: We will appoint ‘Ali ؓ. He said: By my life, you will not appoint him. By Him in whose hand is my soul, if you appointed him, he would establish you upon the truth even if you disliked it. He said: Then al-Walid b. ‘Uqbah ؓ said: We know the caliph after you. He sat up and said: Who? He said: ‘Uthman b. ‘Affan ؓ—and al-Walid was ‘Uthman's half-brother through his mother. He said: But what about ‘Uthman's ؓ love of wealth and his kindness to his family?"],[2919,"Abu ‘Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah and Mu‘adh b. Jabal ؓ were whispering to one another about something. I said to them: Have you not kept in mind the testament of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? They began reminding one another of it, and they said: The beginning of this nation is prophethood and mercy, then there will be a caliphate and mercy, then there will be a biting kingship, then there will be arrogance, tyranny, and corruption in the nation. They will consider wine and private parts lawful, and there will be corruption in the nation—they will be given victory and provision for that until they meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[2920,"A man came to ‘Abd Allah b. Mas‘ud ؓ and said: Has your Prophet told you how many caliphs there will be after him? He said: Yes, and no one has asked me about it before you, even though you are among the youngest of the people. He said: They will be the number of the chiefs of Musa—twelve chiefs."],[2921,"The first to greet him with the title of command in Kufah was Mughirah b. Shu‘bah ؓ, and he disliked it, then he accepted it."],[2923,"During the expedition of Dhat al-Salasil, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an army and appointed ‘Amr b. al-‘As ؓ over them, and Abu Bakr ؓ was among them. It was the expedition of which the people of Syria boast, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed ‘Amr b. al-‘As ؓ over an army that included Abu Bakr ؓ, and he ordered them to call to arms any Muslims they passed by. They passed by us at our home and called us to arms, so we went out with them. I said: I will choose for myself a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ to serve and learn from, for I cannot come to Madinah whenever I wish. So I chose Abu Bakr ؓ and accompanied him. He had a Fadak cloak that we would drape over him when he rode, and we would all wear it when we dismounted—the same cloak for which Hawazin reproached him, saying: This one with the large cloak—we are to follow him after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? When we finished our expedition and returned, I had not asked him about anything. I said to him: I have accompanied you, and I have a right upon you, yet I have not asked you about anything. Teach me what will benefit me, for I cannot come to Madinah every week. He ؓ said: That was already on my mind before you mentioned it. Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the obligatory prayer, give the prescribed zakat, perform pilgrimage to the House, fast Ramadan, and never take command over two men. I said: As for prayer and zakat, I know them. As for command, people only attain good through command. He said: You have pressed me, and I have exerted myself for you. People entered Islam willingly and unwillingly, and Allah gave them refuge from oppression. They are Allah's refugees, Allah's neighbors, and under Allah's protection. Whoever wrongs any of them breaks his covenant with his Lord. By Allah, if one of you loses a sheep or camel belonging to his neighbor, he remains angry for his neighbor's sake for the rest of his life, and Allah is behind his neighbor. When we returned to our homes, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, and the people pledged allegiance to Abu Bakr ؓ, and Abu Bakr ؓ was appointed as successor. I said: Who was appointed successor after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? They said: Your companion, Abu Bakr. So I came to Madinah and kept seeking him out until I found him alone. I took his hand and said: Do you not recognize me? I am your companion. He said: Yes. I said: Do you not remember what you told me: Never take command over two men—yet you have taken command over the people? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while the people were still new to leaving the days of ignorance, and my companions placed this burden on me, and I feared they would apostatize. By Allah, he kept apologizing until I excused him. Jarir added in it: He said: In the days of ignorance I used to drive sheep, and the matter kept progressing with me until I became an ‘arif during the governorship of al-Hajjaj."],[2924,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad ؓ on an expedition. When he returned, he said: \"How did you find your expedition?\" He said: \"I kept going until I thought that those with me were my servants. By God, I will never take charge of two men as long as I live.\""],[2925,"He wanted to appoint a man from among the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, but the man disliked that. Umar ؓ became angry and said: \"This matter in which we are engaged must have helpers.\" When the man saw that, he relented and said: \"I will go to my family and instruct them, then I will return.\" He said: \"Yes.\" So he left him, and his paternal uncle met him and said: \"I urge you not to do it.\" He said: \"What about his command?\" He said: \"You return and I return with you; when he sees you, he will say to you: 'Have you not returned?' Say: 'O Commander of the Faithful, I ask you to excuse me.'\" So he did that, and he said: \"Who forbade you?\" He said: \"So-and-so\"—meaning his uncle. He said: \"Indeed I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say\"—and he had wanted to appoint a man over some affair of the Muslims, but the man said: \"O Messenger of God, I ask you to excuse me.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I choose for you to sit, for no man is ever put in charge of ten without coming to God Almighty in fetters on the Day of Resurrection, until his deeds are what release him.\" Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ was reclining, so he sat up straight and began calling out: \"What deed will release him?\" He repeated this several times."],[2926,"Umar ؓ wrote to him about his covenant, but he said: \"I have no need of it. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The governors will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and made to stand on the bridge of Hell. Whoever was obedient to God, God will take him by His right hand and save him. Whoever was disobedient to God, the bridge will collapse with him into a valley of fire, blazing fiercely.'\" He said: \"So Umar ؓ sent for Abu Dharr and Salman ؓ and said to Abu Dharr ؓ: 'Did you hear this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes, by God, and after the valley there is another valley of fire.'\" He said: \"He asked Salman ؓ, but he disliked telling him anything. Umar ؓ said: 'Who will take it with all its consequences?' Abu Dharr ؓ said: 'One whose eye God has plucked out, whose nose He has cut off, and whose cheek He has cleft to the ground.'\""],[2927,"He appointed Sa'd b. 'Ubadah, and he came to the Prophet ﷺ to greet him. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Beware, O Sa'd, lest you come on the Day of Resurrection carrying on your neck a camel with a loud bray.\" He said: \"O Messenger of God, if I do that, will that happen?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"You know, O Prophet of God, that I am asked and I give, so excuse me.\" So he excused him."],[2929,"Musaylima wrote to the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"From Musaylima b. Habib to Muhammad, the Messenger of God ﷺ. Peace be upon you. Now then, Quraysh have half the earth and we have half the earth, but Quraysh are a people who transgress.\" And the two men bore witness that Muhammad ﷺ is the Messenger of God. They said: \"Musaylima does not deny that, except that he has been made a partner with you in the affair, and a prophethood has been brought to him alongside your prophethood.\""],[2930,"Mu'awiya stood on the pulpit and said: \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'People are followers of Quraysh in this matter, their best in the pre-Islamic era are their best in Islam if they gain understanding. Were it not that Quraysh would become arrogant, I would have told them what they have with God.'\""],[2931,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ and he said: \"O assembly of Quraysh, you are the governors after me of this affair... do not die except as Muslims, and hold fast to the rope of God all together\" to the end of the verse, \"and preserve me in the Ansar and their children and their children's children.\""],[2932,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ and he said: \"The ally of a people is one of them, and the son of a people's sister is one of them.\""],[2933,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed the people one day and said: \"Verily, the rulers are from Quraysh. Verily, the rulers are from Quraysh, as long as they uphold three things: when they judge, they are just; when they make a covenant, they fulfill it; and when they are asked for mercy, they show mercy. Whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people.\""],[2934,"The year of famine pressed hard upon us, [affecting] Nabighah b. Ja'dah, while we were with Ibn al-Zubayr ؓ in Makkah. He stood after leading the people in the morning prayer in the Sacred Mosque and said: \"You have imitated for us al-Siddiq when you governed us, and Uthman and al-Faruq, so the destitute rejoiced. Abu Layla came to you, cleaving through the darkness, the darkness of night, a traverser of the desert, sturdy. So that you might raise a side that the vicissitudes of nights and the calamitous time have shattered.\" Ibn al-Zubayr ؓ said to him: \"Restrain yourself, Abu Layla, for poetry is the least of your means to us. As for the choice of our wealth, it belongs to the family of al-Zubayr. As for its surplus, the Banu Asad keep us preoccupied from you. But you have two rights in the wealth of God: a right due to your seeing the Messenger of God ﷺ, and a right due to your partnership with the people of Islam.\" He ordered that mounts be loaded for him with grain and dates. Abu Layla began to hasten and eat from the dates and grain, while Ibn al-Zubayr ؓ said to him: \"Hardship has taken its toll on you, Abu Layla.\" When he had satisfied his appetite, he said: \"I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Quraysh have not governed but they have been just; have not been asked for mercy but they have shown mercy; have not spoken but they have spoken truth; and have not promised good but they have fulfilled it. So I and the prophets will be at the forefront of the Hawd for those who are driven away.'\""],[2936,"I came to Madinah after Abu Bakr ؓ had died and Umar ؓ had been appointed as his successor. I said to Umar: \"Raise your hand so that I may pledge allegiance to you upon what I pledged allegiance to your companion before you: upon hearing and obedience as much as I am able.\""],[2937,"I witnessed Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ while he was accepting the pledge of allegiance from the people after the death of the Messenger of God ﷺ. A group would gather around him and he would say to them: \"Pledge allegiance to me upon hearing and obedience to God and His Book, then to the commander.\" I clung to my whip, and I was at that time a boy who had reached puberty or around that. When those with him had dispersed, I came to him and said: \"I pledge allegiance to you upon hearing and obedience to God and His Book, and to the commander.\" He said: \"He looked me up and down.\""],[2938,"The Messenger of God ﷺ called the believing women to the pledge of allegiance. Asma' said: \"O Messenger of God, will you not uncover your hand for us?\" He said: \"I do not shake hands with women.\""],[2939,"I came to Umar ؓ and pledged allegiance to him while I was a boy, upon the Book of God and the Sunnah of His Prophet, that it is for us and upon us. He laughed and accepted my allegiance."],[2940,"Hind bt. Utbah b. Rabi'ah ؓ came to the Messenger of God ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him. He said: \"Go and change your hand.\" She said: \"So she went and changed it with henna, then came to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: 'I accept your allegiance upon that you do not associate anything with God, do not steal, and do not commit adultery.' She said: 'Does a free woman commit adultery?' He said: 'And do not kill your children for fear of poverty.' She said: 'Have you left us any children to kill?' She said: 'So she pledged allegiance to him.' Then she said to him, while wearing two gold bracelets: 'What do you say about these two bracelets?' He ﷺ said: 'Two embers from the embers of Hell.'\""],[2942,"God, Blessed and Exalted, supports Islam with men who are not from its people."],[2943,"God, Mighty and Majestic, indeed supports this religion with the wicked man."],[2945,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent out a military expedition and had them recite. An old man recited, then a young man recited, so he appointed the young man. The old man said: \"You appointed him over me, while I am older than him in age?\" He ﷺ said: \"He has more Qur'an than you.\""],[2946,"I went out with Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ to Makkah. The governor of Makkah, Nafi' b. 'Alqamah—who was named after an uncle of his—met us. He asked: \"Whom have you appointed as your successor over the people of Makkah?\" He said: \"Abd al-Rahman b. Abza.\" He said: \"You chose a man from the clients and appointed him over the Quraysh and the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ who are there?\" He said: \"Yes, I found him to be the best reciter of the Book of God among them, and Makkah is a land that is frequently visited, so I wanted them to hear the Book of God, Mighty and Majestic, from a man with excellent recitation.\" He said: \"What a good opinion you have. Abd al-Rahman b. Abza is among those whom God raises through the Qur'an.\""],[2948,"He was standing over the head of the Messenger of God ﷺ while ʿUrwa b. Masʿūd was speaking to him. Al-Mughīra said to him, 'You will surely restrain your hand, or it will not return to you,' and al-Mughīra was girded with a sword. ʿUrwa said, 'Who is this?' He said, 'This is your nephew al-Mughīra.' He said, 'O treacherous one, I have not yet washed my head of your treachery.'"],[2949,"Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq ؓ gave a sermon and said: 'By God, I am not the best of you. I was averse to this position of mine, and I wished there were among you someone who could suffice me. Do you think that I would act among you according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of God ﷺ? If so, I would not be able to establish it. The Messenger of God ﷺ was protected by revelation, and an angel was with him. But I have a devil that comes upon me. So when I become angry, avoid me, lest I affect your hair and your skin. Indeed, tend to me: if I am upright, help me; if I deviate, correct me.' Al-Ḥasan said: 'A sermon, by God, none after him gave the like of it.'"],[2951,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ used to command his governors, and they would meet him at the pilgrimage season. He would say: 'O people, I have not appointed your governors—or he said: my governors—to take from your skins, your wealth, or your honor. I appointed them over you only to restrain among you and to distribute among you. So whoever has suffered an injustice at the hands of any of them, let him stand up.' On that day none stood except one man, who said: 'O Commander of the Faithful, your governor struck me a hundred lashes.' He said: 'Stand and take retaliation from him.' ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ ؓ said: 'O Commander of the Faithful, if you open this door against your governors, it will become a precedent followed after you.' He said: 'Shall I not exact retaliation from him, when I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ exact retaliation from himself?' ʿAmr said: 'Let us appease him.' He said: 'Then appease him.' So they ransomed him for two hundred dinars, two dinars for each lash."],[2952,"ʿUmar ؓ gave us a sermon and said: 'O people, we used to recognize you when the Messenger of God ﷺ was among us...' and he mentioned the ḥadīth. In it: 'I do not send my governors to strike your skins.' He mentioned it. ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ ؓ leapt up and said: 'O Commander of the Faithful, consider: if a Muslim man were in charge of a flock and disciplined some of his flock, would you exact retaliation from him?' He said: 'Yes, by the One in whose hand is ʿUmar's soul. How could I not exact retaliation from him, when I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ exact retaliation from himself? Indeed, do not strike the Muslims and humiliate them; do not withhold their rights and lead them to disbelief; do not confine them and tempt them; and do not send them into the thickets and cause them to perish.'"],[2954,"Take compensation for what I have done and go.' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Will you grant it to me?' He said: 'I will not do that.' He ﷺ said: 'What do you want then?' He said: 'I want to exact retaliation from you, O Prophet of God.' He ﷺ said: 'Yes.' The man said: 'Come out from among these people.' So he came out from among them and gave the man the palm branch to exact retaliation from him ﷺ. He uncovered his belly, and ʿUmar ؓ came to hold the Prophet ﷺ from behind. He said: 'You stumbled with your sandal and your teeth broke.' When the man drew near to strike the Prophet ﷺ, he threw down the palm branch, kissed his navel, and said: 'O Prophet of God, this is what I wanted, so that the tyrants after you might be subdued.' ʿUmar ؓ said: 'You are more reliable in deed than I.' Thus in the Dār al-ʿĀṣima edition and in the sources of extraction in Abū Yaʿlā (Abū Hirm). Al-Ḥāfiẓ in Taʿjīl al-Manfaʿa said about Abū Hirm: 'Thus it is in the original, and al-Ḥusaynī wrote it in his own hand, and those who followed him, without a zāy, and that is what is in the History of Ibn ʿAsākir in the handwriting of the author's son. Ibn ʿAsākir affirmed that he is Abū Hurayra al-Ḥimṣī, and he pointed out in the biography of Ṣadaqa that the correct is Abū Hurayra, and that whoever said Abū Hirm erred, and that he is unknown. God knows best.'"],[2956,"It reached ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ that Saʿd had installed a door, then said: 'The sound has ceased.' He sent for Muḥammad b. Maslama ؓ, who came to him. He said: 'Go to Saʿd, burn his door, then take him by the hand and bring him out to the people and say: Sit here for the people.' He said: Muḥammad sent his servant in his place to his house, instructing him to bring him two riding camels and provisions from his family. Then he set out walking toward Kufa until he reached the cemetery of Kufa. He saw a Nabataean entering Kufa with reeds on a donkey, selling them. He bought them from him and stipulated that he should deposit them at the door of the amir. He came and deposited his reeds at the door of the amir, lit his fire stick, and Saʿd came. It was said: 'There is a tall, imposing black man here, wearing a lower garment and an upper garment, with a dark-red silk turban without a cap.' He said: 'That is Muḥammad b. Maslama; let him accomplish his task, let no one interfere with him.' He burned the door until it became charcoal. Then Saʿd came out to him and asked him, swearing by God that he had not uttered the word that had reached the Commander of the Faithful, and that a liar had conveyed it to him. He said: Then he offered him lodging, but he refused and returned the way he came. He said: Saʿd sent his provisions after him, but he returned them with his messenger, saying: 'Take your food back to your companion, for he has a family, and we have surplus provisions.' He said: They traveled and ran out of food for some days. The first human being they encountered was a woman with sheep. Muḥammad b. Maslama stood to pray, and the servant went and bargained with the sheep's owner for a small sheep, paying with a headband he had. He said: He threw it down to slaughter it, while Muḥammad was standing praying. He gestured to him not to slaughter it. When he finished, he said: 'What is this sheep? If there is an owner among the flock, bargain with him or hand over the sale of the slave woman and bring it; but if she is merely a shepherdess, return it, for hunger is better than eating from an unlawful source.' He said: Then he traveled until he came to ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ and told him what had happened and what Saʿd had sent after him, and that he had returned it with his messenger. ʿUmar ؓ said: 'What prevented you from accepting it from him?'"],[2959,"ʿUyayna b. Ḥiṣn and al-Aqraʿ b. Ḥābis ؓ came to Abū Bakr ؓ and said: 'O successor of the Messenger of God, we have salty land with no pasture and no benefit. If you see fit to grant it to us?' He said: He granted it to them and wrote them a document, and he had ʿUmar ؓ witness it, though he was not among the people. They went to ʿUmar ؓ to have him witness it. When ʿUmar ؓ heard what was in the document, he took it from their hands, spat on it, and erased it. They became angry and spoke harshly to him. He said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ used to win hearts, but Islam then was small.'"],[2961,"When Abu Bakr ؓ was appointed as caliph, he sat in his house sorrowful. Umar ؓ entered upon him and began to reproach him, saying: \"You have burdened me with this matter,\" and he complained to him about judging between the people. Umar ؓ said to him: \"Do you not know that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'If a governor exercises ijtihad and reaches the truth, he gets two rewards; and if he exercises ijtihad and errs from the truth, he gets one reward'?\" It was as if Umar's ؓ hadith made it easy for Abu Bakr."],[2962,"Two litigants came disputing to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Amr, judge between them.\" I said: \"O Prophet of God, you are more entitled to that.\" He ﷺ said: \"Even so.\" I said: \"On what basis shall I judge?\" He said: \"If you judge correctly between them, you get ten good deeds; and if you exercise ijtihad and err, you get one good deed.\""],[2963,"Rewards in place of good deeds."],[2965,"He came as a delegate to Umar ؓ, and his appearance and manner pleased Umar. Umar ؓ complained of coarse food he had eaten, so al-Rabi said: \"O Commander of the Faithful, you are the most deserving of people of soft food, soft clothing, and a comfortable mount.\" He struck his head with a palm branch and said: \"By God, you only intended by this to flatter me. I had thought there was good in you. Shall I not tell you a parable of me and these people? It is like a people who traveled and entrusted their provisions to one of them, saying: 'Spend it on us.' Is he allowed to take anything exclusively for himself over them?\" Al-Rabi said: \"No.\" He said: \"This is the parable of me and them.\" Then Umar ؓ said: \"I do not appoint my governors to insult your honors.\""],[2966,"A man entered upon me at noon. I said: \"What is your need, O servant of God?\" He said: \"I and a companion of mine were searching for some camels of ours. My companion went on searching, and I entered the shade to seek shelter and drink from the drink.\" She said: \"I got up to some sour milk of ours—or perhaps she said: to some sour mixed drink—and gave him to drink from it. I examined him and said: 'O servant of God, who are you?' He said: 'Abu Bakr.' I said: 'Abu Bakr, the companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ whom I have heard of?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: \"Then I remembered our raiding Khath'am in the pre-Islamic era, and our fighting one another, and what God Almighty brought of harmony and the ropes of the tents—like this, he interlocked his fingers. I said: 'O servant of God, how long will this affair of the people be?' He said: 'As long as the leaders remain upright.' She said: I said: 'And what are the leaders?' He said: 'Have you not seen the chief who is in the encampment, whom they follow and obey? They are those as long as they remain upright.'\""],[2967,"He sent to Umar some khabis (a sweet dish) that was well made, and they made it in baskets covered with felt. When it reached Umar ؓ, he uncovered the load from the khabis and said: \"Will the Muslims be satiated in their saddles from this?\" The messenger said: \"No.\" Umar ؓ said: \"I do not want it.\" And he wrote to Utbah ؓ: \"To proceed: It is not from your labor nor from your mother's labor. So satiate those with you of the Muslims in their saddles from what you are satiated with in your saddle.\""],[2968,"There was a man who used to associate with the Prophet ﷺ in the pre-Islamic era, called 'Iyad. He gave him a gift, and the Prophet said: \"Have you embraced Islam?\" He said: No. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The froth of the polytheists is not lawful for us,\" meaning their gifts."],[2969,"'Ali ؓ used to sweep the treasury, then pray in it. Two men would testify that he never withheld its wealth from the Muslims."],[2971,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to mark the protected pasture of Madinah: at the peaks of Dhat al-Jaysh, [and] at the landmarks of al-Masnu'ah, and at the peaks of Makhid, and at the peaks of Qanat."],[2973,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us, and he mentioned the hadith, in which is: \"Whoever wrongs a woman by withholding her dowry, then he is, in the sight of Allah, the Exalted, an adulterer. And Allah, the Exalted, will say to him on the Day of Resurrection: 'My servant, I gave you in marriage upon My covenant, yet you did not honor My covenant?' Then Allah, the Exalted, will take charge of seeking her right, and He will exhaust all his good deeds, and whatever remains of them, it will be commanded that he be taken to the Fire. And whoever has two wives and does not treat them justly in the division of his self and his wealth, he will come on the Day of Resurrection fettered, with his side leaning, until he enters the Fire.\""],[2974,"No one should stand by while a man is being killed unjustly, for the curse descends upon those who are present when they do not defend him. And no one should stand by while a man is being beaten unjustly, for the curse descends upon [those who] are present when they do not defend him."],[2975,"'Uthman b. 'Affan ؓ forbade 'umrah during the months of Hajj, or forbade tamattu' with 'umrah leading to Hajj. 'Ali ؓ entered ihram for it right there, so 'Uthman ؓ descended from the pulpit, took something and walked with it to 'Ali ؓ. [Talhah and al-Zubayr ؓ stood up and took it from him, and he walked to 'Ali ؓ]. He almost poked his eye with his finger, saying to him: \"You are indeed astray and leading others astray,\" while 'Ali ؓ did not reply to him at all."],[2976,"I witnessed 'Ali and 'Uthman ؓ when there was some provocation from Satan between them, and neither of them left anything unsaid to his companion. If I wished to recount to you what happened between them, I could, but they did not part until each sought forgiveness for his companion."],[2977,"I was sitting with 'Uthman ؓ when an old man came. When the people saw him, they said: Abu Dharr. When 'Uthman ؓ saw him, he said: Welcome to my brother, [so Abu Dharr ؓ said: Welcome to my brother]. By my life, you have been harsh in your determination. By Allah, if you had resolved that I should crawl, I would have crawled as much as I could."],[2978,"A man came and said: O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, what do you say about a man eager for jihad and dutiful, while his commanders impose upon him things he cannot count? He said: By Allah, I do not know what to say to you except that we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and perhaps we were not commanded with anything except that we did it."],[2980,"Whoever dies without having any allegiance upon him dies a death of ignorance. And whoever casts it off after having pledged it—Aswad said: from his neck—will meet Allah the Exalted with no excuse. They both said it together."],[2981,"We used to recite: Allah the Exalted will surely support this religion with men who have no share in the Hereafter."],[2982,"The prayer to the prayer is an expiation for what is between them, except for three: associating partners with Allah, abandoning the Sunnah, and breaking the covenant. They said: We know associating partners with Allah, but what is abandoning the Sunnah and breaking the covenant? He said: Abandoning the Sunnah is rebelling against obedience, and breaking the covenant is when a man pledges allegiance to someone, then rises against him with the sword to fight him."],[2983,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ advising some of his family, saying: \"Do not contend with the people of authority over the matter, even if you see that it is the truth.\""],[2984,"She said to those with her: \"How will you be when there are two callers: one calling to the Book of God, and one calling to the authority of God?\" They said: \"We will answer the caller to the Book of God.\" She said: \"Rather, answer the caller to the authority of God, for the Book of God is with His authority.\""],[2985,"Salama b. Yazid ؓ asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying: \"What do you think if rulers are appointed over us who demand their rights from us and deny us our rights?\" He remained silent two or three times. Then al-Ash'ath b. Qays narrated it and said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Listen and obey, for upon them is what they are burdened with, and upon you is what you are burdened with.'\""],[2986,"You have been tested by this authority and it has been tested by you. If it is just, it has the reward and you have gratitude. If it is unjust, upon it is the sin and upon you is patience."],[2987,"Umm Salama wrote to the people of Iraq: \"God is free from, and has freed His Messenger from, anyone who supports [rebels] and separates from the community. So do not support [rebels] and do not separate. Peace be upon you and the mercy of God.\""],[2989,"Umar ؓ said to Abu Bakr ؓ when 'Amr b. al-'As ؓ prevented people from lighting a fire: \"Do you not see what this man is doing to the people? He prevents them from their benefits.\" Abu Bakr ؓ said: \"Leave him, for the Messenger of God ﷺ appointed him over us because of his knowledge of war.\""],[2992,"The best of God's servants, Mighty and Majestic, in rank before God Almighty on the Day of Resurrection is a just and gentle ruler. The worst of God Almighty's servants in rank before God, Mighty and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection is a tyrannical and harsh ruler."],[2993,"Whoever is given authority over any affair of the Muslims and does not deal justly among them, upon him is the curse of God.\" And the curse of God is His damnation."],[2994,"The justice of a ruler among his subjects for a single day is better than the worship of a worshipper among his family for a hundred years, or fifty years."],[2995,"I am not one to praise a ruler.\" I said: \"Why is that?\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The rulers will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, the just and the unjust among them, until they stand on the bridge of Hell. Then God, Mighty and Majestic, will say: \"My demand is upon you.\" So no unjust ruler in his judgment, no one who takes bribes in his rulings, no one who gives ear to one of the two disputants will remain but he will fall into the Fire for seventy autumns.'\""],[2997,"Any man who appoints [a man] over ten people, knowing that among the ten there is one better than the one he appointed, has deceived Allah and His Messenger and deceived the community of Muslims. And the one who strikes beyond the prescribed limit will be brought and He will say: 'My servant, why did you strike beyond what I commanded you?' He will say: 'I was angry.' [He will say]: 'Was your anger to be more severe than My anger?' And the one who falls short will be brought and He will say: ['My servant, why did you fall short'?] [He will say: 'I had mercy on him']. He will say: 'Was your mercy to be greater than My mercy?' Then both of them will be commanded to be cast into the Fire."],[2998,"Whoever appoints a man over a group while among that group is one more pleasing to Allah than him has betrayed Allah, betrayed His Messenger ﷺ, and betrayed [all] the believers."],[2999,"Two classes of my nation will not attain my intercession, and will never attain my intercession, or I will not intercede for them: a tyrannical, oppressive, harsh ruler, and every extremist who deviates."],[3000,"Two men of my nation will not attain my intercession: a tyrannical, harsh, oppressive imam, and another who goes to extremes in religion and deviates in it."],[3001,"A governor who trades in his subjects is not just."],[3002,"Allah, the Exalted, does not make a servant a guardian over a flock, small or large, but He will ask him about it: whether he upheld his command among them or neglected it, until He asks him specifically about his own household."],[3004,"'Ubada came as a pilgrim from Syria. He arrived in Madinah and went to 'Uthman b. 'Affan ؓ and said: 'Shall I not tell you something I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There will be rulers over you who command you to do what you recognize and they themselves do what you disapprove of. Those have no right to obedience.\"'"],[3005,"Mu'adh ؓ said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if we have rulers who do not follow your Sunnah and do not adopt your command? What do you order us regarding them?' He said: 'There is no obedience to one who does not obey Allah.'"],[3007,"'Arifah: its beginning is blame, its end is regret, and the punishment on the Day of Resurrection.' I said: 'O Abu Hurayrah, except for those among them who fear Allah.' He said: '[I only] narrate to you as I heard.'"],[3008,"2586 2263/2 - [And] Abu Ya'la said: Shuja' b. Makhlad narrated to us, Wahb b. Jarir narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastawa'i narrated to us, with it."],[3009,"The arif will have a gate of Hell opened for him every year."],[3010,"Do not be an arif or a policeman. I said: Why? He said: They will burden you with debts and will not forget you."],[3011,"Do not be an arif or a policeman."],[3012,"A man who knows us. He said: Your arif is only the bold, the cunning, the dark wolf, the persistent, the greedy; when it is said to him 'Here', he seizes, and when it is said to him 'Give', he retreats."],[3013,"A funeral passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: Blessed is he if he was not an arif."],[3014,"People must have an arif, and the arif is in the Fire. He said: And the policeman will be brought and it will be said to him: Put down your whip and enter the Fire."],[3015,"There will come upon people a time when rulers over you will be fools; they will advance the worst of people and delay the best of them, and delay the prayer from its times. Whoever of you reaches that should never be an arif, nor a policeman, nor a tax collector, nor a traitor."],[3017,"In the name of God, the Compassionate, the Merciful. This is a letter from Muhammad b. Abdullah, the unlettered Prophet, the Qurashi, the Hashimi, the Messenger of God and His Prophet to all His creation: to al-Ala b. al-Hadrami and those Muslims with him—a covenant he covenanted to you. Fear God, O Muslims, as much as you are able, for I have sent over you al-Ala b. al-Hadrami and appointed him as commander, to fear God alone with no partner, to be gentle to you, and to conduct himself among you with truth, and to judge between you and those he meets of the people according to what God, Mighty and Majestic, sent down in His Book of justice. I command you to obey him as long as he does that and distributes equitably, and is merciful when mercy is sought. So listen to him and obey, and support and assist him well. For I have over you a right of obedience, a great right; you cannot estimate its full measure, and words cannot reach the true essence of the greatness of God and the right of His Messenger. Just as God and His Messenger have over all people in general, and over you in particular, an obligatory right, so obedience to him and fulfillment of his covenant [and may God be pleased with whoever holds fast to obedience and magnifies the right of its people and the right of its governors]. Likewise, Muslims have over their governors an obligatory right and obedience, which God Almighty has ordained for whoever holds fast to obedience and magnifies the right of its people and the right of its governors. For in obedience is the attainment of every good sought and deliverance from every evil feared. I call God to witness regarding anyone I appoint over any affair of the Muslims, small or great, who does not act justly among them, that he has no obedience, and he is dismissed from what I appointed him to, and the protection of the Muslims with him is absolved, along with their oaths and their covenant [and their protection]. Then let them ask God Almighty for guidance, and then let them appoint over themselves the best of them in their own view. Behold, if any calamity befalls al-Ala, then Khalid b. al-Walid ؓ, the Sword of God, is his successor among them for al-Ala b. al-Hadrami. So listen to him and obey as long as you know he is upon the truth, until he opposes the truth for something else. Proceed with the blessing of God and His help, victory, well-being, guidance, and success. Whomever you meet among people, call them to the Book of God sent down and the practices of His Messenger ﷺ, and to making lawful what God made lawful for them in His Book, and forbidding what God forbade them in His Book, and to casting off rivals and renouncing polytheism and disbelief, and to disbelieving in the worship of the tyrant and al-Lat and al-Uzza, and to abandoning worship of Jesus son of Mary, and Ezra son of Harwa, and the angels and the sun and the moon [and the fires], and everything taken as a rival besides God Almighty, and to taking God and His Messenger as guardians, and to renouncing what God and His Messenger renounced. When they do that and affirm it and enter into allegiance, then explain to them what is in the Book of God to which you call them. For it is the Book of God sent down with the Trustworthy Spirit upon His chosen one among the worlds, Muhammad b. Abdullah, His servant, Messenger, and Prophet [and beloved]. He sent him as a mercy to the worlds [in general], white and black among them, humans and jinn. The Book of God contains the news of everything that was before you and what will be after you, so that it may be a barrier between people by which God Almighty separates some of them from others, and in it is the turning away of some of them from others. It is the Book of God, dominant over the books, confirming what is in them of the Torah, the Gospel, and the Psalms. In it God informs you of what was before you that you missed in your first ancestors, to whom the messengers and prophets of God came, how their response was and with what He sent them, and how their affirmation of the signs of God Almighty or their denial of them was. And God Almighty informed in His Book of their affairs and their deeds, and the deeds of those of them who perished in their religion, so that you may avoid that and not do the like, lest there befall you from the Book of God Almighty of His punishment, wrath, and vengeance the like of what befell them because of their evil deeds and their contempt for God's command. And He informed you in His Book of the deeds of those who passed before you so that you may do the like of their deeds. He made clear to you in this Book of His all of that matter, as a mercy from Him to you and compassion from your Lord upon you. It is guidance from error, clarification from blindness, recovery from stumbling, deliverance from trial, light from darkness, healing at events, protection from destruction, right direction from misguidance, clarity from confusion, and the decisive criterion between this world and the Hereafter. In it is the perfection of your religion. When you present this to them and they affirm it to you, then complete the allegiance. Then present to them Islam, which is the five prayers, giving the zakat, pilgrimage to the House, fasting Ramadan, the major ablution from janabah, purification before prayer, dutifulness to parents, maintaining ties with Muslim kin, and good companionship [even] toward polytheist parents. If they do that, they have become Muslims. Then call them thereafter to faith and establish for them its laws and landmarks. Faith is the testimony that there is no god but God alone with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant [and Messenger], and that what Muhammad brought is the truth, and that what is other than it is falsehood, and faith in God, His angels, His books, His messengers and prophets, and the Last Day, and faith in what is before it and after it of the Torah, the Gospel, and the Psalms [and the resurrection, the gathering, and the reckoning], and Paradise and Hell, death and life, and faith in God and His Messenger and for all believers. When they do that and affirm it, they are submissive believers. Then guide them thereafter to excellence and teach them that excellence is to do good between them and God Almighty in fulfilling the trust and His covenant which He covenanted to His messengers, and the covenant of His messengers to His creation and the leaders of the believers, and submission and the safety of Muslims from every harm of tongue or hand, and to seek for the rest of the Muslims what he seeks for himself, and the affirmation of the promises of the Lord and meeting Him and seeing Him, and bidding farewell to the world at every hour, and self-reckoning at the completion of every day and night, and provision from night and day, and care for what God has obligated to be performed to Him in secret and openly. When they do that, they are submissive, believing, excellent ones. Then describe to them the major sins and guide them to them, and warn them of destruction in the major sins, for the major sins are the destructive ones. The first of them is associating partners with God; indeed, God does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, and sorcery, and the sorcerer has no share [in the Hereafter], and severing ties of kinship—may God curse them—and fleeing from the battlefield, for he has incurred wrath from God, and embezzlement; he will bring what he embezzled on the Day of Resurrection and it will not be accepted from them, and killing a believing soul—its recompense is Hell—and slandering chaste women—they are cursed in this world and the Hereafter—and consuming the orphan's property; they consume fire in their bellies and will burn in a blaze, and consuming usury; then announce war from God and His Messenger. When they desist from the major sins, they are submissive, believing, excellent, God-fearing ones. Then call them in like manner to worship. Worship is fasting, standing [in prayer], humility, [submissiveness], bowing, prostration, turning [to God], certainty, tenderness, declaring God's oneness, glorification, praise, magnification, charity after zakat, humbleness, tranquility, mutual consolation, supplication, earnest entreaty, acknowledgment of sovereignty and servitude, and deeming little what one does of much righteous work. When they do that, they are believing, submissive, excellent, God-fearing, worshipping ones and have completed worship. Then call them at that point to jihad and explain it to them, and make them desire what God made them desire of the virtue of jihad and its reward with God. If they are summoned, then accept their pledge and call them until you pledge them to the practice of God and the practice of His Messenger. Upon you is the covenant of God and His protection, seven sureties—meaning God is guarantor for fulfillment seven times—that you will not break your hands from a pledge nor violate the command of any governor among the governors of the Muslims. When they affirm this, accept their pledge and seek forgiveness from God for them. When they go out fighting in the path of God, anger for God Almighty and support for His religion, then whoever they meet among people, let them call them to what they were called to of the Book of God, by answering it, then its Islam, faith, excellence, God-fearing, worship, and jihad. Whoever follows them is the incited, the abundant, the submissive, the believer, the excellent, the God-fearing, the worshipper, the fighter; he has what you have and upon him is what is upon you. And whoever refuses this to you, fight them until they return to the command of God and to His religion. Whoever you make a treaty with and give the protection of God, fulfill it for him. Whoever submits and gives you satisfaction, he is of you and you are of him. Whoever fights you over this after you have made it heard to him, kill him. Whoever assaults you, fight him. Whoever schemes against you, scheme against him. Whoever gathers against you, gather against him. Whoever assassinates you, assassinate him, or deceives you, then deceive him without transgressing, or plots against you, then plot against him without transgressing, secretly or openly. For whoever avenges after being wronged, upon such there is no way [of blame]. Know that God is with you, sees you and sees your deeds, and knows all that you do. So fear God and be on guard. This is only a trust with which my Lord entrusted me, to convey it to His servants as an excuse from Him to them and a proof from Him with which I argue against all creation whom this book reaches. Whoever acts upon what is in it will be saved, whoever follows what is in it will be guided, whoever disputes by it will succeed, whoever fights by it will be aided, and whoever leaves it will go astray until he returns to it. So learn what is in it, listen with your ears, retain it in your hearts, and preserve it in your minds, for it is light for the eyes, spring for the hearts, and healing for what is in the breasts. This suffices as a matter and lesson, a deterrent, admonition, and caller to God [and His Messenger]. This is the good in which there is no evil. The letter of Muhammad, servant of God, His Messenger and Prophet, to al-Ala b. al-Hadrami when he sent him to Bahrain to call to God and His Messenger, commanding him to call to what is in it of lawful and forbid what is in it of unlawful, and to guide to what is in it of right direction and forbid what is in it of error. A letter with which the Prophet of God entrusted al-Ala b. al-Hadrami and his successor the Sword of God, Khalid b. al-Walid, and he has left no excuse to them in the bequest of what is in this letter [and] to the Muslims with them, and he made no excuse for any of them in wasting any of it, neither the governors nor the governed. Whoever of all creation this letter reaches has no excuse and no argument, and he is not excused for ignorance of anything in this letter. This letter was written on the third of Dhu al-Qa'dah, four years having passed of the migration of the Prophet of God except two months. Witnessed the letter on the day it was written: Ibn Abi Sufyan dictating it to him, Uthman [b. Affan] ؓ, the Messenger of God ﷺ [seated], al-Mukhtar b. Qays al-Qurashi, Abu Dharr al-Ghifari, Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman al-Absi, Qusayy b. Abi Umar al-Himyari, Shabib b. Abi Marthad al-Ghassani, al-Mustanir b. Abi Sa'sa'ah al-Khuza'i, Awanah b. Shammakh al-Juhani, Sa'd b. Malik al-Ansari, Sa'd b. Ubadah al-Ansari, Zayd b. Umayr, the naqibs, a man from Quraysh, a man from Juhaynah, and four from the Ansar, until the Messenger of God ﷺ handed it to al-Ala b. al-Hadrami and the Sword of God, Khalid b. al-Walid ؓ. [This passage was omitted from the Dar al-Asimah edition; it is established from Zawa'id al-Harith and It-haf al-Busiri]."],[3019,"Indeed, the judge will descend in his station in Hell farther than Aden."],[3020,"Uthman b. Affan ؓ said to Ibn Umar ؓ: Judge between the people. He said: I will not judge between two men, nor lead them in prayer. He said: Your father ؓ used to judge. He said: My father used to judge, and if something was unclear to him, he asked the Prophet ﷺ, and if something was unclear to the Prophet ﷺ, he asked Gabriel ﷺ . But I do not find anyone to ask, and I am not like my father. It has reached me that judges are three: a man who feared [God] but his desire swayed him, so he is in the Fire; [a man who undertook judgment and judged ignorantly, so he is in the Fire]; and a man who strove and was correct; that one escapes with neither gain nor loss. Have you heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever seeks refuge in God has sought refuge in a true refuge? He said: Yes. He said: Then I seek refuge in God from you making me a judge. So he excused him and said: Do not tell anyone."],[3021,"Allah, the Exalted, is with the judge as long as he does not deliberately incline to injustice, or as long as he does not intentionally deviate, and He grants him success in [attaining] the truth as long as he does not desire other than it."],[3022,"Whoever is placed in authority over the people and then hides himself from them [at the time of] their poverty and need, Allah will hide Himself from him on the Day of Resurrection."],[3023,"If one of you is tested with judging between the Muslims, let him not judge while angry; and let him treat them equally in the sitting place, in looking, and in gesturing; and let him not raise his voice over one of the two litigants above the other."],[3024,"When he would become angry or hungry, he would get up and not judge between anyone."],[3025,"A judge does not judge except when he is full and quenched."],[3026,"Judging is not a calculation that you compute, but rather a touch that passes over the heart."],[3027,"When Ibn Abbas ؓ was asked about something, if it was in the Book of Allah, the Exalted, he would speak according to it. If it was not in the Book of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and there was something from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would relate it. And if it was not in the Book of Allah nor in the judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and there was something from Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ, he would adopt it. If there was nothing from them, he would exercise his own judgment."],[3029,"A man came and stayed with Ali ؓ, and he hosted him. The man said: \"I want to engage in a dispute.\" Ali ؓ said to him: \"Move away, for the Prophet ﷺ forbade us to host a litigant unless his opponent is with him.\""],[3030,"I witnessed Abu Hurayrah ؓ judging. Al-Harith b. al-Hakam came and sat on his cushion upon which he used to recline. He said: Abu Hurayrah thought that he had come for some need other than a judgment. He said: Then a man came and sat in front of Abu Hurayrah ؓ. He said to him: \"What is your matter?\" He said: \"Al-Harith has made a claim against me.\" Abu Hurayrah said to him: \"Get up and sit with your opponent, for it is the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.\""],[3031,"Whoever takes the side of a litigant in a dispute without knowledge of his case will not cease to be under the wrath of Allah, the Exalted, until he desists."],[3033,"Ali ؓ distributed a share, so he called a man to calculate [the shares] among the people. They said: \"Give him [something].\" He said: \"If he wishes, but it is unlawful gain (suht).\""],[3035,"The briber and the bribed are in the Fire."],[3036,"Abu Ya'la narrated it from Ahmad b. Mani'. Al-Bazzar said: We do not know it from A'ishah ؓ except through this chain. Ishaq b. Yahya was alone in transmitting it, and he is weak."],[3037,"I was sitting with 'Abdullah, and a man asked him: What is illicit gain (suht)? He said: Bribes. He said: What about injustice in judgment? He said: That is disbelief. Then he recited: 'And whoever does not judge by what God has sent down, those are the disbelievers.'"],[3039,"The proof is upon the claimant, and the oath is upon the defendant."],[3040,"He ruled that if the claimant has no proof, then the defendant must take an oath."],[3041,"Two just witnesses that you separated by mutual consent after the sale or by choice; otherwise, his oath by God that you did not separate by mutual consent after the sale or by choice."],[3043,"I heard my father say to al-Hakam b. 'Utaybah... and he mentioned it. Al-Tirmidhi reported it from Muhammad b. 'Ali, from Jabir, and he indicated the hadith of 'Ali ؓ."],[3044,"I was with 'Abd al-Hamid in Kufa, and he used to rule by an oath along with a witness. Some people of Kufa disapproved of that, so he wrote to 'Umar b. 'Abd al-'Aziz ؓ about it. He wrote back that I should rule by an oath along with a witness. An elder among their leaders stood up and said: I witnessed Shurayh ruling by an oath along with a witness in this mosque."],[3046,"The drum is forbidden, the tambourine is forbidden, musical instruments are forbidden, and wind instruments are forbidden."],[3047,"No cuckold will enter Paradise."],[3048,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered a crier, who called out when he reached the mountain pass: The testimony of a litigant or one accused is not acceptable, and the oath is upon the defendant."],[3049,"Abd Allah b. Abi Mulaykah wrote to Ibn Abbas ؓ asking him about the testimony of children. He replied: It is not acceptable, because Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: from those whom you approve as witnesses. [And concerning black slaves who slaughtered a donkey, that if their master is made liable, there is no amputation for them.]"],[3050,"The testimony of a child against a child and the testimony of a slave against a slave is acceptable."],[3051,"One religious community does not inherit from another, and the testimony of one religious community is not acceptable against another, except the community of Muhammad ﷺ, for their testimony is acceptable against others."],[3052,"The Prophet ﷺ rejected the testimony of a man because of his lying."],[3053,"Beware of these poisoned dice-like pieces that are thrown in gambling, for they are part of gambling."],[3054,"He heard Muhammad b. Kab al-Qurazi asking Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Said al-Khudri ؓ: What did you hear your father narrate from the Prophet ﷺ? He said: I heard my father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The likeness of one who plays backgammon then stands to pray is like one who performs ablution with pus and pig's blood, saying: His prayer is not accepted."],[3055,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ with a son of his and said: O Messenger of Allah, I want you to witness a charity I am giving to this son of mine. The Prophet ﷺ said: Do you have other children? He said: Yes. He said: Have you given them the like of this? He said: No. The Prophet ﷺ said: Then I will not witness."],[3057,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us, and he mentioned the hadith, in which is: \"Whoever wrongs a woman by withholding her dowry, then he is, in the sight of Allah, the Exalted, an adulterer. And Allah, the Exalted, will say to him on the Day of Resurrection: 'My servant, I gave you in marriage upon My covenant, yet you did not honor My covenant?' Then Allah, the Exalted, will take charge of seeking her right, and He will exhaust all his good deeds, and whatever remains of them, it will be commanded that he be taken to the Fire. And whoever has two wives and does not treat them justly in the division of his self and his wealth, he will come on the Day of Resurrection fettered, with his side leaning, until he enters the Fire.\""],[3058,"Whoever gives testimony by which he makes lawful the property of a Muslim or sheds his blood has made himself deserving of the Fire.\""],[3059,"I saw 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ make a false witness stand in the evening in a waist-wrapper, striking himself, then he let him go.\""],[3062,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed - meaning on the day of Khaybar - the woman who joins hair extensions and the one who has it done, and the woman who tattoos and the one who is tattooed.\""],[3064,"Indeed Allah, exalted is He, is good and loves the good, clean and loves cleanliness, generous and loves generosity, magnanimous and loves magnanimity, so clean your courtyards and do not resemble the Jews who gather rubbish in their homes.\""],[3066,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turbaned me on the day of Ghadir Khumm with a turban and let it hang down behind me, then he said: 'Indeed Allah, exalted is He, supported me on the day of Badr and Hunayn with angels wearing this turban.' And he said: 'Indeed the turban is a barrier between disbelief and faith...' and he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[3068,"Abu Lubabah was sitting with Ka'b ؓ, [and Abu Lubabah said]: 'How bad is the garment of pride.' Ka'b ؓ said: 'Did you hear it from the Prophet ﷺ?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'I do not reject your knowledge. I find in the Book of Allah: Whoever wears a garment of pride, Allah will not look at him until he takes it off, even if it is precious.' Then Abu Lubabah ؓ said: 'How bad is the heart of the fat one.' Ka'b ؓ said: 'Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'No.' Ka'b ؓ said: 'I do not reject your knowledge. I find in the Book of Allah, exalted is He: The example of the fat one and the heart of the emaciated one is like that of a fat sheep and an emaciated sheep upon which rain fell, and it reached the heart of the emaciated one but did not reach the heart of the fat one.' Then Abu Lubabah ؓ said: '[Whoever worships Allah], Allah, mighty and majestic is He, will suffice him in his needs.' Ka'b ؓ said: 'Did you hear it from the Prophet ﷺ?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'I do not reject your knowledge. I find in the Book of Allah, exalted is He: There is no servant who worships Allah, mighty and majestic is He, except that Allah, exalted is He, guarantees the heaven and the earth for his provision until he dies or [as long as] he lives.'\""],[3069,"While a man from those before you went out in two garments and strutted in them, Allah [blessed and exalted is He] commanded the earth and it seized him, and he will sink in it until the Day of Resurrection."],[3070,"Allah, exalted is He, will not look at the one who drags his lower garment."],[3071,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a sermon and mentioned the hadith, and in it: 'Whoever wears a garment and struts in it, he will be swallowed up from the edge of Hell and will sink in it as long as the heavens and the earth endure; because Qarun wore a fine garment and strutted, and he was swallowed up, and he will sink in it until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[3072,"A man came walking in two garments of his, having let his waist-wrapper trail, looking at his two sides, and he was swaggering, when Allah, exalted is He, caused the earth to swallow him, and he will be sinking in it until the Day of Resurrection."],[3073,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he mentioned the hadith, and at its end: And beware of dragging the waist-wrapper, for dragging the waist-wrapper is from arrogance."],[3074,"‘Abdullah ؓ saw a man dragging his waist-wrapper, so he said: Raise your waist-wrapper. He said: I have thin shanks."],[3075,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas ؓ said: \"While I was circumambulating the House, I saw a woman and she pleased me.\" And it was said: The beauty of a woman you do not know does not harm you."],[3076,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man dragging his waist-wrapper, so he said to him: Raise your waist-wrapper, for Allah does not love the arrogant. He said: O Messenger of Allah, my shanks are thin. He said: That is uglier than what is in your shanks."],[3077,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who wore (fine clothes) did not criticize those who did not wear (them), and those who did not wear (them) did not criticize those who wore (them)."],[3079,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man of disheveled appearance, so he said: Do you have wealth? He said: Yes, of various kinds of wealth. He ﷺ said: Then let its effect be seen on you, for Allah, exalted is He, loves to see the effect of His blessing on His servant and hates wretchedness and feigning wretchedness.\""],[3080,"Allah is beautiful and loves beauty; He loves to see [the effect of] His blessing on His servant."],[3081,"Adopt the ways of Ma‘add, be rough, shoot arrows, and walk barefoot."],[3082,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a cotton shirt, short in length and short in sleeves."],[3083,"'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ bought two sunbulani anjijani shirts for seven dirhams, and he clothed Qanbar with one of them. When he wanted to put on [the other], his lower garment had a patch of tanned leather."],[3085,"I got married during the time of my father, so he invited the people, and Abu Ayyub was among those he invited. They had hung green curtains, so Abu Ayyub came and entered—while my father was standing—and he looked and saw the house covered with green curtains. He said, 'O 'Abdullah, do you cover the walls?' My father said, feeling shy, 'O Abu Ayyub, the women overpowered us.' He said, 'Whoever I feared the women would overpower, I did not fear they would overpower you.' Then he said, 'By Allah, I will not eat food for you, nor will I enter a house for you,' and then he left."],[3086,"'Abdullah b. Yazid was invited to a meal, and when he came he saw the house furnished (with curtains) and sat outside and wept. It was said to him, 'What makes you weep?' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ...' and he mentioned the hadith. He said: One day he saw a man who had patched his burdah with a piece of fur, so he faced the rising of the sun and said, gesturing with his hand—Hammad described it with his hands, palms inward and extended—'The world has appeared before you,' meaning it has advanced, 'until we thought it would fall upon us. One of you goes out in one fine garment and returns in another, and you cover your houses as you cover the Ka'bah.' 'Abdullah b. Yazid said, 'How can I not weep when I have seen you covering your houses as you cover the Ka'bah?'"],[3088,"A fine garment and a Syrian cloth came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he clothed me with the fine garment and clothed Usamah ؓ with the cloth. I went out in my fine garment, and he ﷺ said to Usamah, 'What did you do with your cloth?' He said, 'I clothed my wife with it.' He ﷺ said, 'Tell her to wear underneath it a thin garment that does not describe the size of her bones to men.'"],[3090,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her while she was applying henna, and he said, 'Why not, O mother of so-and-so, like this on the back of his hand,' meaning the pattern."],[3092,"I asked him while I was perfumed with khalouq, and he said to me, 'Go and perform ghusl.' So I went and performed ghusl, then returned. He did the same three times. He said: Then I went and fell into a well, and I took a dry stone and began to seek water for wudu, then I performed ghusl and came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'State your need.'"],[3093,"Three people the angels do not approach: the one perfumed with khalouq, the drunkard, and the junub (one in a state of major ritual impurity)."],[3094,"I went with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the Jews of Banu Qaynuqa', and he saw a man perfumed with khalouq, so he withdrew his hand. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, perhaps he is a bridegroom.' He ﷺ said, 'Even so. Go and wash it off him, then scrub him, then wash it off him, then scrub him, [then wash it off him, then scrub him].'"],[3095,"I saw 'Abdullah b. Busr, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ؓ, wearing a yellow turban and a yellow outer garment."],[3096,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing two garments dyed with saffron: an outer garment and a turban."],[3097,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of the conquest of Makkah to pledge allegiance to him, and he saw that his hand was perfumed with khalouq, so he withdrew his hand. A man said to him, 'May your mother be bereft of you! The Prophet ﷺ withdrew his hand from you only because it is perfumed with khalouq.' So he washed his hand and then came to the Prophet ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him."],[3099,"We used to enter upon 'A'ishah ؓ while we were young boys, and upon us were saffron-dyed garments."],[3100,"A young man came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing a saffron-dyed cloak, and the Messenger ﷺ said: \"If this were under the pot of your family, it would be better for you.\" So the young man went away and then came to the Prophet ﷺ the next morning, and he said: \"What did you do with your garment?\" He said: \"I did what you commanded me.\" He ﷺ said: \"That is not what I commanded you; why did you not give it to some of your womenfolk?\""],[3102,"I entered upon Abu Bakr ؓ while he was ill, and I saw Asma' bt. 'Umays ؓ defending [him], and her hands were tattooed [i.e., decorated with henna]."],[3104,"He forbade that the skins of beasts of prey be used as bedding."],[3106,"The horses of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out, and Ukaydir of Dumah heard of them. Then he mentioned the hadith, saying: \"Then Ukaydir brought out a cloak woven with gold, of the kind that Khosrau used to clothe them. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Return with your cloak, for no one wears this in this world except that he will be deprived of it in the Hereafter.' So he returned with it. When he reached his home, he felt uneasy about returning his gift, so he came back and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we are a household who find it difficult to have our gifts returned, so accept my gift from me.' He said: 'Go and give it to 'Umar ؓ.' 'Umar ؓ had heard what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about it, so he wept and his eyes shed tears, and he thought that misery had befallen him. He went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'Has something new happened concerning me?' He said: 'In this cloak, what I heard; then you sent it to me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until he put his hand over his mouth, then he ﷺ said: 'I did not send it to you to wear it, but to sell it and use its price.'\""],[3107,"A striped silk garment was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he sent it to 'Ali ؓ. He went out wearing it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali ؓ: \"I am not pleased for you except with what I am pleased for myself. I did not clothe you with it to wear it; I clothed you with it so that you could make it into head covers among the Fatimahs.\""],[3108,"I asked 'A'ishah ؓ about silk that women wear. She said: \"We used to be clothed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with garments called siyara'.\""],[3109,"I was with Ibn Mas'ud ؓ when two sons came wearing shirts of silk. He tore them off them and said: \"This is only for women, not for men.\""],[3110,"Gold and silk are lawful for the females of my Ummah and forbidden for its males."],[3111,"Sa'd b. Malik entered upon Ibn 'Amir ؓ while he was reclining on a mattress of fine silk. He said: \"To sit on burning coals of ghada wood is dearer to me than to sit on this.\""],[3113,"Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf entered with his son Muhammad, who was wearing a silk shirt. 'Umar ؓ stood up, grabbed him by the collar, and tore it. Abd al-Rahman said: 'May Allah forgive you, you frightened the boy and terrified him.' He said: 'You clothe them in silk?' He said: 'Yet I wear silk, and they are like you.'"],[3114,"Ibn 'Awf entered upon 'Umar ؓ wearing a silk shirt. 'Umar ؓ said: \"It has been mentioned to me that whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.\" Abd al-Rahman said: \"I hope to wear it in this world and the Hereafter.\""],[3115,"'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf ؓ complained to the Prophet ﷺ about an abundance of lice, and said, \"O Messenger of God, do you permit me to wear a shirt of silk?\" He permitted him. When the Messenger of God ﷺ and Abu Bakr ؓ passed away and 'Umar ؓ became caliph, he ['Abd al-Rahman] came to him with his son and Abu Salama, wearing a shirt of silk. 'Umar ؓ said, \"What is this?\" Then he put his hand into the collar of the shirt and tore it down to its bottom. 'Abd al-Rahman ؓ said to him, \"Do you not know that the Messenger of God ﷺ permitted it for me?\" He said, \"He only permitted it for you because you complained of lice. As for others, no.\""],[3117,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to wear a white cap."],[3118,"I saw al-Hasan with a white head and beard, wearing a quilted white cap."],[3119,"He saw Ibn 'Umar ؓ with his waist-wrapper at the middle of his shin, his shirt above that, and his cloak above the shirt."],[3120,"'Uthman ؓ used to have his waist-wrapper at the middle of his shins. He was asked about that, and he said, \"This is how our companion — meaning the Prophet ﷺ — wore his waist-wrapper.\""],[3121,"If your waist-wrapper is wide, wear it over one shoulder; if it is narrow, wrap it around your waist."],[3123,"The Prophet ﷺ made one of his wives stand, and measured a span or two spans from the hem of her garment, and said, \"Do not exceed this.\""],[3125,"The two red things destroy them: gold and saffron."],[3126,"'A'ishah ؓ forbade gold and silver vessels. They did not cease [urging] her until she permitted gold."],[3127,"Abu Umamah As'ad b. Zurarah ؓ entrusted the Messenger of God ﷺ with my mother and my maternal aunt. Jewelry containing gold and pearls, called ri'ath, was brought to him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ adorned them with those ri'ath. I later saw that jewelry in the possession of my family."],[3129,"A man from among the Persians came to the mosque having grown his moustache long and shaved his beard. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"What made you do this?\" He said, \"My Lord commanded me to do this.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"God Almighty commanded me to let my beard grow and trim my moustache.\""],[3131,"They used to dislike plucking gray hair."],[3133,"He saw some hair of the Messenger of God ﷺ dyed with henna. He said: \"We would soak it in water, and drink that water.\""],[3134,"A man entered upon the Prophet ﷺ with a white head and beard. He ﷺ said: \"Are you not a Muslim?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He ﷺ said: \"Then dye [it].\""],[3135,"Dye with henna, for it is pleasant in fragrance and calms dizziness."],[3136,"Whoever changes whiteness to blackness, God Almighty will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."],[3137,"\"Gray hair is light.\" And he added: \"except for one who dyes it or plucks it.\""],[3139,"Whoever grows gray in Islam, it will be light for him as long as he does not change it."],[3140,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ would not change his gray hair. He was asked about that: \"Why do you not change it, when Abu Bakr ؓ used to change it?\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever grows gray in Islam, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection,' and I will not change my gray hair.\""],[3143,"We waited for the Prophet ﷺ to come out to us in Ramadan. He ﷺ came out of the house of Umm Salamah ؓ, and she had applied kohl to him and filled his eye with kohl."],[3145,"He wore a ring on his right hand and said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ wore a ring on the right.\""],[3146,"Aqil ؓ killed a man from the polytheists on the day of Mu'tah, and took his ring and a slave girl who was with him. He brought them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who took the ring and put it on his finger, then said: 'Were it not for this image (i.e., engraving).' He said: So he gave Aqil ؓ his ring and his slave girl as spoils."],[3147,"Ziyad entered upon Umar ؓ with a gold ring on his hand. Umar ؓ said: 'You have adopted gold rings.' Abu Musa ؓ said: 'But my ring is of iron.' Umar ؓ said: 'That is fouler and more evil. Whoever of you wears a ring, let him wear a silver ring.'"],[3148,"A woman would make buttons for the sleeve of her garment and put one on her finger to cover the ring."],[3149,"The Prophet ﷺ used to wear a ring on his right palm."],[3150,"When Anas ؓ related a hadith to his companions that they did not understand, they would go to al-Hasan ؓ and he would explain it to them. One day al-Hasan explained to them the hadith: 'Do not engrave Arabic on your rings,' meaning: 'Do not engrave Muhammad.'"],[3151,"The engraving on the ring of Hudhayfah ؓ was two cranes facing each other, and between them: 'Praise be to Allah.'"],[3152,"Talhah ؓ had a gold ring."],[3153,"I saw on the hand of Anas b. Malik ؓ a gold ring."],[3154,"The Prophet ﷺ was on the pulpit wearing a gold ring. He said to the people: 'You look at it and I look at it,' and he threw it away."],[3155,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade qassiyyah (silk garments from Egypt), mayathir (saddle cloths), gold rings, and mufaddam (a type of cloth)."],[3156,"They used to permit a young boy to wear a gold ring, but when he reached puberty he would discard it."],[3157,"I saw the sandal of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a heel strap and two laces."],[3158,"We entered upon an old man called Muhajir, and I had on a sandal with two qibals (straps). He said: 'I had left it because of its being well-known.' So he said: 'What is this?' I said: 'I wanted to leave it because of its being well-known.' He said: 'Do not leave it, for the sandal of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was like this.'"],[3159,"I came to a shoemaker in Madinah and said: 'Make my sandal.' He said: 'If you wish, I will make it like this, and if you wish, I will make it as I saw the sandal of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' [I said: 'And did you see the sandal of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?'] He said: 'I saw it in the house of Fatimah ؓ.' He (the narrator) said: 'I think he said: In the house of Fatimah bt. Ubayd Allah b. Abbas.' I said: 'Make it as you saw the sandal of the Prophet ﷺ.' He said: 'So he made it with two qibals.' He said: 'And when I arrived, Ibn Sirin had already taken it.'"],[3160,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade [that the sword be adorned with silver]."],[3162,"He forbade branding on the face. Al-Abbas ؓ said: 'I will not brand except at the end of a bone,' so he branded on the two ja'iratain (the two sides of the rump)."],[3163,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a donkey branded between its eyes, and he disliked that, and he spoke harshly about it."],[3164,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade castrating horses and beasts. Ibn Umar ؓ said: 'In it is [the increase] of creation.'"],[3165,"A camel that had been branded on its face was brought past the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'If only the owners of this camel had kept the fire away from this animal.' He said: 'I said: I will brand in the farthest place from its face.' He said: 'So I branded on the root of the tail.'"],[3167,"Yahya b. Ya'mar used to give fatwa in Khurasan that when a man buys [the sacrificial animal] and names it, and the ten (days) enter, he should refrain from his hair and nails until he sacrifices. Qatadah said: 'I mentioned that to Sa'id b. al-Musayyab, and he said: Yes.' I said: 'From whom?' He said: 'From the companions of Muhammad ﷺ.'"],[3168,"When the ten (days) entered, Ibn Sirin used to dislike a man taking from his hair, to the extent that he disliked boys shaving their hair."],[3169,"Two young, salt-and-white rams were gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he sacrificed them."],[3170,"Indeed, the Messenger of God ﷺ was brought two horned, large, castrated salt-and-white rams. He laid one of them down and said: 'In the name of God, and God is greatest. O God, [this is] on behalf of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad.' Then he laid down the other and said: 'In the name of God, and God is greatest. O God, [this is] on behalf of Muhammad and his community—those who bear witness to Your oneness and bear witness to my conveying [the message].'"],[3171,"The best shroud is the hulla, and the best sacrificial animal is the horned ram."],[3172,"Indeed, my family would have a thousand sheep, and I would select from them a jadha' and slaughter it."],[3173,"He disliked that anyone but a Muslim should slaughter the sacrificial animal."],[3174,"I asked Ibn 'Umar ؓ about a cow or a camel—does it suffice for seven? He said: 'How so? Does it have seven souls?' I said: 'The companions of Muhammad ﷺ who are in Kufa gave me this ruling.' The people said: 'Yes, the Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar ؓ said that.' Ibn 'Umar ؓ said: 'I was not aware.'"],[3175,"I asked Ibn 'Umar ؓ about a man who offers a cow as a sacrificial animal—may he sell its hide and give its price in charity? He said: 'There is no harm in that.'"],[3176,"When it is difficult for you regarding the sacrificial animal, a jadha' of sheep will suffice for you."],[3177,"A man slaughtered before the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed on the Day of Sacrifice, and he ﷺ said: 'It will not suffice for you.' The man said: 'O Messenger of God, we have a jadha'ah.' He ﷺ said: 'It will suffice for you, but it will not suffice for anyone after you.'"],[3178,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and a man came and entered with a fat, excellent young goat and a lean, inferior young sheep. He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this is a lean, inferior young sheep, and this is a fat, excellent young goat, and it is the better of the two. Should I sacrifice it?' He ﷺ said: 'Sacrifice it, for Allah loves the better.'"],[3179,"And 'Abd b. Humayd said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us with this."],[3180,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Fatimah ؓ: 'Arise, O Fatimah, and witness your sacrifice. Indeed, with the first drop of its blood that falls, you will have forgiveness for every sin. Indeed, it will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with its meat and blood seventy times over, then placed in your scale.' Abu Sa'id al-Khudri ؓ said: 'Is this for the family of Muhammad specifically, for they are worthy of the good they are singled out with, or for the family of Muhammad and the people generally?' He said: 'Rather, for the family of Muhammad and the people generally.'"],[3181,"I witnessed Abu Hurayrah ؓ at the prayer place say to two men: 'Do you have anything to sacrifice?' They said: 'No.' So he went with them to his house and brought out his sheep. He said: 'May Allah accept from Abu Hurayrah, and from so-and-so and so-and-so.' Then he took its liver or something from it, and they ate from it. Then he divided it into three parts, and the two men went away with two-thirds of it, and one-third entered the house of Abu Hurayrah ؓ."],[3182,"A man asked Ibn 'Umar ؓ about the sacrificial animal, and he said: 'Avoid and shun the one-eyed whose defect is clear, the lame whose lameness is clear, the sick whose sickness is clear, and the emaciated whose emaciation is clear.'"],[3183,"Abu Bakr and 'Umar ؓ attended the season but did not sacrifice."],[3184,"'Umar ؓ used to perform Hajj and not sacrifice.' Ibrahim said: 'They used to perform Hajj having their provisions and their gold with them, yet they would not sacrifice.'"],[3186,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us with this."],[3187,"The Prophet ﷺ performed 'aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ with two rams."],[3188,"I brought Ibn al-Zubayr to the Prophet ﷺ, and he chewed a date for him and said: \"This is Abdullah, and you are Umm Abdullah.\""],[3189,"Whoever has a child born to him and calls the adhan in its right ear and the iqamah in its left ear, Umm al-Sibyan will not harm him."],[3190,"For the aqiqah: for a boy, two rams; and for a girl, one ram.\""],[3191,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us with this."],[3194,"The fetus is slaughtered until the blood within it comes out."],[3195,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about the fetus, and he said: 'Its slaughter is the slaughter of its mother.'"],[3197,"It is disliked to sharpen the knife while the sheep is looking."],[3198,"No marriage is valid without a guardian."],[3199,"I asked Abu Dharr ؓ about slaughtered animals, and he said: 'We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the mount of one of us became unruly, and he stabbed it with a sword in its temple.'"],[3200,"He used to say at the time of slaughter: 'In the name of Allah, and Allah is most great. O Allah, it is for You and from You, accept from so-and-so.'"],[3201,"Anas ؓ, when he slaughtered, said: 'In the name of Allah, and Allah is most great.'"],[3202,"The slaughtered animal of a Muslim is lawful even if he does not mention the name of Allah, as long as he did not do so intentionally; and the same applies to the slave."],[3203,"The slaughtered animal of a Muslim is lawful, whether he mentions the name of Allah the Exalted or does not mention it; and if he mentions, he mentions nothing but the name of Allah."],[3204,"When a Muslim slaughters and forgets to mention the name of Allah the Exalted, let him eat, for in the Muslim there is a name from the names of Allah the Exalted.\""],[3205,"Whoever dedicates [a sacrifice] to other than Allah, upon him is the curse of Allah; and whoever says about me what I did not say, likewise..."],[3207,"He was [sick with fever], so fox meat was prescribed for him, but he disliked it, and said: 'It is a beast of prey.'"],[3208,"A dabb lizard was brought to the Prophet ﷺ on a platter, [and he ﷺ said]: 'Eat, for I find it distasteful.'"],[3209,"A dabb lizard was gifted to us, so I cooked it. Then two men from her people entered upon her, and she offered it to them. Then the Prophet ﷺ entered while they were eating, and he ﷺ placed his hand, then lifted it and said: 'What is this?' She said: 'A dabb lizard gifted to me, so I cooked it.' He ﷺ threw it away, and they went to throw away what was in their hands. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: 'Eat, for you are people of Najd and you eat it, while we are people of Tihamah and we find it distasteful.'"],[3210,"I will not eat from meat that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not eat from."],[3211,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon, and interrupted his sermon and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the dabb lizard?' He ﷺ said: 'A nation of the Children of Israel was transformed, and I do not know which of the animals was transformed.'"],[3212,"A dabb lizard was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'A nation that was transformed.'"],[3213,"The dabb lizard was eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not eat it nor did he forbid [it].\""],[3214,"The Prophet ﷺ handed the spear to Abu Rafi' ؓ and ordered him to kill the dogs of Madinah, so he killed them except one dog. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and he ordered him to kill it."],[3215,"Jibril ﷺ came and asked permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He gave him permission, but he was slow to come in. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took his cloak and went to him while he was standing at the door. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'We have given permission.' He said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but we do not enter a house in which there is an image or a dog.' So they looked and found a puppy in one of their houses. Abu Rafi' ؓ said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me when I woke up, and I did not leave a dog in Madinah without killing it. Then I came upon a woman in a remote area who had a dog that barked in her defense, and I felt compassion for her, so I left it and came to him ﷺ and informed him. He commanded me to kill it, so I returned to the dog and killed it.' He said: 'The people said: What is lawful for us, O Messenger of Allah, of this community that you commanded to be killed?' Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent down: 'And what you have trained of hunting animals, as trainers' (Qur'an 5:4)."],[3216,"'O Abu Rafi', kill every dog in Madinah.' He said: 'I found some women in Madinah from al-Baqi' who had a dog. They said: O Abu Rafi', the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has sent our men on a military expedition, and this dog benefits us after Allah, Exalted. By Allah, no one can come to us unless one of our women stands and gets between him and it. Mention it to the Prophet ﷺ.' He said: 'Abu Rafi' mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: O Abu Rafi', kill it, for Allah, Exalted, will protect them.'"],[3217,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to kill dogs. I went out and did not see a dog without killing it. Then there was a dog going around, and I went to kill it, but a person from inside a house called out to me: 'What do you want to do?' I said: 'I want to kill this dog.' She said: 'I am a woman in a remote area, and this dog protects me from wild animals and alerts me to intruders.' So I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he commanded me to kill it."],[3219,"Whoever keeps a dog that is not a dog for livestock or a hunting dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day."],[3221,"I was sitting with Abu Hurayrah ؓ and he mentioned a story ... He said: Then he began to narrate, saying: 'One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was outside while we were sitting with him, when a wolf came to him and sat on its haunches in front of him, then wagged its tail. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: This is the wolf, and this is the envoy of the wolves. What do you think? Would you give it something from your wealth? The people said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we will not give it anything from our wealth. A man got up and threw a stone at it, and it turned back howling. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The wolf, and what about the wolf? Three times.'"],[3222,"The lifespan of a fly is forty nights, and all flies are in the Fire except the bee."],[3223,"All flies are in the Fire except the bee."],[3225,"The sound of the rooster, its beating with its wings, is its bowing and prostration."],[3226,"The white rooster is my friend, and the friend of my friend, and the enemy of my enemy."],[3227,"It guards the house of its owner and nine houses around it, and he would keep it overnight in his house."],[3229,"I came out of the mosque, and there was a man calling out behind me. I said, “Who is this?” They said, “ʿAlī ؓ.” I walked behind him until he came upon the fish sellers, and he said, “No floater is to be sold in our market.”"],[3230,"I saw ʿAmmār b. Yāsir on the Messenger of Allah’s ﷺ white mule, and he was saying, “Where are the butchers?” Then he said, “Indeed I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to you: do not eat the ḥashā.” Al-Naḍr said: meaning the spleen. Then he said, “Where are the fish sellers?” They said, “Here they are.” So he moved until he stood over them and said, “Indeed I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to you: do not eat from the ṣillawr or the anqalīs.”"],[3232,"I entered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon my maternal aunt Maymūna ؓ. She said to him, “Shall we present to you something that Ḥafīd Umm ʿAtīq gifted to us?” So she brought him ﷺ roasted ḍabb lizards. When he saw them, he spat three times and did not eat from them, and he ordered us to eat."],[3233,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of Khaybar the eating of domesticated donkey, and of every beast of prey with fangs."],[3234,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, most of my wealth is in donkeys; may I acquire from them?” He ﷺ said, “Does it not graze on open land and eat from trees?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Then acquire from them.”"],[3235,"The prohibition of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from eating the meat of donkeys came to us while we were at Khaybar, and the pots were boiling with it, so we overturned them on their faces."],[3236,"That he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the meat of domesticated donkeys, and he mentioned to them something of their matter, and he permitted them regarding it."],[3237,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the jallāla: that its meat be eaten or its milk be drunk."],[3238,"If you shoot a bird and it falls off a mountain and dies, do not eat it, for I fear the fall killed it. And if you shoot a bird and it falls into water, do not eat it, for I fear the water killed it."],[3240,"A man informed Ibn ʿUmar that Saʿd eats hyenas, and Ibn ʿUmar ؓ did not disapprove of that."],[3241,"ʿAṭāʾ saw no harm in eating them, saying: 'They are game.'"],[3242,"He forbade the milk of a jallālah sheep, meaning one that eats filth."],[3243,"A cow broke loose and drank wine; they feared for it and came to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: 'Eat, and there is no harm in eating it.'"],[3244,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade eating every predator with fangs and every bird with talons."],[3246,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon and mentioned a very long hadith, in which [he said]: 'Whoever feeds [others] food for ostentation and reputation, Allah Almighty will feed him from the pus of Hell, and that food will be fire in his belly until judgment is passed among people.'"],[3247,"There was a man from Banū Rabāḥ called Ibn Uthāl, a poet, who came with al-Farazdaq to water at the outskirts of Kufa, on condition that this one would hamstring a hundred camels and this one a hundred camels when they came to the water. When they came, they attacked them with swords, cutting their hocks. The people went out on donkeys and mules seeking the meat, while ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ was in Kufa. He went out on the white mule of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, calling: 'O people, do not eat their meat, for it has been consecrated to other than Allah Almighty.'"],[3250,"I love to go out with this staff of mine to the mountains and hunt wild animals with it."],[3252,"I took my bow and hunted birds; some I caught while still alive and some I did not. I met Ibn Masʿūd, Zayd b. Thābit, and Ḥudhayfah b. al-Yamān ؓ, and I began separating the properly slaughtered ones. They said: 'What is this?' I said: 'These are those I caught alive, and these are those I did not.' They mixed them all together and said: 'We heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Eat whatever your bow returns to you.'"],[3253,"When a man sends his hunting animal and then mentions the name of Allah Almighty, let him eat [the game] as long as it has not eaten [from it]."],[3254,"About the prey of the goshawk and the falcon: if they eat from it, then eat it."],[3255,"About the goshawk and the falcon: if they eat from it, then eat, for it only teaches it by its eating."],[3256,"The eagle, the falcon, and the goshawk are among the birds of prey."],[3257,"I asked ʿAṭāʾ about the miʿrāḍ that strikes with its broad side. He said: If you strike with its broad side, then whatever it hits, eat it."],[3259,"I set up snares at al-Abwāʾ, and a bird fell into one of the snares but escaped, so I went out after it and found a man who had taken it. We disputed over it and raced together to the Messenger of God ﷺ. We found him taking a midday nap at al-Abwāʾ under a tree, shading himself with a leather mat. We brought our dispute to him, and he divided it between us into two halves."],[3261,"Everything in the sea is slaughtered. He said: I mentioned that to ʿAṭāʾ, who said: As for birds, I think you should slaughter them."],[3262,"Every creature in the sea has been slaughtered by God, Exalted is He, for you, so eat it."],[3263,"Every creature among the creatures of the sea and the land that does not have blood that flows does not require ritual slaughter."],[3266,"ʿAlī ؓ entered upon Umm Hāniʾ ؓ at midday and she said: Present some food to Abū al-Ḥasan. She said: So I presented what was in the house. ʿAlī ؓ said: Why do I not see any blessing with you? Umm Hāniʾ ؓ said: Is this not a blessing? He said: I do not mean this. Do you not have a sheep? I said: No, by God, we do not have a sheep."],[3268,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ in which our provisions ran out, and there was no food for us to eat except locusts until we returned from our expedition."],[3269,"We sent to Abū Hurayrah ؓ to ask him about locusts—he was sleeping—and his family said: He sees us eating them, and he neither eats them nor forbids us."],[3270,"Abu Sa'id ؓ would see us eating locusts and would not command us or forbid us, and we did not know what prevented him - out of disgust or dislike."],[3271,"Umar ؓ used to strike for the two rakʿahs after ʿAsr."],[3272,"I saw 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ smacking his lips. I said, 'What is the matter with you, O Commander of the Believers?' He said, 'I crave fried locusts.'"],[3273,"Locusts became scarce in one of the years in which 'Umar ؓ governed. He asked about them and was not informed of anything, so he grieved over that. He sent a rider to Yemen, a rider to Syria, and a rider to Iraq, asking whether any locusts had been seen or not. The rider from Yemen came to him with a handful of locusts and threw them before him. When he saw them, he said 'Allahu Akbar' three times, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, created a thousand nations, six hundred of them in the sea and four hundred on land. The first thing to perish from these nations is the locust. When they perish, the rest will follow in succession like a string of beads when its thread is cut.'"],[3275,"A cow of ours became wild. A man went out and struck it below the neck and above the shoulder blade. It fell down dead. The Prophet ﷺ was asked, and he said: 'A domesticated cow, when it becomes like a wild animal, is made lawful by what makes a wild animal lawful.'"],[3276,"We bought a cow during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to share in its meat. It broke loose from us and became difficult to control. A freed slave of ours called Dhakwan confronted it with a sword in his hand while it was running about on the hard ground. It headed toward a hill, and when it passed by him, he struck it with the sword at the base of its neck or on its shoulder, piercing it with the sword, and it fell. We did not manage to slaughter it properly. I went out with 'Abd Allah b. Thabit b. al-Jidh' and we met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We mentioned its situation to him, and he said: 'Eat it. If any of these animals escapes you, restrain it with what you restrain a wild animal.'"],[3278,"'A'ishah ؓ kept seeing a snake in her house, so she ordered it to be killed. She was approached in a dream and told: 'Why did you kill 'Abd Allah the Muslim?' She said: 'If he had been a Muslim, he would not have looked upon the wives of the Prophet ﷺ without permission.' It was said to her: 'But you knew that he would only look when you had gathered your clothes around you.' When morning came, she gave twelve thousand (dirhams) in charity."],[3279,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about killing snakes. He said: 'Man and snake were created alike. If he sees it, it frightens him; if it bites him, it hurts him. So kill it wherever you find it.'"],[3280,"The snake is the most wicked of the wicked, so kill it."],[3282,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'When you see a lion, say Allahu Akbar three times, saying: Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, mightier than everything and greater. I seek refuge with Allah from the evil of what I fear and am wary of. You will be protected from its evil, if Allah Almighty wills. And if a dog barks at you, say: O assembly of jinn and mankind, if you are able...'"],[3284,"Do not disturb birds in their nests at night, for the night is a protection for them."],[3287,"Whoever is concerned about the hunger of his Muslim brother and feeds him until he is satisfied, and gives him drink until he is quenched, Allah will forgive him."],[3288,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us, so I brought him food. Some of those present withdrew, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \"What is the matter with them?\" He said: \"They are fasting.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no Muslim in whose presence food is eaten but that the angels send blessings upon him.\""],[3291,"Qays b. ʿĀṣim bequeathed to his sons at the time of his death, saying: \"I enjoin upon you the fear of Allah Almighty. Give leadership to your eldest, for when a people give leadership to their eldest, they succeed their fathers; but when they give leadership to their youngest, they are belittled among their peers. I also enjoin you to acquire wealth, for it is a means of honor for the generous and a means of being dispensed from the ignoble. And beware of begging.\""],[3293,"If a guest spends the night deprived, then it is a right upon the Muslims to support him until they take his hospitality from his crops or his livestock."],[3294,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we come across camels that have milk and are left unmilked, and we are in need.\" He ﷺ said: \"Call out 'O owner of the camels' three times. If he comes, then (ask him); otherwise, untie their udder straps and drink, then tie them again and leave some milk for the next milking.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, advise me.\" He ﷺ said: \"Establish prayer, give zakah, fast Ramadan, perform Hajj to the House, perform ʿUmrah, be dutiful to your parents, maintain ties of kinship, honor the guest, enjoin good, forbid evil, and move with the truth wherever it moves.\" He said: I then said: \"O Messenger of Allah, lost animals come to us; is there any reward for us if we give them water?\" He ﷺ said: \"Yes, in every living being with a thirsty liver there is a reward.\""],[3296,"The guest has a right upon his host for three (days); whatever is more is charity. The guest should depart and not cause pain to the people of the house where he stays."],[3297,"Some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled and ran out of provisions. They passed by a Bedouin tribe and asked them for hospitality, but they refused. Then they asked to buy from them, but they refused. So they seized them and took some of their food. The Bedouins went to ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ complaining about them, and the Anṣār became worried. ʿUmar ؓ said: \"Do you deny the wayfarer what Allah creates night and day in the udders of camels and sheep? The wayfarer has more right to the water than the one who builds a structure over it.\""],[3299,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"When you eat, begin with salt and end with salt, for salt is a cure for seventy diseases, the first of which are insanity, leprosy, vitiligo, toothache, sore throat, and stomach pain.\""],[3300,"Whoever eats any of these meats should wash his hand from its smell and harm, and not annoy the person next to him."],[3301,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade peeling a fresh date."],[3302,"He used to say when he finished his food: “Praise be to Allah who fed us and gave us drink, and praise be to Allah who sufficed us and sheltered us, and praise be to Allah who bestowed favor upon us and was bountiful. We ask Him by His mercy to protect us from the Fire, for many a one who is not sufficed finds no place to turn and no shelter.”"],[3303,"Whoever eats until he is full and drinks until he is quenched and then says: “Praise be to Allah who fed me and satisfied me, and gave me drink and quenched me,” will emerge from his sins like the day his mother gave birth to him."],[3304,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never ate reclining except once, then he sat up and said: “I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger.”"],[3305,"I was the guide of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from al-ʿArj to Madinah, and I saw him eating reclining."],[3306,"As for me, I do not eat reclining."],[3307,"Let food cool, for hot food has no blessing."],[3308,"He was asked: Which food is most unlawful or most foul? He said: That you eat from your camel while it looks at you."],[3309,"He was brought khabis in a bowl of silver or gold, so he ordered it to be transferred onto a flat loaf, then he ate from it."],[3310,"The most beloved food to Allah [Exalted is He] is that over which many hands gather."],[3311,"When you eat food, remove your sandals, for it is more relaxing for your feet."],[3312,"When food is brought close to one of you while he has two sandals on his feet, let him remove his sandals, for that is more relaxing for the feet and it is part of the Sunnah."],[3313,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to eat standing and sitting."],[3314,"'Umar ؓ went to relieve himself, then came out, and food was brought to him. It was said to him, 'Will you not perform ablution?' He said, 'I only clean myself with my left hand and eat with my right hand.'"],[3315,"When he wanted to eat, he would wash his hands."],[3316,"The Prophet ﷺ came out from the privy and ate. It was said to him, 'Will you not perform ablution?' He said, 'Do I intend to pray that I should perform ablution?'"],[3317,"Whoever forgets to mention the name of Allah, the Exalted, at the beginning of his meal, let him say when he remembers: 'In the name of Allah, at its beginning and its end,' for he will then start his meal anew and the evil that would have afflicted him from it will be prevented."],[3318,"A dish of watba (a kind of food) was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and a Bedouin took it with three morsels. He ﷺ said, 'Indeed, had he said: In the name of Allah, it would have sufficed them all.' And he said: 'When one of you forgets the name of Allah upon his food, let him say when he remembers: In the name of Allah, at its beginning and its end.'"],[3319,"I prepared a khazira (a type of thick soup) for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he came with two men, so I brought it near to them. A Bedouin passed by, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ invited him to the food, and he took it with one morsel. He ﷺ said: 'Put it down, and mention the name of Allah, the Exalted, and eat.' He said: So he ate until he was full, and there was still some left over."],[3320,"She made a khazira for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and brought it to him. He ate from it along with some of his companions, and some of it remained. A Bedouin passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ invited him. The Bedouin took all of it in his hand, so the Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Put it down.' He put it down. Then he said to him: 'Say: In the name of Allah, and take from what is nearest to you.' She said: So he ate until he was full, and there was still some left over."],[3321,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade eating while standing."],[3323,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ate vinegar made from khamr."],[3325,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a piece of cheese, and it was said, \"This is a food that the Magians make.\" He ﷺ said, \"Mention the name of God over it and eat.\""],[3326,"He saw no harm in eating cheese."],[3327,"There is no harm in the cheese of the Magians."],[3329,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, \"O ʿAlī, eat olive oil and anoint yourself with olive oil, for whoever anoints himself with olive oil, Satan will not come near him for forty nights.\""],[3330,"I heard ʿĀʾishah ؓ say, when olive oil was mentioned in her presence, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command that it be eaten and used for anointing, and he would say, 'It is a blessed tree.'\""],[3332,"He used to eat melon with ripe dates, and he would say, \"Both are good.\""],[3333,"Honor your paternal aunt, the palm tree, for it was created from the clay from which Adam was created, and there is no tree other than it that is pollinated."],[3335,"Eat chicory and do not detest it, for there is not a day but a drop from Paradise falls upon it."],[3337,"ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān ؓ made khabīṣ with honey, clarified butter, and wheat, and he brought it in a large bowl to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said, \"What is this?\" He said, \"This, O Prophet of God, is something the Persians make from wheat, honey, and clarified butter; they call it khabīṣ.\" He said, \"So he ate.\""],[3339,"A man prepared food for the Prophet ﷺ and invited him. He said, \"Will you permit me to bring Saʿd?\" So he gave him permission. Then he prepared food and said, \"Will you permit me to bring Saʿd?\" [So he gave him permission. Then he prepared food and said, \"Will you permit Saʿd?\"], for he is your companion."],[3341,"When one of you is invited, let him respond, even if he is fasting."],[3343,"A man prepared [food] and invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions. A man said: 'I am fasting.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Your brother has prepared food and invited you; break your fast and make up [a day] in its place.'"],[3344,"Eating in the markets is a disgrace."],[3346,"He entered the lavatory and found a morsel or a piece of bread in the channel for feces and urine. He took it, removed the filth from it, washed it thoroughly, and then handed it to his servant, saying: 'O boy, remind me of it when I perform ablution.' When he performed ablution, he said: 'Hand me the morsel'—or he said: 'the piece of bread.' The boy said: 'O my master, I ate it.' He said: 'Go, for you are free for the sake of Allah.' The boy said to him: 'O my master, why did you set me free?' He said: 'Because I heard my mother Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, mention from her father, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said: \"Whoever finds a morsel or a piece of bread in the channel for feces or urine, takes it, removes the filth from it, washes it thoroughly, then eats it—it will not settle in his stomach until he is forgiven.\" So I would not employ a man from the people of Paradise.'"],[3347,"A woman asked the Prophet ﷺ."],[3348,"Make use of the sheep, for it is but a drink provided by Allah Almighty. When you milk them, do not exhaust them, and leave the milk that draws [the young]."],[3349,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, camels pass by us while we are in drought, and they have full udders.' He ﷺ said: 'Milk and drink, and leave what draws the young.'"],[3350,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would avoid drinking from a cracked vessel."],[3351,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking from a vessel with a broken edge."],[3352,"My uncle sent me to the Ansar to collect a debt from a man among them. A man among them brought a drink in a vessel, and one of them blew into it. The other said: 'Do not do that, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid it.'"],[3353,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drinking one day, and he drank in three breaths. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you drank water in three breaths?' He ﷺ said: 'Yes, it is more quenching, more wholesome, and more healthful.'"],[3354,"He forbade a man from drinking from the mouth of a waterskin."],[3355,"\"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited blowing into the drink.\" He said: \"And he saw a man blowing into the drink, then he drank while standing, so he said: 'If you can vomit it, then vomit it.'\""],[3357,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that will admit me into Paradise.' He ﷺ said: 'Speak justice and give surplus.' He said: 'What if I cannot do that?' He ﷺ said: 'Then feed food and spread peace.' He said: 'What if I cannot do that or am unable to do that?' He ﷺ said: 'Do you have any camels?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then look for a camel from your camels and a waterskin, and look for a household that does not drink water except every other day, and give them water to drink. For perhaps your camel will not perish and your waterskin will not tear until Paradise becomes due for you.'"],[3359,"Whoever withholds surplus water, Allah will withhold His surplus from him on the Day of Resurrection."],[3360,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ during a famine or distress that had befallen the people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: 'Distribute them among yourselves.' So a man would take the hand of one man, and a man would take the hands of two men. The people were avoiding me because of what they saw of my height and size, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took my hand and took me to his house. He milked a sheep, and I drank its milk. Then he milked another, and I drank its milk, until he had milked seven for me. He said: So I left. Then when the next day came, I embraced Islam. Then I came, and he milked a single sheep for me, and I was full and quenched. I said: 'By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I have never been full or quenched before today.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The believer drinks in one intestine, and the disbeliever in seven intestines.'"],[3361,"He came with a group of his people wanting to embrace Islam. They attended the Maghrib prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he said the salam, he said: 'Each man should take the hand of his companion.' No one remained in the mosque except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and me. I was a tall man, no one could be put before me. The Messenger of Allah took me to his house and milked a goat for me, and I finished it [until he had milked seven goats for me and I finished them all]. Then a pot dish was brought to me and I finished it. Umm Ayman ؓ said: 'May Allah starve the one who starved the Messenger of Allah ﷺ this night.' He ﷺ said: 'Enough, O Umm Ayman. He ate his provision, and our provision is upon Allah, the Exalted.' Then the next morning they sat down, and he gathered with his companions, and each man began to tell about those they had gone with. Jahjah said: 'Seven goats were milked for me and I finished them all, and a pot was made and I finished it all.' Then they prayed the Maghrib prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Each of you should take the hand of his companion.' No one remained in the mosque except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and me. I was big and tall, no one could be put before me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me to his house and milked a goat for me, and I was quenched and full. Umm Ayman ؓ said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is this not our guest?' He said: 'Yes.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, he ate tonight in the intestine of a believer, and before that he ate in the intestine of a disbeliever. The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the believer eats in one intestine.'"],[3364,"O people, seek treatment, for Allah the Exalted did not create any disease but that He created for it a cure, except old age."],[3366,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Umm Salamah ؓ, and with her was a boy whose nostrils were gushing blood. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'What is this?' They said: 'He has the 'udhrah (inflammation of the throat/tonsils).' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Why do you torment your children? It is enough for one of you to take Indian costus, rub it with water seven times, and then pour it into his mouth.' He said: So they did that, and he recovered."],[3369,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'O 'Ali, do not face the sun, for facing it is a disease, and having it behind you is a cure.'"],[3371,"Whichever of you is afflicted with fever, let him pour a jar of cold water over himself."],[3372,"When one of you has a fever, let him sprinkle cold water on himself for three nights at the time of dawn."],[3374,"In talbinah there is healing from every disease."],[3376,"Dye with henna, for it is pleasant in fragrance and calms dizziness."],[3378,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by purslane while he had a sore on his leg, and he treated it with it and it healed. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: “May Allah bless you. Grow wherever you wish, for you are a healing from seventy diseases, the least of which is headache.”"],[3380,"Fumigate your houses with frankincense, myrrh, and thyme."],[3382,"I entered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while his hand was in mine. He came upon a man of shabby appearance and said: “O Abu so-and-so, what has brought you to the state I see?” He said: “Sickness and harm, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Shall I not teach you some words by which Allah may remove from you sickness and harm?” He said: “No, it would not please me to have them even if I had been present with you at Badr and Uhud.” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed, then said: “Would the people of Badr and the people of Uhud attain what the contented poor person attains?” Abu Hurayrah ؓ said: I said, “Teach me, O Messenger of Allah.” He ﷺ said: “Say, O Abu Hurayrah: ‘I have put my trust in the Ever-Living who does not die. Praise be to Allah who has not taken a son, and who has no partner in dominion’—the verse. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon me after my condition had improved and said: ‘Mahyam?’ I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, I have not ceased saying the words you taught me.’”"],[3384,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gargled with sesame oil."],[3386,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he smiled. We said: “O Messenger of Allah, what made you smile?” He said: “I marvel at the believer and his distress at illness. If he knew what he has in illness, he would love to remain ill until he meets his Lord.” Then he smiled a second time, raised his head to the sky, and looked at it. They said: “What made you smile, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “I marvel at two angels who descended from the sky seeking a believer in his prayer place where he used to pray, but they did not find him. They ascended to Allah Almighty and said: ‘O Lord, Your servant so-and-so, we used to record for him such-and-such deeds every day, but You have detained him in Your bonds,’ meaning illness. Allah Almighty said to them: ‘Record for My servant the like of what he used to do every day and night, and do not reduce anything from it. He shall have the reward of what he did in addition to the reward for what I have detained him with.’”"],[3387,"“I marvel at the believer and his distress at illness. If he knew what he has in illness, he would love to remain ill until he meets his Lord.” Then he smiled a second time, raised his head to the sky, and looked at it. They said: “What made you smile, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “I marvel at two angels who descended from the sky seeking a believer in his prayer place where he used to pray, but they did not find him. They ascended to Allah Almighty and said: ‘O Lord, Your servant so-and-so, we used to record for him such-and-such deeds every day, but You have detained him in Your bonds,’ meaning illness. Allah Almighty said to them: ‘Record for My servant the like of what he used to do every day and night, and do not reduce anything from it. He shall have the reward of what he did in addition to the reward for what I have detained him with.’”"],[3388,"A man may have a rank with Allah Almighty that he does not attain by deeds until he is afflicted in his body, and thus he attains it through that affliction."],[3389,"Abu Bakr said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, and he added between Jabalah and Ibn Mas'ud: from someone who informed him."],[3390,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell ill and it became severe for him. When he recovered, I said: “If any one of us did this, I would fear for her.” He ﷺ said: “Do you not know that the believer is afflicted severely in his pain so that his sins may be removed from him?”"],[3391,"He went to the mosque of Damascus in the afternoon to perform the noon prayer early, and he met Shaddad b. Aws and another man with him. He said: “Where do you two intend, may Allah have mercy on you?” They said: “We intend to go here to a sick brother of ours to visit him.” He said: He went with them until they entered upon that man. They said to him: “How are you this morning?” He said: “I have entered the morning in the blessing of Allah and His grace.” He said: Shaddad said to him: “Rejoice in the expiations of sins and the removal of errors, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: When I afflict a believing servant of Mine and he praises Me for what I have afflicted him with, then he rises from his bed that day like the day his mother gave birth to him, free from sins. And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: I have bound this servant of Mine and afflicted him, so record for him what you used to record for him while he was healthy.’”"],[3392,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a tree and shook it until as much of its leaves fell as Allah willed to fall. Then he ﷺ said: \"Pains and calamities are faster in removing the sins of the son of Adam than I am in [removing the leaves from] this tree.\""],[3395,"\"The example of the believer is like that of a grain stalk: it bends at times and stands upright at times.\""],[3396,"\"A man may have a station with Allah Most High that he does not attain through any deed. He remains afflicted with what he dislikes until He causes him to attain it.\""],[3397,"Abu Ya'la said: 'Uqbah b. Mukram narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us with this [wording]. Ibn Hibban considered it sound."],[3398,"\"There is no Muslim who is afflicted with a calamity, and then remembers his calamity after forty years and renews his istirja' (saying 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return'), except that Allah gives him at that moment the like of the reward he was given on the day he was afflicted.\""],[3399,"Abu Hurayrah ؓ entered upon me while I was sick and overcome. He said: \"Did your companion pray?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"I have been informed that there is no servant who complains of illness except that Allah Most High writes for him [the reward of] what he used to do when healthy, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, takes his soul or restores him.\""],[3400,"\"There is no servant who becomes ill with an illness except that Allah commands his two guardian angels: 'Whatever evil deed he performs, do not write it down; and whatever good deed he performs, write it as ten good deeds. And write for him [the reward of] the deeds he used to do when he was healthy, even if he does not perform them.'\""],[3402,"\"It used to be said: A man's affliction in his eyesight is like his affliction in his own self.\""],[3403,"\"When I take the two precious ones of My servant, I will not be satisfied with any reward for him less than Paradise.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, even if it is one?\" He ﷺ said: \"Even if it is one.\""],[3404,"When I take the two precious ones of My servant and he remains patient and seeks reward, I will not be satisfied with any reward for him less than Paradise."],[3405,"When I take from My servant his two precious ones, while he is deeply attached to them, I will not be satisfied with any reward for them less than Paradise, if he praises Me for them."],[3407,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting, he said: \"Which of you would love never to fall ill?\" We hurried to answer, saying: \"We would, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"Would you love to be like braying donkeys?\" The Prophet ﷺ changed color until we saw the change in his face. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Would you not love to be people of trial and expiations?\" They said: \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" He ﷺ said: \"By Him in whose hand is my soul, the believer is surely tried with affliction, and that is a mark of honor for him with God Most High. He is surely tried with affliction until he attains thereby a station with God Most High that he would not attain without being tried with it, and God Most High brings him to that station.\""],[3408,"A woman came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, I have a daughter who is such and such” – she mentioned her beauty and comeliness – “and I would give her to you in marriage.” He ﷺ said: “I have accepted her.” She kept praising her until she mentioned that she had never had a headache or any complaint. He said: “I have no need of your daughter.”"],[3409,"A hefty bedouin, a man of large build, came to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “When did you last have a fever?” He said: “I do not know what it is.” He ﷺ said: “And a headache?” He said: “I do not know what it is.” He ﷺ said: “Have you ever been afflicted in your wealth?” He said: “No.” He ﷺ said: “Have you ever lost a child?” He said: “No.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “God detests the obstinate, ill-tempered man who is not bereaved of a child and not afflicted in his wealth.”"],[3411,"“Part of perfect piety is concealing afflictions.”"],[3413,"'Amr b. Hurayth visited al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ. 'Ali ؓ said to him: “Do you visit al-Hasan while your heart holds what it holds?” 'Amr said: “You are not my Lord to turn my heart wherever you wish.” He said: “That does not prevent us from giving you sincere advice. I heard the Messenger ﷺ say: ‘No Muslim visits his brother but God Most High sends seventy thousand angels for him.’”"],[3414,"“When a man goes out intending to visit a believing brother, he wades in mercy up to his waist. When he sits by the sick person and settles down, mercy overwhelms him.”"],[3415,"“Whoever combines fasting on Friday, visiting a sick person, attending a funeral, and freeing a slave, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.”"],[3416,"“Whoever visits a sick person continues to wade in mercy until, when he sits down, he is immersed in it.” 'Abd added: “Then, when he returns, he continues to wade in it until he comes back to where he started.”"],[3417,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us and mentioned the hadith at length, and in it: “Whoever visits a sick person, for every step he takes until he returns to his home, he gets seventy thousand good deeds, the erasure of seventy thousand bad deeds, and the raising of seventy thousand degrees. Seventy thousand angels are appointed for him, visiting him and seeking forgiveness for him until the Day of Resurrection. Whoever tends a sick person for a day and a night, God Most High will raise him with His intimate friend Ibrahim ﷺ until he crosses the Sirat like flashing lightning. Whoever strives to fulfill a sick person’s need comes out of his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him.” A man from the Ansar said: “What if the sick person is his relative or one of his family?” He said: “Who has a greater reward than one who strives to meet his family’s need?”"],[3418,"“Consider how long the visitors stay with the sick person.” He said: “They say: ‘Any Lord, even for a brief moment—if it is a brief moment—’ He says to His angels: ‘Record for My servant the worship of a thousand years.’ And if they stay for an hour, He says: ‘Record for him a dahr (a long period).’ And a dahr is ten thousand years. If he dies before that, he enters Paradise; and if he lives, no single sin is written against him. If it is morning, seventy thousand angels pray over him until evening, and he is in the garden’s harvesting. If it is evening, seventy thousand angels pray over him until morning, and he is in the garden’s harvesting. In the Dar al-‘Asimah edition: (harb), and what is established is from Musnad Abu Ya‘la and Itḥāf al-Buṣayrī. In the Dar al-‘Asimah edition: (iḥtasabū), and what is established is from Musnad Abu Ya‘la and Itḥāf al-Buṣayrī.”"],[3419,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went to a man to visit him, and he mentioned it... and he added: “He said it, and he was healed.”"],[3421,"‘Umar wrote to his governors in Syria: “When you hear that the epidemic has been lifted, write to me.” I came while he was sleeping, and that was after his return from Sargh, and I heard him when he got up from his sleep say: “O God, forgive me for returning here from Sargh.”"],[3422,"She heard the Messenger of God ﷺ advising some of his family, and he said: “If death afflicts the people while you are among them, remain steadfast.”"],[3424,"“O Messenger of God, a land of ours called Abyan is the land of our provisions and our countryside, but it is pestilential.” He ﷺ said: “Leave it, for proximity to disease leads to ruin.”"],[3426,"“There is no ruqyah except for that about which Solomon took a covenant from it.”"],[3427,"I complained of an ailment, so they carried me to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He spent the night reciting the Qur’an over me and blowing on me with it."],[3428,"When he complained of pain, he would blow into his hands and then pass them over his face."],[3429,"“These words are a cure for every disease: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God, and all His names in general, from the evil of poisonous and noxious creatures, from the evil of the evil eye, from the evil of the envier when he envies, and from the evil of Ibn Qitrah and what he begat. Thirty-three of the angels came to their Lord and said: ‘There is a plague in our land.’ The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘Take from the dust of your land and wipe your foreheads with it. It is the ruqyah of Muhammad. Whoever takes a bribe for it or conceals it from anyone will never succeed.’” Type: Marfū‘."],[3430,"He recited into the ear of an afflicted person, and he regained consciousness. The Messenger of God ﷺ asked him: “What did you recite into his ear?” He said: “I recited: ‘Did you think that We created you in vain…’ until the end of the surah.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If a man with certainty recited it over a mountain, it would move.”"],[3431,"I used to perform ruqyah in the Jahiliyyah for the fever of gib (a type of fever). When Islam came, I mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: \"Present it to me.\" He ﷺ then said: \"Perform ruqyah with it; there is no harm in it.\" By God, were it not for that, I would never have performed ruqyah with it on any person ever."],[3432,"Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf ؓ visited a sick man among the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ. They said—he mentioned some words—and he said: \"Do not say that. Rather, say as the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say when he visited a sick person: 'O God, remove from him what he finds, and reward him in what You have tried him with.'\""],[3433,"I fell ill, and the Messenger of God ﷺ used to seek protection for me. One day he sought protection for me and said: \"In the name of God, the Merciful, the Compassionate. I seek protection for you with God, the One, the Eternal, who did not beget and was not begotten, and none is equal to Him, from the evil of what you find.\" When the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up to leave, he said: \"O 'Uthman, seek protection with it, for you have never sought protection with anything like it.\""],[3435,"\"Most of those who die from my community, after the decree of God, His book, and His predestination, die from the evil eye.\""],[3436,"One day I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, and there was a pot boiling with meat. A piece of fat appealed to me, so I took it and swallowed it, and I suffered from it for a year. Then I mentioned it to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: \"There were in it the souls of seven people.\" Then he ﷺ wiped my belly, and I threw it up green. By the One who sent him with the truth, my belly has not hurt me until this moment."],[3438,"\"There is no contagion and no bad omen. Who infected the first one?\""],[3439,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by 'Usfan, and there was a leper, so he quickened his pace and said: \"If any disease were contagious, it would be this one.\""],[3440,"\"There is no contagion, no bad omen, no Safar, and no Haamah.\""],[3441,"\"There is no contagion and no Haamah, and a sick person does not infect a healthy one.\""],[3442,"While 'Umayr b. Sa'd was among a group of people from Palestine—and he was called 'Naseej Wahdih' (unique in his kind)—we sat on a large bench in his house. He said to his servant: \"Boy, bring the horses to water.\" In the house there was a stone trough. He brought them to water. Then he said: \"Where is so-and-so?\" He said: \"She is mangy, dripping blood,\" or he said \"water\"—Ibrahim was unsure. He said: \"Bring her to water.\" One of the people said: \"Then all the camels will get mange.\" He said: \"Bring her to water, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'There is no contagion, no bad omen, and no Haamah. Do you not see the camel that is in the desert and then a spot appears on its chest or flanks that was not there before? Who infected the first one?'\""],[3443,"Superstition does not harm except the one who is superstitious."],[3444,"Indeed, superstition is only what turns you back or makes you proceed."],[3445,"He is not of us who practices magic or has it practiced for him, or is superstitious or has superstition for him, or practices divination or has it practiced for him."],[3446,"He is not of us who practices magic or has it practiced for him, or is superstitious or has superstition for him, or practices divination or has it practiced for him."],[3447,"I brought a young boy to 'A'ishah so that she might supplicate for him. They lifted a pillow on which the boy was, and 'A'ishah ؓ saw a razor beneath it. She said, \"What is this?\" He said, \"We place it as protection from the jinn and fright.\" He said, \"So 'A'ishah ؓ took it and threw it away, saying, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to hate superstition and dislike it.'\""],[3449,"The growth of hair in the nose is a protection from leprosy."],[3451,"We entered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon a man from the Ansar who had a swelling. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Why do you not lance it for him?\" He said, \"So it was lanced while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was witnessing.\""],[3453,"\"O people, where are you being taken? Do you give your children wine to drink? Indeed, your children were born upon the natural disposition, and Allah has not placed your cure in what He has forbidden for you.\""],[3454,"A daughter of mine complained of illness, so I steeped something for her in a brass vessel. The Prophet ﷺ entered while it was boiling and said, \"What is this?\" I said, \"My daughter is ill, so I steeped this for her.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has not placed your cure in what is unlawful.\""],[3456,"Whoever goes to a fortune-teller, a sorcerer, or a soothsayer and asks him and believes what he says has disbelieved in what was sent down upon Muhammad ﷺ."],[3459,"Whoever goes to a soothsayer and believes what he says has disbelieved in what was sent down upon Muhammad ﷺ."],[3460,"Indeed, the fortune-tellers are the soothsayers of the non-Arabs. Whoever believes in a soothsayer has disbelieved in what was sent down upon Muhammad ﷺ."],[3461,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ twice... And he mentioned the hadith. He said: We came in a caravan from al-Rabadhah until we disembarked near Madinah, and with us was our lady companion. He said: While we were sitting, a man came to us wearing two white garments. He greeted us and we returned his greeting. He said: From where have the people come? We said: From al-Rabadhah, and south of al-Rabadhah. He said: And with us was a red camel. He said: Will you sell me the camel? We said: Yes. He said: For how much? We said: For such-and-such sa's of dates. He said: He did not reduce anything for us, and said: I have taken it. Then he took hold of the camel's head until he entered Madinah and disappeared from us. We blamed each other, saying: You gave your camel to a man you do not know! The lady companion said: Do not blame yourselves, for I have seen a face that would never betray you. I have never seen a man whose face more resembled the full moon on the night of Badr than his face. When the evening came, a man came and said: Peace be upon you. Indeed I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to you, and he commands you to eat until you are full, and to take full measure until you receive your due. So we ate until we were full, and took full measure until we received our due. When the next day came, we entered Madinah, and behold the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing on the pulpit delivering a sermon to the people."],[3463,"A man among us complained of a severe illness, and the physicians said: 'He will not recover except by cauterization.' His family wanted to cauterize him, but some of them said: 'No, until we consult the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' So they consulted him, and he said: 'No.' Then the man recovered. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him, he said: 'Is this the companion of Banu so-and-so?' They said: 'Yes.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, if this man had been cauterized, people would have said: It was only the cauterization that cured him.'"],[3464,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ with a son of hers whose belly was swollen with water. She said: 'O Messenger of Allah, my son has been afflicted with what you see; should I cauterize him?' He ﷺ said: 'Do not cauterize your son.' She resolved not to cauterize him. Then a camel stumbled over him and struck him, or kicked him, and burst his belly, and he recovered. She returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah. I asked your permission to cauterize my son, and you forbade me. Then a camel passed by him and struck him, or kicked him, and burst his belly, and he recovered.' He ﷺ said: 'Indeed, had I given you permission, you would have claimed that it was the fire that cured him.'"],[3465,"'Umar ؓ made me swear that I would certainly be cauterized."],[3466,"If there is healing in anything with which you treat yourselves, it is in the incision of a cupper, or a drink of honey, or a cauterization with fire that causes pain, but I do not like to be cauterized."],[3467,"I entered with 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud ؓ upon Khabbab ؓ, and he had been cauterized. He said: 'O Abu 'Abdullah, do you not know that we have been forbidden from this and it is disliked for us?' Khabbab ؓ said: 'The affliction became severe, and the physicians said: There is no remedy for you except this.' 'Abdullah said: 'I was not afraid that you would do this.'"],[3469,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped and gave the cupper his wages."],[3470,"When I was taken up to the heaven, I did not pass by a group of angels except that they said: 'O Muhammad, you should practice cupping.'"],[3471,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about cupping, and he said: 'It is good.'"],[3472,"When one of you has a surge of blood, let him shed it, even with a sharp arrowhead."],[3473,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped in the middle of his head, and he called it al-Munqidh (the deliverer)."],[3474,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had himself cupped on his horn after he was poisoned."],[3475,"I heard Muhammad b. Sirin say to a servant who wanted to be cupped at the beginning of the month: 'Do not get cupped at the beginning of the month, for cupping at the beginning of the month is of no benefit.'"],[3476,"In the day of Friday there is an hour in which no one gets cupped except that he dies."],[3477,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped while he was in ihram for a pain he felt in his head."],[3480,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was among a group of his companions. He said: I said: 'Are you the one who claims that you are the Messenger of God?' He ﷺ said: 'Yes.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, which deeds are most beloved to God?' He ﷺ said: 'Faith in God.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, then what?' He ﷺ said: 'Then maintaining family ties.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, which deeds are most hateful to God, exalted be He?' He ﷺ said: 'Associating partners with God.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, then what?' He said: 'Severing family ties.' He said: I said: 'O Messenger of God, then what?' He ﷺ said: 'Commanding evil and forbidding good.'"],[3481,"I was with Ibn Abbas ؓ when a man came to him and asked him: 'Who are you?' He claimed a distant kinship to him, so he softened his speech to him and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Know your lineages so that you may maintain your family ties; for there is no nearness for the womb when it is severed, even if it is close, and no distance for it when it is maintained, even if it is distant.'"],[3483,"Angels do not descend upon a people among whom there is a severer of family ties."],[3484,"Mercy does not descend upon a people among whom there is a severer of family ties. A man from among his companions said: 'O Messenger of God, I have a maternal aunt whom I do not speak to.' He ﷺ said: 'Go to her and speak to her.'"],[3485,"Moisten your family ties, even with the greeting of peace."],[3486,"The womb is a branch from the Merciful, holding onto His waist, pleading for its right. He says: 'Are you not content that I maintain ties with whoever maintains you and sever ties with whoever severs you? Whoever maintains you has maintained Me, and whoever severs you has severed Me.'"],[3487,"The womb is a branch from Me. Whoever maintains it, I maintain him, and whoever severs it, I sever him."],[3489,"God, Mighty and Majestic, indeed supports this religion with the wicked man."],[3490,"He gathered them at their anchorage during their naval expedition, on the ship of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari ؓ. He said: When our lunch was ready, we sent for Abu Ayyub al-Ansari ؓ and the people of his ship. Abu Ayyub came to us and said: 'You invited me while I am fasting, and it was incumbent upon me to answer you. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"A Muslim has six obligatory rights over a Muslim. Whoever abandons any of them has abandoned an obligatory right for his brother: to answer him when he invites him, to greet him when he meets him, to bless him when he sneezes, to visit him when he is ill, to follow his funeral when he dies, and to counsel him when he seeks counsel.\"'"],[3491,"And there was among us a humorous man, and a man who supervised our expenses."],[3492,"Ahmad b. Mani said: Ismail b. Ulayya narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, with it."],[3493,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go to the weak among the Muslims, visit their sick, and attend their funerals."],[3494,"Ishaq said: It was mentioned to us from Sufyan b. Husayn that he used to mention, meaning from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah, from his father ؓ , from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. I say: The route of Sufyan b. Husayn was transmitted with full chain by Abu Ya'la and al-Tabarani, and Sufyan in his narration from al-Zuhri is weak, but it is strengthened by the narration of al-Walid from al-Awza'i."],[3495,"Whoever supports his Muslim brother in his absence, Allah will support him in this world and the Hereafter. And whoever conceals the faults of his Muslim brother, Allah will conceal his faults in this world and the Hereafter."],[3497,"They used to say: The Muslim is the mirror of his brother; he shows him from himself what he does not see from himself."],[3498,"The believer is a branch of the believer. If he has a need, he should make an effort for him; he rejoices at his joy and grieves at his grief. He is the mirror of his brother; if he sees in him what he dislikes, he corrects him, straightens him, guides him, and disputes with him in private and in public."],[3499,"Ahmad b. Mani said: Ismail b. Ulayya narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, with it."],[3500,"If a man insults you and taunts you about something he knows about you, do not taunt him about something you know about him, for the bad consequence of that will be upon him and its final benefit will be yours."],[3502,"A man entered upon me at noon. I said: \"What is your need, O servant of God?\" He said: \"I and a companion of mine were searching for some camels of ours. My companion went on searching, and I entered the shade to seek shelter and drink from the drink.\" She said: \"I got up to some sour milk of ours—or perhaps she said: to some sour mixed drink—and gave him to drink from it. I examined him and said: 'O servant of God, who are you?' He said: 'Abu Bakr.' I said: 'Abu Bakr, the companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ whom I have heard of?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: \"Then I remembered our raiding Khath'am in the pre-Islamic era, and our fighting one another, and what God Almighty brought of harmony and the ropes of the tents—like this, he interlocked his fingers. I said: 'O servant of God, how long will this affair of the people be?' He said: 'As long as the leaders remain upright.' She said: I said: 'And what are the leaders?' He said: 'Have you not seen the chief who is in the encampment, whom they follow and obey? They are those as long as they remain upright.'\""],[3503,"I was with the Najadat… and he mentioned the hadith. He said: When Ibn Umar ؓ saw that I was afraid, he said: 'Do you fear entering the Fire?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Would you like to enter Paradise?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Are your parents alive?' I said: 'I have my mother.' He said: 'By Allah, if you speak softly to her and feed her food, you will surely enter Paradise, as long as you avoid the major sins.'"],[3504,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ advising some of his family, saying: \"Do not contend with the people of authority over the matter, even if you see that it is the truth.\""],[3505,"'Abd said: 'Umar b. Sa'id narrated to us, \"other than Sa'id\" narrated to us from al-Zuhri, that the one who gave this advice was Thawban ؓ."],[3506,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Zanjuyah narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated to us, Sa'id b. 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us with this. 2143/3 - And 'Abd said."],[3507,"We used to read among what was read: “Do not renounce your fathers, for that is disbelief on your part.”"],[3508,"“The prayer is being established, and my father is calling me?” He said: “Answer your father.”"],[3509,"“If your mother calls you while you are in prayer, then answer her; but if your father calls you, do not answer him until you finish.”"],[3510,"“There is no Muslim who wakes up with both parents pleased with him except that he will have two gates of Paradise; and if only one, then one. And there is no Muslim who wakes up with both parents angry with him except that he will have two gates of the Fire; and if only one, then one.”"],[3511,"I see him as a man, O Messenger of Allah, what if they wrong him? Heﷺ said: “Even if they wrong him, even if they wrong him, even if they wrong him,” three times."],[3512,"I said to Ibn ʿAbbas ؓ: “I am a man eager for jihad, and there is no one of my people except that he has joined the garrisons or the jihad, except my parents,” or he said: “except my family and my two parents,” or he said: “my father is averse to that.” He looked at me and said: “A man will not have two parents and wake up treating them well except that a gate to Paradise is opened for him, and he will not spend the evening treating them well except that two gates of the gates of Paradise are opened for him.” He said: I said: “Treating them well?” He said: “Yes. And if there is only one, and he wakes up treating him well, a gate of the gates of Paradise is opened for him, and none of them is angry with him or one of them, so he ؓ continues until he is pleased.” I said: “Even if he was wronging him?” He said: “Even if he was wronging him.”"],[3513,"He came to the Prophetﷺ and said: “My father has usurped my wealth.” He said: “You and your wealth belong to your father.”"],[3514,"“Indeed Allah, Exalted is He, increases the lifespan of a man by his dutifulness to his father.”"],[3515,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit one day. When he placed his foot on the lowest step, he said: “Amin.” Then he placed his foot ﷺ on the second, and said: “Amin.” Then he placed his foot ﷺ on the third step, and said: “Amin.” When he ﷺ finished his sermon and descended, they said: “O Messenger of Allah, you did such and such?” He ﷺ said: “Indeed Jibril ﷺ came to me when I placed my foot on the lowest step and said: ‘O Muhammad, whoever reaches his two parents or one of them and is not forgiven, then dies and enters the Fire, may Allah distance him. Say: Amin.’ I said: ‘Amin.’”"],[3517,"Abu Yaʿla said: Abu Maʿmar al-Hilali narrated to us, Hafs b. Ghiyath narrated to us, from Muhammad b. ʿAmr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah ؓ, something similar to it."],[3518,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and prayed with him. When he finished the prayer, he looked at the faces of the people; he could hardly make out their faces after the prayer was finished. When it drew near, he departed. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, advise me.”"],[3519,"Kindness to parents is an expiation for major sins, and a man continues to be able to be kind as long as there is among his clan someone older than him."],[3520,"A man said: O Messenger of God, whom should I be kind to? He said: Your mother. He said: Then whom? He said: Your mother. He said: Then whom? He said: Then your father. He said: Then whom? He said: The nearest to you. He said: Then whom? He said: The closest, then the next closest."],[3521,"Al-Hudhayl b. Hafsah used to gather firewood in the summer and strip it, and take reeds and split them. Hafsah said: I used to feel cold, and he would come with the brazier until he placed it behind me while I was praying, though he had someone who could suffice him if he wished. He would light that stripped firewood and split reeds as fuel to warm me without the heat harming me. She said: Sometimes I wanted to turn to him and say: My son, go back to your family, then I would remember what he wanted and leave him be. He used to go on military expeditions and perform Hajj. He was struck by a fever when the Hajj was near, and he recovered, and I was not aware until he had entered the state of ihram for Hajj. I said: My son, it is as if you feared that I would prevent you; I would not do so. He said: She had a milch-camel, and he used to send me a portion of milk in the morning, and I would say: My son, you know that I do not drink it while I am fasting. He would say: O mother of al-Hudhayl, the best milk is that which has spent the night in the udder of the camels; give it to drink to whomever you wish. She said: When he died, God Almighty granted me patience as He willed, except that I felt a choking grief that would not go away. While I was praying one night, reciting Surah al-Nahl, I came to this verse: \"And do not exchange the covenant of God for a small price. Indeed, what is with God is better for you, if only you knew. What is with you will perish, and what is with God will remain. And We will surely reward those who were patient with their reward according to the best of what they used to do.\" She said: I repeated it, and God removed what I had been feeling."],[3522,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, whom should I be kind to? He said: Your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, the nearest to you, the nearest to you."],[3523,"I came to Madinah, and 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar ؓ came to me and said: Do you know why I came to you? I said: No. He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever wishes to maintain ties with his father in his grave, let him maintain ties with his father's brothers after him.' And there was between my father 'Umar and your father brotherhood and affection, so I wished to maintain that."],[3524,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: I desire to fight in jihad but I am not able to. He ﷺ said: Is either of your parents still alive? He said: My mother. He ﷺ said: Then strive in God's cause by being kind to her. If you do that, you are a pilgrim, a performer of 'umrah, and a warrior in jihad, if your mother is pleased with you. So fear God and be kind to her."],[3525,"Whoever is kind to his parents, blessed is he, and God will increase his lifespan."],[3526,"Ibn 'Umar ؓ set out for Hajj, until when he was between Makkah and Madinah, he came to a tree he recognized and sat beneath it. Then he said: I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ beneath a tree when a young man came from these mountain paths until he stood before the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I have come to fight in jihad with you in the path of God Almighty, seeking thereby the face of God, Mighty and Majestic, and the Hereafter. He ﷺ said: Are both your parents alive? He said: Yes. He ﷺ said: Then go back and be kind to them. He said: So he turned back to where he came from."],[3527,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'An ally of a people is one of them, and the son of a people's sister is one of them.'"],[3529,"Whoever claims affiliation to other than his father, or attributes himself to other than his patrons out of aversion to them, upon him is the curse of God, and whoever insults his father or his parents, likewise."],[3530,"The Prophet ﷺ had two freed slaves: an Abyssinian and a Nabataean. They insulted each other while the Prophet ﷺ was listening. One said to his companion: O Abyssinian, and the other said: O Nabataean. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Do not say this; you are but two men from among the companions of Muhammad ﷺ.'"],[3532,"Whoever has a daughter born to him and does not bury her alive, does not humiliate her, and does not prefer his sons over her, God Almighty will admit him to Paradise because of her."],[3533,"Whoever has two daughters born to him and treats them well as long as they accompany him or he accompanies them, Allah (Mighty and Majestic) will admit him to Paradise because of them."],[3534,"Allah, the Exalted, does not make a servant a guardian over a flock, small or large, but He will ask him about it: whether he upheld his command among them or neglected it, until He asks him specifically about his own household."],[3535,"\"Whoever shelters an orphan from among the Muslims, bringing him into his food and drink until he is satisfied, Paradise becomes incumbent for him, unless he commits a sin that is not forgiven. And whoever supports three daughters, disciplining them and treating them well, Paradise becomes incumbent for him.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or two daughters?\" He said, \"Or two daughters,\" until if they had said, \"One,\" he would have said, \"One.\" \"And whoever loses his two precious ones, his reward is upon Allah: Paradise.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what are his two precious ones?\" He ﷺ said, \"His two eyes.\" Ibn Abbas ؓ, when he narrated this hadith, would say, \"This is among the precious and outstanding hadiths.\" [Raised to the Prophet]"],[3536,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he passed beyond a farsakh he would shorten the prayer."],[3537,"A judge does not judge except when he is full and quenched."],[3538,"2636 2204 / 2 - Abu Ya'la said: Al-Hasan narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us with this:"],[3540,"Whoever sponsors an orphan, whether his own or someone else's, I and he will be in Paradise like these two fingers—the middle finger and the index finger that is next to it."],[3541,"Abu Ya'la said: Umayya b. Bistam narrated to us, Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us, Muhammad b. Amr narrated to us with this chain. This is how Muhammad b. Amr narrated it, and Sufyan disagreed with him, from Safwan."],[3542,"\"I and the sponsor of an orphan, whether his own or someone else's, will be in Paradise like these two,\" and Sufyan gestured with his two fingers."],[3543,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us, and mentioned the hadith, in which: And whoever retracts a testimony or conceals it, Allah will feed him his own flesh on the heads of the creatures [on the Day of Resurrection], and will enter him into the Fire while he chews his tongue. And whoever bears false witness against a Muslim or a disbeliever will be hung by his tongue on the Day of Resurrection, then placed with the hypocrites in the lowest depth of the Fire. And whoever claims to have seen a dream he did not see is like one who bears false witness... the hadith."],[3545,"\"I and the sponsor of an orphan, whether his own or someone else's, will be in Paradise if he fears Allah Almighty, like these two,\" and al-Humaydi gestured with his two fingers."],[3546,"And Ahmad b. Mani‘ said: ‘Ali b. ‘Asim narrated to us, from Muslim with it."],[3547,"«How excellent is what you said, O boy! O Bilal, go to our family and bring us whatever food you find with them.» So Bilal ؓ brought twenty-one dates. He said: He placed them in his palm, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured with his hand toward his mouth, and we saw that he was supplicating. Then he ﷺ said: «Seven for you, seven for your mother, and seven for your sister; you eat a date in the morning and a date in the evening.» The boy was from among the sons of the Muhajirun. When he stood up, Mu'adh ؓ followed him, placed his hand on his head, wiped it, and said: «May Allah mend your orphanhood, O boy, and make you a successor to your father.» The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «I saw you and what you did.» He said: «O Messenger of Allah, it was out of mercy for him.» He ﷺ said: «By the One in whose hand is my soul, no man takes in an orphan and treats him well, then places his hand on his head, except that Allah, blessed and exalted, records for him a good deed for every hair, expiates for him a sin for every hair, and raises him a degree for every hair.»"],[3548,"«How excellent is what you said, O boy! O Bilal, go to our family and bring us whatever food you find with them.» So Bilal ؓ brought twenty-one dates. He said: He placed them in his palm, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured with his hand toward his mouth, and we saw that he was supplicating. Then he ﷺ said: «Seven for you, seven for your mother, and seven for your sister; you eat a date in the morning and a date in the evening.» The boy was from among the sons of the Muhajirun. When he stood up, Mu'adh ؓ followed him, placed his hand on his head, wiped it, and said: «May Allah mend your orphanhood, O boy, and make you a successor to your father.» The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «I saw you and what you did.» He said: «O Messenger of Allah, it was out of mercy for him.» He ﷺ said: «By the One in whose hand is my soul, no man takes in an orphan and treats him well, then places his hand on his head, except that Allah, blessed and exalted, records for him a good deed for every hair, expiates for him a sin for every hair, and raises him a degree for every hair.»"],[3549,"«I and the one who sponsors an orphan will be in Paradise like these two,» and he gestured with his index and middle fingers."],[3550,"«No orphan sits with a people at their food bowl but that a devil draws near their bowl.»"],[3551,"«There is no house of a king or a prophet more honored than a house in which there is an orphan.»"],[3552,"«I will be the first for whom the gate of Paradise is opened, except that a woman will come, hastening before me. I will say to her: 'What is with you? Who are you?' She will say: 'I am a woman who stayed with my orphans.'»"],[3553,"«I and the one who sponsors an orphan will be in Paradise like these two,» and he joined his index and middle fingers. «And the one who strives for the orphan, the widow, and the poor is like the one who fights in the path of Allah, or the one who fasts and stands in prayer without slackening.»"],[3554,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: «O Messenger of Allah, I have an orphan in my care. Should I beat him?» He said: «Yes, as you would beat your own child.»"],[3556,"«You will never encompass the people with your wealth, so let your cheerful face and good character encompass them.»"],[3557,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to wear a white cap."],[3558,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met Abu Dharr and said: «O Abu Dharr, shall I not guide you to two qualities that are lighter on the back and heavier on the scale?» He said: «Yes, O Messenger of Allah.» He ﷺ said: «You must have good character and prolonged silence. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no creatures have done the like of them.»"],[3559,"«The most complete of the believers in faith are those with the best character. Indeed good character reaches the degree of fasting and prayer.»"],[3560,"Dye with henna, for it is pleasant in fragrance and calms dizziness."],[3561,"We do not know anyone who narrated it in this manner except Zakariyya."],[3562,"The most complete of the believers in faith are those with the best character."],[3563,"\"O Umm 'Abd, do you know who is the best of the believers in faith?\" She said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He ﷺ said: \"Those with the best character, who are easygoing and gentle. A servant does not attain the reality of faith until he loves for people what he loves for himself, and until his neighbor is safe from his harm.\""],[3564,"He heard a man insulting another man, raising his voice, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Obscenity is a defect, and bad ownership is a defect.\""],[3565,"\"Indeed, Allah the Exalted has one hundred and seventeen character traits. Whoever comes to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, with a single one of them will enter Paradise.\""],[3567,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3568,"Asma' bt. 'Umays ؓ was given the choice: \"Which of your husbands do you choose?\" She said: \"I choose so-and-so, the one from whom I was widowed, and he was the best of them in character.\" Two had been killed while married to her."],[3569,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3570,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3571,"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing a Muslim man is given? He said: \"Good character.\" He said: Then what is the worst thing a Muslim is given? He said: \"If you would dislike something to be seen of you in the gathering of the people, then do not do it when you are alone.\""],[3572,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3574,"We said to Umm al-Darda' ؓ : Narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and do not narrate to us something you heard from other than him. She ؓ said: I heard him say:"],[3575,"\"A man may attain the rank of one who fasts and prays at night through good character, and yet he may be recorded as a tyrant while he only rules over his own household.\""],[3576,"And Ahmad b. Mani' said: Al-Haytham b. Kharijah narrated to us, Isma'il b. 'Ayyash narrated to us with it."],[3577,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who loves to be praised, and it was as if he feared for himself. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Is it not enough for you to live praised and die missed? I was sent only to perfect noble character.\""],[3578,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the leader of the God-fearing. He said: \"He is the God-fearing one of good character.\""],[3579,"\"Bad character spoils deeds just as vinegar spoils honey.\""],[3580,"\"The best of you are those with the best character.\""],[3581,"\"Whoever has bad character torments himself, has more worries, and makes his body ill. Whoever disputes with men loses his honor and his manliness falls.\""],[3582,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: Which part of faith is most excellent? He said: \"Good character.\" He repeated it to him, and he said: \"Good character.\" He repeated it to him a third or fourth time, then either he made him stand or sit. He ﷺ said: \"That you meet your brother with a cheerful face.\" He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept commending good character, saying: \"It is from Allah,\" and condemning bad character, saying: \"It is from Satan.\" Then he said: \"Do you not look at the redness of his eyes and the swelling of his jugular veins?\""],[3585,"\"Whoever looks into his neighbor's house and sees a man's private parts, or a woman's hair, or any part of her body, Allah, exalted is He, has the right to enter him into the Fire with the hypocrites who used to spy on women's private parts. He will not leave this world until Allah, exalted is He, disgraces him and exposes his private parts to onlookers on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever harms his neighbor without right, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him and his abode is the Fire. Indeed, Allah, exalted is He, will ask a man about his neighbor just as He asks him about the rights of his household. Whoever neglects the right of his neighbor is not from us. Whoever spends the night with deceit in his heart towards his Muslim brother spends the night and morning in the wrath of Allah, exalted is He, until he repents and returns. If he dies upon that, he dies upon other than Islam.\" Then he ﷺ said: \"Indeed, whoever deceives us is not from us,\" until he said that three times. \"Whoever backbites a Muslim, his fast is invalidated and his ablution is broken. If he dies while doing so, he dies like one who regards as lawful what Allah, exalted is He, has forbidden. Whoever walks with tale-bearing between two people, Allah, exalted is He, will set upon him in his grave a fire that burns him until the Day of Resurrection, then He will enter him into the Fire. Whoever pardons his Muslim brother and suppresses his anger, Allah, exalted is He, will give him the reward of a martyr. Whoever transgresses against his brother, acts arrogantly towards him, and despises him, Allah, exalted is He, will gather him on the Day of Resurrection in the form of a small ant, and the servants will trample him with their feet, then he will enter the Fire, and he will remain in the wrath of Allah until he dies. Whoever defends his Muslim brother's honor from backbiting he hears mentioned about him in a gathering, Allah, exalted is He, will repel from him a thousand doors of evil in this world and the Hereafter. If he does not defend him and is pleased with what they say, he will bear the same burden of evil as their sin. Whoever says to his slave, or someone else's slave, or any Muslim: 'No labbayka and no sa'dayka (i.e., I will not answer your call),' he will plunge into the Fire. Whoever harms a Muslim is not from us and we are not from him in this world and the Hereafter. Whoever hears of an indecent act and spreads it is like the one who committed it. Whoever hears of a good deed and spreads it is like the one who did it. Whoever honors his Muslim brother only honors his Lord, so what do you think? Whoever has two faces and two tongues in this world, Allah will give him two faces and two tongues in the Fire. Whoever walks in severing relations between two people bears a burden of sin equal to the reward given to one who reconciles between two people, and the curse is incumbent upon him until he enters Hell, where the punishment will be multiplied for him. Whoever walks in helping his Muslim brother and benefiting him will have the reward of the fighters in the path of Allah, exalted is He. Whoever walks in backbiting him and spreading his faults, the first step he takes is as if he places it in Hell, and his private parts will be exposed on the Day of Resurrection before the heads of all creatures. Whoever walks to a relative or a womb-relative for a need or an illness he has, Allah, exalted is He, will give him the reward of a hundred martyrs. If he also maintains ties with him, he will have for every step forty thousand good deeds, and by it forty million sins will be erased from him, and forty million degrees will be raised for him, and it is as if he worshipped Allah, exalted is He, for a hundred thousand years. Whoever walks in spreading corruption among relatives and severing ties between them, Allah is angry with him and curses him, and he bears the sin of one who severs the womb. Whoever works to separate a woman from her husband, the curse of Allah is upon him in this world and the Hereafter, and Allah has forbidden him from looking at His face. Whoever leads a blind man to the mosque, or to his home, or to any of his needs, the reward of freeing a slave is written for him for every step he raises or lowers, and the angels send blessings upon him until he parts from him. Whoever walks with a blind man to fulfill a need until it is accomplished, Allah will give him a clearance from the Fire and a clearance from hypocrisy, and Allah, exalted is He, will fulfill for him seventy thousand needs of this world, and he will remain immersed in mercy until he returns. Whoever walks to help a weak person in a need or benefit, Allah, exalted is He, will give him his book in his right hand. Whoever neglects his family and severs his womb, Allah, exalted is He, will deprive him of the best reward on the day He rewards the doers of good, and he will be gathered with the destroyed ones, until he comes with a way out, and how can there be a way out? Whoever relieves his brother of a distress of this world, Allah will relieve him of the distresses of this world and the Hereafter, and He will look at him with a look of mercy by which he will attain Paradise. Whoever walks in reconciling a woman and her husband, he will have the reward of a thousand martyrs truly killed in the path of Allah, and for every step he will have the worship of seventy years: its fasting and its night prayers. Whoever does a favor to his brother and then reminds him of it, he has nullified his reward and disappointed his efforts. Indeed, Allah, exalted is He, has forbidden Paradise to the one who reminds of favors, the miser, the arrogant, the tale-bearer, the gluttonous oppressor, the rude and boastful, the harsh and cruel, the bastard, and the habitual drunkard. Whoever builds a structure on the side of a road to shelter the wayfarer, Allah will send him on the Day of Resurrection with a pearl on his forehead and his face shining for the people of the gathering, until they say: This is one of the angels, and its like will not be seen until he crowds with Ibrahim ﷺ in Paradise, and by his intercession forty thousand men will enter Paradise. Whoever digs a well until its water springs forth and makes it available for the Muslims, he will have the reward of those who perform ablution from it and pray, and for every hair of every one who drinks from it, human or jinn, beast or wild animal or bird, or other than that, he will have good deeds, and for every hair in that he will have the freeing of a slave, and on the Day of Resurrection his intercession will bring to the Pond, the Pond of Holiness, the number of the stars of the sky.\" It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the Pond of Holiness? He ﷺ said: \"My Pond, my Pond, my Pond. Whoever intercedes for his brother in a need of his, Allah looks at him, and it is incumbent upon Allah, exalted is He, not to punish a servant He has looked at, if that was at his request to intercede for him. If he intercedes for him without his request, he has, in addition to that, the reward of seventy martyrs. Whoever visits his Muslim brother, he has for every step until he returns the freeing of a hundred thousand slaves, the erasure of a hundred thousand sins, and a hundred thousand degrees are written for him.\" We said to Abu Hurayrah: Did not the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever frees a slave, it is his ransom from the Fire\"? He said: Yes, and the rest of it is raised for him in the treasures of the Throne with his Lord, Blessed and Exalted is He. This hadith in its entirety is fabricated upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the one accused of it is Maysarah b. 'Abd Rabbihi, may he not be blessed."],[3587,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must not enter the bathhouse with his wife."],[3589,"It has reached us that when the Day of Resurrection comes, a caller will call out: “Where are the people of pardon?” He said: “Then Allah, the Exalted, will reward them for the pardoning they used to do toward people.”"],[3591,"If a Muslim brother apologizes to someone and that person does not accept his excuse, he will come on the Day of Resurrection bearing the same burden as a tax collector."],[3592,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3594,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3596,"“I will tell you what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did. It was my night with him. I ground some barley and made him a flat loaf. He returned and closed the door. Whenever he ﷺ wanted to sleep, he would close the door, tie the water-skin, turn over the cup and the plate, and extinguish the lamp. I waited for him to return from his mosque so I could feed him the loaf, but he did not return until sleep overcame me. A domestic sheep belonging to our neighbor came and took it, then chewed it away. I became distressed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up, so I hurried to the door. He said: “Take what you can find of your loaf, but do not harm your neighbor because of her sheep.”"],[3597,"The bed of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was like what a person is placed in in his grave, and the mosque was at his head."],[3599,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3601,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3603,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3605,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3606,"A man sneezed in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “What should I say, O Messenger of Allah?” He ﷺ said: “Say: ‘Praise be to Allah.’” The people asked: “What should we say to him, O Messenger of Allah?” He ﷺ said: “Say: ‘May Allah have mercy on you.’” The man asked: “What should I reply to them?” He ﷺ said: “May Allah guide you and set your affairs right.”"],[3608,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3609,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3610,"May Allah have mercy on Labid. He said: \"Gone are those in whose protection one could live, and I remain among a succession like the skin of a mangy camel.\" My father used to say: May Allah have mercy on Aishah ؓ. How would it be if she saw our time now?"],[3611,"This poetry is eloquent speech of the Arabs. By it the beggar is given, anger is suppressed, and people attain their goal in their assembly."],[3612,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3613,"For one of you to have his belly filled with pus or blood is better for him than to have it filled with poetry with which I was lampooned."],[3614,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about poetry. He said: \"It is speech. Its good is good, and its bad is bad.\""],[3615,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3616,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey. He heard two men singing to each other, one of them saying to his companion... and he mentioned some poetry. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Who are these two?\" It was said to him: \"So-and-so and so-and-so.\" He ﷺ said: \"May Allah Almighty plunge them headlong into the trial, and thrust them into the Fire with a violent thrust.\""],[3617,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3619,"He gave something to a poet. It was said to him: \"O Abu Nujayd, will you give to a poet?\" He said: \"I am ransoming my honor from him.\""],[3620,"A man praised Allah Almighty and praised His Messenger ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him because of his praise of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, who created him, and he did not give him because of his praise of himself."],[3621,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3623,"I entered upon ʿĀʾishah ؓ ... and mentioned the hadith. She said: A woman among the women said: “O Mother of the Believers, my tenant touches my shin,” so she turned her face away from her and said: “Make her leave,” and the woman was made to leave her. Then she turned to the women and said: “O women of the believers, what prevents a woman, if she commits a sin and it is concealed for her, from concealing what God, Mighty and Majestic, has concealed, and not revealing it to people? For people find fault but do not change, while God changes and does not find fault.”"],[3625,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[3627,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, teach me a deed by which I may enter Paradise, and make it concise.” He ﷺ said: “Do not get angry.”"],[3628,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[3630,"“Whoever receives a favor from me that is due, he must repay it. If he does not have the means to repay it, then let him publicly praise the giver. If he does not do that, then he has been ungrateful.”"],[3631,"“Whoever is given a gift and finds the means, let him repay it. If he does not find the means, let him praise the giver for it. Whoever praises it has thanked him, and whoever conceals it has been ungrateful. Whoever pretends to have been given what he was not given is like one who wears two garments of falsehood.”"],[3632,"And al-Harith said: 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Aban narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, with it. :"],[3633,"“Two traits, whoever has them, God, Exalted is He, records him as thankful and patient: one who looks at someone above him in religion and follows him, and one who looks at someone below him in worldly matters and praises God, Exalted is He, for the favor He has bestowed upon him over that person. And two traits, whoever has them, God does not record him as patient, nor record him as thankful: one who looks at someone above him in religion and does not follow him, and looks at someone above him in worldly matters and grieves over it.”"],[3635,"“Whoever leads a blind person forty cubits, or fifty cubits, the freeing of a slave is written for him.”"],[3636,"“Whoever leads a blind person forty steps, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.”"],[3638,"“Shall I not tell you about your men who will be among the people of Paradise? The Prophet is in Paradise, the martyr is among the people of Paradise, the ṣiddīq is among the people of Paradise, the newborn is among the people of Paradise, and a man who visits his brother for the sake of God, Exalted is He, in a distant part of the city is in Paradise.”"],[3639,"\"There is no servant who visits a brother for the sake of God, the Exalted, except that God, the Exalted, says to him in the dominion of His Throne: 'My servant has visited Me, and his hospitality is incumbent upon Me, and I will not be satisfied with hospitality for My servant except in Paradise.'\""],[3640,"\"Whoever is in the assistance of his brother, God, the Mighty and Majestic, is in his assistance as long as he is in the assistance of his brother; and whoever unties a knot, God unties from him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[3641,"\"Whoever does not show mercy to our young and does not respect our elders is not one of us.\""],[3642,"\"Visit intermittently, and you will increase in love.\""],[3644,"Uyaynah b. al-Mundhir ؓ was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and with him was another man, and he had some of his wives with him. That man asked for a drink, and a beverage was brought. When he began to drink, they screened him. Uyaynah said: 'O Messenger of God, what is this?' He ﷺ said: 'This is a trait that God, the Exalted, gave to some people and withheld from you; this is modesty.'"],[3645,"\"O 'A'ishah, if obscenity were a man, it would be an evil man.\""],[3646,"\"Every religion has a character, and the character of Islam is modesty.\""],[3647,"\"The first thing to be lifted from this nation is modesty and faith, so ask God, the Exalted, for them.\""],[3648,"I and a companion of mine entered upon a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ called Usayr. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Modesty brings nothing but good.\""],[3650,"\"Lying is not permissible except in three cases: a man lies in war, for war is deception; a man lies between two men to reconcile them; and a man lies to his wife to please her.\""],[3651,"\"He was sent.\""],[3652,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent out a raiding party. They passed by a man from the desert dwellers. They said: 'O bedouin, slaughter a sheep for us.' He said: He brought them a young goat from his flock, and they slaughtered it. He said: They spent the day cooking and roasting until midday, and he shaded himself with his shadow over his flock. They said: 'O bedouin, bring out your flock so that we may take a midday nap in the shade.' He said: 'I adjure you by God, for they are pregnant; if I bring them out and the scorching wind strikes them, they will miscarry.' They said: 'Our own selves are dearer to us than your flock.' He said: So they brought them out, and the scorching wind struck them, and they miscarried. He said: Then they departed from him and left him, until they came to Madinah. There he was, having preceded them to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he informed him of the news. When they came, he ﷺ asked them about what he mentioned, but they denied it. He leaned on a man among them and said: 'O so-and-so, if what is in your companions is good, then perhaps it is with you; tell me the truth.' The man said: 'The bedouin spoke the truth, O Messenger of God; the matter is as he said.' Then he ﷺ said: 'Do you fall into lying as moths fall into the fire? Every lie is written, no doubt, except that a man lies in war, for war is deception, or lies between two men to reconcile them, or a man lies to his wife to please her.'"],[3653,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a raiding party to Ḍāḥiyat Muḍar. They camped in a desert land. When morning came, there was a tent, and in its courtyard there were sheep resting. They came to the owner of the sheep and stood before him, saying, 'Give us a sheep to slaughter.' He brought out a ewe, but they rejected it. Then he brought out another ewe, and they rejected it. He said, 'I have nothing in my flock except its ram or a recently lambed ewe.' So they took a ewe from the flock. When they moved on, they had no shade to shelter from the heat, and they were in a land with no shade. The bedouin had said that his sheep were in his shade. They said, 'We have more right to the shade than these sheep.' So they came to him and said, 'Take out your sheep that are sheltering in this shade.' He said, 'If you take out my sheep, they will fall ill and miscarry their young, and I am a man who has purified himself and submitted.' But they took out his sheep, and within just an hour they became feverish and miscarried their young. The bedouin hurried off until he reached Madinah and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, telling him what had been done to him. He became very angry at that, then he seated him until the people arrived. He asked them, and they said, 'He lied.' So some of the anger left the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The bedouin said, 'By the One by whom I swear, I hope that Allah will inform you of my news and their news.' It occurred to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he was truthful. He then took each of them aside one by one. When he had taken one of them aside and adjured him by Allah, the Exalted, to tell him as the bedouin had told him, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and said: 'O people, do not let yourselves follow one another in lying as moths follow one another into the fire. All lying is written against the son of Adam except three traits: a man who lies to his wife to please her...'"],[3654,"'Indeed, lying blackens the face, and talebearing is the punishment of the grave.'"],[3656,"Do not be deceived by a person's prayer or fasting, but if he speaks he is truthful, if he is entrusted he fulfills, and if he is given charge he is scrupulous."],[3657,"'No lying is proper in seriousness or jest.'"],[3658,"Jibril ﷺ came and asked permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He gave him permission, but he was slow to come in. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took his cloak and went to him while he was standing at the door. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'We have given permission.' He said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but we do not enter a house in which there is an image or a dog.' So they looked and found a puppy in one of their houses. Abu Rafi' ؓ said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me when I woke up, and I did not leave a dog in Madinah without killing it. Then I came upon a woman in a remote area who had a dog that barked in her defense, and I felt compassion for her, so I left it and came to him ﷺ and informed him. He commanded me to kill it, so I returned to the dog and killed it.' He said: 'The people said: What is lawful for us, O Messenger of Allah, of this community that you commanded to be killed?' Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent down: 'And what you have trained of hunting animals, as trainers' (Qur'an 5:4)."],[3659,"'Accept six things from me and I will accept Paradise for you.' It was said, 'What are they, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'When you speak, do not lie; when you promise, do not break it; when you are entrusted, do not betray; lower your gazes, guard your private parts, and restrain your hands.'"],[3661,"'He used to lean on a stalk of the Ibn Ṭāb date palm, and Zayd used to lean on it in his house and when going to his properties.'"],[3663,"'The Prophet ﷺ ruled that the owner of a riding beast is more entitled to its front.'"],[3664,"Al-Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī and ʿAbd Allāh b. Jaʿfar ؓ came to meet the Prophet ﷺ, and he ﷺ placed one in front of him and the other behind him."],[3665,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a journey, and ʿAbd Allāh b. Jaʿfar and al-Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī ؓ came to meet him. He ﷺ placed the older of them behind him and carried the younger in front of him."],[3666,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ seated me behind him on the rear of his camel at night. I began to doze, and he would touch me and say: 'O you, O daughter of Ḥuyayy, O Ṣafiyyah.'"],[3667,"'O you, O daughter of Ḥuyayy, O Ṣafiyyah.'"],[3668,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came from Khaybar, having seated Ṣafiyyah bt. Ḥuyayy ؓ on his luggage, while Abū Rāfiʿ ؓ was on a camel. When we approached Madinah, he said: 'O Abū Rāfiʿ, dismount from the camel and let Ṣafiyyah ride it, for I fear dawn may break before we enter Madinah.' So Abū Rāfiʿ proceeded until he brought her into Madinah."],[3669,"Abu al-Darda' ؓ saw a man riding while a person was running behind him, so he said: \"O so-and-so, if only you had carried this one behind you.\" He said: \"Would I carry this 'ilj behind me?\" He said: \"Then if you had sent him to where you want.\" He said: \"I did not do that.\" He said: \"Then if you had taken a lighter one instead of him.\" He said: \"I did not do that.\" He said: \"Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'If a person runs behind someone while he is riding, Allah, the Exalted, will only increase him in distance.'\""],[3670,"'Umar ؓ saw a man with a person running behind him while he was riding, or he was told about that, and he said: \"May Allah cut off his heart, may Allah cut off his heart.\""],[3672,"\"O Abu Ayyub, shall I not guide you to a charity that pleases Allah and His Messenger by giving it?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"You reconcile between people when they have become corrupt with each other, and you bring them close when they have grown distant.\""],[3673,"\"Shall I not guide you to a charity that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and His Messenger ﷺ love? You reconcile between people when they hate each other and have become corrupt with each other.\""],[3675,"\"The best charity is reconciling between people.\""],[3677,"\"When one of you comes to the door of his room, let him mention the name of Allah, for then his companion from the devils who is with him will turn back. When you enter your rooms, mention the name of Allah and its inhabitant from the devils will leave. When you set out, mention the name of Allah over the first saddle cloth you place on your mounts, so that the devil does not share the riding with you. If you do not do so, he shares with you. When you eat, mention the name of Allah, so that he does not share your food with you, for if you do not, he shares your food with you. Do not leave garbage with you overnight in your rooms, for it is his seat. Do not leave the towel overnight in your houses, for it is his bed. Do not spread out the saddle cloths that are on the backs of mounts. Do not dwell in houses that are not locked. Do not spend the night on roofs that are not walled. When you hear the barking of a dog or the braying of a donkey, seek refuge in Allah, for a donkey does not bray and a dog does not bark except when it sees him.\""],[3679,"\"Be good neighbors to the blessings of Allah; do not drive them away, for seldom do they leave a people and return to them.\""],[3681,"A man asked Abu Musa ؓ about seeking permission from his parents. He said: \"Yes, seek permission. Would it please you to see something private from them?\""],[3682,"A man asked Hudhayfah ؓ, saying: \"Should I seek permission from my mother?\" He said: \"If you do not seek permission from her, you will see from her what displeases you.\""],[3683,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade seeking permission while facing the door.\""],[3684,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while he was at al-Jurf upon our return from Khaybar, saying: \"Do not come to women at night after the 'Isha' prayer.\""],[3685,"«The doors of the Messenger of God ﷺ used to be knocked on with fingernails.»"],[3687,"Umm Ayman was a slave woman belonging to Umm Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet ﷺ. Whenever she entered, she would say, 'Greetings, not upon you.' The Prophet ﷺ gave her permission to say, 'Peace be upon you.'"],[3689,"Ibn Abbas ؓ wrote to a dhimmi and began with the greeting of peace. I said to him, 'Do you initiate the greeting?' He said, '«God is Peace.»'"],[3690,"The Prophet ﷺ wrote to a man not of the Islamic faith, '«You are in peace»', so he wrote to the Prophet ﷺ with peace, and the Prophet ﷺ wrote at the end of the letter, greeting him."],[3691,"«A man from the polytheists wrote to the Messenger of God ﷺ with the greeting of peace, so the Messenger of God ﷺ wrote back returning the greeting.»"],[3692,"Abu Musa ؓ wrote to a Persian nobleman and greeted him with peace in his letter. It was said to him, 'You greet him when he is a disbeliever?' He said, 'He wrote to me greeting me, so I returned it to him.'"],[3693,"«If you have a need from him, begin with the greeting of peace.»"],[3694,"We were sitting with Ali ؓ when the bishop of Najran came, and he made room for him. A man said to him, 'Do you make room for this Christian, O Commander of the Faithful?' He said, '«They used to make room for them when they came to the Messenger of God ﷺ.»'"],[3695,"«Whoever greets you from God's creation, return it to him even if he is a Magian, for God the Exalted says: 'When you are greeted with a greeting, greet with better than it'—that is for the people of Islam—'or return it'—that is upon the polytheist.»"],[3697,"«When a man speaks, then turns around, it is a trust.»"],[3699,"«When you send a messenger, send one with a handsome face and a good name.»"],[3700,"«Seek good with those of handsome faces.»"],[3701,"Seek good from those with handsome faces."],[3702,"When you seek needs, seek them from those with handsome faces."],[3704,"Adopt the ways of Ma‘add, be rough, shoot arrows, and walk barefoot."],[3706,"The worst of people are three: a man who is arrogant toward his parents and belittles them; a man who strives to corrupt between a man and a woman, supporting him against her unjustly until he separates them, then marries her after him; and a man who strives to corrupt among people with lies until they become enemies and hate one another."],[3707,"Three are cursed by Allah Almighty on the Day of Resurrection: a man who turns away from his parents; another who strives to separate a man and his wife so that he may marry her after him; and another who spreads tales among the believers so that they become enemies and hate one another."],[3708,"\"O people, shall I not inform you of the best among you?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He ﷺ said, \"The best of you are those who, when seen, Allah is remembered and their hearts are stirred. Shall I not inform you of the worst among you?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the worst of you are those who walk about with slander, corrupting between loved ones, and seeking hardship for the innocent.\""],[3709,"Whoever has two tongues in this world, Allah will give him two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection."],[3710,"Abu Ya'la said: Humayd b. Mas'ada narrated to us, from 'Ar'ara b. al-Birind, from Isma'il b. Muslim, from al-Hasan and Qatada, from Anas ؓ, and he mentioned it."],[3713,"A man was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and it was said, \"How incapable he is!\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You have backbitten your brother.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we said what is in him.\" He ﷺ said, \"If you said what is not in him, you would have slandered him.\""],[3714,"Ma'iz b. Malik came, and he mentioned the hadith about his stoning. He said: Then two men passed by him and said, \"What a failure this one is! Allah concealed him, yet he did not conceal himself.\" So he was agitated as a dog is agitated. Then the Prophet ﷺ came upon a carcass and said, \"Bite from this carcass.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this is a carcass; we cannot.\" He ﷺ said, \"What you have gotten from your brother is more foul than this carcass.\""],[3715,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man stood up, and a man after him fell upon him (backbit him). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Pick your teeth.\" He said, \"From what should I pick my teeth, O Messenger of Allah? I have not eaten meat that I might pick my teeth.\" He ﷺ said, \"Indeed, you have just eaten the flesh of your brother.\""],[3716,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, and a man from the group said, 'O Messenger of God, how incapable is so-and-so!' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'You have eaten the flesh of your brother and backbitten him.'"],[3717,"And 'Amr b. al-Dahhak b. Makhlad narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj with it. : :"],[3718,"Backbiting is that you mention about your brother the worst of what you know in him; if you mention what is not in him, that is slander."],[3720,"The expiation for backbiting is that you seek forgiveness for the one you backbit."],[3722,"'Shall I teach you what Noah taught his son?' They said, 'Yes.' He ﷺ said, 'O my son, I command you with two things and forbid you from two things: I forbid you from associating anything with God, for whoever associates anything with God, God has forbidden Paradise to him; and I forbid you from arrogance, for no one whose heart contains a mustard seed of arrogance will enter Paradise. And I command you to say: There is no god but God alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent, for if the heavens were a ring, it would break them. And I command you to say: Glory be to God and with His praise, for it is the prayer of creation and the glorification of creation, and by it creation is provided sustenance.' A man said, 'O Messenger of God, is it arrogance for a man to have a riding animal he rides, or a garment he wears, or food to which he invites his companions?' He ﷺ said, 'No, but arrogance is to reject the truth and disparage people. I shall inform you of five things; whoever has them is not arrogant: tethering a sheep, wearing wool, riding a donkey, sitting with the poor believers, and a man eating with his family.'"],[3723,"'O my son, I command you with two things and forbid you from two things: I forbid you from associating anything with God, for whoever associates anything with God, God has forbidden Paradise to him; and I forbid you from arrogance, for no one whose heart contains a mustard seed of arrogance will enter Paradise. And I command you to say: There is no god but God alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent, for if the heavens were a ring, it would break them. And I command you to say: Glory be to God and with His praise, for it is the prayer of creation and the glorification of creation, and by it creation is provided sustenance.' A man said, 'O Messenger of God, is it arrogance for a man to have a riding animal he rides, or a garment he wears, or food to which he invites his companions?' He ﷺ said, 'No, but arrogance is to reject the truth and disparage people. I shall inform you of five things; whoever has them is not arrogant: tethering a sheep, wearing wool, riding a donkey, sitting with the poor believers, and a man eating with his family.'"],[3724,"A Bedouin man came wearing a jubbah of fine silk brocade adorned with gold, and he mentioned the hadith, in which it states that Noah said to his son..."],[3725,"Shall I inform you of the testament of Noah ﷺ ?"],[3726,"God, Mighty and Majestic, will say on the Day of Resurrection: 'I established a lineage, and you established a lineage. I made the noblest of you the most pious of you, but you say, \"O so-and-so, son of so-and-so, I am nobler than you.\" Today I raise My lineage and lower your lineage. Where are the pious?'"],[3727,"A man may attain the rank of one who fasts and stands in prayer through forbearance, and he may be recorded as a tyrant though he only possesses his own household."],[3728,"'There is no man on earth who dies with an atom's weight of arrogance in his heart except that God will place him in the Fire.' A man from the Ansar said, 'O Messenger of God, I love beauty, in the strap of my sword, and washing my clothes from dirt, and in fine shoelaces and sandals.' He said, 'That is not what I mean; arrogance is only one who rejects the truth and disparages people.' He said, 'O Prophet of God, what is rejecting the truth and disparaging people?' He ﷺ said, 'Rejecting the truth is that you have a debt owed by a man, and he denies it, claiming he owes nothing, and a man commands him to fear God but he refuses. As for disparagement, it is one who approaches people with his nose in the air, and when he sees the weak and poor among people, he does not greet them or sit with them out of contempt for them; that is one who disparages people.' The Prophet ﷺ then said, 'Whoever patches his garment, mends his sandal, rides a donkey, visits the sick slave, and milks the sheep has freed himself from pride.'"],[3729,"There is no human being but has wisdom in his head, and it is in the hand of an angel; if he humbles himself, the angel raises him, and if he is arrogant, the angel lowers him."],[3730,"«Whoever humbles himself for Me thus, I will raise him thus,» and he placed the palm of his hand toward the ground, then he placed the palm of his hand toward the sky, and raised it toward the sky."],[3731,"A man sought permission during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"Grant permission to the riding companion of al-Nuʿman b. al-Mundhir.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Your great ones are more insignificant to Allah than the beetles that push dung with their noses.» He said: Then a man sought permission and said: \"Indeed my praise is an adornment and my blame is a disgrace.\" He ﷺ said: «You have lied; that is Allah, Blessed and Exalted.»"],[3732,"The companions of Ibn Masʿud were bitten by the cold, and they began to feel ashamed to come in worn-out cloaks and woolen wraps. He missed them, and it was said to him: \"Their situation is such and such.\" So Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman came one morning in a woolen wrap, and they said: \"Ibn Masʿud has come in a woolen wrap.\" Then the second day came, then the third day came. When they saw him in the woolen wrap, they came in their cloaks all together. He recognized faces that he had missed and said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: «No one will enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride,» or he said: «an atom of pride.»"],[3734,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ related a hadith, and we did not rejoice at anything after Islam more intensely than our rejoicing at it. He ﷺ said: «The believer is rewarded for removing harm from the road, for guiding to the way, for interpreting for the one with a speech impediment, and for giving the gift of milk. Indeed, he is rewarded for merchandise wrapped in his garment: he touches it, and his hand misses it.»"],[3736,"«I have not spat on my right side since I embraced Islam.» It was said to Sufyan: \"Not in prayer or otherwise?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[3737,"«I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spitting to his right, to his left, and in front of him.»"],[3739,"A traveling group from Mudar came with a bell, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered that they cut it off. From that time the bell was disliked, and he said: «The angels do not accompany a traveling group that has a bell.»"],[3741,"Abu Musa ؓ wrote to ʿAmir b. ʿAbd Allah: \"From ʿAbd Allah b. Qays to ʿAmir b. ʿAbd Allah, who is called Ibn ʿAbd Qays. To proceed: If you have changed, then return; and if you have not changed, then continue. And peace be upon you.\""],[3743,"«Women are not entitled to the side of the road.»"],[3745,"«I left the Prophet ﷺ heading to my family, and I passed by boys playing. Their play pleased me, so I stood over the boys. The Prophet ﷺ came to me, stood over them, greeted the boys, then sent me on an errand for him. I returned to my mother after the time I usually returned to them. My mother said: \"What kept you today, my son?\" I said: \"The Prophet ﷺ sent me on an errand.\" She said: \"What errand?\" He said: I said: \"Mother, it is a secret.\" She said: \"My son, keep the secret of the Prophet of Allah ﷺ.\""],[3746,"«I have a secret from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; if I were to tell it to anyone among the people, I would tell you.»"],[3747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, and it was the first thing he enjoined upon me, he said: «My son, conceal my secret and you will be a believer.» My mother and the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to ask me about the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I would not inform them of it. I will never inform anyone of the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ever."],[3748,"\"O my son, conceal my secret and you will be a believer.\" My mother and the wives of the Messenger of God ﷺ used to ask me about the secret of the Messenger of God ﷺ, but I would not tell them. And I will never inform anyone of the secret of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He also said: \"O my dear son, perfect your ablution, and your guardian angels will love you and your lifespan will be increased. O Anas, be thorough in washing from janabah, for you will leave your place of washing with no sin or error upon you.\" I said: \"How is thoroughness, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"Wet the roots of the hair and cleanse the skin.\" \"O my dear son, if you can, always remain in a state of ablution, for whoever death comes to while he is in a state of ablution will be granted martyrdom. O my dear son, if you can, always be praying, for the angels pray for you as long as you are praying. O Anas, when you bow, place your palms firmly on your knees, spread your fingers, and keep your elbows away from your sides.\""],[3750,"\"Two should not converse privately excluding the third, for that hurts the believer, and God hates hurting the believer.\""],[3752,"\"Whoever says: 'Peace be upon you,' ten good deeds are written for him. Whoever says: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of God,' twenty good deeds are written for him. Whoever says: 'Peace be upon you, the mercy of God, and His blessings,' thirty good deeds are written for him.\" He confirmed it and said: \"Yes.\""],[3753,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of Khaybar the eating of domesticated donkey, and of every beast of prey with fangs."],[3754,"A group of us gathered and said: \"O Messenger of God, we are people of high and low lands, and we have gatherings in which we talk.\" He ﷺ said: \"Give gatherings their due.\" We said: \"What is their due, O Messenger of God?\" He ﷺ said: \"Lower your gazes, return the greeting, guide the blind, enjoin good, and forbid evil.\""],[3755,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"Peace be upon you.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Ten.\" Then another came and said: \"Peace be upon you and the mercy of God.\" He ﷺ said: \"Twenty.\" Then another came and said: \"Peace be upon you, the mercy of God, and His blessings.\" He ﷺ said: \"Thirty.\""],[3756,"\"Indeed, God Almighty is Peace, so do not begin with anything before Him. When it is said: 'Peace be upon you,' then say: 'Peace be upon you.'\""],[3757,"\"Peace comes before speech, and do not invite anyone to food until he gives the greeting of peace.\""],[3758,"\"The rider greets the walker, the walker greets the sitter, and when two walkers meet, whichever begins with the greeting is more virtuous.\""],[3759,"My father sent me to Ibn Umar ؓ. I entered upon him without permission. He taught me, saying: \"When you want to enter, ask permission. If permission is given to you, then greet and enter.\" Then he said: \"What is your need?\" I said: \"My father sent me to ask you to write for him the value of your property in Khaybar in exchange for dried yogurt.\" So he wrote it for him and said: \"Have you made it a waqf?\" I said: \"Yes.\""],[3760,"\"Spread peace among yourselves.\""],[3761,"\"And pride is pride.\""],[3762,"\"meaning abundant hardship\""],[3763,"A cow of ours became wild. A man went out and struck it below the neck and above the shoulder blade. It fell down dead. The Prophet ﷺ was asked, and he said: 'A domesticated cow, when it becomes like a wild animal, is made lawful by what makes a wild animal lawful.'"],[3765,"\"By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not inform you of something which, if you do it, you will love one another? Spread peace among yourselves.\""],[3766,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me—and the first thing he enjoined upon me was that he said: \"O my dear son, conceal my secret, and you will be a believer.\" So my mother and the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would ask me about the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I would not inform them of it, and I would never inform anyone of the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. \"O my dear son, when you leave your house, let not your eye fall upon anyone from the people of the Qiblah except that you greet him with peace, for you will return forgiven. And O my dear son, when you enter your home, greet yourself and your family. And O my dear son, if you can rise in the morning and reach the evening with no deceit in your heart toward anyone, then do so, for that is lighter for you in the reckoning. And O my dear son, if you follow my advice, then let nothing be dearer to you than death.\""],[3767,"\"O my dear son, conceal my secret, and you will be a believer.\" So my mother and the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would ask me about the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I would not inform them of it, and I would never inform anyone of the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. \"O my dear son, when you leave your house, let not your eye fall upon anyone from the people of the Qiblah except that you greet him with peace, for you will return forgiven. And O my dear son, when you enter your home, greet yourself and your family. And O my dear son, if you can rise in the morning and reach the evening with no deceit in your heart toward anyone, then do so, for that is lighter for you in the reckoning. And O my dear son, if you follow my advice, then let nothing be dearer to you than death.\"\" type=\"marfu'\""],[3769,"\"My father sent me, and al-Abbas sent al-Fadl his son, to the Prophet ﷺ. We entered upon him, and he seated us on his right and on his left, and he embraced us with the tightest embrace you could see.\""],[3771,"\"If I entered while people were praying, I would not greet them with peace.\""],[3773,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for me during his illness in which he died. I came to him and found him sleeping, so I leaned over him, and he ﷺ raised his hands and embraced me.\""],[3774,"\"When Ja'far ؓ returned from Abyssinia, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ embraced him.\""],[3775,"\"There are no two servants who love each other for the sake of Allah Almighty, and one of them meets his companion, shakes his hand, and they both invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, except that they do not separate until their sins are forgiven, the past and the later.\""],[3777,"Thabit said to Anas: \"O Abu Hamzah, did you touch the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with your hand?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then give it to me,\" so he gave him his hand and he kissed it."],[3779,"«When any of you is given a gift of sweet basil, let him not reject it, for it has come out of Paradise.»"],[3780,"«Do not refuse perfume, for it is light to carry and pleasant in smell.»"],[3782,"A man called the Prophet ﷺ three times, and each time he responded to him: «Labbayk, labbayk.»"],[3784,"«When two people exchange insults, the sin of what they say is upon the one who initiated it, unless the one wronged transgresses.»"],[3785,"We bought a cow during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to share in its meat. It broke loose from us and became difficult to control. A freed slave of ours called Dhakwan confronted it with a sword in his hand while it was running about on the hard ground. It headed toward a hill, and when it passed by him, he struck it with the sword at the base of its neck or on its shoulder, piercing it with the sword, and it fell. We did not manage to slaughter it properly. I went out with 'Abd Allah b. Thabit b. al-Jidh' and we met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We mentioned its situation to him, and he said: 'Eat it. If any of these animals escapes you, restrain it with what you restrain a wild animal.'"],[3786,"«None of you should say: 'My soul has become evil (khabuthat nafsī),' but let him say: 'My soul has become sluggish (laqisat nafsī).'»"],[3787,"«Do not curse the night, the day, the sun, the moon, or the winds, for they are sent as mercy for some people and as punishment for others.»"],[3788,"«The one who speaks obscenity and the one who listens to it are equal in sin.»"],[3789,"I saw Usāma ؓ praying by the grave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Marwān b. al-Ḥakam came out and said: 'You are praying by his grave?' He said: 'I love him.' Then he said to him a foul word and turned away. Usāma ؓ finished and said to Marwān: 'You have harmed me. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: «Allah, Exalted is He, hates the obscene, foul-mouthed person, and you are an obscene, foul-mouthed person.»"],[3790,"«Cursing a believer is like killing him, and if he says to him: 'O disbeliever,' it is like killing him.»"],[3791,"A rooster crowed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and a man said: 'O Allah, curse it.' The Prophet ﷺ said: «Do not revile it or curse it, for it calls to prayer.»"],[3792,"«Do not revile him or curse him, for he calls to prayer.\" type=\"marfu\"\""],[3793,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a flea bit a man, so he cursed it. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Do not curse it, for it woke a prophet among the prophets for prayer.\""],[3794,"Fleas were mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"They wake one for prayer.\""],[3795,"We stopped at a place, and fleas annoyed us, so we cursed them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not curse them, for what a good creature it is! It woke you for the remembrance of Allah, Exalted is He.\""],[3796,"A man traveled with the Prophet ﷺ and cursed his camel. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O servant of Allah, do not travel with us on a cursed camel.\""],[3797,"\"O servant of Allah, do not travel with us on a cursed camel.\""],[3799,"\"Guard yourselves from people by thinking ill of them.\""],[3800,"\"Guard yourselves from people by thinking ill of them.\""],[3801,"\"Test a person and you will hate him.\""],[3803,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when some of the people spoke in a manner resembling rhymed prose. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Stand up, O Salamah.\""],[3805,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was traveling, he came upon the grave of a man whom he named. Abu Bakr ؓ said: \"May Allah curse the occupant of this grave, for he was an enemy of Allah.\" He (the narrator) said: His son was traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Rather, may Allah curse Abu Quhafah, for by Allah, he did not entertain guests nor fight the enemy.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not revile the dead, lest you harm the living.\""],[3807,"\"Riba has seventy-two doors, the least of which is like a man having intercourse with his mother, and the most serious riba is a man's attack on the honor of his companion.\""],[3808,"\"Whoever is present when his Muslim brother is backbitten and supports him, Allah will support him in this world and the Hereafter. But whoever abandons supporting him while able to do so, Allah will forsake him in this world and the Hereafter.\""],[3809,"Abu Ya'la said: 'Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, 'Ali b. Mushir narrated to us, from Abu Isma'il al-'Abdi, from Anas ؓ, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said something similar. I say: Abu Isma'il is Aban mentioned before it."],[3811,"Whoever consumes a meal at the expense of a Muslim man, Allah will feed him the like of it from the boiling water of Hell; and whoever clothes himself at the expense of a Muslim man with a garment, Allah, the Exalted, will clothe him with the like of it from Hell; and whoever takes a stand for a Muslim man in a position of showing off, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will take a stand for him in a position of showing off on the Day of Resurrection."],[3813,"The best of your youth are those who imitate your elders, and the worst of your elders are those who imitate your youth."],[3815,"Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, becomes angry when the sinner is praised."],[3816,"And the Throne shook."],[3818,"Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas missed a rak'ah of the dawn prayer, so he stood up to make it up. The Prophet ﷺ stood up and the people sat around him. When Thabit b. Qays finished the prayer, he came to a man and said: 'Make room for me,' so he made room for him. Then he came to a second and said: 'Make room for me,' so he made room for him. Then he came to a third and said: 'Make room for me,' but he said: 'Behind you there is plenty of room. Why are you stepping over people?' He looked at his face and said: 'O son of such-and-such a woman!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard it and said: 'Who is this who has reproached the man shortly before by his mother?' They were silent. Then he said a second time: 'Who is this who has reproached the man shortly before by his mother?' Thabit stood up and said: 'I missed a rak'ah, and I have deafness in my ear, so I wanted to draw near to you, and the people sat around you.' He mentioned the story. He said: 'So I reproached him for a mother who lived in the pre-Islamic era, while other women were better than her.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Thabit b. Qays, raise your head above this assembly. Among them are the black, the white, and the red. You are no better than these except through piety.'"],[3819,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us until he made the young women in their houses hear, or he said in their chambers. He said: 'O assembly of those who have believed with their tongues but faith has not entered their hearts, do not backbite the Muslims, and do not pursue their private faults. For whoever pursues the private fault of his brother, Allah will pursue his private fault, and whoever Allah pursues his private fault, He will expose him even in the innermost part of his house.'"],[3820,"No man sees a private fault of his brother and conceals it for him except that Allah will admit him to Paradise."],[3821,"The Muslim is the mirror of the Muslim, so if he sees something in him, let him remove it."],[3822,"The Prophet ﷺ had two freed slaves: an Abyssinian and a Nabatean. They insulted each other while the Prophet ﷺ was listening. One of them said to his companion: 'O Nabatean,' and the other said: 'O Abyssinian.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Do not say this; you are only two men from the companions of Muhammad ﷺ.'"],[3824,"Envy almost overtook destiny, and poverty almost became disbelief."],[3825,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a mat be spread at the door of houses, and he said: 'Move it away from the door a little.'"],[3827,"When you buy something you do not want your neighbor to benefit from, then conceal it."],[3828,"When your neighbor's child comes to you, put something in his hand, for it attracts affection."],[3829,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoining [kindness to] the neighbor so much that we thought or we saw that he would make him an heir."],[3830,"A man from al-ʿAwālī came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Jibrīl ﷺ were praying where funeral prayers are offered. When he finished, the man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, who is this I saw with you?' He ﷺ said: 'And you saw him?' He said: 'Yes.' He ﷺ said: 'You have seen much good. This is Jibrīl ﷺ . He kept enjoining me [to be kind] to the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.'"],[3831,"Whoever's neighbor asks him to support [something] against his wall, let him do so."],[3832,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so is my neighbor and he harms me.' He said: 'Refrain from harming him and be patient with his harm.' Only a short while passed before he came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so, my neighbor who used to harm me, has died.' He ﷺ said: 'Time is sufficient as an admonisher, and death is sufficient as a separator.'"],[3833,"O Messenger of Allah, I have two neighbors; to which of them should I give a gift? He ﷺ said: 'The nearer of them.'"],[3834,"A man should not be satiated while his neighbor is hungry."],[3835,"I passed by and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on al-Ṣafā with his cheek against the cheek of a man. Then he left. Soon after, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called me, so I went straight to him. He said: 'O Muḥammad b. Maslamah, what prevented you from greeting?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I saw you do something with that man that you had not done with anyone else, and I disliked interrupting your conversation. Who was that, O Messenger of Allah?' He ﷺ said: 'Jibrīl. If you had greeted, we would have returned your greeting.' He said: 'And what did he say to you, O Messenger of Allah?' He ﷺ said: 'He kept enjoining me [to be kind] to the neighbor until I expected him to command me to make him an heir.'"],[3836,"The right of the neighbor is forty cubits, like this, and like this, and like this, and like this: to the right, to the left, in front, and behind."],[3837,"Give affection to your friend, for it is more lasting."],[3838,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to make brotherhood between two of his companions, and the night would grow long for one of them until he met his brother, and he would meet him with affection and gentleness, and say: 'How have you been since I last saw you?' As for the common people, not three [days] would pass for either of them without him knowing the condition of his brother."],[3839,"When a man takes another as a brother, he should ask him his name, his father's name, and who he is, for that is more conducive to affection."],[3840,"The believer who mixes with people and endures their harm has a greater reward than the believer who does not mix with people and does not endure their harm."],[3841,"Abu Bakr said: Muhammad b. 'Ubayd narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Yahya b. Waththab, from a man among the companions of Muhammad ﷺ ؓ, in marfu' form, something similar."],[3842,"Everything has two ends and a middle. If one of the ends is held, the other inclines; and if the middle is held, the two ends become balanced. And he said: Adhere to the middle courses of things."],[3843,"Love your beloved moderately, for perhaps he may become hateful to you one day; and hate the one you hate moderately, for perhaps he may become your beloved one day."],[3844,"A Muslim does not increase in brotherhood for the sake of Allah, the Exalted, except that he increases in degree by it."],[3845,"When one of you loves a servant, let him inform him, for he will find the like of what he finds."],[3846,"A man passed by Ibn 'Abbas ؓ, and he said: This man loves me. They said: How do you know, O Ibn 'Abbas? He said ؓ: Because I love him."],[3847,"Whoever establishes a brotherhood in Islam, Allah, the Exalted, raises him a degree in Paradise by it. No two servants love each other for the sake of Allah, the Exalted, and then are separated except because of a sin one of them commits. And no two servants love each other for the sake of Allah, the Exalted, except that the better of them in the sight of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, is the one who loves his companion more."],[3848,"Those who love one another will be upon a pillar of red ruby, overlooking the people of this world. He said: The people of Paradise will say: Come out with us to look at those who love one another for the sake of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. He said: They will come out and look at them, their faces like the night of the full moon, written on their foreheads: These are those who love one another for the sake of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."],[3849,"At the top of the pillar are seventy thousand chambers; their beauty shines upon the people of Paradise as the sun shines upon the people of this world. And in it: Upon them are green garments of fine silk."],[3850,"Indeed in Paradise there are pillars of ruby, upon them chambers of chrysolite, with open doors, shining as the brilliant star shines. We said: O Messenger of Allah, who will dwell in them? He ﷺ said: Those who love one another for the sake of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, those who sit together for the sake of Allah, the Exalted, and those who are intimate for the sake of Allah, glorified be His majesty."],[3851,"No two men ever loved each other except that the better of them was the one who loved his companion more."],[3852,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ sat, Abdullah would remove his sandals from his feet and place them in his sleeves, and when he stood, he would put them on him. And he would walk with a staff in front of him until he entered the room."],[3853,"I have not lied since I became Muslim except one lie. I was preparing the saddle for the Messenger of God ﷺ when a man from al-Ta'if came to saddle, and he said: 'Which saddle is most pleasing to the Messenger of God ﷺ?' I said: 'The Ta'ifi one with the front pommel.' He said: 'And the Messenger of God ﷺ used to dislike it.' So when he saddled it and it was brought, the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Who saddled this for us?' I said: 'So-and-so, whom you brought from al-Ta'if, saddled it for you.' Then the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Return the mount to Ibn Mas'ud.'"],[3854,"They asked the Prophet ﷺ about an uncircumcised man who performs the pilgrimage to the House of God Almighty. He said: 'No. God forbade me from that until he becomes circumcised.'"],[3855,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us with this. This is a hasan chain, and the name of the father of Munyah is 'Ubayd b. Abi Barzah. Al-Abbas al-Asfati attributed her genealogy on the authority of Ibn Yunus:"],[3856,"They do good deeds, and indeed they are given their rewards according to the measure of their intellects."],[3857,"Umar, Abu Hurayrah, and Ubayy b. Ka'b entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, who is the most knowledgeable of people?' He ﷺ said: 'The intelligent one.' They said: 'Then who is the most devoted worshipper among people?' He ﷺ said: 'The intelligent one.' They said: 'Then who is the most virtuous of people?' He said: 'The intelligent one.' They said: 'O Messenger of God, is not the intelligent one the one whose manliness is complete, whose eloquence is evident, and whose status is great?' He said: 'Indeed all of that is but the enjoyment of the worldly life (the verse), but the intelligent one is the one who is God-fearing, even if in this world he is lowly, remote, and humble.'"],[3858,"Indeed a man attains by his good character the rank of one who fasts and stands in prayer, and a man's good character is not complete until his intellect is complete. Then his trustworthiness and his faith are complete: he obeys his Lord and disobeys his enemy Iblis."],[3859,"People will be held accountable according to the measure of their intellects."],[3860,"O Messenger of God, by what do people excel one another in this world? He ﷺ said: 'By intellect.' I said: 'And in the Hereafter?' He ﷺ said: 'By intellect.' She said: I said: 'They are only rewarded according to their deeds.' He ﷺ said: 'Did they do deeds except according to the measure of intellect that God Almighty gave them? So according to the measure of intellect they were given, their deeds were, and according to the measure of their deeds they will be rewarded.'"],[3861,"For everything there is a tool and equipment, and the tool and equipment of the believer is intellect. The pillar of the believer is intellect. For everything there is a goal, and the goal of worship is intellect. For every people there is a shepherd, and the shepherd of the worshippers is intellect. For every merchant there is capital, and the capital of the strivers is intellect. For every household there is a caretaker, and the caretaker of the houses of the truthful is intellect. For every ruin there is reconstruction, and the reconstruction of the Hereafter is intellect. For every matter there is an outcome to which it is attributed and by which it is remembered, and the outcome of the truthful by which they are attributed and remembered is intellect. For every tribe there is a tent to which they resort, and the tent of the believers is intellect."],[3862,"The support of a person is his intellect, and there is no religion for one who has no intellect."],[3863,"O people, understand [the commands] from your Lord, and humble yourselves with the intellect concerning what you have been commanded and what you have been forbidden. Know that He warns you before your Lord. Know that the intelligent one is he who obeys God Almighty, even if he is of ugly appearance, lowly in rank, base in station, shabby in condition. And the ignorant one is he who disobeys God, even if he is of beautiful appearance, noble in station, good in condition, eloquent and articulate. Monkeys and pigs are more intelligent regarding God Almighty than one who disobeys Him. Do not be deceived by the people of this world honoring you, for tomorrow you will be among the losers."],[3864,"O Messenger of God ﷺ, [what about] a man who has good intellect but many sins? He said: There is no human being except that he has errors and sins that he commits. Whoever's innate character is intellect, and whose natural disposition is certainty, sins will not harm him. It was said: How is that, O Messenger of God? He said ﷺ: Because whenever he errs, he does not wait long before he rectifies that with repentance and regret for what he did, so that erases his sins, and there remains for him an excellence by which he enters Paradise."],[3865,"The angels strove and exerted themselves in obedience to God by intellect, and the believers strove and exerted themselves in obedience to God according to the measure of their intellects. So the most knowledgeable of them in obedience to God, Mighty and Majestic, is the most abundant of them in intellect."],[3866,"I said: O Messenger of God, what do you think about the saying of God, Mighty and Majestic: 'Which of you is best in deed'—what does He mean by it? He said ﷺ: 'Which of you is best in intellect.' Then he said ﷺ: 'The most complete of you in intellect is the most intense of you in fear of God, and the best of you in reflecting upon what he has been commanded and forbidden, even if he is the least of you in voluntary deeds.'"],[3867,"Indeed, two men may set out to the mosque and pray, and one of them departs while his prayer is heavier than Mount Uhud, while the other departs and his prayer does not equal the weight of a speck of dust. Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi ؓ said: How can that be? He said: When one of them has better intellect. He said: How is that? He said: When he is more scrupulous regarding the prohibitions of God, Mighty and Majestic, and more eager to hasten to good, even if he is inferior to the other in voluntary deeds."],[3868,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said to Tamim al-Dari ؓ: What is sovereignty (leadership) among you? He said: Intellect. He said: You have spoken the truth. I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ just as I asked you, and he said just as you said. Then he said: I asked Gabriel ﷺ : What is sovereignty among people? He said: Intellect."],[3869,"For everything there is a support, and the support of the believer is his intellect. According to the measure of his intellect is his worship of his Lord. Have you not heard the saying of the wicked one at his regret: 'If only we had listened or used our intellect, we would not be among the companions of the Blaze.'"],[3870,"Consult the intelligent one and you will be guided aright, and do not disobey him lest you regret."],[3871,"The best of my companions and the most excellent of them is the most God-fearing of them. Abu Sa'id said: The most God-fearing of them is the most intelligent of them; thus said the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[3872,"Indeed, the ignorant one reveals nothing but a fault, even if he is considered judicious and charming by people. And indeed, the intelligent one reveals nothing but excellence, even if he is considered defective and contemptible by people."],[3873,"He recited: 'Blessed is He in whose hand is dominion' up to His saying: 'That He may test you, which of you is best in deed.' He said: 'Which of you is best in intellect, most scrupulous regarding the prohibitions of God, and quickest of them in obedience to God, Mighty and Majestic.'"],[3874,"How many an intelligent one, whose affair is known to God, while he is despised among people, ugly in appearance, will be saved tomorrow. And how many one with a glib tongue, beautiful appearance, and fine clothing will perish tomorrow on the Day of Resurrection."],[3875,"God Almighty divided the intellect into three parts. Whoever has them, his intellect is complete, and whoever lacks them, he has no intellect: sound knowledge of God Almighty, sound obedience to Him, and sound patience with His decree."],[3876,"The questions became many upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he said: O people, for every path there is a mount and an allegiance and a clear proof. The most reliable mount of people, the best of them in guidance and in knowledge of soundness, is the best of them in intellect."],[3877,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from the expedition of Uhud, he heard people saying: So-and-so was braver than so-and-so, and so-and-so was bolder than so-and-so, and so-and-so endured what no one else endured, and the like of this, praising them. The Prophet ﷺ said: As for this, you have no knowledge of it. They said: How is that, O Messenger of God? He said ﷺ: Each of them fought according to the measure of intellect God allotted to them, and their victory and intention were according to the measure of their intellects. Those among them who were struck were struck at different stations. When the Day of Resurrection comes, they will divide their stations according to the measure of their intentions and intellects."],[3878,"A people praised a man in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ until they went far in praising him for the attributes of good. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: How is the man's intellect? They said: O Messenger of God, we tell you about his diligence in worship and the kinds of good, and you ask us about his intellect! The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Indeed the fool, by his foolishness, hits upon something greater than the immorality of the immoral. Servants will be raised tomorrow in ranks and attain nearness to their Lord according to the measure of their intellects."],[3879,"O Ibn Salam, if you wish you may ask me, and if you wish I will inform you. He said: Inform me. He said: The angels brought near did not encompass the creation of the Throne, and they have no knowledge of it, nor do its bearers who carry it. When God created the heavens and the earth, the angels said: Our Lord, have You created a creation greater than the heavens and the earth? He said: Yes, the seas. They said: Have You created a creation greater than the seas? He said: Yes, the Throne. They said: Have You created a creation greater than the Throne? He said: Yes, the intellect. They said: Our Lord, how great is the measure of the intellect and its creation? He said: Far be it, its knowledge cannot be encompassed. He said: Do you have knowledge of the number of the sand? They said: No. He said: I created the intellect in various kinds like the number of the sand. Among people, some were given one grain of that, and some two, three, and four grains, and some were given a faraq, and some were given a wasq, and some were given two wasqs, and some were given more than that, up to what God willed of multiplication. Ibn Salam ؓ said: So who are those, O Messenger of God? He said: The workers in obedience to God Almighty according to the measure of their deeds, their striving, and their certainty. The light that God Almighty placed in their hearts and their understanding in that—all of it is according to the measure of what He gave them. According to that measure the worker among them acts and rises in ranks. Ibn Salam ؓ said: By the One who sent you with guidance and the religion of truth, I have not found a single letter differing from what I found in the Torah. Moses ﷺ was the first to describe this attribute, and you are the second. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: You have spoken truth, O Ibn Salam."],[3880,"A man has not acquired anything better than an intellect that guides its possessor to guidance and turns him away from destruction. The faith of a servant is not complete, nor is his religion upright, until his intellect is complete."],[3881,"I said: O Messenger of God, to what will people end up on the Day of Resurrection? He said: To their deeds. Whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it. I said: Which of them is best in deeds? He said ﷺ: The best of them in intellect. I said: This is in this world, so which of them is best in the Hereafter? He said ﷺ: The best of them in intellect. Indeed the intellect is the master of deeds in both abodes altogether."],[3882,"A man said: O Messenger of God, what do you think of a man who stands in prayer at night, fasts during the day, performs Hajj and Umrah, fights in the path of God Almighty, visits the sick, maintains kinship ties, escorts funerals, and honors the guest—until he counted these ten qualities—what is his station with God Almighty on the Day of Resurrection? He said ﷺ: His reward on the Day of Resurrection in all of that will be according to the measure of his intellect."],[3883,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him: O Uwaymir, increase in intellect, and you will increase in nearness to your Lord. He said: May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God, how can I do that? He said ﷺ: Avoid what God, Mighty and Majestic, has forbidden, and perform the obligatory duties of God Almighty; you will be a man of intellect. And do voluntary acts of righteous deeds—through them you will increase in rank and honor in this present world, and through them you will attain nearness and might from your Lord."],[3884,"I said to Ibn Umar ؓ: Which pilgrim to the House of God is best and greatest in reward? He said ؓ: One who combines three qualities: sincere intention, abundant intellect, and spending from lawful means. This was mentioned to Ibn Abbas ؓ, and he said: He spoke truth. I said: If his intention is sincere and his spending is from lawful means, what harm does the smallness of his intellect cause him? He said: O Abu al-Hajjaj, you ask me about what I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, a servant does not obey his Lord with anything—not jihad, nor any kind of piety among the kinds of what comes from him—if he does not understand it. If an ignorant person, by his intellect, surpassed the diligent in worship, what he corrupts would be more than what he sets right."],[3885,"Abu Bakr ؓ went out one day, and the Prophet ﷺ met him. He said to him: What have you brought, O Messenger of God? He said ﷺ: The intellect. He said: With what were you commanded? He said: With the intellect. He said: With what will people be recompensed on the Day of Resurrection? He said: With the intellect. He said: How can we attain intellect? He said: The intellect has no limit, but whoever declares lawful what God has made lawful and forbids what God has made forbidden is called a man of intellect. If he strives in worship and excels—or rises—in the ranks of good but has no share of intellect to guide him to follow the command of God Almighty and avoid what He has forbidden, then those are the greatest losers in deeds, whose effort goes astray in the life of this world while they think they are doing well."],[3886,"The description of the man of intellect: he forbears with one who is ignorant toward him, pardons one who wrongs him, humbles himself to one who is below him, and races ahead of one who is above him in seeking righteousness. When he wants to speak, he reflects; if it is good, he speaks and gains; if it is evil, he remains silent and is safe. When a trial presents itself to him, he seeks protection in God and restrains his hand and tongue. When he sees a virtue, he seizes it. Modesty does not leave him, nor does greed appear from him. These are ten qualities by which the man of intellect is known. He said: And the description of the ignorant man: he wrongs one who associates with him, imitates one who is below him, and exalts himself over one who is above him. His speech is without reflection; if he speaks, he sins; if he remains silent, he is heedless. When a trial presents itself to him, he hastens to it and it destroys him. When he sees a virtue, he turns away from it and is slow toward it. He does not fear his past sins, nor does he refrain from sins in what remains of his life. He is slack in righteousness, slow toward it, unconcerned about what he has missed of that or wasted. These are ten qualities of the description of the ignorant man who is deprived of intellect."],[3887,"The least fault of a man is to sit in his house."],[3888,"Indeed, 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ gathered every boy whose name was the name of a prophet, and he brought them into a house and wanted to change their names. Their fathers testified that the Messenger of God ﷺ had named them. He said: My father, Muhammad b. 'Amr b. Hazm, was among them."],[3889,"You name them Muhammad, then you curse them."],[3890,"Whoever eats until he is full and drinks until he is quenched and then says: “Praise be to Allah who fed me and satisfied me, and gave me drink and quenched me,” will emerge from his sins like the day his mother gave birth to him."],[3892,"Whoever has three children born to him and does not name one of them Muhammad has been ignorant."],[3893,"And al-Bazzar said: Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Shababah narrated to us with this."],[3894,"A boy was born to the brother of Umm Salama. They named him al-Walid. They brought him in to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: Have you named him? They said: Yes, they named him al-Walid. He ﷺ said: Stop, stop! His name is 'Abd al-Rahman. You have named him with the name of your Pharaohs? There will surely be a man in my community called al-Walid; he will be worse for my community than Pharaoh was for his people. 'Abd al-Rahman said: I said to him: Which al-Walid is he? He ﷺ said: If al-Walid b. Yazid becomes caliph, it is he; otherwise it is al-Walid b. 'Abd al-Malik."],[3895,"A slave woman belonging to 'Umar ؓ had a name from the Persian names. 'Umar ؓ named her Jamila. 'Umar said: Between me and you is the Prophet ﷺ. So we came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to her: You are Jamila. 'Umar ؓ said: Take her, in spite of your nose."],[3896,"He was present at the spoils of Hunayn with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and his name was Ghurab. The Messenger of God named him Muslim."],[3897,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a land called Ghabara and said: It is Khadira."],[3898,"And Abu Bakr said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Al-A'mash, from Al-Hasan, from Jabir ؓ, something similar to it."],[3899,"My father sent me, and al-Abbas sent his son al-Fadl ؓ to the Prophet ﷺ ... and he mentioned the hadith. He said: When we came to them, they said: 'What is behind you? Asad or Said?'"],[3900,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey. A man approached. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw him, he said: 'What a bad brother of the clan' or 'what a bad man.' When he came close, he made room for him in his sitting place. When he got up and left, they said: 'O Messenger of God, when you saw him you said: \"What a bad brother of the clan\" or \"what a bad man,\" then you made room for him in your sitting place.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'He is a hypocrite; I treat him gently to fend off his hypocrisy, and I fear he may corrupt someone else against me.'"],[3901,"When one of you enters upon a group of people and room is made for him, let him sit, for it is only an honor from God, Mighty and Majestic, with which his Muslim brother has honored him. If no room is made for him, let him look for the widest place and sit there."],[3902,"The best of gatherings is the most spacious of them."],[3903,"He passed by a gathering on a road and said: 'Beware of sitting on roads, for they are the path of the Fire and of Satan.' Then he went on, so that they thought it was a firm command. Then he came back and said: 'Unless you fulfill the right of the road.' They said: 'What is the right of the road?' He said ﷺ: 'That you lower your gazes, guide the lost, and return the greeting of peace.'"],[3904,"He used to dislike a man sleeping on his stomach and a woman lying on her back."],[3906,"Abu Said ؓ was complaining of pain in his leg. His brother entered upon him while he had placed one leg over the other and was lying down. He struck him with his hand on his painful leg and hurt him. Abu Said said: 'You have hurt me! Did you not know that my leg is painful?' He said: 'Yes.' Abu Sa`id said: 'What made you do that?' He said: 'Did you not hear that the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from that?'"],[3907,"A bed was spread for Abu Ayyub al-Ansari on a flat roof. He ordered it to be taken down during part of the night, and it was brought down. He said: 'I almost spent the night with no protection for me.'"],[3908,"Whoever spends the night on a roof that has no barrier, protection from him is absolved. Whoever throws at night, protection from him is absolved. Whoever rides the sea while it is turbulent, protection from him is absolved."],[3909,"“Which of you would love never to be ill?” We hurried to answer, saying, “We would, O Messenger of God.” He said, “Would you love to be like braying donkeys?” The Prophet ﷺ changed color until we saw the change in his face. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Would you not love to be people of trial and expiations?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He ﷺ said, “By Him in whose hand is my soul, the believer is surely tried with affliction, and that is a mark of honor for him with God Most High. He is surely tried with affliction until he attains thereby a station with God Most High that he would not attain without being tried with it, and God Most High brings him to that station.\" (marfu')"],[3910,"'Amr b. Hurayth visited al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ. 'Ali ؓ said to him: “Do you visit al-Hasan while your heart holds what it holds?” 'Amr said: “You are not my Lord to turn my heart wherever you wish.” He said: “That does not prevent us from giving you sincere advice. I heard the Messenger ﷺ say: ‘No Muslim visits his brother but God Most High sends seventy thousand angels for him.’”"],[3911,"Deliberateness is from God, Most High, and haste is from Satan. There is nothing more full of excuses than God, Mighty and Majestic, and there is nothing more beloved to God, Most High, than praise."],[3912,"\"There is no contagion and no Haamah, and a sick person does not infect a healthy one.\""],[3913,"I entered with my father upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he whispered to him privately without me. I said: 'O father, what did the Messenger of God ﷺ say to you?' He said: 'He ﷺ said to me: \"When you intend a matter, you must be deliberate until God brings you a way out of your affair.\"'"],[3914,"until Allah brings you relief from your affair"],[3915,"When I was taken up to the heaven, I did not pass by a group of angels except that they said: 'O Muhammad, you should practice cupping.'"],[3916,"The parable of the righteous companion is like the parable of the owner of musk; if he does not give you some, some of its fragrance will reach you. And the parable of the evil companion is like the parable of the owner of the bellows; if he does not burn your clothes, some of its smell will reach you, or its odor will offend you."],[3917,"It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which of our companions is best? He ﷺ said: The one whose sight reminds you of Allah, whose speech increases you in good deeds, and whose actions remind you of the Hereafter."],[3918,"The womb is a branch from Me. Whoever maintains it, I maintain him, and whoever severs it, I sever him."],[3919,"Make your resting places good, make one head into two heads, and fear the crawling creatures before they make you fear them."],[3920,"Sheep are a blessing, camels are an honor for their owners, goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses, and the slave is your brother, so be good to him. If you see him overwhelmed, then help him."],[3921,"Sheep are a blessing, and camels are an honor for their owners."],[3922,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded the rich to keep sheep, and he commanded the poor to keep chickens."],[3923,"Sheep are a blessing."],[3924,"Among the worst of your slaves are the blacks; if they are hungry they steal, and if they are full they commit adultery."],[3925,"I brought the camels of zakah to the Prophet ﷺ, and he wiped my head and supplicated for good for me."],[3926,"I went out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ were sitting, and there was a small boy crying. The Prophet ﷺ said to Umar ؓ: 'Hold the child close to you, for he is lost.' So Umar ؓ held him close. While we were sitting, a woman came wailing, I think, saying: 'Oh my son!' and crying. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Call the woman, for she is the mother of the child, and she has uncovered her head; there is no veil on her head, out of grief for her son.' She came and took the child from Umar's lap while crying, and the child was in her lap. She turned, and when she saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, she said: 'Oh, what disgrace! Do I not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said then: 'Do you see this woman as merciful to her child?' His companions ؓ said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ; this is enough mercy.' He ﷺ said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, Allah the Exalted is more merciful to the believers than this woman is to her child.'"],[3927,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and some of them got a sparrow chick. The sparrow began to alight on their saddles, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that its chick be returned to it. Then he ﷺ said: 'Allah is more merciful to His servant than this sparrow is to its chick.'"],[3928,"By the One in whose hand is my soul, Allah does not place His mercy except upon a merciful one. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, all of us are merciful.' He said: 'It is not the mercy of any one of you specifically, until he has mercy on all people.'"],[3929,"A man passed by the Prophet ﷺ with two chicks of a bird, while their father was hovering over them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You took these two chicks while their father is hovering over them. Why did you not leave one of them for him, so that his eye might be cooled by it?'"],[3930,"Indeed Allah the Exalted will have mercy on His believing servant on the Day of Resurrection, with the mercy of a sparrow."],[3931,"Whoever buys something from the servants and his character does not match his own character, let him sell and buy until their character matches his. For people are of different dispositions. And do not torture the servants of Allah."],[3933,"Fear Allah, fear Allah, regarding those whom your right hands possess. Fill their bellies, clothe their backs, and speak to them gently."],[3934,"The first to enter Paradise will be a slave, if he obeys Allah the Exalted and obeys his master."],[3935,"Gabriel ﷺ kept advising me about the slave, until I thought that he would set a limit for him when they reach it, they would be freed."],[3936,"Whatever you lighten for your servant from his work, it will be a reward for you in your scales."],[3937,"The Prophet ﷺ gave Ali and Fatimah ؓ a servant and said: 'Be good to him, for I saw him praying.'"],[3938,"Obey your parents, even if they command you to leave your property. Do not abandon prayer deliberately, for whoever abandons prayer deliberately has disassociated himself from the protection of Allah, the Exalted. Beware of wine, for it is the key to every evil. Beware of disobedience, for it angers Allah, the Mighty and Sublime. Do not dispute authority with its people, even if you think that you are right. Spend on your family from your means, and do not raise your staff from them, and make them fear Allah, the Mighty and Sublime."],[3939,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said regarding the slaves: Honor them as you honor your children, and feed them from what you eat, and clothe them from what you wear."],[3940,"I was with the Commander of the Believers, Umar ؓ. He said: Go, and inform me who that is? He said: And when he ؓ sent a man on an errand, he would say: When you return, inform me of what I sent you for, and what is brought back to me. So I said: You commanded me to inform you who that is, and it is Suhayb ؓ, and with him is a slave woman. He ؓ said: Let him join us, even if a slave woman is with him."],[3941,"When a noble person of a people comes to you, honor him."],[3942,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade shaking hands with the polytheists, or giving them honorifics (kunyas), or welcoming them."],[3944,"We were with Abu Sa'id ؓ one day when all of a sudden Abdullah b. Umar ؓ entered, and I saw him looking changed, gloomy and sad, and upon him was the trace of dust. Abu Sa'id ؓ called for water for him and he performed ablution."],[3946,"Sawda al-Yamaniyya came to visit Aisha, and Hafsa bint Umar ؓ was with her. Sawda ؓ came in a fine appearance and good condition, wearing a shift of Yemeni striped cloth, and a veil likewise, and on her were two dots like lentils of aloe and saffron on her shoes. She (Alila) said: I caught up with women beautifying themselves with it. Hafsa said to Aisha ؓ: O Mother of the Believers, the Messenger of God ﷺ will come and see us while we are shabby, and this one between us is shining. She ؓ said: Fear God, O Hafsa, fear God, O Hafsa. She said: I will ruin her adornment. She ؓ said: Do it. (She said: What do you say?) And in Sawda's ear there was heaviness (deafness). Hafsa said to her: O Sawda, the one-eyed man (Dajjal) has come out. She said: Yes! And she was terrified, and began trembling. She said: Where can I hide? She said: Go to the tent—a tent of theirs made of palm leaves in which they cooked, and in it were cooking pots and spider webs. She went and hid there. The Messenger of God ﷺ came while the two of them were laughing, unable to speak from laughter. He ﷺ said: What is this laughter? Three times. They pointed with their hands toward the tent. He ﷺ went and found Sawda trembling. He said to her: O Sawda, what is wrong with you? She said: O Messenger of God, the one-eyed man has come out. He ﷺ said: He has not come out, and he will certainly come out. He has not come out, and he will certainly come out. (He has not come out, and he will certainly come out.) Then he ﷺ entered and brought her out, and began brushing the dust and spider webs from her."],[3947,"The heart of the son of Adam is like a sparrow, it flips over seven times in a day."],[3948,"A child is the fruit of the heart, a source of cowardice, miserliness, and sorrow."],[3949,"'Religion is sincere counsel.' They said: 'To whom, O Messenger of God?' He ﷺ said: 'To the Book of God, Exalted is He, to His Prophet, and to the leaders of the Muslims.'\" type=\"marfu'\""],[3950,"The dream is of three stations: of them is what a person talks to himself about, and it is nothing; and of them is what is from Satan, so if he sees something he dislikes, let him seek refuge in God from Satan the accursed, and let him spit on his left side, for it will not harm him after that; and of them is good news from God. And the dream of a Muslim is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood. So let him present it to a sincere person of sound judgment, and let him say good, and let him interpret it well."],[3951,"When one of you sees a dream, let him present it to one who is sincere, and let him say good, and let him interpret it well."],[3952,"Safiyya said while she was with her family: I saw as if I and this one whom Allah sent, and an angel steering us with his wing. They rejected her vision and spoke harshly to her."],[3953,"I saw three moons fall into my chamber, or he said: into my lap. Abu Bakr ؓ said: Good. Yahya b. Sa'id al-Ansari said: I heard people saying that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was buried in the house of 'A'isha ؓ, Abu Bakr ؓ said: This is one of your moons, and the best of them."],[3954,"Abu Bakr ؓ was the best interpreter of dreams of this ummah after the Prophet ﷺ."],[3955,"I saw as if three moons fell into my chamber. I asked Abu Bakr ؓ, and he said: O 'A'isha, if your vision is true, three of the best people on earth will be buried in your house. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died and was buried, Abu Bakr ؓ said to me: O 'A'isha, this is the best of your moons, and it is one of them."],[3956,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us and mentioned a long hadith, in which he said: Whoever claims to have seen a dream that he did not see is like one who bears false witness, and on the Day of Resurrection he will be tasked with tying two grains of barley together, and he will be punished until he ties them, but he will never be able to tie them."],[3957,"I heard Abu Hurayra ؓ say to Ibn 'Abbas ؓ: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The dream of a Muslim is one of forty parts of prophethood. Ibn 'Abbas ؓ said: Of sixty. Abu Hurayra ؓ said: He heard me say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, and he says: Of sixty? Ibn 'Abbas ؓ said: And I say: Al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib ؓ said it."],[3958,"The dream of a believer is glad tidings from Allah Most High, and one of forty-six parts of prophethood. He said: I narrated it to Ibn 'Abbas ؓ, and he said: Al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib told me: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: One of fifty parts of prophethood."],[3959,"The dreams of prophets are true."],[3960,"While I was drawing water tonight, some black sheep and some light-colored sheep came to me. Abu Bakr ؓ came and drew a bucket or two, in which there was weakness; may Allah forgive him. Then 'Umar ؓ came and turned it into a large bucket, filled the troughs and quenched the drinkers. I have never seen a stronger man among people draw water better than him. I interpreted the black sheep as the Arabs and the light-colored sheep as the non-Arabs."],[3961,"I saw in a dream, as a sleeper sees, black sheep followed by light-colored sheep. I interpreted the black as the Arabs and the light-colored as the non-Arabs."],[3962,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: I saw in a dream that my head was cut off, and I was looking at it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed and said: With which eye were you looking at your head when it was cut off? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not remain long after that until he passed away. They interpreted the cutting of his head as the death of the Prophet ﷺ, and his looking as following his Sunnah."],[3963,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen to fight them and call them, and when they said: There is no god but Allah, their blood and wealth became forbidden to me."],[3964,"Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, his blood is forbidden to me except for three: the one who abandons his religion, the married adulterer, and one who kills a soul unjustly."],[3965,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'I have a hypocrite neighbor who does such-and-such.' He ﷺ said: 'Does he say: There is no god but Allah?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'From killing those I have been forbidden.'"],[3966,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a sermon and mentioned a long hadith, in which he said: 'Indeed, my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, has commanded me to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah. If they say it, they protect from me their blood and their wealth, except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah, Mighty and Majestic.'"],[3967,"Abu Bakr met Talha and said: 'Why do I see you this morning looking gloomy?' He said: 'No, except for a word I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Indeed it is an obligation (or a cause of salvation), but I did not ask him about it.' He said: 'But I know it.' He said: 'What is it?' He said: 'There is no god but Allah.'"],[3968,"I was told that Abu Bakr met Talha."],[3969,"Uqba b. Amir ؓ came to Mu'awiya while he was in Jerusalem. He did not stay long before he left. He was sought but not found. He said: 'So we came to him, and there he was praying in an open area of land. He said: What brought you? We said: We came to renew our covenant with you, or to fulfill something of your right. He said ؓ: I have your reward for it. We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he mentioned a hadith. He said: Then Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ said: O Ibn Amir, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah, his heart confirming his tongue, will enter through whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes.'"],[3970,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a sermon and mentioned the hadith, and in it he said: 'O people, whoever meets Allah, the Exalted, while he testifies that there is no god but Allah sincerely, will enter Paradise.' Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ stood up and said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, how does one make it sincere? Will he not mix with it other than it? Explain to us so that we may know it.' He ﷺ said: 'Eagerness for this world and amassing it without its right, being pleased with it, and people who say the sayings of the learned but do the deeds of the wicked. Whoever meets Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and there is nothing of these traits in him, saying: There is no god but Allah, will enter Paradise.'"],[3971,"Whoever dies believing in Allah and the Last Day, it will be said to him: Enter Paradise through whichever of the eight gates of Paradise you wish."],[3972,"Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ came to us in Yemen and said: 'I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to you: that you worship Allah, the Exalted, and do not associate anything with Him, and that you obey me; I will not spare you any good. And indeed the return is to Allah, the Exalted, and to Paradise and the Fire: an abode without departing, everlasting without death.'"],[3973,"The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Umar ؓ : \"Gather for me those of Quraysh who are here.\" So he gathered them. Then he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, shall you go out to them or shall they enter?\" He ﷺ said: \"Rather, I will go out to them.\" So he went out and said ﷺ : \"O assembly of Quraysh, is there anyone among you other than yourselves?\" They said: \"No, except the sons of our sisters.\" He ﷺ said: \"The son of a people's sister is from them.\" Then he ﷺ said: \"O assembly of Quraysh, know that the people most entitled to the Prophet are the God-fearing. So beware lest the people come on the Day of Resurrection with deeds while you come with the worldly life, carrying it, and I turn my face away from you.\" Then he ﷺ recited: \"Indeed the people most entitled to Abraham are those who followed him and this Prophet.\""],[3974,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have left no desire, nor lust, except that I have committed it.' He ﷺ said: 'Do you not testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah?' – three times – He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'That suffices.'"],[3975,"Marwan b. al-Hakam said to Ayman b. Khuraym: 'Will you not come out and fight with us?' He said: 'My father and my uncle witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and they enjoined me not to fight anyone who testifies that there is no god but Allah. If you bring me a guarantee of safety from the Fire, I will fight with you.' He said: 'Go, for we have no need of you.'"],[3976,"When Marwan fought al-Dahhak b. Qays, he sent to Ayman b. Khuraym al-Asadi and said: 'We would like you to fight with us.' He said: 'My father and my uncle witnessed Badr and enjoined me not to fight anyone who testifies that there is no god but Allah. If you bring me a guarantee, I will fight with you.' He said: 'Go,' and he spoke ill of him and insulted him. Then Ayman b. Khuraym began to say: 'I am not one to kill a man who prays, on the authority of another from Quraysh; to him his authority, and to me my sin. I seek refuge in Allah from ignorance and recklessness. Should I kill a Muslim for no reason? It will not benefit me as long as I live.'"],[3977,"There is no loneliness upon the people of \"There is no god but Allah\" in their graves, and it is as if I see the people of \"There is no god but Allah\" shaking off the dust from their heads and saying: \"Praise be to Allah who has removed sorrow from us.\""],[3978,"\"There is no god but Allah\" protects the servant from the wrath of Allah (Mighty and Majestic) as long as they do not prefer the compassion of their worldly life over their religion. If they do that, then say, \"There is no god but Allah\" (Mighty and Majestic), Allah (Mighty and Majestic) says: \"You have lied.\""],[3979,"Whoever says, \"There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent,\" one hundred times, no sin will follow him that day, nor will any deed outstrip him."],[3980,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he descended a mountain pass, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was riding alone. When the road opened up for him, he laughed and said, \"Allahu Akbar,\" so we said, \"Allahu Akbar\" because of his takbir. Then he traveled a short distance, then he laughed and said, \"Allahu Akbar,\" so we said, \"Allahu Akbar\" because of his takbir. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled a short distance, then he laughed and said, \"Allahu Akbar,\" so we said, \"Allahu Akbar\" because of his takbir. Then we caught up with him ﷺ, and the people said: \"We said 'Allahu Akbar' because of your takbir, but we do not know what made you laugh.\" He ﷺ said: \"Jibril ﷺ came to me, and when the road opened up, Jibril (peace and blessings be upon him) turned to me and said: 'Rejoice and give good news: whoever says, \"There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner,\" will enter Paradise and be forbidden from the Fire.'\""],[3981,"\"O so-and-so, did you do such and such?\" He said: \"No, by the One besides whom there is no god, I did not do it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ knew that he had done it. He repeated it to him several times, and each time he said: \"No, by the One besides whom there is no god, I did not do it,\" while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ knew that he had done it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Your sin has been expiated by your affirmation of 'There is no god but Allah.'\""],[3982,"\"If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much, and you would go out crying out in supplication, not knowing whether you will be saved or not.\""],[3983,"Supplication is the believer's weapon, the pillar of the religion, and the light of the heavens and the earth."],[3984,"From Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar ؓ. Hammad said: \"Thabit did not hear it from Ibn 'Umar ؓ; between them is a man.\""],[3985,"Whoever says eleven times: \"There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, the One, the Eternal Refuge; He neither begets nor is born, nor is there to Him any equivalent,\" Allah (Blessed and Exalted) will record for him two thousand, two thousand good deeds."],[3986,"Supplication is the believer's weapon, the pillar of the religion, and the light of the heavens and the earth."],[3987,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu al-Nadr al-Tammar narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us with it. (113) And a hadith about its virtue will come, Allah willing, in the chapter on seeking forgiveness."],[3988,"\"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Hisham b. al-Mughirah used to feed food, entertain guests, maintain kinship ties, and free captives\"—she meant prisoners—\"and if he had lived to see Islam, he would have embraced it. Does he have any reward for that?\" She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Your uncle used to give for the sake of the world, its mention, and its beauty, and he never said: 'My Lord, forgive me my sin on the Day of Judgment.'\""],[3990,"Islam will come on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah (Mighty and Majestic) will say: \"You are Islam and I am as-Salam (the Source of Peace). Today, through you I give, and through you I take.\""],[3991,"He passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said to him: \"O Harith, how have you entered upon the morning?\" He replied: \"I have entered upon the morning as a true believer.\" He ﷺ said: \"Consider what you say, for everything has a reality. So what is your reality?\" He ؓ said: \"I have turned myself away from the world, spending my day thirsty and my night awake. It is as if I am looking at the Throne of my Lord appearing, and as if I am looking at the people of Paradise visiting one another therein, and as if I am looking at the people of the Fire howling therein—meaning, crying out.\" He ﷺ said: \"O Harith, you have come to know, so adhere to it,\" three times."],[3992,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Submit (become Muslim) and you will be safe.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam?\" He ﷺ said: \"That you submit your heart to Allah (Blessed and Exalted), and that the Muslims be safe from your tongue and your hand.\" He said: \"Which Islam is best?\" He said: \"Iman (faith).\" He said: \"What is Iman?\" He ﷺ said: \"That you believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and in the Resurrection after death.\" He said: \"Which Iman is best?\" He said: \"Hijrah (migration).\" He said: \"What is hijrah?\" He said: \"That you abandon sin.\" He said: \"Which hijrah is best?\" He said: \"Jihad.\" He said: \"What is jihad?\" He said: \"That you fight the disbelievers when you meet them, then you do not act treacherously with the spoils and do not show cowardice.\" Then two deeds are among the best of deeds, unless they are equaled by an accepted Hajj or an Umrah."],[3993,"From your tongue and your hand."],[3994,"Then you do not act treacherously with the spoils and do not show cowardice."],[3995,"And the Resurrection after death, and Paradise, and the Fire."],[3996,"It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, which Islam is best?\" He ﷺ said: \"The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.\" It was said: \"Which Iman is best?\" He ﷺ said: \"Patience and magnanimity.\" It was said: \"Which believers have the most Iman?\" He ﷺ said: \"The best of them in character.\" It was said: \"Which jihad is best?\" He ﷺ said: \"The one whose horse is slaughtered and whose blood is shed.\" It was said: \"Which prayer is best?\" He ﷺ said: \"Long devotion (standing).\" It was said: \"Which charity is best?\" He ﷺ said: \"The effort of one with little.\" It was said: \"Which hijrah is best?\" He said: \"That you abandon what Allah has forbidden you.\" They narrated it in abridged form."],[3997,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about Iman. He said: \"Patience and magnanimity.\""],[3998,"Islam is outward, and Iman is in the heart. Then he pointed with his hand to his chest: \"Taqwa (God-consciousness) is here, taqwa is here.\""],[4000,"Allah (Exalted) appoints two angels over His believing servant, who record his deeds. When Allah (Mighty and Majestic) takes the soul of His believing servant, they say: \"O Lord, You appointed us over Your believing servant to record his deeds, and You have taken him to You. Grant us permission to ascend to heaven.\" He (Glorified and Exalted) says: \"My heaven is full of My angels who glorify Me.\" They say: \"Grant us permission to dwell on earth.\" He (Mighty and Majestic) says: \"My earth is full of My creation who glorify Me. But stand at the grave of My servant, and glorify Me, declare My oneness, magnify Me, and praise Me until the Day of Resurrection, and write it for My servant.\""],[4001,"\"O Abdullah, do you know which of the bonds of Islam is most firm?\" I said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He ﷺ said: \"Allegiance for the sake of Allah (Mighty and Majestic), love for the sake of Allah (Mighty and Majestic), and hatred for the sake of Allah (Blessed and Exalted).\""],[4002,"And Abu Bakr said: Zayd b. al-Hubab narrated to us, al-Sa'q b. Hazn al-Bakri narrated to us with it. :"],[4003,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would order his bed to be prepared for him and it would be spread for him, and he would face the qiblah. When he retired to it, he would place his right hand under his cheek, then he would whisper, and we did not know what he was saying. Then at the end of that, he would raise his voice and say: \"O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Mighty Throne, God and Lord of everything, Revealer of the Torah, the Gospel and the Furqan, Splitter of the grain and the date-stone, I seek refuge in You from the evil of everything for which You hold the forelock. O Allah, You are the First, so there is nothing before You, and You are the Last, so there is nothing after You, and You are the Outward, so there is nothing above You, and You are the Inward, so there is nothing below You. Settle our debt and make us free from poverty.\""],[4004,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when a bearer of good news came from a military expedition and informed him of the victory of Allah Almighty which He granted to his expedition, and of the conquest of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, which He opened for them. He said: O Messenger of Allah, while we were seeking the enemy, and Allah Almighty had defeated them, I caught up with a man with a sword. When he sensed that the sword had reached him, he turned while running and said: 'I am a Muslim,' so I killed him. But, O Prophet of Allah, he was only seeking protection. He ﷺ said: 'Did you not split open his heart to see whether he was truthful or lying?' He said: If I had split open his heart, it would not have informed me; is his heart anything but a lump of flesh? He said: 'So you killed him, not knowing what was in his heart, nor believing his tongue?' He said: O Messenger of Allah, ask forgiveness for me. He ﷺ said: 'I will not ask forgiveness for you.' Then he died, and they buried him, but he appeared on the surface of the earth three times. When his people saw that, they felt ashamed and feared (from what befell his burden), so they threw him into one of those mountain passes."],[4005,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ"],[4006,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out an expedition, and victory was granted to it. They sent their bearer of good news to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. While he was informing him of the victory of Allah Almighty (for them) and of the number of those whom Allah killed among them, he said: I singled out a man from among them. When I approached him to kill him, he said: 'I am a Muslim,' but I killed him. He ﷺ said: 'So you killed him after he said, \"I am a Muslim\"?' He said: O Messenger of Allah, he only said that seeking protection. He ﷺ said: 'Why did you not split open his heart?' He said: And would I know that, O Messenger of Allah? He ﷺ said: 'You did not believe his tongue, nor did you know his heart. You are indeed his killer. Leave me, and do not accompany me.' He said: Then the man died, and the earth threw him out twice, so he was cast into one of those valleys. Some of the people of knowledge said: The earth conceals those who are more putrid than him, but it is a lesson."],[4007,"When one of you levels his spear at a man, and if it is at the hollow of his neck and he says: 'There is no god but Allah,' then let him lift the spear away from him."],[4008,"Whoever guarantees me six things, I guarantee him Paradise. It was said: And what are they, O Messenger of Allah? He ﷺ said: When he speaks, he is truthful; when he promises, he fulfills; when he is entrusted, he is faithful; and he lowers his gaze, guards his private parts, and restrains his hand."],[4009,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: What saves the servant from the Fire? He said: 'Faith in Allah.' I said: O Prophet of Allah, is there any action with faith? He said: 'That you give from what Allah has provided you, or that he gives from what Allah has provided him.' I said: O Prophet of Allah, what if he is poor and cannot find anything to give? He said: 'He enjoins good and forbids evil.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if he is unable to enjoin good or forbid evil? He ﷺ said: 'Then let him do something for an inept person.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if he is inept and cannot do anything? He ﷺ said: 'He helps one who is overcome.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if he is weak and cannot help one who is overcome? He ﷺ said: 'Do you want to leave any good for your companion?' He ﷺ said: 'Then let him withhold his harm from people.' I said: O Prophet of Allah, what if he does this, will he enter Paradise? He said: 'There is no believer who performs any of these traits but that it will take him by the hand until he enters Paradise.'"],[4010,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him, and I said to him: On the condition that if I leave my religion and enter your religion, Allah Almighty will not punish me in the Hereafter? He ﷺ said: 'Yes.'"],[4011,"Let no man among you neglect to perform a thousand good deeds for Allah, that is, to glorify Allah a thousand times. For he will not do the like of that, if Allah, Exalted is He, wills, in his day of sins, and whatever good he does besides that will be abundant."],[4012,"I was supporting the Prophet ﷺ against my chest, and he ﷺ said: 'Whoever says, \"There is no god but Allah,\" and it is sealed for him with it, will enter Paradise.'"],[4013,"The Messenger of Allah sent him on a military expedition, and they took captives from the Bedouins. When they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, some of them claimed that they were already Muslims. He said: 'Who knows that?' They said: 'Iyad heard it from us.' He ﷺ said: 'O Iyad, did you hear it or witness it?' I said: I heard the call to prayer: 'and there is no god but Allah.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set them free."],[4014,"Go out and announce among the people: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah, Paradise is guaranteed for him. He (Abu Bakr) ؓ said: So I went out, and Umar b. al-Khattab met me and said, 'What is the matter with you, O Abu Bakr?' I said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ told me...' and he mentioned it. He said: Then he (Umar) said, 'Go back, for I fear that they will rely upon it.' So I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'What made you return?' I informed him of Umar's ؓ statement, and he ﷺ said, 'He spoke the truth.'"],[4015,"Whoever comes with the testimony that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, the Fire is forbidden for him."],[4016,"An old man came forward, leaning on a staff, until he stood before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have committed treacherous acts and immoral deeds. Will I be forgiven?' He ﷺ said, 'Do you not bear witness that there is no god but Allah?' He said, 'Yes, and I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah.' He ﷺ said, 'Your treacherous acts and immoral deeds have been forgiven.'"],[4018,"It was said to Wahb b. Munabbih, 'Is not the key to Paradise: there is no god but Allah?' He said, 'Yes, but there is no key except that it has teeth. Whoever comes to the door with its teeth, it will be opened for him, and whoever does not come to the door with its teeth, it will not be opened for him.'"],[4019,"Faith is a leader, (and action is) a driver, and the soul is restive between them. If the leader leads but the driver does not drive, that does not avail anything. And if the driver drives, the soul follows him willingly or unwillingly."],[4020,"When he was on his deathbed, I said to him, 'Do I not see that you are dying?' He said, 'Yes, and this is a bad time for lying. Whoever dies while convinced of three things: knowing that Allah, Most High, is the Truth, that the Hour is coming, and that Allah will resurrect those in the graves.' He said: Then he said something in which he encouraged them, if it was not: 'except that he will be forgiven,' but I am not sure."],[4021,"Whoever among you knows that I have power to forgive sins, I forgive him and do not care, as long as he does not associate anything with Me."],[4022,"Three things: whoever does not have them, then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will forgive whatever else He wills for him: whoever dies without associating anything with Allah, and was not a sorcerer following sorcerers, and did not bear malice against his brother."],[4023,"There was a man called Yazid b. Umayra al-Saksaki, and he was a student of Mu'adh b. Jabal. He mentioned the hadith. He said: Mu'adh ؓ passed away and Yazid joined al-Kufa. He came to the gathering of Abdullah b. Mas'ud ؓ but he was not there. They began discussing faith. Some of them said, 'If I testify that I am a believer, I would testify that I am in Paradise.' Yazid said, 'I testify that I am a believer, but I do not testify that I am in Paradise.' Then Ibn Mas'ud ؓ came and was informed of that. Ibn Mas'ud ؓ said to Yazid, 'Is that so?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'And why is that?' Yazid said, 'O Abu Abd al-Rahman, Allah Most High says: \"Indeed, those who believe, and those who are Jews, and the Sabians, and the Christians, and the Magians, and those who associate others with Allah...\" Which of these are you, O Abu Abd al-Rahman?' Ibn Mas'ud said, 'From those who believe.' Yazid said, 'Yes, truly.' Then Ibn Mas'ud said to Yazid, 'By Allah, were you a student of Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ?' He said, 'Yes.' Ibn Mas'ud ؓ said, 'Mu'adh was a nation, devoutly obedient, upright, and he was not of the polytheists.' His companions said, 'Indeed, Ibrahim was a nation, devoutly obedient to Allah.' Ibn Mas'ud ؓ said, 'Mu'adh ؓ was a nation, devoutly obedient to Allah, upright.'"],[4024,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'I owe a believing slave for my mother, and I have a black non-Arab slave.' He ﷺ said, 'Bring her.' So he brought her, and he ﷺ said, 'Do you testify that there is no god but Allah?' She said, 'Yes.' He ﷺ said, 'Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah?' She said, 'Yes.' He ﷺ said, 'Set her free.'"],[4025,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me, 'You and I will drink milk whose color has not changed.' I said, 'How does Allah revive the dead?' He ﷺ said, 'Have you not passed by a barren land, then passed by it lush, then passed by it barren, then passed by it lush?' I said, 'Yes.' He ﷺ said, 'Thus is the resurrection.' He said: I said, 'How can I know that I am a believer?' He ﷺ said, 'There is no one from this nation—or from my nation—who does a good deed and knows that it is good, and that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will reward him for it with good, or does an evil deed and knows that Allah, Most High, will recompense him for it with evil or forgive it, except that he is a believer.'"],[4026,"The polytheists seized 'Ammar b. Yasir ؓ and tortured him, and he conceded to them in some of what they wanted from him. He complained about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"How do you find your heart?\" He said: \"At peace with faith.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Then if they return, you return.\""],[4027,"I said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"Advise me.\" He said: \"Establish the prayer, give the zakah, fast Ramadan, perform Hajj and 'Umrah, enjoin good, and forbid evil.\""],[4028,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ advising one of his family members, saying ﷺ: \"Do not associate anything with Allah, even if you are cut into pieces or burned with fire. And beware of disobedience, for it incurs the wrath of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic.\""],[4029,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him a supplication and commanded him to keep reciting it with his family every day. He ﷺ said: 'Say when you enter the morning: Here I am, O Allah, here I am. Here I am, and at Your service; all good is in Your Hands, and from You, and for You, and to You. Whatever word I speak, whatever deed I do, whatever vow I make, whatever oath I swear, Your will precedes all of that. What You will happens, and what You do not will does not happen. There is no might nor power except with You. Surely You have power over all things. O Allah, whatever prayer I pray, let it be for the one upon whom You have prayed; whatever curse I utter, let it be upon the one whom You have cursed. You are my protector in this world and the Hereafter. Cause me to die as a Muslim and join me with the righteous.'"],[4030,"'Abd said: 'Umar b. Sa'id narrated to us, \"other than Sa'id\" narrated to us from al-Zuhri, that the one who gave this advice was Thawban ؓ."],[4031,"Modesty is from faith."],[4032,"Patience is half of faith, gratitude is two-thirds of faith, and certainty is all of faith."],[4033,"O these people, indeed simplicity in dress and appearance is from faith."],[4034,"The handles of faith are four, and Islam follows them. The handles of faith are: to believe in Allah alone, and in Muhammad and what he brought; to believe in Allah and know that you will be resurrected after death; to establish prayer; to give zakah; to fast Ramadan; to perform Hajj to the House; and to strive in the path of Allah, the Exalted."],[4035,"The handles of Islam and the foundations of the religion are three, upon which Islam is built. Whoever abandons one of them is a disbeliever whose blood is lawful: the testimony that there is no god but Allah, establishing the obligatory prayer, and fasting Ramadan. Then Ibn 'Abbas ؓ said: \"You find a man with much wealth who does not give zakah, yet he remains a disbeliever, and his blood is not lawful. And you find a man with much wealth who has not performed Hajj, yet he remains a disbeliever, and his blood is not lawful.\""],[4036,"Indeed, before the Most Merciful, Blessed and Exalted, there is a tablet in which there are three hundred and fifteen laws. The Most Merciful says: \"By My might and majesty, no servant of My servants will come to Me not associating anything with Me, having one of them, except that he enters Paradise.\""],[4037,"Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad b. Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri' narrated to us with it. :, :"],[4038,"Whoever departs this world upon sincerity to Allah, His worship without associating any partner, the establishment of prayer, and the giving of zakah departs it while Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is pleased with him. Anas said: 'That is the religion of Allah which the messengers brought and conveyed from their Lord before the confusion of reports and the divergence of desires. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: \"If they repent\" — he said: they cast off rivals and their worship, established prayer, and gave zakah, so leave their way open.'"],[4039,"I was guarding the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night when I stood up, so he took my hand and leaned on it. We came upon a man praying in the mosque raising his voice. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Perhaps he is showing off.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, he is praying and supplicating.' He ﷺ released my hand and said: 'You will never attain this matter by overpowering,' or he said 'by harshness.' He said: Then we went out another night and passed by a man praying raising his voice. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, perhaps he is showing off.' He ﷺ said: 'No, rather he is awwah (one who sighs frequently out of fear of Allah).' He said: The man was 'Abd Allah Dhu al-Bijadayn ؓ, and the other was a bedouin."],[4041,"There were three of us who accompanied the Prophet ﷺ: Buraydah, Mihjan, and Sukbah. Mihjan said to Buraydah: 'Will you not pray as Sukbah prays?' He said: 'No. I saw myself coming with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Uhud, walking along with his hand in mine, when he ﷺ saw a man praying. He said: \"Do you consider him earnest? Do you consider him sincere?\" I went to praise him, but when we drew near he ﷺ withdrew his hand from mine and said: \"Woe to you! Be silent, do not let him hear you lest you destroy him. The best of your religion is its easiest.\"'"],[4042,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed the people and said: 'Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has given every possessor of a right his right. Allah has ordained obligations, established sunnahs, set limits, made lawful what is lawful, made unlawful what is unlawful, and legislated Islam, making it easy, spacious, and wide, not narrow. O people, there is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant. Whoever breaks the protection of Allah, the Exalted, He will seek him out; whoever breaks my protection, I will dispute with him; and whoever I dispute with, I will overcome him with proof. Whoever breaks my protection will not attain my intercession, nor will he come to me at the Pond. Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has not permitted killing except in three cases: an apostate after faith, a fornicator after being married, or a murderer of a soul, who is killed for it. O Allah, have I conveyed?'"],[4043,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed the people and said: 'Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has given every possessor of a right his right. Allah has ordained obligations, established sunnahs, set limits, made lawful what is lawful, made unlawful what is unlawful, and legislated Islam, making it easy, spacious, and wide, not narrow. O people, there is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant. Whoever breaks the protection of Allah, the Exalted, He will seek him out; whoever breaks my protection, I will dispute with him; and whoever I dispute with, I will overcome him with proof. Whoever breaks my protection will not attain my intercession, nor will he come to me at the Pond. Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has not permitted killing except in three cases: an apostate after faith, a fornicator after being married, or a murderer of a soul, who is killed for it. O Allah, have I conveyed?'"],[4044,"'When I narrate to you a hadith, I inform you of its confirmation from the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: No servant says: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest, and blessed is Allah, except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, appoints over them an angel who places them under his wings and ascends with them to the sky. They do not pass by any assembly of angels except that they seek forgiveness for the one who said them, until they greet the Face of the Most Merciful, Mighty and Majestic. Then Abdullah recited: To Him ascend the good words, and the righteous deed raises it.'"],[4045,"I pledge allegiance to you on the condition that you do not associate anything with Allah, do not steal, do not commit adultery, and do not kill the soul that Allah has forbidden except with right. Whoever among you commits any of this and his punishment is hastened for him, it is an expiation. Whoever is concealed, his affair is up to Allah: if He wills, He punishes him, and if He wills, He has mercy on him. Whoever does not commit any of it, I guarantee him Paradise.' This is the wording of 'Abd al-Wahid. In the narration of Hammad: 'Do you know upon what you have pledged allegiance to me?' They said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He ﷺ said: 'Upon that you do not associate anything with Allah,' and the rest is similar, and he said: 'Then it is an expiation for his sin,' and he said: 'Then his reckoning is upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic.'"],[4046,"The parable of the believer is like the palm tree: if you consult it, it benefits you; if you walk with it, it benefits you; if you share with it, it benefits you."],[4047,"Suwayd, that is Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us: Fudayl b. 'Iyad narrated to us, from Layth, similarly."],[4048,"The believer among the people of faith is like the head to the body: the believer suffers for the people of faith as the body suffers for what is in the head."],[4049,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say when he asked him: 'What is faith, O Messenger of Allah?' He ﷺ said: 'Faith is that you believe in Allah, the Exalted, and His Messenger.' Then he asked him a second time and he said the same. Then he asked him a third time and he said: 'Would you like me to tell you what pure faith is?' He said: 'That is what I wanted.' He ﷺ said: 'Pure faith is that when you do wrong or oppress anyone—your servant, your slave woman, or any of the Muslims—you give charity and fast, and when you do good you rejoice.'"],[4050,"Every trait upon which the believer is sealed or folded, except treachery and lying."],[4051,"We do not know it as ascribed and raised except through 'Ali b. Hashim."],[4052,"A servant does not attain pure faith until he abandons jesting and lying, and abandons disputation, even if he is in the right."],[4053,"Islam is eight shares: Islam is a share, prayer is a share, zakah is a share, Hajj is a share, fasting Ramadan is a share, commanding good is a share, forbidding evil is a share, and jihad in the path of Allah the Exalted is a share. And whoever has no share has failed."],[4054,"(M) Al-Bazzar said: And Muhammad b. Sa'id b. Yazid b. Ibrahim narrated to us, Ya'qub b. Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yazid b. 'Ata' narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Silah, from Hudhayfah ؓ, from the Prophet ﷺ as marfu'. Al-Bazzar said: No one traced it back except Yazid. Al-Daraqutni and others said: The correct view is that it is mawquf."],[4055,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Do you know which of the people of faith is best in faith?' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the angels.' He ﷺ said: 'They are so, and that is rightfully theirs, and what prevents them, for Allah the Exalted has placed them in the station He placed them. But others.' We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the prophets.' He ﷺ said: 'They are so, and that is rightfully theirs, but others.' We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, who are they?' He ﷺ said: 'A people who come after me, while they are in the loins of men. They believe in me though they have not seen me, and they find the hanging page and act according to what is in it. These are the best of the people of faith in faith.'"],[4056,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Tell me about the best of the people of faith in faith.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the angels.' He ﷺ said: 'They are so, and that is rightfully theirs, and what prevents them, for Allah the Exalted has placed them in the station He placed them. But others.' They said: 'The prophets whom Allah the Exalted honored with His message and prophethood.' He ﷺ said: 'They are so, and that is rightfully theirs, and what prevents them, for Allah the Exalted has placed them in the station He placed them.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the martyrs who were martyred with the prophets.' He ﷺ said: 'They are so, and that is rightfully theirs, and what prevents them, for Allah the Exalted honored them with martyrdom with the prophets. But others.' They said: 'Who then, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Peoples in the loins of men.'"],[4057,"Abu Musa Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, Muhammad b. Abi Humayd narrated to us, with it."],[4058,"I was sitting with 'Abdullah ؓ, and they mentioned the companions of the Prophet ﷺ and the virtue that came before them. He said: 'Indeed, the matter of Muhammad ﷺ was clear to whoever saw him. And by the One besides whom there is no god, there is no one better than faith in the unseen.' Then he recited: 'Alif Lam Mim. This is the Book about which there is no doubt, a guidance for the God-fearing... to the successful.'"],[4059,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have an aged father and brothers, so I go to them that perhaps they may become Muslim, and I bring them to you.' He ﷺ said: 'If they become Muslim, it is better for them. And if they refuse, Islam is vast and wide.'"],[4060,"The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer, and no one plunders a plunder of high value at which people raise their heads while he is a believer."],[4061,"I asked Jabir ؓ: 'Did you hear the Prophet ﷺ say: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer?' He said: 'I did not hear it, but I was told that Ibn 'Umar ؓ used to say it.'"],[4062,"When you see an adulterer and a wine-drinker, what do you say about them? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: These are obscenities, and in them is punishment. Shall I not inform you of the greatest of major sins? We said: Yes. He ﷺ said: Associating partners with Allah. Allah the Exalted said: 'And whoever associates partners with Allah has certainly fabricated a tremendous sin' [Quran 4:48]. And disobedience to parents. Then the Mighty and Majestic said: 'Be grateful to Me and to your parents; to Me is the final destination' [Quran 31:14]. He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was reclining, so he sat up straight and said: Indeed, and false speech; indeed, and false speech."],[4063,"It is disbelief in Allah for one to claim a lineage that is not known, and it is disbelief in Allah to disown a lineage, even if it is distant."],[4064,"Five will not enter Paradise: a habitual wine-drinker, one who severs family ties, one who believes in magic, one who reminds others of his favors, and a soothsayer."],[4065,"Whoever deceives a man concerning his family or his servant is not from us."],[4066,"Ibn Abbas ؓ was asked about major sins. He said: Everything that Allah has forbidden in the Quran is a major sin, and he mentioned the gaze."],[4067,"There is no servant who worships Allah the Exalted without associating anything with Him, establishes prayer, gives zakat, fasts Ramadan, and avoids major sins, except that he will enter Paradise. It was said: What are the major sins? He ﷺ said: Associating partners with Allah the Exalted, and killing a soul."],[4068,"Whoever walks to the authority of Allah the Exalted on earth to humiliate it, Allah the Exalted will humiliate his neck on the Day of Resurrection along with the punishment stored for him. And the authority of Allah the Mighty and Majestic is the Book of Allah the Exalted and the Sunnah of His Prophet ﷺ."],[4069,"'When I narrate to you a hadith, I inform you of its confirmation from the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: No servant says: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest, and blessed is Allah, except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, appoints over them an angel who places them under his wings and ascends with them to the sky. They do not pass by any assembly of angels except that they seek forgiveness for the one who said them, until they greet the Face of the Most Merciful, Mighty and Majestic. Then Abdullah recited: To Him ascend the good words, and the righteous deed raises it.'"],[4070,"Indeed, Allah the Exalted has imposed obligations, so do not neglect them; He has set limits, so do not transgress them; He has forbidden things, so do not violate them; and He has remained silent about things out of mercy for you, not out of forgetfulness, so do not seek them out."],[4071,"When you enter upon your Muslim brother, eat from his food and do not ask, and drink from his drink and do not ask."],[4072,"Three things are from the foundations of the religion: gathering behind every righteous and sinful person, praying over whoever dies from the people of the Qiblah, and striving under the leadership of whoever is in authority; you will have your reward."],[4073,"Whoever makes lawful the sacred things of the Quran has not believed in the Quran."],[4074,"Ata' reported from Mujahid, from Suhayb. Ibn 'Adi mentioned it."],[4075,"Indeed, a man said to his brother: 'May Allah not forgive you.' It was said to him: 'Rather, may Allah not forgive you.'"],[4076,"A man stepped on a man's neck while he was prostrating. He said: 'You stepped on my neck while I am prostrating? By Allah, may Allah not forgive you.' He said: 'He swore against Allah, Exalted is He, so He forgave him.'"],[4077,"Mu'awiyah said to Ibn 'Abbas ؓ: 'Are you upon the religion of Ibn Abi Talib?' He said: 'No, nor the religion of Ibn 'Affan.' Mu'awiyah said: 'Then upon which religion are you?' He said: 'Upon the religion of Muhammad ﷺ.'"],[4078,"A man came to Abu Dharr ؓ and asked him about faith. He recited: 'It is not righteousness that you turn your faces toward the east or the west, but righteousness is [in] one who believes in Allah' until His saying, Exalted is He: 'Those are the ones who have been true, and it is those who are the righteous.' The man said: 'I did not ask you about righteousness.' Abu Dharr ؓ said: 'A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about what you asked me. The Prophet ﷺ recited to him what I recited to you, and he said to him what you said to me. When he refused to be satisfied, he said to him: 'Come closer.' He came closer. He said: 'Indeed, when a believer does a good deed, it pleases him and he hopes for its reward; and when he does an evil deed, it grieves him and he fears its punishment.'"],[4079,"And al-Harith said: 'Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us with it."],[4081,"When Allah wants to create a soul, the angel of the wombs says, turning aside: 'O Lord, male or female?' He said: 'Then Allah, Exalted is He, decrees His command. Then he says: 'O Lord, wretched or blessed?' Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, decrees His command. Then he writes between his eyes what he will meet, even the misfortune that will befall him.'"],[4082,"When the drop is created in the womb, the angel of the wombs says: 'O Lord, what should I write?' Then Allah, Exalted is He, decrees His command. He says: 'Male or female?' Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, decrees His command."],[4083,"Whoever speaks about divine decree with anything will be questioned about it on the Day of Resurrection."],[4084,"The beginning of the destruction of the nations was from the direction of divine decree. And you will be tested, or you will be tested, O nation, by them. If you meet them, or if you catch up with them, then ask them, or be the ones asking, and do not enable them to ask."],[4085,"Whoever denies divine decree or disputes about it has rejected what I came with and disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad ﷺ."],[4086,"The Prophet ﷺ came out from the door of the house heading to the room, and he heard people disputing among themselves about divine decree, saying: 'Did not Allah, Exalted is He, say such and such a verse? Did not Allah, Mighty and Majestic, say such and such a verse?' He said: 'The Prophet ﷺ opened the door of the room, and it was as if a pomegranate seed had been burst on his face. He said: 'Is this what you were commanded? Or is this what you were sent with? Those before you were destroyed only by things like this: they struck the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, some parts against others. Allah commanded you with something, so follow it, and He forbade you from something, so desist.' He said: 'After that, people did not hear anyone speak about it until Ma'bad al-Juhani came, and al-Hajjaj seized him and killed him.'"],[4087,"And al-Harith said: 'Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us with it."],[4088,"Allah Almighty took a handful and said: \"For Paradise, by My mercy,\" and took a handful and said: \"For the Fire, and I do not care.\""],[4089,"Amr b. Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us: al-Hakam b. Sinan al-Abdi narrated to us, with it."],[4090,"I fear for my community after me five things: denial of divine decree and belief in the stars."],[4091,"The ruin of my community lies in three: the Qadariyyah, tribalism, and transmitting reports without verification."],[4092,"The first thing Allah Almighty created was the Pen, and He commanded it to write everything."],[4093,"This clan of Quraysh will remain secure until you turn them away from their religion as disbelievers, protected. A man stood up to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, am I in Paradise or in the Fire?\" He said: \"In Paradise.\" Then another stood up and said: \"Am I in Paradise or in the Fire?\" He ﷺ said: \"In the Fire.\" Then he ﷺ said: \"Keep silent about me as long as I keep silent about you. Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would tell you of your number in the people of the Fire, until you recognize them at death. And if I were commanded to do it, I would do it.\""],[4094,"There was never any heresy whose origin was not denial of divine decree."],[4095,"And al-Harith said: 'Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us with it."],[4096,"When divine decree is mentioned, refrain; and when my companions are mentioned, refrain."],[4097,"And when the lunar mansions are mentioned, refrain."],[4098,"There will be in my community people who disbelieve in Allah and in divine decree while they are unaware, just as the Jews and Christians disbelieved. He said: I said: \"May I be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, how do they say?\" He ﷺ said: \"They say: good is from Allah and evil is from Iblis.\" He said: \"And they recite the Book of Allah Almighty upon that, and they disbelieve in Allah, Mighty and Majestic, after faith and knowledge. What enmity, hatred, and argument will my community encounter from them! Those are the heretics of this community. In their time will be the tyranny of the ruler, and what a tyranny, injustice, and selfishness! Then Allah Almighty will send upon them a plague, and most of them will perish. Then there will be metamorphosis and sinking into the earth, and few among them will be saved. On that day everyone will have little joy and intense grief. Then there will be metamorphosis: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will transform most of those into monkeys and pigs.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wept until we wept for his weeping. It was said: \"What is this weeping, O Messenger of Allah?\" He ﷺ said: \"Out of mercy for them, the wretched ones; for among them is the diligent worshipper and the devoted worshipper, even though they are not the first to have fallen into this saying and become distressed by it. Indeed, most of the Children of Israel who perished perished because of it.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, what is faith in divine decree?\" He ﷺ said: \"To believe in Allah alone, and to know that no one besides Him possesses harm or benefit, and to believe in Paradise and the Fire, and to know that Allah Almighty created them before creation, then created His creation and made whomever He willed for Paradise and whomever He willed for the Fire.\""],[4099,"And Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad al-Dawraqi narrated to us, al-Muqri' narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, 'Amr b. Shu'ayb narrated to us, and he mentioned it in full. <hidden matn linked=\"26035751\" text=\"I was sitting with Sa'id b. al-Musayyib when some of the people said, 'O Abu Muhammad, there are men who say that Allah, Exalted is He, decreed everything except evil.' He said, 'By Allah, I never saw Sa'id get as angry as he did that day, until they thought about leaving. Then he said, 'They have done it, woe to them, if only you knew. By Allah, I heard a hadith about them that would suffice them as a warning.' He said, 'I said, 'What is that, may Allah have mercy on you, O Abu Muhammad?' He said, then he looked at me after his anger had subsided and said.\""],[4100,"That he heard a man say: evil is not by decree, so Ibn 'Abbas said: Between us and the people of qadar (the verse): 'Those who associate partners with Allah will say, \"If Allah had willed, we would not have associated partners, nor would our forefathers\"' up to 'If He had willed, He would have guided you all.' Ibn 'Abbas said: And incapacity and ability are from the decree. Tawus said: And the two speakers from the Qadariyyah speak without knowledge, so avoid speaking about the decree."],[4101,"That a man came to Makkah speaking about the decree, so he said: Show him to me, I will take him by his head. By Allah, if his neck falls into my hands, I will crush it, and if his nose falls into my hands, I will bite it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: It is as if I see the women of Banu Fahm circumambulating al-Khazraj, their buttocks clashing, associating partners (with Allah), and this is the first shirk in Islam. By Allah, their evil will not stop with them until they remove Allah from decreeing good, as they removed Him from decreeing evil."],[4102,"Indeed, in some of what Allah, Exalted is He, revealed in the Books: Indeed I am Allah, there is no deity but Me. I have decreed good and evil."],[4103,"That a man said: O Messenger of Allah, are actions initiated, or has the decree been settled? He ﷺ said: When Allah, Exalted is He, brought forth the progeny of Adam ﷺ from his back and made them testify against themselves, then He poured them out from His two hands, He said: These are for Paradise and these are for the Fire. So the people of Paradise are facilitated for the deeds of the people of Paradise, and the people of the Fire are facilitated for the deeds of the people of the Fire."],[4104,"The Magians of this nation, even if they fast and pray—meaning the Qadariyyah."],[4105,"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion."],[4106,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say in his supplication: O Guardian of Islam and its people, make me firm in it until I meet You with it."],[4107,"\"There is no contagion and no bad omen. Who infected the first one?\""],[4108,"And His Throne is upon the water. So the people of Paradise are its people, and the people of the Fire are its people."],[4109,"Indeed, Allah, Exalted is He, created the heavens and the earth, created Paradise and the Fire, and created Adam. Then He scattered his progeny in His two hands, then poured them out, and said: These are for this one, and I do not care, and these are for this one, and I do not care. And He wrote the people of Paradise and what they will do, and He wrote the people of the Fire and what they will do. Then He folded the record and it was raised up."],[4110,"It is enough of a blessing for a person to be granted success in his religion."],[4111,"A servant does not believe and his faith is not complete until he believes in divine decree, its good and its evil, its bitter and its sweet, its harm and its benefit."],[4112,"Adam and Moses (peace be upon them) argued. Moses said to Adam: You are the one whom Allah created with His own hand, breathed into you from His spirit, and caused you to dwell in His Paradise, then you destroyed us and led us astray. He mentioned as much as Allah willed of this. Adam ﷺ said to him: You are the one whom Allah chose with His words and His messages, yet you blame me for a matter Allah had decreed for me before He created the heavens and the earth? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: So Adam defeated Moses in argument, so Adam defeated Moses in argument."],[4113,"Do you blame me for a matter that was decreed for me before I was created? So Adam defeated Moses in argument, so Adam defeated Moses in argument."],[4114,"Adam met Moses (peace be upon them). Moses said: O Adam, then he mentioned it, and he added: And He made His angels prostrate to you, but he did not say: You destroyed us and led us astray. He said: You did what you did and brought your offspring out of Paradise. And he added: And He brought you near as a confidant and gave you the Torah. How long before I committed it do you find the sin I committed written against me? He said: Forty years."],[4115,"Whoever does not believe in divine decree, its good and its evil, I am free of him."],[4116,"I said to Muhammad b. Sirin: This hadith: Every newborn is born upon the fitrah — who said it? He said: The one who knew it said it."],[4117,"Every newborn is born upon the fitrah until his tongue expresses it. His parents make him a Jew or a Christian."],[4118,"I was in Damascus when seventy heads of the Haruriyyah were brought and set up. Abu Umamah ؓ came, entered the mosque, prayed two rak'ahs, then came out, stood over them, and began to shed tears for a while. Then he said: What does Iblis do to the people of Islam? three times. Then he said: O Abu Ghalib, you are in a land where its whims are many and its terrors are many. I said: Yes. He said: May Allah protect you from them... I said: Why do you shed tears? He said: Out of mercy for them, for they were from the people of Islam. Then he said: Do you recite Surah Al 'Imran? I said: Yes. He said: Recite this verse: It is He who sent down to you the Book; in it are verses [that are] precise. He said: These had deviation in their hearts, so they were led astray. Then he recited: On the day when faces turn white. I said: Are they these? He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The Children of Israel divided into seventy-one sects, all in the Fire except the main body. A man beside me said: O Abu Umamah, do you not see what the main body is doing? He said: Upon them is what they are burdened with, and upon you is what you are burdened with. If you obey him, you will be guided. Hearing and obedience are better than disobedience and division. They judge for us, then they kill us. I said to him: This hadith — did you narrate it from something, or did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or do you say it from your own opinion? He said: Then I would be bold to narrate to you what I did not hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard it from him twice or three times, until they said seven."],[4119,"I was in Basra at the time of 'Abd al-Malik when the heads of the Khawarij were brought."],[4120,"The community of Moses ﷺ divided into seventy-one sects, seventy of them in the Fire and one in Paradise. The community of Jesus ﷺ divided into seventy-two sects, seventy-one of them in the Fire and one in Paradise. And my community will exceed the two communities together by one sect: seventy-two in the Fire and one in Paradise. They said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He ﷺ said: The main body."],[4121,"In my community there are more than seventy callers, all of them calling to the Fire. If I wished, I would inform you of their fathers and their tribes."],[4122,"Two categories of my community will not enter Paradise: the Qadariyyah and the Murji'ah."],[4123,"Two groups of my ummah will not come to the Pond: the Qadariyyah and the Murji'ah."],[4124,"A caller will call out on the Day of Resurrection: 'Let the adversaries of Allah, the Exalted, stand up—and they are the Qadariyyah.'"],[4125,"Abu Ya'la said: Musa narrated to us, Sulayman b. 'Abdullah al-Marwazi narrated to us, Baqiyyah b. al-Walid narrated to us, with this. :"],[4126,"When the delegation of the people of Basra came to 'Umar ؓ , among them al-Ahnaf b. Qays, he sent them off and kept him with him. Then he said: 'Do you know why I detained you? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ warned us against every hypocrite with a knowledgeable tongue. I feared that you might be one of them, and I hope that you are not one of them. So finish your business and rejoin your family.'"],[4127,"Moderation in the Sunnah is better than striving in innovation."],[4128,"No year comes upon the people except that they introduce an innovation in it and kill a Sunnah in it, until innovations live and Sunnahs die."],[4129,"Ibn Mas'ud ؓ stood over a group of people, some of them relating stories to others. He said: 'By Allah, you have certainly preferred the companions of Muhammad ﷺ openly, and you have certainly initiated an innovation wrongfully. Follow and do not innovate. By Allah, if you follow, you have certainly preceded with a clear precedence; and if you innovate, you have certainly wronged with a distant wrong'—or he said: 'you have gone astray with a distant straying.'"],[4130,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ admonished us with an admonition. A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this is as if it is the admonition of one bidding farewell. So what do you enjoin upon us?' He ﷺ said: 'I enjoin you to fear Allah, the Exalted, and to adhere to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly-guided, rightly-directed caliphs. Bite onto it with the molar teeth. And if a black slave is placed in authority over you, listen to him and obey. And every innovation is misguidance.'"],[4131,"While 'Umayr b. Sa'd was among a group of people from Palestine—and he was called 'Naseej Wahdih' (unique in his kind)—we sat on a large bench in his house. He said to his servant: \"Boy, bring the horses to water.\" In the house there was a stone trough. He brought them to water. Then he said: \"Where is so-and-so?\" He said: \"She is mangy, dripping blood,\" or he said \"water\"—Ibrahim was unsure. He said: \"Bring her to water.\" One of the people said: \"Then all the camels will get mange.\" He said: \"Bring her to water, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'There is no contagion, no bad omen, and no Haamah. Do you not see the camel that is in the desert and then a spot appears on its chest or flanks that was not there before? Who infected the first one?'\""],[4132,"'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ gathered the people for the arrival of the delegation. He said to Zayd b. Arqam: 'Look at the companions of Muhammad ﷺ and give them permission first, then the generation that follows them.' They entered and stood in rows before him. He looked and saw a huge man wearing a patched cloak. 'Umar ؓ gestured to him, so he came. 'Umar ؓ said: 'Eeh' three times. The man said: 'Eeh' three times. 'Umar ؓ said: 'Uff, stand up.' He stood up. He looked and saw al-Ash'ari, a man of light body, short and squat. He gestured to him, so he came. 'Umar ؓ said: 'Eeh.' Al-Ash'ari said: 'Eeh.' 'Umar ؓ said: 'Eeh.' He said: 'O Commander of the Faithful, ask and open a topic, and we will tell you.' 'Umar ؓ said: 'Uff, stand up, for a shepherd of sheep will never benefit you.' He looked and saw a white man of light body. He gestured to him, so he came. 'Umar ؓ said: 'Eeh.' He leaped up, praised Allah, the Exalted, extolled Him, and admonished him by Allah. Then he said: 'You have been placed in charge of the affair of this ummah. So fear Allah, the Exalted, in what you have been placed in charge of regarding the affair of this ummah and the people of your flock, especially in your own self. For you are accountable and will be questioned about what you were entrusted with, and you are a trustee. You must fulfill the trust that is upon you, so that you are given your reward according to the measure of your deeds.' 'Umar ؓ said: 'No man has spoken truthfully to me since I was made caliph except you. Who are you?' He said: 'I am al-Rabi' b. Ziyad.' He said: 'The brother of al-Muhajir b. Ziyad?' He said: 'Yes.' 'Umar ؓ equipped an army and appointed al-Ash'ari over them. Then he said: 'Look at Rabi' b. Ziyad. If he is truthful in what he said, then he has help in this matter, so appoint him. Then let not ten days pass without you checking on his work and writing to me about his conduct in his post, so that it is as if I myself appointed him.' Then 'Umar ؓ said: 'Our Prophet enjoined us, saying: \"The most fearful thing I fear for you after me is a hypocrite with a knowledgeable tongue.\"'"],[4133,"There will be people who deny the Dajjal, deny the rising of the sun from the west, deny the punishment of the grave, and deny people who will come out of the Fire after they have been burnt."],[4134,"After me, I do not fear for you a believer who is certain in faith, nor an open disbeliever. As for the believer who is certain, his faith restrains him; and as for the open disbeliever, his disbelief is clear. But I fear for you after me a man whose tongue is knowledgeable but whose heart is ignorant—he says what you recognize and does what you disapprove of."],[4135,"A man in Madinah said in a gathering: 'Which of you will narrate to me a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' Ali ؓ said to him: 'I will. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I do not fear for my Ummah a believer or a disbeliever. As for the believer, his faith will restrain him, and as for the disbeliever, his disbelief will restrain him. But I fear for a man between them who recites the Quran until, when it becomes smooth on his tongue, he interprets it in a way other than its true interpretation. He says, 'What do you know?' and does what you condemn, and thus he goes astray and leads others astray.\"'"],[4136,"Whoever introduces into Islam a new thing, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither sarf nor 'adl will be accepted from him. It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the hadath (new thing)?' He ﷺ said: 'Whoever kills a soul without a soul, or mutilates without just retaliation, or innovates a bid'ah without a Sunnah.' He said: 'Al-'adl is the ransom, and al-sarf is repentance.'"],[4137,"Indeed Qatadah came to him to sit, so he said to him: 'If you sit, I will stand up.' They said: 'O Abu Muhammad, he is a faqih (jurist).' He said: 'Iblis is more of a faqih than him, since he said: \"My Lord, because You have sent me astray.\"'"],[4138,"There is nothing worshipped beneath the shade of the sky more hateful to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, than a followed whim."],[4140,"O Nafi', bring me close to the road of the pilgrims. He said: That was after his eyesight had weakened. So he did so, and he looked at the owners of the litters and said: 'May Allah have mercy on you, how comfortable you are!' Then he looked at the owners of the black sacks with men on them and said: 'You are the pilgrims. Perhaps I will not meet you after this year of mine, so listen to a hadith from me that I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The people of our Qiblah are believers; nothing removes them from faith except the door through which they entered it.\"'"],[4141,"O people, there will be a people from this Ummah who deny stoning (rajm), deny the Dajjal, deny the rising of the sun from its west, deny the punishment of the grave, deny intercession, and deny a people who will come out of the Fire after they have been burned to cinders."],[4142,"And they deny divine decree (qadar), and they deny the Basin (al-Hawd), and he did not mention the Dajjal, nor the rising of the sun, nor the punishment of the grave."],[4143,"And Abu Ya'la said: Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, similar to the first except the rising of the sun and the punishment of the grave. (117) And the hadith of Abu Umamah ؓ regarding that has passed in the section on the splitting of nations. : :"],[4144,"A man passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they spoke about him and praised him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Who will kill him?' Abu Bakr ؓ said: 'I will.' He went and found him standing praying, having drawn a line around himself. Abu Bakr ؓ returned and did not kill him when he saw him in that state. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Who will kill him?' 'Umar ؓ said: 'I will.' He went and saw him in his line, standing praying, so he returned and did not kill him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Who will kill him?' 'Ali ؓ said: 'I will.' He ﷺ said: 'You will not reach him.' He said: He went and found that he had gone."],[4145,"A daughter of mine complained of illness, so I steeped something for her in a brass vessel. The Prophet ﷺ entered while it was boiling and said, \"What is this?\" I said, \"My daughter is ill, so I steeped this for her.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has not placed your cure in what is unlawful.\""],[4148,"In the end of time there will be a people called al-Rafidah; they reject Islam and cast it off. Fight them, for they are polytheists."],[4149,"If a man insults you and taunts you about something he knows about you, do not taunt him about something you know about him, for the bad consequence of that will be upon him and its final benefit will be yours."],[4150,"The Prophet ﷺ looked at 'Ali ؓ and said: This one is in Paradise. Among his followers are a people who know Islam, then reject it; they have a nickname, they are called al-Rafidah. Whoever meets them should know that they are polytheists."],[4152,"I asked Jabir ؓ: Are there any tyrants among the people who pray? He said: No. And I asked him: Is there any polytheist among them? He said: No."],[4153,"I asked Jabir ؓ while he was living in Makkah, and he was staying with Banu Fihr. A man asked him: Did you used to call anyone from the people of the Qiblah a polytheist? He said: God forbid! And he was alarmed by that. I said: Did you used to call anyone among them an unbeliever? He said: No."],[4154,"I said to him: O Abu Hamzah, some people testify against us of unbelief and polytheism. Anas ؓ said: Those are the worst of creation and creatures."],[4156,"\"Whoever shelters an orphan from among the Muslims, bringing him into his food and drink until he is satisfied, Paradise becomes incumbent for him, unless he commits a sin that is not forgiven. And whoever supports three daughters, disciplining them and treating them well, Paradise becomes incumbent for him.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or two daughters?\" He said, \"Or two daughters,\" until if they had said, \"One,\" he would have said, \"One.\" \"And whoever loses his two precious ones, his reward is upon Allah: Paradise.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what are his two precious ones?\" He ﷺ said, \"His two eyes.\" Ibn Abbas ؓ, when he narrated this hadith, would say, \"This is among the precious and outstanding hadiths.\" [Raised to the Prophet]"],[4157,"Whoever makes a pronouncement about My servant, I will admit My servant to Paradise and admit him to Hell."],[4158,"O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, something comes into my chest and I wish I were charcoal. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Praise be to God, who has made Satan despair of being worshipped in this land of yours ever again, but he is satisfied with the trivial acts of your deeds."],[4159,"A man said to 'A'ishah ؓ: One of us speaks to himself about something, that if he uttered it his hereafter would be gone, and if it became apparent he would be killed. She said: She said Allahu Akbar ؓ three times, then said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about it, and he said Allahu Akbar three times, then said: The believer is only tested."],[4160,"A man stood up to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God ﷺ, there is something in my chest, that if I revealed it I would perish; am I destroyed? He ﷺ said: No, God Almighty has pardoned my nation for what their souls whisper, as long as they do not speak or act."],[4161,"A man said in the presence of ‘Abdullāh: “I am a believer.” So ‘Abdullāh said to him: “Then say: ‘I am in Paradise.’” He said: “I believe in Allah, His angels, His books, and His messengers.”"],[4162,"The thing I fear most for you is a man’s admiration of his own opinion. Whoever says, ‘I am a scholar,’ he is ignorant. Whoever says, ‘I am in Paradise,’ he is in the Fire."],[4163,"Whoever claims that he is a believer, he is a disbeliever. Whoever claims that he is in Paradise, he is in the Fire. Whoever claims that he is a scholar, he is ignorant. He said: Then a man disputed with him, saying: “If you take authority, then we have Paradise.” He said: ‘Umar ؓ said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever claims that he is in Paradise, he is in the Fire.”"],[4164,"A man’s faith is not complete until he makes an exception in all his speech—or he said: in his words."],[4165,"I said to al-Ḥasan b. ‘Alī ؓ: “These Shī‘ah claim that ‘Alī ؓ will be resurrected?” He said: “They have lied. Those are not Shī‘ah. If he were to be resurrected, we would not have married his wives or divided his inheritance.”"],[4166,"Whatever Allah, Mighty and Majestic, promises as a reward for a deed, He will fulfill it for him. Whatever He promises as a punishment for a deed, He has the choice in it."],[4167,"If he fears Allah (Mighty and Majestic)."],[4168,"I heard more than one of the commentators say: “The Most Merciful rose over the Throne” means He ascended."],[4169,"When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, created the Trumpet, He gave it to Isrāfīl, and he is holding it to his mouth, his eyes fixed on the Throne, waiting until he is commanded—and he mentioned the ḥadīth. He said in it: Then Allah, Exalted is He, will place His Throne wherever He wills on the earth, and eight will carry His Throne that day, whereas today they are four: their feet are at the boundary of the lowest earth, and the earths and the heavens are above their haunches, and the Throne is upon their shoulders. They have a loud voice in glorification, and their glorification is to say: “Glory be to the King, Owner of the dominion. Glory be to the Owner of the Throne, Owner of might. Glory be to the Living who does not die. Glory be to the One who causes creatures to die and does not die. All-Glorious, All-Holy, Lord of the angels and the Spirit. All-Holy, All-Holy. Glory be to my Lord, the Most High. Glory be to the Owner of dominion, might, pride, and greatness. Glory be to Him forever and ever.”"],[4170,"A group of Jews came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “We ask you about three things that no one knows except a prophet: tell us about the bearers of the Throne—who are they? And about the semen of a man and the semen of a woman?” He ﷺ said: “As for the bearers of the Throne, vermin carry it with their horns, and the spot in the sun is from their sweat. The semen of a man is white and thick, and the semen of a woman is yellow and thin.” And he mentioned the third, so they said: “We bear witness that you are a prophet. This is how we find it in the Torah.”"],[4171,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, veiled Himself from His creation with four things: with light, then darkness, then fire, then darkness—or with fire, then darkness, then light, then darkness."],[4172,"Below Allah, Blessed and Exalted, are seventy thousand veils of light. No one hears the sound of any of those veils except that his soul departs."],[4173,"Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad b. 'Imran al-Akhnasi narrated to us, Muhammad b. Fudayl narrated to us, 'Abd Allah b. Sa'id narrated to us with it."],[4174,"Hassan b. Thabit ؓ recited some verses, and he ؓ said: 'I bear witness, by Allah's permission, that Muhammad is the Messenger above the heavens from on high. And that Abu Yahya and Yahya, both of them have an accepted deed in his religion. And that the brother of al-Ahqaf, when he stood among them, he stands with the essence of Allah among them, and he is just.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'And I.'"],[4175,"Abu Ya'la said: Ishaq, who is Ibn Abi Isra'il, narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, with this chain."],[4176,"Indeed, Iblis sat in wait for the son of Adam on all his paths. He sat for him on the path of Islam and said: 'Will you submit and abandon your religion, your family, your children, and your birthplace?' But he disobeyed him and submitted. Then he sat for him on the path of emigration and said to him: 'Will you emigrate? Emigration is like a horse in its length, it does not move.' But he disobeyed him and emigrated. Then he sat for him on the path of jihad and said to him: 'Will you fight? Jihad is as its name implies, it exhausts wealth and self. You will fight and be killed, and your wife will be married and your wealth divided.' But he disobeyed him and fought. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever has these qualities is guaranteed by Allah, Mighty and Majestic, that if he dies, is killed, drowns, or burns, Allah, Exalted, will admit him to Paradise.'"],[4177,"It has reached me that Luqman the Wise used to say: 'O my son, do not learn knowledge to boast with it among the scholars, to argue with the foolish, or to show off with it in gatherings. And do not abandon knowledge out of disdain for it, preferring ignorance. O my son, when you see a people remembering Allah, Exalted, sit with them. For if you are learned, your knowledge will benefit you; and if you are ignorant, they will teach you. And perhaps Allah, Exalted, will look upon them with His mercy, and it will reach you along with them.'"],[4178,"We entered upon Ibn 'Abbas ؓ, and he said: 'No man treads a path seeking knowledge therein, but Allah, Exalted, makes easy for him a path to Paradise. And whoever's deeds slow him down, his lineage will not speed him up.'"],[4179,"O Ibn Mas'ud, do you know which of the bonds of faith is firmest? I said: 'At your service, O Messenger of Allah, Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said this to me three times. He ﷺ said: 'Indeed, the firmest bond of faith is love for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and hatred for the sake of Allah, Exalted.' Then he ﷺ said to me: 'O Ibn Mas'ud.' I said: 'At your service, O Messenger of Allah.' He ﷺ said: 'Do you know which of the people is most virtuous?' I said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best,' until he said it three times. He ﷺ said: 'Indeed, the most virtuous of them in knowledge is the one who has understanding in their religion.' Then he ﷺ said: 'O Ibn Mas'ud.' I said: 'At your service, O Messenger of Allah.' He ﷺ said: 'Do you know which of the people is most knowledgeable?' until he said it three times. I said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He ﷺ said: 'The most knowledgeable of them is the one who sees the truth most clearly when people differ, even if he is deficient in deeds, and even if he crawls on his backside.'"],[4180,"Al-Tayalisi said: Al-Sa'q narrated to us, and he mentioned it in abbreviated form."],[4181,"The Prophet ﷺ affirmed Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt in a verse of his poetry. He said: \"A man and a bull under his right foot, and the vulture for the other, and a lion lying in wait.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"He spoke the truth.\" He said: \"And the sun rises at the end of every night, red, its color becoming rosy. It refuses, so it does not rise for us in its gentleness except tormented, and unless it is whipped.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"He spoke the truth.\""],[4182,"Indeed, Allah, Exalted, would not gather the nation of Muhammad ﷺ upon misguidance."],[4183,"And indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, would not gather the nation of Muhammad ﷺ upon misguidance."],[4184,"Indeed, Allah, Exalted, has protected you from three things: that you all agree upon misguidance, that the people of falsehood prevail over the people of truth, and that I supplicate against you with a supplication that would destroy you. And He has replaced this with the Beast, the Dajjal, and the Smoke."],[4185,"I said to Ibrahim: \"You narrate to me, so give me its chain.\" He said: \"Whatever I said to you as 'Abdullah said,' then [it is]...\""],[4186,"It would not please me for the disagreement among the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ to be [as valuable as] red camels, because if we take the saying of these we are right, and if we take the saying of those we are right."],[4187,"Ibn Mas'ud and Ubayy b. Ka'b ؓ disagreed about a man praying. Ubayy ؓ said: \"He prays in one garment,\" and Ibn Mas'ud ؓ said: \"In two garments.\" This reached 'Umar ؓ, so he sent for them and said: \"Two men from the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ have disagreed on a single ruling; by which of the two sayings should the people act?\" Then he said: \"Verily, the saying is what Ubayy ؓ said, and Ibn Mas'ud did not fall short.\""],[4188,"'Ammar ؓ was asked about a matter, and he said: \"Has this happened yet?\" They said: \"No.\" He said: \"Leave us until it happens; when it happens, we will examine it for you.\""],[4189,"Do not hasten toward a calamity before it descends, for if you do not, there will not cease to be among the Muslims someone who, when he speaks, is granted success, or is guided aright. But if you hasten toward the calamity before it descends, the path will lead you astray here and there."],[4190,"I asked Tawus about something, and he said: \"Has this happened?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Our companions informed us from Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ that he said: 'Do not hasten toward a calamity before it descends.'\""],[4191,"I was with Ubayy when a man came and said: \"I did not see 'Abdullah b. 'Amr yesterday, and I fear he may elude me, so I would like you to ask him something for me.\" He said: \"Go and ask him yourself.\" He said: \"'Abdullah was standing in front of his tent when a man came out to the open area, went to him, then returned.\""],[4192,"I said to 'Amr b. Qays al-Mula'i: \"Write this hadith for me.\" He said: \"No, for Ibrahim al-Nakha'i said: 'Do not write, lest you rely on it.' Then Ibrahim said: 'Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ said: The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us while we were writing some hadith, and he said: \"What is this, O Mu'adh?\" We said: \"We heard it from you, O Messenger of God.\" He ﷺ said: \"This Quran suffices you from anything else.\" So we did not write anything after that.'\""],[4193,"I wrote a book from my father, and my father said: \"Were it not that it contains a verse from the Book of God Almighty, I would have burned it.\" Then he called for a washing tub or a large vessel himself, then said: \"Away from me, away from me. Whatever you heard from me, I did not write down any book from the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" He said: \"You nearly destroyed your father.\""],[4194,"I was sitting with 'Umar ؓ when a man from 'Abd al-Qays whose residence was in al-Sus was brought to him. 'Umar ؓ said to him: \"Are you so-and-so son of so-and-so, the 'Abdi?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He struck him with a stick he had. The man said: \"What is my fault, O Commander of the Faithful?\" 'Umar ؓ said to him: \"Sit down.\" He sat down. Then he recited to him: \"In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Alif Lam Ra. These are the verses of the clear Book. Indeed, We have sent it down as an Arabic Quran so that you may understand. We relate to you the best of stories...\" He recited it to him three times and struck him three times. The man said: \"What is my fault, O Commander of the Faithful?\" He said: \"Are you the one who copied the Book of Daniel?\" He said: \"Command me with your command and I will follow it.\" He ؓ said: \"Go and erase it with hot water and white wool. Then do not read it yourself, nor teach it to anyone among the Muslims. If it reaches me that you have read it or taught it to any Muslim, I will destroy you as a punishment.\" Then he ؓ said to him: \"Sit down.\" He sat before him. He said: \"I went and copied a book from the People of the Book, then brought it in a piece of leather. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: 'What is this in your hand, O 'Umar?' I said: 'O Messenger of God, a book I copied to add knowledge to our knowledge.' The Messenger of God ﷺ became angry until his eyes reddened. Then the call to prayer was made: 'Gather for prayer.' The Ansar said: 'Your Prophet has been angered! To arms! To arms!' They came and surrounded the pulpit of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: 'I brought it to you white and pure, so do not be confused, and let not the confused deceive you.' 'Umar ؓ said: 'I stood up and said: I am content with God as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with you as Messenger.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ descended.\""],[4195,"I said: \"O Messenger of God, I would like to retain your hadith, but my heart cannot retain it, so may I use my right hand to help?\" He ﷺ said: \"If you wish.\""],[4196,"I said: \"O Messenger of God, should I record knowledge in writing?\" He ﷺ said: \"Yes.\""],[4197,"We did not write anything of the hadiths in the era of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except the tashahhud and the istikhara."],[4198,"When we asked Anas ؓ many questions about hadith, he would bring us some old sacks of his, throw them to us, and say: 'These are hadiths that I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, wrote down, and memorized.'"],[4199,"I was with Abu Hurayrah ؓ. He said: I used to write down some of what I heard from him. When I wanted to leave him, I brought the writings and read them to him, and said: 'Did I hear this from you?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[4200,"I wrote from her mouth – meaning Fatimah bt. Qays – a book."],[4201,"Whoever hears of a virtue from Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and does not believe in it will not attain it."],[4202,"Hafsah brought a book to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ containing stories of Yusuf, and began to read it. The Prophet ﷺ's face kept changing color, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, if Yusuf had come to you and you followed him and abandoned me, you would have gone astray.'"],[4203,"Part of a person's understanding is his walking, his entering, and his exiting."],[4204,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ feared that he might forget something, he would tie a thread on his hand to remind himself."],[4205,"If one of you fears forgetting, let him say: 'Praise be to Allah, the Reminder of the forgetful.'"],[4206,"Dust the book; it is more successful for it."],[4207,"The example of knowledge that is not spoken of is like the example of a treasure from which nothing is spent in the way of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[4208,"Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will come on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire... And whoever speaks about the Qur'an without knowledge will come on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire."],[4209,"Do not seek knowledge in order to vie with the scholars, nor to dispute with the foolish, nor to attract people's attention. Whoever does that will be in the Fire."],[4210,"Indeed, a servant will be asked on the Day of Resurrection about the surplus of his deeds, just as he is asked about the surplus of his wealth."],[4211,"The religion will prevail until it crosses the seas, and seas will be crossed with horses in the path of Allah, exalted be He. Then after them will come people who recite the Quran and say: 'We have recited the Quran; who among us recites better? Who among us is more knowledgeable in fiqh? Who among us is more learned?' Then he turned to his companions and said: 'Is there any good in those?' They said: 'No.' He said: 'Those are from you, from this nation, and those are the fuel of the Fire.'"],[4213,"Equip me, for I am leaving on such-and-such a day. He said: That day came to him while some of his equipment remained, so he said: Have you finished? I said: A little remains. He said: Then I am leaving. I said: May Allah set the commander aright; if you stayed until the rest of your equipment is finished. He said: No, I dislike lying to my family, for then they would lie to me, and I dislike breaking my promise to them, for then they would break their promises to me, and I dislike betraying them, for then they would betray me."],[4214,"Whoever fabricates a false hadith is like one who narrates it. It was said: How does he fabricate it? He ﷺ said: It is a man who meets another man and says: It was such-and-such, and thus opens the way for him. Let none of you be a key to evil and falsehood."],[4215,"I dictated a hadith to Salamah b. 'Alqamah, and he narrated it to me. Then he returned and said: If you want your companion to lie, dictate to him."],[4216,"Muhammad b. Sirin used to converse and laugh, but when the hadith came, he became reverent."],[4217,"\"O Abu Dharr,\" and I said: \"At your service and gladly.\" He said: \"Have you prayed today?\" I said: \"No.\" He ﷺ said: \"Rise and pray,\" so I rose and prayed as long as Allah, the Exalted, willed, then I returned and sat. He ﷺ remained silent for a long time without speaking to me, so I said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has disliked my company.\" Then he ﷺ turned to me and said: \"O Abu Dharr.\" I said: \"At your service and gladly.\" He ﷺ said: \"Seek refuge in Allah from the evil of the devils of mankind and jinn.\" I said: \"May my father and mother be sacrificed for you; do humans have devils?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Does not Allah, Mighty and Majestic, say: 'Devils of mankind and jinn, inspiring one another'—the verse?\" Then he ﷺ turned to me and said: \"O Abu Dharr.\" I said: \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah.\" He ﷺ said: \"Shall I not teach you a phrase that is a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?\" I said: \"Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you.\" He ﷺ said: \"Say: 'There is no might nor power except with Allah.'\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ persisted in not speaking until that lasted long from him. So I initiated the speech and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you commanded me to pray; what is prayer?\" He ﷺ said: \"It is a good that is placed; whoever wishes takes little, and whoever wishes takes much.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is fasting?\" He ﷺ said: \"An obligatory duty that suffices.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is charity?\" He ﷺ said: \"Multiplied manifold, and with Allah is more.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best?\" He ﷺ said: \"Faith in Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and Jihad in the path of Allah, the Exalted.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which martyrs are best?\" He ﷺ said: \"One whose blood is spilled and whose horse is hamstrung.\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which slaves are best?\" He ﷺ said: \"The most expensive in price and the most precious to their owners.\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best?\" He ﷺ said: \"An effort from one of little means, and a secret to a poor person.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what if I do not find anything to give in charity?\" He ﷺ said: \"You help a weak person or you make something for an unskilled person.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what if I cannot?\" He ﷺ said: \"Then you restrain this—and he ﷺ pointed to his tongue—for it is a good charity a person gives on behalf of himself.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which verse revealed to you of the Quran is greatest?\" He ﷺ said: \"The Verse of the Throne. And do you know what the likeness of the heavens and the earth is in relation to the Throne?\" I said: \"No, unless you teach me from what Allah, the Exalted, has taught you.\" He ﷺ said: \"The likeness of the heavens and the earth in the Throne is but like a ring cast in a desert, and the excellence of the Throne over the heavens and the earth is like the excellence of the desert over that ring.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how many were the prophets (peace be upon them)?\" He ﷺ said: \"They were one hundred twenty-four thousand.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, were all of them messengers?\" He ﷺ said: \"No, the messengers among them were three hundred fifteen men.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which of them was first?\" He ﷺ said: \"Adam ﷺ .\" I said: \"Was Adam a prophet?\" He ﷺ said: \"Yes; Allah formed his clay, created him with His hand, breathed into him of His spirit, and spoke to him directly.\" Then the people became many around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Shall I not inform you of the most miserly of people?\" I said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He ﷺ said: \"One in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not send blessings upon me ﷺ.\""],[4218,"When I came to Anas ؓ, he would call for perfume and wipe his hands and cheeks with it."],[4219,"O people, stay away from me! I was with those more knowledgeable than me, and if I knew that I would remain until I was needed, I would have learned for you. Stay away from me!"],[4220,"The good report is brought by a righteous man, and the bad report is brought by a bad man."],[4221,"Whoever hears of a virtue from Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and does not believe in it will not attain it."],[4222,"I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hadiths that I heard and memorized. Nothing prevents me from narrating them except that I see my companions contradicting me regarding them."],[4223,"Discuss, for discussion reminds one of other hadiths."],[4224,"We used to come to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri ؓ and he would say: Discuss, for discussion stirs up other hadiths."],[4225,"I said to Abu Sa'id ؓ: Write down for us. He said: I will never write for you; take from me as we used to take from the Prophet ﷺ. And Abu Sa'id ؓ used to say: Discuss, for hadith reminds one of another hadith."],[4226,"Keep mentioning hadith so that it does not become obsolete."],[4227,"This community will act for a time according to the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, then act for a time according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then act according to opinion. When they act according to opinion, they have gone astray and led others astray."],[4228,"The example of the hypocrite is like a sheep between two flocks: when it goes to these, they butt it, and when it goes to those, they butt it. Ibn Umar ؓ said: It is not like that; rather, he said, \"between two herds of sheep.\" Ubayd b. Umayr said: \"Between two flocks\" and \"between two herds of sheep\" are the same. Ibn Umar ؓ said: Had I not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say it, I would not have said it."],[4229,"Abu al-Darda' ؓ, when he narrated a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, would say: \"Like this or similar to it.\""],[4232,"Whoever says about me what I did not say, or claims allegiance to me, or ascribes himself to other than his patrons, let him take his seat between the two eyes of Hell. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, does it have two eyes? He ﷺ said: Yes. Have you not heard the words of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: \"When it sees them from a distant place, they will hear its raging and roaring\"? So we refrained from speaking until he noticed that about us and said: What is the matter that I do not hear you conversing? We said: O Messenger of Allah, how can we converse when you said what you said? We cannot relate the hadith exactly; we advance and delay, and we add and omit. He ﷺ said: I did not mean that; I meant the one who intends to find fault with me and to disgrace Islam."],[4233,"I was with Salman ؓ when we passed by the Tigris. He said: 'O brother of Banu 'Abs, dismount and drink.' So I dismounted and drank. Then he said: 'Dismount and drink.' So I dismounted and drank. He said: 'O brother of Banu 'Abs, how much did your drinking diminish from the Tigris?' I said: 'How could my drinking diminish the Tigris?' He said: 'Likewise, knowledge does not perish, so take from it what benefits you.'"],[4234,"There are two greedy types whose greed is never satisfied: one greedy for seeking knowledge, whose greed is never satisfied; and one greedy for seeking wealth, whose greed is never satisfied."],[4235,"I came to Abu Dharr ؓ while he was at the middle Jamrah and the people had gathered asking him for legal verdicts. A man came and stood before him and said: 'Did not the Commander of the Faithful forbid you from giving legal verdicts?' He raised his head to him and said: 'Are you a watcher over me? If you were to place the sword upon this'—and he pointed to the back of his neck—'then I thought that I could convey a word I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before you passed it upon me, I would convey it.'"],[4236,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a sermon and mentioned a hadith, in which he said: 'Whoever learns knowledge, is humble in it, and teaches it to the servants of Allah, the Exalted, seeking thereby what is with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, there will be no one in Paradise with a greater reward or a higher station than him, nor will there be in Paradise any station or lofty degree, precious and valuable, except that he has in it the most abundant share and the most abundant of positions. Verily, knowledge is the best of worship, and the essence of religion is piety. The scholar is only the one who acts upon his knowledge, even if he has little knowledge.'"],[4237,"I entered the mosque of Iliya and prayed two rak'ahs facing a pillar. A man came and prayed nearby, and the people inclined toward him. He was 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr b. al-'As ؓ. Then a messenger of Yazid b. Mu'awiyah came saying, 'Respond!' He said: 'This one wants to forbid me from narrating as his father used to forbid me. Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say...' Then he mentioned a hadith."],[4238,"'Uthman ؓ was asked, and he mentioned a hadith traced back to the Prophet, in which he said: 'As for Abu Jad: the Ba' is the splendor of Allah, the Jim is the beauty of Allah, and the Dal is the religion of Allah, which He approved for Himself, His angels, His prophets, His messengers, and His righteous creation. As for Hawaz: the Ha' is the disgrace of the people of the Fire, and the Za' is the roaring of Hell upon the enemies of Allah and the people of disobedience. As for Hutti: the sins of the sinners were wiped away by seeking forgiveness. As for Kalamun: the Kaf is the perfection of the people of Paradise, and they said: \"Praise be to Allah, who has fulfilled His promise to us.\" As for the Nun: it is the fish from whose liver they will eat before entering Paradise. As for Sa'fas: a measure for a measure and a gem for a gem, and as you judge, you shall be judged. As for Qarashat: they were brought to account.'"],[4239,"When I narrate to you a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and you do not find its confirmation in the Book of Allah, the Exalted, nor do you find it good in the character of people, then it is false."],[4240,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us an admonition that made the skins tremble, the eyes shed tears, and the hearts quake. We said: 'It is as if this is the admonition of one bidding farewell, O Messenger of Allah, so what do you enjoin upon us?' He ﷺ said: 'That you fear Allah, the Exalted, and that you follow my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided, rightly led successors after me. Bite onto it with the molar teeth, for every innovation is misguidance.'"],[4241,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ gave us a sermon."],[4242,"He saw Ibn 'Umar ؓ with the button of his shirt undone. He was asked about that, and he said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing it.'"],[4243,"Whoever revives a Sunnah from my Sunnah and people act upon it, he will have the reward of those who act upon it, without their rewards being diminished in anything. And whoever introduces an innovation and it is acted upon, he will bear the burdens of those who act upon it, without their burdens being diminished in anything."],[4245,"Abu Ayyub went out to 'Uqbah b. 'Amir while he was in Egypt to ask him about a hadith he had heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he mentioned the story."],[4246,"Abu Sayyad narrated to him that he was with Maslamah one day at midday when a man on his mount entered upon him. He asked permission to see Maslamah and said, 'O Maslamah!' Maslamah ordered a slave girl of his, saying, 'Look who this is.' She said, 'An old man who has arrived on his mount.' He said, 'Call Maslamah for me.' I said, 'Should I call the emir for you?' He said, 'Return to him and ask him who you are.' He said, 'I am so-and-so.' Maslamah stood up quickly, and the man was one of the Companions ؓ, and said, 'I heard a hadith from the Prophet ﷺ, and the closest of the people to him that day was 'Uqbah b. 'Amir ؓ, so I wanted to ask him about it to be certain. Come with me to him, O Maslamah.' He said, 'Rather, I will send for him and he will come to me.' He said, 'Your authority has pleased you. Order Abu Sayyad to go with me to 'Uqbah.' When 'Uqbah ؓ saw him, he welcomed him and took his hand. The man said, 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say...' and he mentioned the hadith."],[4247,"A man from the people of Madinah came to Egypt and said to the doorkeeper of its emir, 'Tell the emir to come out to me.' The doorkeeper said, 'No one has said this to us since we settled in this place except you; it was only said, \"Seek permission for us to see the emir.\"' He said, 'Go to him and tell him, \"So-and-so is at the door.\"' The emir came out to him, and he said, 'I have come to you only to ask you about a hadith regarding the sutrah of a Muslim's 'awrah.'"],[4248,"I came to Madinah seeking knowledge, and behold the people were in the mosque of the Messenger of God ﷺ in circles, circles, conversing. He said: I began to pass by the circles until I came to a circle in which there was a pale man wearing two garments, as if he had just arrived from a journey. I heard him say: 'The people of the knots have perished, by the Lord of the Ka'bah; I do not grieve for them.' He said it three times. He said: I sat with him, and he spoke about what had been decreed for him, then he stood up. When he stood up, I asked about him: 'Who is this?' They said: 'Ubayy b. Ka'b ؓ, the leader of the Muslims.' I followed him until he reached his house, and he was shabby in appearance and shabby in clothing, one part resembling another. I greeted him, and he returned the greeting. Then he asked me: 'From which people are you?' I said: 'From the people of Iraq.' He said ؓ: 'The most questioning of people.' When he said that, I became angry, so I knelt on my knees, faced the qiblah, raised my hands, and said: 'O God, we complain of them to You. We spend our wealth, weary our bodies, and travel our mounts seeking knowledge, but when we meet them, they frown at us and say things to us.' Ubayy ؓ wept and began to appease me, and said: 'Woe to you, go there.' Then he said: 'O God, I make a covenant with You that if You keep me alive until Friday, I will speak of what I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ and will not fear the blame of any blamer for Your sake.' Then I think he stood up. When he said that, I left him and began waiting for Friday to hear his words. He said: When it was Thursday, I went out for some of my needs, and behold the streets were crowded with people. I did not enter any street but people met me. I said: 'What is the matter with the people?' They said: 'We think you are a stranger?' I said: 'Yes.' They said: 'The leader of the Muslims, Ubayy b. Ka'b ؓ, has died.' He said: I met Abu Musa ؓ in Iraq and told him the hadith. He said: 'Alas! If only he had lived until he conveyed to us the statement of the Messenger of God ﷺ.'"],[4249,"Knowledge is better than gold, and a righteous soul is better than pearls."],[4250,"The seeker of knowledge, or the possessor of knowledge, everything seeks forgiveness for him, even the fish in the sea."],[4251,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[4252,"Whoever seeks knowledge and attains it, God Almighty gives him a double portion of reward; and whoever seeks knowledge but does not attain it, God, Mighty and Majestic, gives him a single portion of reward. He then explained it, saying: Whoever seeks knowledge and attains it, God, Blessed and Exalted, gives him the reward for what he learned and the reward for what he acted upon; and whoever seeks knowledge but does not attain it, God Almighty gives him the reward for what he learned, and the reward for what he did not learn is dropped from him."],[4253,"When they prayed the morning prayer, they would sit in circles, circles, reciting the Qur'an and learning the obligatory duties and the sunnahs."],[4254,"God Almighty has not been worshipped with anything more excellent than understanding in religion."],[4255,"God, Mighty and Majestic, has not been worshipped with anything more excellent than understanding in religion, and a single jurist is harder on Satan than a thousand worshippers."],[4256,"Everything has a pillar, and the pillar of this religion is fiqh."],[4257,"Teach and do not be harsh, for the teacher is better than the harsh one."],[4258,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque while a group was remembering Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and a group was discussing fiqh. He ﷺ said: “Both gatherings are upon good. As for those who remember Allah Almighty and ask their Lord, if He wills He gives them, and if He wills He withholds from them. And these teach the people and learn. I was only sent as a teacher, and this is better.” Then he ﷺ sat with them."],[4259,"May Allah have mercy on Labid. He said: \"Gone are those in whose protection one could live, and I remain among a succession like the skin of a mangy camel.\" My father used to say: May Allah have mercy on Aishah ؓ. How would it be if she saw our time now?"],[4260,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Which of the people is most knowledgeable?” He ﷺ said: “The one who gathers the knowledge of the people to his own knowledge, and every possessor of knowledge is hungry [for more].”"],[4261,"The virtue of the scholar over the worshipper is like my virtue over my ummah."],[4262,"The scholar is preferred over the worshipper by seventy degrees, between each two degrees is as between heaven and earth."],[4263,"Teach and make things easy, and do not make things difficult.” He said it three times. “And if you become angry, be silent.”"],[4264,"Whoever preserves for my ummah forty hadiths of what benefits them in the matter of their religion will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection among the scholars, and the scholar is preferred over the worshipper by seventy degrees, Allah knows best what is between each two degrees."],[4265,"Shall I inform you about the most generous? The most generous is Allah Almighty, and I am the most generous of the children of Adam, and the most generous of them after me is a man who learned knowledge and spread his knowledge; he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection as a nation alone, and a man who strove with his life in the path of Allah until he was killed."],[4266,"The death of a scholar is an irreparable calamity, and a gap that cannot be filled, and he is a star that has been extinguished. The death of a tribe is easier than the death of a scholar."],[4267,"While Imran b. Husayn ؓ was sitting with some of his companions, narrating to them, a man said: “Do not narrate to us except from the Qur'an,” or “We only want the Qur'an.” He said: “Have you considered, if you and your companions were left to the Qur'an, would you find that the Zuhr prayer is four [rak'ahs] and the 'Asr prayer is four and the Maghrib prayer is three, with recitation in the first two rak'ahs? Have you considered, if you and your companions were left to the Qur'an, would you find that for every two hundred [dirhams] five [are due], and for camels such and such, and for cattle such and such? Have you considered, if you and your companions were left to the Qur'an, would you find that tawaf around the House is seven [circuits], and between al-Safa and al-Marwah such and such?”"],[4268,"Perhaps a man will belie me while he is reclining on his couch, and the hadith from me reaches him, and he says: “What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say? Leave this and bring what is in the Qur'an.”"],[4269,"Whoever desires knowledge, let him prefer the Qur'an, for in it is the knowledge of the first and the last."],[4270,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with the charity of our camels and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the charity of our camels. He said: So he ordered it ﷺ and it was distributed. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, in it there is what is between a gift for you and charity. He said: So I set aside the gift from the charity, and I stayed for some days. The people talked that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sending Khalid b. al-Walid ؓ to the slaves of Egypt as their charity collector. He said: I said: We have wealth, and my family has no property, so should I not give their charity before he comes to me? So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he was on a she-camel, and with him was a black man who had aligned his head with the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; I have never seen anyone among the people taller than him. When I approached him, he leaned toward me. He said: The Prophet ﷺ restrained him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the people have talked that you are sending Khalid b. al-Walid ؓ to the slaves of Egypt as their charity collector. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hands until we saw the whiteness of his armpits, then said: O Allah, I do not make it lawful for them to lie about me. Al-Munaqqa' said: I have never narrated a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except a hadith that the Book spoke of or a Sunnah informed of. He is lied about during his lifetime, so how about after his death ﷺ?"],[4272,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with the charity of our camels, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the charity of our camels. He said: So he ordered it ﷺ and it was distributed. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, in it there is what is between a gift for you and charity. He ﷺ said: Separate it. So I separated the gift from the charity, and I stayed for some days. The people talked that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sending Khalid b. al-Walid ؓ to the slaves of Mudar as their charity collector. He said: I said: We have wealth, and my family has no property, so should I not give their charity before he comes to my family? So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he was on a she-camel, and with him was a black man who had aligned his head with the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; I have never seen anyone among the people taller than him. When I approached him, he leaned toward me. He said: The Prophet ﷺ restrained him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the people have talked that you are sending Khalid b. al-Walid ؓ to the slaves of Mudar as their charity collector. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hands until we saw the whiteness of his armpits, then said: 'O Allah, I do not make it lawful for them to lie about me.' Al-Munaqqa' said: I have never narrated a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except a hadith that the Book spoke of or a Sunnah informed of. He is lied about during his lifetime, so how about after his death ﷺ?"],[4273,"Refresh the hearts so they may comprehend the remembrance."],[4274,"Talk to these hearts, for they are quick to become dull."],[4275,"The Qur'an was recited in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ and poetry was chanted, and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, Qur'an and poetry in one gathering? He ﷺ said: 'Yes.'"],[4276,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[4277,"Whoever lies about me deliberately to mislead people thereby, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[4278,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take a resting place or a house in Hell."],[4279,"Whoever says about me something I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[4280,"I entered the mosque and there was an old man sitting beside the pulpit, called Salim or Aslam. He said: I used to travel with 'Umar ؓ and recite rajaz poetry for him, and he would not narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We said to him: If only you would narrate to us. He ؓ said: I heard him ﷺ say: 'Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.'"],[4281,"Nasr b. Ali narrated to us, Muslim narrated to us, from al-Dujayn, from Aslam the freed slave of Umar, from Umar ؓ, from the Prophet ﷺ, and he mentioned it."],[4282,"Sufyan, meaning Ibn Waki, narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Dujayn with it."],[4283,"\"Whoever lies about me deliberately\""],[4284,"\"Whoever lies about me deliberately or rejects something I commanded, let him take his seat in a house in Hell.\""],[4285,"\"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[4286,"We were with al-Mughirah b. Shubah ؓ while he was in the mosque and with him were the people of Kufa. Then Said b. Zayd ؓ came, and al-Mughirah ؓ made room for him, saying, \"Here, sit.\" He seated him with him on the couch. Said ؓ said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, lying about me is not like lying about anyone else. Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[4288,"\"When a servant reaches sixty years of age, Allah Most High has excused Himself to him regarding his lifespan.\" Or he said: \"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has conveyed to him regarding his lifespan.\""],[4289,"He was asked: What do you wish for the one you love? He said: Death. He was asked: And if he does not die? He said: That his wealth and children become few."],[4290,"\"Jibril ﷺ said to me: 'O Muhammad, live as long as you wish, for you will die; love whom you wish, for you will part from him; and do what you wish, for you will meet it.'\""],[4291,"The gift of the believer is death."],[4292,"Abu Yala said: Abu Hammam narrated to us, Muawiyah b. Amr narrated to me, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us with it."],[4293,"\"How amazing is the heedless one from whom heedlessness is never lifted, and how amazing is the seeker of this world while death seeks him, and how amazing is the one who laughs with his mouth wide open while he does not know whether he has pleased Allah or angered Him.\""],[4294,"A woman died and the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ used to laugh about her. A certain person said: 'Woe to her; she has found rest.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Only the one who is forgiven finds rest.'"],[4295,"'Which of the believers is most astute?' They said: 'God and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'The most astute of believers is the one who remembers death most and is best prepared for it.'"],[4296,"'Which of the people is most astute?' I said: 'God and His Messenger know best.' He ﷺ said: 'The most astute of people is the one who remembers death most and is best prepared for God.'"],[4297,"'Let one of you adopt a remembering tongue, or a grateful heart, or a believing wife who helps him in his faith—or helps one of you in his faith.'"],[4298,"'You give birth for death and build for ruin, and you are eager for what perishes and abandon what remains. How welcome to you are these three: death, illness, and poverty.'"],[4299,"Jesus son of Mary ﷺ said: 'O children of Adam, give birth for death and build for ruin. Your souls perish while your dwellings remain.'"],[4300,"He used to say in his sermon: 'The truest speech is the Word of God; the firmest handhold is the word of piety; the best religion is the religion of Abraham ﷺ ; the best narrative is this Qur'an; the best way is the way of Muhammad ﷺ; the noblest speech is the remembrance of God Almighty; the best of matters are their resolutions; the worst of matters are their innovations; the best guidance is the guidance of the prophets (prayers and peace be upon them); the noblest death is the killing of martyrs; the worst misguidance is misguidance after guidance; the best deed or knowledge—Bishr was uncertain—is what benefits; the best guidance is what is followed; the worst blindness is blindness of the heart; the upper hand is better than the lower hand; little that suffices is better than much that distracts; a soul you save is better than an authority you cannot manage; the worst treachery is treachery at the time of death; the worst regret is the regret of the Day of Resurrection; among people are those who do not come to Friday prayer or the prayer except lagging behind, and do not remember God Almighty except in vain talk; the greatest sin is the lying tongue; the best wealth is wealth of the soul; the best provision is piety; the summit of wisdom is fear of God Almighty; the best thing cast into the heart is certainty; doubt is from unbelief; wailing is from the deeds of the Age of Ignorance; embezzlement is from the coals of Hell; hoarding is a branding from the Fire; poetry is the flutes of Iblis; wine is the mother of all sin; women are the snares of Satan; youth is a branch of madness; the worst earnings are the earnings of usury; the worst food is consuming the wealth of orphans; the fortunate is the one who takes heed from others; the wretched is the one who was wretched in his mother's womb; each of you is sufficed by what his soul is content with; he will end up in a space of four cubits; the best of affairs is what is immediate; the most certain part of a deed is its ending; the worst vessels are the vessels of falsehood; everything that is coming is near; insulting a Muslim is wickedness and fighting him is unbelief; eating his flesh is among the sins against God Almighty; the sanctity of his wealth is like the sanctity of his blood; whoever swears an oath by God Almighty, He will prove him false; whoever forgives, God will forgive him; whoever pardons, God will pardon him; whoever suppresses anger, God Almighty will reward him; whoever bears calamities patiently, God Mighty and Majestic will help him; whoever recognizes affliction will be patient with it; whoever does not recognize it will deny it; whoever denies it, God Blessed and Exalted will let him go to waste; whoever seeks reputation, God will make him heard of; whoever intends the world, it will overpower him; whoever obeys Satan disobeys God Mighty and Majestic; whoever disobeys God Almighty, He will punish him.'"],[4301,"He used to deliver this sermon every Thursday evening. He said: We used to consider it the sermon of the Prophet ﷺ: 'O people, the truest speech is the Book of God Almighty; the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ; the worst of matters are their innovations; every innovation is a heresy; every heresy is misguidance. Indeed, O people, you will be made to stand on a single open plain, the sight will reach you, the caller will make you hear. Indeed, the wretched is the one who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is the one who takes heed from others.'"],[4302,"Umar ؓ stood before the people as a preacher when they entered Syria at al-Jabiyah and said: 'Learn the Qur'an so you may be known by it, and act upon it so you may be among its people. It will never reach the station of one who has a right that he be obeyed in disobedience to God Almighty. Know that no statement of truth or momentous reminder brings near a term or pushes away provision. Know that between the servant and his provision there is a veil.' He said: 'His provision appears to him; but if he plunges ahead, the veil is torn, and he will not attain beyond his provision. Train the horses, compete in archery, wear sandals, use the tooth-stick, adopt the ways of Ma'add. Beware of the character of the non-Arabs, of living next to tyrants, of a cross being seen among you, of sitting at a table where wine is drunk, of entering the bathhouse without a waist-wrapper, and of letting your women enter the bathhouses—for that is not lawful. Beware of earning from the non-Arabs after you settle in their lands what keeps you in their land, for you will soon return to your own lands. Beware of yellow dye: do not put it on your necks. Hold to the wealth of the Arabs: livestock, with which you move wherever you move. Know that drinks are made from raisins, honey, and dates; whatever of them has aged is wine, which is not lawful. Know that God Almighty will not purify three persons, nor look at them, nor bring them near on the Day of Resurrection: a man who gives his leader a pledge intending worldly gain—if he obtains it, he fulfills it; if not, he does not; a man who goes out with merchandise after the afternoon prayer and swears that he was given such-and-such for it, so it is bought because of his word; and insulting a Muslim is wickedness and fighting him is unbelief. It is not lawful for you to abandon your brother for more than three days. Whoever goes to a sorcerer, a soothsayer, or a diviner and believes what he says has disbelieved in what was sent down upon Muhammad ﷺ.'"],[4303,"I served the Messenger of God ﷺ when I was eight years old. The first thing he ﷺ taught me was to say to me: 'O my son, perfect your ablution...' And he mentioned the hadith, and at the end of it: 'Do not spend a night or reach a morning with any deceit in your heart toward anyone of the people of Islam. This is from my way. Whoever takes my way has loved me, and whoever loves me is with me in Paradise. O my son, if you act upon this and preserve my instruction, let nothing be dearer to you than death, for in it is your rest.'"],[4304,"Abu Ya'la said: Yahya b. Ayyub narrated to us; Muhammad b. al-Hasan b. Abi Yazid narrated to us; 'Abbad al-Minqari narrated to us, from 'Ali b. Zayd, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Anas ؓ, and he mentioned the like of it and more complete than it."],[4305,"'And greet in your house; God Almighty will increase your blessings. Honor the elderly of the Muslims and show mercy to their young. I and you will come like these two.' And he ﷺ joined his fingers."],[4306,"«If you sleep in a state of purity and then die, you die as a martyr. O Anas, honor the elderly and be merciful to the young."],[4307,"Indeed, everything has an honor, and the most honorable of gatherings is that which faces the qiblah. And one is only seated with trustworthiness. Kill the snake and the scorpion even if you are in your prayer. Whoever loves to be the most honorable of people, let him fear Allah Almighty. Whoever loves to be the strongest of people, let him put his trust in Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Whoever loves to be the richest of people, let him have more confidence in what is in the hand of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, than in what is in his own hand. Shall I inform you of the worst of you? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He ﷺ said: The one who alights alone, withholds his assistance, and lashes his slave. Shall I inform you of something worse than this? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He ﷺ said: The one who hates people and they hate him. Shall I inform you of something worse than this? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He ﷺ said: The one who does not overlook a slip, does not accept an excuse, and does not forgive a sin. Shall I inform you of something worse than this? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He ﷺ said: The one from whose good no one hopes and from whose evil no one is safe. Indeed, Jesus son of Mary ﷺ stood among his people and said: O Children of Israel, do not speak wisdom in the presence of the ignorant, for you would wrong it; and do not withhold it from its people, for you would wrong them. And do not wrong, and do not repay an oppressor with oppression, lest your virtue be nullified before your Lord. O Children of Israel, matters are of three types: a matter whose right guidance is clear, so follow it; a matter whose error is clear, so avoid it; and a matter over which there is disagreement, so refer it to its knower. 3128"],[4308,"I knew ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ؓ when he was governor over us in Madinah during the time of al-Walīd b. ʿAbd al-Malik, and he was a young man. He mentioned it. I said: In the Sunan there is something of its beginnings."],[4309,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one day to the mosque, and there was a group of people conversing; their talk made them laugh. He stopped and greeted, then said: «Remember the destroyer of pleasures: death.» Then he ﷺ went out another time, and there was a group of people talking and laughing. He said: «By the One in Whose hand is my soul, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.» He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ also went out, and there was a group of people talking and laughing. He greeted, then said: «Verily, Islam began as something strange, and it will return as something strange, so blessed are the strangers on the Day of Resurrection.» It was said to him: Who are the strangers, O Messenger of Allah? He ﷺ said: «Those who are righteous when the people are corrupt."],[4310,"I was present with Abū al-Dardāʾ ؓ when death came to him, and he said: I will tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: «Worship Allah Almighty as if you see Him; for if you do not see Him, He sees you. Count yourself among the dead. Beware of the supplication of the wronged, for it is answered. Whoever among you can attend the late evening prayer and the dawn prayer in congregation, let him do so, even if crawling."],[4311,"Worship Allah Almighty as if you see Him… He mentioned it as mawqūf up to his saying: \"the wronged.\" And he added: And know that a little which suffices you is better than much which distracts you; and that debt does not wear out, and kindness is not forgotten."],[4312,"He forbade a man three things and enjoined upon him three things. As for what he forbade him, he said: «Do not break a covenant, do not help in breaking it, and do not oppress, for whoever is oppressed, Allah Almighty will certainly help him. Beware of the plot of the evil, for the evil plot does not beset except its own people, and for them there is a pursuer from Allah Almighty.» As for what he enjoined upon him: «That you remember death often, for it will console you from everything else; and you must supplicate, for you do not know when you will be answered; and you must be grateful, for it is increase.» Then Sufyān recited: \"If you are grateful, I will surely increase you.\""],[4313,"«With Allah, Blessed and Exalted, are treasuries of good and evil; their keys are men."],[4314,"«The best of you are those with the best character."],[4315,"We accompanied Jundub to the fort of al-Mukātab, and we said to him: Counsel us. He said: Hold to the Qurʾān, for it is the light of the dark night and the guidance of the day; so act upon it despite hardship and poverty. If trial befalls you, then put forward your wealth before your life; and if the trial surpasses that, then put forward your wealth and your life before your religion. For the deprived is the one deprived of his religion, and the robbed is the one robbed of his religion. Verily, there is no wealth that avails after which comes the Fire, and no poverty that impoverishes after which comes Paradise. The Fire’s prisoner is never released, and its poor are never enriched."],[4316,"«Verily, among the people of the worst station is the one who destroys his Hereafter for the worldly life of another."],[4317,"«Whoever witnesses a matter and dislikes it is like one who was absent from it, and whoever is absent from a matter and approves of it is like one who witnessed it."],[4318,"O Salman, indeed the world is a prison for the believer and a paradise for the disbeliever."],[4319,"Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gives the world based on the intention of the Hereafter, but He does not give the Hereafter based on the intention of the world."],[4320,"Indeed, a good deed I do today is more beloved to me than twice its like with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, because when we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Hereafter concerned us and the world did not concern us, but today the world has inclined us."],[4321,"The angels of the night and the angels of the day gather at the ‘Asr prayer and the Fajr prayer. The angels of the day ascend at the ‘Asr prayer, and the angels of the night remain among you, and the angels of the night ascend at the Fajr prayer, and the angels of the day remain among you. They say: “We came to them while they were praying, and we left them while they were praying. We left among them a man whom no good or affliction ever befell except that he knew it was from You.” So He says: “Test My servant,” or “Increase My servant.” Sufyan said: I do not know which of the two he began with. He said: So they test him. Then He says: “Test him,” and he is tested. Then He says: “Test him,” while He is most knowing. Then they say: “The affliction has reached its limit, O Lord.” He says: “Increase him,” and he is increased. Then He says: “Increase him,” and he is increased. Then He says: “Increase him,” and he is increased. Then He says: “Increase him,” while He is most knowing. Then they say: “The increase has reached its limit, O Lord.” He says: “How did you leave My servant in affliction, and how did you see him in ease?” They say: “O Lord, the most patient of servants and the most grateful.” He says: “Record My servant among those who will not be replaced or changed until he meets Me.”"],[4322,"It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which faith is best? He ﷺ said: “Patience and generosity.”"],[4323,"No household remains patient for three days under hardship except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, brings them provision."],[4324,"Indeed people today are like a tree with leafy branches, and soon people will become like a thorny tree. If you oppose them, they oppose you; if you leave them, they will not leave you; and if you flee from them, they will pursue you.” He said: I said: And how is the way out, O Messenger of Allah? He ﷺ said: “Lend them from your honor for the day of your poverty.”"],[4325,"Whoever guards his tongue, Allah the Exalted will cover his faults; whoever restrains his anger, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will withhold His punishment from him; and whoever apologizes to Allah the Exalted, He will accept his excuse."],[4326,"\"Whoever is in the assistance of his brother, God, the Mighty and Majestic, is in his assistance as long as he is in the assistance of his brother; and whoever unties a knot, God unties from him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4327,"And Abu Musa narrated to us: ‘Isa b. Shu‘ayb al-Darir, Abu al-Fadl, informed us: al-Rabi‘ b. Sulaym al-Numayri narrated to us, from Abu ‘Umayr b. Anas, from his father, something similar. :"],[4328,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: ‘Abd al-Salam b. Hashim al-Bazzar narrated to us: Khalid b. Burd al-‘Ijli narrated to me, from his father, from Anas ؓ, with it. :"],[4329,"Whoever is able to attain worldly gain and is able not to take it, Allah the Exalted will marry him to the wide-eyed maidens wherever He wills; and whoever is invited by a prostitute to herself and leaves her out of fear of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, Allah the Exalted will marry him to the wide-eyed maidens wherever He wills."],[4330,"«O son of Adam, stand up to Me and I will walk to you; walk to Me and I will run to you»"],[4331,"The Prophet ﷺ said to ʿUmar ؓ : «Gather your people for me». So he gathered them, and they were at the door. Then he ﷺ said: «Indeed, my friends among you are the God-fearing. Beware lest people come with [good] deeds while you come with burdens that you carry on your backs»"],[4332,"«Every person has three friends. As for one friend, he says: “What you spend is yours, and what you hold back is not yours”—that is his wealth. As for another friend, he says: “I am with you, but when you reach the king’s door, I will leave you and return”—that is his family and servants. As for another friend, he says: “I am with you wherever you enter and wherever you leave”—that is his deeds. Then he will say: “You were the least of the three in my esteem”»"],[4333,"«Just as grapes are not harvested from thorns, the wicked will not occupy the stations of the righteous. They are two paths; whichever you take will lead you to its people»"],[4334,"Indeed, Allah, blessed and exalted, built His religion upon four pillars. Whoever does not bear them patiently and act upon them will meet Allah, exalted, among the transgressors. He [i.e., someone] said: “And what are they, O Abu Dharr?” He ؓ said: “To surrender Allah’s lawful [matters] for Allah, and Allah’s unlawful for Allah, and Allah’s command for Allah, and Allah’s prohibition for Allah—none is to be entrusted with them except Allah.” He said: Abu al-Qasim ﷺ said: «Just as grapes are not harvested from thorns, so the wicked will not attain the stations of the righteous»"],[4335,"Two men brought a dispute before Muharib b. Dithar. He said: A man testified against one of them, and the one testified against said: “By Allah, I did not know that he was a truthful man; if you ask about him, he will surely be praised or deemed reliable, yet he testified falsely against me, and I do not know what emboldened him to do that.” Muharib said: “O man, fear Allah, for I heard ʿAbdullah b. ʿUmar ؓ say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, while admonishing a man that day.” Then he mentioned the hadith, and said: «Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection, the birds will beat their wings and cast out what is in their bellies, though they have no claim to be sought»"],[4336,"«And they have no claim to be sought»"],[4337,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out—then he mentioned the hadith, and in it: «Indeed, the work of the Hereafter is grief upon a high ground» three times, «while the work of the Fire is easy with desire. The happy one is he who is shielded from trials»"],[4338,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out at noon and found Abu Bakr ؓ in the mosque. He said: «What brought you out at this hour?» He ؓ replied: “The one who brought you out, O Messenger of Allah, brought me out.” Then ʿUmar b. al-Khattab ؓ came, and he ﷺ said: «What brought you out, O Ibn al-Khattab?» He ؓ said: “The one who brought you both out, O Messenger of Allah, brought me out.” Then ʿUmar ؓ sat down, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began talking to them. Then he said: «Do you have the strength to go to this palm grove, so that you may get food, drink, and shade?» He said: We said: “Yes.” He said: «Come with us to the house of Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayyihan al-Ansari.» The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went ahead of us, greeted, and sought permission three times, while Umm al-Haytham ؓ was behind the door listening to the words and wanting the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to grant her more of his greeting. When he ﷺ was about to leave, Umm al-Haytham ؓ came out behind them and said: “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah I heard your greeting, but I wanted you to increase us in your greeting.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said good words to her and said: «Where is Abu al-Haytham? I do not see him.» She said: “He is nearby; he went to fetch us fresh water. Enter, for he will come soon, if Allah, exalted, wills.” She spread a mat for them under a tree. Then Abu al-Haytham came and rejoiced at them, and his eye was comforted by them. He climbed a palm tree and cut a bunch of dates. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «That is enough for you, O Abu al-Haytham.» He said: “O Messenger of Allah, you will eat from its ripe dates, its unripe dates, and its hanging clusters.” Then he brought them water, and they drank after it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «This is part of the bliss about which you will be asked.» Then Umm al-Haytham ؓ stood up to knead dough for them and bake bread. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and ʿUmar lay down for the midday nap. They woke up when their food was ready. The food was placed before them, and they ate until they were full and praised Allah, exalted. Umm al-Haytham ؓ returned to them the rest of the bunch, and they ate from its ripe dates and its clusters. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ greeted them and supplicated for them."],[4339,"…until we came to the house of Malik b. al-Tayyihan, Abu al-Haytham al-Ansari ؓ . And he [the narrator] added at its end: Then he supplicated for them for good, and then he ﷺ said to Abu al-Haytham: «When you hear that some slaves have come to us, come to us.» Abu al-Haytham ؓ said: When I heard that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had been brought slaves, I went to Madinah, and he gave me a head [i.e., a slave], whom I contracted to manumit for forty thousand dirhams. I never saw a head with greater blessing than his. ʿAbdullah b. ʿIsa said: I narrated it to Ismaʿil b. Muslim al-Makki, and he narrated something similar to me, and added in it: Umm al-Haytham said to him: “Would you supplicate for us?” He ﷺ said: «May the fasting break their fast at your place, may the righteous eat your food, and may the angels send blessings upon you»"],[4340,"«Who is this?» ʿUmar ؓ hastened to reply: “This is Abu Bakr and ʿUmar.” He ﷺ said: «What brought you two out at this hour?» ʿUmar ؓ said: “I went out and entered the mosque, and I saw the figure of Abu Bakr ؓ and said: ‘Who is this?’ He said: ‘Abu Bakr.’ I said: ‘What brought you out at this hour?’ He mentioned what had happened. I said: ‘By Allah, nothing brought me out except what brought you out.’” Then the Prophet ﷺ said: «And by Allah, nothing brought me out except what brought you two out. Come with us to the Waqifi Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayyihan; perhaps we will find something with him to feed us.» So we went out walking until we reached the garden in the moonlight. We knocked on the door, and the woman said: “Who is this?” ʿUmar ؓ said: “This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and ʿUmar.” She opened the door for us, and we entered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Where is your husband?» She said: “He went to fetch us fresh water from the palm-grove of Banu Harithah; he will come to you now.” He said: He came carrying a water-skin until he brought it to a palm tree and hung it on one of its stumps. Then he turned to us and said: “Welcome and greetings! No one has ever been visited by people like those who have visited me.” Then he cut a bunch of dates for us, brought it to us, and we began to pick from it in the moonlight and eat. Then he took a knife and went among the sheep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Beware of the milking ewe,» or he said: «Beware of the one with milk.» He ؓ took a sheep, slaughtered it, and skinned it. He said to his wife: “Get up,” so she ground flour, baked bread, and began cutting meat into the pot and lighting fire under it until the bread and meat were ready. He crumbled bread and poured over it from the broth and meat. Then he brought it to us and placed it before us, and we ate until we were full. Then he went to the water-skin, which the wind had cooled, so it was cold. He poured into a vessel and handed it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who drank. Then he handed it to Abu Bakr ؓ, who drank. Then he handed it to ʿUmar ؓ, who drank. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Praise be to Allah, who brought us out—nothing brought us out but hunger—and then we returned having obtained this. You will surely be asked about this on the Day of Resurrection; this is part of the bliss.» Then he ﷺ said to the Waqifi: «Do you not have a servant to fetch you water?» He said: “No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah.” He ﷺ said: «When captives come to us, come to us, and we will order a servant for you.» Not long after, captives came to him, and the Waqifi went to him. He said: «What brings you?» He said: “O Messenger of Allah, your promise that you made to me.” He said: «These are captives; get up and choose from them.» He said: “You choose for me.” He ﷺ said: «Take this boy and treat him well.» He said: He took him and went with him to his wife. She said: “What is this?” He told her the story. She said: “What did you say to him?” He said: “I said to him: ‘You choose for me.’” She said: “You did well. He told you: ‘Treat him well,’ so treat him well.” He said: “What is treating him well?” She said: “That you set him free.” He said: “Then he is free for the sake of Allah, exalted.”"],[4341,"«Flour was never sifted for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at all»"],[4342,"Hafsah bint Umar said to Umar ؓ: If only you would wear softer clothes than yours and eat softer food than yours. He ؓ said: I will take my case against you to yourself. Did you not know of the matter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr, such and such? So she wept. He ؓ said: I told you, but I will share with them in their harsh life, perhaps I will share with them in their pleasant life. He agreed to it and said: Yes."],[4344,"I went out on a cold morning from my house hungry and weak, and the cold had made me shiver. I took a worn-out hide that we had, cut a hole in it, put it around my neck, and tied it over my chest to keep warm. By Allah, there was nothing in my house to eat, and if there had been anything in the house of the Prophet ﷺ, it would have reached me. I went out to some parts of al-Madinah and looked at a Jew in a garden through a gap in his wall. He said: What is wrong with you, O Bedouin? Would you like a date for every bucket? I said: Yes, open the garden. He opened it for me, and I entered. I began drawing a bucket and he would give me a date, until when I filled my palm, I said: I have enough from you now. So I ate them, then drank from the water. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and sat with him in the mosque while he ﷺ was among a group of his companions ؓ. Suddenly Mus'ab ibn 'Umayr ؓ appeared before us wearing a patched cloak. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him, he remembered what he had been in of luxury, and saw his current condition, so his eyes shed tears and he wept. Then he said: \"How will you be when one of you goes out in one garment in the morning and another in the evening, and your houses are veiled as the Ka'bah is veiled?\" We said: We will be better that day; we will be spared the burden and will be free for worship. He ﷺ said: \"You are better today than you will be on that day.\""],[4345,"And Abu Ya'la said: 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, something similar. I say: al-Tirmidhi narrated it from the path of Ibn Ishaq with it in abridged form. 3157/3 - Ahmad narrated from the hadith of Mujahid, from 'Ali ؓ part of the story of the dates."],[4346,"And Abu Ya'la said: 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, something similar. I say: al-Tirmidhi narrated it from the path of Ibn Ishaq with it in abridged form. 3157/3 - Ahmad narrated from the hadith of Mujahid, from 'Ali ؓ part of the story of the dates."],[4347,"\"O my little daughter, by Allah, there is no food in the house for any liver to eat except what you see – for a small thing in front of him – but go back, for Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will provide for you.\" When she came to me and told me, I left and went until I came to Banu Qurayzah, and there was a Jew at the edge of a well. He said: O 'Ali, would you water some palm trees of mine and I will feed you? I said: Yes, so I made a deal with him to draw every bucket for a date. I began drawing, and every time I drew a bucket he gave me a date, until my hands were full of dates. I sat down and ate, then drank from the water. Then I said: Woe to you, stomach, today I met good. Then I drew likewise for the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then I placed it down, and I set off returning. When I was on part of the road, I saw a dinar thrown. When I saw it, I stopped looking at it and debating with myself whether to take it or leave it. I refused except to take it, and I said: I will consult the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I took it. When I came to her, I told her the news. She said: This is provision from Allah Almighty, so go and buy flour for us. I went to the market, and there was a Jew from the Jews of Fadak selling barley flour. I bought from him, and when I measured it, he said: Are you not from Abu al-Qasim? I said: His cousin, and his daughter is my wife. So he gave me back the dinar. I came to her and told her the news. She said: This is provision from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, so go and pawn it for eight carats of gold with meat. I did, then I brought it to her and cut it for her. She set up, kneaded, and baked, then we made food and sent for the Messenger of Allah. He came to us, and when he saw the food, he said: \"What is this? Did you not come to me just now asking me?\" We said: Yes, sit, O Messenger of Allah, and we will tell you the news. If you consider it good, you will eat and we will eat. We told him the news, and he said: \"It is good, so eat in the name of Allah.\" Then he ﷺ stood up and went out, and there was a Bedouin woman rushing as if her heart had been torn out. She said: O Messenger of Allah, my father sent me with a dinar, and it fell from me. By Allah, I do not know where it fell. Please, by my father and mother, see if it is mentioned to you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Call 'Ali ibn Abi Talib for me.\" I came to him ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Go to the butcher and tell him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ says to you: Your carats are on me, so send the dinar.\" He sent it, and he gave it to the Bedouin woman, so she went away."],[4348,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we entered one of the gardens of the Ansar. We began picking dates and eating. He said to me: \"O Ibn 'Umar, why do you not eat?\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not desire it. He ﷺ said: \"But I desire it, and this is the morning of the fourth day since I have not tasted food or found it. If I wished, I would call upon my Lord and He would give me the like of the kingdom of Kisra and Qaysar. How will it be with you, O Ibn 'Umar, if you remain among a people who store up a year's provision and certainty weakens?\" By Allah, we had not moved or gone until it was revealed: \"And how many a creature carries not its own provision; Allah provides for it and for you, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has not commanded me to hoard the world or follow desires. Whoever hoards it seeking a lasting life, verily life is in the hand of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Indeed, I do not hoard a dinar or a dirham, nor do I store provision for tomorrow.\""],[4349,"'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr ؓ prepared food for 'A'ishah ؓ and began raising one dish and putting down another. He said: She ؓ turned her face to the wall weeping. 'Urwah ؓ said to her: You have spoiled it for us. She said: \"By the One who sent him with the truth, he did not see sieves from the time Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent him until he was taken in death.\""],[4350,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept on a bed stuffed with palm fiber and a pillow stuffed with palm fiber. He ﷺ got up and it left marks on his skin, so I wept. He ﷺ said: \"O Umm Salamah, what makes you weep?\" I said: What I see of the marks of this. He ﷺ said: \"Do not weep, for by Allah, if I wished the mountains to travel with me, they would travel.\""],[4351,"When death came to him, he said: I die upon a matter that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not initiate, nor Abu Bakr nor Umar ؓ. Indeed, I have not left behind any gold or silver except what is in this sword of mine, so sell it and shroud me with it."],[4352,"The Arabs used to say: \"Whoever eats bread becomes fat.\" When we conquered Khaybar, we drove them away from a loaf of bread they had. I sat upon it and ate until I was full, then I began looking at my shoulders to see if I had become fat."],[4353,"Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali, 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas, and 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far ؓ entered upon me and said: Make for us food from what the Prophet ﷺ loved to eat. She said to al-Hasan: O my son, we do not desire it today. So she took barley, ground it, sifted it, made a loaf from it, and made its condiment oil, sprinkled pepper on it, and brought it to them. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ loved this and enjoyed eating it."],[4354,"A nephew of ours married and he made food. Ibn Sirin said: A man among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would remain for days without eating. If he found a hide, he would be content with it; if he did not find one, he would tie a stone to his stomach."],[4355,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us in the expedition of Nakhlah, and with us was 'Amr ibn Suraqah. He was a man with a delicate stomach, tall. He became hungry and his back bent, so he could not walk. He fell upon us, so we took a slab of stones and tied it to his stomach, then fastened it to his back, and he walked with us. We came to a tribe of Arabs and they hosted us, and he walked with us. Then he said: I used to think that the two legs carry the stomach, but now I see that the stomach carries the two legs."],[4356,"Indeed, the worst of my nation are those who were brought up in luxury and whose bodies grew upon it."],[4357,"A man died during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[4358,"'Umara was alone in narrating it, and 'Abd al-Rahman narrated rejected reports from unknown narrators."],[4359,"'Umar ؓ summoned me, and there before him was a leather mat on which gold was scattered like chaff. Ibn 'Abbas ؓ said: And al-hatha is straw. He said: Come, divide it among your people. Allah knows best whether, in withholding this from His Prophet and from Abu Bakr, He intended good or evil. Then 'Umar ؓ began to weep, and he said in his weeping: By the One in Whose hand is my soul, He did not withhold it from His Prophet ﷺ and from Abu Bakr ؓ intending evil for them, but He gave it to me intending good for me."],[4360,"'Umar ؓ summoned me."],[4361,"I fear for you in the trial of prosperity more than I fear for you in the trial of adversity. You were tested with the trial of adversity and you were patient, and indeed the world is green and sweet."],[4362,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited Bilal ؓ, and he brought out to him piles of dates. He said: \"What is this, O Bilal?\" He ؓ said: \"Dates I have stored up, O Messenger of Allah.\" He ﷺ said: \"Do you not fear that you will hear a hissing for them in Hellfire? Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear decrease from the Owner of the Throne.\""],[4363,"Whoever has little wealth, many dependents, prays well, and does not backbite the Muslims will come on the Day of Resurrection while he is with me like these two."],[4364,"I was with Salman ؓ, and he mentioned a story. He said: Then he mentioned the treasures of Chosroes. He said: Indeed, the One who gave you those treasures, granted them to you, and opened them for you was holding back His treasuries while Muhammad ﷺ was alive. They used to wake up with not a single dinar or dirham, nor a mudd of food. So what is that, O brother of Banu 'Abs? Then we passed by threshing floors where grain was being winnowed, and he said: Indeed, the One who gave you those treasures, granted them to you, and opened them for you was holding back His treasuries while Muhammad ﷺ was alive. They used to wake up with not even a mudd of food. So what is that, O brother of Banu 'Abs?"],[4365,"'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ summoned a man from Banu Jumah called Sa'id b. 'Amir b. Hidhyam and said to him: \"I am appointing you over such-and-such a land.\" He said: \"Will you excuse me, O Commander of the Faithful?\" He said: \"By Allah, I will not. You have placed it upon my neck and then you leave me?\" 'Umar ؓ said: \"Should we not assign a stipend for you?\" He said: \"You have already made for me in my 'ata' what suffices me without it, and more than what I want.\" He said: When his 'ata' came out, he would buy provisions for his family and give the rest as charity. His wife would say to him: \"Where is the surplus of your 'ata'?\" He would say: \"I have loaned it.\" Then some people came to him and said: \"Your family has a right over you, and your in-laws have a right over you.\" He said: \"I am not one to prefer them over the pursuit of the maidens of Paradise. If one of the best women of Paradise were to appear, the earth would shine for her as the sun shines. And I am not one to lag behind the first emancipation after I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'People will be gathered for the reckoning, and the poor believers will come walking quickly like doves. It will be said to them: \"Stop for the reckoning.\" They will say: \"We have no reckoning and you did not give us anything.\" Their Lord, Mighty and Exalted, will say to them: \"My servants have spoken the truth.\" Then a gate of Paradise will be opened for them, and they will enter it seventy years before the rest of the people.'\""],[4366,"The righteous have not adorned themselves in this world with anything like renunciation of it."],[4367,"When you see someone who renounces the world, draw near to him, for he is granted wisdom."],[4368,"Wealth is not from abundance of possessions; true wealth is contentment of the soul."],[4369,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he turned to Usamah b. Zayd ؓ, say: 'O Usamah, beware of every hungry liver that will dispute with you before Allah Most High on the Day of Resurrection. Beware the supplication of servants who have melted their flesh and burned their skin in the winds and hot sand, and who have parched their livers until their eyesight failed. If you wish, look at them, and the angels rejoice over them. Through them earthquakes and trials are averted.' Then he wept until his sobbing grew intense, then said: 'Woe to this nation! What will it meet from those among them who obey their Lord? How will they kill them and call them liars because they obeyed Allah, Blessed and Exalted?' Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will the people then be upon Islam?' He ﷺ said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then for what will they fight?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Umar, the people abandoned the path and rode mounts, wore the softest clothes, and the sons of Persia served them, adorning themselves as a woman adorns herself for her husband. When the friends of Allah Most High speak, upon them are cloaks, their backs bent, they have slain themselves with thirst. When one of them speaks, he is called a liar, and it is said to him: \"You are the companion of Satan and the head of misguidance; you forbid the adornment of Allah Most High and the good things of provision.\" They recite the Book of Allah Most High without religion, and they despise the friends of Allah. Know, O Usamah, that the closest of people to Allah Most High on the Day of Resurrection is the one whose grief, thirst, and hunger in this world were prolonged—the pure, the righteous, who, when they are present, are not brought near, and when they are absent, are not missed. The regions of the earth know them; they are known among the inhabitants of heaven and hidden from the inhabitants of earth. The angels surround them. People enjoy ease while they enjoy hunger and thirst. People wear soft clothes while they wear the roughest clothes. People spread out beds while they spread out their foreheads and knees. People laugh while they weep. O Usamah, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not combine for them hardship in this world and the Hereafter; theirs is Paradise. If only I had seen them, O Usamah! For them is glad tidings in the Hereafter, and the earth is merciful through them, and the Compeller is pleased with them. People neglected the deeds and character of the prophets, while they preserved them. The desirous one is he who desires Allah Most High with a desire like theirs, and the loser is he who opposes them. The earth weeps when it loses them, and Allah Most High is wrathful with every land that has none like them. O Usamah, when you see them in a village, know that they are a safeguard for that village; Allah Most High does not punish a people among whom they are. Take them for yourself, that you may be saved through them. Beware of abandoning what they are upon, lest your foot slip and you fall into the Fire. They were deprived of the lawful things Allah permitted them; they sought the bounty of the Hereafter and abandoned food and drink despite ability. They did not scramble after the world as dogs scramble after carcasses. People were occupied with the world while they occupied themselves with obedience to Allah, Blessed and Exalted. They wore patched garments and ate broken pieces. You see them disheveled and dusty; people think there is a disease in them, but that is not the case. People think their minds have gone, but they have not gone; rather, they looked with their hearts upon the One who took their minds away from the world, so in this world, among the people of the world, they walk without minds. O Usamah, they became rational when people's minds departed; for them is glad tidings in the Hereafter.'"],[4370,"Indeed, what destroyed those before you was this dinar and this dirham, and they will destroy you."],[4371,"Four things are from a person's happiness: that his wife be compatible, his children be righteous, his brothers be upright, and his sustenance be in his own land."],[4372,"If a man entered a house within a house and persisted there in a deed, people would soon speak of it. There is no worker who performs a deed except that Allah Most High clothes him with the garment of his deed—if good, then good; if evil, then evil."],[4373,"Abu al-Darda' ؓ wrote to Maslamah b. Mukhallad: 'To proceed: When a servant acts in obedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, loves him; and when He loves him, He makes him beloved to His creation. When a servant acts in disobedience to Allah Most High, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hates him; and when Allah Most High hates him, He makes him hateful to creation.'"],[4374,"I met an old Bedouin shaykh at al-Raml and said to him: 'Did you meet anyone from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Who?' He said: 'Abdullah b. Amr b. al-As ؓ.' I said to him: 'What did you hear him say?' He said: 'I heard him ؓ say: \"Secure your worldly affairs as if you will live forever, and work for your Hereafter as if you will die tomorrow.\"'"],[4375,"Shall I inform you of those for whom the Fire is forbidden tomorrow? It is forbidden for every gentle, easy, close, and lenient person."],[4376,"The world is the believer's prison and the disbeliever's paradise."],[4377,"If the world weighed as much as a mosquito's wing in the sight of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, He would not have given a disbeliever a drink of water from it."],[4378,"Some people from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited Khabbab ؓ and said: 'Rejoice, O Abu Abdullah, you will meet Muhammad ﷺ at the Pond.' He said: 'How with this?' and he pointed to the top and bottom of the house. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said: 'What suffices any of you from the world is like the provision of a rider.'"],[4379,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ while he was on the pulpit saying: \"What is little and sufficient is better than what is abundant and distracting.\""],[4380,"\"If a servant were to flee from his provision as he flees from death, his provision would still come to him just as death comes to him.\""],[4381,"The world is only like a water pool; its clear part has gone, and its muddiness remains."],[4382,"The clear part of the world has gone, and nothing remains of it but turbidity; and death today is a gift for every Muslim."],[4383,"Al-Harith said: Muawiya b. Amr narrated to us; Za'ida narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abi Ziyad, from Abu Juhayfa, with this chain, and he did not mention Ibn Masud ؓ."],[4385,"The believer who mixes with people and endures their harm has a greater reward than the believer who does not mix with people and does not endure their harm."],[4386,"Al-Harith said: Muawiya b. Amr narrated to us; Za'ida narrated to us, from al-Amash, with this chain."],[4387,"Accustom yourselves to patience, for trial is about to befall you, just as what befell us did not befall you while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[4388,"I was dearer to your father than you, and you are dearer to me than my son. Two traits I enjoin upon you: be sincere to the believer and associate with the wicked, for the wicked is pleased with you by good character, and it is a right upon us to be sincere to the believer."],[4389,"I came to Amr b. Hurayth to rent a house from him in his home. He said: \"Rent it, for it is blessed for its owner and blessed for whoever dwells in it.\" I said: \"From what is that?\" He said: \"I came to the Prophet ﷺ when a camel had been slaughtered and he had ordered it to be divided. He said to the one dividing it: 'Give Amr a share of it.' But he did not give me and neglected me. The next day I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while there were dirhams in front of him. He said: 'Did you take the share I ordered for you?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, he did not give me anything.' He said: Then he ﷺ took some dirhams and gave them to me. I brought them to my mother and said: 'Take these dirhams that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took with his own hand and gave to me; keep them until we see what to put them in.' Then time took its course until I bought this house. My mother said: 'When you want to pay its price, do not pay until you call me so I may supplicate for blessing for you.' So I called her when I had prepared it. She said to me: 'Take these dirhams and include them in it.' So I included them and mixed them, and she said: 'Go with them.'\""],[4390,"We performed Umrah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in an Umrah he performed. He shaved his hair, and the people raced to his hair. I raced to the forelock and took it. Then I made a cap and put it in the front of my cap; I did not direct it in any direction except that it was opened for him."],[4391,"I asked Umm Sulaym ؓ for some of the perfume which she used to mix with the sweat of the Prophet ﷺ, and she gave me some of it. When Muhammad died, he was embalmed with that perfume."],[4392,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, my nephew has exerted himself in worship and exhausted himself. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"That is the fervor of Islam. Every fervor has a lull, so watch for his lull. If he keeps close [to moderation], then perhaps [he will be fine], but if he perishes, then woe to him.\""],[4393,"On the day of Siffin a man said: O God, curse the people of Syria. Ali ؓ said: \"Do not revile the people of Syria as a whole, for among them are the abdal.\" He said it three times."],[4394,"\"Do not revile the people of Syria as a whole, for among them are the abdal.\" He said it three times. Type: mawquf."],[4395,"\"Do not revile the people of Syria as a whole, for among them are the abdal.\" He said it three times. Type: mawquf."],[4396,"\"Gently, for the sake of God Almighty, gently! Were it not for humble youths, bowing elderly, suckling infants, and grazing beasts, punishment would have been poured upon you abundantly.\""],[4397,"We do not know it except with this chain of transmission."],[4398,"\"Indeed God Almighty preserves a righteous man in his children, his grandchildren, and the small house in which he was born, and the small houses around it, so they remain under protection.\""],[4399,"Ka'b ؓ used to recount stories. Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"No one recounts stories except a ruler, one commanded, or a self-conceited person.\" It was said to Ka'b ؓ: May your mother be bereaved of you! Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ says such-and-such. So he stopped recounting stories. Then Mu'awiya commanded him to recount stories, and he considered it permissible because of that."],[4400,"Ali ؓ passed by a storyteller and said: What is he saying? They said: He is recounting stories. He ؓ said: No, but he is saying: Know me!"],[4401,"The Messenger of God ﷺ delivered a sermon to us, and in it he admonished us with a discourse that made eyes shed tears, hearts tremble, skins shiver, and inner organs quake. He ﷺ commanded Bilal ؓ, who called out: Prayer in congregation! Then he mentioned the hadith in full, in which there is: \"Whoever chooses this world over the Hereafter, his is the Fire. Whoever honors a man of worldly status and praises him out of greed for his worldly goods, God Almighty is displeased with him, and he will be in the rank of Qarun in the lowest part of Hell. Whoever builds a building for show and reputation, on the Day of Resurrection he will be made to carry it from seven earths, with fire blazing around his neck, then thrown into the Fire.\" It was said: How does one build a building for show and reputation? He said: \"He builds beyond what suffices him, and he builds it for display. Whoever learns the Quran but does not act upon it, and prefers the fleeting goods and adornment of this world over it, incurs the displeasure of God Almighty, and he will be in the rank of the Jews and Christians who cast the Book of God Almighty behind their backs and sold it for a small price. Whoever is discontent with his provision and spreads his complaint, no good deed of his will be raised to God Almighty, and he will meet God, Mighty and Majestic, while He is displeased with him. Whoever marries a woman lawfully with lawful wealth, intending thereby pride and showing off, God Almighty will only increase him in humiliation and disgrace, and God Almighty will stand him, in proportion to what he enjoyed from her, on the brink of Hell, then he will fall into it for seventy autumns. Whoever humiliates a poor Muslim because of his poverty and belittles him, he has belittled the right of God Almighty, and he will remain in God Almighty's hatred and displeasure until he appeases him. Whoever honors a poor Muslim will meet God Almighty on the Day of Resurrection while He is smiling at him. Whoever is presented with this world and the Hereafter and chooses this world over the Hereafter will meet God Almighty without any good deed with which to protect himself from the Fire, but if he chooses the Hereafter over this world, he will meet God Almighty while He is pleased with him. Whoever's eyes shed tears out of fear of God, Blessed and Exalted, for every drop of his tears he will have the like of Mount Uhud in his scale, and for every drop that falls from his eye he will have in Paradise, on its edge, cities and palaces such as no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has never occurred to the heart of any describer.\""],[4402,"A man asked Abu Musa ؓ about seeking permission from his parents. He said: \"Yes, seek permission. Would it please you to see something private from them?\""],[4403,"When Salman ؓ fell ill with the illness in which he died, Sa'd ؓ came to visit him while he was governor of Kufa. Salman ؓ began to weep, and he mentioned the hadith, then said: As for you, O man, fear God Almighty in your intention when you intend, in your hand when you distribute, and in your tongue when you judge."],[4404,"The Children of Israel were ruined only when they told stories."],[4405,"Some people disputed about storytelling; some approved of it and others disliked it. They came to Anas b. Malik ؓ, mentioned that to him, and asked him. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was sent with fighting and was not sent with storytelling."],[4406,"Abdullah b. Yazid was invited to a meal. When he came and saw the house furnished with curtains, he sat outside weeping. It was said to him, \"What makes you weep?\" He said ؓ: When the Messenger of God ﷺ used to see off an army and reached the Thaniyyat al-Wada', he ﷺ would say, \"I entrust to God your religion, your trusts, and the final outcomes of your deeds.\" One day he saw a man who had patched his cloak with a piece of fur, so he said: He faced the rising of the sun, and said this with his hand—Hammad described it with his two hands, palms inward, and extended his hands—\"The world has appeared before you—meaning it has approached—until we thought it would fall upon us. One of you goes out in one fine garment and returns in another, and you cover your houses as you cover the Ka'bah.\" Abdullah b. Yazid said, \"Should I not weep when I see you covering your houses as you cover the Ka'bah?\""],[4408,"Nothing has eradicated Islam like miserliness."],[4409,"When the depth of the night comes, an angel appears and says, \"Glorify the King, the Most Holy.\" Then another angel appears and says, \"Glorify the King, the Most Holy.\" At that the birds move their wings. Then another angel appears and says, \"O seeker of good, come forward.\" Then another angel appears and says, \"O seeker of evil, refrain.\" Then another appears and says, \"O God, give a successor to one who spends.\" Then another appears and says, \"O God, give ruin to one who withholds.\""],[4410,"Leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt."],[4411,"\"Whoever loves to meet God, Mighty and Majestic, God Most High loves to meet him; and whoever hates to meet God Most High, God, Mighty and Majestic, hates to meet him.\" The people wept and said, \"O Messenger of God, which of us does not hate death?\" He ﷺ said, \"That is not what I mean. But God, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'Then if he is of those brought near, then rest and fragrance and a garden of bliss.' When that is the case, he loves to meet God Most High, and God, Mighty and Majestic, is more loving of meeting him. But if he is of the deniers, the astray, then a lodging of boiling water. When that is the case, he hates to meet God Most High, and God, Mighty and Majestic, is more hating of meeting him.\""],[4412,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned polytheism and said, \"It is more hidden among you than the crawling of an ant.\" Abu Bakr ؓ said, \"O Messenger of God, is polytheism anything but making another god with God?\" He ﷺ said, \"May your mother be bereaved of you, O Abu Bakr! Polytheism is more hidden among you than the crawling of an ant. I will show you something that, if you do it, will remove from you the minor polytheism and its major, or the small polytheism and its large. Say: O God, I seek refuge in You from associating anything with You knowingly, and I seek Your forgiveness for what I do not know.\""],[4413,"Regarding His saying, Most High: 'Or have they assigned to God partners who created like His creation...'"],[4414,"\"Polytheism is more hidden among you than the crawling of an ant.\" Then he ﷺ said, \"Shall I not show you what removes from you the minor and major of that?\" Say: \"O God, I seek refuge in You from associating anything with You knowingly, and I seek Your forgiveness for what I do not know.\""],[4415,"\"Shall I not show you what removes from you the minor and major of that?\" Say: \"O God, I seek refuge in You from associating anything with You knowingly, and I seek Your forgiveness for what I do not know.\""],[4416,"Whoever perfects his prayer when people see him and performs it badly when alone, that is only contempt by which he belittles his Lord."],[4417,"We were with al-Sāʾib b. Yazīd when al-Zubayr b. Sahl b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf ؓ came to him, and on his face was a mark of prostration. He said: \"Who is this?\" We said: \"Al-Zubayr b. Sahl.\" He said: \"By Allah, this is not the sign that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has named. I have prostrated on my face for eighty years, yet prostration has left no mark between my eyes.\""],[4418,"A speaker among the Muslims said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is salvation tomorrow?\" He ﷺ said: \"Do not deceive Allah, Exalted is He.\" He said: \"And how is Allah, Mighty and Majestic, deceived?\" He ﷺ said: \"That you do what Allah has commanded you, seeking by it other than Him. So beware of showing off, for it is associating partners with Allah, Mighty and Majestic. The one who shows off will be called on the Day of Resurrection before all creation by four names: O sinner, O disbeliever, O loser, O treacherous one. Your deeds have gone astray and your reward is nullified. You have no share today with Allah, Exalted is He. Seek your reward from the one for whom you used to work, O deceiver.\" He (the narrator) said: I said to him: \"By Allah, besides whom there is no god, did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"By Allah, besides whom there is no god, I heard this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, unless it is something I did not intend.\" Yazīd said: \"I think he recited verses from the Qur'an: 'So whoever hopes for the meeting with his Lord, let him work righteous deeds' and 'Indeed, the hypocrites seek to deceive Allah, but He is deceiving them.'\""],[4419,"\"The son of Adam will be brought on the Day of Resurrection as if he were a lamb—or perhaps he said: as if he were a camel—and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: 'O son of Adam, I am the best of dividers. Look at the deeds you did for Me, and I will reward you for them; and look at the deeds you did for other than Me, and they will reward you for what you did for them.'\""],[4420,"'Shall I teach you what Noah taught his son?' They said, 'Yes.' He ﷺ said, 'O my son, I command you with two things and forbid you from two things: I forbid you from associating anything with God, for whoever associates anything with God, God has forbidden Paradise to him; and I forbid you from arrogance, for no one whose heart contains a mustard seed of arrogance will enter Paradise. And I command you to say: There is no god but God alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent, for if the heavens were a ring, it would break them. And I command you to say: Glory be to God and with His praise, for it is the prayer of creation and the glorification of creation, and by it creation is provided sustenance.' A man said, 'O Messenger of God, is it arrogance for a man to have a riding animal he rides, or a garment he wears, or food to which he invites his companions?' He ﷺ said, 'No, but arrogance is to reject the truth and disparage people. I shall inform you of five things; whoever has them is not arrogant: tethering a sheep, wearing wool, riding a donkey, sitting with the poor believers, and a man eating with his family.'"],[4421,"And Abu Bakr said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Musa, with it."],[4422,"\"Indeed, Allah, Exalted is He, did not make any sacred thing forbidden except that He knew someone among you would violate it. Beware, I am holding you by your belts lest you tumble into the Fire as flies tumble.\""],[4423,"\"Holding you by your belts\"—and he added: \"as moths, flies, and beetles tumble.\""],[4424,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me—and the first thing he enjoined upon me was that he said: \"O my dear son, conceal my secret, and you will be a believer.\" So my mother and the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would ask me about the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I would not inform them of it, and I would never inform anyone of the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. \"O my dear son, when you leave your house, let not your eye fall upon anyone from the people of the Qiblah except that you greet him with peace, for you will return forgiven. And O my dear son, when you enter your home, greet yourself and your family. And O my dear son, if you can rise in the morning and reach the evening with no deceit in your heart toward anyone, then do so, for that is lighter for you in the reckoning. And O my dear son, if you follow my advice, then let nothing be dearer to you than death.\""],[4425,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū ʿAlī narrated to us, Yūnus narrated to us, with this. :"],[4426,"Uways ؓ saw a man praying, standing and sitting. He said: \"What is the matter with you?\" He said: \"I stand, and Satan comes and says: 'You are showing off,' so I sit. Then my soul urges me to pray, so I stand, and he says: 'You are showing off,' so I sit.\" He said: \"If you were alone, would you pray this prayer?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then pray, for you are not showing off.\""],[4427,"A man came to Ibn ʿUmar ؓ, and he said to him: \"How are you and al-Ḍaḥḥāk b. Qays ؓ?\" He said: \"We and he, when we meet him, we say to him what he likes, and when we turn away from him, we say something else.\" He said: \"That is what we used to consider hypocrisy while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[4428,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū ʿAlī narrated to us, Yūnus narrated to us, with this. :"],[4429,"I said to ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar ؓ: \"O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, we enter upon the ruler when he passes a judgment we see as unjust, and we say: 'May Allah grant you success,' and we look to the man among us who praises him.\" He ؓ said: \"As for us, the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we do not do that.\""],[4430,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū ʿAlī narrated to us, Yūnus narrated to us, with this. :"],[4432,"“Among my ummah are some who, if one of them were to stand at the door of any of you and ask him for a dinar, he would not give it to him; or for a dirham, he would not give it to him; or for a fils, he would not give it to him. Yet if he were to ask Allah, the Exalted, for the whole world, He would not give it to him. And He only withholds it from him because of His honoring him. But if he were to ask Allah, the Exalted, for Paradise, He would give it to him. And if he were to swear by Allah, He would fulfill his oath.”"],[4433,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū ʿAlī narrated to us, Yūnus narrated to us, with this. :"],[4434,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed along a road, and a black woman passed by. A man said to her, “The road!” But she said, “The road? What is it?” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Leave her, for she is a tyrant.”"],[4435,"“In Hell there is a valley called Habhab. It is incumbent upon Allah, Blessed and Exalted, to make every tyrant dwell in it.”"],[4436,"«Cursing a believer is like killing him, and if he says to him: 'O disbeliever,' it is like killing him.»"],[4437,"\"A man may attain the rank of one who fasts and prays at night through good character, and yet he may be recorded as a tyrant while he only rules over his own household.\""],[4438,"The companions of Ibn Masʿud ؓ were bitten by the cold, and they began to feel ashamed to come in their old worn-out garments and cloaks. He missed them, and it was said to him, “Their situation is such-and-such.” So Abu Abd al-Rahman came in the morning wearing a cloak, and they said, “Ibn Masʿud ؓ has come in a cloak.” Then the second day came, then the third day. When they saw him in the cloak, they came in their cloaks, and he recognized faces he had missed. He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘No one will enter Paradise who has in his heart an atom’s weight of arrogance,’ or he said, ‘a speck of arrogance.’”"],[4439,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said in the hadith to Muʿadh ؓ : “As long as you remain silent, you are safe. When you speak, it is either for you or against you.”"],[4440,"“Silence is wisdom, but few practice it.”"],[4441,"“Whoever wants to be safe, let him keep to silence.”"],[4442,"“O my son, let your house suffice you, weep over your sin, and restrain your tongue.”"],[4443,"“I forbid you three things: gossip and idle talk, wasting wealth, and excessive questioning.”"],[4445,"Indeed a man speaks a word to make those around him laugh, and it has brought about more than ʿUkāẓ, yet he does not perceive it."],[4446,"\"Indeed a man speaks a word to make those around him laugh, and it has brought about more than ʿUkāẓ, yet he does not perceive it.\" Type: Marfūʿ"],[4447,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was addressing the people, saying: \"Whoever guards what is between his jaws and guards what is between his legs, he will be in Paradise.\""],[4448,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Guard what is between your jaws and your legs.\" He said: So I arose, saying: \"It is sufficient for me.\""],[4449,"\"Whoever has two shirts, let him clothe one of them or give one of them as charity.\""],[4450,"A man used to sit with Masrūq, and he was among the last to bid him farewell. He said: \"O Abū ʿĀʾishah, you are the foremost of the Qurʾān reciters and their master, and your adornment is adornment for them, and your disfigurement is disfigurement for them. So do not tell yourself of poverty or of long life.\""],[4451,"If there is excellence in the congregation, then safety is in seclusion."],[4452,"\"Indeed God, Mighty and Majestic, loves every sorrowful heart.\""],[4453,"We do not know it except through this chain of transmission. And al-Ḥākim declared it authentic. :"],[4454,"I would not love that it missed me. Indeed the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed sharpness of temper affects the best of my community.\""],[4455,"\"Indeed sharpness of temper affects the best of my community.\" Type: Marfūʿ"],[4456,"\"Sharpness of temper affects the best of my community.\""],[4457,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, be pleased with me.” He ﷺ turned away from me three times. Then I said: “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, is indeed appeased until He is pleased.” He said: So he ﷺ became pleased with me."],[4458,"We do not know for him anything except this hadith, meaning ʿAmr b. Mālik. :"],[4459,"It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, which of our sitting companions is best?” He ﷺ said: “The one whose sight reminds you of Allah, whose speech increases you in knowledge, and whose deeds remind you of the Hereafter.”"],[4460,"“The one whose sight reminds you of Allah, whose speech increases you in knowledge, and whose deeds remind you of the Hereafter” – marfūʿ."],[4461,"It was said to ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ: “What made you leave the vicinity of the grave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and dwell among the graves, meaning al-Baqīʿ?” He replied: “I found them to be truthful neighbors, expiating sins and reminding of the Hereafter.”"],[4462,"“Whoever wishes to outstrip the diligent striver, let him refrain from sins.”"],[4464,"Praise for a servant is not established on earth until it is established in heaven."],[4465,"“No servant weeps so that his eyes shed tears from fear of Allah, the Exalted, but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will never enter him into the Fire, until the rain of the sky returns.” It is also said that he ﷺ stood on the pulpit when the people returned from Muʾtah, and in his hand was a piece of bread. When he ﷺ mentioned their affair, his eyes overflowed, and he ﷺ wiped his face and said: “Indeed, I am only a human being. I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan. A man may think he is abundant through his brother. Who has a promise with me?” Then Salmān al-Fārisī ؓ said: “I do, O Messenger of Allah,” and he ﷺ gave it to him. He said: And Barakah ؓ said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ attended to his daughter while she was dying, and she was married to ʿUthmān ؓ, his ﷺ eyes overflowed, and Barakah ؓ wept and tore at her hair. He ﷺ rebuked her, and she said: “Do you weep, O Messenger of Allah, while we are silent?” He ﷺ said: “What you saw from me is mercy for her, and indeed I am only a human being. The believer is in every good station from Allah, the Exalted, whether in hardship or ease.”"],[4466,"Jibrīl (peace and blessings be upon him) came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was weeping. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What makes you weep?” He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “By Allah, my eye has not dried since Allah, the Exalted, created the Fire, out of fear that I might disobey Him and He cast me into it.”"],[4467,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us, and he mentioned the hadith in full. He said: Then he ﷺ descended, and a group of the Ansar ؓ hastened to him before he came down from the pulpit and said: “May our lives be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah. Who can bear these hardships, and how can one live after this day?” He ﷺ said to them: “And you, may my father and mother be your ransom. I entreated my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, concerning my community, and He said to me: ‘The gate of repentance is open until the trumpet is blown.’” Then he ﷺ said: “Whoever repents one year before his death, Allah will turn to him.” Then he ﷺ said: “A year is a long time. Whoever repents one month before his death, Allah will turn to him.” Then he ﷺ said: “A month is a long time. Whoever repents one week before his death, Allah will turn to him.” Then he ﷺ said: “A week is a long time. Whoever repents one day before his death, Allah will turn to him.” Then he ﷺ said: “A day is a long time. Whoever repents one hour before his death, Allah will turn to him.” Then he ﷺ said: “Whoever repents before he gargles with death, Allah will turn to him.” Then he ﷺ descended, and it was the last sermon he delivered."],[4468,"“Repent to your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, for I repent to Him seventy times a day or more than seventy.”"],[4470,"I heard Muʿtamir, with it."],[4471,"“A hundred times.”"],[4472,"“Allah, Exalted is He, is more pleased with the repentance of His servant who has transgressed against himself than a man who lost his mount, so he searched for it right and left until he became exhausted or despaired of it, and when he thought he had perished, he looked and found it in a place he had not expected to find it. For Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is more pleased with the repentance of His prodigal servant than that man with his mount when he found it.”"],[4473,"“A man among those before you met a learned man or a worshipper and said: ‘The other has killed ninety-nine people, all of them unjustly. Do you find any repentance for me?’ He said: ‘No,’ so he killed him. Then he met another and said: ‘The other has killed a hundred people, all of them unjustly. Do you find any repentance for me?’ He said: ‘If I told you that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not accept the repentance of one who repents, I would have lied. Here is a monastery in which there are people who worship. Go to them and worship Allah, Mighty and Majestic, along with them. Perhaps Allah, Exalted, will accept your repentance.’ So he set out toward them and died before reaching them. The angels of punishment and the angels of mercy disputed over him, so Allah, Exalted, sent an angel saying: ‘Measure between the two places; whichever he was closer to, he belongs to them.’ They measured and found him closer to the monastery of the penitents by a fingertip, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, forgave him.”"],[4474,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat one day while we were with him and said: “Allah, Exalted, is not overwhelmed by any sin that He forgives. A man before you killed ninety-eight people. He came to a monk and said to him: ‘I have killed ninety-eight people; do you find any repentance for me?’ He said: ‘No,’ so he killed him. Then he came to another monk and told him that he had killed ninety-nine people; do you find any repentance for me? He said: ‘No,’ so he killed him. Then he came to another and told him that he had killed a hundred people; do you find any repentance for me? He said: ‘You have transgressed greatly, and I do not know. But here are two villages: one is called Naḍrah; its people do the deeds of the people of Paradise, and no one else remains among them. The other is called Kafrah; its people do the deeds of the people of the Fire, and no one else remains among them. Go to the people of Naḍrah, and if you do their deeds and repent, do not doubt your repentance.’ So he set out toward it, until when he was between the two villages, his appointed time overtook him. The angels, peace be upon them, asked their Lord about him. He, Majestic and Exalted, said: ‘Look at which of the two villages he was closer to, and record him among its people.’ They found him closer to Naḍrah by a fingertip, so they recorded him among its people.”"],[4475,"“Paradise has eight gates: seven are closed, and one gate is open for repentance until the sun rises from its direction.”"],[4476,"\"Test a person and you will hate him.\""],[4477,"ʿAli ؓ mounted me behind him, then he rode with me into a cemetery, then he raised his head to the sky and said: “O Allah, forgive me my sins; none forgives sins except You.” Then he turned to me ؓ and smiled. I said: “O Commander of the Faithful, you seek forgiveness from your Lord and then turn to me smiling?” He said ؓ: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted me behind him, then he rode with me to the side of the Ḥarrah, then he raised his head to the sky and said: ‘O Allah, forgive me my sins; none forgives sins except You.’ Then he turned to me ﷺ and smiled. I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, you seek forgiveness from your Lord and then turn to me smiling?’ He ﷺ said: ‘I smiled because my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, smiled in amazement at His servant, knowing that none forgives sins except Him.’”"],[4478,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came while we were sitting and said: “There is no morning I have ever reached except that I sought forgiveness from Allah, Exalted, a hundred times in it.”"],[4479,"“Adhere to ‘there is no god but Allah’ and seeking forgiveness, and do them abundantly. For Iblis said: ‘I destroyed people with sins, but they destroyed me with “there is no god but Allah” and seeking forgiveness. When I saw that, I destroyed them with caprices, while they think they are rightly guided.’”"],[4480,"“No people sit in a gathering and engage in conversation, then seek forgiveness from Allah, Blessed and Exalted, before they disperse, except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, forgives them for what they engaged in.”"],[4481,"The Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon to us, and he mentioned the hadith, in which he said: “The scholar is only one who acts upon his knowledge, even if his knowledge is little. Do not belittle any act of disobedience, even if it seems small in your eyes, for there is no small sin with persistence, and no large sin with seeking forgiveness. Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will ask you about your deeds, even about one of you touching the garment of his brother. Know that a servant will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection upon what he died upon. Allah, Exalted, has created Paradise and the Fire, so whoever chooses the Fire over Paradise, may Allah, Exalted, distance him. Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has not left anything He prohibited except that He has made it clear to you, so that he who lives may live upon clear proof, and he who perishes may perish upon clear proof.”"],[4482,"«Indeed for every believer there is a sin that he has become accustomed to, time after time, or a sin that he will not abandon until he dies or the Hour rises upon him. The believer was created as one who sins, is tested, errs, and forgets; but if he is reminded, he remembers.»"],[4483,"«By Him besides whom there is no god, I have not seen anyone who was more fearful for the extremists than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ there was none who was more fearful than Abu Bakr ؓ. And indeed I see that Umar ؓ was more fearful for them or of them.»"],[4484,"When a man takes another as a brother, he should ask him his name, his father's name, and who he is, for that is more conducive to affection."],[4485,"A man passed by Ibn 'Abbas ؓ, and he said: This man loves me. They said: How do you know, O Ibn 'Abbas? He said ؓ: Because I love him."],[4486,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were reciting to one another, and he ﷺ said: «Praise be to Allah, the Book of Allah is one. Among you are the red and the black. Recite three times before there come a people who straighten its letters as an arrow is straightened, who hasten with it and do not delay it.»"],[4487,"«Indeed this Quran has a period of keenness, then people have a period of slackness from it. If one's slackness is toward moderation, then how good it is, but if one's slackness is toward turning away, then those are the losers.»"],[4488,"A man passed by Ibn 'Abbas ؓ, and he said: This man loves me. They said: How do you know, O Ibn 'Abbas? He said ؓ: Because I love him."],[4489,"Indeed al-Abbas ؓ built a room, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: «Demolish it.» He said: Or should I give its price in charity? He ﷺ said: «Demolish it» three times."],[4490,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a part of the houses of the Ansar ؓ, and he raised his head and saw a dome that had been built. He ﷺ said: «O Anas, whose dome is this?» I said: It belongs to so-and-so. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Every building is a burden on its owner on the Day of Resurrection, except a building that is just sufficient.» That reached the Ansari man ؓ, and he broke it down. Then the Prophet ﷺ passed by after that and did not see it, so he ﷺ said: «O Anas, what happened to the dome?» I said: Its owner heard your words and broke it down. He ﷺ said: «May Allah forgive him.»"],[4491,"«Whoever dwells in the desert for more than two months, it is Bedouinism.»"],[4492,"Bedouinism is two months; anything beyond that is becoming an Arab."],[4493,"«Whoever dwells in the desert becomes harsh.»"],[4494,"«Whoever lives in the desert becomes coarse»"],[4495,"Abd Allah b. Sa'd used to go out to his companions in Tustar to visit them. He would stay on the day of his arrival and the next, and leave on the third. They would say to him: \"If only you would stay.\" He would say: \"I heard my father say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me—or I heard him forbidding—residing permanently (in a place).\""],[4496,"And al-Hasan b. Sufyan said in his Musnad: Wasil b. Abd Allah b. Badr narrated to us; my father Abd Allah b. Badr narrated to me with it."],[4498,"He used to sit with him in Kufa. While he was one day on a bench of his, with beneath him such-and-such a woman and such-and-such a woman, two wives of rank and beauty, and he had from them a child like the most beautiful of children, a sparrow chirped above his head, then emptied its belly and he flicked it away with his hand, then said: \"By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Abd Allah, for the family of Abd Allah to die and then I follow them is dearer to me than for this sparrow to die.\""],[4500,"«And there is no gulp more beloved to Allah than a gulp of anger that a servant suppresses for the sake of Allah. No servant suppresses it for the sake of Allah except that Allah fills his interior with faith»"],[4501,"Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ was in a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. A man passed by them and asked them, so they answered him. Then he came to Mu'adh ؓ while he had placed his head on his saddle talking to himself. He said: \"What did you ask them about?\" He said: \"I asked them about such-and-such, so they said such-and-such; and I asked them about such-and-such, so they said such-and-such.\" Mu'adh ؓ said: \"Two phrases: if you adopt them, you will have adopted the best of what they said, and if you abandon them, you will have abandoned the best of what they said. If you begin with your share of this world, your share of the Hereafter will elude you, and perhaps you will not attain between them what you want. But if you begin with your share of the Hereafter, it will pass by your share of this world and arrange it for you in an orderly manner, then it will revolve with you wherever you turn.\""],[4502,"«Deliberation in everything is good, except in the work of the Hereafter»"],[4503,"«When Allah the Exalted loves a servant, He protects him from the world, just as one of you keeps protecting his sick one from water»"],[4505,"And Abu Ya'la said: Kamil b. Talhah narrated to us, from him. Al-Tirmidhi also narrated it from the hadith of Ismail b. Ja'far, from Umarah, and he made the Companion Qatadah b. al-Nu'man ؓ. Some of them sent it mursal from Ismail, and did not mention anyone above Mahmud. Likewise Bishr b. al-Mufaddal narrated it from Umarah b. Ghaziyyah ؓ."],[4506,"And Abu Ya'la said: Kamil b. Talhah narrated to us, from him. Al-Tirmidhi also narrated it from the hadith of Ismail b. Ja'far, from Umarah, and he made the Companion Qatadah b. al-Nu'man ؓ. Some of them sent it mursal from Ismail, and did not mention anyone above Mahmud. Likewise Bishr b. al-Mufaddal narrated it from Umarah b. Ghaziyyah ؓ."],[4507,"The poor among the Muslims complained about the superiority the rich had over them. They said: O Messenger of God, these are our brothers: they believed as we believed, prayed as we prayed, fasted as we fasted, but they have an advantage over us in wealth: they give charity and maintain family ties, while we are poor and cannot do that. He ﷺ said: Shall I not tell you something that, if you do it, you will catch up with their virtue? Say after every prayer: 'God is greatest' eleven times, 'Praise be to God' eleven times, 'Glory be to God' eleven times, and 'There is no god but God alone, no partner with Him' eleven times: you will attain the like of their virtue. The rich heard of that and said the same as the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded them. They came to him and said: O Messenger of God, our brothers say the same as we say. He ﷺ said: That is the grace of God, which He gives to whom He wills. Shall I give you glad tidings, O company of the poor? The poor believers will enter Paradise before their rich ones by half a day, which is five hundred years."],[4508,"And Musa recited: \"And indeed, a day with your Lord is like a thousand years of those which you count.\" (Quran 22:47)"],[4509,"The world is green and sweet, so whoever fears Allah in it and acts righteously therein (will be safe); otherwise he is like one who eats but is never satisfied. The distance between people is like the distance between two stars: one rises in the east and the other sets in the west."],[4510,"Free yourselves, as much as you can, from the concerns of this world. For whoever makes the world his greatest concern, Allah, the Exalted, will scatter his affairs and place poverty before his eyes. And whoever makes the Hereafter his greatest concern, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will gather his affairs together, place contentment in his heart, and whenever a servant turns his heart to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, the hearts of the believers will be drawn to him with love and mercy, and Allah, the Exalted, will hasten to him every good."],[4511,"Whoever's intention is seeking the Hereafter, Allah, the Exalted, will gather his affairs, and the world will come to him submissively. And whoever's intention is seeking the world, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will place poverty before his eyes, scatter his affairs, and nothing of the world will come to him except what has been decreed for him."],[4512,"The best provision is what suffices, and the best remembrance is what is hidden."],[4513,"Two hungry wolves, one at the head of the flock and the other at its rear, do not cause as much corruption in sheep as a man's love for worldly honor and wealth causes in his religion."],[4514,"Whoever seeks the world through unlawful means, accumulating and boasting, showing off, will meet Allah, Blessed and Exalted, while He is angry with him. And whoever seeks the world through lawful means, to refrain from begging, to provide for his family, and to be kind to his neighbor, will meet Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, with his face like the full moon."],[4515,"Abu Ya'la said: Ishaq, meaning Ibn Abi Isra'il, narrated to us, Fudayl b. 'Iyad narrated to us, Hajjaj b. Furafisa narrated to us, something similar. This is disconnected between Makhul and Abu Hurayrah ؓ."],[4516,"\"There is no god but Allah\" protects from the wrath of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, as long as they do not prefer their worldly life over their religion. But if they do that and then say, \"There is no god but Allah,\" Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will say: \"You lie.\""],[4517,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what of the world is enough for me?\" He ﷺ said, \"What satisfies your hunger and covers your nakedness. And if you have a house to shelter you or a mount to ride, then excellent! Excellent!\""],[4518,"When the Prophet ﷺ was sent, Iblis's troops came to him and said, \"A prophet has been sent, and a nation has been brought forth.\" He said, \"Do they love the world?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"If they love it, I do not care if they do not worship idols. They will not escape me, for I will come to them morning and evening with three things: taking wealth without right, spending it without right, and withholding it from its right. And all evil follows from this.\""],[4519,"Uthman ؓ forbade hoarding, but a man kept interceding until he left his client [continue hoarding]. Then al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam ؓ entered the market and found the clients of Banu Umayyah hoarding. He began striking them. While he was doing so, Uthman ؓ approached on a mule or a mount. Al-Zubayr walked to him, took hold of the mule's bridle, and shook it violently. I think he said to him: \"You and you...\" But it was harsh speech. Then he left him. When Uthman dismounted, a cushion was placed for him and he sat on it. Al-Zubayr ؓ came and greeted him, saying, \"By Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, I know you have a right over me, but I am a man who, when I see something wrong, cannot be patient.\" Uthman ؓ said to him, \"Sit,\" and he seated him on the cushion beside him."],[4520,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me one day, and I knew that something was troubling him. He did not speak to anyone, performed ablution, and went out. I heard from the rooms, and I heard him saying: \"Allah says: O people, enjoin good and forbid evil before you call upon Him and He does not answer you, before you ask Him and He does not give you, and before you seek His help and He does not help you.\""],[4521,"Indeed, 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ objected to Ubayy b. Ka'b ؓ concerning the reading of a verse. Ubayy ؓ said: 'I heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ while you, O 'Umar, were distracted by the trading in al-Baqi'.' 'Umar ؓ said: 'You have spoken the truth. I only wanted to test whether there is among you anyone who speaks the truth. There is no good in a ruler before whom the truth is not spoken, nor does he speak it.'"],[4522,"Mu'awiya mentioned fleeing from the plague in a sermon, and 'Ubada b. al-Samit ؓ said: 'You have lied! Your mother Hind knows better than you.' Then he prayed, and then he sent for 'Ubada ؓ, and the Ansar gathered around him, so he detained them. 'Ubada ؓ entered, and Mu'awiya said to him: 'Do you not fear God, Exalted is He, and feel ashamed before your leader? You called me a liar on the pulpit?' 'Ubada ؓ said: 'Do you not know that I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the Night of al-'Aqaba, that I would not fear the blame of any blamer for the sake of God? So how about when I have called it a lie against God, Exalted is He?' Then Mu'awiya came out at the time of 'Asr prayer and prayed. Then he took hold of the leg of the pulpit and said: 'O people, I mentioned a hadith to you on the pulpit, and 'Ubada ؓ called me a liar. I entered the house and asked, and found that the hadith is as 'Ubada had narrated to me. So take from him, for he is more knowledgeable than I.'"],[4523,"There will be certain defects and defects. It is sufficient for a man, when he sees something he is unable to change, to know in his heart that he disapproves of it."],[4524,"Abu Mas'ud ؓ entered upon Hudhayfa ؓ while he was ill, and leaned him against himself. Abu Mas'ud ؓ said to him: 'Counsel us.' He said: 'Indeed, misguidance—true misguidance—is that you acknowledge what you used to deny, and deny what you used to acknowledge. Beware of shifting from one position to another in the religion of God, Exalted is He.'"],[4525,"You shall enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong, or God, Mighty and Majestic, will set over you the worst among you, then the best among you will supplicate but they will not be answered."],[4526,"Religion is sincere advice. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He ﷺ said: To Allah's Book, His Prophet, and the leaders of the Muslims."],[4527,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us with this. This is a hasan chain, and the name of the father of Munyah is 'Ubayd b. Abi Barzah. Al-Abbas al-Asfati attributed her genealogy on the authority of Ibn Yunus:"],[4528,"Gabriel ﷺ commanded me to give sincere counsel."],[4529,"Four characteristics, one of them is Mine, one is yours, one is between Me and you, and one is between you and My servants. As for the one that is Mine: that you worship Me and do not associate anything with Me. As for the one that is yours: whatever good you do, I will repay you for it. As for the one between Me and you: from you is supplication and upon Me is the answer. As for the one between you and My servants: be pleased for them what you would be pleased for yourself."],[4530,"When Ja'far ؓ arrived from Abyssinia to the Prophet ﷺ, the Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'What is the most amazing thing you saw?' He ؓ said: 'I saw a woman carrying a basket of food on her head. A horseman rushed past and knocked it down. She sat gathering her food, then turned to him and said: Woe to you on the day when the King sets up His throne and takes for the oppressed from the oppressor.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, affirming her words: 'Sanctified is not—or how can be sanctified—a community whose weak cannot take his right from its strong without fear.'"],[4532,"'What is the most amazing thing you saw?' He ؓ said: 'I saw a woman carrying a basket of food on her head. A horseman rushed past and knocked it down. She sat gathering her food, then turned to him and said: Woe to you on the day when the King sets up His throne and takes for the oppressed from the oppressor.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, affirming her words: 'Sanctified is not—or how can be sanctified—a community whose weak cannot take his right from its strong without fear.'\" type=\"marfu'\""],[4533,"'What is the most amazing thing you saw?' He ؓ said: 'I saw a woman carrying a basket of food on her head. A horseman rushed past and knocked it down. She sat gathering her food, then turned to him and said: Woe to you on the day when the King sets up His throne and takes for the oppressed from the oppressor.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, affirming her words: 'Sanctified is not—or how can be sanctified—a community whose weak cannot take his right from its strong without fear.'\" type=\"marfu'\""],[4534,"“May a nation not be sanctified that does not give the weak among them their right without hesitation.”"],[4535,"“Indeed, Allah, the Exalted, does not punish the common people for the deeds of the elite, but when sins become manifest and are not condemned, both the common people and the elite are seized.”"],[4536,"“Indeed I command you to do what I do not do, but I hope to be rewarded for it.”"],[4537,"“It is not appropriate for a person who witnesses a rightful situation except to speak about it, for it will not hasten his appointed time nor deprive him of a provision that is his.”"],[4538,"The support of a person is his intellect, and there is no religion for one who has no intellect."],[4539,"“The best of people are the most intelligent of people.” Ibn Abbas ؓ said: “And that is your Prophet ﷺ.”"],[4540,"A Christian man from the people of Jurash, a merchant, arrived; he had eloquence and dignity. It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, how intelligent this Christian is!” He rebuked the speaker and said: “Stop! The intelligent one is the one who acts in obedience to Allah, Blessed and Exalted.”"],[4541,"“O son of Adam, fear your Lord, honor your parents, and maintain family ties; your lifespan will be increased, your ease will be facilitated, your hardship will be lightened, and your provision will be expanded. O son of Adam, obey your Lord and you will be called intelligent, and do not disobey your Lord lest you be called ignorant.”"],[4542,"“The death of a thousand devoted worshippers who pray at night and fast during the day is lighter than the death of one intelligent person who has understood from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, His command, and knows what Allah has made lawful for him and what He has forbidden, and benefits from his knowledge and people benefit from him; even if he does not add much beyond the obligatory duties that Allah, the Exalted, has prescribed upon him.”"],[4543,"“Indeed, Allah, the Exalted, has special servants whom He will lodge in the highest gardens; they were the most intelligent of people.” He said: “They are those whose concern is to race to their Lord and hasten to what pleases Him. They renounce the world, its excesses, and its leadership, and it becomes insignificant to them. So they endure a little and rest for a long time.”"],[4544,"Indeed, the ignorant one reveals nothing but a fault, even if he is considered judicious and charming by people. And indeed, the intelligent one reveals nothing but excellence, even if he is considered defective and contemptible by people."],[4545,"We came upon a man from the desert dwellers, and the bedouin said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took my hand and began teaching me from what Allah the Exalted had taught him. Among what I memorized was that he said: \"Do not abandon anything out of fear of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, but that Allah the Exalted will replace it for you with something better.\""],[4546,"And Abu Ya`la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us with this. :. 2815 - And he said:. 2815 - [3] :, :"],[4547,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4548,"\"Whoever intends a good deed and performs it, ten good deeds are written for him. If he does not perform it, one good deed is written for him. And if he intends an evil deed and performs it, one evil deed is written against him. If he does not perform it, nothing is written against him.\""],[4549,"\"If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much, and you would go out crying out in supplication, not knowing whether you will be saved or not.\""],[4550,"We do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'bah except Muslim b. Ibrahim. And the daughter of Abu al-Darda', we do not know her. : :"],[4551,"“No servant weeps so that his eyes shed tears from fear of Allah, the Exalted, but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will never enter him into the Fire, until the rain of the sky returns.” It is also said that he ﷺ stood on the pulpit when the people returned from Muʾtah, and in his hand was a piece of bread. When he ﷺ mentioned their affair, his eyes overflowed, and he ﷺ wiped his face and said: “Indeed, I am only a human being. I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan. A man may think he is abundant through his brother. Who has a promise with me?” Then Salmān al-Fārisī ؓ said: “I do, O Messenger of Allah,” and he ﷺ gave it to him. He said: And Barakah ؓ said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ attended to his daughter while she was dying, and she was married to ʿUthmān ؓ, his ﷺ eyes overflowed, and Barakah ؓ wept and tore at her hair. He ﷺ rebuked her, and she said: “Do you weep, O Messenger of Allah, while we are silent?” He ﷺ said: “What you saw from me is mercy for her, and indeed I am only a human being. The believer is in every good station from Allah, the Exalted, whether in hardship or ease.”"],[4552,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4553,"\"When a servant's skin shivers out of fear of Allah the Exalted, his sins fall away from him as leaves fall from a dry tree.\""],[4554,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4555,"When the emigrants by sea returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Will you not tell us of the wonders you saw in the land of Abyssinia?\" Some young men among them said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah. While we were sitting, an old woman from their monks passed by carrying a water jar on her head. She passed by a young man from among them, and he placed one of his hands between her shoulders, so she fell on her knees and her jar broke. When she rose, she turned to him and said: 'You will know, O treacherous one, when Allah the Exalted sets up the Footstool and gathers the first and the last, and the hands and feet speak of what they used to earn—you will know how my affair and your affair will be before Him tomorrow.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"She spoke the truth, she spoke the truth. How can Allah sanctify a people from whose strong the weak do not receive justice?\""],[4556,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4557,"\"Will you not tell us of the wonders you saw in the land of Abyssinia?\" A group of their young men said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God. While we were sitting, an old woman from their monks passed by carrying a water-skin on her head. She passed by a young man from among them, and he placed one of his hands between her shoulders, so she fell onto her knees and her water-skin broke. When she rose, she turned to him and said, 'You will come to know, O treacherous one, when God Almighty sets up the Throne and gathers the first and the last, and the hands and feet speak of what they used to earn. You will come to know how my case and your case will be before Him tomorrow.'\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"She spoke the truth, she spoke the truth. How can God sanctify a people from whose strong the weak are not given recompense?\""],[4558,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4559,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4560,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was in my house and had a tooth-stick in his hand. He called for a young servant of his or hers until anger became apparent on the face of the Prophet ﷺ. Umm Salamah ؓ went out to the neighbors and found the servant girl playing among them. She said, \"Do I not see you playing with this lamb while his Messenger ﷺ is calling you?\" She said, \"No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I did not hear you.\""],[4561,"\"It was mentioned to me that supplication remains between heaven and earth, none of it ascending until blessings are invoked upon the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[4562,"Abu Dharr ؓ sat with the Messenger of God ﷺ, or the Messenger of God ﷺ sat with him, and he said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you prayed the forenoon prayer?\" Then he mentioned the hadith, in which he said, \"The most misguided of people is the one in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not invoke blessings upon me ﷺ.\""],[4563,"\"O Abu Dharr, have you prayed the forenoon prayer?\" He ﷺ said, \"Arise and pray.\" So I arose and prayed as long as God Almighty willed, then I returned and sat. He ﷺ remained for a long time without speaking to me, so I said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ has disliked my sitting with him.\" Then he ﷺ turned to me and said, \"O Abu Dharr.\" I said, \"At your service, and good fortune.\" He ﷺ said, \"Seek refuge in God from the evil of the devils of mankind and jinn.\" I said, \"May my father and mother be your ransom, do mankind have devils?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Does not God, Mighty and Majestic, say: 'Devils of mankind and jinn, inspiring one another' [the verse]?\" Then he ﷺ turned to me and said, \"O Abu Dharr.\" I said, \"At your service, O Messenger of God.\" He ﷺ said, \"Shall I not teach you a word that is a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?\" I said, \"Yes, may my father and mother be your ransom.\" He ﷺ said, \"Say: There is no might and no power except with God.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ persisted in not speaking until that lasted a long time. Then I resumed the conversation and said, \"O Messenger of God, you commanded me to pray. What is prayer?\" He ﷺ said, \"A good thing placed [before you]; whoever wishes may take little, and whoever wishes may take much.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, what is fasting?\" He ﷺ said, \"An obligatory duty that suffices.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, what is charity?\" He ﷺ said, \"Multiplied many times over, and with God is more.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, which deed is best?\" He ﷺ said, \"Faith in God, Mighty and Majestic, and striving in the path of God Almighty.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, which martyrs are best?\" He ﷺ said, \"The one whose blood is shed and whose horse is hamstrung.\" He said, \"I said, 'O Messenger of God, which slaves are best [to free]?' He ﷺ said, 'The most expensive in price and the most precious to their owners.'\" He said, \"I said, 'O Messenger of God, which charity is best?' He ﷺ said, 'The effort of one with little, given secretly to a poor person.' I said, 'O Messenger of God, what if I do not find anything to give in charity?' He ﷺ said, 'You help a weak person or do something for an unskilled person.' I said, 'O Messenger of God, what if I am not able?' He ﷺ said, 'Then withhold this'—and he ﷺ pointed to his tongue—for it is a good charity that a person gives on behalf of himself. I said, 'O Messenger of God, which verse of the Qur'an revealed to you is greatest?' He ﷺ said, 'The Verse of the Throne. And do you know what the heavens and the earth are like in relation to the Throne?' I said, 'No, unless you teach me from what God Almighty taught you.' He ﷺ said, 'The likeness of the heavens and the earth in the Throne is only like a ring thrown in a vast desert. And the excellence of the Throne over the heavens and the earth is like the excellence of the desert over that ring.' I said, 'O Messenger of God, how many were the prophets, peace be upon them?' He ﷺ said, 'They were one hundred and twenty-four thousand.' I said, 'O Messenger of God, were all of them messengers?' He ﷺ said, 'No, the messengers among them were three hundred and fifteen men.' I said, 'O Messenger of God, which of them was the first?' He ﷺ said, 'Adam, ﷺ .' I said, 'Was Adam a prophet?' He ﷺ said, 'Yes. God formed his clay and created him with His hand, breathed into him from His spirit, and spoke to him directly.' Then the people became numerous around the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Shall I not inform you of the most miserly of people?' I said, 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He ﷺ said, 'The one in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not invoke blessings upon me ﷺ.'\""],[4564,"\"There is no servant who invokes blessings upon me sincerely from his own self, except that God Almighty records for him ten blessings, records for him ten good deeds, erases from him ten evil deeds, and raises him by ten degrees.\""],[4566,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to us, \"Do not make me like the traveler's cup. When the traveler hangs up his provisions, he takes his cup and fills it with water. If he needs to perform ablution, he performs ablution; if he needs to drink, he drinks; otherwise, he pours out what is in it. Place me at the beginning of the supplication, in the middle of the supplication, and at the end of the supplication.\""],[4567,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4568,"\"God, Blessed and Exalted, has given me an angel from among the angels who stands at my grave when I die. No servant invokes blessings upon me without him saying, 'O Muhammad, so-and-so son of so-and-so is invoking blessings upon you,' naming him by his name and his father's name. Then God, Mighty and Majestic, blesses him in return ten times.\""],[4569,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4570,"The Prophet ﷺ ascended one step of the pulpit and said: “Amin.” Then he ascended another step and said: “Amin.” Then he ascended the third and said: “Amin.” Then he settled ﷺ and sat. His Companions ؓ said: “O Prophet of Allah, for what have you said Amin?” He ﷺ said: “Jibril ﷺ came to me and said: ‘May his nose be rubbed in dust, a man who reaches his parents or one of them in old age and does not enter Paradise.’ He said: ‘I said: Amin.’ ‘And may his nose be rubbed in dust, a person who reaches Ramadan and is not forgiven.’ He said: ‘I said: Amin.’ ‘And may his nose be rubbed in dust, one in whose presence you are mentioned and he does not invoke blessings upon you.’ He said: ‘I said: Amin.’”"],[4571,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4572,"“Increase invoking blessings upon me on Friday, for they are presented to me.”"],[4573,"We said: “O Messenger of Allah, we have learned how to greet you with peace, but how do we invoke blessings upon you?” He ﷺ said: “Say: ‘O Allah, place Your prayers and Your mercy upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You placed them upon the family of Ibrahim. Indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.’”"],[4574,"I said to Ibn Umar ؓ: “How is the invocation of blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ?” Ibn Umar ؓ said: “O Allah, place Your prayers, Your blessings, and Your mercy upon the master of the messengers, the imam of the God-conscious, the seal of the prophets Muhammad, Your servant and messenger, the imam of good and the leader of good. O Allah, raise him on the Day of Resurrection to a praiseworthy station that the first and the last will envy. And bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.”"],[4575,"“There is no one from the nation of Muhammad who invokes blessings upon Muhammad or greets him except that it reaches him: ‘So-and-so invokes blessings upon you and so-and-so greets you.’”"],[4576,"“Invoke blessings upon the prophets of Allah and His messengers, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent them as He sent me. May Allah’s prayers and peace be upon them all.”"],[4577,"“Invoke blessings upon the prophets of Allah and His messengers, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent them as He sent me. May Allah’s prayers and peace be upon them all.”"],[4578,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4579,"“Heedlessness is in three: heedlessness of the remembrance of Allah, Mighty and Majestic; from the time the dawn prayer is held until the sun rises; and a person’s heedlessness of himself until debt mounts upon him.”"],[4580,"Uqba b. Amir ؓ came to Mu'awiya while he was in Jerusalem. He did not stay long before he left. He was sought but not found. He said: 'So we came to him, and there he was praying in an open area of land. He said: What brought you? We said: We came to renew our covenant with you, or to fulfill something of your right. He said ؓ: I have your reward for it. We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he mentioned a hadith. He said: Then Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ said: O Ibn Amir, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah, his heart confirming his tongue, will enter through whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes.'"],[4581,"Zubayd recited the Qur’an for twenty years, completing it in a day and a night, and for twenty years completing it in two days and two nights. He said: “By Allah, it was as if there was light on his face.” The Prophet ﷺ, when he sensed negligence or heedlessness among his Companions, would call out to them in his loudest voice: “Death has come to you successively, either misery or happiness.” Umar b. Hafs said: “And this old man said to us: ‘I am better this year than last year. Last year I had a sheep, and this year I have no sheep.’” And a man said to him: “I want to marry a woman, so supplicate to Allah, Exalted is He, for me to marry me to a righteous woman.” He said: “So he supplicated to Allah, Exalted is He, and a righteous woman was prepared for him.”"],[4582,"All deeds of righteousness are half of worship, and supplication is half. When Allah, Exalted is He, wills good for a servant, He turns his heart to supplication."],[4583,"And 'Abd said: al-Hasan b. Musa narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us with it."],[4584,"Shall I not guide you to what will save you from your enemy and increase your provisions? Supplicate to Allah, Exalted is He, in your night and your day, for supplication is the believer's weapon."],[4586,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ one day when he said: \"The likeness of the believer is that of a tree whose leaves do not fall. Do you know what it is?\" They said: \"No.\" He said: \"It is the date palm: its leaves do not fall, and the supplication of the believer does not fall.\""],[4587,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us. :"],[4588,"When you supplicate, let the young among you, the old, the blind, and the eloquent all supplicate, for you do not know which of you will be answered."],[4589,"Perhaps Allah, Mighty and Majestic, delays the supplication for a servant and gives it to him on the Day of Resurrection, not wanting that he be afflicted with some worldly gain."],[4590,"She was praying, and the Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"You should use comprehensive and all-encompassing supplications.\" When she finished, she asked him ﷺ about that, and he ﷺ said: \"Say: 'O Allah, I ask You for all good, what I know of it and what I do not know, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, what I know of it and what I do not know, and I seek refuge in You from the Fire and from any word or deed that brings one near to it. O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and for any word or deed that brings one near to it. O Allah, I ask You for the good that Your servant and Messenger Muhammad asked You for.'\""],[4591,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us. :"],[4592,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us. :"],[4593,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: \"Shall I not teach you from what Jibril ﷺ taught me?\" I said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He ﷺ said: \"Say: 'O Allah, forgive me my sins, my deliberate acts, my jesting, and my seriousness, and do not deprive me of the blessing of what You have given me, and do not test me by what You have withheld from me.'\""],[4594,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say frequently: \"O God, I ask You for health, chastity, trustworthiness, good character, and contentment with the decree.\""],[4595,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us. :"],[4596,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us. :"],[4597,"A man said: \"O God, forgive me and Muhammad alone.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"You have indeed restricted it from many people.\""],[4598,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us. :"],[4599,"When hardship befell him and he supplicated, he would raise his hands until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen ﷺ."],[4600,"The Prophet ﷺ raised his hands in supplication until the whiteness of his armpits was seen ﷺ."],[4601,"\"When you ask God (Mighty and Majestic), ask Him with the palms of your hands, and do not ask Him with their backs.\""],[4602,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ exerted himself in supplication for someone, he ﷺ would say: \"May God make upon you the prayer of a righteous people, who are not sinful nor wicked, who stand in prayer at night and fast during the day.\""],[4603,"One of them, when he would exert himself in supplication for his brother..."],[4604,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by him while he was supplicating with his palms spread out, and he said: \"Make it one, for He is One.\""],[4605,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us. :"],[4606,"Let one of you say 'Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi rajirun' (Indeed we belong to Allah and indeed to Him we return) for everything, even for a shoelace, for it is among the calamities."],[4607,"When the shoelace of one of you breaks, let him say 'Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi rajirun' (Indeed we belong to Allah and indeed to Him we return), for it is among the calamities. And ask Allah, Mighty and Majestic, even for a shoelace, for if He does not make it easy, it will not be easy."],[4609,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us. :"],[4610,"I was with 'Ammar ؓ when a man came to him and said: Shall I not teach you some words? It was as if he was raising them to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: \"When you take your place of lying down at night, say: 'O Allah, I have submitted myself to You, and turned my face to You, and entrusted my affair to You, and leaned my back upon You, I believe in Your Book which You sent down and Your Prophet whom You sent. O Allah, my soul You have created; to You belongs its life and to You belongs its death. If You take it, have mercy on it, and if You delay it, guard it with the guarding of faith.'\""],[4611,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ complaining to him of need. He ﷺ said: \"Shall I not direct you to something better than that? You should declare the oneness of Allah, Exalted is He, thirty-three times when you go to bed, and glorify Him thirty-three times, and praise Him thirty-four times. That is one hundred, better for you than the world and all that is in it.\""],[4612,"Whoever sleeps in a state of purity and then wakes up during the night, he will not ask Allah, Exalted is He, for anything of the affairs of the Hereafter or this world except that He will give it to him."],[4614,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us. :"],[4615,"Whoever says when he wakes up, as Allah, Exalted is He, has returned his soul to him: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise; in His hand is all good, and He is over all things capable,' his sins will be forgiven, even if they are like the foam of the sea."],[4617,"Khalid b. al-Walid ؓ was suffering from sleeplessness, or insomnia afflicted him, and he complained of that to the Prophet ﷺ. He commanded him to seek refuge at the time of sleeping with Allah's perfect words from His wrath and punishment, from the evil of His servants, and from the whisperings of the devils and that they should come near."],[4618,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us. :"],[4619,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left my house, he would raise his head to the sky and say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from slipping, or going astray, or doing wrong, or being wronged, or acting ignorantly, or being treated ignorantly.'"],[4620,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us. :"],[4622,"A safeguard for my community from drowning when they embark on the sea is to say: “In the name of God, its course and its berth. Indeed, my Lord is Forgiving, Merciful. And they did not appraise God with true appraisal…” [Qur'an 11:41, 6:91]"],[4624,"Caution does not avail against destiny, but supplication does repel [it]."],[4626,"There is no harm in saying “Amen” to the supplication of a monk when he supplicates for you. He said: “They are answered concerning us, but not answered concerning themselves.”"],[4627,"“Shall I not inform you of a matter that is true—whoever utters it at the beginning of his lying down during his illness, God Almighty will save him from the Fire?” He said: “Yes, by my father and mother.” He ﷺ said: “Know that if you reach the morning, you will not reach the evening, and if you reach the evening, you will not reach the morning. If you say this at the beginning of your lying down during your illness, God Almighty will save you by it from the Fire: ‘There is no god but God. He gives life and causes death, and He is Ever-Living and does not die. Glory be to the Lord of servants and lands. Praise be to God, abundant, good, and blessed praise, in every state. God is greatest—the pride of our Lord, His majesty, and His power in every place. O God, if You have made me ill in order to take my soul in this illness of mine, place my soul among the souls of those for whom the best has preceded from You. If you die in that illness, then [you go] to the good pleasure of God Almighty and Paradise, and if you have committed sins, God, Mighty and Majestic, will relent toward you.’”"],[4628,"“What has been said—and no one before has said a word better than ‘There is no god but God’—nor have those who ask asked their Lord for anything better than forgiveness.”"],[4630,"“Do not supplicate against your children, lest that coincide with a response from God, Mighty and Majestic.”"],[4631,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us. :"],[4632,"“When one of you intends a journey, let him greet his brothers, for they increase him by their supplications to his supplication in good.”"],[4633,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ ascended an elevated piece of land, he would say: “O God, Yours is the height above every height, and Yours is the praise in every state.”"],[4635,"Fear the supplication of the wronged."],[4637,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the wind rise, he would face it, kneel down, and then say: 'O Allah, make it winds and do not make it a wind; O Allah, make it a mercy and do not make it a punishment.'"],[4638,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed the people and said: 'Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has given every possessor of a right his right. Allah has ordained obligations, established sunnahs, set limits, made lawful what is lawful, made unlawful what is unlawful, and legislated Islam, making it easy, spacious, and wide, not narrow. O people, there is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant. Whoever breaks the protection of Allah, the Exalted, He will seek him out; whoever breaks my protection, I will dispute with him; and whoever I dispute with, I will overcome him with proof. Whoever breaks my protection will not attain my intercession, nor will he come to me at the Pond. Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has not permitted killing except in three cases: an apostate after faith, a fornicator after being married, or a murderer of a soul, who is killed for it. O Allah, have I conveyed?'"],[4639,"He used to say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the evil of what the wind brings, and from the evil of what the messengers bring.'"],[4640,"The wind is from the breath of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. When you see it, ask Allah, Exalted is He, for its good, and seek refuge with Allah from its evil."],[4641,"When the wind blew strongly, he would say: 'O Allah, make it a fertilizing wind, not a barren one.'"],[4643,"If one of your mounts strays in a wilderness, let him call out: 'O servants of Allah, restrain it! O servants of Allah, restrain it!' For Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has a presence on earth that will restrain it."],[4645,"He sat in a gathering, and when he wanted to leave, he said: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise; I bear witness that there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You.' A man from the group said: 'What is this supplication, O Messenger of Allah?' He ﷺ said: 'Words that Gabriel ﷺ taught me, expiations for the sins of the gathering.'"],[4647,"A man said in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Praise be to Allah, much good and blessed praise.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Who said these words?' The man fell silent, thinking that he had displeased the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Who is he? He has spoken nothing but truth.' The man said: 'I said them, O Messenger of Allah, hoping for good.' He ﷺ said: 'By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I saw thirteen angels rushing to take up your words, each trying to be the one to raise them to Allah, Mighty and Majestic.'"],[4648,"Whoever says: 'Glory be to your Lord, the Lord of Might, above what they describe; and peace be upon the messengers; and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds' has filled the fullest measure."],[4650,"Let no man among you neglect to perform a thousand good deeds for Allah, that is, to glorify Allah a thousand times. For he will not do the like of that, if Allah, Exalted is He, wills, in his day of sins, and whatever good he does besides that will be abundant."],[4651,"Whoever among you is unable to endure the night vigil, or is too miserly to spend his wealth, or too cowardly to fight the enemy, let him increase in remembrance of Allah, Exalted is He."],[4653,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and said: “O people, God Almighty has detachments of angels that alight and stand over the gatherings of remembrance on earth, so graze in the meadows of Paradise.” They said: “Where are the meadows of Paradise, O Messenger of God?” He ﷺ said: “The gatherings of remembrance. So go forth in the morning and evening in the remembrance of God Almighty, and remind yourselves of Him. Whoever would love to know his station with God Almighty, let him look at how the station of God, Mighty and Majestic, is with him. For God Almighty places the servant in the station that he assigns to Him from his own self.”"],[4654,"“O people, God Almighty has detachments of angels that alight and stand over the gatherings of remembrance on earth, so graze in the meadows of Paradise.” They said: “Where are the meadows of Paradise, O Messenger of God?” He ﷺ said: “The gatherings of remembrance. So go forth in the morning and evening in the remembrance of God Almighty, and remind yourselves of Him. Whoever would love to know his station with God Almighty, let him look at how the station of God, Mighty and Majestic, is with him. For God Almighty places the servant in the station that he assigns to Him from his own self.”"],[4656,"When you enter upon your Muslim brother, eat from his food and do not ask, and drink from his drink and do not ask."],[4657,"“O people, God Almighty has detachments of angels that alight and stand over the gatherings of remembrance on earth, so graze in the meadows of Paradise.” They said: “Where are the meadows of Paradise, O Messenger of God?” He ﷺ said: “The gatherings of remembrance. So go forth in the morning and evening in the remembrance of God Almighty, and remind yourselves of Him. Whoever would love to know his station with God Almighty, let him look at how the station of God, Mighty and Majestic, is with him. For God Almighty places the servant in the station that he assigns to Him from his own self.”"],[4658,"“There is no spot on which God Almighty is remembered (for prayer) or remembrance except that it rejoices in the remembrance of God, Mighty and Majestic, to its farthest extent among the (seven) earths, and it boasts over the spots around it.”"],[4659,"(And) there is no servant who stands in a desolate tract of land intending prayer except that the earth is adorned for him."],[4660,"“Race to the meadows of Paradise.” They said: “O Prophet of God, what are the meadows of Paradise?” He ﷺ said: “The circles of remembrance.”"],[4661,"“Satan places his snout on the heart of the son of Adam. If he remembers God, Mighty and Majestic, he withdraws; if he forgets, he swallows his heart. That is the whisperer who withdraws.”"],[4662,"We entered upon Ibn ʿAbbās ؓ, and a man said to him: “Which deed is best?” He said: “Remembrance of God; God is Greater,” three times. Then he said: “No people sit in a house among the houses of God, Blessed and Exalted, studying the Book of God Almighty and passing it around among themselves, except that the angels shade them with their wings and they are the guests of God, Blessed and Exalted, until they rise.”"],[4663,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ traveling in a group from Jumdān, the Messenger of God ﷺ stopped and said: “O Muʿādh, where are the foremost?” I said: “Some have gone ahead and some have stayed behind.” He ﷺ said: “Where are the foremost who are devoted to the remembrance of God, Mighty and Majestic? Whoever would love to graze in the meadows of Paradise, let him increase in the remembrance of God, Mighty and Majestic.”"],[4664,"No human being has done a deed more saving for him from the punishment of God, Mighty and Majestic, than the remembrance of God Almighty. They said: “Not even striving in the path of God, Mighty and Majestic?” He said: “No, even if he strikes with his sword, for God says: ‘And the remembrance of God is greater.’”"],[4665,"The gatherings are three: profitable, safe, and harmful. The profitable one is the one in which Allah, the Exalted, is mentioned abundantly. The safe one is the one in which one remains silent, neither gaining nor losing. The harmful one is the one in which one's speech and actions are in disobedience to Allah, Blessed and Exalted."],[4666,"The gatherings are three: among them are the profitable, among them are the safe, and among them are the harmful. The profitable is a servant who remembers Allah, Mighty and Majestic, so Allah, the Exalted, remembers him. The safe is a servant who has not dictated to his scribe any good or evil. The harmful is the one who engages in falsehood, so he brings harm upon himself."],[4668,"To sit with people who remember Allah, Mighty and Majestic, from the dawn prayer until sunrise is more beloved to me than what the sun has risen upon. And to remember Allah from the afternoon prayer until sunset is more beloved to me than freeing eight descendants of Ishmael, the blood money of each of them being twelve thousand. We calculated their blood monies while we were in the gathering, and it reached ninety-six thousand. There are some who say: four descendants of Ishmael. By Allah, he only said eight, the blood money of each of them being twelve thousand."],[4669,"To sit with people who remember Allah, Mighty and Majestic, after the dawn prayer until the sun rises is more beloved to me than freeing four descendants of Ishmael. And to remember Allah, Mighty and Majestic, after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets is more beloved to me than freeing eight necks from the descendants of Ishmael."],[4670,"To pray the dawn prayer and sit with people who remember Allah, the Exalted, until sunrise is more beloved to me than what the sun has risen upon. And to pray the afternoon prayer and sit with people who remember Allah, Mighty and Majestic, until sunset is more beloved to me than freeing eight necks from the descendants of Ishmael, the blood money of each neck being twelve thousand."],[4671,"To sit with people who remember Allah, the Exalted, from the morning until the sun rises is more beloved to me than what the sun has risen upon."],[4672,"To sit with people who remember Allah, the Exalted, from the afternoon prayer until the sun sets is more beloved to me than freeing eight descendants of Ishmael."],[4673,"All of them are Muslims."],[4674,"Whoever prays the dawn prayer, or he said the morning prayer, then remains seated in his place and does not engage in anything of worldly matters but remembers Allah, the Exalted, until he prays four rak'ahs of the forenoon prayer, he will come out of his sins like the day his mother gave birth to him, with no sin upon him."],[4676,"Will not one of you stand and pray four rak'ahs, and say in them what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: 'Your light is complete, and You guided, so to You be praise. Your forbearance is great, and You pardoned, so to You be praise. You spread Your hand and gave, so to You be praise. Your face is the greatest of faces, Your honor is the greatest of honors, and Your gift is the best and most pleasant of gifts. You are obeyed, our Lord, and You thank; You are disobeyed, our Lord, and You forgive. You answer the distressed, remove grief, heal the sick, forgive sin, and accept repentance. No one can repay Your favors, and no one's words can reach Your praise.'"],[4678,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when morning came, he would say: 'We have entered the morning and the dominion belongs to Allah, and grandeur, majesty, creation, night and day, and whatever dwells in them belong to Allah alone, with no partner. O Allah, make the beginning of this day righteous, its middle successful, and its end prosperous. I ask You for the good of this world and the Hereafter.'"],[4679,"We were sitting with a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ؓ, when someone came to him and said: 'Go to your house, for it has caught fire.' He said: 'My house has not caught fire.' He went, then came back, and it was said to him: 'Go to your house, for it has caught fire.' He said: 'No, by Allah, my house has not caught fire.' It was said to him: 'You are told that your house has caught fire, and you swear by Allah that it has not caught fire?' He ؓ said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever says in the morning: \"My Lord is Allah, there is no god but Him, upon Him I rely, and He is the Lord of the Mighty Throne. Whatever Allah wills happens, and whatever He does not will does not happen. There is no might nor power except with Allah, the Most High, the Magnificent. I bear witness that Allah is capable of all things, and that Allah has encompassed all things in knowledge. I seek refuge in Allah, who holds the sky from falling upon the earth except by His permission, from the evil of every creature, my Lord is holding its forelock. Indeed, my Lord is on a straight path.\" He will not see that day in himself, his family, or his wealth anything he dislikes. And I have said it today.'"],[4680,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him a supplication and commanded him to keep reciting it with his family every day. He ﷺ said: 'Say when you enter the morning: Here I am, O Allah, here I am. Here I am, and at Your service; all good is in Your Hands, and from You, and for You, and to You. Whatever word I speak, whatever deed I do, whatever vow I make, whatever oath I swear, Your will precedes all of that. What You will happens, and what You do not will does not happen. There is no might nor power except with You. Surely You have power over all things. O Allah, whatever prayer I pray, let it be for the one upon whom You have prayed; whatever curse I utter, let it be upon the one whom You have cursed. You are my protector in this world and the Hereafter. Cause me to die as a Muslim and join me with the righteous.'"],[4681,"He used to supplicate with these invocations when he entered the morning and when he entered the evening: 'O Allah, I ask You for sudden good, and I seek refuge with You from sudden evil, for the servant does not know what may suddenly befall him when he enters the morning and when he enters the evening.'"],[4682,"When the servant says upon entering the morning: 'O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no partner to You. I have entered the morning, and the dominion has entered the morning belonging to Allah, with no partner to Him.' When the servant says it upon entering the morning and upon entering the evening, I expiate for him whatever he has committed between them, or he said: whatever he has incurred between them."],[4683,"Ibn Umar ؓ, when he entered the morning, would say: 'O Allah, make me among the greatest of Your servants in share of every good You distribute in the morning: light by which You guide, mercy You spread, provision You extend, harm You remove, affliction You repel, tribulation You divert, and evil You ward off.'"],[4685,"A crow with full wings was brought to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ. He ؓ said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'No game is hunted, no tree is cut, no branch is severed except due to a lack of glorification.' Then he ؓ released the crow."],[4686,"'When I narrate to you a hadith, I inform you of its confirmation from the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: No servant says: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest, and blessed is Allah, except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, appoints over them an angel who places them under his wings and ascends with them to the sky. They do not pass by any assembly of angels except that they seek forgiveness for the one who said them, until they greet the Face of the Most Merciful, Mighty and Majestic. Then Abdullah recited: To Him ascend the good words, and the righteous deed raises it.'"],[4687,"'That I say: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest, is more beloved to me than spending the like of their number in the way of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.'"],[4688,"I said to a jurist in Makkah: We have a jurist—meaning al-Hasan—who, when he is silent, his constant refrain is: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, glory be to Allah the Magnificent. He said: This companion of yours is indeed a jurist. No servant says it seven times except that a house is built for him in Paradise."],[4689,"'Whoever declares the oneness of Allah one hundred times, magnifies Allah one hundred times, and glorifies Allah one hundred times, it is better than freeing ten slaves and slaughtering seven camels.'"],[4690,"'There is no morning in which the servants enter the morning except that a crier cries out: O creatures, glorify the King, the Holy One.'"],[4692,"Hidden remembrance, which the recording angels do not hear, is favored by seventy times. And he says: 'When the Day of Resurrection comes and Allah, the Exalted, gathers the creatures for their reckoning, and the recording angels come with what they recorded and wrote, Allah, the Exalted, says to them: Look, is anything left for him? They say: Our Lord, we have not left anything of what we knew and recorded except that we have counted and written it. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: You have with Me something hidden that you do not know, and I will reward you for it. That is hidden remembrance.'"],[4694,"'When one of you strikes his servant, and the servant mentions Allah, Mighty and Majestic, then raise your hands.'"],[4696,"When you see a fire, say the takbir."],[4697,"When a great sin occurs or a dark wind blows, you should say the takbir, for it clears away the black dust."],[4699,"Any people who sit in a gathering and then disperse before remembering Allah Almighty and invoking blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, that gathering will be a regret for them on the Day of Resurrection."],[4700,"No people ever sit in a gathering without remembering Allah Almighty except that it will be a regret for them on the Day of Resurrection."],[4702,"Abu Dharr ؓ sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he mentioned the hadith, saying: \"Seek refuge in Allah from the devils among humans and jinn.\""],[4703,"Whoever says, 'I ask Allah for Paradise' seven times, Paradise says, 'O Allah, admit him into Paradise.' And whoever seeks refuge from the Fire seven times, the Fire says, 'O Allah, protect him from the Fire.'"],[4704,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yunus, who is Ibn Khabbab, from Abu 'Alqamah, from Abu Hurayrah ؓ, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said something similar."],[4705,"Al-Bazzar said: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, and he mentioned it."],[4706,"Ka'b ؓ narrated to us that he said, concerning what is found written in the Torah: 'Indeed, Satan cannot bear a servant who, from evening until morning, says: O Allah, I seek refuge in Your name and Your perfect words from evil in the specific and the general, and I ask You by Your name and Your perfect words for the best of what is asked and the best of what You give, and the best of what You conceal and the best of what You reveal. O Allah, I ask You by Your name and Your perfect words from the evil of what the day clears away, if it is day, and if it is night, he says: from the evil of what the night covers.'"],[4707,"I bear witness that Allah is true, that meeting Him is true, that the Hour is true, that Paradise is true, and that the Fire is true. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and death, from the punishment of the grave, and from the punishment of Hell."],[4708,"The Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from deafness and dumbness, and I seek refuge in You from sin and debt, and I seek refuge in You from death by being crushed.'"],[4709,"And I seek refuge in You from drowning, and I seek refuge in You from anxiety."],[4710,"«Whoever seeks refuge in Allah Almighty ten times in a day from the devil, Allah Almighty will appoint an angel for him to drive away the devil from him.»"],[4711,"«Shirk among you is more hidden than the crawling of an ant.»"],[4713,"Abu Dharr ؓ sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he mentioned the hadith similar to a hadith before it in which he said: Then he ﷺ said: «Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?» I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He ﷺ said: «Say: There is no might and no power except with Allah.»"],[4714,"I met Abu Ayyub al-Ansari ؓ, and he said: Shall I not command you with what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me, that I should say often: There is no might and no power except with Allah, for it is from the treasures of Paradise?"],[4715,"«Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? Say often: There is no might and no power except with Allah.»"],[4716,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ one day and I said: There is no might and no power except with Allah. He ﷺ said: «Do you know its interpretation?» I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He ﷺ said: «There is no turning away from disobedience to Allah except with Allah's protection, and no strength to obey Allah except with Allah's might. Thus.»"],[4717,"«There is no might and no power except with Allah is from the treasures of the Throne.»"],[4720,"«Allah Almighty created in Paradise a wind after the wind by seven years, and besides it is a closed door, and the wind comes to you only from the gap of that door. If that door were opened, it would scatter what is between heaven and earth. It is with Allah Almighty al-Azyab, and with you the south wind.»"],[4721,"«Allah Almighty created in Paradise a wind after the wind by seven years, and besides it is a closed door, and the wind comes to you only from the gap of that door. If that door were opened, it would scatter what is between heaven and earth. It is with Allah Almighty al-Azyab, and with you the south wind.» (Marfu')"],[4722,"«Between the lowest heaven and the earth is a journey of five hundred years, and the thickness of each of them is a journey of five hundred years, and between each heaven and the one that follows it is a journey of five hundred years, up to the seventh heaven, and the earths are like that, and between the seventh heaven and the Throne is like all of that.»"],[4723,"«The heavens: the first of them is a restrained wave, the second is of rock, the third is of iron, the fourth is of brass, the fifth is of silver, the sixth is of gold, and the seventh is of ruby.»"],[4724,"The Throne is a red ruby."],[4726,"Sunday is a day of planting and building, Monday is a day of travel, Tuesday is a day of blood, Wednesday is a day of taking in which there is no giving, Thursday is a day of entering upon the ruler, Friday is a day of marriage and cohabitation, and Saturday [is a day of...]"],[4728,"I said to Ka'b: 'What holds this earth upon which we are?' He said: 'The command of Allah, the Exalted.' He said: I said: 'I know that the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is what holds it, but what is that command of Allah?' He said: 'A green tree in the hand of an angel among the angels, standing on the back of the whale, curled up, and the heavens are beneath the Throne.' I said: 'Who inhabits the second earth?' He said: 'The barren wind; when He willed to destroy 'Ad, He revealed to its keepers: \"Open a door from it.\" They said: \"Our Lord, like the nostril of an ox?\" He said: \"Then it would cast away the earth and whoever is upon it.\" So it was made like the place of a signet ring.' He said: I said: 'Who inhabits the third earth?' He said: 'The stones of Jahannam.' He said: I said: 'Who inhabits the fourth earth?' He said: 'The sulfur of Jahannam.' I said: 'Does it have sulfur?' He said: 'Yes, by the One in Whose hand is my soul, and seas into which if the mountains were thrown they would crumble from its heat.' He said: I said: 'Who inhabits the fifth earth?' He said: 'The serpents of Jahannam.' I said: 'Does it have serpents?' He said: 'Yes, by the One in Whose hand is my soul, like valleys.' I said: 'Who inhabits the sixth earth?' He said: 'The scorpions of Jahannam.' I said: 'Does it have scorpions?' He said: 'Yes, by the One in Whose hand is my soul, like the celestial sphere, and they have tails like spears. One of them would meet the disbeliever and sting him one sting, and his flesh would fall off his feet.' He said: I said: 'Who inhabits the seventh earth?' He said: 'That is Sijjin; in it Iblis is fettered. The angels sought help against him, so Allah, the Exalted, imprisoned him in it, a hand in front of him and a hand behind him, and a leg in front of him and a leg behind him. His troops bring him news, and he has a time when he will be sent forth.'"],[4730,"\"Souls are mobilized troops: those that knew each other become intimate, and those that did not know each other differ.\""],[4732,"\"Permission was granted to me to speak about an angel whose feet have pierced the seventh earth while the Throne is upon his shoulder, saying: 'Glory be to You! Where were You and where will You be?'\""],[4734,"\"Allah, the Exalted, created the jinn in three kinds: a kind of serpents, scorpions, and creeping things of the earth; a kind like the wind in the air; and a kind upon whom is reckoning and punishment. And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created mankind in three kinds: a kind like cattle—Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'They have hearts wherewith they understand not'—the verse; a kind whose bodies are the bodies of the children of Adam and whose spirits are the spirits of devils; and a kind in the shade of Allah, the Exalted, on a day when there is no shade but His shade.\""],[4735,"\"Allah, the Exalted, created the jinn in three thirds: a third have wings with which they fly in the air, a third are serpents and dogs, and a third settle and depart.\""],[4737,"Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad b. Yahya al-Zimmani narrated to us, Makki b. Ibrahim narrated to us, Musa b. 'Ubaydah narrated to us, from 'Umar b. al-Hakam, from 'Abdullah b. 'Amr, and from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ؓ with it."],[4738,"\"Below Allah, Blessed and Exalted, are seventy thousand veils of light and darkness; no soul hears anything of the sound of those veils but that its soul departs.\""],[4740,"\"O Abu Dharr,\" and I said: \"At your service and gladly.\" He said: \"Have you prayed today?\" I said: \"No.\" He ﷺ said: \"Rise and pray,\" so I rose and prayed as long as Allah, the Exalted, willed, then I returned and sat. He ﷺ remained silent for a long time without speaking to me, so I said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has disliked my company.\" Then he ﷺ turned to me and said: \"O Abu Dharr.\" I said: \"At your service and gladly.\" He ﷺ said: \"Seek refuge in Allah from the evil of the devils of mankind and jinn.\" I said: \"May my father and mother be sacrificed for you; do humans have devils?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Does not Allah, Mighty and Majestic, say: 'Devils of mankind and jinn, inspiring one another'—the verse?\" Then he ﷺ turned to me and said: \"O Abu Dharr.\" I said: \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah.\" He ﷺ said: \"Shall I not teach you a phrase that is a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?\" I said: \"Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you.\" He ﷺ said: \"Say: 'There is no might nor power except with Allah.'\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ persisted in not speaking until that lasted long from him. So I initiated the speech and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you commanded me to pray; what is prayer?\" He ﷺ said: \"It is a good that is placed; whoever wishes takes little, and whoever wishes takes much.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is fasting?\" He ﷺ said: \"An obligatory duty that suffices.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is charity?\" He ﷺ said: \"Multiplied manifold, and with Allah is more.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best?\" He ﷺ said: \"Faith in Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and Jihad in the path of Allah, the Exalted.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which martyrs are best?\" He ﷺ said: \"One whose blood is spilled and whose horse is hamstrung.\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which slaves are best?\" He ﷺ said: \"The most expensive in price and the most precious to their owners.\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best?\" He ﷺ said: \"An effort from one of little means, and a secret to a poor person.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what if I do not find anything to give in charity?\" He ﷺ said: \"You help a weak person or you make something for an unskilled person.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what if I cannot?\" He ﷺ said: \"Then you restrain this—and he ﷺ pointed to his tongue—for it is a good charity a person gives on behalf of himself.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which verse revealed to you of the Quran is greatest?\" He ﷺ said: \"The Verse of the Throne. And do you know what the likeness of the heavens and the earth is in relation to the Throne?\" I said: \"No, unless you teach me from what Allah, the Exalted, has taught you.\" He ﷺ said: \"The likeness of the heavens and the earth in the Throne is but like a ring cast in a desert, and the excellence of the Throne over the heavens and the earth is like the excellence of the desert over that ring.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how many were the prophets (peace be upon them)?\" He ﷺ said: \"They were one hundred twenty-four thousand.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, were all of them messengers?\" He ﷺ said: \"No, the messengers among them were three hundred fifteen men.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which of them was first?\" He ﷺ said: \"Adam ﷺ .\" I said: \"Was Adam a prophet?\" He ﷺ said: \"Yes; Allah formed his clay, created him with His hand, breathed into him of His spirit, and spoke to him directly.\" Then the people became many around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Shall I not inform you of the most miserly of people?\" I said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He ﷺ said: \"One in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not send blessings upon me ﷺ.\""],[4742,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which of the prophets was first?\" He ﷺ said: \"Adam.\" I said: \"Was he a prophet?\" He ﷺ said: \"Yes, a prophet spoken to.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how many prophets are there?\" He ﷺ said: \"Three hundred fifteen, a great multitude.\""],[4743,"Abu Dharr ؓ asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"How many prophets are there?\" He ﷺ said: \"One hundred twenty-four thousand.\" He said: \"How many messengers among them?\" He ﷺ said: \"Three hundred fifteen, a great multitude.\""],[4744,"\"One hundred twenty-four thousand.\" He said: \"How many messengers among them?\" He ﷺ said: \"Three hundred fifteen, a great multitude.\""],[4745,"And Abu Bakr said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Musa b. Ubaydah narrated to us, with it."],[4746,"Among my brothers from the prophets (peace be upon them) who had passed were eight thousand prophets, then 'Isa son of Maryam (peace be upon them both), then I."],[4748,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[4749,"The prophets are alive in their graves, praying."],[4750,"We do not know of anyone who followed al-Hasan b. Qutaybah in his transmission of it from Hammad:"],[4752,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[4754,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by al-Hijr in the valley of Thamud and said ﷺ: 'Hasten your journey, and do not stay in this village whose people were destroyed.'"],[4755,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[4757,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[4758,"No one narrated it from Ayyub except Sa'id, and no one from him except Yazid."],[4760,"Yusuf and his mother were given a third of all beauty."],[4761,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and he honored him. He said to him: 'Come to us.' So he came to him and he said: 'Ask for your need?' He said: 'A she-camel to ride, and some goats for my family to milk.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Are you unable to be like the old woman of the Children of Israel?' They asked him, and he ﷺ said: 'When Musa ﷺ traveled with the Children of Israel from Egypt, they lost their way. He said: What is this? Their scholars said: When Yusuf ﷺ was near death, he took a covenant from us by Allah, Exalted is He, that we would not leave Egypt until we carry his bones with us. He said: Who knows the place of his grave? They said: An old woman of the Children of Israel. So he sent for her, and she came to him. He said: Show me the grave of Yusuf. She said: Not until you grant me my request. He said: What is your request? She said: That I be with you in Paradise. He disliked granting her that, so Allah, Exalted is He, revealed to him: Grant her her request. So she went with them to a lake—a place where water collects—and said: Drain this water. So they drained it. She said: Dig. So they dug and brought out the bones of Yusuf ﷺ . When they lifted them to the ground, behold, there was a path like daylight.'"],[4762,"A man said to Ya'qub ﷺ : 'What took away your sight and bent your back?' He said: 'As for what took my sight, it was weeping for Yusuf; and as for what bent my back, it was grief for his brother Binyamin.' He said: Then Jibril ﷺ came to him and said: 'O Ya'qub, do you complain to Allah, Exalted is He?' He said: 'I only complain of my anguish and sorrow to Allah.' Jibril ﷺ said to him: 'Allah knows best what you say than you do.' Then Jibril ﷺ left, and Ya'qub entered his house and said: 'O Lord, You have taken away my sight and bent my back; so return to me my two sweet-smelling ones that I may smell them once, then do with me what You will.' Jibril ﷺ came to him and said: 'O Ya'qub, Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, sends you greetings and says: Rejoice, for if they had been dead I would have raised them for you and comforted your eyes. And He says to you: O Ya'qub, do you know why I took away your sight and bent your back? And why the brothers of Yusuf did what they did?' He said: 'Because an orphan and a poor man came to you while he was fasting and hungry, and you and your family had slaughtered a sheep and eaten it, and you did not feed him. And He says: I have not loved anything of My creation as much as I love the orphans and the poor.'"],[4764,"When Allah, Exalted is He, sent Musa ﷺ to Pharaoh, he said: 'What shall I say?' He said: 'Say: Ahyah Shar Ahyah.' Al-A'mash said: They interpreted it as: 'The Living before everything, and the Living after everything.'"],[4765,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: 'Do not be like those who abused Musa, and Allah cleared him of what they said' — he said: Musa and Harun went up the mountain, and Harun died. The Children of Israel said: 'You killed him! He was more loving to us than you, and gentler to us than you.' So they abused him with that. Then Allah, Exalted is He, commanded the angels, and they carried him until they passed by the Children of Israel. The angels (peace be upon them) spoke of his death until the Children of Israel knew that he had died. Then they took him and buried him. No one of Allah's creation, Exalted is He, saw his grave except the vulture; so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, made it deaf and mute."],[4766,"Among the companions of Musa ﷺ who crossed the sea were twelve tribes; on every path there were twelve thousand, all of them from the children of Ya'qub ﷺ ."],[4767,"The sea was split for the Children of Israel on the day of Ashura."],[4769,"Al-Abbas ؓ had a house near the mosque. Umar ؓ asked him: 'Give it to me — or sell it to me — so I can include it in the mosque.' He refused. Umar ؓ said: 'Then appoint a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to judge between me and you.' So he appointed Ubayy b. Ka'b ؓ, and he ruled against Umar ؓ. Umar ؓ said: 'You are indeed one of the boldest of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'Or rather one of the most sincere to you, O Commander of the Believers.' Then he said: 'Do you not know that Dawud ﷺ was commanded to build the House of the Sanctuary, and he incorporated houses without their owners' permission? When the building reached the waists of men, its construction was prevented. So he said: \"O Lord, then in my progeny after me?\"'"],[4771,"When Dawud ﷺ brought the vessel near his mouth to drink and remembered his sin, he wept until the vessel overflowed with his tears."],[4773,"I do not know whether Uzayr was a prophet or not."],[4775,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah: 'No prophet ever lived long except that the prophet ﷺ after him lived half the lifespan of his predecessor. Isa lived forty, and I twenty.'"],[4777,"'Akkaf b. Wada'ah al-Hilali came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger ﷺ said to him: 'O 'Akkaf, do you have a wife?' He said: 'No...' — the hadith, and in it: 'They are the companions of Yusuf, Dawud, and Karsaf.' He said: 'What is Karsaf, O Messenger of Allah?' He said ﷺ: 'A man among the Children of Israel on one of the seashores, fasting by day and standing in prayer by night, never slackening in prayer and fasting. Then after that he disbelieved in Allah the Almighty because of a woman he fell in love with, and he abandoned the worship of his Lord that he had been upon. Then Allah, Exalted is He, took care of him because of what had preceded from him, and accepted his repentance.'"],[4779,"Al-Khidr ﷺ is in the sea, and Al-Yasa' ﷺ is on land. They meet every night at the barrier which Dhu al-Qarnayn built between the people and Ya'juj and Ma'juj. They perform Hajj and Umrah every year, and drink from Zamzam a single drink that suffices them until the next year."],[4781,"There was among the Children of Israel, or among some of the kings, a man. He said: 'I do not know anyone today more mighty than me.' He said: Then Allah, Exalted is He, sent to him the weakest of His creation, and it entered his nostril. He began to say: 'Strike, strike!' So they struck his head with axes until they crushed his head."],[4782,"A man killed ninety-nine people. Then he wanted to repent, so he went to a monk in a barren land and said, \"O monk, I have killed ninety-nine people. Is there any repentance for me?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"No doubt, by Allah, I will complete them to a hundred with you.\" Then he went to another monk and said, \"I have killed ninety-nine people and completed them to a hundred with a monk. Is there any repentance for me?\" He said, \"You have gone to excess against yourself and committed a grave sin, but whoever repents, Allah turns to him.\" He said, \"So he threw away the sword and said, 'By Allah, I will serve you until death separates us.'\" He said, \"He made a covenant with him not to disobey him.\" He said, \"Then some people came who were travelers or afflicted with drought, and he used to practice medicine. The man said, 'Do you command me to do anything?' He said, 'Go and stoke the oven.' He said, 'So he went and stoked it until it became hot.' He said, 'It has become hot, so what do you command me?' He said, 'Go and fall into it.' He said, 'So he went and fell into it.' Then the monk remembered and stood up, and those with him stood up, and there he was in the oven, sweating, and the fire did not harm him. The monk said, 'I have come to know that your repentance has been accepted, so I will serve you forever until you depart from me.' Ibn Mas'ud ؓ said, 'Among the Children of Israel, when one of them committed a sin, he would wake up with the expiation for his sin written on the threshold of his door. Allah the Exalted has favored you over them, for you have been commanded to seek forgiveness, and you seek forgiveness from Allah the Exalted.' He said, 'And He has given this nation a verse which I would not love to have in exchange for the world and all that is in it: And those who, when they commit an immorality or wrong themselves, remember Allah and seek forgiveness for their sins...'\""],[4783,"There was a man from among those before you among disbelieving people, and among them were righteous people. The man said, 'As long as I have been in my disbelief, I will surely go to this righteous village and become a man from among them.' So he set out, but his appointed time overtook him on the way. The angel and the devil disputed over him; this one said, 'I have more right to him,' and that one said, 'I have more right to him.' So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent one of His soldiers to them and said, 'Measure the distance between the two villages; to whichever of them he was closer, he belongs to it.' So they measured between the two villages and found him closer to the righteous village, so he was from among them."],[4784,"Report about the Children of Israel, and there is no sin, for among them were wonders."],[4785,"A monk worshiped Allah the Exalted in his hermitage for sixty years. Then a woman came down beside him, and he went down to her and stayed with her for six nights. Then he became remorseful and fled, and came to a mosque and stayed there for three days without eating. Then a loaf of bread was brought to him, and he broke it into two halves and gave half to a poor person on his right and half to another on his left. Then Allah the Exalted took his soul. The sixty years were weighed in one pan and the six nights in another, and the six nights outweighed them. Then the six nights were weighed against the loaf, and the loaf outweighed them."],[4786,"A man devoted himself to worship for sixty years."],[4787,"Five of the Children of Israel used to enter into a pomegranate rind."],[4788,"\"A prophet supplicated against his nation, and it was said to him, 'Would you like me to inflict famine upon them?' He said, 'No.' It was said to him, 'Would you like me to cast their might between them?' He said, 'No.' He said, 'Then the plague was inflicted upon them as a precise death, burning hearts and reducing numbers.'\""],[4790,"\"Whoever recites a hundred verses in a night will not be recorded among the heedless. Whoever recites two hundred verses will be recorded among the devout. Whoever recites from a thousand to five hundred verses will wake up with a qintar of reward, a carat of which is like a great hill.\""],[4792,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for me, for my children, and for my children's children. I heard my father say to a sister of mine who was older than me: You are among those whom the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached."],[4793,"\"Whoever recites a hundred verses in a night, the Qur'an will not dispute with him. Whoever recites two hundred, Allah the Exalted will record for him the devoutness of a night. Whoever recites from a hundred to a thousand will wake up with a qintar, and a qintar is the blood money of one of you: twelve thousand. And the smallest of houses in good is the house in which the Qur'an is not recited.\""],[4794,"Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad b. Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri' narrated to us with it. :, :"],[4795,"«Whoever recites a letter from the Book of Allah Almighty, Allah Almighty records for him a good deed. I do not say that Alif Lām Mīm is a letter, but the letters are separate: alif, lām, and mīm.»"],[4797,"«O people, I have left among you that which, if you hold fast to it, you will never go astray: the Book of Allah.»"],[4798,"And ʿAbd said: Abū Bakr narrated to us with it (140), and it has already been mentioned in the chapter on the sanctity of Makkah."],[4799,"«Act according to the Qurʾān: deem lawful what it declares lawful, deem unlawful what it declares unlawful, follow its example, and do not disbelieve in any part of it. Whatever is unclear to you, refer it to Allah (Mighty and Glorious) and to the people of knowledge after me, so that they may inform you. And believe in the Torah and the Gospel, and do not reject what the prophets received from their Lord. Let the Qurʾān and the clarity within it suffice you, for it is an intercessor whose intercession will be accepted, and a witness whose testimony will be believed. Indeed, for every verse of it there is a light on the Day of Resurrection. I was given Sūrat al-Baqarah from the early Reminder, and I was given Ṭā Hā and the Ṭawāsīn from the tablets of Moses, and I was given the Opening of the Book and the closing verses of Sūrat al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne, and I was given the Mufaṣṣal as an additional gift.»"],[4800,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4801,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4802,"«The Qurʾān was revealed in seven letters, each of which has an outward and an inward meaning.»"],[4803,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4804,"ʿUthmān ؓ said from the pulpit: I adjure by Allah Almighty any man who heard the Prophet ﷺ say: «The Qurʾān was revealed in seven letters, all of them sufficient and healing» to stand up. They stood up until they could not be counted, and they testified to that. Then ʿUthmān ؓ said: And I testify with you, three times: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say that."],[4805,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4806,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were reciting the Qur'an, teaching one another, and he said ﷺ: \"Praise be to Allah. The Book of Allah is one. Among you are the virtuous, and the red and the black. Recite the Qur'an before there comes a people who recite it, pronouncing the letters of the Qur'an as an arrow is straightened, but it does not go beyond their collarbones. They hasten its reward and do not defer it.\""],[4808,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4810,"When Uthman ؓ was writing the mushafs, they were uncertain about three verses, so they wrote them on the shoulder blade of a sheep. And they sent me to Ubayy b. Ka'b and Zayd b. Thabit ؓ. I entered upon them and handed it to Ubayy b. Ka'b ؓ, and he read it and found in it: \"There is no alteration for the creation; that is the upright religion.\" So he wiped away with his hand ؓ one of the two lams and wrote it: \"There is no alteration for Allah's creation.\" He said: And he found ؓ in it: \"Look at your food and your drink; it has not changed with time.\" So he wiped away the nun and wrote it: \"it has not changed with time.\" And he read ؓ from it: \"So give respite to the disbelievers.\" So he wiped away the alif and wrote it: \"So give respite.\" He said ؓ: And I do not know him except that he said regarding it, then Zayd b. Thabit ؓ looked at it, then I departed with it to Uthman ؓ, and they established it in the mushafs as such."],[4812,"Ibn Abbas ؓ heard a man saying: \"The first recitation.\" Ibn Abbas ؓ said: \"What is the first recitation?\" A man said to him: \"O Ibn Abbas, Umar ؓ sent Ibn Mas'ud ؓ as a teacher to the people of Kufa, and they memorized his recitation. Then Uthman ؓ changed the recitation, so they call it the first recitation.\" Ibn Abbas ؓ said: \"It is the last recitation that Jibril presented to the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[4814,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4815,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4816,"“Whoever does not chant the Qur'an is not one of us.”"],[4817,"Abu Musa ؓ was reciting one night while the wives of the Prophet ﷺ were listening. It was said to him, so he said: \"Had I known, I would have beautified it beautifully and made it melodious.\""],[4818,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4821,"I was with Ali ؓ, and he heard their clamor in the mosque while they were reciting the Qur'an. He said: \"Glad tidings to these. These were the most beloved of people to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[4822,"“Whoever recites the Qur'an and acts according to what is in it and dies in the community will be raised on the Day of Resurrection with the noble and righteous scribes. Whoever recites the Qur'an while it slips away from him, Allah the Exalted will give him his reward twice. Whoever is eager for it but cannot do it and does not abandon it, Allah the Exalted will raise him with the nobles of his family, and they will be favored over creatures as eagles are favored over the rest of the birds, and as a spring in a meadow is favored over what surrounds it. Then a caller will call: Where are those who were not distracted from reciting My Book by tending livestock? They will stand up, and one of them will be clothed with the crown of honor and given bliss in his right hand and eternity in his left. Then his parents, if they were Muslims, will be clothed with a garment better than the world and what is in it. They will say: How do we have this, when our deeds did not reach this? It will be said: Your child used to recite the Qur'an.”"],[4823,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4824,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4826,"“Part of exalting Allah, the Exalted, is honoring the elderly Muslim, the bearer of the Qur’an, and the just ruler.”"],[4827,"A man obtained twenty-five uqiyyahs of gold from spoils of war, so he came to the Prophet ﷺ to ask him to supplicate for him, but he turned away from him. Then he returned, and he turned away from him. Then he returned again, and he turned away from him and said: “What so-and-so gained is better than what you gained: he learned five verses.”"],[4828,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4829,"Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū Bakr narrated to us with this."],[4830,"There was in Madinah a disabled man. He said to his family: Place me on the road of the Messenger of God ﷺ to his mosque. He said: So the disabled man was placed on the road of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Whenever he ﷺ went back and forth to the mosque, he would greet the disabled man. Then the disabled man's family came to take him back, and he said: No, by God, I will not leave this place as long as the Messenger of God ﷺ lives, so build me a hut. They built him a hut, and he remained in it. Whenever the Messenger of God ﷺ passed to the mosque, he would enter the hut and greet the disabled man, and whenever he ﷺ got a bit of food, he would send some to the disabled man. He said: While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, a man came and announced the death of the disabled man to him. The Messenger of God ﷺ rose, and we rose with him, until when he drew near the hut, he ﷺ said to his companions: Let no one approach the hut except me. He ﷺ drew near the hut, and there was Jibril (peace and blessings be upon him) sitting by the disabled man. He said: O Messenger of God, if you had not come to us, we would have taken care of him for you. But since you have come, you are more entitled to him. So the Messenger of God ﷺ went to him, washed him with his own hand, shrouded him, prayed over him, and placed him in the grave."],[4831,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by his companions ؓ while they were sitting waiting for him. When he came out, he stood over them and sat down, then said: “Do you not testify that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and testify that I am the Messenger of Allah, and testify that this Qur’an is from Allah, Mighty and Majestic?” They said: “Yes, we testify to this.” He ﷺ said: “Rejoice, for this Qur’an is a rope from Allah, the Exalted, one end of it is in the hand of Allah, the Exalted, and the other end is in your hands. So hold fast to it; you will not go astray or perish after it, ever.”"],[4832,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'What do you think of a man who recites at the beginning of the night and then steals at its end?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When he recites at its beginning, its end prevents him from stealing in the dark.'"],[4833,"“The Qur’an is wealth after which there is no poverty, and there is no wealth without it.”"],[4834,"“The Qur’an will come on the Day of Resurrection in the finest appearance and the best form.” He said: “It will say: ‘O Lord, You have given every worker the reward of his work, so where is the reward of my work?’ He said: ‘Then the companion of the Qur’an will be clothed in a robe and crowned with the crown of sovereignty.’ He said: ‘It will say: “O Lord, I desired for him something greater than this.”’ He said: ‘Then he will be given eternity in his right hand and bliss in his left hand.’ He said: ‘It will be said to him: “Are you pleased?” He will say: “Yes, O Lord.”’”"],[4835,"“When one of you rises at night (to pray), let him recite aloud, for the Shaytan and the wicked jinn flee from his loud recitation, and the angels in the air and the inhabitants of the house listen to his recitation and pray with his prayer. When this night has passed and the newly appointed angels arrive, they say: ‘Wake him at his usual time, and be gentle with him.’ When death comes to him, the Qur’an comes and stands at his head while they are washing him. When they finish with him, it enters until it is between his chest and his shroud. When he is placed in his grave and Munkar and Nakir come to him, the Qur’an comes out until it is between him and them. They say to it: ‘Get away from us, for we want to question him.’ It says: ‘By Allah, I will not leave him.’ Abu ‘Abd al-Rahman said: In the book of Mu‘awiyah b. Hammad, up to this point: “until I enter him into Paradise. If you two have been commanded regarding him with something, then your affair is up to you.” Then it looks at him and says: ‘Do you know me?’ He says: ‘No, by Allah.’ It says: ‘I am the Qur’an that kept you awake at night, made you thirsty during the day, and withheld you from your desires, your hearing, and your sight. You will find me among friends as a true friend and among brothers as a true brother. So rejoice, for after the questioning of Munkar and Nakir, there is no worry or grief upon you.’ Then they leave him, and the Qur’an ascends to its Lord and asks for a bed and a cover for him. He said: ‘Then a bed, a cover, and a lamp from Paradise are ordered for him, and jasmine from the jasmine of Paradise. Then a thousand angels from among the close angels of the lowest heaven carry him.’ He said: ‘The Qur’an gets to him before them and says: “Did you feel lonely after me? I did not cease with my Lord from whom I came until I ordered for you a bed, a cover, and light from the light of Paradise.” Then the angels enter upon him, carry him, spread that bed beneath him, place the cover under his heart, and the jasmine at his chest. Then they carry him until they lay him on his right side. Then they ascend from him, and he lies back on it, and he keeps looking at the angels until they reach the heaven. Then the Qur’an is raised at the side of the grave, and it is expanded for him as much as it is willed to be expanded.’ Abu ‘Abd al-Rahman said: In the book of Mu‘awiyah b. Hammad, according to me: ‘it is expanded for him a distance of four hundred years of travel. Then the jasmine is lifted from his chest and placed at his nose, and he smells it fresh until the day the Trumpet is blown. Then it comes to his family once or twice every two days, brings him news of them, and supplicates for good and favorable treatment for them. If one of his descendants learns the Qur’an, it gives him glad tidings of that. If his progeny is an evil progeny, it comes to the house morning and evening and weeps over him until the day the Trumpet is blown,’ or as he said.”"],[4837,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us, and he mentioned the hadith, and in it: \"Whoever learns the Qur'an then deliberately forgets it will meet Allah afflicted with leprosy and in chains, and Allah Almighty will set upon him for every verse a serpent that will bite him in the Fire. And whoever learns the Qur'an but does not act upon it, preferring the debris of this world and its adornment over it, has made himself deserving of Allah's wrath and will be in the rank of the Jews and Christians who cast the Book of Allah (Mighty and Majestic) behind their backs and sold it for a small price. And whoever recites the Qur'an for show and reputation, or desiring thereby the world, will meet Allah (Almighty) with his face a bone with no flesh upon it, and the Qur'an will shove him from behind until it hurls him into the Fire, and he will fall into it with those who fall. And whoever recites it but does not act upon it, Allah Almighty will raise him on the Day of Resurrection blind, and he will say: 'My Lord, why have You raised me blind when I used to see?' Your Lord will say: 'Thus Our signs came to you, but you forgot them; and thus today you will be forgotten.' Then he will be commanded to the Fire. And whoever learns the Qur'an seeking the face of Allah Almighty and understanding in the religion of Allah (Mighty and Majestic) will have a reward like all that Allah Almighty has given the angels, the prophets, and the messengers. And whoever learns the Qur'an for show and reputation, to argue with the foolish, boast over the scholars, and seek thereby the world, Allah Almighty will scatter his bones on the Day of Resurrection, and he will be among the people most severely punished, and no type of punishment will remain but he will be punished with it, due to the severity of Allah's punishment and His wrath upon him.\""],[4838,"We used to consider among the greatest of sins that a man learns the Qur'an then sleeps away from it until he forgets it."],[4839,"Abu Musa ؓ gathered those who had recited the Qur'an, and they were close to three hundred. He extolled the Qur'an, then said: \"This Qur'an will be for you a reward, a treasure, and a burden upon you. Follow the Qur'an, and do not let the Qur'an follow you. For whoever follows the Qur'an, it will lead him to the gardens of Paradise; and whoever the Qur'an follows, it will push him from behind and cast him into the Fire.\""],[4840,"He said: \"I dislike for the reciter to be fat.\""],[4841,"\"Do not strike the Book of Allah, one part against another, for that causes doubt to fall into your hearts.\""],[4842,"\"Do not argue about the Qur'an, for arguing about it is disbelief.\""],[4844,"\"They used to dislike teaching their children the Qur'an until they reached the age of discernment.\""],[4846,"\"Apply i'rab to the Qur'an, and seek out its rare meanings.\""],[4847,"\"Apply i'rab to the Qur'an and seek out its rare meanings.\" (marfu')"],[4849,"\"Indeed, Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ would not recite the Qur'an in less than three (days).\""],[4850,"Abdullah ؓ used to complete the Qur'an from one Friday to the next, and in Ramadan he would complete it in three (days)."],[4851,"\"Indeed, Abdullah ؓ used to recite the Qur'an every three (days), and he rarely took from it during the daytime.\""],[4853,"“Which sky will shade me, and which earth will carry me, if I say about the Book of Allah what I do not know, or what I have not heard?”"],[4854,"He would not explain anything of the Qur'an except a few verses that Jibril ﷺ taught him."],[4855,"He mentioned that among my Ummah there will be people who recite the Qur'an, scattering it as dates are scattered, interpreting it other than its proper interpretation."],[4857,"He was asked about the Opening of the Book, and he said: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ told us—then his color changed and he repeated it for a while when he mentioned the Prophet ﷺ—then he said: It was sent down from a treasure beneath the Throne."],[4860,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Ubayy b. Ka'b ؓ while he was praying in the mosque, so he turned to him. When he finished praying, he caught up with him and placed his hand in his hand, saying: “I hope you will not leave the mosque until you learn a surah the like of which Allah the Exalted has not sent down in the Torah or the Gospel.” He said: So I began to walk slowly, hoping that he would mention it, and I said: What you promised me, O Messenger of Allah? He ﷺ said: “What do you recite when you begin the prayer?” I said: Al-hamdu lillahi rabb al-'alamin until I came to the end of the surah. The Prophet ﷺ said: “It is the seven oft-repeated verses and the great Qur'an that I have been given.”"],[4862,"“The Opening of the Book equals two-thirds of the Qur'an.”"],[4864,"“Whoever recites Al-Baqarah in a night will be crowned with a crown in Paradise.”"],[4865,"Umar ؓ stopped at Al-Rawha' and saw people rushing to some stones. He said: What is this? They said: They say that the Prophet ﷺ prayed facing these stones. He said: Glory be to Allah! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was only riding and passed by a valley, and the prayer time came so he prayed. Then he narrated and said: I used to visit the Jews on the day of their study, and they said: None of your companions is more honored by us than you, because you come to us. I said: That is only because I marvel at the Books of Allah the Exalted, how they confirm one another, how the Torah confirms the Furqan and the Furqan confirms the Torah. The Prophet ﷺ passed by one day while I was speaking with them, and I said: I adjure you by Allah and by what you recite from His Book, do you know that he is the Messenger of Allah? They said: Yes. I said: Then you are ruined! By Allah, if you know that he is the Messenger of Allah, then why do you not follow him? They said: We are not ruined, but we asked him who brings him his prophethood, and he said: Our enemy Jibril, because he (peace and blessings be upon him) descends with severity, harshness, war, and destruction and the like. I said: Who is your ally among the angels? They said: Mika'il, he descends with rain and mercy and so on. I said: And what is their status with their Lord? They said: One of them is on His right, and the other on the other side. I said: Then it is not permissible for Jibril to be an enemy of Mika'il, nor is it permissible for Mika'il to make peace with the enemy of Jibril. I bear witness that they and their Lord are at peace with those who are at peace with them, and at war with those who are at war with them. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ intending to inform him, but when I met him ﷺ he said: “Shall I not tell you of verses that have been sent down to me?” I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He ﷺ recited: Say: Whoever is an enemy to Jibril—for he brought it down upon your heart by Allah's permission, confirming what was before it, and as guidance and good tidings for the believers. I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I did not leave your presence except to come to you to inform you of what they said to me and what I said to them, and I found that Allah the Exalted had preceded me. Umar ؓ said: I have seen myself as strong in Allah as a stone."],[4866,"This Venus, the Arabs call it Al-Zuharah and the non-Arabs call it Anahid. The two angels used to judge between people. She came to each of them without the other's knowledge, and one of them said to his companion: O my brother, I have something in my mind that I want to mention to you. He said: Mention it, O my brother, perhaps what is in my mind is like what is in your mind. They agreed on a matter regarding her. She said to them: No, not until you tell me by what you ascend to heaven and by what you descend to earth. They said: By the greatest name of Allah we descend, and by it we ascend. She said: I will not comply with what you want until you teach it to me. One of them said to his companion: Teach it to her. He said: How can we face the severity of Allah's punishment? The other said: We hope for the vastness of Allah's mercy, Mighty and Majestic. So they taught it to her, and she uttered it and flew up to heaven. An angel was terrified by her ascent, bowed his head, and never sat again. Allah the Exalted transformed her, and she became a star."],[4867,"“May Allah curse Suhayl—he was a tax collector in Yemen and was transformed. And may Allah curse Venus, for she tempted the two angels.”"],[4868,"Regarding His saying, the Exalted: A whirlwind with fire in it, he said: “The whirlwind is the strong wind.”"],[4869,"Regarding His saying, exalted is He, “like a rainstorm from the sky” [2:19], he said: “Al-ṣayyib is rain.”"],[4870,"Regarding His saying, exalted is He, “Those who consume ribā do not stand except as one stands whom Satan has driven to madness by touch” [2:275], he said: “They will be recognized on the Day of Resurrection by that; they will not be able to stand except as stands the one driven to madness and choking. That is because they said, ‘Trade is only like ribā,’ and they lied against God, mighty and majestic is He, while God has permitted trade and forbidden ribā, up to His saying, ‘but whoever returns [to it]’ [2:275], so he consumed ribā; those are the companions of the Fire, they will abide therein eternally. And His saying, mighty and majestic is He, ‘O you who believe, fear God and give up what remains of ribā’ [2:278], the verse. He said: It has reached us, by God, that this verse was revealed concerning Banū ʿAmr b. ʿAwf of Thaqīf and Banū al-Mughīrah of Banū Makhzūm. Banū al-Mughīrah used to charge ribā to Thaqīf. When God, exalted is He, made His Messenger ﷺ victorious over Makkah and abolished all ribā that day, and the people of al-Ṭāʾif had made peace on condition that their ribā would remain theirs, and whatever ribā was owed to them was remitted, and the Messenger of God ﷺ wrote at the end of their treaty: ‘They have what the Muslims have, and they owe what the Muslims owe: they shall not consume ribā nor cause it to be consumed.’ Then Banū ʿAmr b. ʿUmayr came to Banū al-Mughīrah before ʿAttāb b. Asīd ؓ, who was governor of Makkah. Banū al-Mughīrah said: ‘He has not made us the most wretched of people regarding ribā? It has been remitted for all people except us.’ Banū ʿAmr b. ʿUmayr said: ‘We made peace on condition that our ribā would remain ours.’ So ʿAttāb b. Asīd ؓ wrote about that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and this verse was revealed: ‘And if you do not, then be informed of war from God and His Messenger. But if you repent, you may have your principal, neither wronging nor being wronged’ [2:279] – you do not wrong by taking more, nor are you wronged by being deprived of it. ‘And if someone is in hardship, then deferral until ease. But to give charity is better for you, if you only knew’ [2:280]. And fear a day in which you will be returned to God, then the verse [2:281]. They mentioned that this verse was revealed from [the Surah of] Women [al-Nisāʾ]; it was the last of the Qurʾan to be revealed.”"],[4871,"They wandered for forty years in an area of twelve farsakhs, and a stone like the head of a bull was placed among them; whenever they halted, twelve springs gushed from it."],[4872,"Regarding His saying, exalted is He, “And We shaded you with clouds” [2:57], [he said]: “They shaded them in the wilderness.”"],[4873,"A man would divorce and then say, ‘I was joking,’ and would manumit and then say, ‘I was joking.’ So God, mighty and majestic is He, revealed: ‘And do not take the verses of God in jest’ [2:231], the verse. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘Whoever divorces or manumits and then says, “I was joking,” his statement is of no effect; it takes effect upon him and is binding.’"],[4874,"He used to recite: “And look at the bones, how We spread them out” [variant of 2:259]."],[4875,"Zayd b. Thābit ؓ used to recite: “And look at the bones, how We raise them up” [variant of 2:259]."],[4876,"Regarding His saying, blessed and exalted is He, “to your food and your drink – it has not changed – and look” [2:259], he said: “It did not change.”"],[4877,"Abū Dharr ؓ asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about faith, so he recited: “Righteousness is not that you turn your faces toward the east or the west” [2:177]."],[4878,"Al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī ؓ was asked about faith when he returned from Syria, and he recited: “Righteousness is not…” the verse [2:177]."],[4879,"\"There is no Muslim who is afflicted with a calamity, and then remembers his calamity after forty years and renews his istirja' (saying 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return'), except that Allah gives him at that moment the like of the reward he was given on the day he was afflicted.\""],[4880,"I bear witness that the salam [advance sale] with a deferred term has been permitted by God, exalted is He, and He has allowed it. God, exalted is He, whose mention is majestic, said: ‘O you who believe, when you contract a debt for a specified term, write it down’ [2:282]."],[4881,"Abd Allah ؓ used to consider it to be the morning (prayer) — meaning the middle prayer."],[4882,"And I asked him — meaning the Prophet ﷺ — about the middle prayer. He ﷺ said: \"It is the 'Asr (afternoon) prayer, the one that was neglected.\""],[4883,"He used to write down copies of the Qur'an during the time of the Prophet's ﷺ wives ؓ. He said: Hafsah ؓ asked me to write a copy for her, and she said: \"When you reach this verse in Surah Al-Baqarah, do not write it until you come to me, and I will dictate it to you as I memorized it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" When I reached it, I brought her the page I was writing on, and she said: \"Write: 'Guard strictly the prayers, and the middle prayer, and the 'Asr prayer, and stand before Allah devoutly obedient.'\""],[4884,"\"No obscenity\" — he said: \"Obscenity is sexual intercourse. And no wickedness\" — he said: \"Wickedness is disobedience. And no disputing during Hajj\" — he said: \"Disputing is quarreling.\""],[4885,"Suhaib ؓ came as an emigrant to the Prophet ﷺ. A group of Quraysh followed him, so he dismounted from his riding beast, emptied what was in his quiver, then said: \"O people of Quraysh, you know that I am one of the best archers among you. By Allah, you will not reach me until I shoot every arrow I have in my quiver, then I will strike with my sword as long as anything remains in my hand — then do whatever you wish. If you wish, I will guide you to my buried treasure in Makkah, and you will let me go.\" They said: \"Yes, we accept.\" When he arrived in Madinah to the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The deal has profited, Abu Yahya! The deal has profited, Abu Yahya!\" He said: And it was revealed: \"And of the people is he who sells himself seeking the pleasure of Allah, and Allah is kind to His servants.\""],[4887,"Umar ؓ said: \"O Messenger of Allah, this is the station of our Lord's close friend (Ibrahim). Should we not take it as a place of prayer?\" Then it was revealed: \"And take the station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer.\""],[4888,"Regarding His saying, the Most High: \"...unless Allah comes to them in shadows of clouds and the angels...\" — he said: \"Shadows of clouds, formed into layers.\""],[4889,"\"Mankind was one nation\" — he said: \"All of them were upon Islam.\" And Al-Kalbi said: \"All of them were upon disbelief.\""],[4890,"A man had anal intercourse with his wife during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and people said: \"So-and-so had anal intercourse with his wife.\" Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \"Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish.\""],[4892,"While I was praying one night, I saw something like lanterns — light descending from the sky. When I saw that, I fell prostrate. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Why did you not continue, O Abu 'Atik?\" He said: \"I could not; when I saw it, I fell prostrate.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you had continued, you would have seen wonders. Those were angels descending for the Qur'an.\""],[4893,"Usayd b. Hudayr ؓ said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"],[4894,"Usayd b. Hudayr ؓ said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"],[4895,"While Usayd b. Hudayr ؓ was praying one night, he said: (Then there covered me) something like (a cloud) containing lamps, while my wife was sleeping beside me and she was pregnant, and the horse was tethered in the house. I feared that the horse would bolt and startle the woman, causing her to miscarry, so I stopped my prayer. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ in the morning, and he ﷺ said: 'Recite, Usayd, for that was an angel listening to the Quran.'"],[4896,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided Surah al-Baqarah."],[4897,"Indeed, everything has a hump, and the hump of the Quran is Surah al-Baqarah. Whoever recites it in his house at night, Satan will not enter his house for three days, and whoever recites it during the day, Satan will not enter his house for three days."],[4898,"I would not think that anyone with sound intellect would sleep until he recites the last verses of Surah al-Baqarah, for they are from a treasure beneath the Throne."],[4900,"Abu Dharr ؓ sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he mentioned a hadith similar to a previous one, in which: I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which verse that Allah has revealed to you is the greatest?' He ﷺ said: 'Allah - there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence,' until its end."],[4901,"When 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf ؓ entered his house, he would recite Ayat al-Kursi in its corners."],[4902,"The best of the Quran is Surah al-Baqarah, and the greatest verse in it is Ayat al-Kursi. Indeed, Satan flees from a house in which Surah al-Baqarah is recited."],[4904,"When 'Uthman ؓ was killed, he mentioned a story from 'Ali ؓ then said: 'Indeed, the first House [of worship] established for mankind was that at Bakkah.' He ؓ said: 'Verily, it was not the first house that ever existed. Noah (peace and blessings be upon him) was before Abraham (peace and blessings be upon him), and they lived in houses, and Abraham lived in houses. But it was the first House established for mankind, blessed and a guidance for the worlds, in which are clear signs, the Station of Abraham, and whoever enters it is safe.'"],[4905,"Al-Harith said: Al-'Abbas b. al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, with it (146). And in the chapter on the Battle of Uhud from the Maghazi there is a hadith explaining His saying, Exalted is He: 'Then after distress, He sent down upon you security - drowsiness...' all the verses."],[4906,"And whoever enters it is safe. He said: 'It is like your saying: Enter and you are safe.'"],[4907,"I never thought that any of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ desired the worldly life until it was revealed: 'Among you are some who desire this world, and among you are some who desire the Hereafter.'"],[4908,"No relative comes to his kin asking him from the surplus of what Allah, Exalted is He, has given him, and he withholds it from him, except that on the Day of Resurrection a serpent will be brought out for him, hissing, until it encircles his neck. Then he recited: 'And let not those who withhold what Allah has given them of His bounty think...' the verse."],[4909,"You are the best nation produced for mankind: you enjoin what is right, forbid what is wrong. They are those who emigrated to Madinah."],[4910,"Al-Harith b. Suwayd had accepted Islam, then he joined his people and disbelieved. So Allah, Exalted is He, sent down this verse: How shall Allah guide a people who disbelieved after their belief and had witnessed that the Messenger is true? (to the end of) the verse. He said: A man from his people carried them to him and read them to him. Al-Harith said: By Allah, I know you to be truthful, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is more truthful than you, and Allah, Exalted is He, is the most truthful of the three. Then he returned and accepted Islam with a good Islam."],[4911,"Drowsiness during battle is a security [from Allah], and drowsiness in prayer is from Satan."],[4912,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Umar ؓ: 'Gather for me those of Quraysh who are here.'"],[4913,"I said to Ibn Abbas ؓ: Ibn Masud ؓ recites (And it is not for a prophet to yaghalla) with a fathah on the ghayn. He said to me: It would be permissible for him to yaghalla and to (kill), but it is yaghulla (meaning) with a dammah on the ghayn: And Allah (Mighty and Majestic) would not make a prophet a defrauder."],[4915,"I traveled to Aishah ؓ about this verse: It is not according to your wishes, nor the wishes of the People of the Book. Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it. She said: It is what afflicts you in this world."],[4916,"The major sins are seven: associating partners with Allah, killing a soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, disobedience to parents, fleeing from battle, slandering chaste women, consuming riba, and consuming the property of an orphan."],[4917,"I was with the Najadat and committed sins that I think are only major sins. I came to Ibn Umar ؓ and he said: They are (nine), and he counted them: associating partners with Allah, killing a soul without right, fleeing from battle, slandering a chaste woman, consuming riba, consuming the property of an orphan, deviation in the Sacred Mosque, the one who (practices sorcery), and causing one's parents to weep (through disobedience). When Ibn Umar ؓ saw my fear, he said: Do you fear entering the Fire? I said: Yes. He said: Would you like to enter Paradise? I said: Yes. He said: Are your parents alive?"],[4918,"Al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad ؓ went out on a military expedition, and they passed by a group of polytheists. They fled, but one man stayed with his family and property and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. Al-Miqdad ؓ killed him. It was said to him: 'You killed him while he testified that there is no god but Allah?' He said: He wished he could have fled with his family and property. They said: This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so ask him. They came to him and mentioned that to him. He ﷺ said: 'You killed him while he testified that there is no god but Allah?' He said: O Messenger of Allah, he wished he could have fled with his property and family. He said: Then this verse was revealed: O you who believe, when you go forth in the path of Allah, then be discerning, up to His saying: Thus you were before."],[4919,"I have been hoping for the caliphate ever since the Messenger of God ﷺ said what he said: “O Mu’awiya, if you gain sovereignty, then act well.”"],[4920,"I came to Madinah, and a man brought me to the daughter of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas ؓ, and she narrated to me the story of Thabit... Then she mentioned the hadith... She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Rather, you will live a praiseworthy life, be killed as a martyr, and Allah will admit you to Paradise.\" When the day of Yamamah came, he went out with Khalid ibn al-Walid ؓ to Musaylimah the Liar. He said: When he met the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and attacked them, they were routed. He said: He said to Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah ؓ: \"This is not how we used to fight alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Then each of them dug a pit, and the people attacked them. They kept fighting until they were killed, may Allah have mercy on them. Thabit ؓ had a precious coat of mail, and a Muslim man passed by him and took it. While a Muslim man was sleeping, Thabit ibn Qays ؓ came to him in his dream and said: \"I enjoin upon you a bequest: beware of saying, 'This is a dream,' and neglecting it. When I was killed yesterday, a Muslim man passed by me and took my coat of mail. His dwelling is at the far end of the army, and by his tent is a horse prancing in its tether. He has placed a cooking pot over the coat of mail and put a saddle on top of the pot. Go to Khalid ibn al-Walid ؓ and tell him to send for my coat of mail and take it. When you come to the successor of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, inform him that I owe such-and-such a debt, and I am owed such-and-such a debt. So-and-so, my slave, is free, and so-and-so. Beware of saying, 'This is a dream,' and neglecting it.\" The man went to Khalid ibn al-Walid ؓ and informed him, so he sent for the coat of mail. He looked at a tent at the far end of the army, and there was a horse prancing in its tether. He looked in the tent and found no one there. They entered, lifted the saddle, and beneath it was a cooking pot. They lifted it, and the coat of mail was under it. It was brought to Khalid ibn al-Walid ؓ. When he came to Madinah, the man told Abu Bakr ؓ of his dream, and he executed his bequest after his death. We do not know of any Muslim whose bequest was executed after his death except Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas ؓ."],[4921,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when revelation descended upon him. When revelation descended upon him ﷺ, his gaze became fixed, his eyes open, and his hearing and sight were devoted to what came to him from Allah, Exalted is He. When he finished, he said to the scribe: 'Write: Not equal are those believers who sit back—except those who are disabled—and those who strive in the path of Allah with their wealth and their lives, the verse.' He said: Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind man, stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is our sin? Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down [a revelation]. We said to the blind man: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is receiving revelation. He said: He remained standing, saying: O Allah, I repent to You. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, he said: 'Write: except those who are disabled.'"],[4922,"A man said to Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ: I know the most severe verse in the Book of Allah, Exalted is He. Umar ؓ raised his hand and struck him with a whip and said: Why did you search for it until you knew it? The man left. The next day, Umar ؓ said to him: The verse you mentioned yesterday? He said: Did you let me tell you about it? Umar ؓ said to him: I did not sleep last night. He said: O Commander of the Faithful, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it, the verse. None of us does evil except he is recompensed for it. Umar ؓ said to him: When it was revealed, neither food nor drink benefited us until Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, sent down after that and gave concession. He said: And whoever does evil or wrongs himself, then seeks forgiveness of Allah, he will find Allah Forgiving, Merciful."],[4923,"When Uthman ؓ was killed—and he mentioned a hadith in which: Then another stood up and asked him, meaning Ali ؓ: And if a woman fears from her husband contempt or evasion, there is no sin upon them if they make terms of peace between them. He ؓ said: 'About the like of this ask. It is a man who has two wives, and one of them becomes unable or is ugly, so he makes peace with her that he will come to her once every two or three nights.'"],[4924,"Al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwām ؓ brought a dispute with a man before the Messenger of God ﷺ. The man said, “He ruled in his favor only because he is his aunt’s son.” Then God Most High revealed: “But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in what arises between them…” (Q 4:65)."],[4925,"Al-Zubayr ؓ and a man brought a dispute to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ﷺ ruled in al-Zubayr’s favor. The man said, “He ruled in his favor only because he is his aunt’s son,” and he jabbed at him with his mouth. A Jew said, “Look at this one disparaging his prophet. We are more obedient than them: our prophet commanded us to kill ourselves, and we killed ourselves.”"],[4926,"“Killing in the path of God Most High expiates all sins except the trust (amānah). The martyr in the path of God, Mighty and Glorious, will be brought and it will be said: ‘Return your trust.’ He will say: ‘From where can I return it? The world has already passed away.’” He said: “Then it will be said: ‘Take him to the pit (al-hāwiyah).’ When he reaches the bottom of the pit, his trust will be made to appear before him in the form it had on the day it was lost. He will lift it and place it on his shoulder, then climb up through the Fire until he thinks he has emerged from it, but it will fall, and he will fall after it forever and ever.” Then ʿAbdullāh recited: “Indeed, God commands you to render trusts to their owners” (Q 4:58)."],[4927,"“When this verse was revealed: ‘They ask you for a ruling. Say: God gives you a ruling concerning the kālah’ (Q 4:176), the Prophet ﷺ was in his home. He looked and saw Ḥudhayfah ؓ, so he ﷺ recited it to him and Ḥudhayfah ؓ learned it. Then Ḥudhayfah ؓ looked and saw ʿUmar ؓ, so he recited it to him and he learned it. When ʿUmar ؓ became caliph, he wanted to judge concerning the kālah, so he met Ḥudhayfah ؓ and asked him about it. He said: ‘By God, I would be a fool if I thought your rule would burden me with a shackle and you say “teach it to me” — it is exactly what I told you.’ ʿUmar said: ‘May God have mercy on you, that is not what I meant.’ Ḥudhayfah said: ‘It was revealed to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he taught it to me, and I taught it to you just as he taught it to me. By God, I will never add anything to that.’”"],[4928,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us with this. :"],[4929,"“Fear God Most High and render the trust, for God, Mighty and Glorious, says: ‘And render trusts to their owners’ (Q 4:58).”"],[4930,"Ḍamrah b. Jundub left his home as an emigrant. He said to his family: “Carry me and take me out of the land of the polytheists to the Messenger of God ﷺ.” Then revelation came down: “And whoever leaves his home as an emigrant to God…” (Q 4:100)."],[4931,"I used to go regularly to Abū al-Dardāʾ ؓ and heard him narrating from the Prophet of God ﷺ that he said: “A messenger from my Lord, Mighty and Glorious, came to me and said: ‘And whoever does evil or wrongs himself, then seeks God’s forgiveness, will find God Forgiving, Merciful’ (Q 4:110). The verse before it had been hard on them: ‘Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it’ (Q 4:123). So I wanted to give glad tidings to my companions. I said: ‘O Messenger of God, even if he commits adultery and steals, then seeks God’s forgiveness, He will forgive him?’ He ﷺ said: ‘Yes.’ Then I said: ‘The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Yes, in spite of ʿUwaymir’s nose.’ Then Kaʿb b. Dhuhl ؓ said: ‘I saw Abū al-Dardāʾ ؓ tapping his own nose with his finger.’”"],[4933,"“Render to the allies their covenants that your oaths have bound.” They asked: “And what is their covenant, O Messenger of God?” He ﷺ said: “Paying blood-money on their behalf and supporting them.”"],[4934,"Moses ﷺ chose two men from each tribe, and they entered the city of the tyrants. Every people went out forbidding their own tribe from entering, except Joshua b. Nūn and Caleb b. Yūqannah."],[4935,"They wandered for forty years in an area of twelve parasangs. A stone the size of a bull’s head was placed among them. When they camped, twelve springs gushed from it, and when they set out, they loaded it on a bull and it held fast."],[4936,"“That they should enter upon them”"],[4937,"They wandered for twelve farsakhs for forty years. He made for them a stone like the head of an ox, carried on an ox. When they halted at a place, they would put it down, and Moses ﷺ would strike it, and twelve springs would gush forth from it. When they traveled, they would carry it on an ox, and the water would be held back."],[4938,"Regarding His saying, exalted is He: 'He said: Then it will be forbidden to them for forty years, they will wander in the land'—he said: It is forbidden for them to ever enter it, and they will wander in the land for forty years."],[4939,"He was with the Prophet ﷺ in his dwelling, and Surah al-Ma'idah was revealed to him. We knew it was revealed to him when the shoulder of his she-camel al-Adba' broke from the weight of the surah."],[4940,"I have not seen a people better than the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ. They asked him only thirteen questions until he passed away, all of them from the Quran."],[4941,"Regarding His saying, blessed and exalted is He: 'They are listeners to falsehood'—he said: meaning the Jews of Madinah. 'Listeners to another people'—he said: the people of Fadak who did not come to you, until the end of the verse."],[4942,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Musa ؓ: 'They are the people of this one,' meaning His saying: 'Then Allah will bring a people whom He loves and who love Him.'"],[4943,"When it was later revealed: 'And judge between them by what Allah has sent down,' the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Today we judge the Jews and the Christians, and others besides them among the religions.'"],[4944,"I asked Salman ؓ about this verse: 'That is because among them are qissisun (priests) and ruhban (monks).' He said: 'Leave the qissisun in the monasteries and ruins. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me to recite it: \"That is because among them are siddiqun (truthful ones) and ruhban.\"'"],[4945,"They are the monks in the monasteries and ruins—leave them there. Salman ؓ said: 'I recited to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"That is because among them are qissisun,\" and he taught me: \"That is because among them are siddiqun.\"'"],[4946,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us with this. :"],[4947,"They were with Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ when they mentioned this verse: 'Today I have perfected your religion for you.' A man from the Jews said ... the full hadith. Umar ؓ said: 'Allah, exalted is He, perfected the matter for us, so we know that after that the matter is in decline.'"],[4948,"The Prophet ﷺ recited Surah al-Ma'idah and Surah al-Tawbah in his sermon, then the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Permit what Allah has permitted in them and forbid what Allah has forbidden in them.'"],[4949,"When I heard people saying: \"Every beast of prey with a canine tooth is forbidden,\" I said: \"I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden to one who eats it...\" until the end of the verse. He said: \"Indeed a cooking pot in whose water there is yellowness, but that does not make it forbidden.\""],[4950,"He wrote to me—meaning Ibn 'Umar ؓ —\"We have neighbors from the Samaritans who read some of the Torah and the Gospel, but do not believe in the unseen. What do you think about their slaughtered animals?\" So he wrote to him: \"If they read some of the Torah and some of the Gospel, and they observe the Sabbath, then their slaughtered animals are like the slaughtered animals of the People of the Book.\""],[4951,"A man from the people of Fadak committed adultery. The people of Fadak wrote to some Jews in Madinah: \"Ask Muhammad about this. If he orders you to flog, then take it from him; but if he orders you to stone, then do not take it from him.\" So they asked him about it. He said: \"Send to me the two most learned men among you.\" They brought a one-eyed man called Ibn Suriya and another. The Prophet ﷺ said to them: \"Are you two the most learned of those before you?\" They said: \"Our people have inclined to that.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to them: \"Do you not have the Torah, which contains the ruling of Allah, Exalted is He?\" They said: \"Yes.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I adjure you by the One who parted the sea for Musa, shaded you with clouds, saved you from the people of Pharaoh, and sent down manna and quails upon the Children of Israel: What do you find in the Torah concerning stoning?\" One of them said to the other: \"We have never been adjured by anything like this.\" Then he said: \"We find that repeated looking is fornication, and embracing is fornication. If four witnesses testify that they saw him engaging in the act as a probe enters a kohl container, then stoning becomes obligatory.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"That is it.\" So he ordered him and he was stoned. Then the verse was revealed: \"So if they come to you, judge between them or turn away from them...\""],[4952,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us with this. :"],[4953,"Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Hurayrah asked Ibn 'Umar ؓ about many fish cast up by the sea. Ibn 'Umar ؓ said: \"Are they dead?\" He said: \"Yes.\" So he forbade him. He said: \"When he entered, he called for the Mushaf and recited: 'Lawful to you is the game of the sea and its food as provision.' He said: 'Its food is what comes out of it, so eat it; there is no harm. And everything in it may be eaten dead, whether it is in it or dead beside it.'\""],[4954,"\"The Negus sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a delegation from among his companions,\" the hadith. And the verse was revealed concerning them: \"You will surely find the most intense of people in animosity toward those who believe are the Jews and those who associate others with Allah; and you will surely find the nearest of them in affection to those who believe are those who say, 'We are Christians.' That is because among them are priests and monks, and they are not arrogant.\""],[4955,"Surah Al-An'am was revealed accompanied by a clamor of angels who had stretched the lowest heaven down to the earth. It is Makkan except two verses: \"Say, come, I will recite...\""],[4956,"He said to his companions: \"What do you say about these two verses: 'Indeed, those who say, \"Our Lord is Allah\" and then remain upright' and 'those who believe and do not mix their faith with wrongdoing'?\" They said: \"Those who say, 'Our Lord is Allah,' then act upon it, then remain upright upon His command.\" They said: \"And those who believe and do not mix their faith with wrongdoing—they have not sinned.\" He said: \"You have burdened it with something severe. 'Those who believe and do not mix their faith with wrongdoing'—he says: with shirk (associating partners with Allah). And 'those who say, \"Our Lord is Allah,\" then remain upright upon it'—they did not deviate from it by shirk or anything else.\""],[4957,"Concerning His saying, Exalted is He: \"And do not follow [other] paths, for they will separate you from His way.\" He said: \"Innovations and ambiguities.\""],[4958,"Some people came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"We have committed great sins.\" He did not think he replied to them. When they turned away, the verse was revealed: \"And when those who believe in Our verses come to you, say, 'Peace be upon you. Your Lord has prescribed mercy upon Himself...'\" So he called them ﷺ and recited it to them."],[4959,"Concerning His saying: \"And no leaf falls...\" He said: \"There is no tree on land or in the sea but that an angel is assigned to it who records every leaf that falls from it.\""],[4960,"\"Let a man beware lest he be from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in nothing. Then she recited: 'Indeed, those who have divided their religion and become sects—you are not [associated] with them in anything.'\""],[4961,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us with this. :"],[4962,"Al-Bazzar said: 'Ali b. al-Mundhir narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, something similar.\""],[4963,"Regarding His words, Blessed and Exalted: \"And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His countenance. You are not accountable for them in anything, nor are they accountable for you in anything, that you should drive them away and thus be of the wrongdoers\" (Qur'an 6:52). He said: Al-Aqra' b. Habis and 'Uyaynah b. Hisn al-Fazari ؓ came and found the Prophet ﷺ sitting with Bilal, Suhayb, Khabbab ؓ and some of the weak believers. When they saw them around him ﷺ, they despised them. They came to him and had a private audience with him ﷺ. They said: 'We would like you to make for yourself a special gathering with us, through which the Arabs will recognize our superiority. Indeed, we are the nobles of the Arabs; delegations come to you, and we feel ashamed that the Arabs should see us with these slaves. When we come to you, dismiss them from us; then when we have finished, seat them if you wish.' He ﷺ said: 'Yes.' They said: 'Then write for us a document to that effect.' So he ﷺ called for a parchment and called 'Ali ؓ to write, while we were sitting in a corner. Then Gabriel (peace and blessings be upon him) descended with His saying, Exalted: \"And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His countenance...\" up to His saying: \"...of the wrongdoers\" (Qur'an 6:52). Then He, Majestic and Exalted, said: \"And when those who believe in Our verses come to you, say: 'Peace be upon you. Your Lord has prescribed mercy upon Himself'\" (Qur'an 6:54). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the parchment from his hand, then called us, and we came to him while he ﷺ was saying: 'Peace be upon you. Your Lord has prescribed mercy upon Himself.' We drew near to him ﷺ until we placed our knees on his knee. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sit with us, and when he wanted to rise, he would rise and leave us. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \"And keep yourself patient with those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His countenance, and do not let your eyes pass beyond them, desiring the adornment of this worldly life\" (Qur'an 18:28). He said: So he sat with the nobles. \"And do not obey one whose heart We have made heedless of Our remembrance\" (Qur'an 18:28), referring to 'Uyaynah and al-Aqra', \"and who follows his own desire, and whose affair is ever in neglect\" (Qur'an 18:28) — meaning destruction. Then He struck for them the parable of two men and the parable of the life of this world. Thereafter, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sit with us, and when the time came for him to rise, we would rise and leave him; otherwise he ﷺ would remain patient forever until we rose.\""],[4964,"Abu Bakr said: Ahmad b. al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Asbat b. Nasr narrated to us, and he mentioned it in full. Ibn Majah also transmitted it from the route of 'Amr al-'Anqazi in abbreviated form.\""],[4966,"\"We indeed heard Allah say: 'Indeed, those who took the calf [for worship] will receive anger from their Lord and humiliation in the life of this world; and thus do We recompense the fabricators' (Qur'an 7:152).\" He said: \"And we do not see the people except that they have fabricated a lie; I think it will surely afflict them.\""],[4967,"Abu Qilabah recited this verse and said: 'By Allah, it applies to every fabricator until the Day of Resurrection — humiliation in the life of this world.'\""],[4968,"\"The seventy whom Moses selected from his people were seized by the earthquake because they did not forbid the calf and did not approve of it.\""],[4969,"\"Therein you will live, and therein you will die\" (Qur'an 7:25). He said: The earth — from it Allah Almighty created Adam, and in it they will be buried when they die, and from it they will be brought forth. The sky will rain for forty nights, and the dead will emerge from the earth.\""],[4970,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the People of the Heights (A'raf). He said: 'They are people who were killed in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, in disobedience to their fathers. Their being killed in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, kept them from the Fire, and their disobedience to their fathers kept them from Paradise.'\""],[4972,"Someone said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who are the People of the Heights?' He ﷺ said: 'People who went out in the path of Allah Almighty without the permission of their fathers, and were martyred. Their martyrdom kept them from entering the Fire, and their disobedience kept them from entering Paradise.'\""],[4973,"\"People who went out in the path of Allah Almighty without the permission of their fathers, and were martyred. Their martyrdom kept them from entering the Fire, and their disobedience kept them from entering Paradise.\" [Marfu' type]"],[4974,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about metamorphosis: does it produce offspring? He ﷺ said: 'No one was ever metamorphosed and had offspring or descendants.'\""],[4976,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a military expedition, and Allah Almighty granted it victory and success. Whoever brought something to him, he gave him a share of it after the fifth. Some men returned while others went ahead, took captives, and fought, leaving the spoils behind them and did not obtain any of the spoils. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what about men among us who went ahead and took captives, while other men stayed behind and did not engage in fighting, yet you gave them a share of the spoils?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent, then Jibril ﷺ came down with: 'They ask you about the spoils of war. Say: The spoils of war belong to Allah and the Messenger. So fear Allah and set things right among yourselves.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called them and said: 'Return what you have taken, and distribute it among yourselves with fairness and equality.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we have already spent and eaten.' He said: 'Then count that as your share.'"],[4977,"A man asked Ibn Abbas ؓ about the nafal (extra share of spoils). He said: 'The horse is from the nafal, and the salab (personal belongings of a slain enemy) is from the nafal.' The man repeated the question, and he said: 'This is like what happened with Sabigh, whom Umar ؓ beat.'"],[4978,"Regarding the words of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: 'And others besides them whom you do not know; Allah knows them' he said: 'They are the jinn.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Satan does not confuse anyone in a house that has a noble horse.'"],[4979,"We heard al-Zubayr ؓ reciting this verse: 'And fear a trial which will not strike those who have wronged among you exclusively.' He said: 'I recited this verse for a long time, and I did not think I was among its people, but now we have become among its people.'"],[4981,"'The last part of the Quran to be revealed was: There has certainly come to you a Messenger from among yourselves. Grievous to him is what you suffer; he is concerned over you and to the believers is kind and merciful.'"],[4982,"\"Verily, the last of the Quran to be revealed was: There has certainly come to you a Messenger from among yourselves; dear to him is what you suffer; he is keen over you; to the believers he is kind and merciful.\""],[4983,"\"Verily, the last of the Quran to be revealed was: There has certainly come to you a Messenger from among yourselves; dear to him is what you suffer; he is keen over you; to the believers he is kind and merciful.\""],[4984,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ passed by a man reciting: 'And the first forerunners among the Muhajirin and the Ansar' until he completed the verse. Umar ؓ said: 'Stop, stop. Who taught you this surah?' The man said: 'Ubayy b. Ka'b ؓ taught it to me.' Umar ؓ said: 'Do not leave me until we go to him.' He came and asked permission while Ubayy was reclining. He granted him permission, and Umar said: 'This man claims that you taught him such-and-such a verse,' and he recited it to him. Ubayy said: 'He is truthful.' Umar ؓ said to Ubayy: 'Did you receive it directly from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes.' Umar ؓ repeated three times, and each time Ubayy ؓ said: 'Yes.' Then he said: 'I bear witness that Allah Almighty revealed it to Muhammad ﷺ. Jibril (peace and blessings be upon him) brought it from Allah, Blessed and Exalted. He did not consult al-Khattab nor his son about it.' Umar ؓ went out saying: 'Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar.'"],[4985,"4928 4128 / 2 - Abu Ya'la said: Mahmud b. Khidash narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ubayd narrated to us: Talhah narrated to us with this."],[4986,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[4987,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the sa'ihin (those who wander or travel). He ﷺ said: 'They are the ones who fast.'"],[4988,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[4989,"A man from the hypocrites died, and I did not pray over him. Umar ؓ said: \"What prevented you from praying over him?\" I said: \"He was one of them.\" He said: \"Am I, by Allah, one of them?\" I said: \"No.\" He said: (Then he wept)."],[4990,"O Prophet, strive against the disbelievers and the hypocrites. He said: Striving against the disbelievers is with the sword, and striving against the hypocrites is with the tongue."],[4991,"I saw smoke in the mosque of opposition when it collapsed."],[4992,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[4993,"When this verse was revealed: \"And those who hoard gold and silver,\" it became burdensome upon the Muslims, and they said: \"None of us can leave for his child wealth that remains after him.\" He said: \"I will relieve you.\" So they set out, and Umar ؓ set out, and Thawban ؓ followed him, and he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Prophet of Allah, this verse has become burdensome upon your companions.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"We did not prescribe zakat except for what remains of your wealth, and inheritance was prescribed in wealth so that it remains after you.\" He said: So Umar ؓ said the takbir, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Shall I not tell you what is hoarded? The righteous woman: when he looks at her, she pleases him; when he commands her, she obeys him; and when he is absent from her, she protects him.\""],[4994,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[4995,"Abu Talhah ؓ recited this verse: \"Go forth, light and heavy, and strive with your wealth and your selves in the path of Allah.\" Then he said: \"I do not hear that Allah Almighty has given any excuse to anyone.\" Then he went out to Syria and remained there as a warrior until he died there."],[4996,"He spent the night dragging a rope on his back for two sa' of dates. I returned with one of them to my family, and I brought the other to the Prophet ﷺ to draw near to my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, with it. I informed him ﷺ of what had happened, and he said: \"Spread it in the mosque.\" The hypocrites said and mocked him: \"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, was surely in no need of the sa' of this poor man.\" Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: \"Those who criticize the volunteers...\" the verse."],[4998,"Whoever says one takbir in the path of Allah Almighty - and he mentioned the hadith, which has preceded in the virtue of jihad - he said: \"He will look at the Possessor of Majesty and Honor morning and evening, just as you see the sun without doubting its sight, and he will have honor and bliss as Allah, Glorified and Exalted, said: 'For those who do good is the best and an increase.' And he said: 'Those who do good' are those who said: 'There is no god but Allah.' And 'the best' is Paradise, and 'the increase' is looking at the face of Allah Almighty.\""],[4999,"He used to recite: \"In that, then, let them rejoice.\""],[5001,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[5002,"\"Hud and its sisters\":"],[5003,"\"Hud and its sisters\":"],[5004,"I heard al-Dahhak b. Qays reciting: “(You do with our wealth what You will).”"],[5006,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: “We relate to you the best of stories” [to the end of] the verse, he said: Allah (Exalted is He) sent down the Qur'an to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he recited it to them for a time. They said: “O Messenger of Allah, if only you would tell us stories?” So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent down: “Alif Lam Ra. These are the verses of the clear Book” up to His saying: “We relate to you the best of stories” [to the end of] the verse. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it to them for a time. They said: “O Messenger of Allah, if only you would speak to us?” So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: “Allah has sent down the best statement, a Book whose parts resemble each other” [to the end of] the verse. In all of that they were commanded with the Qur'an. Khallad said: Another added to it, saying: They said: “O Messenger of Allah, if only you would remind us?” So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: “Has the time not come for those who believe that their hearts should become humbly submissive at the remembrance of Allah” [to the end of] the verse."],[5008,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[5009,"Al-Bazzar also narrated it from al-Husayn b. al-Aswad and Isma'il b. Hafs, from 'Amr b. Muhammad, and he said: We do not know it from Sa'd except through this chain."],[5010,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[5011,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[5012,"Regarding His saying: “And she prepared for them a banquet,” he said: “Citron.”"],[5013,"Regarding His saying: “The king's cup,” he said: “It is the Persian measure (makkuk) from which non-Arabs drink, whose two ends meet.”"],[5014,"The cup (suwa') and the drinking vessel (siqaya) are one; it is the vessel from which one drinks."],[5015,"Yusuf (peace and blessings be upon him) was reproached for his saying: “Mention me to your master,” so Satan made him forget the remembrance of his Lord, and for his saying to his brothers: “Indeed, you are thieves.” They said: “If he steals, a brother of his stole before.” And he said: “That is so he may know that I did not betray him in secret.” Then Jibril (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: “Not even when you desired?” He said: “And I do not acquit myself” [to the end of] the verse."],[5017,"O Allah, if You have written us with You as wretched, then erase us and write us as felicitous; and if You have written us as felicitous, then confirm us, for You erase what You will and confirm, and with You is the Mother of the Book."],[5018,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[5019,"Regarding His saying (Exalted is He): \"Allah eliminates what He wills and confirms, and with Him is the Mother of the Book,\" he said: Allah (Mighty and Majestic is He) eliminates what He wills of things from the original [record], and He adds to it what He wills. I said to him: \"Who narrated this to you?\" He said: \"Abu Salih, from Ibn 'Abbas ؓ, from the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[5021,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[5022,"Allah (Mighty and Majestic is He) did not create and bring forth any soul more noble to Him than Muhammad ﷺ, and I have not heard Allah (Blessed and Exalted is He) swear by the life of anyone except by his life, for He said: \"By your life, indeed they were in their intoxication, wandering blindly.\""],[5024,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent 'Ammar b. Yasir ؓ to the well of the polytheists to draw water from it, and around it were three rows of guards protecting it. He drew water into his water-skins, then came forward until he reached the first row, and they seized him. He said: \"Leave me, for I am only drawing water for your companions.\" So they released him. Then he returned a second time, and they seized him and did the same to him, then released him. He went and returned again, and they seized him and did the same to him. When they tried to make him utter disbelief, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent the cavalry and they rescued him. Then this verse was revealed concerning him: \"Except him who is forced [to renounce his religion] while his heart is at peace with faith.\""],[5025,"'Abdullah ؓ recited: \"Indeed Mu'adh was an ummah, devoutly obedient to Allah, a hanif.\" Farwah b. Nawfal said: \"He forgot [the words] 'Indeed Ibrahim.'\" 'Abdullah ؓ said: \"I did not forget. We used to liken him to Ibrahim.\" And 'Abdullah ؓ was asked about \"ummah,\" and he said: \"A teacher of good.\" And he was asked about \"qanit,\" and he said: \"Obedient to Allah (Exalted is He) and His Messenger ﷺ.\""],[5026,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[5027,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."],[5029,"Allah (Mighty and Majestic is He) revealed this letter on the tongue of your Prophet ﷺ: \"And your Lord has enjoined [upon you] that you not worship except Him,\" but one of the two waws was attached to the other, so he recited for us: \"And your Lord has decreed that you not worship except Him. And had it been revealed as 'decreed,' no one would have associated anything with Him.\" Maymun used to say: \"Indeed, upon its interpretation there is light. Allah (Blessed and Exalted is He) said: 'He has ordained for you of religion what He enjoined upon Noah.'\""],[5030,"Regarding His saying (Mighty and Majestic is He): \"And We certainly gave Musa nine clear signs,\" he said: \"His hand, his staff, the years [of famine], the flood, the locusts, the lice, the frogs, the blood, and the decrease in fruits.\""],[5031,"Regarding His saying (Mighty and Majestic is He): \"And We certainly gave Musa nine clear signs,\" he said: \"The years [of famine]: He withheld rain from them, and the decrease in fruits, the flood, the locusts, the lice, the frogs, the blood, his staff, and his hand.\""],[5032,"Regarding His saying (Exalted is He): \"And do not recite [too] loudly in your prayer or [too] quietly,\" he said: \"They used to raise their voices in supplication: 'O Allah, have mercy on me.' When this verse was revealed, they were commanded not to whisper and not to raise their voices.\""],[5034,"A man does not become senile."],[5035,"A man does not become senile."],[5036,"Abu Abdullah al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abdullah b. Dawud narrated to us with this chain. : :"],[5037,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the sun when it set and said: 'In the intense fire of Allah. Were it not that it is restrained by the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, it would destroy everything on earth.'"],[5038,"Abu al-Darda' ؓ, when he narrated a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, would say: \"Like this or similar to it.\""],[5039,"And he found beside them a people – he said: A city with twelve thousand gates. Were it not for the voices of its inhabitants, people would hear the roar of the sun when it sets."],[5040,"A curtain, a structure. No building was ever erected in it, and no structure was ever built over them in it. When the sun rose, they entered their tunnels until the sun declined."],[5042,"The straitened livelihood which Allah, Exalted is He, mentioned is the punishment of the grave."],[5043,"Abu al-Samh informed him from Ibn Hujayrah, from Abu Hurayrah ؓ, and he mentioned something similar in the course of a hadith."],[5044,"Regarding His saying, Exalted is He: 'Ta-Ha' – meaning: 'O man,' and it is in Nabataean."],[5045,"When the calf lowed, they prostrated, and when it fell silent, they raised their heads."],[5046,"Regarding His saying, Exalted is He: 'lowing' – he said: It lowed once; it did not repeat. Do you not see that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'Does it not return to them any word?' And He, Majestic and Exalted, said: 'Do they not see that it does not speak to them nor guide them to a way?'"],[5047,"A guest came to the Prophet ﷺ, so he sent me to a Jew and said: 'Tell him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ says to you: Sell to us or lend us until Rajab.' I told him, and he said: 'By Allah, I will not sell to him or lend him except with a pledge.' I returned to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and he ﷺ said: 'By Allah, if he had sold to me or lent me, I would have repaid him. I am trustworthy in heaven, trustworthy on earth. Go with my iron armor.' So I went with it, and this verse was revealed as consolation to the Prophet ﷺ: 'And do not extend your eyes toward what We have given to pairs of them to enjoy.'"],[5049,"Whoever intends an evil deed and does not do it, nothing is recorded against him. Yet if he intends, even as far as Aden Abyan, to kill in the Sacred Mosque, Allah will make him taste a painful punishment. Then he recited: 'And whoever intends therein deviation by wrongdoing' (Quran 22:25)."],[5050,"Ibn Amr ؓ used to pitch two tents, one in the permitted area and one in the sacred precinct. He was asked, 'Why not stay with your cousin and family?' He replied, 'Makkah is Bakkah. We have been told that part of deviation therein includes saying: No, by Allah; and Yes, by Allah.'"],[5051,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about the people of a religion I had been with. He mentioned their prayer, fasting, and worship. Then the words of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, were revealed: 'Indeed, those who believe, and those who are Jews, and the Sabians, and the Christians, and the Magians' up to His words: 'a witness' (Quran 22:17)."],[5053,"I was writing this verse while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dictated it: 'And certainly We created man from an extract of clay' until he reached: 'Then We produced him as another creation' (Quran 23:12–14). Muadh b. Jabal ؓ said: 'So blessed is Allah, the best of creators.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed. He said to him: 'Why did you laugh?' He ﷺ replied: 'This verse was concluded as you said: So blessed is Allah, the best of creators.'"],[5054,"Regarding the words of Allah, Exalted is He: 'Our Lord, our wretchedness overcame us' (Quran 23:106), he said: 'The decree.'"],[5056,"I have sought this verse all my life and have not been able to find it: the words of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'And when you are told, \"Return,\" then return' (Quran 24:28). Indeed, when I ask permission to enter upon one of my brothers and he says, 'Return,' I do return, and I am content."],[5057,"Regarding the words of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'He sends the winds, and they stir up clouds, then He spreads them in the sky however He wills and makes them fragments' (Quran 30:48) — he said: 'Pieces, He puts some of them above others. Then you see the rain — meaning the downpour — coming out from its midst, from between them.'"],[5058,"I went out with Umm Mistah al-Ansariyyah ؓ for some need of ours. She stumbled and said, 'May Mistah perish!' I said, 'How bad is what you said about a man who accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' When my innocence was revealed, he ﷺ said, 'O A'ishah, rejoice.' My father and mother ؓ came to me and kissed me. I pushed their chests and said, 'Not by your praise nor by the praise of your companion. I praise Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for what He has excused me, declared my innocence, and how ill you thought of me, since you did not think good of yourselves.'"],[5060,"'A forbidden barrier' (Quran 25:22) — he said: 'When a woman saw something she disliked, she would say: Hijran (a barrier).'"],[5062,"Regarding the words of Allah, Exalted is He: 'In the cities, gathering' (Quran 26:36) — he said: 'The police.'"],[5063,"The Children of Israel entered Egypt as seventy-three persons and left it as six hundred thousand. Pharaoh said: 'Indeed, these are but a small band' (Quran 26:54)."],[5064,"Regarding the words of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'And your movement among those who prostrate' (Quran 26:219) — he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to see behind him in prayer just as he saw in front of him ﷺ.'"],[5065,"Al-Harith said: Muhammad b. Bakkar narrated to us, Abd Allah b. al-Mubarak narrated to us, with this chain."],[5066,"Al-Harith said: Muhammad b. Bakkar narrated to us, Abd Allah b. al-Mubarak narrated to us, with this chain."],[5067,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: \"Indeed, the One who imposed upon you the Qur'an will surely return you to a place of return\" – he said: \"His place of return is his hereafter.\""],[5069,"When it was revealed: \"Alif Lam Mim. The Romans have been defeated in the nearest land...\" the verse, some people met Abu Bakr ؓ and said: \"Do you not see your companion claiming that the Romans will defeat Persia?\" He ؓ said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ has spoken the truth.\" They said: \"Shall we make a bet with you on that?\" He said: \"Yes.\" Abu Bakr ؓ said: \"That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: 'What did you intend by this?' He said: 'O Messenger of God, I did it only to affirm God, Exalted is He, and His Messenger ﷺ.' He said: 'Then challenge them and make the stakes great, and set it for a few years. For if the years pass until the Romans prevail over Persia...' He said: 'Abu Bakr ؓ passed by them and said: 'Would you like to repeat? For repeating is better.' They said: 'Yes.' So they bet with him and increased the stakes. The years had not passed before the Romans prevailed over Persia, and he ؓ took the stakes and brought them to the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'This is for the noble camels.'"],[5071,"The Surah 'Alif Lam Mim Tanzil' and 'Tabarak' are preferred over every other Surah of the Qur'an by sixty good deeds."],[5072,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite every night: 'Tanzil as-Sajdah'."],[5074,"'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ found a mushaf in the lap of a servant boy of his, in which was: \"The Prophet is more worthy of the believers than their own selves, and he is a father to them, and his wives are their mothers.\" He said: \"Erase it, O boy.\" The boy said: \"I will not erase it, and it is in the mushaf of Ubayy b. Ka'b ؓ.\" 'Umar ؓ went to Ubayy b. Ka'b ؓ and said: \"The Qur'an has occupied me, and the trading in the markets has occupied you, when you display your millstone on your neck at the door of Ibn al-'Ajma'.\""],[5075,"Regarding His saying, Exalted is He: \"Their greeting on the day they meet Him is peace\" – he said: \"The day they meet the angel of death. There is no believer whose soul he takes except that he greets him.\""],[5076,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: 'Do not be like those who abused Musa, and Allah cleared him of what they said' — he said: Musa and Harun went up the mountain, and Harun died. The Children of Israel said: 'You killed him! He was more loving to us than you, and gentler to us than you.' So they abused him with that. Then Allah, Exalted is He, commanded the angels, and they carried him until they passed by the Children of Israel. The angels (peace be upon them) spoke of his death until the Children of Israel knew that he had died. Then they took him and buried him. No one of Allah's creation, Exalted is He, saw his grave except the vulture; so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, made it deaf and mute."],[5077,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ for eight months. Whenever he went out to prayer – or he said: \"the dawn prayer\" – he ﷺ would pass by the door of Fatimah ؓ and say: \"Peace be upon you, O people of the house. God only intends to remove from you the impurity, O people of the house, and to purify you thoroughly.\""],[5078,"I was stationed in Madinah for seven months during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: \"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ when dawn broke come to the door of 'Ali and Fatimah ؓ and say: 'Prayer, prayer. God only intends to remove from you the impurity, O people of the house, and to purify you thoroughly.'\""],[5079,"I accompanied the Messenger of God ﷺ for seven months. When morning came, he would come to the door of 'Ali and Fatimah ؓ and say: 'Prayer, may God have mercy on you. God only intends to remove from you the impurity, O people of the house...' the verse."],[5082,"I asked A'ishah ؓ about the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: \"Then We caused to inherit the Book those We have chosen of Our servants\" — to the end of the verse. She said to me: \"O my dear son, all of these are in Paradise. As for the foremost in good deeds: it is he who passed away during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bore witness for him to life and provision. As for the moderate: it is he who followed his trace from among his Companions until he joins him. As for the wrongdoer to himself: it is the like of me and the like of you.\" He (the narrator) said: So she placed herself ؓ among us."],[5084,"Whoever recites Ya-Sin in a night, he will enter the morning forgiven."],[5085,"Whoever recites Ya-Sin seeking thereby the Face of Allah, the Exalted, he will be forgiven. Whoever recites Ya-Sin, it is as if he recited the Qur'an twelve times. Whoever recites Ya-Sin while he is in the throes of death, Ridwan, the keeper of Paradise, will come with a drink from the drink of Paradise and give it to him while he is on his bed, so that he dies satiated and is resurrected satiated."],[5086,"Al-Harith said: Muhammad b. Bakkar narrated to us, Abd Allah b. al-Mubarak narrated to us, with this chain."],[5087,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"O 'Ali, recite Ya-Sin, for in Ya-Sin there are ten blessings: no hungry person recites it but he is filled, no thirsty person but he is given drink, no naked person but he is clothed, no unmarried person but he marries, no fearful person but he is secured, no prisoner but he is released, no traveler but he is helped in his journey, no one whose lost property is missing but he finds it, no sick person but he is cured, and it is not recited over a deceased person but it is lightened for him.\""],[5089,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: \"Gather those who did wrong and their kinds\" — he said: \"And their likes.\""],[5090,"A time came upon us when we did not know the meaning of this verse: \"They glorify Him in the evening and at sunrise\" — until we saw the people praying the Duha prayer."],[5091,"Regarding His saying, Majestic is His Majesty: \"[We subjected the wind to him, blowing gently] wherever he directed\" — he said: \"Ar-rukha' means obedient. As for 'wherever he directed,' he said: 'wherever he wished.'\""],[5093,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: \"And the eminent among them went forth, [saying]: 'Walk on and be patient with your gods'\" — he said: \"'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt.\""],[5094,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: \"We have not heard of this in the latter religion\" — he said: \"In Christianity.\""],[5095,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after the dawn prayer, and he said: \"Indeed, my Lord came to me tonight in the most beautiful form...\" — the hadith in full, and he added at its end: \"O Allah, I ask You for Your love, and the love of those who love You, and the love that will bring me to Your love.\""],[5096,"My Lord came to me in the best form. He said: 'O Muhammad.' I said: 'At Your service, my Lord, and at Your command.' He said: 'Do you know what the highest assembly disputes about?' I said: 'I do not know.' He said: 'Then He placed His hand on my chest, and I felt its coolness between my shoulders' – he said: 'Then He placed His hand between my shoulders, and I felt its coolness in my chest' – and said: 'O Muhammad.' I said: 'At Your service and at Your command.' He said: 'Do you know what the highest assembly disputes about?' I said: 'About degrees and expiations. As for degrees: performing ablution thoroughly in difficult circumstances, walking to congregational prayers, and waiting for the next prayer after the prayer. As for expiations: feeding others, spreading peace, and praying at night while people are asleep. Whoever does that lives well and becomes free of sins like the day his mother gave birth to him.' And He said to me: 'O Muhammad, say: O Allah, I ask You for good deeds, abandoning evil deeds, and love for the poor. And if You intend a trial for a people while I am among them, then take me to You without being tried.'"],[5098,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the interpretation of the words of the Most High: 'To Him belong the keys of the heavens and the earth.' He ﷺ said: 'No one asked me about it before you. Its interpretation is: There is no god but Allah, Allah is Most Great, glory be to Allah and praise be to Him, I seek forgiveness from Allah, and there is no power nor strength except with Allah, the First and the Last, the Outward and the Inward, and in His hand is all good; He gives life and causes death, and He has power over all things. Whoever says it ten times when he reaches the morning will be given ten qualities. The first: he will be guarded from Iblis and his armies. The second: he will be given a qintar of reward. The third: a degree will be raised for him in Paradise. The fourth: he will be married to houris with wide eyes. The fifth: twelve thousand angels will attend it. The sixth: he will have the reward of one who recited the Torah, the Gospel, the Psalms, and the Furqan. And with this, O Uthman, he will have the reward of one who performed Hajj and Umrah and whose Hajj and Umrah are accepted. And if he dies on that day, he will be sealed with the seal of the martyrs.'"],[5099,"Uthman b. Affan ؓ was asked about the keys of the heavens and the earth. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, Allah is Most Great – these are the keys of the heavens and the earth – and there is no power nor strength except with Allah, from the treasures of the Throne...'"],[5100,"He asked Jibril ﷺ about this verse: 'And the trumpet will be blown, and all who are in the heavens and all who are on the earth will fall dead, except whom Allah wills.' Who are those whom He did not will to fall dead? He said: 'They are the martyrs, girded with their swords around the throne of the Most Merciful. The angels will receive them on the Day of Resurrection to the gathering place on noble steeds of ruby, whose saddle blankets are softer than silk. Their stride is as far as the sight of men. They will travel in Paradise, and when the excursion is long, they will say: Let us go to our Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, to see how He judges between His creation. My God smiles at them, and when He smiles at a servant in any place, there is no reckoning upon him.'"],[5102,"Indeed, those who said: Our Lord is Allah, and then remained steadfast – he said: 'They are those who did not associate anything with Allah, the Mighty and Majestic.'"],[5103,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite a verse and then explain it, and I would not love to have the world and all it contains in exchange for it. He said: 'And whatever misfortune befalls you is because of what your own hands have earned, and He pardons much.' Then he said: 'Whoever Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, punishes for his sin in this world, Allah, the Glorious and Exalted, is too generous to repeat it for him in the Hereafter. And whatever Allah, the Most High, pardons in this world, Allah is too generous to pardon it in this world and then take it from him in the Hereafter.'"],[5104,"While Ali ؓ was talking with his companions, he said to them: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ...' then he stood up and did not explain. Then he turned, ؓ, and said: 'Do I not see you?' They said: 'We will not disperse until you explain to us what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.' So he ؓ said: 'And whatever misfortune befalls you is because of what your own hands have earned, and He pardons much. What Allah, the Most High, pardons will never return. And it is in Ha Mim 'Ain Sin Qaf.'"],[5105,"When the verse 'And give the relative his due right' was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Fatimah ؓ and gave her Fadak."],[5106,"Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ addressed us and said: 'You are the believers, and you are the people of Paradise. I hope that those of the Persians and Romans whom you befriend will enter Paradise. When one of them does a deed, you say: You have done well, may Allah have mercy on you. You have done well, may Allah bless you. And Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: And He answers those who believe and do righteous deeds and increases them from His bounty.'"],[5107,"People made too much of this verse: 'Say: I do not ask you any reward for it, except love for relatives.' So I wrote to Ibn Abbas ؓ, and Ibn Abbas ؓ wrote to me: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the central link of lineage in Quraysh; there was no clan of theirs but they had given birth to him. So Allah, the Most High, revealed: 'Say: I do not ask you any reward for it, except affection for what I call you to, except that you love me because of my kinship with you and preserve me for that.'"],[5108,"Abu Yala said: Abu Hammam narrated to us, Muawiyah b. Amr narrated to me, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us with it."],[5109,"When Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ camped at al-Jabiyah, he said to Mu'adh ؓ: 'O Mu'adh, what is the firm handle of this matter?' He said: 'I said: Sincerity, O Commander of the Faithful, and obedience. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Three things, whoever does them has committed a crime: whoever raises a banner unjustly, or disobeys his mother, or walks with an oppressor to support him has committed a crime. Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, says: We will take retribution from the criminals.'"],[5110,"And it is indeed knowledge of the Hour—he said: the descent of Jesus son of Mary."],[5111,"Whoever recites al-Dukhan on the night of Friday will be forgiven."],[5112,"And Abu Ya‘la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. :"],[5113,"And Abu Ya‘la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. :"],[5114,"[Chain of narration]"],[5115,"When 'Abd Allah b. Salam ؓ wanted to embrace Islam, he entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah, sent with guidance and the religion of truth, and that the Jews find you described in the Torah among them.' Then he said to him, 'Send for a group of Jews—so-and-so and so-and-so'—and he named them for him—'and hide me in a room. Ask them about me and my father, for they will inform you. Then I will come out to them and bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah, sent with guidance and the religion of truth, perhaps they will become Muslims.' So the Prophet ﷺ did that: he hid him in his house, sent for the group he had commanded, and called them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, 'What is 'Abd Allah b. Salam among you? And what was his father?' They said, 'Our master and the son of our master, our scholar and the son of our scholar.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do you think if he becomes Muslim you will become Muslims?' They said, 'He will not become Muslim.' He ﷺ said, 'What do you think if he becomes Muslim?' They said, 'He will not become Muslim.' He said, 'What do you think if he becomes Muslim?' They said, 'He will never become Muslim.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him, and he came out to them and said, 'I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah, sent with guidance and the religion of truth, and they know about you what I know.' The Jews said to 'Abd Allah ؓ, 'We never feared this from you, O 'Abd Allah.' He said, 'So they left him, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed concerning that: \"Say: I am not an innovation among the messengers, nor do I know what will be done with me or with you. I follow only what is revealed to me, and I am only a clear warner.\" Say, \"Have you considered: if it is from Allah and you disbelieve in it, and a witness from the Children of Israel bears witness to its like and believes…\" (Q. 46:9-10).'"],[5116,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when he was expelled from Makkah: 'I am leaving you, and I know that you are the best of the lands of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and the most honored to Him. Had your people not expelled me from you, I would not have left. O Banu 'Abd Manaf, if you are the guardians of this matter after me, do not prevent any circumambulator of the House of Allah, Exalted be He, from it for even an hour of night or day.'"],[5117,"And Abu Ya‘la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. :"],[5118,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left Makkah toward the cave, he looked at Makkah and said, 'You are the most beloved of Allah's lands to me, and had your people not expelled me from you, I would not have left you. The most hostile of enemies is one who transgresses against Allah, Exalted be He, in His sanctuary, or kills someone other than his killer, or kills for a vendetta of the pre-Islamic era.' He said, 'So Allah revealed to His Prophet ﷺ: \"And how many a town, stronger in might than your town which expelled you, have We destroyed\" (Q. 47:13).'"],[5119,"The Prophet ﷺ was teaching a young man to recite, and he recited: 'Do they not reflect upon the Quran, or are there locks upon their hearts?' The young man said, 'Upon them are locks until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, opens them.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'You have spoken the truth.' Then some people from Yemen came to him and asked him to write a letter for them. He ordered 'Abd Allah b. al-Arqam ؓ to write a letter for them, and he wrote it and brought it to them. He said, 'You have done well.' 'Umar ؓ thought that he would be in charge of something of the people's affairs. When 'Umar ؓ became caliph, he asked about the young man, and they said, 'He was martyred.' 'Umar ؓ said, 'The Prophet ﷺ said such-and-such, and the young man said such-and-such, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"You have spoken the truth.\" So I knew that Allah would guide him.' And 'Umar ؓ appointed 'Abd Allah b. al-Arqam ؓ over the treasury."],[5120,"Regarding His words, Exalted be He: 'You will be called to a people of great might; you will fight them or they will submit. If you obey, Allah will give you a good reward; but if you turn away as you turned away before, He will punish you with a painful punishment.' He said: 'Persia and Rome.'"],[5121,"And Abu Ya‘la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. :"],[5122,"I came to Ibrahim al-Nakha'i and said: A man has disputed with me, called Sa'd al-'Anazi. Ibrahim said: He is not al-'Anazi, but rather al-Zubaydi. Concerning the saying of the Exalted: 'The bedouins say, \"We believe.\" Say, \"You have not believed, but say, 'We have submitted'\" (49:14), he said: It is submission. Ibrahim said: No, rather it is Islam."],[5123,"And Abu Ya‘la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. :"],[5124,"And Abu Ya‘la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. :"],[5125,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray two rak'ahs before 'Asr. A delegation of Banu al-Mustaliq came to him, and he had sent al-Walid b. 'Uqba to collect the zakah of their wealth after the battle. When they heard of that, some of them rode out and said: We will honor the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, guide him through the land, and speak with him. When he heard of them, he returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, Banu al-Mustaliq have withheld their zakah. When they heard that he had returned, they followed his tracks until they arrived in Madinah. They prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the first row of the first prayer. When he said the salam, they said: We seek refuge in Allah and His Messenger from His anger and the anger of His Messenger. They continued to apologize until the mu'adhdhin came for the 'Asr prayer. Then Allah, the Exalted, revealed: 'O you who believe, if a disobedient person comes to you with information, verify it, lest you harm a people out of ignorance' (49:6)."],[5126,"Then 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ lay down on his back in one of the walled gardens of Madinah, placing one leg over the other. The Jews used to fabricate lies about Allah, Mighty and Majestic, saying that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, finished creation on the Sabbath and then rested. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'And We certainly created the heavens and the earth and what is between them in six days, and no fatigue touched Us' (50:38). Some people used to dislike placing one leg over the other until 'Umar did it."],[5127,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'And the tall palm trees having layered spathes' (50:10), he said: 'Al-basiqat' means tall, and 'al-nadid' means piled one upon another."],[5128,"I asked him – meaning the Prophet ﷺ – about: 'and at the passing of the stars' (52:49)? He said: The passing of prostration is the two rak'ahs after Maghrib, and the passing of the stars is the two rak'ahs before dawn."],[5129,"Regarding the saying of the Exalted: 'So turn away from them, for you are not to blame' (51:54), he said: 'Ali ؓ said: No verse was revealed that was harder on us or greater on us than it. We said: This is nothing but displeasure or hatred, until it was revealed: 'And remind, for indeed, the reminder benefits the believers' (51:55). He said: Remind with the Qur'an."],[5130,"'Ali ؓ came out to us with a cloak wrapped around his head, and he was covered with a khamisa. He said: When it was revealed to us: 'So turn away from them, for you are not to blame' (51:54), it was hard on the companions of the Prophet ﷺ. None of us remained except that he feared destruction, since the Prophet ﷺ was commanded to turn away from them, until it was revealed: 'And remind, for indeed, the reminder benefits the believers' (51:55); then our souls were at ease."],[5131,"That grieved us, and we said: The Prophet ﷺ has been commanded to turn away from us, until it was revealed."],[5132,"I said: Al-Haytham b. Kulayb narrated it in his Musnad from Isma'il b. Ishaq al-Qadi, from Sulayman b. Harb, from Hammad b. Zayd with it, and more completely. And the hadith of Mujahid from 'Ali ؓ is with Ahmad in his Musnad for a different hadith."],[5133,"When Uthman ؓ was killed, that terrified me greatly, and the drawing of the sword among us was a grave matter. I sat in my house, but I had a need, so I set out to the market. There I saw about forty men sitting in the shade of the palace, and a chain had been stretched across the door. I said: I will enter. I went to enter, but the doorman prevented me. The people said to him: Leave him, woe to you. I went in, and there were the nobles of the people, and a cushion. Then Ali ؓ came, a handsome man in his robe, with no shirt or turban. He greeted and sat down. He did not disapprove of anyone among the people except me. He said ؓ: Ask me about whatever you wish, but do not ask me except about what benefits and does not harm. A man said to him: What did you say, so that we would love to tell you and then ask you? He said: Ask me about whatever you wish. He said: By those that scatter with a scattering? He said ؓ: Will you not ask about something other than this? He said: I ask you about what I want. He said ؓ: The winds. He said: What about those that bear a load? He said ؓ: The clouds. He said: What about those that run with ease? He said ؓ: The ships. He said: What about those that distribute a command? He said ؓ: The angels."],[5134,"It is the man who has two wives, and one of them is unable or is ugly, so he makes a settlement with her that he will come to her once every two or three nights. (mawquf)"],[5135,"While the people were with Ali ؓ one day, they found him in a good mood, so they said: Tell us about your companions, O Commander of the Believers... and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then Abdullah b. al-Kawwa' al-A'war, a man from Banu Bakr b. Wa'il, stood up and said: O Commander of the Believers, what are those that scatter with a scattering? He mentioned something similar, and he added regarding: By the sky with its adornment? He said: Having excellent creation. He also added: Do not return to such a thing; do not ask me about such a thing."],[5136,"When it was revealed: So by the Lord of the heaven and the earth, it is certainly true, just as [it is true] that you speak, men went out with sticks in their hands and said: Where are those who burdened our Lord so much that He swore an oath?"],[5137,"Another stood up and said: Tell me about what I ask you. He said: Ask me about what benefits and does not harm. He said: What is the elevated roof? He said: The sky. He said: What is the frequented house? Ali ؓ said to his companions: What do you say? They said: This house is the Kaaba. He said: No, but it is a house in the sky opposite the Sacred House, called al-Durah. Its sanctity in the sky is like the sanctity of this one on earth. Seventy thousand angels enter it every day, then do not return to it."],[5138,"Abu Hurayrah ؓ was asked about this verse, while he was present: Those who avoid major sins and immoralities except al-lamam. He said ؓ: It is the look, the wink, the kiss, and the touching. When the two circumcised parts meet, that is fornication, and the major ablution becomes obligatory."],[5139,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ recited [Sūrat] al-Najm and prostrated, then stood and recited another surah."],[5140,"And Abu Ya‘la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. :"],[5141,"And you are samidun—he said: They would pass by the Prophet ﷺ haughtily. Have you not seen how the stallion struts proudly?"],[5142,"When it was revealed: The host will be defeated and they will turn their backs—the verse—I kept saying: Which host will be defeated? Then on the Day of Badr, I saw the Prophet ﷺ leaping in his armor, saying: The host will be defeated and they will turn their backs. Then I knew that it was that."],[5144,"Regarding His words, exalted is He: The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split—he said ؓ: The splitting of the moon happened in Makkah."],[5145,"The host will be defeated and they will turn their backs—he said: On the Day of Badr."],[5146,"And regarding His saying, exalted is He: \"So it will be an inevitable event\" — he said: \"The Day of Badr.\""],[5147,"Previously mentioned regarding its virtue is the hadith of 'Ali ؓ in the book of manners, in the chapter: What to say when a dog barks at him. [4472, 3739/1] Abu Bakr said: Al-Hasan b. Musa narrated to us."],[5148,"And Abu Ya‘la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. :"],[5149,"And Abu Ya‘la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. :"],[5150,"\"Fair ones, confined in pavilions\" — he said: \"Hollowed pearls.\""],[5152,"And Abu Ya‘la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. :"],[5153,"Regarding His saying, exalted is He: \"And banana trees layered [with fruit]\" — he said: \"Bananas.\""],[5154,"Regarding the saying of Allah, mighty and majestic is He: \"Indeed, We have produced them in a [new] creation and made them virgins, loving, of equal age\" — he said: \"Among them are those who were previously married and those who were not.\""],[5155,"Regarding His saying, mighty and majestic is He: \"A large company of the former peoples and a few of the later peoples\" — he said: \"Both groups are from this nation.\""],[5156,"Musaddad said: Khaqan b. 'Abd Allah b. al-Ahtam narrated to us, from 'Ali b. Zayd, from 'Uqbah b. Suhban, from Abu Bakrah ؓ , from the Prophet ﷺ, with it."],[5157,"And Abu Ya‘la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. :"],[5158,"In the Book of God there is a verse that no one before me acted upon, and no one after me will act upon: the verse of confidential talk: 'O you who believe, when you consult the Messenger in private, offer something in charity before your private consultation...' to the end of the verse. He said: I had a dinar which I sold for ten dirhams, and I consulted the Prophet ﷺ privately. Each time I consulted him, I offered a dirham in charity before my private talk. Then it was abrogated, and no one acted upon it. Then it was revealed: 'Are you afraid to offer charities before your private consultation?' to the end of the verse."],[5159,"Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated it from Abdullah b. Idris from Layth with it. I said: Al-Tirmidhi narrated it through the route of Ali b. Alqamah from Ali ؓ with a different wording."],[5160,"There was a monk who worshiped in a hermitage. A woman had brothers, and something happened to her, so they brought her to him. She adorned herself for him, and he had intercourse with her, and she became pregnant. Satan came to him and said: Kill her, for if they find out about you, you will be disgraced. So he killed her and buried her. They came to him and took him and went away with him. While they were walking with him, Satan came to him and said: I am the one who adorned her for you, so prostrate to me once and I will save you. So he prostrated to him. That is the saying of the Almighty: 'Like the example of Satan when he says to man: Disbelieve; but when he disbelieves, he says: I am free of you.'"],[5161,"A man from the Muslims passed by while fasting for three days, walking, and he could not find anything to break his fast with, so he would wake up fasting. Finally, a man from the Ansar named Thabit b. Qays ؓ noticed him. He said to his family: Tonight I will bring a guest. When you put out your food, let one of you go to the lamp as if to fix it, and let him extinguish it. Then strike your hands toward the food as if you are eating, but do not eat until our guest is full. When evening came, he brought him, and they put out their food. His wife went to the lamp as if to fix it, and she extinguished it. Then they began striking their hands in the food as if eating, but they did not eat, until their guest was full. Their food that night was only a loaf of bread, which was their sustenance. When morning came, Thabit ؓ went to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: O Thabit, God Almighty was amazed last night at you and your deed. He said: Then this verse was revealed about him: 'And they prefer others over themselves even though they are in need.'"],[5162,"Regarding the saying of the Blessed and Exalted: 'And the foremost, the first of the Emigrants,' he said: Those who prayed toward both qiblahs with the Prophet ﷺ."],[5163,"And Abu Ya‘la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. :"],[5164,"Regarding the saying of the Almighty: 'And they will not disobey you in what is right,' he said: It refers to wailing."],[5165,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ embraced Islam, while his wife remained behind among the polytheists. So the Mighty and Majestic revealed: 'And do not hold on to the bonds of disbelieving women'—meaning: if a man embraces Islam and his wife refuses, then he may marry, if he wishes, up to four other women."],[5166,"Ibn Abbas ؓ was asked: How did the Messenger of God ﷺ test women? He said: When a woman came to him to embrace Islam, he ﷺ would make her swear by God: You did not leave out of hatred for your husband; by God, you did not leave seeking worldly gain; by God, you did not leave out of desire for one land over another; by God, you left only out of love for God Almighty and His Messenger ﷺ."],[5167,"«Every person has three friends. As for one friend, he says: “What you spend is yours, and what you hold back is not yours”—that is his wealth. As for another friend, he says: “I am with you, but when you reach the king’s door, I will leave you and return”—that is his family and servants. As for another friend, he says: “I am with you wherever you enter and wherever you leave”—that is his deeds. Then he will say: “You were the least of the three in my esteem”»"],[5168,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ divorced his wife Qutaylah in the pre-Islamic era; she is the mother of Asma' bint Abi Bakr ؓ. She came to them during the truce period between the Messenger of God ﷺ and the disbelievers of Quraysh. She gave Asma' bint Abi Bakr ؓ earrings and other things as a gift. Asma' disliked accepting from her until she went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him. Then God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'God does not forbid you from those who have not fought you because of religion.'"],[5169,"\"I fear for you in the trial of prosperity more than I fear for you in the trial of adversity. You were tested with the trial of adversity and you were patient, and indeed the world is green and sweet.\" Type: Marfu'."],[5170,"Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah wrote a letter to the people of Makkah. God Almighty informed His Prophet ﷺ, so he ﷺ sent Ali and al-Zubayr ؓ in pursuit of the letter. They caught up with the woman on a camel and extracted it from her braids. They brought it to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He sent for Hatib and said: O Hatib, did you write this letter? He said: Yes. He ﷺ said: What prompted you to do that? He said: O Messenger of God, by God, I am sincere to God Almighty and His Messenger ﷺ, but I was a stranger among the people of Makkah, and my family was among them, and I feared for them; so I wrote a letter that will not harm God and His Messenger at all, and perhaps it may benefit my family. Umar ؓ said: I drew my sword and said: O Messenger of God, let me deal with Hatib, for he has disbelieved, and let me strike his neck. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: O Ibn al-Khattab, what do you know? Perhaps God looked upon the people of Badr and said: Act as you wish, for I have forgiven you."],[5171,"Abdullah b. Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul said to his father: By God, you will never enter Madinah until you say: The Messenger of God is the most honorable, and I am the lowliest. He said: Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, it has reached me that you intend to kill my father. By the One who sent you with the truth, I have never looked at his face out of awe of him, and if you wish me to bring you his head, I will bring it to you; but I hate to see the killer of my father."],[5172,"When this verse in Surat al-Baqarah about the waiting periods of women was revealed, they said: 'There remain waiting periods of women that have not been mentioned: the young, the old whose menstruation has ceased, and those who are pregnant.' So Allah revealed the verse in the shorter Surat al-Nisa': 'And those of your women who have despaired of menstruation, if you doubt, their waiting period is three months, and those who have not menstruated, and those who are pregnant, their term is until they deliver their burden.'"],[5173,"Regarding His saying: 'And they should not go out unless they commit a clear indecency' - he said: 'The clear indecency is that she behaves foolishly toward her family. If she does that, it is lawful for them to expel her.'"],[5174,"When Abu Bakr ؓ swore that he would not spend on Mistah ؓ, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'Allah has ordained for you the dissolution of your oaths.' So he dissolved his oath and spent on him."],[5175,"Regarding the saying of the Exalted: 'a sincere repentance' - he said: 'He repents from the sin, then does not return to it.'"],[5176,"Pharaoh drove four pegs for his wife into her hands and her feet. When they dispersed from her, the angels released her, and she said: 'My Lord, build for me a house in Paradise near You.' He said: So her house in Paradise was revealed to her."],[5178,"He said to a man: 'Shall I delight you with a hadith that will make you happy?' He said: 'Yes, O Abu 'Abbas, may Allah have mercy on you.' He said ؓ: 'Recite: \"Blessed is He in whose hand is the dominion\" and memorize it, and teach it to your family, all your children, the children of your household, and your neighbors; for it is the deliverer, and it is the disputer: it will dispute and argue on the Day of Resurrection before its Lord for its reciter, and it will ask its Lord to save him from the Fire when it is in his heart, and Allah, the Exalted, will save its companion thereby from the punishment of the grave.' Ibn 'Abbas ؓ said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I wish that it were in the heart of every person of my nation.'"],[5180,"'On the Day when a shin shall be uncovered' - he said: 'A great light, before which they fall down prostrating.'"],[5181,"Regarding the saying of the Exalted: 'And above them eight will bear the Throne of your Lord that Day' - he said: 'They are four angels carrying it on their shoulders. Each of them has four faces: a face of a bull, a face of a lion, a face of an eagle, and a face of a man. Each of them has four wings: two wings are over his face, for fear that he might look at the Throne and be struck down, and two wings with which they rise. They have no speech except: \"Glorify Allah, the Strong, the Most High. His greatness has filled what is between the heavens and the earth.\"'"],[5183,"Regarding the saying of the Blessed and Exalted: 'It scorches the skin' - he said: 'The flesh of the shins.'"],[5184,"He said to Ibn Mas'ud ؓ: 'I was told that you were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the jinn?' He said: 'Yes.' Then he mentioned the hadith similarly - meaning similar to the hadith of 'Alqamah - and he said: 'He drew a line for me and said: \"Do not leave.\" When he came, he said to me: \"If you had gone out of the line, I would not have been safe from some of them snatching you away.\" And he said: \"The jinn disputed about a slain person among them, and judgment was passed between them with truth.\" And he said: \"I saw them girding themselves with some garments.\" And he said: \"They are the jinn of Nusaybin; they asked him for provisions.\""],[5185,"The Prophet ﷺ set out, and I set out with him until he reached the open desert. Then he drew a line for me and said: 'Do not leave until I return to you.' He ﷺ did not come until dawn came. Then he ﷺ said: 'I was sent to the jinn.' I said: 'What are these sounds that I hear?' He ﷺ said: 'They are their voices when they bade me farewell and greeted me.'"],[5186,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: \"And recite the Qur'an with measured recitation,\" he said: \"Make it clear, distinctly.\""],[5187,"Anas b. Malik ؓ recited this verse: \"Indeed, the night rising is more intense in tread and more upright in speech.\" A man said to him: \"We only recite it: 'and more upright in speech.'\" He said: \"'More upright,' 'more correct,' 'more apt' and the like are all one.\""],[5188,"When it was revealed: \"And leave Me with the deniers, possessors of ease, and allow them respite a little\" – it was only a short while until the Battle of Badr occurred."],[5189,"While Ibn Abbas ؓ was sitting by the well of Zamzam and the people were asking him questions, a man came and asked him about: \"And the night when it departs.\" He remained silent. When the muezzin called the second call to prayer – or the caller called out – he said: \"Where is the one asking about: 'the night when it departs'?\" He said: \"The night has departed.\""],[5190,"We were in the house of A'ishah when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and said: \"There are no two Muslims who lose three children, young ones who have not reached the age of accountability, but they will be brought and made to stand at the gate of Paradise. It will be said to them: 'Enter Paradise, you and your parents.'\" That is His saying, Exalted: \"So the intercession of intercessors will not benefit them.\" Then he added: \"The intercession of their children benefited the parents.\""],[5191,"\"And the winds that blow violently\" – the winds."],[5192,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: \"And We sent down from the rain-laden winds water pouring forth,\" he ؓ said: \"The rain-laden winds are the winds. 'Water pouring forth' means: flowing abundantly.\""],[5193,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: \"They will abide therein for ages,\" he said: \"A 'huqb' is a thousand months, a month is thirty days, a year is three hundred and sixty days, a day is a thousand years of what you count, and 'hiqab' is thirty thousand thousand years.\""],[5194,"He said: \"And what are the runners that hide?\" He said: \"The planets.\""],[5195,"I heard Umar ؓ while he was on the pulpit saying: \"And when the souls are paired,\" he said: \"Their pairing is that every people will be joined with their like.\""],[5196,"I prayed the night prayer behind Umar ؓ, and he recited: \"When the sky is split apart,\" and he prostrated during it."],[5197,"\"You will surely ride stage upon stage,\" he said – meaning your Prophet ﷺ – he says: \"State after state.\""],[5198,"I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ and I heard him say: 'Does he think that no one will ever have power over him? Does he think that no one sees him?'"],[5199,"A puppy entered the house of the Prophet ﷺ and went under the bed and died. The Messenger of God ﷺ remained four days without revelation coming to him. He ﷺ said: 'O Khawlah, what has happened in the house of the Messenger of God ﷺ? Gabriel ﷺ is not coming to me. What has happened in the house of the Prophet of God ﷺ?' She ؓ said: 'O Prophet of God, no day has passed for us better than today.' She said: 'Then the Messenger of God ﷺ took his two cloaks and put them on and went out. I said to myself: If only I could tidy the house and sweep it. I reached with the broom under the bed, and there was something heavy. I kept moving it until the dead puppy appeared to me. I took it with my hand and threw it behind the house. Then the Prophet ﷺ came, his beard trembling—and he ﷺ would tremble inwardly when revelation descended—and he ﷺ said: 'O Khawlah, cover me.' Then God, Mighty and Majestic, sent down upon him: 'By the morning brightness and the night when it covers with darkness, your Lord has not forsaken you, nor does He hate you'—up to His saying: 'and you will be satisfied.' He ﷺ got up from his sleep, and I placed water for him, and he performed ablution and put on his two cloaks."],[5200,"While Abu Bakr ؓ was eating lunch with the Messenger of God ﷺ, this verse was revealed: 'So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it.' Abu Bakr ؓ stopped and said: 'O Messenger of God, will we see every evil we have done?' He ﷺ said: 'What you see of things you dislike, that is your recompense for them, and the good is deferred for its people in the Hereafter.'"],[5202,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us... and he mentioned a very long hadith, in which he said: 'Whoever withholds the ma'un (small kindnesses) from his neighbor when he needs it, God will withhold His bounty from him on the Day of Resurrection and leave him to himself. And whoever is left to himself will perish in the end, and no excuse will be accepted from him.'"],[5203,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: 'O Jubayr, would you like, when you go out on a journey, to be among the best of your companions in appearance and the most provisioned?' I said: 'Yes, by my father and mother.' He ﷺ said: 'Then recite these five surahs: \"Say: O disbelievers,\" \"When the help of God and victory comes,\" \"Say: He is God, the One,\" \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the dawn,\" and \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.\" Begin each surah with \"In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,\" and end your recitation with \"In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.\"' Jubayr ؓ said: 'I was wealthy, with much property, and I would go out on a journey and be among the worst of them in appearance and the least provisioned. But since the Messenger of God ﷺ taught me these and I recited them, I have been among the best of them in appearance and the most provisioned, until I return from my journey.'"],[5204,"I heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ more than twenty times, saying: 'What excellent surahs are these two which I recited in the two rak'ahs: \"The One, the Eternal\" and \"Say: O disbelievers.\"'"],[5205,"Shall I not guide you to a word that will save you from associating partners with God, Blessed and Exalted? Recite \"Say: O disbelievers\" when you go to sleep."],[5206,"This surah was revealed to the Messenger of God ﷺ in the middle of the days of Tashriq at Mina, while he ﷺ was on the Farewell Pilgrimage: 'When the help of God and victory comes'—until he completed it. And the Messenger of God ﷺ knew that it was the farewell."],[5207,"And Abd b. Humayd said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and he mentioned it in full. 1134/3 - Abu Ya'la also narrated it from another route, from Musa."],[5208,"And Abu Ya'la said: Zuhayr—he is Ibn Harb—narrated to us; Buhlul—he is Ibn Muwarriq—narrated to us; Musa b. 'Ubaydah narrated to us; Sadaqah b. Yasar and 'Abd Allah b. Dinar narrated to me from 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar ؓ with its full length."],[5209,"When 'Perish the hands of Abu Lahab, and perish he' was revealed, the one-eyed Umm Jamil bint Harb came, wailing, with a stone in her hand, saying: 'We reject Muzammam, we hate his religion, we disobey his command.' The Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting in the mosque, reciting Qur'an, and Abu Bakr ؓ was with him. He said: 'O Messenger of God, she is coming, and I fear she may see you.' He ﷺ said: 'She will not see me,' and he ﷺ recited Qur'an, seeking protection through it, as God, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'And when you recite the Qur'an, We place between you and those who do not believe in the Hereafter a hidden barrier.' She came and stood by Abu Bakr ؓ, and did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ. She said: 'O Abu Bakr, I have been told that your companion has satirized me.' He ؓ said: 'No, by the Lord of this House, he has not satirized you.' She turned away, saying: 'Quraysh knows that I am the daughter of its chief.' He said: Al-Walid said in his hadith, or someone else said: 'Umm Jamil stumbled while circumambulating the House in her cloak, and she said: 'May Muzammam perish.' Umm Hakim bint 'Abd al-Muttalib said: 'I am chaste, so I am not spoken to; I am knowledgeable, so I am not taught; we are both from the cousins, and Quraysh after him knows best.'"],[5210,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Musa al-Harawi Ishaq b. Ibrahim narrated to us; Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Walid b. Kathir, from Ibn Tadrus, from Asma' ؓ with its full length."],[5211,"When [the verse] 'Perish the hands of Abu Lahab, and perish he' was revealed, the wife of Abu Lahab came to the Prophet ﷺ while Abu Bakr ؓ was with him. When Abu Bakr ؓ saw her, he said, 'O Messenger of God, she is a foul-mouthed woman, and I fear that she may harm you. Would you please leave?' He ﷺ said, 'She will not see me.' She came and said, 'O Abu Bakr, your companion has satirized me.' He ؓ said, 'He does not say poetry.' She said, 'You are believed in my eyes,' and left. I said, 'O Messenger of God, she did not see you.' He ﷺ said, 'An angel kept shielding me with his wing.'"],[5212,"And al-Bazzar said: 'Ibrahim b. Sa'id al-Jawhari and Ahmad b. Ishaq narrated to us, they said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us with it.' [The matn is incomplete.]"],[5213,"Is one of you unable to recite a third of the Quran before going to sleep? It was said, 'O Messenger of God, who can manage a third of the Quran before sleeping?' He ﷺ said, 'He recites: \"Say: He is God, the One,\" and \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak,\" and \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind\"—it is as if he has recited a third of the Quran.'"],[5214,"Whoever recites \"Say: He is God, the One,\" it is as if he has recited a third of the Quran."],[5215,"Whoever recites \"Say: He is God, the One,\" it is as if he has recited a third of the Quran, and good deeds are recorded for him equal to the number of those who believe and those who associate partners [with God]."],[5216,"I heard Anas b. Malik ؓ—then he mentioned the hadith concerning the story of Mu'awiya b. Mu'awiya al-Laythi ؓ and the Prophet's ﷺ funeral prayer over him at Tabuk."],[5217,"Whoever recites the Mu'awwidhat [the two refuge-seeking surahs], it is as if he has recited all that God, Exalted is He, revealed to Muhammad ﷺ."],[5218,"The Prophet ﷺ recited in the dawn prayer “Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of daybreak” and “Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind,” and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The daybreak is Hell.”"],[5219,"Abdullah ؓ used to erase the two Mu'awwidhat from the mushaf and would say, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded that refuge be sought with them, but Abdullah ؓ did not recite them.'"],[5220,"The first apostasy among the Arabs was the apostasy of Musaylima b. Habib the liar, the owner of Yamama, and al-Aswad b. Ka'b al-Ansi in Yemen, during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'I saw in my forearm two bracelets of gold, and I blew on them and they flew away. I interpreted them as the liar of Yamama and the liar of San'a.'"],[5221,"Before the mosque was built, the Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray towards a wooden post. When the mosque was built, a prayer niche was built for him, and he moved to it. That wooden post yearned like a camel, so the Messenger of God ﷺ placed his hand on it, and it became still."],[5222,"The Messenger of God ﷺ delivered a sermon to us, and in it he admonished us with a discourse that made eyes shed tears, hearts tremble, skins shiver, and inner organs quake. He ﷺ commanded Bilal ؓ, who called out: Prayer in congregation! Then he mentioned the hadith in full, in which there is: \"Whoever chooses this world over the Hereafter, his is the Fire. Whoever honors a man of worldly status and praises him out of greed for his worldly goods, God Almighty is displeased with him, and he will be in the rank of Qarun in the lowest part of Hell. Whoever builds a building for show and reputation, on the Day of Resurrection he will be made to carry it from seven earths, with fire blazing around his neck, then thrown into the Fire.\" It was said: How does one build a building for show and reputation? He said: \"He builds beyond what suffices him, and he builds it for display. Whoever learns the Quran but does not act upon it, and prefers the fleeting goods and adornment of this world over it, incurs the displeasure of God Almighty, and he will be in the rank of the Jews and Christians who cast the Book of God Almighty behind their backs and sold it for a small price. Whoever is discontent with his provision and spreads his complaint, no good deed of his will be raised to God Almighty, and he will meet God, Mighty and Majestic, while He is displeased with him. Whoever marries a woman lawfully with lawful wealth, intending thereby pride and showing off, God Almighty will only increase him in humiliation and disgrace, and God Almighty will stand him, in proportion to what he enjoyed from her, on the brink of Hell, then he will fall into it for seventy autumns. Whoever humiliates a poor Muslim because of his poverty and belittles him, he has belittled the right of God Almighty, and he will remain in God Almighty's hatred and displeasure until he appeases him. Whoever honors a poor Muslim will meet God Almighty on the Day of Resurrection while He is smiling at him. Whoever is presented with this world and the Hereafter and chooses this world over the Hereafter will meet God Almighty without any good deed with which to protect himself from the Fire, but if he chooses the Hereafter over this world, he will meet God Almighty while He is pleased with him. Whoever's eyes shed tears out of fear of God, Blessed and Exalted, for every drop of his tears he will have the like of Mount Uhud in his scale, and for every drop that falls from his eye he will have in Paradise, on its edge, cities and palaces such as no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has never occurred to the heart of any describer.\""],[5223,"I was given the openings of speech, its comprehensive words, and its conclusions. We said: Teach us from what Allah Almighty taught you. So he taught us the tashahhud."],[5224,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. He would not go to relieve himself until he had gone out of sight and could not be seen. We camped in a desolate land with no trees or landmarks. He ﷺ said, 'O Jabir, go and put some water in the water-skin, then let us go until we cannot be seen.' He ؓ said: And there he ﷺ was, between two trees with some cubits between them. He said to me, 'O Jabir, go to these two trees and say to them: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands you both to come together so that I may sit behind you both.' So they came together, and he ﷺ sat behind them, then they returned to their places. He said: And we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a desolate land, as if birds were shading our heads. A woman with her child came to us and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, this child is seized by the devil three times every day.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped, then took the child and carried him between himself and the front of the saddle. Then he ﷺ said, 'Begone, enemy of Allah, I am the Messenger of Allah.' Then he ﷺ handed the child back to her. When we completed our journey and passed by that place, the woman and her child came to us, and with her were two rams. She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, accept these two from me. By the One who sent you with the truth, it has not returned to him since.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Take one of them and return the other.' He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ moved on, and we moved on with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among us, as if birds were shading our heads. Then a stray camel came and fell down prostrating between the two rows. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped and said to the people, 'Who owns this camel?' A group of young men from the Ansar ؓ said, 'It is ours, O Messenger of Allah.' He ﷺ said, 'What is the matter with it?' They said, 'We worked it for twenty years, and it had a little fat on it, so we wanted to slaughter it and divide it among our servants.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Will you sell it to me?' They said, 'Rather, it is yours, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'As for no, then be good to it until its appointed time comes.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we are more worthy of prostrating to you than the beasts.' He ﷺ said, 'If it were fitting for a human to prostrate to anyone, women would prostrate to their husbands.'"],[5225,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ, 'My people have disbelieved,' and I was informed that he had prepared an army against them. So I came to him and said, 'My people are upon Islam.' He ﷺ said, 'Is it so?' I said, 'Yes.' He said: So I followed him that night until morning, and I called the adhan for prayer when morning came. He gave me a vessel to perform ablution from, and the Prophet ﷺ placed his fingers in the vessel, and springs gushed forth. Then he said, 'Whoever of you wishes to perform ablution, let him perform ablution.' So I performed ablution and prayed. He appointed me over them and gave me their sadaqah. Then a man stood up to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'So-and-so has wronged me.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'There is no good in leadership for a Muslim man.' Then another man came and asked for sadaqah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Sadaqah is a headache in the head and a burning in the belly, and a disease.' So I gave him my two documents: the document of my leadership and my sadaqah. He ﷺ said, 'What is the matter with you?' I said, 'How can I accept them when I have heard from you what I heard?' He ﷺ said, 'It is as you heard.'"],[5226,"I met a man from the Jews and told him what had happened. He began to marvel and said, 'He gave you the price and returned the camel to you.'"],[5227,"Shall I inform you about the most generous? The most generous is Allah Almighty, and I am the most generous of the children of Adam, and the most generous of them after me is a man who learned knowledge and spread his knowledge; he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection as a nation alone, and a man who strove with his life in the path of Allah until he was killed."],[5228,"You will certainly attain your need, but he refused. When he feared that he would be delayed, he struck him lightly with the whip, then went on and prayed the morning prayer with them. When he finished, he ﷺ turned to face the people - and when he did that, they knew something had happened - and the people gathered around him. He ﷺ said, 'Where is the one I struck just now?' He repeated, 'If he is among the people, let him stand up.' The man began to say, 'I seek refuge in Allah and then in His Messenger,' and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept saying, 'Come closer, come closer,' until he came close to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat before him and handed him the whip, saying, 'Take your whip and retaliate.' The man said, 'I seek refuge in Allah from striking His Prophet.' He ﷺ said, 'Take your whip, there is no harm upon you.' He said, 'I seek refuge in Allah from striking His Prophet.' He ﷺ said, 'Unless you forgive.' He said: So he threw down the whip and said, 'I have forgiven, O Messenger of Allah.' Then Abu Dharr stood up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you remember the night of al-Aqabah? I was driving you while you were asleep, and whenever I slowed down or took hold of its halter, it turned aside, so I struck you lightly with the whip. I said, 'The people have come to you,' and you said, 'No harm upon you. Take, O Messenger of Allah, and retaliate.' He ﷺ said, 'I have forgiven.' He said, 'Retaliate, for it is dearer to me.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck him, and he said: I saw him writhing from it. Then he ﷺ said, 'O people, fear Allah. By Allah, no believer wrongs another believer except that Allah, the Exalted, will exact retribution for him on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[5230,"Her maternal uncle, Habib b. Fuwayk, narrated to her that his father took him to the Prophet ﷺ while his eyes were white and he could not see anything with them. He asked him, 'What happened to you?' He said, 'I was training a camel of mine and I placed my foot on a snake's egg, so I was afflicted.' The Prophet ﷺ blew into his eyes and he saw. He said: I saw him putting a thread into a needle, and he was eighty years old, and his eyes were white."],[5231,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one morning and said, 'I saw before the dawn prayer as if I were given the keys and the scales. As for the keys, these are the keys, and as for the scales, they are those with which weighing is done. I was placed in one pan and my ummah was placed in the other, and I outweighed them. Then Abu Bakr ؓ was brought and weighed, and he weighed them. Then Umar ؓ was brought and weighed, and he weighed them. Then Uthman ؓ was brought and weighed, and he weighed them. Then I woke up, and they were lifted.'"],[5232,"Abu Dharr's ؓ eye was injured on the day of Uhud, and the Prophet ﷺ spat into it, and it became the healthier of his two eyes."],[5233,"'Get out, enemy of Allah, for I am the Messenger of Allah.' Then he ﷺ handed him to her and said, 'Take him, and you will not see anything from him that worries you after today, if Allah, the Exalted, wills.' Usamah ؓ said: We completed our Hajj and departed. When we camped at al-Rawha', there was that woman, the mother of the child. She came with a roasted sheep and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I am the mother of the child whom I brought to you.' She said, 'By the One who sent you with the truth, I have not seen anything from him that worries me until this hour.' Usamah ؓ said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'O Usaym' - al-Zuhri said: This is how he used to call him, out of fondness - 'hand me its foreleg.' He said: I pulled off the foreleg and handed it to him ﷺ, and he ate it ﷺ. Then he said, 'O Usaym, hand me the foreleg.' I pulled off the foreleg and handed it to him, and he ate it ﷺ. Then he said, 'O Usaym, hand me the foreleg.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you said \"hand me,\" and I handed it to you and you ate it. Then you said \"hand me,\" and I handed it to you and you ate it. Then you said \"hand me the foreleg,\" but the sheep has only two forelegs.' He ﷺ said, 'If you had reached for it, you would have kept finding a foreleg in it as long as I told you.' He ﷺ said, 'O Usaym, get up and go out and see if you can find a place that would conceal the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' I went out and walked until I was tired, and I had not passed the people, and I did not see anything that I thought would conceal anyone, for the people had filled the space between the two mountains. I informed him, and he ﷺ said, 'Did you see any trees or piles of stones?' I said, 'Yes, I saw small palm trees, and beside them were piles of stones.' He ﷺ said, 'O Usaym, go to the palm trees and say to them: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands you to join one another so that you may be a screen for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. And say the same to the stones.' So I went to the palm trees and said to them what he ﷺ had commanded me. By the One who sent him with the truth, it was as if I was watching them pull themselves along by their roots and soil until they clung to one another and became like a single palm tree. And I said that to the stones, and by the One who sent him with the truth, it was as if I was watching them pull themselves along stone by stone until some rose upon others and they became like a wall. I came to him ﷺ and informed him, and he ﷺ said, 'Take the water-skin.' I took it, and we walked until we approached them. I went ahead of him ﷺ and put down the water-skin, then I returned to him. He ﷺ went aside until he relieved himself, then he came back, peace and blessings be upon him, carrying the water-skin. I took it from him ﷺ, and we returned. When he ﷺ entered the tent, he ﷺ said, 'O Usaym, go to the palm trees and say to them: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands each palm tree to return to its place. And say that to the stones.' So I went to the palm trees and said to them. He said: By the One who sent him with the truth, it was as if I was watching them pull themselves along with their soil until each palm tree returned to its place. And I said that to the stones, and by the One who sent him with the truth, it was as if I was watching them pull themselves along stone by stone until each stone returned to its place. I came to him ﷺ and informed him of that. This is a good chain, and Mu'awiyah b. Yahya al-Sadafi is weak, but his hadith has a witness from the route of Ya'la b. Murrah, narrated by Ahmad and others."],[5234,"Go and send them back. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my mount has become exhausted.' He ﷺ said, 'O brother of Suda', you are obeyed among your people.' I said, 'Rather, Allah, the Exalted, guided them through you to Islam.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'Shall I not appoint you over them?' I said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote a document for me and appointed me. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, order for me something from their sadaqat.' So he ﷺ wrote another document for me. Al-Suda'i ؓ said: That was during one of his journeys. He ﷺ stopped at a place, and the people of that place came to him complaining about their governor, saying, 'O Messenger of Allah, he seized us for something that was between him and his people in the Jahiliyyah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Did he do that?' They said, 'Yes.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to his companions, and I was among them, and said, 'There is no good in leadership for a believing man.' Al-Suda'i ؓ said: His ﷺ words entered my heart. Then another man came to him ﷺ and asked him, saying, 'O Messenger of Allah, give me.' He ﷺ said, 'Whoever asks people while he is self-sufficient, it is a headache in the head and a disease in the belly.' The man said, 'Give me from the sadaqat.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah, Mighty and Majestic, did not accept in it the judgment of a prophet or anyone else until He judged in it Himself and divided it. If you are from those parts, I will give you - or we will give you your due.' Al-Suda'i ؓ said: That entered my heart, that I had asked him while I was self-sufficient. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled with us from the beginning of the night. I kept close to him - and I was strong - and his companions ؓ would fall behind him and lag, until no one remained with him except me. When it was time for the morning adhan, he ﷺ commanded me, and I called the adhan. I kept saying, 'Shall I call the iqamah, O Messenger of Allah?' He ﷺ would look toward the east at the dawn and say, 'No.' When the dawn broke, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dismounted and went to relieve himself. Then he returned to me, and his companions ؓ had caught up with him. He ﷺ said, 'Is there any water, O brother of Suda'?' I said, 'No, except a little that is not enough for you.' He ﷺ said, 'Put it in a vessel, then bring it to me.' I did so, and he placed his palm ﷺ in the vessel. I saw between every two of his fingers ﷺ a spring gushing forth. He said, 'O brother of Suda', if I were not ashamed before my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, we would have drunk and given drink. Call out to my companions: Whoever has a need for water, let him take it.' I called out, and those who wanted took some. Then he ﷺ stood for prayer. Bilal ؓ wanted to call the iqamah, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The brother of Suda' called the adhan, so he will call the iqamah.' Al-Suda'i ؓ said: I called the iqamah. When he ﷺ finished the prayer, I brought him the two documents and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, excuse me from these two documents.' He ﷺ said, 'What has appeared to you?' I said, 'I heard you, O Prophet of Allah, say: There is no good in leadership for a believing man, and I believe in Allah and His Messenger. And I heard you say to the beggar: Whoever asks people while he is self-sufficient, it is a headache in the head and a disease in the belly, and I asked you while I was self-sufficient.' He ﷺ said, 'That is it. If you wish, accept, and if you wish, leave.' I said, 'Rather, I leave.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'Guide me to a man whom I can appoint over you.' I guided him to a man from the delegation who had come to him, and he appointed him over us. Then I said, 'O Prophet of Allah, we have a well. In winter, its water suffices us and we gather around it, but in summer its water decreases, so we disperse to other waters around us. We have embraced Islam, and all those around us are enemies. So pray to Allah, the Exalted, for us regarding our well, that its water may suffice us and we may gather around it and not disperse.' He called for six pebbles, rubbed them in his hand, and supplicated over them. Then he ﷺ said, 'Go with these pebbles, and when you come to the well, throw them in one by one, and mention the name of Allah, the Exalted.' Al-Suda'i ؓ said: We did so, and he said: After that, we could not see its bottom. Ahmad and Abu Dawud narrated part of it separately."],[5235,"3853 3218 / 3 - And Abū Yaʿlā said: Abū Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazīd narrated to us, with it."],[5236,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the market, a woman took hold of the rein of his mount while he was on a donkey. She said, “O Messenger of God, my husband does not come near me, so separate me from him.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Who is her husband?” He called him and said, “What is the matter with you and her? She has come complaining of your harshness, complaining that you do not come near her.” He said, “O Messenger of God, by the One who has honored you, I was with her only last night.” The woman wept and said, “He lies. Separate me from him, for he is one of the most hateful of God’s creatures to me.” The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled, then took his head and her head and brought them together, and said, “O God, draw each of them near to the other.” Jabir ؓ said, “We remained as long as God willed, then the Messenger of God ﷺ passed by the market, and there was a woman carrying leather goods. When she saw him ﷺ she threw down the leather and came to the Prophet ﷺ, saying, ‘O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, God has not created anything more beloved to me than him, except you.’”"],[5237,"I entered the mosque and recognized hunger in the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ. I went out until I came to Umm Sulaym ؓ, the mother of Anas b. Malik ؓ, who was married to Malik, the father of Anas. I said, “O Umm Sulaym, I recognized hunger in the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Do you have anything?” She said, “I have something,” and gestured with her hand. He said to her, “Prepare it and make it good.” So she sent Anas ؓ to the Messenger of God ﷺ. I said, “Whisper it in his ear and invite him.” When Anas ؓ came, the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Did your father send you to invite us, my son?” He said, “Yes.” He ﷺ said to his Companions ؓ, “Go in the name of God.” Anas ؓ turned and hurried back until he came to Abu Talhah ؓ and said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ has come to you with the people.” He said, “I and he went out until we met the Messenger of God ﷺ at the door on the resting place of the step. I said, ‘O Messenger of God, what have you done to us? We only recognized hunger in your face, so we prepared something for you to eat.’ He ﷺ said, ‘Enter and rejoice.’ He said, ‘The Messenger of God ﷺ took it and gathered it in the dish with his hand, then prepared it.’ He ﷺ said, ‘Is there any—’ as if he meant condiment. He said, ‘They brought him ﷺ a small skin with something—or nothing—in it. The Messenger of God ﷺ handled it with his hand and extracted the ghee from it, then said ﷺ, ‘Let ten enter upon me, ten at a time.’ They all ate and were satisfied. The Messenger of God ﷺ said concerning the surplus that remained, ‘Eat, you and your families.’ So they ate and were satisfied.”"],[5238,"I had a ewe, and I collected its ghee in a small skin and filled the skin. Then I sent it with a foster daughter, saying, ‘O foster daughter, deliver this skin to the Messenger of God ﷺ so he may use it as a condiment.’ The foster daughter went with it until she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, ‘O Messenger of God, this is ghee that Umm Sulaym ؓ sent to you.’ He ﷺ said, ‘Empty her skin for her.’ The skin was emptied and returned to her, and she left. Umm Sulaym ؓ came and saw the skin full and dripping. She said, ‘O foster daughter, did I not command you to take it to the Messenger of God ﷺ?’ She said, ‘I did. If you do not believe me, go and ask the Messenger of God ﷺ.’ Umm Sulaym ؓ went with her foster daughter and said, ‘O Messenger of God, I sent you with her a skin containing ghee?’ He ﷺ said, ‘She did; she brought it.’ She said, ‘By the One who sent you with the truth and the religion of truth, it is full and dripping with ghee?’ He ﷺ said, ‘Do you marvel that God fed you as you fed His Prophet? Eat and feed others.’ She ؓ said, ‘I came home and measured in a bowl of ours so-and-so much, and left it with what we used as condiment for a month or two.’”"],[5239,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a bedouin came to him and said, ‘Will you accept a good thing? That you testify that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God?’ He said, ‘Who will testify for you?’ The Prophet ﷺ said, ‘This tree.’ So he called it while it was on the bank of the valley, and it came cutting through the ground until it stood before him ﷺ. He asked it to testify, and it testified three times, then returned to its place. The bedouin said, ‘I will go to my people. If they follow me, I will bring them to you; otherwise I will return to you and stay with you.’”"],[5240,"“The one whose sight reminds you of Allah, whose speech increases you in knowledge, and whose deeds remind you of the Hereafter” – marfūʿ."],[5241,"And al-Bazzar said: ‘Ali b. al-Mundhir narrated to us. And al-Hasan b. Sufyan said: ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Umar al-Ju‘fi narrated to us. They both said: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us with it. Ibn Hibban authenticated it. :. al-Hasan b. Sufyan :. :"],[5242,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5243,"Al-Bazzar said: Muhammad b. Marzuq narrated to us; Dawud b. Shabib narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us with it. [ :"],[5244,"He ﷺ was at al-Hajun, and the polytheists rejected him. He ﷺ said, ‘O God, show me a sign.’ He said, ‘Call a tree.’ He ﷺ called a tree, and it said in it: then he commanded it ﷺ and it returned to its place of growth.”"],[5245,"Abu Sufyan ؓ was sitting in a corner of the mosque when the Prophet ﷺ came out from one of his houses wrapped in a garment. Abu Sufyan ؓ said, while in his place, ‘I wonder by what means you have overcome me.’ He said, ‘Then the Prophet ﷺ came until he struck his back with his hand, then said, “I overcame you by God, the Mighty and Majestic.” He ؓ said, “I bear witness that you are the Messenger of God.”’"],[5246,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5247,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5248,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5250,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, then he saw nearly a hundred wolves sitting on their haunches. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'These are delegations of wolves; they ask you to give them some of your surplus food, and they will guarantee you safety regarding everything else.' They complained to him ﷺ of need. He said: 'Give them permission.' He said: 'So they gave them permission, and they howled.'"],[5251,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5252,"And Musa recited: \"And indeed, a day with your Lord is like a thousand years of those which you count.\" (Quran 22:47)"],[5253,"Gabriel ﷺ commanded me to give sincere counsel."],[5254,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped, then he said to me: 'Take this blood and bury it away from animals and people.' He said: 'So I went and sought a place for it, then I came back.' He said to me: 'What did you do?' I said: 'I drank it.' He ﷺ smiled."],[5255,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a pottery vessel in which he urinated. When morning came, he ﷺ would say: 'O Umm Ayman, pour out what is in the pottery vessel.' One night I got up thirsty and drank what was in it. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'O Umm Ayman, pour out what is in the pottery vessel.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I got up thirsty and drank what was in it.' He ﷺ said: 'You will never complain of your stomach after this day of yours, ever.'"],[5256,"My life is good for you: you narrate and are narrated to. My death is good for you: your deeds are presented to me. Whatever good I see, I praise Allah for it; and whatever evil, I ask Allah's forgiveness for you."],[5257,"A man from the outskirts of Madinah would invite the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the middle of the night for barley bread, and he would accept his invitation."],[5258,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered Aisha to prepare something for Usama's affair, either mucus or something else, and it seemed she disliked it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it from her, undertaking that himself."],[5259,"I was walking with the Prophet ﷺ, and he found a date-palm spathe containing dates. He took one date and gave me one date."],[5260,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never put his knees forward in front of a sitting companion, nor did he ever extend his hand to someone and then withdraw it before the other let go. No one ever sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and then stood up before he stood up."],[5261,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among the gentlest of people with others. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never refused, on a cold morning, to accept water from a slave, a slave woman, or a child to wash his face and forearms. No one ever asked to whisper in his ear but that he inclined toward him, and he would not turn away until the other turned away. No human ever reached for his hand ﷺ but that he gave it to him, and he would not withdraw it until the other withdrew his."],[5262,"Abu Ya'la said: Abdullah b. Muhammad b. Ishaq al-Adhrami narrated to us, Abu Qatan narrated to us, Mubarak b. Fadala narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us from him. Ibn Hibban authenticated it."],[5263,"A man called out to the Prophet ﷺ three times, each time he (the Prophet) would reply to him: 'Labbayk, labbayk.'"],[5264,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a gift, and he looked but did not find anything to put it in, so he said ﷺ: 'Put it in the hollow, for I am only a servant; I eat as a servant eats and drink as a servant drinks.'"],[5266,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, I have married off my daughter, and I would love for you to help me with something.' He ﷺ said: 'I have nothing, but when tomorrow morning comes, bring me a wide-mouthed bottle and a stick from a tree. And it is between me and you that you knock on the side of the door.' He said: So he came to him ﷺ with a wide-mouthed bottle and a stick from a tree. He ﷺ began to wipe the sweat from his forearms until the bottle was filled. Then he ﷺ said: 'Take it and tell your daughter to dip this stick into the bottle and perfume herself with it.' He said: When she perfumed herself with it, the people of Madinah would smell the fragrance of that perfume, so they called them the houses of the perfumed ones."],[5267,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ passed along any road of Madinah, the scent of musk would be found from him, and it would be said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by.'"],[5268,"A bedouin man came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing a jubbah of sijān (a type of fabric) adorned with gold. He stood at the head of the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'This companion of yours elevates every shepherd, son of a shepherd, and lowers every horseman, son of a horseman.' He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ took hold of the collar of his jubbah and said: 'Sit down, for I see on you the clothes of one who has no intellect. God Almighty did not send any prophet before me except that he had herded sheep.' He said: It was said: 'And you, O Messenger of God?' He ﷺ said: 'Yes, for qarārīṭ and half qarārīṭ.' Then the Prophet ﷺ said: 'When death approached Prophet Nūḥ ﷺ , he said to his son: I enjoin upon you a bequest...'"],[5269,"The Messenger of God ﷺ never said to me about something he disliked: 'How ugly is what you did,' nor about something that pleased him: 'How beautiful is what you did.'"],[5270,"Persia will face a blow or two blows, then there will be no Persia after this ever. Byzantium has horns; every time one horn perishes, another horn succeeds it. They are people of patience and people of the sea. Far from it, until the end of time, they are your companions as long as there is any good in life."],[5271,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, wipe my face and supplicate to God Almighty for me.' He said: He ﷺ wiped her face and supplicated to God Almighty for her. She said: 'O Messenger of God, lower your hand.' So he ﷺ lowered his hand onto her chest. She said: 'O Messenger of God, lower your hand.' But he ﷺ refused and distanced himself from her."],[5272,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ for him to wipe her face, so he ﷺ wiped it and supplicated for her. She said: 'O Messenger of God, lower your hand after he had placed it on her chest.' He ﷺ said: 'Get away from me.'"],[5273,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ, so he wiped her face. Women used to come to him ﷺ, and he would wipe their faces and supplicate for them. She said: 'O Messenger of God, lower your hand.' He said: He pushed her away and said: 'Get away from me.'"],[5274,"The Prophet ﷺ was given the strength of forty men in sexual intercourse."],[5275,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was given the strength of forty-some men, every man from the people of Paradise."],[5276,"We brought dates to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he knelt on his knees, took a handful, and said: 'Take this to so-and-so.' And he took a handful and said: 'Take this to so-and-so,' until he ﷺ distributed among his wives handful by handful. Then he took a handful, eating from it and casting the pits with his left hand. A domestic animal passed by him, so he handed it to her, and she ate it."],[5277,"My aunt ؓ sent me to the Prophet ﷺ, and I came to him while he had jewelry that the ruler of Bahrain had gifted him. He ﷺ took from that jewelry a fill of his two hands, then said: 'O my little daughter, this is for you.'"],[5278,"He ﷺ liked cucumbers, and he loved cucumbers."],[5280,"I never saw the belly of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that I remembered folded sheets of paper, one upon another."],[5281,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left us, and no bird flapped its wings in the sky except that he mentioned to us some knowledge of it."],[5283,"I was given the keys of speech and its seals. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, teach us from what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, taught you.' So he taught us."],[5284,"I was sitting with Umar ؓ — and he mentioned a long story in which — the Prophet ﷺ said: 'O people, I have been given the comprehensive words and their seals, and speech has been shortened for me in a concise manner.'"],[5285,"Allah, exalted, did not assure anyone of His creation except Muhammad ﷺ. He said: 'That Allah may forgive you your past and future sins.' And He said regarding the angels, peace be upon them: 'And whoever of them says, \"I am a god besides Him,\" that one We shall recompense with Hell.'"],[5286,"There is none of you except that with him is a devil. They said: 'And with you?' He ﷺ said: 'And with me, except that Allah, exalted, helped me against him, so he submitted. And there is none of you whose deeds will admit him to Paradise.' They said: 'Not even you?' He ﷺ said: 'Not even me, unless Allah, Mighty and Majestic, envelops me with His mercy.'"],[5287,"So he submitted."],[5288,"Indeed the most honored of Allah's creation to Him is Abu al-Qasim ﷺ, and Paradise is in the heaven, and the Fire is in the earth. When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will raise the creatures nation by nation and prophet by prophet, until Ahmad ﷺ and his nation are the last of the nations to be stationed. Then the bridge of Hell will be placed, then a caller will call out: 'Where is Ahmad and his nation?' He will stand, and his nation, both its righteous and its wicked, will follow him."],[5289,"I am the foremost of the Arabs."],[5290,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, are you the master of the Arabs?' He ﷺ said: 'I am the master of the children of Adam, and no boast. Adam is under my banner, and no boast.'"],[5291,"No one surpasses Muhammad ﷺ, and no one surpasses Ibrahim ﷺ , the friend of my Lord, Mighty and Majestic."],[5292,"\"God, Blessed and Exalted, has given me an angel from among the angels who stands at my grave when I die. No servant invokes blessings upon me without him saying, 'O Muhammad, so-and-so son of so-and-so is invoking blessings upon you,' naming him by his name and his father's name. Then God, Mighty and Majestic, blesses him in return ten times.\""],[5293,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ in the mosque, and his gaze ﷺ turned to a man walking in the mosque. He said: 'Labbayk, O Messenger of Allah,' and he did not dispute the speech except that he said: 'O Messenger of Allah.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Do you read the Torah?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'And the Gospel?' He said: 'Yes, and the Qur'an, and by the One in Whose hand is my soul, if I wished I could read it.' He said: 'Then he adjured him: Do you find me as a prophet in the Torah and the Gospel?' He said: 'I will tell you. We find one like you, and your appearance, and like your emergence, and we hoped that you would be among us. But when you emerged, we feared that you might be him, so we looked, and found that you are not him.' He ﷺ said: 'By the One in Whose hand is Muhammad's soul, I am indeed him, and they are indeed my nation, and they are indeed more than seventy thousand and seventy thousand.'"],[5294,"When Nahawand was conquered, the Muslims took captives from the Jews. The head of the exilarch came and received the Jewish captives. A man among the Muslims had obtained a beautiful, radiant slave girl. He said to me: 'Would you walk with me to this person? Perhaps he will set a price for me for this slave girl.' So I went with him, and we entered upon an arrogant old man who had an interpreter. He said to a man with him: 'Ask this slave girl: has this Arab had intercourse with her?' He said: 'I saw that he became jealous when he saw her beauty, so he spoke to her in his own language, and I understood what he said. I said to him: 'You have sinned by what you find in your Book, by asking this slave girl about what is behind her clothes.' He said to me: 'You lie. What do you know of what is in my Book?' He said: I said: 'I know your Book better than you.' He said: 'You know my Book better than me?' I said: 'Yes, I know your Book better than you.' He said: 'Who is this?' They said: 'Abd Allah b. Salam.' He said: 'So I left him that day, and he sent a messenger to me saying: 'You must come to me by an oath,' and he sent me a mount. He said: 'So I went to him seeking reward, hoping that he would embrace Islam. He detained me for three days, while I read the Torah to him and he wept. I said to him: 'By Allah, he is indeed the prophet whom you find in your Book.' He said to me: 'What should I do with the Jews?' He said: I said: 'The Jews will not avail you anything against Allah.' But he refused to embrace Islam, and wretchedness overcame him.'"],[5295,"Some people of Quraysh rode the sea at the time of the Prophet's ﷺ mission, and the wind cast them upon an island among the islands of the sea. There was a man on it. He said: 'Who are you?' They said: 'We are people of Quraysh.' He said: 'What is Quraysh?' They said: 'The people of the Sanctuary, and the people of such and such.' When he understood, he said: 'We are its people, not you.' And it turned out he was a man of Jurhum. He said: 'Do you know why Ajyad was named that? Our horses were excellent and returned to it.' He said: 'Then they said: A man has emerged among us claiming to be a prophet,' and they mentioned his affair to him. He said: 'Follow him. Were it not for my present condition, I would have joined you to go to him.'"],[5296,"Umar saw a woman in her finery and said to her: 'Do you think your kinship to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will avail you anything against Allah?' She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'My intercession will benefit.'"],[5297,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were in the mosque, and he had bound his head with a cloth during the illness in which he died. He headed towards the pulpit, and we followed him. He said: 'By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I am indeed standing at the Pond this very hour...' the hadith, and in it is the virtue of Abu Bakr ؓ, and at its end: 'Then he descended ﷺ, and he did not stand until that hour.'"],[5298,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to reconcile between them, and the prayer time arrived. Bilal said to Abu Bakr ؓ: 'The prayer time has arrived, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is not present. Would you like me to call the adhan and the iqamah, and you lead the people in prayer?' He ؓ said: 'If you wish.' So Bilal ؓ called the adhan and the iqamah, and Abu Bakr ؓ advanced and led the people in prayer. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came after he had finished, and said: 'Did you pray?' They said: 'Yes.' He ﷺ said: 'Who led you?' They said: 'Abu Bakr ؓ.' He ﷺ said: 'You have done well. It is not fitting for a people among whom Abu Bakr is present that anyone other than him should lead them.'"],[5299,"Allah, Exalted be He, dislikes in heaven that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ be wronged on earth."],[5300,"When the verse was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ: \"Indeed, those who lower their voices in the presence of the Messenger of God\" – Abu Bakr ؓ said: \"I swear that I will not speak to the Prophet ﷺ except in a whisper like a secret conversation.\""],[5301,"A man came from a military expedition, and between him and the Messenger of God ﷺ there was a relationship through women, and he was in the house of A'ishah ؓ. He entered and greeted, and he ﷺ said: \"Welcome to a man who has remained safe and gained spoils. State your need.\" He said: \"Which of the people is most beloved to you?\" He ﷺ said: \"This one behind me\" – and she was A'ishah ؓ. He said: \"I did not mean from the women; I meant from the men.\" He ﷺ said: \"Her father.\""],[5304,"There was a mutual reproach between Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ. Abu Bakr apologized to Umar ؓ, but he did not accept it from him. That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and it distressed him. Then Umar ؓ went to him and sat down, but he turned away from him. Then he moved and sat on the other side, but he turned away from him. Then he stood and sat in front of him, but he turned away from him. He said: \"O Messenger of God, I see you turning away from me, and I do not think that is for anything except something that has reached you about me. What is the state of my kneeling while you turn away from me? By God, I do not care if I do not live in this world for even an hour while you are turning away from me.\" He ﷺ said: \"You are the one to whom Abu Bakr apologized, and you did not accept it from him. I came to you all, and you said: 'You have lied,' while my companion said: 'You have spoken the truth.'\" Then he ﷺ said: \"Will you leave me and my companion alone?\" three times."],[5305,"I was taken up to the lowest heaven, and I did not pass by any heaven except that I found in it: Muhammad is the Messenger of God, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq behind me."],[5306,"A woman entered the Fire because of a cat... the hadith. And in it: Abu Bakr and Umar will testify to that, while Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ are not present. He ﷺ said: \"While a man was among his sheep, a wolf came and took a sheep...\" the hadith. And in it: Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ will testify to that, similarly. \"While a man was riding a cow...\" the hadith, and in it: Abu Bakr and Umar will testify to that, while Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ are not present. He said: \"While a man was walking in a fine garment, pleased with himself, God Almighty caused the earth to swallow him...\" the hadith, and in it: Abu Bakr and Umar will testify to that, while Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ are not present."],[5307,"I saw Abu Bakr ؓ as a man of light flesh, fair-skinned."],[5308,"Abu Bakr ؓ used to dye his hair with henna."],[5309,"While A'ishah bint Talhah ؓ was saying to her mother Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr ؓ: \"My father is better than your father,\" A'ishah the Mother of the Believers ؓ said: \"Shall I not judge between you two? Abu Bakr ؓ entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'O Abu Bakr, you are the freed one of God from the Fire.'\" She ؓ said: \"From that day he was called Atiq. And Talhah ؓ entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'You, O Talhah, are among those who have fulfilled their vow.'\""],[5310,"By God, I was in my house one day, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was in the courtyard with his companions ؓ, and the curtain was between me and them, when Abu Bakr ؓ came. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever is pleased to look at the one freed by God from the Fire, let him look at Abu Bakr ؓ. And his name that his family gave him was Abdullah b. Uthman, but the name Atiq prevailed over him.'"],[5311,"If I do not prefer Abu Bakr and Umar over Ali ؓ, I would have belied Ali; and I am more in need of affirming Ali ؓ than of belying him."],[5312,"I saw Abu Bakr ؓ in the campaign of Dhat al-Salasil, and his beard was like the flame of the arfaj."],[5313,"I said to Abu Bakr ؓ, 'O Caliph of Allah,' and he ؓ said, 'I am the Caliph of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I am content with that.'"],[5314,"I saw Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ with a palm branch in his hand, while he was saying, 'Listen to the Caliph of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[5315,"If the faith of Abu Bakr ؓ were weighed against the faith of all the people of the earth, it would outweigh them."],[5316,"I wish I were a hair on the chest of Abu Bakr ؓ."],[5317,"This pulpit of mine is on one of the gates of Paradise. A man was given the choice by his Lord, Mighty and Glorious, between living in this world as long as Allah willed for him to live, and meeting his Lord, and Abu Bakr ؓ wept... the hadith, like the hadith of Abu Sa'id ؓ, and in it: but love and the brotherhood of faith."],[5318,"Abu Bakr ؓ said to me, 'We have no wealth except a bowl and a milch-camel. When I die, send them both to Umar ؓ.' When he died, she sent them to Umar ؓ, and he said, 'May Allah have mercy on Abu Bakr. He has indeed made it difficult for those who come after him.'"],[5319,"They once struck the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he lost consciousness. He said: 'Abu Bakr ؓ stood up and began calling out, \"Woe to you! Would you kill a man for saying, 'My Lord is Allah'?\" They said, \"Who is this?\" He said, \"The son of Abu Quhafah.\"'"],[5320,"Al-Qasim b. Muhammad was a truthful and silent man. When Umar b. Abd al-Aziz ؓ became caliph, he said: 'Today the virgin will speak from her chamber.' I heard my aunt A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ ؓ, say: 'When the Prophet ﷺ passed away, the Arabs apostatized altogether, the people craned their necks (in anticipation), and the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ became like goats scattered in a thicket. By Allah, they did not differ over a single word except that my father flew with its understanding.' Then she mentioned Umar ؓ and said: 'Whoever saw Umar ؓ knew that he was created as a burden for Islam.' Then she said ؓ: 'He was, by Allah, skilled and unmatched, a man of his own kind. He had prepared for affairs their counterparts. I have not seen the like of his character ؓ, until you count seven qualities which I do not remember.'"],[5321,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, and by Allah, if what descended upon my father had descended upon the firm mountains, they would have crumbled."],[5323,"That he mentioned Abu Bakr ؓ and praised him, and said: 'He begot me twice.'"],[5324,"A camel from the spoils broke (its leg), so Umar ؓ slaughtered it and invited some of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ to eat. Al-Abbas ؓ said to him: \"If you did this every day, we would just come and sit with you?\" He ؓ said: \"I will not do the like of it again. I had two companions (the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr ؓ) who passed away after following a certain path. If I act differently from their way, I will be made to follow a path other than theirs.\""],[5325,"We, the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ, had no doubt that tranquility spoke upon the tongue of Umar."],[5326,"“Heedlessness is in three: heedlessness of the remembrance of Allah, Mighty and Majestic; from the time the dawn prayer is held until the sun rises; and a person’s heedlessness of himself until debt mounts upon him.”"],[5327,"Abu Sufyan ؓ came and sat near the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"Have you not seen your son-in-law? Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ proposed to her, and she refused him.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"What prevented her from (marrying) Umar ؓ? There is no man in Madinah better than Umar ؓ—except if he were a prophet.\" He said: So I said to the one…"],[5328,"The people of Najran came to Ali ؓ and said: \"We ask you by your own hand and your intercession with your tongue to return us (to our previous status).\" He said: \"Umar ؓ was rightly guided in his affairs. If he were criticized one day, he would be criticized on that day (i.e., the day of his stabbing).\""],[5329,"\"O Ammar, Jibril ﷺ came to me just now. I said: 'O Jibril, tell me about the virtues of Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ.' He said: 'O Muhammad, if I were to tell you the virtues of Umar ؓ for as long as Nuh remained among his people—nine hundred and fifty years—his virtues would not be exhausted. Indeed, Umar ؓ is one good deed among the good deeds of Abu Bakr ؓ.'\""],[5330,"If there was anyone who did not know lying, it was Umar."],[5331,"If a camel died lost in my jurisdiction (i.e., through my negligence), I would fear that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, would question me about it."],[5332,"A man from the Muhajirun entered upon Abu Bakr while he was suffering in his illness and said to him: \"You have appointed Umar over us, and he has been harsh with us even without authority. So how will it be when he rules over us? He will be even harsher and harsher. What will you say to Allah when you meet Him?\" Abu Bakr said: \"Sit me up.\" So they sat him up. He said: \"Are you trying to frighten me with Allah? Do you know me? I will say when I meet Him: 'I appointed over them the best of Your people.'\""],[5333,"I do not know anyone among the people who was more knowledgeable after the Messenger of Allah than Umar b. al-Khattab."],[5334,"I wish that I could leave it—meaning the governorship—evenly, with nothing for me and nothing against me."],[5335,"Khalid narrated to us, from Yahya b. 'Ubaydillah, with this (narration)."],[5336,"He used to say: O Allah, do not make my killing at the hand of a man who has prostrated to You a single prostration."],[5337,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a washed garment on Umar ؓ and said ﷺ: Is this garment of yours new or washed? He said ؓ: Washed, O Messenger of Allah. He said ﷺ: Wear new, live praiseworthy, and die as a martyr, and Allah will grant you the delight of the eye in this world and the Hereafter."],[5338,"Umar ؓ sent for me, so I came to him. When I reached the door, I heard his sobbing. I said: Has the Commander of the Faithful been afflicted? I entered and took hold of his shoulder and said: No harm, no harm, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: Rather, the severest harm. Then he took my hand and brought me inside, and there were bags piled one on top of another. He said: Now the family of al-Khattab has become insignificant before Allah, the Exalted. If Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, had willed, He would have given this to my two companions—meaning the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr ؓ—and He would have established for me a practice in it that I could follow. I said: Sit with us and let us think. Sit with us and let us think. So we assigned four thousand to each of the Mothers of the Believers ؓ, and we assigned four thousand to each of the Muhajirun, and two thousand to each of the rest of the people."],[5339,"When Umar ؓ was struck, Hafsah ؓ entered upon him and said: O companion of the Messenger of Allah, O in-law of the Messenger of Allah, O Commander of the Faithful. Umar said to Ibn Umar ؓ: Seat me, O Abdullah, seat me, for I cannot bear what I hear. So he leaned him against his chest ؓ. Then he said to her: I adjure you by the right I have over you not to mourn me after this sitting of yours. As for your eyes, I do not control them. Indeed, no deceased person is mourned with what is not in him except that the angels curse him."],[5340,"When Umar ؓ departed from Mina, he made his camel kneel at al-Abtah. Then he piled up a heap of pebbles and threw himself upon it, pressing his garment to it and lying on his back. He stretched his hand toward the sky and said: O Allah, my strength has weakened, my age has advanced, and my flock has scattered, so take me to You without negligence or excess. Then he ؓ came to Madinah and gave a sermon: O people, I have established for you the sunnahs, I have ordained for you the obligations, and I have left you upon a clear path—Yahya clapped his hands—unless you lead people astray to the right and left. And he mentioned the hadith. Said: Dhul-Hijjah had not ended before Umar was killed."],[5341,"Khalid narrated to us, from Yahya b. 'Ubaydillah, with this (narration)."],[5343,"When Umar ؓ was stabbed, we entered upon him while he was saying: Do not rush to this man. If I live, I will see my opinion about him; if I die, he is your affair. They said: O Commander of the Faithful, by Allah, he has been killed and cut to pieces. He said ؓ: Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return. Then he said ؓ: Woe to you, who is he? They said: Abu Lu'lu'ah. He said ؓ: Allah is greatest. Then he ؓ looked at his son Abdullah ؓ and said: O my son, what kind of father was I to you? He said: The best of fathers. He said ؓ: I adjure you to carry me until you press my cheek to the ground, so that I die as a slave dies. Abdullah ؓ said: By Allah, that is hard for me, O father. He said: Then he said: Get up and do not argue with me. So he got up and carried him until he pressed his cheek to the ground. Then he said ؓ: O Abdullah, I adjure you by the right of Allah, the Exalted, and the right of Umar, when I die and you bury me, do not wash your head until you sell from the properties of the family of Umar for eighty thousand and place it in the treasury of the Muslims. Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf ؓ, who was at his head, said: O Commander of the Faithful, what is the value of these eighty thousand? You have harmed your dependents, or the family of Umar. He said ؓ: Get away from me, O Ibn Awf. Then he looked at Abdullah ؓ and said: O my son, and thirty-two thousand I spent in twelve pilgrimages I performed during my governance and in needs that came to me from messengers arriving from the provinces. Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf ؓ said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, rejoice and think well of Allah, the Exalted. There is no one among us of the Muhajirun but has taken the like of what you took from the fay' that Allah, the Exalted, has assigned to us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away while pleased with you, and you have with him ﷺ prior merits. He said ؓ: O Ibn Awf, Umar wishes that he had come out of it as he entered it. I wish to meet Allah, the Exalted, and that you do not hold me accountable for little or much. * Thumamah: Ali ibn al-Madini and others spoke about him. The narration of the story of Umar ؓ in the two Sahihs does not contain most of what is mentioned here."],[5344,"And Abu Yaʿla said: Abu Bakr narrated to us, with this."],[5345,"He took a straw and said: I wish I were this. I wish my mother had not given birth to me. I wish I were a forgotten thing, forgotten."],[5346,"Woe to me, and woe to my mother, if Allah does not forgive me—three times—then something between them was settled."],[5348,"Two men mentioned Uthman ؓ. One of them said: He was killed as a martyr. The other clung to him and brought him to Ali ؓ, saying: This one claims that Uthman ؓ was killed as a martyr?! Ali ؓ said to him: Did you say that? He said: Yes. Do you not remember the day I came to the Prophet ﷺ and with him were Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, and you? I asked the Prophet ﷺ and he gave me; I asked Abu Bakr ؓ and he gave me; I asked Umar ؓ and he gave me; I asked Uthman ؓ and he gave me; and I asked you and you refused me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to bless me. He said ﷺ: What prevents you from being blessed when a Prophet, a Siddiq, and two martyrs have given you? Three times. He said ؓ: Leave him."],[5349,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5350,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5351,"Uthman ؓ used to fast during the day and stand in prayer at night, except for a short sleep at its beginning."],[5352,"When ʿUthmān ؓ heard the adhan, he would say, 'Welcome to those who proclaim justice, and to the prayer—welcome and greetings.'"],[5353,"I saw Uthman ؓ one night at the Maqam, having stepped forward, and he recited the Quran in a single rak'ah, then he finished."],[5354,"Uthman ؓ looked down upon us on the Day of the House, and he said: \"O people, do not kill me, for if you kill me you will be like this\"—and he interlaced his fingers ؓ."],[5355,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5356,"And Abu Bakr said: Abu Usamah narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5357,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ met al-Walid b. Uqba ؓ, and al-Walid said to him: \"Why do I see that you have become distant from the Commander of the Faithful Uthman ؓ?\" He said: \"Convey to him from me that I did not flee on the day of Aynayn—Asim said: it is the day of Uhud—and I did not stay behind from Badr, and I did not abandon the sunna of Umar ؓ.\" He went to inform Uthman of that, and Uthman ؓ said: \"As for his saying 'the day of Aynayn,' how can he reproach me for a sin from which God Almighty has pardoned [me]? He, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'Those of you who turned back on the day the two hosts met...' [the verse]. As for his saying 'I stayed behind on the day of Badr,' I was nursing Ruqayya, the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, until she died, and he allotted me a share, and whoever the Messenger of God ﷺ allotted a share has indeed participated. As for his saying 'I abandon the sunna of Umar ؓ,' I am not able to bear it, neither I nor he.\" So I came to him and narrated that to him."],[5358,"Uthman ؓ raised his voice at Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ, and Abd al-Rahman b. Awf said to him: \"For what reason did you raise your voice, when I witnessed Badr and you did not, and I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ and you did not, and I did not flee on the day of Uhud while you fled?!\" Uthman ؓ said: \"As for your saying that you witnessed Badr and I did not, the Messenger of God ﷺ left me behind with his daughter, and he allotted me a share, and gave me my reward. As for your saying that you pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ and I did not, the Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to some people among the polytheists, and you know that. When I was detained, he ﷺ struck his right hand on his left and said: 'This is for Uthman.' And the left hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ is better than my right hand. As for your saying that I fled on the day of Uhud and you did not flee, God Almighty said: 'Those of you who turned back on the day the two hosts met...' [the verse]. So why do you reproach me for a sin from which God Almighty has pardoned [me]?!\""],[5359,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5360,"The first of the Muslims to emigrate with his family to Abyssinia was Uthman ؓ. His news was withheld from the Prophet ﷺ, and he ﷺ kept going out looking for news. A woman from Quraysh arrived and said to him: \"O Abu al-Qasim, I saw your son-in-law heading off on his journey, with his wife on a donkey of these [small, creeping] creatures, and he was driving it, walking behind her.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"May God Almighty accompany them. Uthman is the first to emigrate with his family to God—Mighty and Majestic—after Lot ﷺ .\""],[5361,"While I was sitting, Gabriel ﷺ came to me, carried me on his right wing, and admitted me to the Garden of Eden. While I was in it, I noticed with my eyes an apple. The apple split into two halves, and out of it came a maiden. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: I have not seen anyone more beautiful in beauty than her, nor more perfect in loveliness. She glorified God Almighty with a glorification the like of which the first and the last have not heard. I said: Who are you? She said: I am al-Ḥawrāʾ. My Lord, may His majesty be glorified, created me from the light of His Throne. I said: For whom are you? She said: I am for the trustworthy, the generous, the wronged caliph, ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān ؓ."],[5363,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5364,"By God, it is indeed the covenant of the unlettered Prophet: They will betray you after me."],[5365,"This community will betray you after me."],[5366,"I heard ʿAlī ؓ say on the pulpit: By God, it is indeed the covenant of the unlettered Prophet: This community will betray me."],[5367,"And Abu Bakr said: Abu Usamah narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5368,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5369,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5370,"We used to say that the most judicious of the people of Madinah was Ibn Abī Ṭālib ؓ."],[5371,"Al-Bazzār said: Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. al-Junayd narrated to us, Yaḥyā b. Muḥammad b. al-Sakan narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated to us with it. Al-Ḥākim deemed it authentic. : :"],[5372,"The first of you to come to me at the Pond is the first of you in Islam: ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ."],[5373,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5374,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between the people and left me out. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you established brotherhood between your companions and left me out?!\" He ﷺ said, \"Do you think I left you out? I only left you for myself. You are my brother and I am your brother.\" He said, \"If anyone disputes with you, say: I am the servant of Allah and the brother of His Messenger ﷺ. No one will claim it after you except a liar.\""],[5375,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ali ؓ : \"O Ali, take the door and let no one enter upon me, for I have visitors from the angels who asked their Lord to visit me.\" So Ali ؓ took the door, and Umar ؓ came and sought permission. He said, \"O Ali, seek permission for me to see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Ali ؓ said, \"There is no permission for anyone over the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So Umar ؓ went back, thinking that this was due to displeasure from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Umar ؓ could not bear it, so he returned and said, \"Seek permission for me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said, \"There is no permission for anyone over the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He ؓ said, \"Why?\" He ؓ said, \"Because visitors from the angels are with him, and they asked their Lord to visit him.\" He ؓ said, \"And how many are they, O Ali?\" He ؓ said, \"Three hundred and sixty angels.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ ordered the door to be opened, and Umar ؓ mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, \"O Messenger of Allah, indeed he...\""],[5376,"And Abu Bakr said: Abu Usamah narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5377,"We were at al-Juhfah by Ghadir Khumm when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us, took the hand of Ali ؓ and said, \"Whoever's mawla I am, Ali is his mawla.\""],[5378,"Abu Hurayrah ؓ entered the mosque and people gathered around him. A young man stood up to him and said, \"I implore you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever's mawla I am, Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him'?\" He ؓ said, \"O Allah, yes.\""],[5379,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5380,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. 3931/3 - And al-Bazzar said: Ali b. Shubrumah al-Bahili narrated to us, Ahmad b. Yahya al-Sufi narrated to us, a man narrated to us, from Mansur b. Abi al-Aswad, from Dawud and Idris, from their father, from Abu Hurayrah ؓ with it."],[5381,"I found in my book from Muhammad b. Miskin, from Abdullah b. Yusuf, from Ikrimah b. Ibrahim, from Idris al-Awdi with it."],[5382,"When Fatimah was given in marriage to Ali... the hadith has already been mentioned in the Book of Marriage, and in it: He said: \"O Fatimah, I have not failed to marry you to the most beloved of my family to me.\""],[5383,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5384,"Al-Bazzar said: Amr b. Ali and Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us, both saying: Harami b. Umarah narrated to us with it. It is not reported from the Prophet ﷺ except with this chain, and nothing has come from Abu Uthman, from Ali ؓ other than this. : :"],[5385,"On the night Fatimah was given in marriage to Ali ؓ , the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Do not do anything until I come to you.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not wait long before he followed them. He ﷺ stood at the door and asked permission, then entered, and there was Ali ؓ keeping away from her. He said: \"I already know that you are the flame of Allah and His Messenger.\" He ﷺ called for water, rinsed his mouth, then returned it to the vessel, then he ﷺ sprinkled her chest and his chest ؓ and invoked blessings upon them, then he ﷺ left them."],[5386,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5387,"Some birds were gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ﷺ distributed them among his wives ؓ, so each woman received [one]."],[5388,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated it to us. : :, :"],[5389,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ embrace Ali ؓ and kiss him, saying, \"May my father be ransomed for the unique martyr, may my father be ransomed for the unique martyr.\""],[5390,"I was sitting in the mosque with two men and we were discussing Ali ؓ and spoke ill of him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ approached, angry, with anger recognizable on his face. I said, \"I seek refuge in Allah from the anger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He ﷺ said, \"What do you have against me? Whoever harms Ali has harmed me,\" saying it three times. He said: After that, someone would come to me and say, \"Ali ؓ is alluding to you,\" saying, \"Beware the trial of al-Ukhaynis.\" I would say, \"Did he name me?\" They would say, \"No.\" I would say, \"The khunnas among people are many. Allah forbid that I should harm the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after hearing from him what I heard.\""],[5392,"When the Prophet ﷺ was sent, Iblis's troops came to him and said, \"A prophet has been sent, and a nation has been brought forth.\" He said, \"Do they love the world?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"If they love it, I do not care if they do not worship idols. They will not escape me, for I will come to them morning and evening with three things: taking wealth without right, spending it without right, and withholding it from its right. And all evil follows from this.\""],[5393,"I came to Sa'd b. Malik ؓ in Madinah, and he said, \"It has been mentioned to me that you all revile Ali ؓ?\" He said, \"We have done so.\" He said, \"Perhaps you have reviled him?\" I said, \"Allah forbid.\" He said, \"Do not revile him, for if a saw were placed on the parting of my hair on condition that I revile Ali ؓ, I would never revile him after hearing from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what I heard.\""],[5394,"Two men are destroyed because of me: an excessive lover and a lying hater."],[5395,"I heard Ali ؓ say from the pulpit, pointing with his index and middle fingers: \"Two men are destroyed because of me: an extreme lover and a hateful detester.\""],[5396,"I heard him narrate from Ali ؓ the like of it, except that he did not mention the two fingers:"],[5397,"What do you have against me? Whoever harms Ali ؓ has harmed me."],[5398,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought me and found me sleeping in a small stream. He ﷺ said, \"Get up. How blameworthy are the people who call you Abu Turab.\" He said: He ﷺ saw that I felt something in myself from that, so he ﷺ said, \"Get up, for by Allah I will surely please you. You are my brother and the father of my children; you fight for my Sunnah and fulfill my protection. Whoever dies in my era is a captive of Allah Almighty, and whoever dies in your era has fulfilled his vow. Whoever dies loving you after your death, Allah Almighty seals for him with security and faith as long as the sun rises or sets. Whoever dies hating you dies a death of Jahiliyyah and will be held to account for what he did in Islam.\""],[5399,"The Prophet ﷺ attended the tree at Khumm, then came out holding the hand of Ali ؓ and said: \"Do you not bear witness that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is your Lord?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He ﷺ said: \"Do you not bear witness that Allah and His Messenger have more right over you than your own selves, and that Allah and His Messenger are your guardians?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"So whoever's guardian is Allah and His Messenger, indeed this one is his guardian. I have left among you that which, if you hold fast to it, you will never go astray: the Book of Allah, the Exalted, its rope is in my hand and its rope is in your hands, and my household.\""],[5400,"The Prophet ﷺ took him by the hand on the day of Ghadir Khumm and said: \"O Allah, whoever's guardian I am, Ali is his guardian.\""],[5401,"I was near the house of the Prophet ﷺ among a group of the Muhajirun and Ansar ؓ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: \"Shall I tell you who are the best among you?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He ﷺ said: \"The best among you are those who fulfill their promises and are pure. Indeed, Allah the Exalted loves the considerate, the God-fearing.\" He said: \"Then Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ passed by, and he ﷺ said: 'The truth is with this one, the truth is with this one.'\""],[5402,"I saw Ali ؓ commanding something and Uthman ؓ forbidding it, so I said to Ali ؓ: \"There is surely evil between you two.\" He ؓ said: \"Between us is nothing but good, but the best of us is the one who most follows this religion.\""],[5403,"Ali ؓ delivered a sermon and said: \"O people, by Allah, besides whom there is no deity, I have not taken anything from your wealth, small or large, except this.\" He ؓ took out a bottle from the sleeve of his shirt containing perfume, and said: \"A dehaqan gave it to me as a gift.\""],[5404,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came while we were lying in the mosque, and he struck us with a fresh palm branch that was in his hand and said: \"Do you sleep in the mosque?! Indeed, one should not sleep in the mosque.\" He said: \"So we quickly got up, and Ali ؓ got up with us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Come, O Ali. Indeed, what is permissible for me in the mosque is permissible for you. By Him in whose hand is my soul, you will drive away people from my pond on the Day of Resurrection, just as a stray camel is driven away from water with a stick you have made of 'awsaj. It is as if I am looking at your station beside my pond.'\""],[5406,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and prayed Maghrib with him. Then he stood and prayed until he prayed Isha. Then he left and I followed him. He said: \"An angel appeared to me and asked his Lord's permission to greet me and give me good news that Fatimah ؓ is the mistress of the women of Paradise, and that al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ are the young men of Paradise.\""],[5407,"Ali ؓ proposed to me, and that news reached Fatimah ؓ, so she went to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"Asma' ؓ is married to Ali ؓ.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It was not for her to harm Allah and His Messenger ﷺ.\""],[5408,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. : :"],[5409,"Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ wanted to propose to the daughter of Abu Jahl. People said: \"Do you think the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would be affected by that?\" Some said: \"What of it? She is just a woman among women.\" Others said: \"He will certainly be affected by this: marrying the daughter of Allah's enemy along with the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" That reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he praised Allah the Exalted and extolled Him, then said: \"Now then, what is the matter with people who claim that I am not affected concerning Fatimah ؓ? Indeed, Fatimah is a part of me. It is not for anyone to marry the daughter of Allah's enemy while married to the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[5410,"Khadijah ؓ is the best of the women of her time, Maryam (peace be upon her) is the best of the women of her time, and Fatimah ؓ is the best of the women of her time."],[5411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited us and spent the night with us, while al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ were sleeping. Al-Hasan ؓ asked for water, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to a water skin and squeezed it into a cup, then came to give him water. Al-Husayn ؓ reached out to drink, but he ﷺ stopped him and began with al-Hasan. Fatimah ؓ said: \"It is as if he is more beloved to you?\" He ﷺ said: \"No, but he asked for water first.\" Then he ﷺ said: \"I and you and these two—and I think he said—and this sleeping one, meaning Ali ؓ, on the Day of Resurrection will be in one place.\""],[5412,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. : :"],[5413,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah: \"In every year the Qur'an was presented to me, and this year it was presented to me twice, and I am going to die.\" So she wept. Then he said: \"You are the first of my family to join me.\""],[5414,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me to Fatimah ؓ, and she came walking with the gait of her father. He spoke to her, and she wept. She was asked ؓ, and she said: \"I will not disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to anyone.\""],[5415,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. : :"],[5416,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. : :"],[5417,"Indeed, Fatimah ؓ guarded her chastity, so Allah the Exalted made her descendants forbidden to the Fire."],[5418,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. : :"],[5419,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. : :"],[5420,"I proposed to the Prophet ﷺ for his daughter Fatimah ؓ. 'Ali ؓ sold a coat of mail of his and some of what he sold of his belongings, and it reached four hundred dirhams and eighty dirhams. The Prophet ﷺ commanded that two-thirds of it be spent on perfume and one-third on clothes. He ﷺ blew into a jar of water and commanded them to bathe with it. And he commanded her ﷺ not to precede him in nursing her child. He said: But she preceded him ﷺ in nursing Husayn ؓ. He said: As for Hasan ؓ, he ﷺ placed something in his mouth—I do not know what it was. He was the more learned of the two men."],[5421,"Whoever would like to look at a man from the people of Paradise, let him look at Husayn b. 'Ali ؓ, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say it."],[5422,"I heard the jinn mourning over Husayn ؓ."],[5424,"He said concerning al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ : Whoever loves me, let him love these two."],[5425,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. : :"],[5426,"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ wrestled in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began saying, \"Hai, Hasan!\" Fatimah ؓ said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, it is as if he—meaning al-Hasan—is dearer to you than al-Husayn ؓ?\" He ﷺ said, \"Jibril (peace and blessings be upon him) is helping al-Husayn, and I love to help al-Hasan ؓ.\""],[5427,"My eye saw and my ear heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he took the hand of Hasan or Husayn ؓ —and my stronger belief is that it was Husayn—and placed his feet upon his feet."],[5428,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this. : :"],[5429,"Every children of a mother have a paternal kin to whom they belong, except the children of Fatimah ؓ, for I am their guardian and I am their paternal kin."],[5430,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would prostrate, and al-Hasan or al-Husayn ؓ would come and climb onto his back ﷺ, so he would prolong the prostration. It was said, \"O Prophet of Allah, you prolonged the prostration?!\" He ﷺ said, \"My son mounted me, and I disliked to hurry him.\""],[5431,"Al-Husayn b. Ali entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the house while I was sitting by the door. I looked and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turning something in his palm, while the boy was sleeping on his stomach. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I saw you turning something in your palm while the boy was sleeping on your stomach and your tears were flowing?\" He said, \"Jibril came to me with the soil in which he will be killed, and informed me that your community will kill him.\""],[5434,"Indeed, I know the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise: a man who kept asking Allah, the Exalted, to keep him away from the Fire, until when the people of Paradise had entered Paradise and the people of the Fire had entered the Fire, he remained between that. He said, 'O Lord, bring me near to the gate of Paradise.' It was said, 'O son of Adam, did you not ask to be kept away from the Fire?' He said, 'O Lord, who is like You? Bring me near to the gate of Paradise.' So he was brought near to it, and he looked at a tree near the gate of Paradise and said, 'O Lord, bring me near to it so that I may shade myself with its shade and eat of its fruit.' He, Majestic and Exalted, said, 'O son of Adam, did you not say [such-and-such]?' He said, 'O Lord, who is like You? Then bring me near to it.' Then he saw something better than that and said, 'O Lord, bring me near to it.' He, majestic is His majesty, said, 'O son of Adam, did you not say [such-and-such]?' He said, 'O Lord, who is like You? Then bring me near.' It was said to him, 'Run, and you shall have whatever your feet reach and your eyes see.' He said, 'So he ran until he became exhausted' – meaning he became tired – and said, 'O Lord, is this mine and this?' He will say, 'You shall have the like of it and multiples of it.' He will say, 'My Lord is pleased with me. If He permitted me to clothe the people of Paradise and feed them, I would do so generously.'"],[5435,"I know the last man of my nation to cross the bridge: a man who writhes on the bridge like a boy when his father brings him near; his hand slips once, and the Fire touches it, and his foot slips once, and the Fire touches it. He said: Then the angels say to him: Have you considered if Allah, Exalted is He, raises you in this place of yours and you walk upright, will you tell us of every deed you did? He said: Then he says: Yes, by His might, I will not conceal any of my deeds. He said: Then they say to him: Arise and walk upright. So he arises and walks until he crosses the bridge, then they say to him."],[5436,"I heard Abu Dharr ؓ while he was holding the door ring, saying: O people, whoever knows me, he knows me; and whoever does not know me, he does not know me. I am Abu Dharr. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The likeness of my household among you is like the ark of Nuh; whoever boards it is saved, and whoever stays behind from it perishes."],[5437,"He saw Abu Dharr ؓ standing at the door calling out: O people, do you know me? Whoever knows me, he knows me; and whoever does not know me, then I am Jundub, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I am Abu Dharr al-Ghifari. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The likeness of my household among you is like the ark of Nuh; whoever boards it is saved, and whoever stays behind from it drowns. And the likeness of my household among you is like the Gate of Hittah."],[5438,"Al-Bazzar narrated it through al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Dharr ؓ, and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Hanash:"],[5439,"Fatimah, daughter of the Prophet ﷺ, came, and upon her was awe, carrying al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ at her waist, and in her hand was a pot for al-Hasan, containing hot food, until she brought it to the Prophet ﷺ. When she placed it in front of him, he ﷺ said: Where is Abu Hasan? She said: In the house. So he called him, and they all sat eating. Umm Salamah ؓ said: The Prophet ﷺ never shared his food with me, nor did he ever eat food while I was with him, except that he shared it with me before that day — meaning, he invited me to it. When he finished, he wrapped them ﷺ with his garment."],[5440,"Ali ibn al-Husayn ؓ had some people come to him and they praised him. He said: Woe to you, how lying you are and how bold against Allah the Exalted! We are a people from among the righteous of our people, and it is enough for us that we be among the righteous of our people."],[5442,"Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf ؓ fainted with a swoon until they thought that his soul had departed. Umm Kulthum ؓ went out to the mosque seeking help with what she was commanded of patience and prayer. When he regained consciousness, he said: Did I faint? They said: Yes. He said: You spoke truth. Two angels came to me and said: Come, we will take you to judgment before the Mighty, the Trustworthy. Then another angel said: Return him, for this one is among those for whom happiness was written while they were in their mothers' wombs, and his sons will enjoy him for as long as Allah the Exalted wills. He lived after that for a month, then died ؓ."],[5443,"Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf ؓ said to the members of the consultative council: Would you like me to choose for you and be exempted from it? Ali ؓ said: Yes, I am the first to be pleased, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: You are trustworthy among the inhabitants of the heavens, trustworthy among the inhabitants of the earth."],[5444,"And Musaddad said: Durust narrated to us, from him."],[5445,"No prophet ever died until a man from his nation led him in prayer."],[5449,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for me, for my children, and for my children's children. I heard my father say to a sister of mine who was older than me: You are among those whom the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached."],[5451,"He entered with Musa b. Talhah upon Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ , and he drew him close until he seated him with him on the bed. Then he took Musa's forearm and squeezed it, then said: 'Take it easy, O son of my brother, for by Allah, I hope that Allah – Mighty and Majestic – will make me and your father – meaning Talhah ؓ – among those from whose hearts Allah has removed rancor, as brothers on couches facing one another.'"],[5452,"By Allah, I was in my house one day, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions ؓ were in the courtyard, with a curtain between me and them, when Talhah b. Ubayd Allah ؓ came. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever is pleased to look at a man walking on the earth who has fulfilled his vow, let him look at Talhah ؓ.'"],[5453,"Talhah ؓ was mentioned in the presence of Umar ؓ, and he said: 'That is a man in whom there has been pride since his hand was injured with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[5455,"There is no death I would die that is more beloved to me than to be killed unjustly."],[5456,"Beware of the supplication of Sa'd."],[5458,"I asked my Lord – Blessed and Exalted – that I should not marry into any of my nation, nor give in marriage any of my nation, except that he would be with me in Paradise, and He granted me that."],[5459,"A firm resolve from my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and a covenant He made with me – that I should not marry into any household, nor give any of my daughters in marriage, except that they would be my companions in Paradise."],[5460,"When Umar married Umm Kulthum bt. Ali ؓ , he said: 'Will you not congratulate me? For I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Every tie and lineage will be severed on the Day of Resurrection except my tie and my lineage.'"],[5461,"Umar ؓ went out to the people of the Suffah and said: 'Will you not congratulate me?' They said: 'For what, O Commander of the Faithful?' He said ؓ : 'I married Umm Kulthum ؓ , who is related to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Fatimah and Ali ؓ , and I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say...' – and he mentioned it. He said: 'So I wanted to be that.'"],[5463,"While the people were with Ali ؓ one day, they found him in good spirits. They said: 'Tell us about your companions, O Commander of the Faithful.' He said ؓ : 'Which of my companions?' They said: 'The companions of the Prophet ﷺ.' He said ؓ : 'All the companions of the Prophet ﷺ are my companions. Which of them do you want?' They said: 'The group whom we have seen you treat kindly in your mention and praise of them, apart from the rest.' He said ؓ : 'Which of them?' They said: 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud ؓ.' He said: 'He learned the Sunnah and recited the Quran, and that suffices as knowledge.' Then he ended with that, and they did not know what he meant by his saying 'that suffices as knowledge' – did it suffice for Abdullah, or did it suffice for the Quran? They said: 'What about Hudhayfah ؓ?' He said ؓ : 'He knew – or was taught – the names of the hypocrites, and he asked about difficult matters until he understood them. If you ask him about them, you will find him knowledgeable about them.' They said: 'What about Abu Dharr ؓ?' He said ؓ : 'A vessel filled with knowledge, and he was ؓ stingy and eager – stingy about his religion, eager for knowledge. He used to ask many questions, and he was given and denied. Indeed, it was filled for him in his vessel until it was full.' They said: 'What about Salman ؓ?' He said ؓ : 'A man from us and to us, the People of the House. Who among you can be like Luqman the Wise? He knew the first knowledge and attained the last knowledge, and he read the first Book and the last Book. He was ؓ a sea that never runs dry.' They said: 'What about Ammar b. Yasir ؓ?' He said ؓ : 'That is a man into whose flesh, blood, bones, hair, and skin Allah the Exalted mixed faith. He never leaves the truth for even an hour; wherever it goes, he goes with it. The Fire should not consume anything of him.' They said: 'Then tell us about yourself, O Commander of the Faithful.' He said ؓ : 'Hold on, Allah has forbidden self-praise.' He said: Then someone said: 'But Allah the Exalted says: And as for the favor of your Lord, proclaim it.' He said ؓ : 'Then I will tell you of the favor of my Lord, Blessed and Exalted: When I asked, I was given; when I was silent, I was approached. And within my faculties, I was filled with abundant knowledge.'"],[5464,"Abu Ya'la said: Musa b. Muhammad b. Hayyan narrated to us, Durust narrated to us, with it."],[5465,"And Musaddad said: Durust narrated to us, from him."],[5466,"Abu Ya'la said: Musa b. Muhammad b. Hayyan narrated to us, Durust narrated to us, with it."],[5467,"Al-Nadr and Sa'd were not strong, and none narrated it except Ja'far. <hidden matn linked=\"26048251\" text=\"Jibril ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Muhammad, Allah the Exalted loves three of your Companions, so love them: Ali b. Abi Talib, Abu Dharr, and al-Miqdad ؓ.' He said: Then Jibril ﷺ came to him and said, 'O Muhammad, Paradise yearns for three of your Companions,' and Anas b. Malik ؓ was with him ﷺ, and he hoped it might be for some of the Ansar. Anas said: He wanted to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about them but was in awe of him. So he went out and met Abu Bakr ؓ and said, 'O Abu Bakr, I was just with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Jibril ﷺ came to him and said, \"Paradise yearns for three of your Companions.\" I hoped it might be for some of the Ansar, but I was too in awe to ask him ﷺ. Would you go in and ask him?' Abu Bakr ؓ said, 'I fear to ask him and then not be among them, and my people would gloat over me.' Then Anas met Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ and said to him the same as he had said to Abu Bakr ؓ, and Umar replied the same as Abu Bakr ؓ had. Then he met Ali ؓ, and Ali ؓ said to him, 'Yes, I will ask him. If I am among them, I will praise Allah the Exalted; and if I am not among them—meaning, it will not harm.' So Ali ؓ entered and said, 'Anas ؓ...'\">"],[5468,"The love of these four does not come together except in the heart of a believer: Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, and Ali, ؓ."],[5469,"We, the community of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while we were numerous, used to say: The best of this Ummah after its Prophet ﷺ is Abu Bakr, then Umar, then Uthman ؓ, then we would fall silent."],[5470,"Umar ؓ recited on the pulpit: 'Gardens of Eden,' and said, 'None will enter it except a prophet—congratulations to you, O companion of the grave—and he pointed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—or a truthful one—congratulations to you, O Abu Bakr—or a martyr, and how can Umar attain martyrdom! Indeed, the One who brought me out of my house at al-Hathamah is able to drive it to me.'"],[5471,"We mentioned Abu Bakr, Umar, and Ali ؓ in his presence, and he said, 'What an excellent view, and I find in my heart for Ali a lingering feeling that I do not find for those two.'"],[5472,"Abu Bakr is the most compassionate of my Ummah and the most merciful of them; Umar is the boldest of my Ummah and the most just of them; Uthman is the most modest of my Ummah and the most generous of them; Ali is the most intelligent of my Ummah and the bravest of them; Abdullah b. Mas'ud is the most pious of my Ummah and the most trustworthy of them; Abu Dharr is the most ascetic of my Ummah and the most truthful of them; Abu al-Darda' is the most excusing of my Ummah and the most God-fearing of them; and Mu'awiya is the most forbearing of my Ummah and the most open-handed of them."],[5473,"And Abu Ya'la said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Ahmad b. 'Abd Allah b. Yunus narrated to us, and he mentioned it."],[5474,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on Hira', and the mountain trembled, so he said ﷺ, 'Be still, Hira', for upon you are none but a prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr.' And upon it were the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talha, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, Sa'd, and Sa'id, ؓ."],[5476,"I fought alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ against the jinn and mankind. It was said, 'How did you fight the jinn?' He said, 'We stopped at a place, and I took my water-skin and bucket to draw water. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Someone will come to you at the water to prevent you.\" When I was at the well, a black man came to me, as if he were a demon, and said, \"You will not draw a bucketful from it today.\" He grabbed me, and I grabbed him and threw him down. Then I took a stone and broke his nose and face. Then I filled my water-skin and came to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"Did anyone come to you at the water?\" I said, \"A black man.\" I told him what I had done. He ﷺ said, \"That was a devil.\""],[5477,"And Abu Ya'la said: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us:"],[5478,"And Abu Ya'la said: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us:"],[5480,"And Abu Ya'la said: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us:"],[5481,"The Prophet ﷺ heard Abu Musa ؓ reciting and said ﷺ: It is as if the voice of this one is from the flutes of the family of David."],[5483,"I descended with the Prophet ﷺ from the mountain pass of Harsha, and the strap of his sandal broke. I handed him my strap, but he refused to accept it, and he ﷺ sat in the shade of a tree to repair his sandal. He ﷺ said to me: Look who you see. I said: This is so-and-so. He ﷺ said: Wretched is the servant of God, so-and-so. Then he ﷺ said to me: Look who you see. I said: This is so-and-so. He ﷺ said: Wretched is the servant of God, so-and-so. Then he ﷺ said to me: Look who you see. I said: This is so-and-so. He ﷺ said: Excellent is the servant of God, so-and-so. The one to whom he ﷺ said 'Excellent is the servant of God' was Khalid ibn al-Walid ؓ. As for the other two, I will not inform anyone about them."],[5484,"And Abu Ya'la said: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us:"],[5485,"Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf ؓ complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about Khalid ibn al-Walid ؓ. He said: O Khalid, why do you harm a man from the people of Badr? If you were to spend gold equal to Mount Uhud, you would not attain his deed. He said: O Messenger of Allah, they revile me, so I respond to them. He ﷺ said: Do not harm Khalid, for he is a sword from the swords of God Almighty, which God has poured upon the disbelievers."],[5486,"Jihad in the path of God Almighty has indeed kept me from much recitation."],[5487,"There is no night in which a bride is gifted to my house and I love her, or in which I am given glad tidings of a boy, more beloved to me than a night of severe frost in a detachment of warriors, in which I attack the enemy at dawn."],[5488,"Khalid ibn al-Walid ؓ encamped near the marzbans, and they said to him: Beware of poison, lest the non-Arabs give it to you to drink. He ؓ said: Bring it to me. It was brought, and he took it in his hand, then swallowed it, and said: In the name of God. It did not harm him at all."],[5489,"We performed Umrah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in an Umrah he performed, and he shaved his hair. I hastened to the forelock and took it, and I made a cap and placed it in the front of the cap. I was never directed in any direction except that it was opened for me."],[5491,"And Abu Ya'la said: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us:"],[5492,"Sa'd entered upon Salman ؓ to visit him, and Salman ؓ wept. Sa'd ؓ said to him: What makes you weep, O servant of God? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while he was pleased with you, you will come to him at the Pond, and you will meet your companions."],[5494,"Whoever would be pleased to look at a man some of whose limbs precede him to Paradise, let him look at Zayd ibn Sawhan ؓ."],[5496,"A man came to Ibn ʿAbbās ؓ and said: “Ḥassān, the accursed, has come.” Ibn ʿAbbās ؓ said: “He is not cursed; he strove with the Messenger of God ﷺ with his tongue and his self.”"],[5497,"Ḥassān b. Thābit ؓ recited to the Prophet ﷺ some verses: “I bear witness, by God’s permission, that Muḥammad / is the Messenger of Him who is above the heavens, from on high; / and that Abū Yaḥyā and Yaḥyā, both of them, / have in his religion a work accepted; / and that the brother of al-Aḥqāf, when he stood among them, / spoke concerning the essence of God, and was just.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “And I [bear witness too].”"],[5499,"And Abu Ya'la said: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us:"],[5501,"He passed by the Prophet ﷺ after he had bought a horse from a Bedouin, and the Bedouin denied the sale, saying: “I did not sell to you.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “You did sell to me.” Khuzaymah b. Thābit ؓ passed by them and heard their words, and said: “I testify that you sold.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “How do you know that when you did not witness us?” He ؓ said: “We have testified to what is greater than that.” The Prophet ﷺ accepted his testimony as that of two men until Khuzaymah ؓ died."],[5502,"The Messenger of God ﷺ bought a horse from Sawāʾ b. Qays al-Muḥāribī, who denied it. Khuzaymah b. Thābit ؓ testified for him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “What led you to testify when you were not present with us?” He ؓ said: “I believed you in what you brought, and I know that you speak nothing but truth.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever Khuzaymah testifies for or against, it suffices him.”"],[5503,"If there were a hundred thousand or more in this mosque, and in it a man from the people of the Fire, and he breathed, and his breath reached it, the mosque and all in it would burn."],[5504,"The Messenger of God ﷺ bought a horse from a Bedouin, and the Bedouin denied it. Khuzaymah b. Thābit ؓ came and said: “O Bedouin, do you deny? I testify against you that you sold it.” The Bedouin said: “If Khuzaymah b. Thābit testifies against me, then give me the price.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O Khuzaymah, we did not call you as a witness; how do you testify?” He ؓ said: “I believe you in the news of heaven; should I not believe you about this Bedouin?” The Messenger of God ﷺ made his testimony equal to that of two men. There was no man in Islam whose testimony counted as that of two men except Khuzaymah b. Thābit ؓ."],[5506,"I seek forgiveness from God—Mighty and Majestic—and turn to Him in repentance every day twelve thousand times, according to the amount of his blood money—or he said: “my blood money.”"],[5508,"Zayd b. ʿAmr and Waraqah b. Nawfal went out seeking the religion until they came to a monk in Mosul. He said to Zayd b. ʿAmr: “Where have you come from, O owner of the camel?” He said: “From the house of Abraham.” He said: “What do you seek?” He said: “I seek the religion.” He said: “Return, for the one you seek is about to appear in your land.” As for Waraqah, he became a Christian. As for me, Christianity was offered to me but it did not suit me. He returned saying: “At Your service, truly, truly; in worship and servitude; righteousness I seek, not the fancy. Do you see one who emigrates like one who says: I believe in what Abraham believed?” Then he would say: “I seek for you, O God, a humble, submissive servant. Whatever You impose on me, I will undertake.” Then he would fall down in prostration. His son came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, my father was as you have seen and as you have heard. Shall I seek forgiveness for him?” He ﷺ said: “Yes, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection as a nation alone.” Zayd b. ʿAmr came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while Zayd b. Ḥārithah ؓ was with him, and they were eating from their food. They invited him to their meal, but Zayd b. ʿAmr said to the Prophet ﷺ: “We do not eat what is slaughtered on stone altars.”"],[5509,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about Zayd b. ʿAmr b. Nufayl, and he ﷺ said: “He will be raised on the Day of Resurrection as a nation alone, between me and Jesus ﷺ .” He ﷺ was asked about Waraqah b. Nawfal, and he said: “I saw him in the midst of the Garden, wearing silk brocade.”"],[5510,"And Abu Ya'la said: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us:"],[5512,"The voice of Abū Ṭalḥah ؓ in the army is better than a thousand men."],[5513,"Abu Talhah ؓ recited Surat Bara'ah and came upon this verse: ﷻGo forth, light and heavy.﷼ He said: ﷻDo I not see my Lord calling me to go forth, young and old? Equip me.﷼ His sons said to him: ﷻYou campaigned with the Messenger of God ﷺ until he passed away, and with Abu Bakr ؓ until he died, and with Umar ؓ, so we will campaign on your behalf.﷼ He said: ﷻEquip me.﷼ So they equipped him, and he rode the sea until he died. They did not find an island to bury him in except after seven days, yet he did not change."],[5514,"And Abu Ya'la said: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us:"],[5516,"The Throne shook out of love for God the Exalted to meet Sa'd ؓ. He said: He only means the bier. God the Exalted said: And he raised his parents upon the throne. He said: Its boards broke apart. He said: And the Messenger of God ﷺ entered his grave and was detained. When he came out, it was said: O Messenger of God, what detained you? He ﷺ said: Sa'd ؓ was squeezed in the grave with a squeeze, so I supplicated to God the Exalted to relieve him."],[5517,"5528 4603 / 2 - And al-Bazzar said: Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us, al-Muqri' narrated to us, from him:"],[5520,"Amir b. al-Akwa' ؓ fought a man in single combat and killed him, and wounded himself. He said: That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: He has two rewards."],[5521,"His uncle was wounded on the day of Khaybar and killed a man, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: You have two rewards."],[5523,"When Suhayb wanted to emigrate to Madinah, the disbelievers of Quraysh said to him: You came to us destitute, then your wealth grew among us and you reached what you reached, and now you want to leave with your self and your wealth! By God, that will not happen. He said to them: What if I give you my wealth, will you let me go? They said: Yes. He said: I call you to witness that I have given you my wealth. That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: Suhayb has profited, Suhayb has profited."],[5524,"Umar ؓ said to Suhayb: O Suhayb, you have three traits that I dislike for you. He ؓ said: Your feeding of food while you have no wealth, your taking a kunya while you have no son, and your claiming Arab lineage while your tongue has an accent. He ؓ said: As for what you mentioned about food, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: The best of you is the one who feeds food. By God, I will never stop feeding food. And he mentioned the kunya, and he said: Upon it I live and upon it I die. And he mentioned the claim, and he said: I am Suhayb b. Sinan, until he traced his lineage to al-Namir b. Qasit. I used to tend sheep for my family, and the Romans raided and enslaved me, so they taught me their language, and that is the accent you see in me."],[5526,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and recited to him my verse: We are a people who do not accustom our horses, when we meet, to swerve and flee. And on the day of terror the colors of our horses are unrecognizable from the stabbing, until you think the dark bay is a sorrel. It is not known of us to return them sound, nor is it disapproved that they be bloodied. Our glory and our forefathers reached the sky, and we seek above that a place to appear. He said: Then the Prophet ﷺ said: To where? I said: To Paradise. He said: Yes, if God the Exalted wills. He ؓ said: And when I recited to him ﷺ: There is no good in forbearance if it has no sudden acts that protect its purity from being turbid. And there is no good in ignorance if it has no intelligent man who, when the matter is brought, sets it right. The Prophet ﷺ said: May God not break your mouth. He said: And he ؓ was among the people with the most beautiful set of teeth, and when a tooth fell out, another grew."],[5528,"Shall I not tell you about the lowest of the people of Paradise? They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'A man will enter from the gate of Paradise, and his servants will meet him and say: \"Welcome, our master! It is time for you to return.\"' He said: 'Then carpets will be spread for him for forty years. Then he will look to his right and to his left and see gardens, and he will say: \"For whom is what is here?\" It will be said: \"For you.\" When he finishes, a red ruby or a green emerald will be raised for him, having seventy branches, in each branch seventy rooms, in each room seventy doors. It will be said to him: \"Recite and ascend.\" He said: 'He will ascend until he reaches the couch of his kingdom and reclines on it. Its width is a mile by a mile, and it has extra space. Seventy thousand dishes of gold will be brought to him, no dish having the same color as its companion. He will find the taste of the last dish like the taste of the first. Then drinks of various kinds will be brought to him, and he will drink as much as he desires. Then the servants will say: \"Leave him and his wives.\" (Abu Shihab said: I think he said:) The servants will withdraw from him, and there will be a houri seated on the couch of her kingdom. He will see the marrow of her leg from behind the flesh and blood. He will say to her: \"Who are you?\" She will say: \"I am one of the houris with large eyes who have been hidden for you.\" He will look at her for forty years without lifting his gaze from her. Then he will raise his gaze to the rooms above him, and there will be another more beautiful than her. She will say to him: \"Is it not time that we have a share of you?\" He will ascend to her and look at her for forty years without turning his gaze away from her. When the bliss has reached its utmost with them, and they think that there is nothing better than them, the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will manifest Himself to them, and they will look at the face of the Most Merciful, and they will forget all the bliss they had witnessed when they look at the face of the Most Merciful. Then He will say: \"O people of Paradise, declare My oneness!\" They will respond with the declaration of oneness. Then He will say: \"O Dawud, glorify Me as you used to glorify Me in the world.\" Dawud will glorify his Lord, Mighty and Majestic.' Ahmad b. Yunus said: I said to Abu Shihab: 'The hadith of Khalid b. Dinar about the mention of Paradise – is it marfu'?' He said: 'Yes.' In the Dar al-'Asima edition: (umm), but what is established is from the Musnad of 'Abd b. Humayd and the Ittihaf of al-Busiri."],[5529,"There was in Madinah a disabled man. He said to his family: Place me on the road of the Messenger of God ﷺ to his mosque. He said: So the disabled man was placed on the road of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Whenever he ﷺ went back and forth to the mosque, he would greet the disabled man. Then the disabled man's family came to take him back, and he said: No, by God, I will not leave this place as long as the Messenger of God ﷺ lives, so build me a hut. They built him a hut, and he remained in it. Whenever the Messenger of God ﷺ passed to the mosque, he would enter the hut and greet the disabled man, and whenever he ﷺ got a bit of food, he would send some to the disabled man. He said: While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, a man came and announced the death of the disabled man to him. The Messenger of God ﷺ rose, and we rose with him, until when he drew near the hut, he ﷺ said to his companions: Let no one approach the hut except me. He ﷺ drew near the hut, and there was Jibril (peace and blessings be upon him) sitting by the disabled man. He said: O Messenger of God, if you had not come to us, we would have taken care of him for you. But since you have come, you are more entitled to him. So the Messenger of God ﷺ went to him, washed him with his own hand, shrouded him, prayed over him, and placed him in the grave."],[5531,"I saw Ibn Umm Maktum on the day of al-Qadisiyyah, wearing armor and holding a banner in his hand."],[5534,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed Umrah, and there was an agreement between him and the people of Makkah that he would not take anyone out of its people. When the Messenger of God ﷺ completed his Umrah, he left Makkah. The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by the daughter of Hamza b. Abd al-Muttalib ؓ, and she said: O Messenger of God, to whom are you leaving me? He ﷺ did not turn to her because of the pact between him and the people of Makkah. Zayd b. Haritha ؓ passed by her, and she said: To whom are you leaving me? He did not turn to her. Ja'far ؓ passed by her, and she appealed to him, but he did not turn to her. Then Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ passed by her, and she said: O Abu al-Hasan, to whom are you leaving me? Ali ؓ took her and placed her behind Fatima ؓ. When they stopped at the nearest place, Zayd came to Ali ؓ and said: We are more entitled to her than you."],[5535,"Ja'far was struck, and I used to love Ja'far ؓ."],[5536,"It was said that Ja'far ؓ received ninety wounds, between sword strikes and spear thrusts."],[5537,"\"When Ja'far ؓ returned from Abyssinia, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ embraced him.\""],[5538,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never dispatched a military expedition in which Zayd b. Haritha ؓ was included without appointing him as their commander."],[5539,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, you established brotherhood between me and Hamza b. 'Abd al-Muttalib ؓ."],[5541,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to my people. I came to them while I was hungry, and I found them eating blood. They said, 'Come.' I said, 'I have come to forbid you from this.' I slept while overcome, and someone came to me in my sleep with a vessel containing a drink and said, 'Take it.' I took it and drank, and I became full and quenched. A man among the people said, 'A man from the nobility of your people has come to you, and you have not honored him with a small draught (of milk).' He said: They brought me their draught, and I said, 'I have no need of it.' They said, 'We saw you in hardship,' so I showed them my stomach, and they all embraced Islam, to the last of them ؓ."],[5542,"I said to Abu Umama ؓ: 'How old were you at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'No one but you has asked me about that before you. I was thirty-three years old. I remember being present at a sermon, and he would lean with the chest of his riding camel, and it would almost unseat me from hearing, so I would put my shoulder against the chest of his camel and push it away.'"],[5544,"There is no man on earth who dies with an atom's weight of pride in his heart but Allah Almighty will place him in the Fire. When Abdullah b. Qays al-Ansari ؓ heard that, he wept. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'O Abdullah b. Qays, why are you weeping?' He said: 'Because of your words.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Rejoice, for you shall be in Paradise.' He said: Then the Prophet ﷺ dispatched an expedition, and he went on a raid and was killed among them as a martyr."],[5546,"Then he passed by, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, Abdullah b. Ja'far ؓ while he was playing with something he was selling, and he was a boy, and he ﷺ said: 'O Allah, bless him in his trade.'"],[5547,"Ibn Numayr narrated to us from Fitr similarly. Its chain is good, meeting the criterion of Abu Dawud. He reported with this chain the beginning of this hadith, but did not mention what I have cited."],[5548,"Allah Almighty blessed him in his sale, or he said: in his transaction."],[5549,"A man brought sugar to Madinah and it became unsellable for him. They said to him: 'Go to Abdullah b. Ja'far ؓ.' So he went to him and bought it from him for ten and eleven (dirhams), and said: 'Whoever wants may take.' The man said: 'Should I take along with them?' He said: 'Take.'"],[5551,"When the verse “Who is it that will lend God a goodly loan...” was revealed, Abu al-Dahdah ؓ said: “O Messenger of God, does God Almighty desire a loan from us?” He ﷺ said: “Yes, O Abu al-Dahdah.” He said: “Show me your hand.” He ﷺ extended his hand to him, and he said: “I have lent my Lord my garden”—his garden contained six hundred palm trees. Then he ؓ came walking until he reached the garden, where Umm al-Dahdah and his family were, and he called out: “O Umm al-Dahdah!” She said: “At your service.” He said: “Leave, for I have lent my Lord.”"],[5553,"He never heard a voice louder than his—meaning Abu Sufyan on the day of al-Yarmuk—while he was under his son’s banner saying: “This is a day of the days of God Almighty. O God, send down Your victory.”"],[5556,"When Amr b. al-As ؓ was near death, he became intensely distressed and began to weep. His son said to him: “Why are you so distressed, when the Messenger of God ﷺ used to appoint you and draw you near?” He said: “He ﷺ used to do that, but I do not know whether he loved me or was simply trying to win me over. However, I bear witness to two men whom the Messenger of God ﷺ died loving: the son of Sumayya, meaning Ammar, and Ibn Mas’ud ؓ.” When his death throes intensified—meaning the final agony—he clasped his hands and placed them at his neck like a collar, saying: “O God, You commanded us and we neglected, You forbade us and we transgressed. Nothing can save us except Your mercy.” He kept repeating this until he died."],[5558,"My father’s grandfather pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[5560,"Al-Harith b. al-Nu’man al-Ansari ؓ came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was conversing privately with Gabriel ﷺ . He sat down and did not greet. Gabriel ﷺ said: “If this man had greeted us, we would have returned his greeting.” He ﷺ asked: “Do you know him?” He replied: “Yes, this is one of the eighty who stood firm with you on the day of Hunayn. Their provision and the provision of their children is upon God, Mighty and Majestic, in Paradise.”"],[5561,"Haritha b. al-Nu’man ؓ came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was conversing privately with Gabriel."],[5563,"I have been hoping for the caliphate ever since the Messenger of God ﷺ said what he said: “O Mu’awiya, if you gain sovereignty, then act well.”"],[5565,"The Messenger of God ﷺ asked me: “From whom are you?” I said: “From Rabi’a.” He said: “From Rabi’a of the horse, those of whom it is said: Were it not for them, the earth would have moved away with its inhabitants. I praise God who has favored you among Rabi’a.”"],[5567,"I gave the Messenger of God ﷺ milk to drink, and he said: “May God grant him enjoyment of his youth.”"],[5569,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Aqil ؓ: “O Abu Yazid, I love you with two kinds of love: love of kinship, and love because of Abu Talib’s love for you.”"],[5572,"My mother took me to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he wiped over my head and prayed for provision for me."],[5573,"My father and my mother took me—the same hadith."],[5575,"I prayed beside a man and began supplicating while holding a pebble. He turned to me and said: O Abu 'Abd Allah, 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud ؓ used to say: If you ask your Lord, do not hold a stone in your hand. When I heard him mention 'Abd Allah, I felt at ease with him and introduced myself. He began to tell me: Abu Bakr ؓ asked permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he granted him permission and gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Then 'Umar ؓ came, and he granted him permission and gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Then 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud ؓ came, and he granted him permission and gave him glad tidings. Then another man came, whom I could name if I wished, and he granted him permission and gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Hudhayfa ؓ was sitting, and he said: Where am I, O Messenger of Allah? He ﷺ said: You are in good, or heading toward good."],[5576,"Where am I? He mentioned it abbreviated from the beginning. : :"],[5578,"He was struck by an arrow while with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in one of his battles. He ﷺ said: O Rafi', if you wish I will remove the arrow but leave the arrowhead, and I will testify for you on the Day of Resurrection that you are a martyr? He said: So he ﷺ did."],[5580,"I hope to meet the Prophet ﷺ and say: O Messenger of Allah, your little servant Anas."],[5582,"When I came to Anas ؓ, he would be told of my location, and I would enter upon him, take his hands and kiss them, saying: May my father be ransomed for these two hands that touched the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. And I would kiss his eyes, saying: May my father be ransomed for these two eyes that saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5584,"I traveled by sea in a ship, and it broke apart with us. I mounted a plank from it, and it cast me into a thicket where there was a lion. Nothing startled me except it. I said: O Abu al-Harith, I am Safina, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah. He said: It struck me with its shoulder, lowered its head, and began nudging me with its shoulder, then walked with me until it set me on the road. Then it struck me with its hand and made a sound for a while, and I thought it was bidding me farewell."],[5587,"'Umar ؓ struck between the shoulders of Ibn Mas'ud ؓ and said: Allah, exalted is He, has placed in your heart, O Ibn Mas'ud, no small amount of knowledge."],[5588,"The first to proclaim the Quran openly in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Makkah was 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud ؓ."],[5589,"He entered the mosque and came to a pillar, stood by it and prayed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the mosque. The Prophet ﷺ said: Our leader is Ibn Mas'ud, while he could not hear him. He recited: Say, O disbelievers, then bowed and prostrated, then stood for the second rak'ah. The Prophet ﷺ said: Be sincere, O Ibn Mas'ud. He recited: Say, He is Allah, the One, then bowed, prostrated, and sat. The Prophet ﷺ said: Supplicate, O Ibn Mas'ud, and you will be answered; ask and you will be given. He ؓ, during that, could not hear him. Ibn Mas'ud ؓ said: O Allah, I ask You for the highest companion, the fullest share of the gardens of bliss, and I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity, and contentment, and glad tidings at the severance of this world. And I ask You for faith that does not turn back, coolness of eyes that never ends, joy that never ceases, success in praise, the garment of piety, the adornment of faith, and the companionship of Your Prophet Muhammad ﷺ in the highest garden of eternity. He said: A man went and gave him the good news."],[5590,"'Abd Allah ؓ was among the people with the finest white garment and the sweetest scent."],[5591,"I do not consider any man more knowledgeable of what was revealed to Muhammad ﷺ than Ibn Mas'ud ؓ. Abu Musa ؓ said: If you say that, he used to hear when others could not hear, and enter where we could not enter ؓ."],[5592,"Ibn Mas'ud ؓ spoke in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, praised and extolled Allah, then said: I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger. Then he ؓ said: I am pleased for you with what Allah and His Messenger are pleased with, and I dislike for you what Allah and His Messenger dislike. The Prophet ﷺ said: I am pleased for my Ummah with what Ibn Umm 'Abd is pleased with for them."],[5593,"Ibn Mas'ud ؓ went to bring the Prophet ﷺ a tooth-stick, and they began looking at the thinness of his legs and marveling. The Prophet ﷺ said: They are heavier in the Scale than Mount Uhud."],[5595,"I used to screen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he bathed, wake him when he slept, and walk with him in the land."],[5597,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, I said to a man of the Ansar: Come, let us ask the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for today they are many. He said: How astonishing of you, O Ibn 'Abbas! Do you think people will need you while among the people are Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ such as they? He said: So I left that, and I began asking the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about hadith. If I heard of a man, I would go to him while he was napping, and I would pillow my cloak at his door, with the wind blowing dust upon me. He would come out, see me, and say: O cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, what brought you? Why did you not send for me so I could come to you? I would say: No, I am more entitled to come to you. Then I would ask him about the hadith. That Ansari man lived until he saw me with people gathered around me asking me, and he said: This youth was wiser than I."],[5598,"I sat with seventy or fifty elders from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and not one of them differed with Ibn 'Abbas ؓ when they met except that he said: It is as you said, or: You have spoken truly."],[5599,"I have not seen anyone more knowledgeable than Ibn 'Abbas ؓ nor more pious than Ibn 'Umar ؓ."],[5600,"I have not seen anyone more reverent of the sacred limits of Allah Almighty than Ibn 'Abbas ؓ. By Allah, if I wished, when I mentioned him, to weep, I would weep."],[5601,"I have not seen Ibn 'Abbas contradicted by anyone without him establishing his point."],[5603,"Abu Dharr ؓ went out to al-Rabadhah, and his appointed time came. He instructed them: Wash me, shroud me, then place me on the main road. The first riders who pass by you, say: This is Abu Dharr, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so help us with his washing and burial. They did so. 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud ؓ came in a group of riders from Iraq, and the funeral bier had been placed on the main road. A boy went up to him and said: This is Abu Dharr, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud ؓ wept and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: You will walk alone, die alone, and be resurrected alone."],[5605,"We went out to perform 'Umrah and headed to the dwelling of Abu Dharr ؓ. There he was coming carrying a camel's bone or it was being carried with him. He came to his dwelling, then came to us and greeted us... and mentioned the hadith. He said to them: For every such-and-such, they slaughter a camel and eat it, and for me in every camel is a bone. A man said: O Abu Dharr, what is your wealth? He ؓ said: I have a herd of camels and a small flock of sheep; in one of them is my son, and in the other is a black slave I bought, and he is to be freed. He serves me until the year ends, then he is free. He said: A man said: O Abu Dharr, by Allah, none of the people we know has more wealth than your companions. He said: By Allah, there is no right in their wealth except that I have the like of it. He said: We began asking him for legal opinions. A man said: O Abu Dharr, we have a man who fasts the entire year except the day of Sacrifice and the day of Breaking the Fast. He ؓ said: He has neither fasted nor broken his fast. He said: But he does such-and-such. He said: He repeated it..."],[5606,"The green sky has not shaded, nor the dusty earth carried, anyone of truer speech than Abu Dharr ؓ. Whoever would like to look at the humility of Jesus son of Mary ﷺ , let him look at Abu Dharr ؓ."],[5607,"I was the fourth of four in Islam: three embraced Islam before me, and I was the fourth. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"Peace be upon you, O Prophet of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, without partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger.\" He said: Then I saw joy in his face ﷺ. He said: \"Who are you?\" I said: \"Jundub, a man from Banu Ghifar.\""],[5608,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"O Abu Dharr, do you think that if I were weighed against forty men among whom you were included, I would outweigh them?\" His wife said to him: \"It is as if you have been reproached.\" He said: \"Be quiet, may Allah fill your mouth with dust.\""],[5609,"I used to hear about Abu Dharr ؓ, and there was no one I was more eager to see and meet than him. Uthman ؓ wrote to him to come to him, so Muawiyah wrote to him: \"If you have any need of Syria and its people, then leave, Abu Dharr, for the people have become burdensome to me.\" Abu Dharr ؓ arrived, and the people cried out: \"This is Abu Dharr, this is Abu Dharr!\" I went out to look at him among those who were looking. He entered the mosque while Uthman ؓ was in it. He went to a pillar and prayed two rak'ahs near it, then came to Uthman ؓ and greeted him. He did not revile him or rebuke him. Uthman ؓ said: \"Where were you on the day when the milch-camels of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were raided?\" He said: \"I was at the well, drawing water.\" Then Abu Dharr ؓ raised his voice and recited: \"And those who hoard gold and silver and do not spend them...\" up to \"...what you used to hoard.\" Then Uthman ؓ ordered him to go out to al-Rabadhah."],[5610,"Indeed, I am the closest of you in seating to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the Day of Resurrection - whoever leaves this world in the same state as when I left him in it. By Allah, there is none of you but has clung to something of this world except me."],[5611,"When he went out to his companions ؓ, he said: \"Uwaymir is the wise man of my Ummah, and Jundub is the outcast of my Ummah. He will live alone, die alone, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will resurrect him alone.\""],[5612,"I wish I were a tree that is cut down."],[5614,"I came to Madinah, and a man brought me to the daughter of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas ؓ, and she narrated to me the story of Thabit... Then she mentioned the hadith... She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Rather, you will live a praiseworthy life, be killed as a martyr, and Allah will admit you to Paradise.\" When the day of Yamamah came, he went out with Khalid ibn al-Walid ؓ to Musaylimah the Liar. He said: When he met the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and attacked them, they were routed. He said: He said to Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah ؓ: \"This is not how we used to fight alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Then each of them dug a pit, and the people attacked them. They kept fighting until they were killed, may Allah have mercy on them. Thabit ؓ had a precious coat of mail, and a Muslim man passed by him and took it. While a Muslim man was sleeping, Thabit ibn Qays ؓ came to him in his dream and said: \"I enjoin upon you a bequest: beware of saying, 'This is a dream,' and neglecting it. When I was killed yesterday, a Muslim man passed by me and took my coat of mail. His dwelling is at the far end of the army, and by his tent is a horse prancing in its tether. He has placed a cooking pot over the coat of mail and put a saddle on top of the pot. Go to Khalid ibn al-Walid ؓ and tell him to send for my coat of mail and take it. When you come to the successor of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, inform him that I owe such-and-such a debt, and I am owed such-and-such a debt. So-and-so, my slave, is free, and so-and-so. Beware of saying, 'This is a dream,' and neglecting it.\" The man went to Khalid ibn al-Walid ؓ and informed him, so he sent for the coat of mail. He looked at a tent at the far end of the army, and there was a horse prancing in its tether. He looked in the tent and found no one there. They entered, lifted the saddle, and beneath it was a cooking pot. They lifted it, and the coat of mail was under it. It was brought to Khalid ibn al-Walid ؓ. When he came to Madinah, the man told Abu Bakr ؓ of his dream, and he executed his bequest after his death. We do not know of any Muslim whose bequest was executed after his death except Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas ؓ."],[5616,"The first person to enter through the gate of the mosque will be a man from the people of Paradise. Abdullah ibn Salam ؓ entered. A man said to him: \"The Prophet ﷺ said such-and-such. What deed of yours do you consider most reliable for your hope?\" He said: \"Indeed, my deeds are weak. The most reliable deed for which I hope is soundness of my heart and leaving what does not concern me.\""],[5618,"My father Hanifah ibn Hudhaym said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I am a man with many sons, and this is the dearest of my sons to me, so bless him.\" He ﷺ said: \"O boy\" - and he took my hand and wiped my head - \"may Allah bless you.\" He said: I indeed saw Hanzalah ibn Hudhaym ؓ being brought a person with a swelling, and he would place his hand on it and say: \"In the name of Allah,\" and the swelling would go away."],[5620,"I went out seeking my stray camels, and I took with me milk in a leather water-skin. Then I said to myself: \"I have not been fair. Where is the water for ablution?\" So I poured out the milk and filled it with water. I said: \"This is for ablution, and this is for drinking.\" I kept seeking my camels. Whenever I wanted to perform ablution, I poured water from the skin and performed ablution, and whenever I wanted to drink, I poured milk and drank it. I continued like that for three days. Asma' al-Bahraniyyah said to him: \"O Abu Ka'b, was it a skin or a milk-skin?\" He said: \"You are indeed idle. Rather, it protected from hunger and quenched thirst. Indeed, I narrated this hadith to a group of my people, among them Ali ibn al-Harith, the chief of Banu Qiyan. He said: 'I do not think what you say is as you said.' I said: 'Allah knows best about that.' Then I returned to my dwelling and slept that night. At dawn prayer, he was at my door. I said: 'May Allah have mercy on you. Why did you trouble yourself to come to me? Could you not have sent for me and I would come to you?' He said: 'I am more entitled to come to you. No sooner did I sleep last night than someone came to me and said: \"You are the one who denies the one who narrates the blessings of Allah, the Exalted.\"' Then I went out until I came to Madinah. I came to Uthman ibn Affan ؓ and asked him about something concerning my religion. I said: \"O Commander of the Faithful, I am a man from Banu al-Harith from the people of Yemen. I want to ask you about some matters, so instruct your doorkeeper not to bar me.\" He ؓ said: \"O Waththab, when the Harithi comes, permit him.\" So whenever I came, I knocked on the door. He said: \"Who is this?\" I said: \"The Harithi.\" He said: \"Enter.\" I entered, and Uthman ؓ was sitting with a group of silent men around him who did not speak, as if birds were on their heads. I greeted and sat down, but I did not ask him about anything because of what I saw of their state."],[5622,"I entered upon al-Bara' ibn Malik ؓ while he was lying on his bed, reciting some verses of poetry as if singing them. I said to him: \"May Allah have mercy on you. Allah has given you something better than this: the Quran.\" He said: \"Do you fear that I might die on my bed? No, by Allah! Allah would not deprive me of that, for I have killed a hundred men in single combat, besides those I fought alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[5624,"I said to Abd Khayr: \"How old are you?\" He said: \"One hundred and twenty years.\" I said: \"Do you remember anything from the days of ignorance?\" He said: \"Yes. We were in the lands of Yemen when a letter from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, calling people to abundant good. My father was among those who went out while I was a boy. When he returned, he said to my mother: 'Order this pot to be poured out for the dogs, for we have embraced Islam.' So he became a Muslim.\""],[5626,"I was born two years into the caliphate of Umar ؓ"],[5628,"Subayh asked Abu Uthman al-Nahdi while I was listening: \"Did you meet the Prophet ﷺ?\" He said: \"Yes. I accepted Islam during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I paid him three charities, but I did not meet him. And I went on several campaigns during the time of Umar ibn al-Khattab ؓ. I witnessed the conquest of al-Qadisiyyah, Jalula', Nihawand, al-Yarmuk, Adharbijan, Mihran, and Rustum. We used to eat ghee and leave the fat.\" He said: \"Then I asked him about vessels.\" He said: \"They were not asked about.\" Meaning the vessels of the polytheists."],[5630,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was talking to his companions, he said: \"A rider from the best people of the East will appear to you from this mountain pass.\" Umar ibn al-Khattab ؓ stood up and went towards that direction. He met thirteen riders, welcomed them, and brought them close. He said: \"Who are the people?\" They said: \"A people from Abd al-Qays.\" He said: \"What brought you to these lands? Trade?\" They said: \"No.\" He said: \"Would you sell these swords of yours?\" They said: \"No.\" He said: \"Perhaps you have come seeking this man?\" They said: \"Yes.\" So he walked with them, talking to them, until he saw the Prophet ﷺ. He said to them: \"This is your companion whom you seek.\" The people threw themselves off their saddles. Some of them ran quickly, some of them jogged, and some of them walked, until they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They took his hand and kissed it, and sat with him. Al-Ashajj remained—he was the youngest of the people. He made the camels kneel, hobbled them, and gathered the people's belongings. Then he came walking calmly until he reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, took his hand and kissed it. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You have two qualities that Allah Almighty and His Messenger love.\" He said: \"What are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He ﷺ said: \"Deliberateness and calmness.\" He said: \"Is it a natural disposition I was created with, or something I have acquired?\" He ﷺ said: \"Rather, it is natural.\" He said: \"Praise be to Allah who created me with what Allah and His Messenger love.\" Then the people turned to some dates and ate them."],[5632,"I heard Abu Anbah al-Khawlani, and he was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and he was among those who ate blood in the pre-Islamic era."],[5634,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him on a military expedition alone."],[5636,"I was born when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah, and the Prophet ﷺ passed away when I was ten years old."],[5637,"Shall I not tell you about the lowest of the people of Paradise? They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'A man will enter from the gate of Paradise, and his servants will meet him and say: \"Welcome, our master! It is time for you to return.\"' He said: 'Then carpets will be spread for him for forty years. Then he will look to his right and to his left and see gardens, and he will say: \"For whom is what is here?\" It will be said: \"For you.\" When he finishes, a red ruby or a green emerald will be raised for him, having seventy branches, in each branch seventy rooms, in each room seventy doors. It will be said to him: \"Recite and ascend.\" He said: 'He will ascend until he reaches the couch of his kingdom and reclines on it. Its width is a mile by a mile, and it has extra space. Seventy thousand dishes of gold will be brought to him, no dish having the same color as its companion. He will find the taste of the last dish like the taste of the first. Then drinks of various kinds will be brought to him, and he will drink as much as he desires. Then the servants will say: \"Leave him and his wives.\" (Abu Shihab said: I think he said:) The servants will withdraw from him, and there will be a houri seated on the couch of her kingdom. He will see the marrow of her leg from behind the flesh and blood. He will say to her: \"Who are you?\" She will say: \"I am one of the houris with large eyes who have been hidden for you.\" He will look at her for forty years without lifting his gaze from her. Then he will raise his gaze to the rooms above him, and there will be another more beautiful than her. She will say to him: \"Is it not time that we have a share of you?\" He will ascend to her and look at her for forty years without turning his gaze away from her. When the bliss has reached its utmost with them, and they think that there is nothing better than them, the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will manifest Himself to them, and they will look at the face of the Most Merciful, and they will forget all the bliss they had witnessed when they look at the face of the Most Merciful. Then He will say: \"O people of Paradise, declare My oneness!\" They will respond with the declaration of oneness. Then He will say: \"O Dawud, glorify Me as you used to glorify Me in the world.\" Dawud will glorify his Lord, Mighty and Majestic.' Ahmad b. Yunus said: I said to Abu Shihab: 'The hadith of Khalid b. Dinar about the mention of Paradise – is it marfu'?' He said: 'Yes.' In the Dar al-'Asima edition: (umm), but what is established is from the Musnad of 'Abd b. Humayd and the Ittihaf of al-Busiri."],[5639,"Hafsah will marry someone better than Uthman, and Uthman will marry someone better than Hafsah. So he ﷺ married his daughter to him."],[5641,"The mistress of the believing women is so-and-so, and Khadijah bint Khuwaylid ؓ was the first of the Muslim women to accept Islam."],[5642,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about Khadijah ؓ because she died before the obligatory duties were prescribed. He ﷺ said: \"I saw her in a river of the rivers of Paradise, in a house of reeds, with no noise in it and no fatigue.\""],[5644,"When the concession of dry ablution with clean earth was revealed to them, Abu Bakr ؓ entered upon A'ishah ؓ and said: \"You are indeed blessed. The concession of dry ablution was revealed for us.\""],[5645,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was wearing a garment with a hem, and as soon as he married me, modesty was cast upon me."],[5646,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah, Exalted, will separate between the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire. And when it is Monday and Thursday, pulpits of light will be placed around the Throne, and pulpits of chrysolite and ruby. The angels entrusted with them will say: 'Our Lord, for whom have You placed these pulpits?' It will be cast upon their mouths: 'For the strangers.' They will say: 'Our Lord, who are the strangers?' It will be cast upon their mouths: 'A people who loved one another for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, without having seen Him.' While they are like that, each man of them will come, knowing his seat better than one of you knows his seat in his pavilion with his wife in the abode of this world. Their nearness to the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will be according to their ranks in Paradise. When the people are complete, the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, will say: 'My servants, My creation, My visitors, and those who loved one another for My majesty without having seen Me – feed them.' They will be fed. Then He will say: 'Give them fruit.' Then they will be brought fruit containing every desire, pleasure, and fragrant scent. Then the Lord will say: 'Give them drink.' They will be brought vessels of which it is not known whether the vessel is whiter or what is in it. Then He will say: 'Clothe them.' They will be brought fruit that cleaves the ground like the breasts of virgin women; in each fruit are seventy garments, no garment resembling its sister. Then He will say: 'Perfume them.' A wind will blow and fill them with strong musk, the like of which no human has ever smelled. Then He will say: 'Remove the cover for them.' Between Allah, Exalted, and the nearest of His creation to Him are seventy thousand veils of light. The nearest of His creation to Him, from among the angels brought near, cannot raise his head to the lowest of those veils. Then those veils will be lifted, and the people will fall prostrate because of what they see of the greatness of Allah, Exalted. The Lord, Majestic and High, will say: 'Raise your heads. You are not in the abode of action; rather, you are in the abode of blessing and abiding. You will have the like of what you are in, and its like with it. Are you pleased, My servants?' They will say: 'We are pleased, our Lord, if You are pleased with us.' Then the people will return to their dwellings, having been doubled in beauty, spouses, food, drink, and everything of their affair in that manner. While they are like that, suddenly something beside them will light up his temples with beauty, and he will say: 'Who are you?' It will say: 'I am the one of whom Allah, Exalted, said: \"And with Us is more.\"' While they are like that, seventy thousand angels will come to each servant, with each angel a vessel unlike its companion, and upon his vessel something unlike its companion. They will consult among themselves as to which of them should be taken from. They will say: 'This, your Lord has sent with me to you, and He conveys peace to you.' He said: 'There are no two servants who became brothers for the sake of Allah, Exalted, but their dwellings face each other. The servant looks to the farthest part of his brother's dwelling, except that when they desire something of the pleasures of women, the veils are let down between them.'"],[5647,"And al-Bazzar narrated it from the route of 'Abd al-Rahman b. Muhammad al-Muharibi, from Abu Sa'id al-Baqqal with it, and more complete than it."],[5648,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I was crying, and he said: 'What makes you cry?' I said: 'Fatimah ؓ insulted me.' He ﷺ said: 'O Fatimah, did you insult A'ishah?' She said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He ﷺ said: 'Do you not love whom I love and hate whom I hate?' She said: 'Yes.' He ﷺ said: 'For I love A'ishah, so love her.' Fatimah ؓ said: 'We will never say anything to A'ishah ؓ that hurts her.'"],[5649,"A'ishah ؓ was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Leave A'ishah alone, for she is a woman who fasts much and prays much at night; she is my wife in this world and the Hereafter.'"],[5650,"A man mentioned A'ishah ؓ in his presence and spoke ill of her, so 'Ammar ؓ said: 'Be silent, you repulsive, rebuked one! Do you hurt the beloved of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?'"],[5651,"No one hates me in this world except that I disavow him in the Hereafter."],[5652,"A man arrived after the death of A'ishah ؓ, and 'Ubayd b. 'Umayr asked him: 'How did you find the people's grief over her?' He said: 'By Allah, their grief was not as intense as all that.' 'Ubayd b. 'Umayr said: 'Only one for whom she was a mother grieves over A'ishah ؓ.'"],[5653,"Umm Salamah ؓ heard the cry over A'ishah ؓ, so she sent her slave girl, saying: 'See what she has done.' She came back and said: 'She has passed away.' Umm Salamah said: 'May Allah have mercy on her. By the One in whose hand is my soul, she was the most beloved of people to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except her father.'"],[5654,"They both came to A'ishah ؓ, and she said: 'O so-and-so, have you heard the hadith of Hafsah ؓ?' He said: 'Yes, O Mother of the Believers.' 'Abd Allah b. Safwan ؓ said: 'And what is that, O Mother of the Believers?' She said: 'There are nine qualities in me that were not in any other woman except what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gave to Maryam daughter of 'Imran ؓ. By Allah, I do not say this to boast over any of my companions.' 'Abd Allah b. Safwan ؓ said: 'What are they, O Mother of the Believers?' She said: 'The angel descended with my likeness; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was seven years old; I was given to him ﷺ when I was nine; he ﷺ married me as a virgin, no other person sharing me with him; revelation came to him ﷺ while he and I were under one blanket; I was the most beloved of women to him ﷺ; verses of the Qur'an were revealed concerning me, and the community almost perished because of them; I saw Jibril ﷺ , and none of his other wives ﷺ saw him besides me; and he ﷺ passed away in my house, with no one present except the angel and me.'"],[5655,"I was given nine things that no woman was given except Maryam... and she mentioned something similar. She said: 'Revelation would descend upon him while he was with his family and they were apart from him, but it would descend upon him ﷺ while I was with him under his blanket. I am the daughter of his caliph and his truthful friend; I was created good and at the hands of a good one, and I have been promised forgiveness and generous provision.'"],[5657,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit her and called her 'the martyr'. She had compiled the Qur'an and hadith. 'Umar ؓ stood among the people and said: 'Umm Waraqah was grieved by her slave boy and her slave girl, and they killed her, then they fled. They were brought and crucified.' 'Umar ؓ said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke the truth; he used to say: \"Come, let us visit the martyr.\"'"],[5659,"I brought the camels of the zakat to the Prophet ﷺ, and he wiped my head and supplicated for me."],[5661,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consummated his marriage with Zaynab bint Jahsh ؓ, and she had been endowed with beauty, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was extremely modest."],[5662,"The Prophet ﷺ had nine wives. One day he ﷺ said, \"The best of you is the one with the longest hand.\" So each one stood and placed her hand against the wall. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I do not mean this; rather, the most generous of you in giving.\""],[5663,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah, Exalted, will separate between the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire. And when it is Monday and Thursday, pulpits of light will be placed around the Throne, and pulpits of chrysolite and ruby. The angels entrusted with them will say: 'Our Lord, for whom have You placed these pulpits?' It will be cast upon their mouths: 'For the strangers.' They will say: 'Our Lord, who are the strangers?' It will be cast upon their mouths: 'A people who loved one another for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, without having seen Him.' While they are like that, each man of them will come, knowing his seat better than one of you knows his seat in his pavilion with his wife in the abode of this world. Their nearness to the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will be according to their ranks in Paradise. When the people are complete, the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, will say: 'My servants, My creation, My visitors, and those who loved one another for My majesty without having seen Me – feed them.' They will be fed. Then He will say: 'Give them fruit.' Then they will be brought fruit containing every desire, pleasure, and fragrant scent. Then the Lord will say: 'Give them drink.' They will be brought vessels of which it is not known whether the vessel is whiter or what is in it. Then He will say: 'Clothe them.' They will be brought fruit that cleaves the ground like the breasts of virgin women; in each fruit are seventy garments, no garment resembling its sister. Then He will say: 'Perfume them.' A wind will blow and fill them with strong musk, the like of which no human has ever smelled. Then He will say: 'Remove the cover for them.' Between Allah, Exalted, and the nearest of His creation to Him are seventy thousand veils of light. The nearest of His creation to Him, from among the angels brought near, cannot raise his head to the lowest of those veils. Then those veils will be lifted, and the people will fall prostrate because of what they see of the greatness of Allah, Exalted. The Lord, Majestic and High, will say: 'Raise your heads. You are not in the abode of action; rather, you are in the abode of blessing and abiding. You will have the like of what you are in, and its like with it. Are you pleased, My servants?' They will say: 'We are pleased, our Lord, if You are pleased with us.' Then the people will return to their dwellings, having been doubled in beauty, spouses, food, drink, and everything of their affair in that manner. While they are like that, suddenly something beside them will light up his temples with beauty, and he will say: 'Who are you?' It will say: 'I am the one of whom Allah, Exalted, said: \"And with Us is more.\"' While they are like that, seventy thousand angels will come to each servant, with each angel a vessel unlike its companion, and upon his vessel something unlike its companion. They will consult among themselves as to which of them should be taken from. They will say: 'This, your Lord has sent with me to you, and He conveys peace to you.' He said: 'There are no two servants who became brothers for the sake of Allah, Exalted, but their dwellings face each other. The servant looks to the farthest part of his brother's dwelling, except that when they desire something of the pleasures of women, the veils are let down between them.'"],[5665,"Maymunah ؓ became gravely ill in Makkah, and she had none of her sister's sons with her. She said, \"Take me out of Makkah, for I will not die in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed me that I would not die in it.\" So they carried her to Sarif, to the tree under which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had consummated his marriage with her, at the site of the dome, and she died there. When we placed her in her grave niche, I took my cloak and placed it under her cheek in the niche, but Ibn Abbas ؓ took it and threw it away."],[5667,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left his wives behind on the day of Uhud in Madinah, he left them in a fortress, among them Safiyyah bint Abd al-Muttalib ؓ, and he left Hassan b. Thabit ؓ with them. A man from the polytheists approached to enter upon them. Safiyyah ؓ said to Hassan b. Thabit ؓ, \"Deal with the man.\" But Hassan ؓ was cowardly and refused. So Safiyyah ؓ took up a sword and struck the polytheist with it until she killed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was informed of that, and he allotted a share of the spoils to Safiyyah ؓ just as he allotted to the men."],[5670,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to Sawdah his decision to divorce her. She said, \"Among all his wives, he divorced me?\" Then she sat in his path from Aisha's house. He passed by her, and she said, \"I adjure you by the One who sent down the Book upon you and chose you over all creation: did you divorce me out of anger you felt toward me? I adjure you by the One who sent down the Book upon you and chose you over all creation: take me back. For by Allah, I have grown old, and I have no need of men, but I wish to be resurrected as one of your wives.\" So he took her back. She then said, \"I give my day and night to the delight of the Messenger of Allah's eye, Aisha.\""],[5672,"When Abu Salamah ؓ was on his deathbed, Umm Salamah ؓ said, \"To whom do you entrust me?\" He said ؓ, \"O Allah, grant Umm Salamah someone better than Abu Salamah.\" When he passed away, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to her. She said, \"I am advanced in age.\" He ﷺ said, \"I am older than you. The dependents are upon Allah Almighty and His Messenger. As for jealousy, I will supplicate Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to remove it.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her and sent her two millstones and a water jar."],[5673,"Shall I not tell you about the lowest of the people of Paradise? They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'A man will enter from the gate of Paradise, and his servants will meet him and say: \"Welcome, our master! It is time for you to return.\"' He said: 'Then carpets will be spread for him for forty years. Then he will look to his right and to his left and see gardens, and he will say: \"For whom is what is here?\" It will be said: \"For you.\" When he finishes, a red ruby or a green emerald will be raised for him, having seventy branches, in each branch seventy rooms, in each room seventy doors. It will be said to him: \"Recite and ascend.\" He said: 'He will ascend until he reaches the couch of his kingdom and reclines on it. Its width is a mile by a mile, and it has extra space. Seventy thousand dishes of gold will be brought to him, no dish having the same color as its companion. He will find the taste of the last dish like the taste of the first. Then drinks of various kinds will be brought to him, and he will drink as much as he desires. Then the servants will say: \"Leave him and his wives.\" (Abu Shihab said: I think he said:) The servants will withdraw from him, and there will be a houri seated on the couch of her kingdom. He will see the marrow of her leg from behind the flesh and blood. He will say to her: \"Who are you?\" She will say: \"I am one of the houris with large eyes who have been hidden for you.\" He will look at her for forty years without lifting his gaze from her. Then he will raise his gaze to the rooms above him, and there will be another more beautiful than her. She will say to him: \"Is it not time that we have a share of you?\" He will ascend to her and look at her for forty years without turning his gaze away from her. When the bliss has reached its utmost with them, and they think that there is nothing better than them, the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will manifest Himself to them, and they will look at the face of the Most Merciful, and they will forget all the bliss they had witnessed when they look at the face of the Most Merciful. Then He will say: \"O people of Paradise, declare My oneness!\" They will respond with the declaration of oneness. Then He will say: \"O Dawud, glorify Me as you used to glorify Me in the world.\" Dawud will glorify his Lord, Mighty and Majestic.' Ahmad b. Yunus said: I said to Abu Shihab: 'The hadith of Khalid b. Dinar about the mention of Paradise – is it marfu'?' He said: 'Yes.' In the Dar al-'Asima edition: (umm), but what is established is from the Musnad of 'Abd b. Humayd and the Ittihaf of al-Busiri."],[5674,"Abu Salamah ؓ came... then he mentioned the hadith about his death, and that Abu Bakr ؓ proposed to her but she refused him, then Umar ؓ proposed but she refused him, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to propose to her. She said ؓ, \"I have three traits.\" Umar ؓ heard what she said in response to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he became angrier for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than he did for himself. He went to her and said, \"Are you the one who refuses the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? With what do you refuse him?\" She said, \"O Ibn al-Khattab, I have such and such.\" And in the hadith: \"As for what you mentioned about jealousy, I will supplicate Allah Almighty to remove it.\" He said: So she became among the women as if she were not one of them; she did not feel the jealousy that women feel."],[5675,"That with which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Salamah ؓ was something worth ten dirhams."],[5678,"Umar ؓ entered upon Hafsah ؓ while she was weeping. He said, \"What is wrong with you? Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ divorce you? He had divorced you once before, then took you back because of me. By Allah, if he divorces you another time, I will never speak to you again.\""],[5679,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divorced Hafsah ؓ. Her maternal uncles Qudamah and Uthman b. Maz'un ؓ came, and she wept, saying, \"By Allah, he did not divorce me out of being satisfied.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, and she covered herself with a garment. He said, \"Jibril ﷺ said to me: Take back Hafsah, for she fasts much and prays much, and she will be your wife in Paradise.\""],[5680,"Yunus b. Muhammad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Imran, from Qays b. Zayd or Yazid, something similar."],[5682,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ captured Safiyyah ؓ on the day of Qurayzah and al-Nadir, the day when Allah, Mighty and Majestic, granted him victory. He came leading her as a captive. When she saw the women, she said: 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah.' So he released her, and her forearm ؓ was in his hand ﷺ. Then he freed her, then he proposed to her and married her, and he gave her as her dowry Razinah."],[5683,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and there was no one among the people more hateful to me than him. He ﷺ said: 'Your people did such and such.' She ؓ said: 'So I did not rise from my seat, and there was no one among the people more beloved to me than him.'"],[5684,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted me behind him on the rear of his camel. She ؓ said: 'I started to doze off, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touched me with his hand and said: \"O you, O daughter of Huyayy.\" And he kept saying: \"O Safiyyah, I apologize to you for what I did to your people. They said to me such and such. They said to me such and such.\"'"],[5685,"I never saw anyone with better character than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5687,"Umm Ayman ؓ set out as an emigrant to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Makkah to Madinah, walking, with no provisions with her, while she was fasting on a very hot day. She was seized by severe thirst until she almost died of extreme thirst. She said: 'When the sun set, I suddenly felt a flapping sound above my head. I raised my head and saw a bucket of water with a white rope. It came near me until, when it was within my reach, I took it and drank from it until I was quenched. After that, I used to fast on hot days and then walk in the sun in order to become thirsty, but I never became thirsty again.'"],[5689,"The Prophet ﷺ had given her at Khaybar the harvest of fifty wasqs of dates and twenty wasqs of barley."],[5692,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to me, but I excused myself to him, and he accepted my excuse. Then Allah revealed: 'O Prophet, indeed We have made lawful to you your wives...' up to His saying: '...who emigrated with you.' She said: 'I was not lawful for him, and I had not emigrated with him; I was among the released ones.'"],[5694,"Umm Malik ؓ came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a small skin of ghee. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Bilal ؓ to squeeze it. Then he returned it to her, and she went back and found it full of ghee. She came and said: 'Has something been revealed concerning me, O Messenger of Allah?' He ﷺ said: 'And what is that, O Umm Malik?' She said: 'You returned my gift to me.' He said: 'So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Bilal ؓ and asked him about that. He said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I squeezed it until I felt ashamed.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Rejoice, O Umm Malik! This is a blessing whose reward Allah has hastened for you.\"'"],[5696,"I used to hear Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ say: 'No one from Quraysh enters a door except that people enter with him.' I did not know the interpretation of his saying until Umar ؓ was stabbed. Then he ordered Suhayb ؓ to lead the people in prayer and ordered that food be prepared for the people."],[5697,"Were it not that Quraysh would become arrogant, I would have told them what they have with Allah, Mighty and Majestic. O Allah, You made their first taste punishment, so make their last taste bounty."],[5698,"[Chain of narration]"],[5699,"Do not revile Quraysh, for the knowledge of their scholar would fill the earth with knowledge. O Allah, You have made the first of Quraysh taste exemplary punishment and retribution, so make their last taste bounty."],[5700,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and heard him say: 'Observe Quraysh, listen to their speech but do not follow their deeds.'"],[5701,"Seek strength and trustworthiness as rulers from Quraysh, for a strong man of Quraysh has two merits over the strongest of others, and a trustworthy man of Quraysh has two merits over the most trustworthy of others."],[5702,"4932 4131 / 2 - Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad b. 'Umar al-Waki'i narrated to us, Mu'ammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us from it."],[5703,"People are followers of Quraysh; the best of them follow the best of Quraysh, and the worst of them follow the worst of Quraysh."],[5704,"Learn from Quraysh and do not teach them, and give precedence to Quraysh and do not put them behind, for a man of Quraysh has the strength of two men from other than Quraysh."],[5706,"A man may stand up from his seat for his brother, except Banu Hashim, for they do not stand for anyone."],[5707,"The first of people to perish will be Quraysh, and the first of Quraysh to perish will be Banu Hashim."],[5709,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: 'For the poor emigrants who were expelled...' (He said): Those who prayed the two qiblahs with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5711,"O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, the children of their children, their freedmen, and their neighbors."],[5712,"We stayed in Madinah for two years before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, building mosques and establishing prayer."],[5713,"I saw al-Hajjaj beating 'Abbas b. Sahl during the governorship of Ibn al-Zubayr ؓ. Sahl b. Sa'd ؓ came to him, an old man with two braids, wearing two garments: an izar and a rida'. He stood before the two rows and said: 'O Hajjaj, do you not preserve among us the bequest of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoin regarding you?' He said: 'To be good to the good-doers of the Ansar and to pardon their wrongdoers.' So he released him."],[5714,"They said: O Messenger of God, we have not seen the like of a people whom we stayed with, meaning the Helpers. They shared their wealth with us and spared us the burden, and we feared that they might have taken all the reward. He ﷺ said: No, as long as you supplicate to God - Mighty and Majestic - for them and praise them, they will not have taken all the reward."],[5715,"O God, bless them, meaning the slave girls of Banu al-Najjar."],[5716,"He used to visit the Helpers frequently, both privately and publicly. When he ﷺ visited privately, he would come to a man in his home, and when he visited publicly, he would come to the mosque."],[5717,"Usayd b. Hudayr ؓ invited me, and I cauterized his sciatic nerve. He told me two hadiths. He said: Two families of my people came to me: a family from Banu Zafar and a family from Banu Mu'awiyah. They said: Speak to the Messenger of God ﷺ for us, or something like that. So I spoke to him, and he ﷺ said: Yes, I will allocate to each family of them a half. If God - Mighty and Majestic - restores, we will restore to them. He said: I said: May God reward you well, O Messenger of God. He ﷺ said: And you, may God reward you well, for you are, as far as I know, chaste and patient. He said: And I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: You will encounter after me preferential treatment. When it was the time of Umar, he distributed garments among the people and sent me one of them. I found it too small, so I gave it to my son. While I was praying, a young man of Quraysh passed by me wearing a garment from those garments, dragging it. I remembered the saying of the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ spoke the truth. A man went to Umar and informed him. He came while I was praying and said: Pray, O Usayd. When I finished my prayer, he said: That garment I sent to so-and-so, and he is a Badri, Uhudi, Aqabi. This young man came to him and bought it from him and wore it. Did you think that would happen in my time? He said: I said: By God, O Commander of the Faithful, I did not think that would happen in your time."],[5719,"Quraysh, the Helpers, Juhaynah, Muzaynah, Aslam, Ghifar, Ashja', and Sulaym are my allies. They have no ally besides God and His Messenger."],[5721,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ along with a man from Banu Amir. He said: From whom are you? They said: From Banu Amir. He said: Welcome to you, you are from me."],[5722,"I came to visit the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and 'A'ishah ؓ, and he was receiving revelation. When it was lifted from him, he ﷺ said to 'A'ishah: 'Hand me my cloak.' He went out and entered the mosque, and there was a group of people in it, no other group being in the mosque. He sat in a corner of the people until the one reminding had finished his reminder. Then he recited: 'The revelation of the prostration.' The people were unable to fit in the mosque, so 'A'ishah ؓ sent to her family: 'Attend the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for I have seen something from him I have never seen.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head, and Abu Bakr ؓ said: \"You prolonged the prostration, O Messenger of Allah.\" He ﷺ said: \"I prostrated in gratitude to my Lord for what He gave me from my nation: seventy thousand who will enter Paradise.\" Abu Bakr ؓ said: \"O Messenger of Allah, your nation is larger and better, so ask for more for them,\" until he said it twice or three times. 'Umar ؓ said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, your nation has encompassed you.\""],[5723,"And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hajjaj, with it."],[5724,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about the tribes of the Arabs. He said: He was distracted from them that day, or they were distracted from him, except that they asked him about three tribes. They asked him about Banu Amir, and he said: A bright camel that eats from the edges of trees. They asked him about Ghatafan, and he said: A flower that gushes water. They asked him about Banu Tamim, and he said: A red hill; those who oppose them will not harm them. And the people said about them, then the Prophet ﷺ said: God has refused for Banu Tamim anything but good. They are large-headed, sound in judgment, firm-footed, the strongest of people in fighting the Dajjal, and the supporters of truth at the end of time."],[5726,"Among the best of people are the kings: the kings of Himyar, Sha'ban, al-Sakun, and the Ash'aris."],[5728,"Banu Najiyah were mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: They are a tribe from me. He said: And I think he said: And I am from them. It may be that the Messenger of God ﷺ said otherwise, meaning Samah b. Lu'ayy. A man said: The attachment to Samah is not fitting. Or it may be that the man said that, and the Messenger of God ﷺ replied to him."],[5729,"They are a tribe from me. Shu'bah said: And I think he said: And I am from them."],[5731,"I said to Sa'd b. Ibrahim: 'Have you heard what is mentioned about Banu Najiyah from the Prophet ﷺ: that they are a clan from me and I am from them, from a reliable source?' He said: 'Yes, that is narrated from Sa'id b. Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl ؓ.' He said: 'And they came to 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf ؓ and gifted him 'ilafiyyah saddles.'"],[5734,"The best dwellings of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar, then Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu al-Harith, then Banu Sa'idah, and in all the dwellings of the Ansar there is good."],[5736,"I do not accept a gift from a Bedouin. Then Umm Sunbulah al-A'rabiyyah came to him with a bowl of milk that she gifted to him. He ﷺ said: 'Pour some of it into this bowl.' So she poured it, and he ﷺ took it and drank. I said to him: 'You said: I do not accept a gift from a Bedouin.' He ﷺ said: 'The Bedouins of Aslam are not Bedouins; rather they are the people of our desert, and we are the people of their settled area. If they call us, we answer them, and if we call them, they answer.'"],[5738,"The best people of the East are 'Abd al-Qays."],[5740,"The delegation of Bajilah came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Begin with the Ahmasiyyin,' and he supplicated for us."],[5742,"When people differ, the truth is with Mudar, and when Rabi'ah becomes mighty, that is a humiliation for Islam."],[5743,"I came to al-Miqdam b. Ma'dikarib in the mosque and said: 'O Abu Yazid, the people claim that you did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'Glory be to Allah! By Allah, I saw him while I was walking with my uncle, and he took hold of this ear of mine and said to my uncle: \"Do you think this one remembers his mother or his father?\" We said to him...'"],[5745,"Al-Hakam b. 'Amr al-Ghifari wrote to Mu'awiyah ؓ from Khurasan: 'The polytheists - meaning - have become numerous against him.' So he wrote to him: 'Appoint Bakr b. Wa'il to be in charge of them, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The enemy will not prevail over Bakr b. Wa'il.'"],[5747,"The furthest people from Islam are the 'Ibad from the Romans."],[5749,"Evil is sixty-one parts: one part is in the jinn and humans, and sixty are in the Berbers."],[5751,"Do not revile the companions of Muhammad ﷺ, for the standing of one of them is better than the deeds of any of you for his entire life."],[5752,"The example of my companions among my nation is like the stars by which they are guided; when they disappear, they become confused."],[5753,"My Companions are like the stars; whoever you follow, you will be guided. Whichever of them you take their saying, you will be guided."],[5754,"If a man had gold equal to Mount Uhud and spent it in the way of Allah, the Exalted, and on widows, the poor, and the orphans, he would never attain the merit of a man from my Companions for even an hour of the day."],[5755,"The best people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then the later ones are worse."],[5757,"And Abu Ya'la said: Zakariyya b. Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us - and he mentioned it."],[5758,"You will continue to be in good as long as there is among you someone who saw me and accompanied me. By Allah, you will continue to be in good as long as there is among you someone who saw someone who saw me and accompanied someone who accompanied me."],[5759,"Do not revile the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ, for Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has commanded seeking forgiveness for them, and He knows that they will innovate and do things."],[5760,"After me, my Companions will have a lapse that Allah, the Exalted, will forgive due to their precedence with me. Some people after me will act upon it and Allah, the Exalted, will cast them into the Fire on their faces."],[5761,"A time will surely come upon the people when an army goes out and it is said: 'Is there anyone among you from the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ?' They will seek him but will not find him. Then an army goes out and it is said: 'Is there anyone among you who saw anyone from the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ?' They will seek him but will not find him. If any of my Companions were beyond the sea, they would come to him."],[5762,"A time will surely come upon the people when an army from their armies goes out and it is said: 'Is there anyone among you who accompanied Muhammad ﷺ, so that you may seek victory through him and be granted victory?' It is said: 'No.' Then it is said: 'Is there anyone among you who accompanied his Companions?' And it is said: 'Who saw someone who accompanied his Companions?' If they heard of him from beyond the seas, they would come to him."],[5763,"An expedition is sent, and it is said: 'Is there anyone among you who accompanied Muhammad ﷺ?' It is said: 'Yes.' So he is sought and the man is found, and victory is sought through the man. Then an expedition is sent, and it is said: 'Is there anyone among you who saw the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ?' He is sought but not found. Even if he were beyond the sea, you would come to him. Then there remain people who recite the Qur'an but do not know what it is."],[5764,"And al-Haytham b. Kulayb said: Ahmad b. Hazim b. Abi Gharazah narrated to us, Ja'far b. 'Awn narrated to us with it. And this chain is authentic, but Abu Sufyan shortened it. Al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it from the path of 'Amr b. Dinar, and Muslim from the path of Abu al-Zubayr, both from Jabir, from Abu Sa'id ؓ, and that is the correct one."],[5765,"A time will come upon the people when, if they hear of a man among my Companions from beyond the sea, they will go to him."],[5766,"Indeed, the people will increase in number while my Companions decrease, so do not revile them. May Allah curse the one who reviles them."],[5767,"The Hour will not be established until a man among my Companions is sought as a stray animal is sought, but he will not be found."],[5768,"He heard Abu Hurayrah ؓ in Madinah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his Companions ؓ: \"How will you be when you are satiated with bread and oil?\" They raised a clamor and glorified Allah for a while, then said, \"When, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"When the cities are conquered.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: \"How will you be when various colors differ for you and you go out in some garments and return in others?\" They said, \"When will that be, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"When the cities are conquered, and Persia and Byzantium are conquered.\" They said, \"Then they are better than us, O Messenger of Allah, for they will attain the conquests.\" He said, \"Rather, you are better than them, and your sons are better than their sons, and the sons of your sons are better than the sons of their sons. They did not take hold of gratitude. They did not take hold of gratitude. They did not take hold of gratitude.\""],[5769,"The likeness of my Companions is that of salt in food; food is only good with salt."],[5770,"Ismail alone narrated it, and he is not a reliable memorizer."],[5771,"\"Would that I could meet my brothers.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, are we not your brothers and Companions?\" He said, \"Yes, but there will be a people who come after you, who believe in me as you believe, and affirm me as you affirm, and support me as you support. So would that I could meet my brothers.\""],[5773,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas ؓ was among a group, and they mentioned Ali ؓ and reviled him. Sa'd ؓ said: \"Gently, about the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for we committed a sin along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'Had it not been for a decree from Allah that had preceded, a great punishment would have touched you for what you took.' I hope that a mercy from Allah, Exalted, preceded for us.\" One of them said: \"By Allah, he hates you and calls you 'al-Ukhaynis.'\" Sa'd ؓ laughed until laughter overcame him, then said: \"Does not a man feel anger toward his brother over a matter between them, yet that does not reach his trustworthiness?\" And he mentioned another word."],[5774,"Leave my in-laws and my Companions, for whoever preserves me among them will have a protector from Allah with him, and whoever does not preserve me among them, Allah will disown him, and whoever Allah disowns is likely to be seized."],[5777,"I came to Madinah during the season of dried curd and clarified butter, while the Bedouins were bringing water skins to draw water. Then I saw a man with a lofty gaze looking at the people, and I thought he was a stranger. I approached and greeted him, and he returned the greeting and said to me: \"Are you from the people of Madinah?\" I said, \"Yes.\" So I sat with him and said, \"Who are you from?\" He said, \"From Banu Hilal, and my name is Kahmas.\" Then he said to me, \"Shall I not narrate to you a hadith that I witnessed from Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said: \"While we were sitting with him\" — and he mentioned the story — then he said: \"Then Umar ؓ said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The best of my nation is the generation in which I am, then the second, then the third, then a people will arise whose oaths precede their testimonies; they testify without being asked to testify; they have clamor in their markets.'\" Mu'awiyah said: Kahmas said: \"Do you fear that these are from those?\""],[5781,"Be upright and rejoice, for Allah, Exalted, is not quick to punish you. A people will come who have no argument."],[5782,"Blessed is the one who saw me and believed in me, and blessed is the one who believed in me and did not see me. Blessed are they, and a goodly return."],[5783,"A man came to Ibn Umar ؓ and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, did you look at the Messenger of God ﷺ with your own eyes? He said: Yes. He said: And did you speak to him with these tongues of yours? He said: Yes. He said: And did you pledge allegiance to him with these right hands of yours? He said: Yes. He said: Tuba (glad tidings) for you, O Abu Abd al-Rahman. He said: Shall I not tell you about something I heard from him? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Tuba for the one who saw me and believed in me, and tuba for the one who believed in me and did not see me - three times."],[5785,"That two men came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he looked at them and said: Madhhijians or Kindians. Then he ﷺ said: Rather Kindians. So they came to him and indeed they were Kindians. One of them said: What do you think, O Messenger of God, of the one who follows what you were sent with and believes you but has not seen you? He said: Tuba for him, then tuba for him."],[5786,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, two riders appeared. When he saw them he said: Kindians, Madhhijians. Until they came and indeed they were two men from Madhhij. He said: One of them approached him to pledge allegiance. When he took his hand he said: O Messenger of God, what do you think of the one who believes in you, believes you, and follows you - what is for him? He said: Tuba for him. Then he wiped over his hand and left. Then the other came forward until he took his hand to pledge allegiance. He said: O Messenger of God, what do you think of the one who believes in you, believes you, and follows you but has not seen you? He said: Tuba for him. Then he wiped over his hand and left."],[5788,"Umar ؓ had a debt owed by a Jew, so he came to him to demand it. He met him and Umar said: No, by the One who chose Muhammad ﷺ over all mankind, I will not leave you while I am demanding something from you. The Jew said: By God, He did not choose Muhammad over all mankind. So Umar slapped him. He said: Between me and you is Abu al-Qasim. He said: Umar said: No, by the One who chose Muhammad over all mankind. I said: By God, God did not choose Muhammad over all mankind, so he slapped me. He ﷺ said: As for you, O Umar, compensate him for his slap. Rather, O Jew, Adam is the chosen one of God, Abraham is the friend of God, Moses is the confidant of God, Jesus is the spirit of God, and I am the beloved of God. Rather, O Jew, God the Mighty and Majestic named Himself with two names with which He named my nation: He is al-Salam and He named my nation the Muslims, and He is al-Mu'min and He named my nation the believers. Rather, O Jew, you sought a day that was stored for us. For us is today, for you is tomorrow, and the day after tomorrow is for the Christians. Rather, O Jew, you are the first and we are the last, the foremost on the Day of Resurrection. Rather, Paradise is forbidden to the prophets until I enter it, and it is forbidden to the nations until my nation enters it."],[5789,"I asked my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, for my nation to spare them from the punishment of the other nations, and He granted it to me."],[5790,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us. He ordered Bilal to call out that prayer was to be held in congregation before he spoke. The people gathered to him, and he ascended the pulpit and said: O people, come forward and make room for those behind you - three times. The people came forward and pressed together, and they turned around but saw no one. Then he ﷺ said: Come forward and make room for those behind you. The people came forward and pressed together, and they turned around but saw no one. He ﷺ said that a third time, and they saw no one. A man stood up and said: For whom should we make room? For the angels? He ﷺ said: No, when they are with you, they are not in front of you or behind you, but on your right and on your left. He said: And they are not in front of us or behind us - are they better than us? He ﷺ said: Rather you are better than the angels. Sit down - so he sat down."],[5791,"The likeness of my nation is that of rain; it is not known whether its beginning is more beneficial or its end."],[5792,"The past nations were one hundred nations; if they testified to the goodness of a servant, Paradise became obligatory for him. And my nation is the fiftieth of them as a nation; so if they testify to the goodness of a servant, Paradise becomes obligatory for him."],[5793,"This nation will remain in goodness as long as when it speaks it is truthful, when it judges it is just, and when mercy is sought from it it shows mercy."],[5795,"This nation is shown mercy; there is no punishment upon it except what it inflicts upon itself. I said: And how does it punish itself? He said: Was there not punishment on the day of al-Nahar? Was there not punishment on the day of al-Jamal? Was there not punishment on the day of Siffin?"],[5797,"He was in the mosque when he saw 'Amr b. al-'As ؓ. He said to me: 'Are you from the people of Yemen?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Come close to me, and I will tell you a hadith that will delight your eyes.' He said: 'So I drew near to him.' 'Amr ؓ said: 'While we were sitting one day, the Messenger of God ﷺ came and sat with us. Then he said: \"Where are my brothers from whom I am and they are from me, I will enter Paradise and they will enter with me?\" Then he stood and left. It was not long before he returned and sat down. Then he said: \"Where are my brothers from whom I am and they are from me, I will enter Paradise and they will enter with me?\" Then he stood and left. Some of us said to others: \"If only we had asked him: 'Are they other than us, O Messenger of God?'\" It was only a little while before the Messenger of God ﷺ returned and said: \"Where are my brothers from whom I am and they are from me, I will enter Paradise and they will enter Paradise with me?\" We said: \"O Messenger of God, are they other than us?\" He said: \"Yes, they are the people of Yemen, the ones cast down in the remote parts of the earth, the ones turned away from the doors of rulers. One of them dies while his need is still in his chest, unfulfilled.\""],[5798,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was in Madinah, he said: \"God is most great, God is most great. God's help and victory have come, and the people of Yemen have come.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of God, who are the people of Yemen?\" He said: \"A people with tender hearts, soft in obedience. Faith is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni.\""],[5799,"Al-Zuhri did not narrate from Abu Hazim any hadith other than this one. I say: Husayn is weak."],[5801,"I was in the mosque on Friday while 'Ali b. Abi Talib was giving a sermon from a brick minbar. Behind me was Sa'sa'a b. Suhan. A man spoke to him about something that was hidden from us, and we recognized anger in his face, so he fell silent. Then al-Ash'ath b. Qays came, stepping over people's necks until he was close. He said: 'O Commander of the Believers, these red-skinned ones have overcome us in your presence.' Sa'sa'a struck me between my shoulders with his hand and said: 'To God we belong and to Him we return. Today he will reveal a matter concerning the Arabs that he was concealing.' He said: 'He became very angry and said: \"Who will excuse me from these fools? One of them wallows in his cushions and abandons people who remember God, Mighty and Majestic. He orders me to expel them, and that I should be among the wrongdoers. By Him who split the grain and created the soul, I heard Muhammad ﷺ say: 'By God, they will strike you back regarding the religion as you struck them regarding it in the beginning.'\""],[5802,"'Ali ؓ was giving a sermon while the mawali had surrounded him."],[5804,"I came to al-Miqdam b. Ma'dikarib in the mosque and said: 'O Abu Yazid, the people claim that you did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'Glory be to Allah! By Allah, I saw him while I was walking with my uncle, and he took hold of this ear of mine and said to my uncle: \"Do you think this one remembers his mother or his father?\" We said to him...'"],[5805,"If faith were suspended from the Pleiades, men from the people of Persia would attain it."],[5806,"From the Banu al-Hamra', the Banu al-Mawali. Sahih."],[5809,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting among his companions, he said: 'May God bless that cemetery' – three times – but no one asked him which cemetery it was, and he did not name anything for them. Then one of his companions entered upon one of his wives, as if she were 'A'isha, and said to her: 'When the Messenger of God ﷺ comes in, ask him about it.' She did so, and he said: 'It is a cemetery in 'Asqalan.'"],[5810,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ one day mentioning the people of a cemetery, and he prayed for it, increasing his prayers for it. He was asked about it, and he said: 'The people of the cemetery of 'Asqalan. They will be escorted to Paradise as a bride is escorted to her husband.'"],[5812,"I came to Madinah during the governorship of 'Uthman ؓ, and there was a man with a thick beard who sat for them and spoke harshly, so they dispersed. I said: 'O 'Abd Allah, I think you have done wrong.' He said: 'These are flatterers. Do you know me?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'I am Abu Dharr. Who are you?' I said: 'From the people of Basra.' He said: 'Shall I not tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: \"Calamities are in Iraq, and that is in Kufa. As for the people of Basra, they are the most correct of the cities in qiblah and the most abundant in muezzins. God will avert from them what they dislike.\"'"],[5813,"The Prophet ﷺ mentioned the people of Kufa, and he mentioned that great calamities will befall them. Then he mentioned the people of Basra, and he mentioned that they are the best of the people of the garrison cities in facing the qiblah, and the most numerous of them in muezzins; what they dislike will be averted from them."],[5814,"I have not seen any reed huts but the reed huts that were with Muhammad ﷺ; what is averted from this one?"],[5816,"You will come upon a people with curly hair, so treat them well, for they will be a strength for you and a means of reaching your enemy, by the permission of Allah Almighty."],[5819,"I came to Ibn Umar ؓ and asked him about something of knowledge. He said: From where are you? I said: From the people of al-Sham. He said: From which people of al-Sham? I said: From Homs. He said: From Homs you came seeking knowledge here? I said: What prevents me from seeking knowledge from someone like you, and you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: I inform you that the first distant group traveled in the footsteps of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until they settled in al-Sham, then your army in particular, so look at what they were upon, for it is the Sunnah."],[5821,"A group of my nation will continue to fight at the gates of Damascus and its surroundings, and at the gates of Damascus and its surroundings, and at the gates of Jerusalem and its surroundings; those who abandon them will not harm them, victorious upon the truth until the Hour is established."],[5822,"You will be organized into armies."],[5823,"I saw the pillar of the Book being pulled out from under my pillow, so I followed it with my eyes, and behold, it was a shining light that was taken to al-Sham. Verily, faith will be in al-Sham when trials occur."],[5824,"You will be organized into armies: an army in al-Sham and an army in Yemen. A man from Khawlan said: O Messenger of Allah, choose for me. He ﷺ said: Upon you is al-Sham, and whoever refuses, let him join his Yemen and draw water from its ponds, for Allah Almighty has guaranteed me al-Sham and its people."],[5825,"Wajj is a sacred valley."],[5827,"Indeed, Wajj has been sacred since the Lord ascended to the heaven on the day He decreed the creation."],[5829,"Excellent are the wet-nurses, the people of Nu'man."],[5831,"This nation will continue to be in good as long as they honor this sacred place with the honor it deserves."],[5834,"I was a young boy of seven or eight years, hearing what I saw and understanding, when a Jew appeared on a fortress crying out at the top of his voice: 'O assembly of Jews!' They gathered to him and said, 'What is the matter with you?' He said, 'The star of Ahmad, with which he was born, rose tonight.' He said: I asked Sa'id b. 'Abd al-Rahman b. Hassan b. Thabit: 'How old was Hassan b. Thabit when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah?' He said: 'Sixty years old.'"],[5835,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was born, Halimah bt. al-Harith came with a group of women from Banu Sa'd b. Bakr seeking infants to nurse in Makkah. Halimah said: 'I set out among the first of the women on a greyish she-donkey of mine, and with me was my husband al-Harith b. 'Abd al-'Uzza, one of Banu Sa'd b. Bakr, then one of Banu Nasirah. Our she-donkey was exhausted, and with me in the caravan was an old she-camel. By Allah, it did not yield a drop of milk in a barren year. The people were so hungry that hardship had worn them down. With me was a son of mine, and by Allah, he did not sleep through our nights, and I found nothing in my breasts to pacify him with, except that we hoped for rain. We had some sheep and we hoped for them. When we arrived in Makkah, there was not one of us but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was offered to her, and she disliked him. We said, \"He is an orphan, and only the father honors the wet-nurse and treats her well.\" We said, \"What can his mother or his uncle or his grandfather do for us?\" All my companions took a nursling, but I found nothing. When I found no one else, I went back to him and took him. By Allah, I only took him because I found no one else. I said to my companion, \"By Allah, I will take this orphan from Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib; perhaps Allah will benefit us through him. I will not return among my companions without taking something.\" He said, \"You have done well.\" She said: So I took him and brought him to the saddle. By Allah, no sooner had I brought him to the saddle than I sat down squeezing my breasts with milk until I quenched him and quenched his brother. His father went to that old she-camel of ours and felt her, and behold she was full of milk, so he milked her and gave me to drink and drank himself. He said, \"O Halimah, do you know? By Allah, you have obtained a blessed soul. Allah, Most High, has given us through them what we never wished for.\" She said: So we spent the best night, full and satisfied, and we would not sleep through our nights because of our child. Then we set out returning to our land, I and my companions. I mounted my greyish she-donkey and carried him with me. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Halimah, I outpaced the caravan, until the women were saying, \"Wait for us! Is this your she-donkey that you set out on?\" I said, \"Yes.\" They said, \"She was exhausted when we came. What is the matter with her?\" She said: I said, \"By Allah, I have carried on her a blessed boy.\" She said: So we went on, and Allah, Most High, kept increasing us in good every day, until we arrived while the land was in a year of drought. Our shepherds would take the flocks out in the morning and bring them back in the evening, and the sheep of Banu Sa'd would return hungry, while my sheep returned full, fat, and laden with milk, so they were milked and we drank. They would say, \"What is the matter with the sheep of al-Harith b. 'Abd al-'Uzza and the sheep of Halimah? They return full and laden with milk while your sheep return hungry. Woe to you! Graze where our shepherds graze.\" So they grazed with them, but their sheep returned only hungry as before, while my sheep returned as they had been. She said: And he ﷺ grew as no other boy grew. He grew in a day as a boy grows in a month, and in a month as a boy grows in a year. When he ﷺ completed two years, we brought him back to Makkah, I and his father. We said, \"By Allah, we will never part with him as long as we are able.\" When we came to his mother, we said to her, \"O wet-nurse, by Allah, we have never seen a child greater in blessing than him, and we fear for him the epidemic of Makkah and its diseases. Leave him with us and we will take him back until you recover from your illness.\" We kept at her until she gave permission, so we returned with him. We stayed for three or four months. While he was playing behind the houses with his brother among some sheep of theirs, his brother came running, while I and his father were in the house. He said, \"My Qurayshi brother: two men in white garments came to him, took him, laid him down, and split open his belly.\" I and his father rushed out, and we found him standing with his color changed. When he saw us, he burst into tears and wept. She said: I and his father embraced him and held him to us, and we said, \"What is the matter with you, may my father and mother be your ransom?\" He said, \"Two men came to me, laid me down, split open my belly, and did something to it, then restored it as it was.\" His father said, \"By Allah, I think my son has been afflicted. Take him back to his family and return him to them before something we fear appears in him.\" She said: So we carried him and brought him to his mother. When she saw us, she disapproved of our state and said, \"What brought you back with him before I asked you for him, when you had been so eager to keep him?\" We said, \"Nothing, except that Allah, Most High, has decreed the completion of nursing, and we are pleased with what you see. We thought returning him to you as you love is dearer to us.\" She said, \"You two have some matter. Tell me what it is.\" She did not let us go until we told her. She said, \"No, by Allah, Allah will not do that to him. My son has a great destiny. Shall I not tell you about him? I conceived him, and by Allah, I never had a pregnancy that was lighter or easier than his. Then, when I conceived him, I saw a light come out of me that illuminated the necks of camels in Busra—or she said: the palaces of Busra. Then I gave birth to him, and by Allah, when he was born, he did not fall as children fall. He fell supporting himself with his hands on the ground, raising his head to the sky. So leave him to me.\" So she took him and we departed."],[5836,"I came with a group from Banu Sa'd b. Bakr seeking infants to nurse in Makkah."],[5837,"Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"],[5838,"O brother of Banu 'Amir, the truth of my saying and the beginning of my affair is the supplication of my father Ibrahim, and my brother 'Isa ibn Maryam gave glad tidings of me. I was the firstborn of my mother, and she carried me as the heaviest thing women carry, until she began complaining to her companions of the weight she felt. My mother saw in a dream that what was in her womb was a light. She said: I began following the light with my eyes, and the light went ahead of my sight until it illuminated for me the easts of the earth and its wests. Then she gave birth to me. When I grew up, idols were made hateful to me, and poetry was made hateful to me. I was nursed among Banu Jusham b. Bakr. While I was one day in the bottom of a valley with companions of mine among the boys, behold, a group of three came with a basin of gold filled with light and snow. They took me from among my companions, and my companions fled until they reached the edge of the valley. They turned to the group and said, \"What do you want with this boy? He is not one of us. He is from Banu Sayyid Quraysh, and he is being nursed among us as an orphan boy with no father. What would killing him avail you? But if you must do something, choose any of us you wish, and we will come to you and you can take us in his place. Leave this boy.\" They did not answer them. When the boys saw that the people would not answer them, they ran away quickly to the settlement to inform them and call for help against the people. One of them came to me and laid me down gently on the ground, then split open what was between my chest and the end of my pubic area while I was watching, and I felt nothing of that. Then he took out my intestines and washed them with that snow, washing them thoroughly. Then he returned them to their place. Then the second one came and said to his companion, \"Step aside.\" Then he inserted his hand into my inside and took out my heart while I was watching. He split it open and took out a black clot and threw it away. Then he gestured with his hand to his right as if reaching for something. Then he brought the seal in his hand, made of the light of prophethood and wisdom, dazzling the eyes of onlookers. He sealed my heart and it became full of light. He sealed it and returned it to its place. I felt the coolness of that seal in my heart for a long time. Then the third one came and moved his companion aside. He passed his hand between my chest and the end of my pubic area, and the split closed by the permission of Allah, Most High. Then he took me by the hand and raised me from my place gently. Then the first one who had split my belly said, \"Weigh him against ten of his community.\" They weighed me and I outweighed them. Then he said, \"Weigh him against a hundred of his community.\" They weighed me and I outweighed them. Then he said, \"Weigh him against a thousand of his community.\" They weighed me and I outweighed them. He said, \"Leave him, for if you weighed him against his entire community, he would outweigh them.\" Then they came to me and embraced me to their chests, kissed my head and between my eyes, and said, \"O beloved, do not be afraid. If you knew what good is intended for you, your eye would be comforted.\" He said: While we were thus, behold, the settlement came with all its people, and my wet-nurse was at the front of the settlement crying out at the top of her voice, saying, \"O poor weak one!\" He said: They crowded around me kissing me and saying, \"How wonderful you are as a weak one!\" Then she said, \"O lonely one!\" He said: They crowded around me kissing me and saying, \"How wonderful you are as a lonely one! You are not lonely, for Allah is with you, and His angels, and the believers of the people of the earth.\" Then she said, \"O orphan! You were taken advantage of among your companions and killed because of your weakness.\" They crowded around me and embraced me to their chests and kissed my head, and said, \"How wonderful you are as an orphan! How honored you are with Allah, Mighty and Majestic! If you knew what good is intended for you.\" He said: They reached the edge of the valley. When my wet-nurse saw me, she said, \"O my son, do I see you still alive?\" She came and bent over me, embracing me to her chest. By the One in whose hand is my soul, I was in her lap, she had embraced me to herself, and my hand was in the hand of one of them, and I thought the people could see them, but they could not. Some of the settlement came and said, \"This boy has been touched by madness or a visitation from the jinn. Take him to the soothsayer to look at him and treat him.\" I said to him, \"O you, there is nothing wrong with me as you claim. I see myself sound, my heart healthy, and there is no defect in me.\" My father—meaning the husband of my wet-nurse—said, \"Do you not see that my son's speech is sound? I hope there is no harm in my son.\" The people agreed to take me to the soothsayer. They carried me until they brought me to him. They told him my story. He said, \"Be quiet until I hear from the boy, for he knows best about his affair.\" So I told him my story from beginning to end. When he heard my words, he embraced me to his chest and cried out at the top of his voice, \"O Arabs, kill this boy and kill me with him! By al-Lat and al-'Uzza, if you leave him, he will change your religion, make fools of your minds and the minds of your fathers, oppose your command, and bring you a religion the like of which you have never heard.\" He said: My wet-nurse snatched me from his hand and said, \"You are more foolish and crazier than him. If I had known this would come from you, I would not have brought him to you.\" Then they carried me and returned me to my family. I woke up saddened by what had been done to me, and the trace of the split between my chest and the end of my pubic area was like a shoelace. That is the truth of my saying and the beginning of my affair. The 'Amiri said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that your affair is true. Tell me about things I will ask you.\" He ﷺ said, \"Ask about yourself.\" He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to questioners before that, \"Ask about whatever appears to you.\" That day he said to the 'Amiri, \"Ask about yourself,\" and he spoke to him in the dialect of Banu 'Amir, and he spoke to him in what he knew. The 'Amiri said..."],[5840,"I performed Hajj in the pre-Islamic era, and behold, a man was circumambulating the House while reciting in rajaz: 'Return to me my rider Muhammad, return him to me and do me a favor.' I said, 'Who is this?' They said, 'This is 'Abd al-Muttalib b. Hashim. Some camels of his went astray, so he sent a son of his after them to look for them, and he was delayed. He never sent him on an errand but he came back with it accomplished.' He said: I did not leave until Muhammad ﷺ came with the camels. He said, 'O my son, by Allah, I grieved for you this time with a grief that I will never part from you again.'"],[5842,"Quraysh was a light before Allah, Mighty and Majestic, two thousand years before He created Adam. That light glorified Allah, and the angels glorified with its glorification. When Allah created Adam, He placed that light in his loins. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then Allah brought it down to the earth in the loins of Adam, and placed it in the loins of Nuh in the ark, and it was cast into the fire in the loins of Ibrahim. He kept transferring me from the loins of the noble to the wombs, until He brought me out from between my parents. They never met in fornication.'"],[5843,"I came from a legitimate marriage, not from fornication, from Adam until my father and mother begot me. Nothing of the fornication of the pre-Islamic era ever touched me."],[5844,"Every tie and lineage will be cut off except my lineage and my tie."],[5846,"I never intended anything indecent that the people of the pre-Islamic era used to intend, except twice in my life, and in both Allah, Most High, protected me from it. One night I said to a young man from Quraysh who was with me in the highlands of Makkah tending sheep for their owners: 'Watch my sheep so I can spend the night in Makkah as the young men do.' He said, 'Yes.' So I went out and came to the nearest house of Makkah. I heard singing, the beating of tambourines, and reed pipes. I said, 'What is this?' They said, 'So-and-so married so-and-so,' for a man of Quraysh married a woman of Quraysh. I enjoyed that singing and that sound until sleep overcame me, and nothing woke me but the touch of the sun. I returned to my companion and he said, 'What did you do?' I told him. Then another night I said to him the same thing, and he did. I went out and heard the like of that, and I was told the like of what I was told. I enjoyed what I heard until sleep overcame me, and nothing woke me but the touch of the sun. Then I returned to my companion and he said, 'What did you do?' I said, 'I did nothing.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'By Allah, after that I never intended any evil of what the people of the pre-Islamic era did, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, honored me with His prophethood.'"],[5847,"I was forbidden from being naked, and that was before prophethood came to him."],[5849,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to attend the gatherings of the polytheists. He said: He heard two angels behind him, one of them saying to the other, 'Let us go so that we may stand behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said, 'How can we stand behind him when his last contact was with touching the idols?' After that, he never attended the gatherings of the polytheists again."],[5850,"Jibril ﷺ entered the Sacred Mosque and began to move about. He caught sight of the Prophet ﷺ sleeping in the shade of the Kaaba, so he woke him. He ﷺ stood up, shaking his head and beard of dust. He took him toward the gate of Banu Shaybah, and Mikail met them. Jibril said to Mikail, 'What prevented you from shaking the Prophet's ﷺ hand?' He said, 'I find on his hand the smell of brass.' It was as if Jibril ﷺ found that objectionable, so he said, 'Did you do that?' It was as if the Prophet ﷺ forgot, then he remembered and said, 'My brother spoke the truth. The day before yesterday I passed by Isaf and Na'ilah, and I placed my hand on one of them and said, \"A people who are content with you two as gods besides Allah are an evil people.\"'"],[5852,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had long forearms, wide shoulders, long eyelashes—the eyelashes of the eye. He was not one to shout in the markets, nor was he obscene or given to obscenity. He ﷺ would turn completely and walk away completely."],[5853,"May Allah have mercy on a person who is easy in selling, easy in buying, easy in taking, easy in giving, easy in settling debts, and easy in demanding repayment. Then he went on. I said to myself, 'Is this the Hashimite who has led people astray? Indeed, it is he!' I looked, and behold, he was a man with a handsome body, a broad forehead, a fine nose, and thin eyebrows. Behold, from the hollow of his throat to his navel was like a black thread of black hair, and he was between two worn garments. He said: He drew near to us and said, 'Peace be upon you.' We returned the greeting. I did not hesitate and said, 'By Allah, I will investigate this, for he speaks well.' I followed him and said, 'O Muhammad.' He turned fully to me and said, 'What do you want?' I said, 'Are you the one who has led people astray, destroyed them, and turned them away from what their fathers worshipped?' He said, 'That is Allah.' I said, 'What do you call to?' He said, 'I call Allah's servants to Allah.' He said: I said, 'What do you say?' He said, 'Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, believe in what has been revealed to me, disbelieve in Al-Lat and Al-ʿUzza, establish prayer, and give zakah?' He said: I said, 'And what is zakah?' He said, 'Our rich give back to our poor.' He said: I said, 'What an excellent thing you call to.' He said: By then, there was no one on earth who breathed more hateful to me than him, and it was not long before he became dearer to me than my children, my parents, and all people. He said: I said, 'I have understood.' He said, 'You have understood?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and believe in what has been revealed to me?' I said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah. I frequent a watering place where many people gather, and I will call them to what you have called me to, for I hope they will follow you.' He said, 'Yes, call them.' So the people of that watering place embraced Islam, men and women. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped his head."],[5854,"I entered with my master upon one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, and she brought out to us some reddish hair and said, 'This is the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[5856,"Ibrahim (peace and blessings be upon him) was commanded to build the House, and he felt constrained by it, not knowing how to build. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down the Sakina, which is a wind that pierces, and it encircled him like a shield, so he built upon it. Each day he would build a course—meaning a wall—while Makkah was intensely hot. When he ﷺ reached the place of the Stone, he said to Ismail (peace and blessings be upon him), 'Go and seek a stone.' Ismail ﷺ went wandering in the mountains, and Jibril ﷺ descended with the Stone. Ismail ﷺ came back and said, 'Where is this from?' He said, 'From the One who does not rely on my building or yours.' So he placed it. Then it fell into ruin, and the Amalekites rebuilt it. Then it fell into ruin, and Jurhum rebuilt it. Then it fell into ruin, and Quraysh rebuilt it. When they wanted to place the Stone, they disputed over it and said, 'The first person to come out of this gate, the gate of Banu Shaybah.' The Prophet ﷺ came out, and they said, 'This is the trustworthy one.' He ﷺ ordered a garment to be spread, placed it on it, and ordered one man from each tribe to take a side of the garment. They lifted it, and the Prophet ﷺ took it and placed it."],[5857,"When the House was demolished after Jurhum, Quraysh rebuilt it. When they wanted to place the Stone, they quarreled over who would place it. They agreed that the first person to enter from this gate would place it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered from the gate of Banu Shaybah. He ordered a garment, placed the Stone in its middle, and ordered each clan to take a side of the garment. They lifted it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it."],[5858,"When they wanted to raise the Stone—meaning Quraysh—they disputed over it and said, 'We will let the first man to come out of this street judge between us.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the first to come out to them. They put it on a cloak, and then all the tribes together lifted it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at that time a young man, meaning before the mission."],[5859,"Allah, exalted is He, revealed to Ibrahim, 'Build Me a house.' He said: Ibrahim ﷺ felt constrained by it, so Allah, exalted is He, sent a wind called the Sakina, also called the Khajuj, which had two eyes and a head. Allah, exalted is He, revealed to Ibrahim to move when it moved and rest when it rested. It moved until it reached the site of the House, and it encircled it like a shield, and it is opposite the Populated House, which seventy thousand angels enter every day and never return to until the Day of Resurrection. Ibrahim and Ismail began building one course each day, and when the heat became intense for them, they sought shade in the shadow of the mountain. When they reached the place of the Stone, Ibrahim said to Ismail, 'Bring me a stone to place as a marker for the people.' Ismail faced the valley and came with a stone, but Ibrahim found it too small and threw it away, saying, 'Bring me another.' Ismail went off, and Jibril descended to Ibrahim with the Black Stone. Ismail came back, and Ibrahim said to him, 'Someone has come to me who did not leave me to rely on your stone.' He said: He built the House and began circumambulating it, and they circumambulated and prayed until they died and passed away. Then the House fell into ruin, and the Amalekites rebuilt it, and they circumambulated it until they died and passed away. Then Quraysh rebuilt it. When they reached the place of the Stone, they differed over its placement and said, 'The first person to appear from the gate.'"],[5860,"In the pre-Islamic era, the Kaaba was built of loose stones, with no mud. It was only as high as a young goat could leap over, and it was not roofed. Its covering was simply placed on top and let hang down. The Black Corner was set on its wall, visible. It had two corners, like a ring, square on one side and round on the other. A ship came from the land of the Romans, and when it was near Jeddah, it broke apart. Quraysh went out to take its timber and found a Roman with it. They took the timber, and he gave it to them. The ship had been heading for Abyssinia, and the Roman on the ship was a merchant. They brought the timber and the Roman. Quraysh said, 'We will build the House of our Lord with this timber.' When they wanted to demolish it, behold, there was a snake on the wall of the House, white-bellied and black-backed. Every time someone approached the House to demolish it or take a stone from it, it rushed at him with its mouth open. Quraysh gathered at the Maqam and cried out to Allah, exalted is He. He said: They said, 'Our Lord, we are not afraid. We intended to honor and adorn Your House. If You approve of that, then so be it; otherwise, whatever You decide, do.' They heard an answer from the sky, and behold, there was a bird larger than a vulture, black-backed, with white belly and legs. It sank its talons into the snake's belly and carried it off, dragging it with its tail hanging down, until it took it toward Ajyad. Quraysh demolished it, and they began rebuilding it with stones from the valley, carrying them on their necks, and they raised it twenty cubits into the air. While the Prophet ﷺ was carrying stones from Ajyad, wearing a striped cloak, the cloak was too tight for him, and part of it slipped from his shoulder, so his private area was visible because of the smallness of the cloak. A voice called out, 'O Muhammad, cover your private area.' He was never seen naked after that. Between its building and what Allah revealed to him was fifteen years. When the army of al-Husayn b. Numayr came... and he mentioned its burning in the time of Ibn al-Zubayr ؓ."],[5861,"We were carrying stones to the House when Quraysh built it. The men carried stones, and the women carried mortar—mortar is what is placed between the rocks. Al-Abbas ؓ said: I and my nephew Muhammad were carrying stones on our necks and putting our lower garments under the rocks. When people came upon us, we would wrap ourselves. While I was with Muhammad in front of me, he fell and lay prostrate. I came running and reached him, and behold, he was looking at the sky. I said to him, 'What is the matter with you?' He stood up and wrapped himself, and said ﷺ, 'I was forbidden to walk naked.' Al-Abbas ؓ said: I kept that from the people for fear they would think it madness."],[5863,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Khadijah retreated in seclusion for a month, and that coincided with Ramadan. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and heard, 'Peace be upon you.' She said: He said, 'I thought it was a sudden encounter with the jinn.' She said, 'Rejoice, for peace is good.' Then one day he ﷺ saw Jibril ﷺ on the sun, with one wing in the east and one wing in the west, and I was frightened by him. She said: He went off intending to go to his family, and behold, Jibril ﷺ was between him and the door. He said: He spoke to me until I felt at ease with him, then he promised me an appointment. I came to the appointment, and Jibril ﷺ was delayed for me. When he wanted to return, behold, he and Mikail (peace be upon them) were there. Jibril ﷺ descended to the earth, and Mikail remained between heaven and earth. He said: Jibril ﷺ took me, threw me down on the back of my neck, split open my belly, and took out of it what Allah, exalted is He, willed. Then he washed it in a basin of gold, then returned it inside, then turned me over as a vessel is turned over, then he sealed my back until I felt the touch of the seal. Then he said to me, 'Recite in the name of your Lord,' and I had never read a book. He took me by the throat until I burst into tears. Then he said, 'Recite in the name of your Lord who created' up to His words, Mighty and Majestic: 'what he did not know.' He ﷺ said: I did not forget anything after that. Mikail ﷺ said, 'His nation has followed him, by the Lord of the Kaaba.' When I came to my house, no stone or tree met me except that it said, 'Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah,' until I entered upon Khadijah, and she said, 'Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah.'"],[5864,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ vowed to retreat in seclusion for a month, he and Khadijah, and that coincided with the month of Ramadan. One night the Prophet ﷺ went out and heard, 'Peace be upon you.' He said: I thought it was a sudden encounter with the jinn. I came quickly until I entered upon Khadijah, and she covered me with a garment and said, 'What is the matter with you, O son of Abdullah?' He mentioned the hadith in a similar way until he said: Until we came to five verses of it, and I did not forget anything after that. Then he weighed me against a man, and I outweighed him. Then he weighed me against another, and I outweighed him, until I was weighed against a hundred men. Mikail ﷺ said from above, 'His nation has followed him, by the Lord of the Kaaba.'"],[5865,"The Prophet ﷺ was sent while he was forty-three years old."],[5867,"I used to go with Usama b. Zayd to the idols of Quraysh that were around the Kaaba. We would go to the places where they would relieve themselves, and we would take dung in our hands and go to the idols of Quraysh and smear them with it. When morning came, they would say, “Who did this to our gods?” So they would go to them and wash them with milk and water."],[5868,"I entered the Kaaba with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he saw images in it. He said to me, “Bring me some water.” So I brought him ﷺ water in a bucket. He began to moisten a cloth with it and then strike the images with it, saying, “May Allah fight the people who depict what they do not create.”"],[5870,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ twice in the market of Dhu al-Majaz while I was selling some goods of mine. He passed by wearing a red cloak of his, and he ﷺ was calling out at the top of his voice, “O people, say: There is no god but Allah, and you will succeed.” A man was following him throwing stones at him, and he had made his heels and Achilles tendons bleed. He was saying, “O people, do not obey him, for he is a liar.” I said, “Who is this?” They said, “This is a young man from Banu Abd al-Muttalib.” I said, “Then who is this who is following him and throwing at him?” They said, “His uncle Abd al-Uzza, who is Abu Lahab.” He said, “When Islam became manifest in Madinah, we came in a caravan from al-Rabadha until we stopped near Madinah.”"],[5871,"Quraysh came to Abu Talib and said, “O Abu Talib, your nephew harms us in our gathering place and in our mosque, so forbid him from harming us.” He said, “O Aqil, bring Muhammad to me.” So I went and brought him. He said, “O son of my brother, your cousins claim that you harm them, so stop that.” He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his eyes to the sky and said, ‘Do you see this sun?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘I am no more able to leave that for you than you are to kindle a flame from it.’” He said, “Abu Talib said, ‘My nephew has not lied to us, so go back.’”"],[5873,"They said to her, “What was the worst thing you saw the polytheists do to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” She said, “The polytheists were sitting in the mosque, talking about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and what he said about their gods. While they were doing that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, so they all stood up to him. The news reached Abu Bakr ؓ, and they said, ‘Help your companion.’ He came out from us, and he had four braids, saying, ‘Woe to you! Would you kill a man for saying: My Lord is Allah, when he has come to you with clear proofs from your Lord?’” She said, “They left the Messenger of Allah ﷺ alone and turned to Abu Bakr ؓ.” She said, “Abu Bakr ؓ returned to us, and he did not touch any of his braids without some of it coming out with it, and he was saying, ‘Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.’”"],[5875,"The beginning of Umar’s ؓ Islam was as follows: Umar ؓ said, “My sister went into labor at night, so I left the house and entered the curtains of the Kaaba on a cold night.” He said, “The Prophet ﷺ came and entered the Hijr wearing his sandals and prayed as long as Allah willed, then he left.” He said, “I heard something the like of which I had never heard, so I went out and followed him. He said, ‘Who is this?’ I said, ‘Umar.’ He ﷺ said, ‘O Umar, you do not leave me alone night or day.’” He said, “I feared that he would supplicate against me, so I said, ‘I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah.’ He ﷺ said, ‘O Umar, keep it secret.’ I said, ‘No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I will declare it openly just as I declared polytheism openly.’”"],[5876,"A man from Banu Zuhra met Umar ؓ before he had accepted Islam, while Umar was carrying a sword. He said, “Where are you heading, O Umar?” Umar said, “I want to kill Muhammad.” He said, “How can you be safe among Banu Hashim or Banu Zuhra if you have killed Muhammad?” Umar said, “I see that you have turned apostate and left your religion.” He said, “Shall I tell you something astonishing, O Umar? Your brother-in-law and your sister have turned apostate and left the religion they were upon.” He said, “So Umar went to them angrily.” Ishaq said, “Meaning in a rage,” until he approached the door, and with them was a man called Khabbab, reciting Surah Ta-Ha to them. He said, “When Khabbab ؓ heard Umar’s footsteps, he hid under a bed of theirs.” Umar said, “What is this murmuring I hear with you?” They said, “We were just talking between ourselves.” He said, “Perhaps you have apostatized and left your religion.” His brother-in-law said, “O Umar, what do you think if the truth is in a religion other than yours?” He said, “Umar turned to his brother-in-law and trampled him severely.” He said, “His sister pushed him away from her husband, so he struck her face and made it bleed.” She said, “What do you think if the truth is in a religion other than yours? I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.” He said, “Umar ؓ said, ‘Show me this book that you were reciting.’” He said, “Umar ؓ could read books.” His sister said, “No, you are impure. Give us a covenant by Allah Almighty that you will return it to us, and get up and perform ghusl and wudu.” He said, “So he did.” He said, “He recited: ‘Ta-Ha. We have not sent down to you the Qur’an that you be distressed’ until His saying: ‘And establish prayer for My remembrance. Indeed, the Hour is coming; I almost conceal it.’” Umar ؓ said, “Show me where Muhammad is.” When Khabbab ؓ heard Umar’s ؓ words, he came out to him and said, “Rejoice, O Umar, for I hope that you are the answer to the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on Thursday evening: ‘O Allah, strengthen the religion with Umar b. al-Khattab or with Amr b. Hisham.’” They said, “He is in the house at the foot of al-Safa,” meaning the Prophet ﷺ, “receiving revelation.” So Umar ؓ went, and at the door were Hamza b. Abd al-Muttalib ؓ and some of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ. When Hamza ؓ saw the people’s fear of Umar ؓ, he said, “Yes, this is Umar. If Allah intends good for him, he will accept Islam and follow the Prophet ﷺ, and if it is otherwise, his killing will be easy for us.” He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to him and grabbed the collar of his garment and his sword strap, and said, ‘Will you not stop, O Umar, until Allah Almighty sends upon you disgrace and punishment like what He sent upon al-Walid b. al-Mughira? O Allah, this is Umar b. al-Khattab. O Allah, strengthen the religion with Umar.’” Umar ؓ said, “I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah,” and he accepted Islam. Then he ؓ said, “Come out, O Messenger of Allah.”"],[5877,"Mujahid b. Musa narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, and he mentioned something similar."],[5878,"He ﷺ said on Thursday evening: “O Allah, strengthen the religion with Umar b. al-Khattab or with Amr b. Hisham.” He said, “Umar ؓ took up his sword, and a man from Banu Zuhra met him...”"],[5880,"Jafar b. Abi Talib ؓ asked permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, “Allow me to go to a land where I can worship Allah Almighty without fearing anyone.” So he allowed him, and he went to the Negus. Amr b. al-As ؓ narrated to me, saying, “When I saw his position, I envied him. I said, ‘By Allah, I will seek the death of this man and his companions.’ So I went to the Negus and entered upon him with him. I said, ‘In your land there is a man whose cousin is in our land, and he claims that there is no god for people except one God. By Allah, if you do not kill him and his companions, I will never cross this sea to you again, neither I nor anyone of my companions.’ He said, ‘Call him.’ I said, ‘He will not come with me, so send a messenger with me.’ He came, and when he reached the door, I called out, ‘Give permission for Amr b. al-As.’ But he called out from behind me, ‘Give permission for Abdullah.’ He said, ‘He heard his voice and gave him permission before me.’ He said, ‘So he and his companions entered.’ He said, ‘Then he gave me permission, and I entered, and there he was sitting.’ He mentioned where his seat was on the couch. When I saw him, I went and sat in front of him, putting him behind my back, and I seated one of my companions between every two of them. He said, ‘The Negus said, “Sacrifice, sacrifice,” meaning, “Speak.”’ Amr said, ‘The cousin of this man is in our land, and he claims that there is no god for people except one God. By Allah, if you do not kill him and his companions, I will never cross this sea to you again, nor anyone of my companions.’ He said, ‘He recited the tashahhud, and that was the first time I heard the tashahhud.’ He said, ‘My cousin has spoken the truth, and I am upon his religion.’ He said, ‘He cried out and said, “Oh!” until I thought that the Abyssinians do not speak.’ He said, ‘Is there a Namus like the Namus of Musa? What does he say about Isa?’ He said, ‘He says: He is the Spirit of Allah and His Word.’ He said, ‘He picked up something from the ground and said, “He has not missed anything of what he said, nor even this. Were it not for my kingdom, I would have followed you.” He said to me, “I do not care if you never come to me again, neither you nor anyone of your companions.” And he said to Jafar ؓ, “Go, for you are safe in my land. Whoever strikes you, I will kill him, and whoever reviles you, I will fine him.” And he said to his doorkeeper, “Whenever this man comes asking permission to enter upon me, give him permission, unless I am with my family. If I am with my family, inform him, and if he insists, then give him permission.”’ He said, ‘We parted, and there was no one I would rather meet alone than Jafar. He met me on a road once, and I saw no one else, and I looked behind me and saw no one. He said, ‘I approached and took his hand and said, “Do you know that I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger?” He said, “May Allah Almighty guide you, so be firm.” He said, ‘He left me and went away.’ He said, ‘I came to my companions, and it was as if they had witnessed with me. They seized me and threw a velvet cloth or a garment over me, and they began to cover my head. I kept sticking my head out from this side once and from that side once, until I escaped with not even a shred of clothing on me.’ He said, ‘I met an Abyssinian woman and took her veil and put it over my private parts. She said such and such, and I said such and such. Then I went to Jafar ؓ, and he said, “What is the matter with you?” I said, “I lost everything I had until not even a shred was left on me. What you see on me is nothing but the veil of an Abyssinian woman.”’ He said, ‘He went, and I went with him until we reached the king’s door. He said, “Give permission for the party of Allah.” The doorkeeper said, “Give him permission, for he is with his family.” He said, “Ask permission.” So he asked permission, and permission was given. He said, “Amr has followed me in my religion.” The king said, “No.” He said, “Yes.” The king said, “No.” He said, “Yes.” Then he said to a man, “Go with him, and if he has done it, then everything he says I will record.” He said, “Yes.” So he began to write down what I said until I left nothing out, even the cup. If I had wanted to take from their wealth to my own, I could have done so.’ This chain is good, except that it contradicts the well-known view that Amr's ؓ acceptance of Islam was at the hands of the Negus himself. Umayr b. Ishaq is alone in narrating it, and no one else narrated from him except Abdullah b. Awn. Ibn Main said, “He is worthless,” and he also considered him reliable once. In general, his hadith is recorded. Al-Bazzar said, “We do not know of it being narrated from Amr ؓ except through this chain.”"],[5881,"The migration from Abyssinia was during the nights of Khaybar."],[5884,"Quraysh gathered one day and said: \"Look for the most knowledgeable among you in sorcery, divination, and poetry; let him go to this man who has divided our assembly, scattered our affairs, and criticized our religion. Let him speak with him and see what he replies.\" They said: \"We know no one other than 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah.\" They said: \"You, O Abu al-Walid.\" So 'Utbah came to him and said: \"O Muhammad, are you better or 'Abd Allah?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent. He said: \"If you claim that these [forefathers] are better than you, they indeed worshipped the deities that you have criticized. And if you claim that you are better than them, then speak so that we may hear your words. By Allah, we have never seen a young lamb more ill-omened for your people than you. You have divided our unity, scattered our affairs, criticized our religion, and disgraced us among the Arabs, until it has spread among them that there is a sorcerer in Quraysh and a soothsayer in Quraysh. By Allah, we await only a cry like that of a pregnant woman [about to miscarry], that some of us will fall upon others with swords until we annihilate each other. O man, if it is need that drives you, we will gather for you until you become the richest single man of Quraysh. And if it is marriage you desire, then choose whichever women of Quraysh you wish, and we will marry you to ten.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Have you finished?\" He said: \"Yes.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: \"In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Ha Mim. The revelation of the Book is from Allah, the Exalted in Might, the Knowing.\" He continued until he reached: \"But if they turn away, then say: I have warned you of a thunderbolt like the thunderbolt of 'Ad and Thamud.\" 'Utbah said to him: \"Enough, enough! Do you have anything other than this?\" He ﷺ said: \"No.\" He returned to Quraysh, and they said: \"What news do you bring?\" He said: \"I did not leave anything that I thought you would say to him except that I said it to him.\" They said: \"Did he answer you?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"By the One who erected it as a building, I understood nothing of what he said except that he warned you of a thunderbolt like the thunderbolt of 'Ad and Thamud.\" They said: \"Woe to you! A man speaks to you in Arabic and you do not know what he said?\" He said: \"No, by Allah, I understood nothing of what he said except the mention of the thunderbolt.\""],[5886,"When I was taken up to the heaven, I reached a palace of pearl, in which there were doors of gold that glittered. It was revealed to me, or I was commanded regarding 'Ali with three qualities: that you are the master of the messengers, the imam of the pious, and the leader of the radiant, marked ones [on the Day of Judgment]."],[5888,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought al-Buraq and mounted it behind Jibril ﷺ . It carried them both. When it came upon a mountain, its hind legs would rise; when it descended, its front legs would rise. It carried us through a gloomy, stinking land, then continued until we emerged into a wide, pleasant land. I said: \"O Jibril, we were traveling through a gloomy, stinking land until we emerged into a wide, pleasant land.\" Jibril ﷺ said: \"That was the land of the Fire, and this is the land of Paradise.\" Then I came upon a man standing in prayer. He said: \"Who is this with you, O Jibril?\" Jibril said: \"This is your brother Muhammad.\" He welcomed me, prayed for blessing for me, and said: \"Ask ease for your nation.\" I said: \"Who is this, O Jibril?\" He said: \"This is your brother 'Isa.\" Then we continued and heard a voice and a roar. We came upon another man. He said: \"Who is this, O Jibril?\" Jibril said: \"This is your brother Muhammad.\" He welcomed me, prayed for blessing for me, and said: \"Ask ease for your nation.\" I said: \"Who is this, O Jibril?\" He said: \"This is your brother Musa.\" I said: \"About whom is his anger and his raised voice?\" He said: \"About his Lord.\" I said: \"About his Lord?!\" He said: \"Yes, for he is known for that and for his intensity.\" Then we continued and saw lamps. I said: \"What is this, O Jibril?\" He said: \"This is the tree of your father Ibrahim. Shall we approach it?\" I said: \"Yes.\" We approached it, and he welcomed me and prayed for blessing for me. Then we went on until we entered the Holy House [Jerusalem]. He tied the mount to the ring that the prophets used to tie their mounts to. Then I entered the Holy House, and the prophets—those whom Allah the Exalted has named and those He has not named—were presented to me. I prayed with them all except these three: Musa, 'Isa, and Ibrahim (peace and blessings be upon them)."],[5889,"Abu Ya'la said: Hudbah b. Khalid and Shayban b. Farrukh narrated to us, saying: Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us."],[5891,"When Suraqah returned from pursuing the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr ؓ, he began to recall what he had seen of the horse and the hardship he had endured in seeking them. Abu Jahl heard of that, and he feared that Suraqah might embrace Islam after seeing what he had seen. So he composed some verses about it: \"O Banu Mudlij, I fear your fool Suraqah, who seeks to mislead you into supporting Muhammad. Beware that he does not abandon your assembly, so that you become scattered after honor and sovereignty. The fool of the tribe thinks he has brought a false argument against a clear, rightly guided path of truth. How can what he says be the truth, when he has not come with clear, upright truth? But he has gone as a stranger, with his displeasure, to Yathrib, away from us—so far is his birthplace! And if he had not come to Yathrib as a fugitive, the falling of the polished Mashrafi sword would have grieved him.\" Suraqah answered him, saying: \"O Abu al-Hakam, by Allah, if you had witnessed the affair of my steed when its legs sank, you would have marveled and would not doubt that Muhammad came to us with a clear proof—so who can conceal it? Restrain the people from him, for I see that one day the signs of his affair will become manifest, through a matter in which victory will be wished for—and alas, if only all people would be at peace with him.\""],[5892,"A man from the polytheists came and faced the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his private parts while urinating. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, does the man not see us?\" He ﷺ said: \"If he saw us, he would not face us with his private parts,\" meaning they were in the cave."],[5893,"The oldest of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, meaning in the migration, were Abu Bakr al-Siddiq and Sahl b. Bayda' ؓ."],[5895,"We remained in Madinah for two years before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, building mosques and establishing prayer."],[5896,"When the Prophet ﷺ met the leaders from the Ansar, he said: \"Will you shelter me and protect me?\" They said: \"What will be for us?\" He ﷺ said: \"Paradise will be for you.\""],[5897,"I came to al-Miqdam b. Ma'dikarib in the mosque and said: 'O Abu Yazid, the people claim that you did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'Glory be to Allah! By Allah, I saw him while I was walking with my uncle, and he took hold of this ear of mine and said to my uncle: \"Do you think this one remembers his mother or his father?\" We said to him...'"],[5899,"Quraysh set a reward of forty uqiyyah for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr. He said: While I was sitting, a man came to me and said: \"The two men for whom Quraysh has set what it has set are near you in such-and-such a place.\" He said: I went to my horse, which was in the pasture, and startled it. Then I took my spear and mounted. He said: I began to drag the spear for fear that the people of the water would share in the reward with me. He said: When I saw them, Abu Bakr ؓ said: \"A seeker is seeking us.\" The Prophet ﷺ turned and said: \"O Allah, suffice me against him as You will.\" He said: My horse became stuck in the mud, though I was on firm ground, and I fell upon a stone and was overturned. I said: \"Call upon the One who did what I see to release it\"—and he made a covenant with him that he would never disobey Him again. He said: He ﷺ supplicated for him, and the horse was freed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Will you give it to me?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then divert the people from us here,\" and he took the coastal route near the sea. He said: So I was for them a seeker at the beginning of the day and a guard at the end of the day. He ﷺ said: \"When we settle in Madinah, if you wish to come to us, then come.\" When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Madinah and was victorious over the people of Badr and Uhud, and those around him embraced Islam, Suraqah said: \"It reached me that he ﷺ intended to send Khalid b. al-Walid ؓ to Banu Mudlij, so I came to him...\""],[5900,"And al-Harith said: Bishr b. 'Umar al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad b. Salama narrated to us its full length. Al-Bukhari has extracted this mentioned hadith with its meaning from another route on the authority of Suraqa ؓ, and in this there is a difference in several places."],[5901,"When the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr ؓ set out, hiding in the cave, they passed by a slave tending sheep, and they asked him for some milk to drink. He said: By Allah, I have no ewe to be milked, except that here is a young she-goat that became pregnant at the beginning of winter, so she has no milk left; she has aborted her young. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Bring her to us. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for blessing upon her, then he milked a bowl and gave Abu Bakr ؓ to drink. Then he milked another and gave the shepherd to drink. Then he milked and drank ﷺ. The slave said: By Allah, who are you? I have never seen anyone like you. He said: Do you think that if I tell you, you will keep it secret? He said: Yes. He ﷺ said: I am Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah. He said: Are you the one whom Quraysh claim is a Sābi’? He ﷺ said: They do say that. He said: I bear witness that you are indeed the Messenger of Allah, and that what you have brought is true, and that no one does what you have done except a prophet. Then he said: Shall I follow you? He ﷺ said: No, not until you hear that we have prevailed. When that reaches you, then come out. So he followed him after he left the cave."],[5904,"The morning of Badr was on Monday, seventeen nights having passed of Ramadan."],[5905,"He said after his eyesight was gone: If I could see, I would show you now at Badr the ravine from which the angels came out; I have no doubt and I do not waver."],[5906,"I came upon Abu Jahl on the day of Badr, and I approached him and struck him, and Allah Almighty killed him. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him, and I found 'Aqil b. Abi Talib with him as a captive. He said: Was it you who killed him? I said: Yes. He said: You lie! I said: O enemy of Allah, do you call me a liar? He said: What mark did you see on him? I said: I saw on his thigh a ring like the ring of a camel. He said: You spoke the truth; it is a brand of fire with which he was cauterized for pain. He said: Abu Jahl said: What does the raging war resent of me, a mature camel of two years, a six-year-old; for such a one my mother bore me."],[5907,"'Amr b. Muhammad and Yahya b. Adam reported to us, they said: Isra'il narrated to us, and he mentioned it."],[5908,"Regarding the Almighty's saying: “And when He showed them to you, when you met, as few in your eyes, and He made you appear few in their eyes,” he said: They appeared few in our eyes, so much so that I said to a man beside me: Do you think they are seventy? He said: I think they are a hundred. Until we captured a man from them and asked him, and he said: We were a thousand."],[5909,"Allah Almighty obliged them to fight one against ten, and that was heavy and hard for them, so Allah Almighty reduced it for them to a man fighting two men. And Allah Almighty revealed about that: “If there are among you twenty steadfast, they will overcome two hundred” to the end of the verses. Then He said: “Were it not for a prior decree from Allah, a great punishment would have touched you for what you took,” meaning the spoils of Badr. He says: Had I not decreed that I will not punish those who disobey Me until I have given them prior warning. Then He said: “O Prophet, say to those captives in your hands,” the verse. Al-'Abbas ؓ said: It was revealed concerning me, by Allah, when I informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of my Islam and asked him to settle with me the twenty uqiyyas that I had taken with me, and he gave me in return twenty slaves, each of whom had traded with wealth in his hand, along with what I hope for from the forgiveness of Allah Almighty."],[5910,"I saw before the defeat of the people, while the people were fighting, something like a black striped cloak coming from the sky, like black ants. I did not doubt that they were the angels, and there was nothing but the defeat of the people."],[5911,"The slogan of the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Badr was: O Victorious One, give death."],[5912,"I said to 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf ؓ: O uncle, tell me about your story on the day of Badr. He ؓ said: Read after the one hundred and twentieth verse of Al 'Imran, and you will find our story: “And when you went forth from your family, assigning the believers positions for battle” to His saying: “that you not falter.” He said: They are those who sought safety from the polytheists, to His saying: “while you were looking on.” He said: It is the believers' wish to meet the enemy, to His saying: “when you slew them by His permission.”"],[5913,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to blind its wells, meaning on the day of Badr."],[5914,"I was at the well of Badr drawing water from it, when a strong wind came, then another strong wind came, the like of which I had never seen except the one before it, then a third strong wind came. The first was Mikail with a thousand angels on the right of the Prophet ﷺ, the second was Israfil with a thousand angels on the left of the Prophet ﷺ, and the third was Jibril ﷺ with a thousand angels. Abu Bakr ؓ was on his right and I was on his left. When Allah Almighty defeated the disbelievers, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted me on a horse. When I was settled on it, he made me ride, and I was on its neck. I supplicated to Allah Almighty, and He made me firm on it. I thrust with my spear until the blood reached my armpit."],[5915,"We were praying with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Battle of Badr when he smiled ﷺ in his prayer. When he finished the prayer, we said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you smile. He ﷺ said: Mikail ﷺ passed by me with traces of dust on his wing, returning from pursuing the people, and he smiled at me, so I smiled back at him."],[5917,"His father Sa'd ؓ went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Badr. When he was at al-Rawha', he died. He wrote his will at the end of his journey, bequeathing to the Prophet ﷺ his mount, his saddle, and three wasqs of barley. He accepted it, then returned it to his heirs, and allotted his share for him."],[5918,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted a share for Ja'far b. Abi Talib ؓ on the day of Badr."],[5920,"On the day of Badr, 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt was brought as a captive. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I will surely kill you. He said: Will you kill me from among Quraysh? He ﷺ said: Yes. Then he turned to his companions ؓ and said: He came to me while I was prostrating and stepped on my neck. By Allah, he did not lift it until I thought my eyes would fall out. And he brought the placenta of a slaughtered camel and threw it on me, until Fatimah came and removed it from my head. He said: Then he was ordered, and he was killed."],[5921,"The two sons of 'Afra' struck him, and Ibn Mas'ud ؓ finished him off, meaning Abu Jahl."],[5923,"They gathered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he walked with them until he reached Baqi' al-Gharqad on a moonlit night. He said: Go forth in the name of Allah. O Allah, help them. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned to his house. They went on until they reached his fortress, meaning Ka'b b. al-Ashraf. Abu Na'ilah called out to him, and he came down to him while he was recently married. His wife said to him: You are a warrior, and a man of war does not come down at such an hour. He said to her: It is Abu Na'ilah. By Allah, if he found me sleeping, he would not wake me. She said: By Allah, I recognize evil in his voice. He said to her: If a young man is called to a thrust, he answers. So he came down to them, and they talked for a while. Then they said: If we walked to Shi'b al-'Ajuz and talked tonight, for we have not done that for a long time. He said: Yes. They went out walking. Then Abu Na'ilah felt his hand in the side of his head and said: I have never seen perfume as fragrant as tonight. Then he walked for a while, then repeated it until he was reassured. He put his hand into the side of his head and grabbed his hair, then said: Strike the enemy of Allah. Their swords fell upon him in confusion. The enemy of Allah screamed a scream, and no fortress remained but a fire was lit on it. Al-Harith's leg was injured. Muhammad b. Maslamah said: When I saw that the swords were not effective, I remembered a short sword in my scabbard. I took it and placed it on his navel and pressed on it until it reached his pubic area, and he fell. Then we left and took the road past Banu Umayyah, then Banu Qurayzah, then Bu'ath, then we traveled at night through the Harrah of al-'Urayd. Al-Harith was delayed and bleeding, so we stopped for him. Then we carried him until we came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the end of the night while he was praying. He came out to us, and we informed him of the killing of the enemy of Allah. He ﷺ spat on the wound of al-Harith, and we returned with him to his house. The people dispersed to their camps. When morning came, the Jews feared because of our attack on the enemy of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever you find of the men of the Jews, kill him. Muhayyisah b. Mas'ud jumped on Ibn Sunaynah, a man from the Jewish merchants, who used to trade with them and mix with them, and killed him. Huwayyisah b. Mas'ud, who was then a polytheist and older than him, began to beat him and say: O enemy of Allah, you killed him? By Allah, there is much fat in your belly from his wealth. He said: By Allah, a man ordered me to kill him, and if he ordered me to kill you, I would strike your neck. He said: By Allah, if Muhammad ordered you to kill me, would you kill me? He said: Yes, by Allah. He said: By Allah, a religion that has brought you to this is indeed amazing. Thus the first Islam of Huwayyisah came from the words of his brother. Muhayyisah composed poetry about that."],[5924,"His wife said: I hear a voice from which I detect the smell of blood. He said: It is only Abu Na'ilah, a brother of mine. If he found me sleeping, he would not wake me. A noble man, when called to a thrust, answers. He named those who came to him with Abu Na'ilah: Muhammad b. Maslamah, 'Abbad b. Bishr, al-Harith b. Mu'adh, and Abu 'Ubays b. Jabir."],[5926,"By Allah, on that day I saw the anklets of the women exposed as they ran when the people were defeated, and I saw nothing to prevent taking them. We thought them all killed, none of them returning to us. The bearers of the banner were struck down and stood firm by it until it came to a slave of his, an Abyssinian called Sawab. Then Sawab was killed and threw down the banner, and no creature of Allah Almighty approached it until 'Amrah bt. 'Alqamah al-Harithiyyah rushed to it and raised it for them, and the people rallied to it. Al-Zubayr ؓ said: By Allah, while we were thus, having gained the upper hand over them, the archers disobeyed the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They came to the camp when they saw it stripped and we had driven them from it. They desired the spoils and abandoned the covenant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They began taking the goods. Then the cavalry came upon us from behind and crushed us, and the people turned in defeat. A crier, whom they thought was Satan, shouted: Indeed Muhammad has been killed. The people were horrified, and they trampled one another, becoming three groups: one third wounded, one third killed, and one third defeated. The war intensified. The archers had disagreed among themselves. A group, seeing the people falling upon the spoils, said: Allah Almighty has defeated the polytheists and the Muslims have taken the spoils, so what are you waiting for? Another group said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has instructed you and forbidden you to leave your place, whether it goes for him or against him. They disputed about that. Then the first group of archers insisted on joining the camp, so the people dispersed and left their place. At that moment the cavalry of the polytheists charged."],[5927,"By Allah, drowsiness was overcoming me when I heard Ibn Qushayr saying it, and I could not hear it from him except as in a dream. Then he recited: \"Indeed, those who turned back among you on the day the two armies met, it was Satan who caused them to slip because of some of what they had earned, and Allah has pardoned them. Indeed, Allah is Forgiving and Forbearing.\" He said: Those who turned back when the people fled were 'Uthman b. 'Affan, Sa'id b. 'Uthman al-Zuraqi, and his brother 'Uqbah b. 'Uthman, until they reached a mountain near Madinah called al-Hajib in the valley of al-A'was. They stayed there for three days. They claimed that when they returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: You went far in it. Then he said: \"O you who believe, do not be like those who disbelieved\" - meaning the hypocrites - \"and said to their brothers when they traveled in the land or were on an expedition, 'If they had been with us, they would not have died or been killed,' so that Allah makes that a cause of regret in their hearts.\" He said: seeking and regretting, and that will not avail them anything. Then the story continued with what He commands His Prophet ﷺ and entrusts to him, until he reached His saying: \"And when a disaster struck you, although you had struck them with twice as much, you said, 'How is this?' Say, 'It is from yourselves'\" - that which came from the archers. He said: And \"What struck you on the day the two armies met was by Allah's permission, and that He might know the believers\" - meaning the openness of their affair and that their matter be manifest - \"and that He might know the hypocrites\" - so their affair would be open; meaning 'Abdullah b. Ubayy and those with him who turned back from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he marched to his enemy. And it was said to them: \"Come, fight in the way of Allah or defend.\" They said: \"If we knew there would be fighting, we would follow you.\" That was their saying when the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them while they were marching to Uhud, when they turned away from them: Will you abandon us and hand us over to our enemy? They said: We do not think there will be fighting. If we thought there would be fighting, we would follow you. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: \"They were closer that day to disbelief than to faith, saying with their mouths what was not in their hearts, and Allah is most knowing of what they conceal\" - those who said to their brothers from their kin, not meaning their brothers in religion, \"If they had obeyed us, they would not have been killed.\" Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: \"Say, 'Then avert death from yourselves, if you are truthful.'\""],[5928,"I saw myself with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud when fear intensified upon us and sleep was sent upon us. There was none of us but his chin - or he said: his chin - was on his chest. By Allah, I heard as in a dream the words of Mu'attib b. Qushayr: \"If we had any say in the matter, we would not have been killed here.\" I memorized them, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed about that: \"Then after distress, He sent down upon you security - drowsiness\" up to His saying: \"we would not have been killed here\" for the saying of Mu'attib b. Qushayr. He said: \"If you had been in your houses\" until: \"And Allah is All-Knowing of what is in the breasts.\""],[5929,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ climbing up in Uhud... and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered 'Ali b. Abi Talib to go to al-Mihras, and he brought him water in his shield. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came with it, and when he wanted to drink from it, he found it had a smell and disliked it, so he washed his face ﷺ with it from the blood that had struck him, while saying: Allah's anger is severe upon whoever made the face of the Messenger of Allah bleed. The one who made him bleed that day was 'Utbah b. Abi Waqqas."],[5930,"On the day of Uhud, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was scratched and his front tooth was broken. Ali ؓ came to him and bent over him, weeping. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Bring me water.” So he brought him water in a bowl from the Mihras. When he brought it near him, he found it foul, so he began washing the blood from him and saying: “Allah's wrath is severe upon a people who wounded the face of His Prophet.” Then he said: “See what Sa'd b. al-Rabi' has done, for I saw twelve spears planted in him.” The messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him and said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to see what you have done.” He said ؓ: “Convey my greetings to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and tell him that I am at my last breath. And convey my greetings to your people and say to them: If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perishes while any of you has an eyelid that blinks, then you have no excuse before Allah Almighty.” Then he said: “Who will take this sword with its due right?” This hadith is narrated by al-Zubayr about himself. He said: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, I will.” But he turned away from me once. I said: “He only turned away from me because of some evil in me.” Then he said: “Who will take this sword with its due right?” I said: “I will.” But he turned away from me two or three times. Then Abu Dujana ؓ said: “I will take it and strike with it until it bends,” or words to that effect. So he gave him the sword. Al-Zubayr said: I followed him to see what he would do. He did not come upon any man of the polytheists except that he killed him. He came upon a man who had been held back from fighting and killed him. Then he came upon a woman who was reciting: “If you advance, we embrace and spread the cushions; or if you retreat, we part with an unloving parting.” He raised the sword over her, then withheld his hand from her. I said: “O Abu Dujana, you did such and such, until you came to the woman and raised the sword over her, then withheld your hand?” He said: “I deemed the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ too noble for her.”"],[5931,"Satan shouted on the day of Uhud: “Muhammad has been killed.” Ka'b b. Malik ؓ said: I was the first to recognize the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I saw his eyes beneath the helmet, so I called out at the top of my voice: “This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He gestured to me to be silent. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: “And Muhammad is but a messenger; messengers have passed away before him. If he dies or is killed, will you turn back on your heels?” — the verse."],[5932,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on the day of Uhud until when he passed Thaniyyat al-Wada', he looked behind him and saw a rough battalion. He ﷺ said: “Who is this?” It was said: “This is 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul with his allies from the Jews of Banu Qaynuqa', and they are the clan of 'Abd Allah b. Salam.” He said: “Have they become Muslims?” He said: “They are upon their own religion.” He said: “Tell them to go back, for we do not seek the help of polytheists against polytheists.”"],[5933,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud wearing two coats of mail. And he said: “Would that I had been left with my companions at the foot of the mountain” — meaning the martyrs of Uhud."],[5934,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wore two coats of mail one over the other on the day of Uhud."],[5935,"From al-Sa'ib b. Yazid, from someone who narrated to him from Talha. : :"],[5936,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the grave of Hamza ؓ. The striped cloak was spread over his head, but his feet were exposed, so it was spread over his feet, but his head was exposed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Spread it over his head and put over his feet some harmal shrub.”"],[5937,"When the people dispersed from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud, I looked at the slain and did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among them. I said: “By Allah, it was not for him ﷺ to flee, and I do not see him among the slain. But I think that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, became angry with us for what we did and raised up His Prophet ﷺ. There is nothing better for me than to fight until I am killed.” So I broke the scabbard of my sword, then charged at the people, and they were dispersed before me, and then I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among them."],[5938,"I witnessed Uhud with my masters. I struck a man from the polytheists, and when I killed him I said: “Take it from me, and I am the Persian man.” This reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “Why did you not say: Take it from me, and I am the Ansari man? For the client of a people is one of them.”"],[5940,"Abu Nu'aym said: Abu 'Amr b. Hamdan narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us with it. From this it follows that Abu Nu'aym and Salama b. Nafi' included 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Uqba among the Companions, but there is no basis for that, and Allah knows best. :"],[5941,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Uhud: “Who saw where Hamza was killed?” A man without weapons said: “I saw where he was killed.” He said: “Go and show us.” He went out until he stood over Hamza ؓ and saw him with his belly split and mutilated. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, he has been mutilated.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked looking at him. He ﷺ stood among the slain and said: “I am a witness over these. Shroud them in their blood, for there is no wound inflicted for the sake of Allah but it will come on the Day of Resurrection bleeding, its color the color of blood and its fragrance the fragrance of musk. Put forward the one who knew more of the Qur'an and place him in the niche of the grave.”"],[5943,"Ali brought his sword to Fatimah on the day of Uhud and said: Wash this sword of mine, for I have fought well today. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: If you have fought well, then Asim b. Thabit, Sahl b. Hunayf, and al-Harith b. al-Simmah also fought well."],[5944,"Abu Bakr, whenever he mentioned the day of Uhud, would say: That day was all Talhah's day. Then he began to narrate, saying: I was the first to return to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Uhud. I saw a man fighting alongside the Messenger of God ﷺ in his defense—I think he was protecting him. I said: Would that I were Talhah, since I missed what I missed. I said: Let it be a man from my own people, more beloved to me. Between me and the east there was a man I did not recognize, and I was closer to the Messenger of God ﷺ than he was, yet he was moving swiftly in a way I could not match. Then it turned out he was Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah. I reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and his front tooth had been broken, he had been wounded in the face, and two rings of the helmet had pierced into his cheeks. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Attend to your companion—meaning Talhah—for he has bled profusely. But we paid no attention to his words. I went to remove that from his face, but Abu Ubaydah said: I adjure you by my right to leave me. So he left him, and he disliked touching it with his hand lest he hurt the Prophet ﷺ. He bit down on it with his mouth and extracted one of the rings, and his front tooth fell out with the ring. I went to do the same as he had done, but he said: I adjure you by my right to leave me. So he did as he had done the first time, and his other front tooth fell out with the ring. Thus Abu Ubaydah became one of the most handsome of people in losing his front teeth. We attended to the Prophet ﷺ, then we went to Talhah in one of the pits. He had seventy-some, or fewer or more, wounds from stabs, strikes, and arrows, and his finger had been cut off. We attended to him."],[5947,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from pursuing the confederates and entered Madinah, he bathed, used incense, and took off his armor."],[5948,"The people dispersed from the Messenger of God ﷺ on the night of the confederates, and only twelve men remained with him. The Messenger of God ﷺ came to me while I was crouching from the cold and said: O Ibn al-Yaman, rise and go to the camp of the confederates and observe their situation. I said: O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, I only rose to come to you out of shame from the cold. He said: The cold of the harrah and the cold of the sabkhah. He ﷺ said: Go, O Ibn al-Yaman, for no harm will befall you from cold or heat until you return to me. So I went until I came to their camp and found Abu Sufyan lighting a fire among a small group around him, and the confederates had dispersed from him. I came and sat among them. Abu Sufyan sensed that someone not of them had entered their midst, so he said: Let each man take the hand of his neighbor. I struck with my right hand on the one to my right and took his hand, and I struck with my left hand on the one to my left and took his hand. I remained among them for a little while, then I got up and came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was standing praying. He gestured to me with his hand to come close, so I drew near to him until he threw over me part of the garment he was wearing to warm me. When he ﷺ finished his prayer, he said: O Ibn al-Yaman, sit and tell the people. I said: O Messenger of God, the people have dispersed from Abu Sufyan, and only a small group remains lighting a fire. God Almighty has poured upon them cold like that which He poured upon us, but we hope from God what they do not hope."],[5949,"On the night of the confederates, the people suffered severe hardship and cold such as they had never experienced before. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood praying, and he prayed as long as God willed. Then he said: Who will stand now and bring us news of the enemy? God will whiten his face on the Day of Resurrection. By God, no man among them was able to stand because of the hardship they were in. Then he ﷺ prayed as long as God willed, then said: Who will stand now and bring us news of the enemy? God will place him with me in Paradise. By God, no man among them was able to stand because of the hardship they were in. Then he ﷺ said: O so-and-so, stand. He said: By the One who sent down the Book upon you, I will not come to you now. Then he ﷺ said: O Hudhayfah, stand. Hudhayfah said: I wanted to swear as my companion had sworn, but the Prophet ﷺ said: You are indeed swearers. So I rose to him ﷺ, and he said to me: Go and bring us news of the enemy, and do not do anything until you return to me. Hudhayfah said: He prayed for me that God would protect me from before me and behind me until I returned. I went, and between me and them was a dry salt marsh, and I had hardly crossed it when I found them in a great state. Abu Sufyan was warming himself by a fire of theirs from the cold, and a small fire of theirs sometimes flared up and sometimes died down. When it flared up, I saw those around it. I said: What am I waiting for? This is an enemy of God, and I have seen his position. I took an arrow from my quiver and placed it in the bow, but then I remembered the Prophet's ﷺ words: Do not do anything until you return to me. So I threw it back into the quiver. Then I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him what they were doing, and he ﷺ began to praise God Almighty. Then God, Mighty and Majestic, sent the wind, and he mentioned the verse: O you who believe, remember the favor of God upon you... (to the end of the verse)."],[5950,"The Messenger of God ﷺ struck with his hands in the trench and said: In the name of God, and with Him we begin. If we worshiped other than Him, we would be wretched. Blessed be a Lord and blessed be a religion."],[5951,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day of the trench: O God, there is no life but the life of the Hereafter, so have mercy on the Ansar and the Muhajirun, and curse Adal and al-Qarah. They burdened us with carrying the stones."],[5952,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered the digging of the trench around Madinah. A group came to him and told him that they had found a boulder they could not break. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up, and we stood with him. He took the pickaxe and struck, and I never heard a strike from a man louder than it. He ﷺ said: God is Greatest! Persia has been conquered. Then he struck another similar blow and said: God is Greatest! Byzantium has been conquered. Then he struck another similar blow and said: God is Greatest! God has brought Himyar as helpers and supporters."],[5953,"The Prophet ﷺ sent al-Zubayr and another man on the night of the confederates, on a moonlit night, and they looked around. Then they came back while the Messenger of God ﷺ was in a woolen cloak belonging to Umm Salamah. He brought them both into the cloak, and the Messenger of God ﷺ clung to Umm Salamah."],[5955,"On that day Sa'd b. Mu'adh ruled that those who had reached puberty should be killed. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: You have judged among them with the judgment of God Almighty from above seven heavens."],[5956,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent Khawwat b. Jubayr to Banu Qurayzah to call them, and they said: Our parable is that of a man who had two wings, one was cut off and the other remained. So they refused."],[5957,"When it was the affair of Banu Qurayzah, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Call to me your chief to judge among His servants, meaning Sa'd b. Mu'adh. He came, and he said to him: Judge. He said: I fear I may not attain God's judgment, Mighty and Majestic, regarding them. He ﷺ said: Judge among them. So he judged, and he ﷺ said: You have attained the judgment of God, Mighty and Majestic, and His Messenger."],[5958,"I have not forgotten the day of the trench while he was handing them the milk, and his hair was dusty - meaning the Prophet ﷺ - and he was saying: 'Indeed the good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirun.'"],[5959,"Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: 'Affan narrated to us: Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us: Ibn 'Awn narrated to us something similar, and the first is more general. (204) And the hadith of Safiyyah ؓ regarding her virtue has already been mentioned. : :"],[5961,"'Uthman said to Abu Dharr ؓ: 'Where were you on the day when the milch-camels of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were raided?' He said: 'I was at the well, giving water.'"],[5963,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them regarding a military expedition he dispatched against Banu Lihyan: 'Let one man from every two of you go forth, and the reward will be shared between them.'"],[5964,"And Ahmad b. Mani' said: Husayn b. Muhammad narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us, something similar. :"],[5966,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to Heraclius, the ruler of the Romans: 'From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Heraclius, the ruler of the Romans. I call you to Islam. If you submit, you will have what the Muslims have, and you will be responsible for what they are responsible for. If you do not enter Islam, then pay the jizyah, for Allah, the Exalted, says: Fight those who do not believe in Allah [Quran 9:29] ... Otherwise, do not come between the farmers and Islam, that they may enter it or pay the jizyah.'"],[5968,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me, and he sent with me a man from the Ansar, and he said: 'Go to Abu Sufyan and kill him in his courtyard.' They became aware of us, so we climbed the mountain. Then a man from Banu Tamim came to us, and I killed him. Then I entered a cave. A man from Banu Dil b. Bakr came to us and entered with us. I said: 'Who are you?' He said: 'From Banu Bakr.' I said: 'And I am from Banu Bakr.' He lay down and raised his voice singing, and he said: 'I am not a Muslim as long as I live, nor do I adhere to the religion of the Muslims.' I said: 'Sleep, and you will find out.' He slept, and I killed him. Then I went out and found two men whom Quraysh had sent. I said to them: 'Surrender as prisoners.' One of them refused, so I killed him, and the other surrendered. I brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5969,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me, and he sent with me a man from the Ansar after Khubayb and his companions ؓ were killed. He said: 'Kill Abu Sufyan in his courtyard.' I went out with my companion until we reached the bottom of Ya'jaj from the direction of the mountain pass. He said: 'My companion was a simple man, with no travel experience. I said to him: 'If you fear anything, go to your camel and ride it until you catch up with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'My companion said to me: 'Would you like to circumambulate the House?' I said: 'I know the people of Makkah better: when it gets dark, they sprinkle their courtyards and sit in them, and I am more recognizable among them than a piebald horse.' He kept at me until we circumambulated seven times. Then we went out and passed by their gatherings. They said: 'This is 'Amr; by Allah, he has not come with good.' And 'Amr ؓ was a daring man called al-Khali' (the outcast). He said: 'We hastened until we climbed the mountain, and I entered a cave. There was 'Uthman b. Malik, or 'Ubayd Allah b. Malik al-Taymi, cutting grass for a horse. When he approached the cave, I said to my companion: 'By Allah, if this man sees us, he will surely point us out.' He said: 'I went out to him and stabbed him with the dagger under his breast, and I gave him the fatal blow. He screamed a scream that the people of Makkah heard.' He said: 'They came, and I returned to my place and entered it. The people of Makkah came and found him with a spark of life. They said: 'Who stabbed you?' He said: ''Amr b. Umayyah.' Then he died before they could get from him any information about our location.' He said: 'Then we went out, and there was Khubayb on his wooden cross. My companion said to me: 'Would you like to take Khubayb down from his cross and bury him?' I said: 'Yes. Move away from me, and if I am delayed, take the road.' I went to Khubayb and took him down from his cross, and carried him on my back. I had not walked with him twenty cubits before the guards surprised me; they had placed guards over him. He said: 'I dropped him, and I will never forget the thud of his body on the ground when I dropped him. Then I took to the yellow mountains until I descended to al-'Alil, the 'Alil of Dajnan, while they were pursuing me. I entered a cave,' and he mentioned the story of the one he killed. 'Then I came out of the cave to lands I knew well. Then I took to a riding camel, and I saw two men whom Quraysh had sent to spy out the news. I said to one of them: 'Surrender as a prisoner.' He refused, so I shot him and killed him, and the other surrendered. I brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5970,"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him alone as a spy to Quraysh. I came to the wooden cross of Khubayb, and I was afraid of being watched. I climbed up and untied Khubayb, and he fell to the ground. I withdrew to a place not far away, and I turned around but did not see Khubayb. It was as if the earth had swallowed him. He said: 'No trace of Khubayb's remains has been seen to this hour.'"],[5973,"The scribe of the document on the day of al-Hudaybiyyah was 'Ali b. Abi Talib."],[5974,"I asked al-Zuhri: 'Who was the scribe of the document on that day?' He laughed and said: 'It was 'Ali ؓ. But if you asked those people - meaning Banu Umayyah - they would say: It was 'Uthman.'"],[5975,"He was standing over the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a sword, and he was veiled. 'Urwah - meaning Ibn Mas'ud al-Thaqafi - began to touch the beard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while speaking to him. Al-Mughirah said to him: 'You must stop your hand, or your hand will not return to you.' And al-Mughirah was girded with a sword. 'Urwah said: 'Who is this, O Messenger of Allah?' He ﷺ said: 'This is your nephew, al-Mughirah.' He said: 'Indeed, O treacherous one. I have not washed my head from your treachery.'"],[5976,"Urwah b. Mas'ud said to his people at the time of al-Hudaybiyyah: 'O my people, I have seen kings and spoken to them. Send me to Muhammad so I may speak with him.' So he came to him at al-Hudaybiyyah. Urwah began to speak with the Prophet ﷺ and reached for the beard of the Prophet ﷺ. Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah was armed with weapons at the head of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Al-Mughirah said to him: 'Withdraw your hand before it does not reach you.' Urwah raised his head and said: 'Is it you? By God, I am still within your treachery, and I have not yet left it.' Urwah returned to his people and said: 'O my people, I have seen kings and spoken with them. I have never seen anyone like Muhammad. He is not a king. I saw the sacrificial animals held back, and I think you will be struck by a calamity.' Then he departed with those of his people who followed him, climbed the wall of al-Ta'if, and testified that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. A man from his people shot him with an arrow and killed him. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Praise be to God who has placed in my community someone like the companion of Yasin.'"],[5977,"We set out with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the year of al-Hudaybiyyah. When we were at al-Suqya, Mu'adh said: 'Who will give us water in our water-skins?' He said: So I went out with some youths with me until we came to al-Uthaya, and we gave water and drew water. He said: Then when it was after the evening prayer of the night, a man was struggling with his camel for water. He said: And it was the Messenger of God ﷺ. I took hold of his riding camel and made it kneel. He said: He came forward and prayed the 'Isha' prayer, and I was on his right. Then he prayed thirteen rak'ahs."],[5979,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me, Abu Qatadah, an ally of theirs from the Ansar, and Abdullah b. Atik to Ibn Abi al-Huqayq to kill him. We went out at night, tracked their doors, and hung them on them from outside. Then we gathered the keys. The group climbed into the palm trees, and I and Abdullah b. Atik entered the stairs of Ibn Abi al-Huqayq. Abdullah b. Atik spoke, and Ibn Abi al-Huqayq said: 'May your mother lose you, Abdullah! How did you get to this land? Get up and open for him, for a nobleman is not turned away from his door at this hour.' She got up, and I said to Abdullah b. Atik: 'Go ahead.' He drew his sword upon them. His wife went to scream, so he drew his sword upon her, but then he remembered the saying of the Messenger of God ﷺ that he forbade killing women and children, so he refrained. Abdullah b. Unays said: I entered upon him in his upper room, and I stood looking at the extreme whiteness of his skin in the darkness of the night. When he saw me, he took a pillow and covered himself with it. I went to raise the sword to strike him, but I could not because of the shortness of the room, so I stabbed him with a thrust. Then I went out, and my companion said: 'Did you do it?' I said: 'Yes.' He entered and stood over him. Then we went out and descended the stairs, and Abdullah b. Atik fell on the stairs and said: 'Oh my leg! My leg is broken.' I said: 'There is nothing wrong with your leg,' and I put down my bow and carried him. Abdullah was short and slight, so I brought him down and found his leg was fine. We went on until we caught up with our companions. The woman cried out: 'Oh father of the house!' and the people of Khaybar rose up to kill him. I remembered the place of my bow and said: 'I will not return until I take my bow.' I went back and found the people of Khaybar in an uproar, and they were saying nothing but 'Who killed Ibn Abi al-Huqayq?' I did not look at the face of any person nor did any person look at my face but I said as they said: 'Who killed Ibn Abi al-Huqayq?' until I came to the stairs. I climbed up with the people, took my bow, and then caught up with my companions. We traveled at night and hid by day. When we hid during the day, we set a watchman to look out for us until we approached al-Madinah. When we were at al-Bayda', I was their watchman. Then I signaled to them with my garment, and they went down and ran briskly. I descended following their tracks and caught up with them until we reached al-Madinah. My companions said to me: 'Did you see anything?' I said: 'No, but I saw what overtook you of exhaustion, and I wanted fear to carry you.' We came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon to the people. He said: 'The faces have succeeded.' We said: 'May your face succeed, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Did you kill him?' We said: 'Yes.' He called for the sword with which he was killed and said: 'This is his food in the edges of the sword.'"],[5981,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said during the expedition of Khaybar: 'Whoever has a weak or refractory mount, let him return.' He ﷺ ordered a caller to announce that, and some people returned. Among the people was a man on a refractory young camel. At night he passed by some black object, and it bolted with him and threw him, breaking his neck. When he was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'What is the matter with your companion?' They said: 'His affair was such and such.' He ﷺ said: 'O Bilal, did you not announce to the people: \"Whoever has a weak or refractory mount, let him return?\"' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'But he refused to pray over him.'"],[5982,"I saw Aslam when they complained to the Prophet ﷺ about severe hardship. He ﷺ called upon the people, and they arose. I saw Aslam be the first to reach the fortress. The sun did not set on that day until God Almighty granted us victory over it, and it was the fortress of al-Sa'b b. Mu'adh in al-Natah."],[5983,"The Messenger of God ﷺ divided on the day of Khaybar: for the horseman three shares, and for the foot soldier one share."],[5984,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent Abu Bakr al-Siddiq with his banner to one of the fortresses of Khaybar. He fought and returned without conquering it, and he had exerted himself. Then he sent Umar b. al-Khattab the next day, and he fought and returned without conquering it, and he had exerted himself. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'I will give the banner to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and God will grant victory at his hands.' Then he ﷺ called for Ali and spat into his eyes, then said: 'Take this banner and go with it until God grants you victory.' Salamah said: He went out with it, by God, trotting briskly, while we followed his tracks behind him, until he planted his banner in a pile of stones beneath the fortress. A Jew looked down at him from the top of the fortress and said: 'Who are you?' He said: 'Ali b. Abi Talib.' The Jew said to his companions: 'You are defeated, by what was revealed to Moses'—or as he said. He did not return until God granted victory at his hands."],[5986,"Usamah b. Zayd came after the killing of his father and stood before the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the eyes of the Messenger of God ﷺ shed tears. Then he came the next day and stood in that same place, and he ﷺ said to him: 'Shall I encounter from you today what I encountered from you yesterday?'"],[5988,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ become angry over the affair of Banu Ka'b with an anger I had not seen him show for a long time. He said: 'May God not help me if I do not help Banu Ka'b.' And he ﷺ said: 'Tell Abu Bakr and Umar to prepare for this expedition.' He said: They came to A'ishah and said to her: 'Where does the Messenger of God ﷺ intend to go?' She said: 'I saw him become angry over the affair of Banu Ka'b with an anger I had not seen him show for a long time.'"],[5989,"On the day of the conquest of Makkah, he gave him the banner of Sa'd b. Ubadah, and al-Zubayr entered Makkah with two banners."],[5991,"The Messenger of God ﷺ granted safety to the people on the day of the conquest of Makkah except for four people: Abd al-Uzza b. Khatal, Miqyas b. Subabah, Abdullah b. Sa'd, and Umm Sarah. As for Abd al-Uzza b. Khatal, he was killed while clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah. He said: A man from the Ansar vowed to kill Abdullah b. Sa'd if he saw him, and he was Uthman's foster brother. He was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ to intercede for him. When the Ansari saw him, he took hold of his sword and went to him, but he found him in the circle of the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Ansari kept hesitating and disliked to advance upon him because he was in the circle of the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ stretched out his hand and accepted his pledge of allegiance, then he ﷺ said to the Ansari: 'I waited for you to fulfill your vow.' He said: 'O Messenger of God, I was in awe of you. Could you not have signaled to me?' He ﷺ said: 'It is not for a prophet to signal.' He said: As for Miqyas b. Subabah, he had a brother with the Messenger of God ﷺ who was killed by mistake. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent with him a man from Banu Fihr to take his blood money from the Ansar. When the blood money was collected for him and he returned, the Fihri slept, and Miqyas jumped up, took a stone, and struck his head with it, killing him. He then went on saying: 'It healed the soul that the one who spent the night in the open, supported, his two garments stained with the blood of the jugular veins. The anxieties of the soul before killing him used to beset me and make me forget the softness of beds. I killed with him a man of Fihr and paid his blood money to the nobles of Banu al-Najjar, lords of Fari'. With that I fulfilled my vow and achieved my revenge, and I was the first to return to the idols.' As for Umm Sarah: she was a freedwoman of Quraysh. She came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and complained to him of need, so he gave her something. Then a man came to her and sent with her a letter to Makkah... And he mentioned the story of Hatib, as it is in the original."],[5992,"The name of Ibn Khatal was ʿAbdullāh. He had two slave girls who would sing satires against the Messenger of God ﷺ. So the Messenger of God ﷺ granted safety to all the people except Ibn Khatal, his two singing girls, ʿAbdullāh b. Saʿd b. Abī Sarḥ, and Miqyas b. Ṣubābah al-Laythī. He ﷺ did not grant them safety, so they were all killed except one of the two singing girls, for she embraced Islam."],[5993,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent word to Quraysh: “To proceed: if you disavow the alliance of Banū Bakr or pay blood money for Khuzāʿah, [then well and good]; otherwise, I declare war on you.” Quraẓah b. ʿAbd ʿAmr b. Nawfal b. ʿAbd Manāf, Muʿāwiyah’s in-law, said: “Banū Bakr are an ill-omened people. We will not pay blood money for what they killed, lest neither short hair nor wool remain for us, and we will not disavow their alliance, for no one else remains upon our religion besides them. Rather, we will declare war on him.”"],[5994,"“Yes, whoever enters the house of Abū Sufyān is safe, and whoever locks his door is safe.” When he went back to Makkah to inform them, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Detain him at a narrow pass in the valley, at the place where the cavalry will be halted, until the armies of God pass by him.” So al-ʿAbbās detained him where the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded. The tribes passed by with their banners, and every time a banner passed, he asked: “Who are these?” I said: “Banū Sulaym.” He said: “What do I have to do with Banū Sulaym?” Then another passed, and he said: “Who are these?” I said: “Muzaynah.” He said: “What do I have to do with Muzaynah?” He kept saying that until the green squadron of the Messenger of God ﷺ passed, containing the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār, in which nothing could be seen but their eyes. He said: “Who is this?” I said: “This is the Messenger of God ﷺ among the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār.” He said: “No one can withstand these. By God, the kingship of your nephew has become great today!” I said: “Woe to you, O Abū Sufyān! It is prophethood.” He said: “Then yes.” I said: “Hasten to your people.” He left until he came to them in Makkah and began shouting at the top of his voice: “O people of Quraysh! This is Muḥammad; he has come to you with what you cannot withstand.” His wife Hind bt. ʿUtbah stood up, grabbed his mustache, and said: “Kill this fat, greasy fool! The camel has become excited from the vanguard of a people.” Abū Sufyān said: “Do not let this woman deceive you about yourselves. Whoever enters the house of Abū Sufyān is safe.” They said: “May God fight you! What does your house avail us?” He said: “And whoever locks his door is safe.” This is a sound hadith. Maʿmar, Ibn ʿUyaynah, and Mālik narrated part of it from al-Zuhrī in the story of the fast, and the two Shaykhs and others included it. Aḥmad narrated part of it from the hadith of Ibn Isḥāq. Abū Dāwūd narrated a very abbreviated part of it from the story of Abū Sufyān, but none of the six imams nor Aḥmad narrated it in full. Al-Dhuhlī narrated it in full in al-Zuhrīyāt from the path of Abū Idrīs from Muḥammad b. Isḥāq, but it does not contain Ibn Isḥāq’s explicit statement of having heard it from al-Zuhrī. The wording here is very good."],[5995,"When the Prophet ﷺ conquered Makkah, Iblīs let out a loud cry, and his offspring gathered around him. He said: “Despair of ever returning the community of Muḥammad to polytheism after this day of yours. But spread among them—meaning in Makkah—wailing and poetry.”"],[5996,"We entered Makkah with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and in the House or around the House there were three hundred and sixty idols worshipped besides God Almighty. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered that they be thrown on their faces, then he said: “Truth has come and falsehood has vanished; indeed falsehood is bound to vanish.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ entered the House and prayed two rakʿahs in it. He saw in it images of Ibrāhīm, Ismāʿīl, and Isḥāq, and they had placed divining arrows in Ibrāhīm’s hand with which he sought omens. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “May God fight them! Ibrāhīm never sought omens with divining arrows.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ called for saffron and smeared it over those images."],[5997,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ intended to march on Makkah, he sent word to some of his companions that he intended to go to Makkah, among them Ḥāṭib b. Abī Baltaʿah, while it spread among the people that he intended to go to Ḥunayn. He said: So Ḥāṭib wrote to the people of Makkah that the Messenger of God ﷺ intends to come to you. He said: So the Messenger of God ﷺ sent me and Abū Marthad... then he mentioned the hadith about the story of the letter that was with the woman at Rawḍat Khākh, which included: Ḥabīb b. Abī Thābit said: She took it out from her private parts."],[5998,"On the day of the conquest, the Prophet ﷺ ordered Bilāl to give the call to prayer on top of the Kaʿbah, while al-Ḥārith b. Hishām and Ṣafwān b. Umayyah were sitting side by side. One of them pointed at Bilāl and said: “Look at this slave.” The other said: “If God dislikes him, He will change him.”"],[5999,"When the Prophet ﷺ halted at Dhū Ṭuwā, Abū Quḥāfah said to his youngest daughter: “Take me up the mountain,” for he was blind that day. Then he mentioned the story, which included: The girl had a silver necklace on her neck, and a man passed by her and snatched it. At the end of it, Abū Bakr said: “O sister, consider that as a loss for God’s sake. By God, trustworthiness among people is indeed rare.”"],[6001,"On the day of Ḥunayn, the people fled from the Messenger of God ﷺ, and no one remained with him except one man called Zayd, holding the bridle of his gray mule. He ﷺ said: “Woe to you, O Zayd! Call the Muhājirūn, for God Almighty has taken a pledge from their necks.” Buraydah ؓ told me that he said: “A thousand of them came forward, having thrown down and broken their scabbards, then they came to the Messenger of God ﷺ until God granted them victory.”"],[6002,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from al-Ṭāʾif, he camped at al-Jiʿrānah and there divided the spoils. Then he performed ʿUmrah from there, and that was two nights before the end of Shawwāl."],[6003,"I came to al-Miqdam b. Ma'dikarib in the mosque and said: 'O Abu Yazid, the people claim that you did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'Glory be to Allah! By Allah, I saw him while I was walking with my uncle, and he took hold of this ear of mine and said to my uncle: \"Do you think this one remembers his mother or his father?\" We said to him...'"],[6004,"When we met the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, they did not stand against us even for the milking of a sheep before we routed them. While we were driving them in their tracks until we reached the rider of the white or gray mule, we encountered men with bright white faces. He said: “May the faces be ugly! Go back!” And we were defeated by their words, so they mounted upon our shoulders, and that was it."],[6005,"I heard Yazid b. Amir al-Suwa'i say, and he had been present at Hunayn with the polytheists, then embraced Islam. We asked him about the terror which Allah the Exalted cast into the hearts of the polytheists on the day of Hunayn, how it was. He said: We would take a pebble and throw it into a metal basin containing water, and it would ring. He said: We would find in our insides something like that."],[6006,"He mentioned a defeat which the Muslims suffered, and the disbelievers pursued them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a handful of earth, then turned with it toward the polytheists and threw it in their faces, saying: 'Return! May the faces be ugly!' He said: No one met his brother except that he complained of pain in his eyes."],[6007,"On the day of Hunayn, the people fled from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, except al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib and Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered al-Abbas to call out: 'O companions of Surat al-Baqarah, O assembly of the Ansar!' Then he urged the call among Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj. When they heard the call, they came. By Allah, I did not liken them except to camels yearning for their young. When they met, the battle intensified. Then he said: 'Now the oven is heated!' He ﷺ took a handful of white pebbles and threw it, and said: 'They are defeated, by the Lord of the Ka'bah!' Ali b. Abi Talib was on that day the most intense in fighting in front of him ﷺ."],[6010,"When we returned from the expedition of Tabuk, he mentioned the hadith. In it: Whoever of you meets any of those who lagged behind, let him not speak to him nor sit with him. In it also: This is Taybah, my Lord settled me in it; it expels the filth of its people as the bellows expels the filth of iron. Whoever of you meets any of those who lagged behind, let him not speak to him nor sit with him."],[6011,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. While we were traveling with him at night, his riding camel turned aside, and I followed him. When he saw me, he said: 'Where are the people?' I said: 'I left them at such-and-such a place.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made his camel kneel, then dismounted, then went away until he was hidden from me, and stayed for the time a man takes to relieve himself... he mentioned the hadith about wiping over the leather socks, and at the end he said: Then he said: 'Your need?' I said: 'I have no need.' Then we rode until we caught up with the people."],[6012,"Who will take this letter to Caesar and for him is Paradise? A man said: 'Even if he is not killed?' He ﷺ said: 'Even if he is not killed.' The man went and brought him the letter. He read it and said: 'Go to your Prophet and tell him that I am his follower, but I do not wish to give up my kingdom.' He sent with him dinars to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He returned and informed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'He has lied,' and he distributed the dinars."],[6014,"Cavalry of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out. Ukaydir of Dumat al-Jandal heard of it, so he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have heard that your cavalry has set out, and I fear for my land and property. Write me a document that nothing belonging to me will be touched, for I acknowledge what is due from me.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote for him."],[6016,"The Negus sent to the Prophet ﷺ a delegation of his companions. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the Quran to them, and they affirmed and embraced Islam. About them this verse was revealed: 'You will surely find the most intense of people in animosity toward those who believe are the Jews and those who associate others with Allah' up to His saying: 'the witnesses.' Then they returned to the Negus, and he embraced Islam. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ learned of his death, and they prayed over him as one prays over a deceased person."],[6018,"I will surely know how long the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will remain among us. He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if only you would take something to sit on that would protect you from the dust and keep the adversary away from you.' He ﷺ said: 'By Allah, I will surely leave them disputing with me over my cloak, stepping on my heels, and their dust covering me, until Allah the Exalted is the one who gives me rest from them.' He said: So I knew that his remaining among us was little. He said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, Umar said: 'By Allah, I hope that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will live until he cuts off the hands and tongues of men among the hypocrites who say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has died.' Al-Abbas said: 'O people, does anyone among you have a covenant or contract from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' They said: 'No.' He said: 'Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not die until he had cut the ropes and joined, fought and made peace, married women and divorced, and left you upon a clear path and a well-marked road. If it is as Umar says, Allah the Exalted is not incapable of uncovering him and bringing him out to us. So leave us alone with him, let us bury him, for he decomposes as people decompose.'"],[6019,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a sermon before his death, and it was the last sermon he gave in Madinah until he joined Allah the Exalted. He mentioned the hadith in full, and in it: O people, my age has grown old, my bones have become thin, my body has been worn out, my soul has been announced to me, my term has drawn near, and I long for my Lord. Indeed this is the last covenant between me and you. As long as I am alive, you see me. When I die, Allah is my successor over every Muslim. Peace be upon you and Allah's mercy and blessings."],[6020,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died of pleurisy."],[6021,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ during his illness, and he had a red band — or he said: a yellow band. He said: 'O cousin, take this band and bind my head with it.' So I bound his head with it. He said: Then he leaned on me until we entered the mosque. He said: 'O people, I am but a human like you. Perhaps my departure from among you has drawn near. Whoever I have wronged in his honor, his person, his hair, or his wealth, here is Muhammad’s honor, hair, person, and wealth; let him rise and take retribution. And let none of you say: I fear enmity and hatred from Muhammad. Indeed, they are not part of my nature nor my character.' He said: Then he left. The next day I came to him, and he said: 'O cousin, I do not think that my standing yesterday sufficed for me. Take this band and bind my head with it.' He said: So I bound his head with it. He said: Then he ﷺ leaned on me until he entered the mosque and said the same as his speech the day before. Then he ﷺ said: 'The most beloved of you to us is the one who seeks retribution.' He said: A man stood up and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, do you remember the day a beggar came to you and asked you, and you said: Who has something to lend us? And I lent you three dirhams.' He ﷺ said: 'O Fadl, give it to him.' So I gave it to him. Then he ﷺ said: 'Whoever is overcome by something, let him ask us so that we may supplicate for him.' He said: A man stood up and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I am a cowardly man who sleeps a lot.' Al-Fadl said: I later saw him as the bravest of us and the one who slept the least. He said: Then he ﷺ came to Aisha’sws house and said to the women the same as he had said to the men."],[6022,"People will console one another for me after my death. People were saying: What is this? And when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, people met one another, consoling one another for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6023,"Abu Bakr ؓ entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was dead and kissed his forehead."],[6024,"The burial of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his concealment from the people were undertaken by four: Ali, al-Abbas, al-Fadl, and Salih ؓ. A niche was dug for him, and bricks were placed over him."],[6025,"A group of Quraysh entered upon him, and he said: Shall I not tell you about Abu al-Qasim ﷺ? They said: Yes. He said: Three days before the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Allah sent down to him Gabriel ﷺ , who said: 'O Ahmad, Allah has sent me to you as an honor to you, a favor to you, and specifically for you. I ask you about what He knows better than you. He says: How do you find yourself?' He ﷺ said: 'I find myself, O Gabriel, distressed.' Then he came to him on the second day and mentioned the same thing exactly. Then he came to him on the third day and mentioned the same thing exactly, and added: 'And I find myself, O Gabriel, grieved.' He said: And with Gabriel ﷺ descended an angel in the air called Isma'il, over seventy thousand angels. Gabriel ﷺ said to him: 'O Ahmad, this is the Angel of Death seeking permission to enter upon you. He has never sought permission from any human before you, and he will never seek permission from any human after you.' He said: 'Give him permission.' So Gabriel ﷺ gave him permission. The Angel of Death said to him: 'O Ahmad, Allah, Mighty and Exalted, has sent me to you and commanded me to obey you. If you command me to take your soul, I will take it, and if you dislike it, I will leave it.' Gabriel ﷺ said: 'Allah, Exalted be He, has longed to meet you.' He ﷺ said: 'O Angel of Death, proceed with what you have been commanded.' Gabriel ﷺ said: 'O Ahmad, peace be upon you. This is my last treading of the earth. You were my only need from this world.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away and condolence came, a comer came whose sound they heard but whose person they did not see. He said: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. In Allah is consolation for every calamity, a successor for every perished one, and a compensation for everything missed. So trust in Allah and hope in Him. For the deprived is the one deprived of the reward, and the afflicted is the one deprived of the reward. And peace be upon you.' He said: Do you know who this is? This is al-Khidr ﷺ ."],[6026,"Men of Quraysh entered upon his father, Ali b. al-Husayn, and he said: Shall I not tell you about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? They said: Yes. So he narrated to us, saying: When he ﷺ fell ill, Gabriel came to him... and he mentioned the hadith in full, except that he said: he is called Isma'il, over one hundred thousand angels, each angel of them over one hundred thousand. And he said in it after 'I will leave it': He said: 'Will you indeed do it, O Angel of Death?' He said: 'Yes, with this I have been commanded, and I have been commanded to obey you.' He said: Then he ﷺ looked at Gabriel, and Gabriel said: 'O Muhammad...' and he mentioned something similar. And he said after his saying 'the reward': Ali ؓ said: Do you know who this is? This is al-Khidr ﷺ ."],[6027,"When 'When the help of Allah and the victory comes' was revealed until the end of the surah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was notified of his own death when it was revealed. So he began the most intense striving ever in the affair of the Hereafter."],[6029,"They heard a sound at the death of the Prophet ﷺ, and al-Abbas hurried, and his leg struck the back of one of the Prophet's ﷺ wives. He said: 'O my mother, O my mother, O my mother, do not blame me for this.' He caught up with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'The highest companion.' Al-Abbas said: I knew that he had been given a choice. When Allah decreed death upon His Prophet ﷺ, Ali b. Abi Talib and al-Fadl b. al-Abbas washed him. Al-Abbas was handing them water from behind the curtain. He said: 'What prevents me from washing him is only that we were boys carrying stones in the mosque.'"],[6031,"Our Prophet and beloved ﷺ announced to us his own death—may my soul be his ransom—a month before his death. When the parting drew near, he ﷺ gathered us in the house of our mother Aisha ؓ. He ﷺ looked at us, and his eyes shed tears. He pronounced the testimony of faith, then said: 'Welcome to you. May Allah keep you alive, have mercy on you, shelter you, preserve you, aid you, benefit you, guide you, grant you success, grant you peace, accept you, provide for you, and raise you. I enjoin upon you fear of Allah, and I entrust you to Allah, and I appoint Him as a guardian over you. I make you witness that I am a clear warner to you, that you should not exalt yourselves over Allah in His servants and His lands. For Allah, Exalted be He, said to me and to you: \"That is the abode of the Hereafter\"—the verse—and He, Mighty and Exalted, said: \"Is there not in Hell a dwelling for the arrogant?\"' We said: When is the appointed time? He ﷺ said: 'The appointed time has drawn near, and the return is to Allah, to the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, to the Garden of Refuge, to the fullest cup, to the highest companion, and to the most pleasant life.' We said: Who will wash you? He ﷺ said: 'Men of my household, the nearest then the nearest.' We said: In what shall we shroud you? He ﷺ said: 'In these garments of mine, or garments of Egypt, or a Yemeni suit.' We said: Who will pray over you? He said: Then he ﷺ wept and we wept. He said: 'Gently, may Allah forgive you and reward you well on behalf of your Prophet. When you have washed me and shrouded me, place me on my bier in this house of mine, at the edge of this grave of mine. Then leave me for a while. The first to pray over me will be my friend and beloved Gabriel, then Michael, then Israfil, then the Angel of Death with all his hosts of angels. Then enter upon me in groups and pray over me and give greetings of peace. Do not harm me with excessive praise, nor with a cry, nor with a wail. Let the men of my household and their women begin the prayer over me, then you after. Convey my greetings of peace to those of my companions who are absent from me. Convey my greetings of peace to those of my brothers who enter with you into my religion. I make you witness that I have sent peace upon whoever follows me in my religion from this day to the Day of Resurrection.' We said: Who will place you in your grave? He ﷺ said: 'My family with many angels, who see you from where you do not see them.'"],[6032,"Our beloved and Prophet—may my father be his ransom, and my soul be his ransom—announced to us his own death a year before his death. When the parting drew near, he mentioned the hadith, and he said at its end: 'And whoever enters with you into your religion after me, I make you witness that I send peace—I think he said—upon him and upon everyone who follows me in my religion from this day of mine to the Day of Resurrection.'"],[6034,"The people differed concerning the burial of the Prophet ﷺ. Abu Bakr ؓ said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'No prophet dies but that he is buried where he is taken.' So draw lines around the bed of the Prophet ﷺ, then bury him where he was taken."],[6035,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was placed near the pulpit, and the people began to pray over him in companies, one after another."],[6036,"I was the last of the people to be with the Prophet ﷺ. We dug for him and made a lahd. When they had buried him and came out, I dropped the axe into the grave and said, 'The axe, the axe!' So I went in and took it, and I wiped my hand over the Prophet ﷺ."],[6037,"He used to narrate to us here in Kufa, and he said: I am the last of the people to see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: When Ali b. Abi Talib came out of the grave after the Prophet ﷺ had been buried, I dropped my ring and said, 'O Abu al-Hasan, my ring!' He said, 'Go down and take your ring.' So I went down and took my ring, and I placed it on the shroud, then I came out."],[6038,"And Abu Ya'la said: Shuja' b. Makhlad narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us with this. : :"],[6041,"He mentioned the Prophet ﷺ and praised him, then he mentioned Abu Bakr ؓ and praised him, then he mentioned Umar ؓ and praised him, then he said: 'After thirty [years], turn your face wherever you wish, for you will not turn it except to weakness or wickedness.'"],[6042,"And Abu Bakr said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, and he mentioned the hadith of Hudhayfah ؓ which was mentioned earlier in the section on the Duha prayer. :"],[6043,"The millstone of Islam will turn after thirty-five years. If they make peace among themselves without fighting, they will enjoy the world for seventy years."],[6044,"Take the gift as long as it is a gift, but when it becomes a bribe for religion, do not take it. You will not leave it; fear and poverty will prevent you from that. Indeed, the millstone of faith is turning, so turn with the Book wherever it turns. Indeed, the ruler and the Book will separate; do not abandon the Book. Indeed, there will be rulers over you: if you obey them, they will lead you astray, and if you disobey them, they will kill you. They said, 'What should we do, O Messenger of Allah?' He ﷺ said, 'As the companions of Jesus son of Mary (peace and blessings be upon him) did: they were carried on wood and sawn with saws. Death in obedience to Allah, Mighty and Exalted, is better than life in disobedience to Him.'"],[6045,"You are in a time of prophethood and mercy. Then there will be a caliphate and mercy. Then there will be such and such, and then a biting kingship. They will drink wine and wear silk, and despite that they will be given victory until the Hour is established."],[6046,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night, and we headed towards the garden of Banu So-and-so. I brought him water for purification, and when he came I placed it for him. He ﷺ began to raise his gaze at me and lower it. He said: 'Woe to you after me.' I wept and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will I remain after you?' He ﷺ said: 'Yes. When you see buildings on Mount Sal', then join the Arabs of the land of Quda'ah. For there will come a day [when corruption is] a bow's length or two, or a spear's length or two.'"],[6047,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, we find you standing before your Lord with your cheeks red, ashamed before your Lord because of what your community has introduced after you."],[6049,"Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari ؓ went out to Madinah when Uthman was killed, while I was feverish. So I mounted and caught up with him at al-Salihin, and he was in a garden. I entered the garden and found a group sitting at the far end of it. He had performed ablution and water was flowing on his beard. He said: I met him and praised Allah Almighty and extolled Him, then I said to him: You had two companions to whom people turned for refuge: Hudhayfah and Abu Musa. I adjure you by Allah Almighty and by Islam: if you heard anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about this trial, tell it to me; otherwise, exercise your own judgment. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: 'Keep to the main body of the community of Muhammad ﷺ, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not gather the community of Muhammad ﷺ upon misguidance. Be patient until a righteous person finds rest or relief is found from a wicked person.'"],[6050,"When Ali ؓ was killed, I met Abu Mas'ud ؓ in the house of a landowner at al-Salihin and said to him, 'Tell me what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and do not conceal it from me.' He said, 'We do not conceal anything, young man. You must keep to the community, and beware of division, for it is tribulation and error. Verily Allah, Exalted is He, would not gather the community of Muhammad ﷺ upon error.'"],[6051,"After me there will be trials like patches of dark night, striking a man as the foreheads of raging bulls strike. A man will enter upon morning as a Muslim and reach evening as a disbeliever, and reach evening as a believer and enter upon morning as a disbeliever. A man said, 'What should we do at that time, O Messenger of Allah?' He ﷺ said, 'Enter your houses and keep your mention hidden.' A man said, 'What do you think if one of us has his house entered upon him?' He said, 'Let him restrain his hand and be the servant of Allah who is killed, not the servant of Allah who kills, for a man may be within the dome of Islam yet consume his brother's wealth, shed his blood, disobey his Lord, disbelieve in his Creator, and Hell becomes incumbent upon him.'"],[6052,"And Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad b. Bakkar narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid b. Bahram narrated to us with it. : :"],[6053,"The days and nights will not pass until a claimant stands and says, 'Who will sell us his religion for a handful of dirhams?'"],[6054,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out after the sun had risen, while people were near the rooms, and said ﷺ, 'O people of the rooms, the Fire has been kindled and trials have come like patches of dark night. If you knew what I know, you would weep much and laugh little.'"],[6056,"Take the gift as long as it is a gift, but when it becomes a bribe for religion, do not take it. You will not leave it; fear and poverty will prevent you from that. Indeed, the millstone of faith is turning, so turn with the Book wherever it turns. Indeed, the ruler and the Book will separate; do not abandon the Book. Indeed, there will be rulers over you: if you obey them, they will lead you astray, and if you disobey them, they will kill you. They said, 'What should we do, O Messenger of Allah?' He ﷺ said, 'As the companions of Jesus son of Mary (peace and blessings be upon him) did: they were carried on wood and sawn with saws. Death in obedience to Allah, Mighty and Exalted, is better than life in disobedience to Him.'"],[6058,"After me there will be leaders: if you obey them, they will declare you disbelievers, and if you disobey them, they will kill you—leaders of disbelief and heads of misguidance."],[6059,"Everything has a defect that corrupts it, and the defect of this religion is evil rulers."],[6060,"'Ubada came as a pilgrim from Syria. He arrived in Madinah and went to 'Uthman b. 'Affan ؓ and said: 'Shall I not tell you something I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There will be rulers over you who command you to do what you recognize and they themselves do what you disapprove of. Those have no right to obedience.\"'"],[6061,"There will be rulers whose commands are not refused; they will tumble into the Fire, one after another."],[6062,"Mu'awiya ؓ addressed us one Friday and said, 'The wealth is our wealth and the spoils are our spoils; we give to whom we will and withhold from whom we will,' and no one replied to him. The following Friday he said the same and no one replied. On the third Friday he said the same, and a man from those present stood up to him and said, 'No! Rather the wealth is our wealth and the spoils are our spoils; whoever comes between us and them, we will take him to judgment with our swords.' After praying, he ordered the man brought in and seated him with him on the couch, then permitted the people and they entered. He said, 'O people, I spoke on the first Friday and no one replied, and on the second and no one replied. On the third, this man revived me—may Allah revive him. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: People will come who speak and are not contradicted; they will plunge into the Fire as monkeys plunge. I feared that Allah would make me one of them. When this man replied to me, he revived me—may Allah revive him—and I hope Allah will not make me one of them.'"],[6064,"By the hundredth year, Allah will send a cold, pleasant wind in which He will take the soul of every believer."],[6065,"Al-Rūyānī said: Al-Ḥasan b. Ibrāhīm narrated to us, ʿUbaydallāh b. Mūsā narrated to us, Bashīr informed us with it. Its chain is ḥasan."],[6067,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A time will come upon the people when the best wealth will be sheep between the two mosques that eat the trees and come to the water. Their owner eats from their milk, drinks from their milk, and wears from their wool—or he said 'their hair'—while the trials will be collapsing among the roots of the Arabs. By Allah, they will not care.\" He said it three times."],[6068,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while addressing the people at Tabūk: \"There is no one among the people like a man who takes hold of his horse's head, striving in the path of Allah Almighty, and avoids the evils of the people; or like a man in the desert enjoying blessings, who honors his guest and gives him his due.\""],[6070,"I set out with Zurʿah b. Ḍamrah and al-Ashʿarī to ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb. I met ʿAbdallāh b. ʿAmr, who said: \"Soon none of the Arabs will remain in the land of the non-Arabs except one killed or a captive whose blood is judged.\" Zurʿah said to him: \"Will the polytheists prevail over the people of Islam?\" He said: \"Who are you from?\" He said: \"From Banū ʿĀmir b. Ṣaʿṣaʿah.\" He said: \"The Hour will not come until the shoulders of the women of Banū ʿĀmir b. Ṣaʿṣaʿah press together around Dhū al-Khalaṣah—an idol that was one of the idols of the pre-Islamic era.\" He said: \"We mentioned the statement of ʿAbdallāh b. ʿAmr to ʿUmar, and he said: 'ʿAbdallāh knows best what he says'—three times. Then ʿUmar gave a sermon on Friday and said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A group of my community will continue to be upon the truth, supported, until the command of Allah comes.\"'\" He said: \"We mentioned the statement of ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb to ʿAbdallāh b. ʿAmr, and ʿAbdallāh b. ʿAmr said: 'The Prophet of Allah ﷺ spoke the truth. When the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, comes, it will be as you said.'\""],[6073,"\"A group of my community will continue to be upon the truth until the Hour comes.\""],[6076,"I went out with Muslim b. ʿUqbah. When we came parallel to a valley in which Muḥammad b. Maslamah was, he sent me to him. I said: \"What do you think if he does not come to you?\" He said: \"Then bring me his head.\" So I came to him and said: \"Answer the amir.\" He said: \"Who is the amir?\" I said: \"Muslim b. ʿUqbah.\" He said: \"What does the amir want to do with me when I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with this hand of mine, and I have not broken it or changed it?\" So I unsheathed my sword and said: \"I will bring him your head.\" He said: \"Then bring it.\" I said: \"What drives you to that?\" He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entrusted me, saying: 'When you see the people pledging allegiance to two amirs, take your sword with which you fought alongside me and strike with it a mountain until it breaks. Then sit in your house until a sinful hand or a decisive death comes to you.'\""],[6077,"\"Would any of you be unable, when a man comes to kill him—meaning from the people of the qiblah—to be like this?\" He placed one of his hands on the other, \"and thus be like the better of the two sons of Adam. Then he will be in Paradise, and his killer will be in the Fire.\""],[6079,"The Prophet ﷺ hid a smoke for Ibn Ṣayyād and asked him what he had hidden for him. He said: \"Dukhkh (smoke).\" He said: \"Be off! You will never exceed your measure.\" When he turned away, the Prophet ﷺ said: \"What did he say?\" Some of them said: \"Dukhkh,\" and some said: \"Dīkh.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You have differed while I am still among you, and after me you will differ even more.\""],[6080,"\"Indeed, what I fear most for you is a man who recites the Qur'an until you see its radiance upon him, and he was a support for Islam, but then he strips away from it, casts it behind his back, attacks his neighbor with the sword, and accuses him of polytheism.\" I said: \"O Prophet of Allah, which of the two is more deserving of being accused of polytheism—the accuser or the accused?\" He ﷺ said: \"Rather the accuser.\""],[6082,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling weapons during trial."],[6084,"Two men disputed before Abu al-Darda' ؓ over a span of land. Abu al-Darda' said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'If you are in a land and you hear two men disputing over a span of land, leave it.' He said: So Abu al-Darda' left and went to Syria."],[6086,"The best of you at the beginning of the two hundredth [year] is the light of burden, the one with few possessions. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is 'light of burden'? He said: 'One who has no family and no wealth.'"],[6087,"A time will come upon the people when celibacy will be permissible, and no one's religion will be safe for a person of religion except one who flees with his religion from one mountain peak to another, and from one burrow to another, like a bird fleeing with its chicks, and like a fox with its cubs. Then he establishes prayer and gives zakat and withdraws from people except for good. A hundred reddish sheep that I pasture at Sal' would be more beloved to me than the kingdom of Banu al-Nadir, and that will be when it is such and such."],[6089,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has placed in this nation five trials: a specific trial, then a general trial, then a specific trial, then a general trial, then a black, dark trial will come, in which people will become like animals. Abu Usamah confirmed it and said: 'Yes.'"],[6090,"On the night whose morning the group whom Umar ibn al-Khattab ؓ had appointed as successors would finish the matter of the caliphate, I prayed Isha and then went to my home and slept. My maternal uncle Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, may Allah have mercy on him, woke me from sleep, saying: 'O Miswar.' He said: I came out wrapped in my garment. He said: 'Did you sleep?' I said: 'Yes, I slept.' He said: 'Take your garment and join me at the mosque.' I did so. When I reached him, he said to me: 'Call for me al-Zubayr and Sa'd, or one of them.' I went and called him. When I brought him to him, he said: 'Stay back from us enough that you do not hear our conversation.' He said: I did so, and they conversed privately a little. Then he said: 'Call for me the other one.' When I brought him to him, he said: 'Stay back from us enough that you do not hear our conversation.' He said: They conversed privately a little. Then he called: 'O Miswar, go and call Ali for me,' and that was when the darkness of Isha had passed. He said: I brought Ali, and he said: 'Stay back from us enough that you do not hear our conversation.' He said: They continued talking from Isha until it was the time of sahur, except that I did not hear from their mouths what I thought they had turned to. When it was sahur, he called me while Ali ؓ was with him, and said: 'Go and call Uthman ؓ for me.' He said: I did so. They conversed privately, and the mu'adhdhin called the adhan for Fajr. He said: They dispersed for ablution, and the people knew that it was the morning of the caliphate, so they gathered for Fajr as they gather for Friday prayer. Abd al-Rahman ؓ ordered the group to sit before the minbar. When the people saw one another and the sun rose, Abd al-Rahman ؓ stood by the minbar, praised Allah Almighty and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: 'O people, you know of the death of the Commander of the Faithful and his appointing us, the group, and my companions agreed that the matter be referred to me, so I choose a man from among them, and these are before you.' Then he faced them one by one and said: 'O so-and-so, upon you is the covenant and pledge of Allah: will you listen and obey the one I appoint, and be content and surrender?' He would say: 'Yes,' raising his voice so the people could hear, until he finished with them one by one: Uthman, Ali, al-Zubayr, and Sa'd ؓ. He said: 'As for Talha, I am a guarantor for his consent.' Then he said: 'I have not ceased toiling for three days asking you about these people, then I asked them about themselves, and I found you, O people, and them united upon Uthman ؓ. Rise, O Uthman.' No man among the Muhajirun, the Ansar, the Arab delegations, or the righteous people said: 'You did not consult us or seek our command.' They were content and surrendered, and they remained six years without criticizing anything. He said: A group of them used to prefer him over Umar ؓ, saying: 'Justice like Umar, and gentleness softer than Umar,' then what happened happened."],[6091,"Whenever he called one of them that night, he would mention their virtues, then say: 'You are indeed worthy of it. If it misses you, then who?' He would say: 'If it misses me, then Uthman ؓ.'"],[6092,"The Prophet ﷺ looked toward Iraq and said: 'O Allah, turn their hearts [to Islam].'"],[6093,"Umar ibn al-Khattab consulted al-Hurmuzan about Isfahan, Persia, and Azerbaijan: which of them should he begin with? He said: 'O Commander of the Faithful, Isfahan is the head, and Persia and Azerbaijan are the two wings. If you cut one wing, the head will resort to the other wing. If you cut the head, the two wings will fall. So begin with Isfahan.' He said: Umar ؓ entered the mosque and found al-Nu'man ibn Muqarrin praying. He waited until he finished his prayer, then said: 'I am appointing you as a governor.' He said: 'As a tax collector, no, but as a warrior.' He said: 'Then you are a warrior.' He said: So he dispatched him and wrote to the people of Kufa to join him, among them al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, Abdullah ibn Amr, al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, and Amr ibn Ma'di Karib ؓ. He said: Al-Nu'man ؓ came to them, and between him and them was a river. He sent al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah to them. Their king was Dhu al-Janahayn. He consulted his companions and said: 'What do you think? Should I sit for them in the posture of war, or should I sit for them in the posture of kingship and its splendor?' They said: 'No, rather sit for them in the posture of kingship and its splendor.'"],[6094,"Khalid ibn al-Walid ؓ wrote to Mihran and Rustam and the lands of Persia: From Khalid ibn al-Walid to Mihran and Rustam: Peace be upon those who follow guidance. To proceed: I offer you Islam. If you accept Islam, you will have what Muslims have and owe what Muslims owe. If you refuse, I offer you the jizyah. If you refuse, then I have men who love fighting as the Persians love wine."],[6095,"Abu Bakr ؓ wrote to Khalid ؓ — meaning on the day of al-Yamamah and the killing of the apostates — to march to al-Hirah then proceed to Syria. When he camped at al-Hirah, he wrote to the people of Persia, then said: 'I would love not to leave until I frighten them.' So he raided them until he reached Sura, killing and taking captives. Then he raided Ayn al-Tamr, killing and taking captives. Then he proceeded to Syria. Amir, meaning al-Sha'bi, said: Ibn Buqaylah — meaning Abd al-Masih al-Himyari — brought out to me the letter of Khalid ibn al-Walid ؓ to them: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Khalid ibn al-Walid to the marzbans of Persia: Peace be upon those who follow guidance. To proceed: I praise Allah, besides whom there is no deity, with the praise He deserves, who has cut off your sacred precincts, dispersed your unity, weakened your might, and stripped away your kingdom. When this letter of mine reaches you, accept from me the covenant of protection, pay the jizyah, and send hostages to me. Otherwise, by Him besides whom there is no deity, I will fight you with a people who love death as you love life. Peace be upon those who follow guidance."],[6097,"A casket was brought to Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ. Most of his companions examined it but did not recognize its value. He said, 'Do you permit me to send it to Aisha ؓ, because of the love the Messenger of God ﷺ had for her?' They said, 'Yes.' It was brought to Aisha ؓ and she opened it. It was said, 'This is what Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ sent to you.' She said ؓ, 'What has Ibn al-Khattab opened for me after the Messenger of God ﷺ? O God, do not keep me alive for next year's gift.'"],[6098,"An army of the Muslims went out with me as their commander until we encamped at Alexandria. A great man among their great ones said, 'Bring out to me a man whom I may speak with and who may speak with me.' I said, 'None shall go out to him except me.' So I went out with an interpreter, and he had his interpreter, until two pulpits were set up for us. He said, 'What are you?' We said, 'We are Arabs, people of thorns and acacia, and we are the people of the House of God, Mighty and Majestic. We were the narrowest of people in land and the worst in livelihood. We ate carrion and blood, and raided one another. We lived the worst life people ever lived, until a man emerged among us who was not the greatest of us that day in nobility, nor the wealthiest. He said, \"I am the Messenger of God to you.\" He commanded us what we did not know and forbade us what we and our fathers had been upon. We reviled him, disbelieved him, and rejected his statement, until a people other than us went out to him and said, \"We believe you, we have faith in you, we follow you, and we will fight whoever fights you.\" He went out to them and we went out against him. He fought us and we fought him. He killed us, prevailed over us, and overcame us. Then he turned to the Arabs near him and fought them until he prevailed over them. If those behind me of the Arabs knew what you are in of life, not one would remain except he would come to you and share with you in what you have of life.' He laughed, then said, 'Your messenger has spoken the truth. Our messengers came to us with the like of what your Messenger brought, and we were upon it, until kings appeared among us. They acted among us according to their whims and abandoned the command of the prophets. If you take up the command of your Prophet, no one will fight you except you will overcome him, and no one will oppose you except you will prevail over him. But if you do like what we did, abandon the command of your Prophet, and act like they did according to their whims, then we and you will be left alone; you will not be more numerous than us, nor stronger than us.' Amr b. al-As ؓ said, 'I have never spoken to a man more cunning than him.'"],[6099,"When the people of Alexandria repelled Amr b. al-As ؓ, he set up a mangonel against it."],[6100,"O Uthman, break your fast with us tonight. My father said: Al-Hasan narrated to me that Muhammad b. Abi Bakr ؓ entered upon him and took hold of his beard. He [Uthman] said ؓ, 'You have seized me with a grip, or sat with me in a seat, that your father would never have sat in' – or he said, 'taken' – then he left and abandoned him. Then a man called 'Black Death' entered upon him ؓ and strangled him, then strangled him again, then left and said, 'By God, I strangled him and I have never seen anything softer than his throat, until I saw his breath reverberating in his body like the breath of a jinn.' He said: Then he left and abandoned him. He said: In the hadith of Abu Sa'id ؓ: A man entered upon him and said, 'Between me and you is the Book of God,' then he left and abandoned him. Then another entered and said, 'Between me and you is the Book of God, Exalted is He,' while the mushaf was in front of him. He struck with a sword, and Uthman ؓ shielded himself with his hand, and it cut it. I do not know whether he severed it fully or cut it without severing. Uthman ؓ said, 'By God, it is the first hand that wrote down the Mufassal.' He said: And in other than the hadith of Abu Sa'id ؓ: Then al-Tujibi entered upon him and struck him with a barbed arrow, and the blood spurted onto this verse: 'God will suffice you against them, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.' He said: Indeed it is in the mushaf and has not been erased since. He said: And the daughter of al-Furafisa ؓ took her jewelry in the hadith of Abu Sa'id ؓ and placed it in her lap, and that was before he was killed ؓ. When he was struck – or killed – she spread her legs over him. Some of them said, 'May God fight her, how large her buttocks are!' Abu Sa'id ؓ said, 'Then I knew that the enemies of God wanted nothing but this world.' I say: Its narrators are trustworthy, hearing from one another."],[6101,"Abdullah b. Salam ؓ, before the people of Egypt came, used to enter upon the leaders of Quraysh and say to them, 'Do not kill this man,' meaning Uthman ؓ. They would say, 'By God, we do not intend to kill him.' Then he would leave, leaning on my arm, saying, 'By God, they will surely kill him.' Then he said to them, 'Do not kill him, for by God he will die within forty days.' But they refused. Then he went out to them after some days and said, 'Do not kill him, for by God he will die within fifteen nights.'"],[6102,"The angels have not ceased surrounding this city of yours since the Messenger of God ﷺ came to it until today. By God, if you kill him, they will depart and never return to you. And the sword has not ceased to be sheathed among you. By God, if you kill him, God will unsheathe it upon you, and it will never be sheathed from you again – or he said, 'until the Day of Resurrection.' No prophet has been killed except that seventy thousand were killed for him, and no caliph has been killed except that thirty-five thousand were killed for him. And he mentioned that seventy thousand were killed for the blood of Yahya b. Zakariyya."],[6103,"Abdullah b. Salam ؓ used to come on a she-donkey from a piece of land of his on Friday."],[6104,"Abdullah b. Salam ؓ used to come from a piece of land of his on a she-donkey or a donkey on Friday, arriving early. When he finished the prayer, he would go to his land. When the people stirred up against Uthman ؓ, Abdullah b. Salam ؓ said to them, 'Do not kill him; seek his repentance. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no nation has killed its prophet and then God set their affairs right until they shed the blood of seventy thousand, and no nation has killed a caliph and then God set their affairs right until they shed the blood of forty thousand. No nation has ever perished except after they raised the Quran against the ruler.' Then he said to them, 'Do not kill him; seek his repentance.' He said: But they did not consider what he said and killed him. He said: Then he sat on the road of Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ until Ali ؓ came to him. He said to him, 'Where do you intend to go?' He said, 'Iraq.' He said, 'Do not go to Iraq. Keep to the pulpit of the Messenger of God ﷺ and adhere to it. I do not know whether it will save you. By God, if you leave it, you will never see it again.' Those around him said, 'Let us kill him.' Ali ؓ said, 'Abdullah b. Salam is a righteous man among us.' Ibn Mughaffal said: I had asked Ibn Salam for permission regarding a piece of land next to his land to buy it. He said to me afterwards, 'This is the beginning of forty years, and after it there will be peace, so buy it.'"],[6105,"My father was the fourth of four who buried Uthman ؓ on the day of the house, after the last evening prayer, in al-Baqi'."],[6106,"When Uthman ؓ was besieged, he remained fasting that day. When it was time to break the fast, he asked them for fresh water. They said, 'You have this well,' and behold, it was a well into which filth was thrown. So he spent that night in his state without eating. When it was near dawn, I came to a neighbor woman of ours over connected rooftops and asked them for fresh water. I brought him a jug of water. When I descended, he ؓ was sleeping at the bottom of the stair, snoring. I woke him and said, 'This is fresh water I have brought you.' He ؓ raised his head, looked at the dawn, and said, 'I am fasting; I have entered the morning fasting.' I said, 'From what? I have not seen anyone bring you food or drink.' He said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ looked down upon me from this roof with a bucket of water and said, \"Drink, O Uthman.\" I drank and was quenched. Then he said, \"Drink more.\" I drank until I was full. Then he ﷺ said, \"The people will disapprove of you. If you leave them, you will break your fast with us.\"' She said: Then they entered upon him that very day and killed him ؓ."],[6107,"Uthman ؓ looked down upon us on the day of the house and said, 'O people, do not kill me, for if you kill me, you will be like this,' and he interlaced his fingers ؓ."],[6108,"Uthman ؓ sought permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he permitted him. He entered with his waist-wrap loosened. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Come close to me, O Uthman.' He came close to him. Then he said, 'Come closer to me, O Uthman.' He came closer until his knee ؓ touched the knee of the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ buttoned his waist-wrap with his own hand. Then he ﷺ said, 'O Uthman, you will come on the Day of Resurrection with your jugular veins gushing blood. I will say, \"Who did this to you?\" You will name and complain, between one who commanded, one who plotted, and one who abandoned. While you are in that state, you will hear a caller crying out from heaven: \"Indeed Uthman ؓ, in the judgment of his enemies, is a friend [of God]. So how will you be, O Uthman, at that moment?\" He ؓ said, \"There is no might and no power except with God,\" three times."],[6109,"Ibn ʿUmar ؓ wore armor on the day of the house, the house of ʿUthmān ؓ, twice. He entered upon him and said: 'I accompanied the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I knew his right of prophethood and right of authority. I accompanied Abū Bakr ؓ, and I knew his right of authority. Then I accompanied ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ, and I knew his right of authority and his right as a father. And I know the same for you.' He ؓ replied: 'May God reward you well, O family of ʿUmar. Stay in your house until my affair comes to you.'"],[6110,"I was besieged in the house with ʿUthmān ؓ. They shot a man from among us and killed him. I said: 'O Commander of the Faithful, striking is now permissible—they have killed one of our men.' He ؓ said: 'I adjure you, O Abū Hurayrah, to cast aside your sword, for it is only myself they seek, and I will shield the Muslims with my own life.' Abū Hurayrah ؓ said: 'So I cast aside my sword, and I do not know where it is even to this hour.'"],[6111,"ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān ؓ sent for ʿAbdullāh b. Salām ؓ while he was besieged. He entered upon him and said to him: 'Raise your head and look at this opening, for the Messenger of God ﷺ looked down from it tonight.' He said: 'O ʿUthmān, have they besieged you?' I said: 'Yes.' He lowered a bucket for me and I drank from it, and indeed I feel its coolness on my liver. Then he ﷺ said: 'If you wish, I will call upon God Almighty and He will grant you victory over them, and if you wish, you may break your fast with us.' ʿAbdullāh ؓ said: 'I asked him: What did you choose?' He said: 'To break fast with him ﷺ.' ʿAbdullāh ؓ returned to his home, and when the day had fully risen, he said to his son: 'Go out and see what has happened to ʿUthmān ؓ, for it is not fitting that he be alive at this hour.' He returned to him and said: 'The man has been killed.'"],[6112,"ʿUthmān ؓ slept on that day on which he was killed—it was Friday. When he awoke, he said: 'Were it not that people would say, \"ʿUthmān ؓ wished for a wish,\" I would tell you something.' He said: We said—"],[6115,"ʿUthmān ؓ began the day speaking to the people. He said: 'I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ in a dream, and he said: \"O ʿUthmān, break your fast with us.\"' He ؓ began that day fasting, and he was killed on that very day ؓ."],[6117,"Al-Bazzār narrated it from Ibrāhīm b. Ziyād, from Isḥāq b. Sulaymān with it. 4385/3 – and al-Ḥākim also related it from the path of Isḥāq b. Sulaymān and deemed it sound:"],[6118,"I was in Kufa when al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī ؓ stood up as a preacher and said: 'O people, last night I saw in my dream a wonder! I saw the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, above His Throne. The Messenger of God ﷺ came and stood at one of the legs of the Throne. Abū Bakr ؓ came and placed his hand on the shoulder of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then ʿUmar ؓ came and placed his hand on the shoulder of Abū Bakr ؓ. Then ʿUthmān ؓ came and was a short distance away. He said: \"O Lord, ask Your servants why they killed me.\" He said: Then two spouts of blood gushed from the sky onto the earth. He said: It was said to ʿAlī ؓ: \"Do you not see what al-Ḥasan ؓ is relating?\" He said—may the pleasure of God Almighty be upon him—: \"He relates what he saw.\""],[6119,"Al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī ؓ said: 'I will not fight after a dream I saw. I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ placing his hand on the Throne, and I saw Abū Bakr ؓ placing his hand on the Prophet ﷺ, and I saw ʿUmar ؓ placing his hand on Abū Bakr ؓ, and I saw ʿUthmān ؓ placing his hand on ʿUmar ؓ, and I saw blood between them. I said: \"What is this blood?\" It was said: \"The blood of ʿUthmān ؓ, for which he is seeking God Almighty.\"'"],[6120,"O God, forgive my father his sin regarding ʿUthmān ؓ."],[6121,"A man from Quraysh called Thumāmah was over Ṣanʿāʾ. When ʿUthmān ؓ was killed, he delivered a sermon and wept intensely. When he recovered, he said: 'Today the caliphate of prophethood has been wrested from the community of Muḥammad ﷺ and has become kingship and compulsion. Whoever seizes something consumes it.'"],[6122,"I saw those who spoke against ʿUthmān ؓ and quarreled in the mosque until I could not see the surface of the sky. A person from the chambers of the Prophet ﷺ pointed with a muṣḥaf and said: 'Do you not know that Muḥammad ﷺ is innocent of those who split their religion and became sects: \"Indeed, those who have divided their religion and become sects—you are not associated with them in anything...\" the verse.'"],[6123,"Abdullah b. al-Zubayr said: I said to Uthman ؓ, \"With you in the house is a group ready to help—Allah, Exalted is He, grants victory with fewer than them—so give me permission to fight.\" He ؓ said, \"I adjure by Allah any man who would shed his blood for me\"—or he said, \"who would shed blood on my account.\""],[6124,"He witnessed the killing of Uthman and said: I was then a boy of fourteen. He said: Safiyyah ordered us to saddle a mule with a howdah, so we saddled it, then walked around it to the gate. There was al-Ashtar with some people. Al-Ashtar said to her, \"Go back to your house,\" but she refused. He raised a short spear or a lance and struck the mule's rump, so the mule steadied while the howdah tilted until it almost fell. When she saw that, she said, \"Take me back, take me back!\" He said: Four men of Quraysh had come out of the house, wounded and being carried; they had been defending Uthman. He mentioned al-Hasan b. Ali, Abdullah b. al-Zubayr, Ibn Khatib, and Marwan b. al-Hakam. I said: Did Muhammad b. Abi Bakr get stained with any of his blood? He said: God forbid! He entered upon him, and Uthman said to him, \"I am not your man,\" and spoke to him some words, then he left without having touched any of his blood. I said: Then who killed him? He said: A man from Egypt called Jabalah. He kept saying, \"I am the killer of Na'thal.\" I said: Where was Uthman then? He said: In the house."],[6125,"The Umayyads are fighting me, claiming that I killed Uthman ؓ, but they lie. They only want kingship. If I knew that swearing to them at the Maqam would remove what is in their hearts—\"By Allah, I did not kill Uthman ؓ, nor did I order his killing\"—I would do it. But they only want kingship. I hope that I and Uthman ؓ are among those about whom Allah, Exalted is He, said: \"And We shall remove whatever rancor is in their breasts...\" [Quran 7:43]."],[6126,"\"Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\" And he ﷺ left me while seeing my place; had he entrusted me with anything, I would have carried it out, until one of his wives ﷺ objected, saying, \"Abu Bakr ؓ is a tender-hearted man; if he stands in your place, the people will not hear him. If only you would order Umar ؓ to lead the people in prayer.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You are like the women of Joseph.\" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, the Muslims looked into their affair, and indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had entrusted Abu Bakr ؓ with the matter of their religion, so they entrusted him with the matter of their worldly affairs. The Muslims pledged allegiance to him, and I pledged allegiance with them. I would go on expeditions when he sent me, take when he gave me, and I was a whip before him ؓ in establishing the prescribed punishments. Had there been any favoritism at the time of his death ؓ, he would have put it in his own son, but he pointed to Umar ؓ, and he did not fail. The Muslims pledged allegiance to him, and I pledged allegiance with them. I would go on expeditions when he sent me, take when he gave me, and I was a whip before him ؓ in establishing the prescribed punishments. Had there been any favoritism at the time of his death ؓ, he would have put it in his own son. But he disliked choosing one man from the tribe of Quraysh and appointing him over the community's affair, for then any evil after him would attach to Umar ؓ in his grave. So he chose six from among us, I being one of them, to select a man for the community. When we gathered, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ jumped up and gave up his share in it on condition that we give him pledges that he would choose one of the five and appoint him over the community's affair. We gave him our pledges, and he took Uthman ؓ by the hand and gave him allegiance. Something came into my mind at that, but when I considered my affair, I found that my covenant had preceded my pledge, so I pledged and submitted. I would go on expeditions when he sent me, take when he gave me, and I was a whip before him ؓ in establishing the prescribed punishments. When Uthman ؓ was killed, I looked into my affair, and the pledge that had been on my neck for Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ was released, and the covenant to Uthman ؓ I had fulfilled. I am a man of the Muslims; no one has a claim or a demand against me. Then one who is not like me jumped into it—meaning Muawiyah ؓ—whose kinship is not my kinship, whose knowledge is not like my knowledge, and whose precedence is not like my precedence. I was more entitled to it than him. The two said: You have spoken truth. Tell us about your fighting these two men—meaning Talhah and al-Zubayr ؓ—your companions in the Hijrah, your companions in the Pledge of Ridwan, and your companions in the consultative council. He ؓ said: They pledged allegiance to me in Madinah and opposed me in Basrah. If a man who pledged allegiance to Abu Bakr ؓ had deposed him, we would have fought him; and if a man who pledged allegiance to Umar ؓ had deposed him, we would have fought him."],[6127,"Muhammad b. Ubayd al-Tanafisi reported to us, from Salim al-Muradi, from al-Hasan ؓ, the same exactly. I say: Abu Dawud and al-Nasa'i narrated a part of it from the hadith of al-Hasan, from Qays b. Abbad."],[6128,"\"Do you know how Allah, Mighty and Majestic, judges those who rebel among this ummah?\" He said: We said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"Its wounded are not finished off, its captives are not killed, and its fugitives are not pursued.\""],[6129,"He said to Ibn Umm Abd: \"Do you know...\" to the end, and he added: \"and their spoils are not distributed. This is Allah's judgment for those who rebel among this ummah, and they, in our view, are the Khawarij.\""],[6130,"I heard Ali ؓ say on the pulpit, when a man came to him and said: \"O Commander of the Faithful, why do I see you turning people away as a man turns away his camels? Is it by a covenant from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or something you have seen?\" He ؓ said: \"By Allah, I have not lied, nor been lied to, nor gone astray, nor been led astray. Rather, it is a covenant from the Prophet ﷺ, and he who fabricates has failed.\""],[6131,"The Prophet ﷺ covenanted with me that I should fight the oath-breakers, the deviators, and the apostates."],[6132,"I was commanded to kill the oath-breakers, the deviators, and the apostates."],[6133,"\"Which of you is the owner of the adorned camel, around whom many will be killed, and she will escape after almost perishing?\""],[6134,"We set out as pilgrims and arrived in Madinah. While we were in our lodgings, putting down our saddles, a messenger came and said: \"The people are alarmed and have gathered in the mosque.\" We went to the mosque—and he mentioned the hadith about Uthman ؓ adjuring the Companions and their acknowledgment ؓ of his virtues. Al-Ahnaf b. Qays said: I met Talhah and al-Zubayr ؓ and said: \"I think this man will be killed. Whom do you command me to pledge allegiance to?\" They said: \"Ali ؓ.\" I said: \"Do you command me to do that and approve it for me?\" They said: \"Yes.\" I left and went to Makkah. While I was there, it was announced that Uthman b. Affan ؓ had been killed, and Aishah, Mother of the Believers ؓ, was in Makkah. I went to her and said: \"I adjure you by Allah, whom do you command me to pledge allegiance to?\" She ؓ said: \"Ali.\" I said: \"Do you command me to do that and approve it for me?\" She said: \"Yes.\" He said: I returned and went to Ali ؓ in Madinah and pledged allegiance to him. Then I returned to my people in Basrah, thinking that the matter had become settled. While we were thus, a messenger came and said: \"Aishah, Mother of the Believers, Talhah, and al-Zubayr ؓ have encamped near al-Khuraybah.\" I said: \"What brought them?\" They said: \"They sent to you seeking support for the blood of Uthman ؓ, who was killed unjustly.\" The most dreadful thing ever came to me. I said: \"Abandoning a people with whom are the Mother of the Believers and the disciple of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is hard, and fighting a man, the cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, whom they commanded me to pledge allegiance to, is hard.\" When I came to them, I said: \"What brought you?\" They said: \"We have come seeking support for the blood of Uthman ؓ, who was killed unjustly.\" I said: \"O Mother of the Believers, I adjure you by Allah! Did I say to you: 'Whom do you command me?' and you said: 'Ali,' and I said: 'Do you command me to pledge allegiance to him and approve it for me?' and you said: 'Yes'?\" She said: \"Yes.\" I said to al-Zubayr ؓ: \"O disciple of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and O Talhah, I adjure you both by Allah! Did I say to you both: 'Whom do you command me to pledge allegiance to?' and you said: 'Ali,' and I said: 'Do you command me to pledge allegiance to him and approve it for me?' and you said: 'Yes'?\" They said: \"Yes.\" I said: \"By Allah, I will not fight you while the Mother of the Believers and the disciple of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ are with you. By Allah, I will not fight the cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man you commanded me to pledge allegiance to. Choose from me one of three options: either open the gate of the bridge for me so I can join such-and-such land—meaning the land of the Persians—until Allah decides His matter as He wills; or I join Makkah; or I withdraw and be near you, not with you nor against you.\" They said: \"We will consult and then send to you.\" He said: They consulted and said: \"As for opening the gate of the bridge for him so he joins the land of the Persians, the deserters and abandoners will join him. As for joining Makkah, he will amaze you among Quraysh and tell them your news; that is not good for you. But make him near here, where you trample on his ear.\" So he withdrew to al-Jalha, two farsakhs from Basrah, and about six thousand people withdrew with him. Then the people met in battle, and the first to be killed was Talhah b. Ubayd Allah ؓ. He said: Ka'b b. Sur was reading the Mushaf and reminding these and those until Ka'b was killed, and whoever was killed among them was killed. Al-Zubayr ؓ reached Safwan from Basrah, at the place of al-Qadisiyyah from you. He said: Al-Na'ir, a man of Banu Mujashi', met him and said: \"Where are you going, O disciple of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Come to me, you are under my protection; no one will reach you.\" So he went with him. He said: A person came to al-Ahnaf b. Qays ؓ and said: \"There is al-Zubayr; he has reached Safwan.\" He said: \"What is he safe from? He gathered the Muslims until they struck each other's brows with swords, then joined his sons and family.\" He said: Uwaymir b. Jurmuz, Fadalah b. Habis, and Nufay' heard him, so they rode in pursuit and met him with al-Na'ir."],[6135,"I came to Madinah while I was performing Hajj... He mentioned the hadith similar to what has preceded. He said: Some foolish people among the people heard him, among them Ibn Jurmuz, Fadalah, and Nufay'. They set out seeking him, and they met him coming with the cattle. 'Umayr b. Jurmuz came at him from behind and stabbed him with a weak stab, while he was on a weak horse of his. Al-Zubayr ؓ charged at him on a horse of his called Dhu al-Khimar. When Ibn Jurmuz thought that al-Zubayr ؓ would kill him, he called out to Fadalah and Nufay', and they charged at al-Zubayr ؓ and killed him."],[6136,"Indeed 'Atikah, the wife of 'Umar, said: Ibn Jurmuz betrayed a stalwart horseman on the day of the encounter, and he was not one to flee. O 'Amr, had you alerted him, you would have found him, not one unsteady with trembling hands, nor one to lose his grip. May your right hand be paralyzed if you killed a believer; upon you has fallen the punishment of the deliberate killer."],[6137,"When the Day of the Camel came and they lined up, 'Ali ؓ called al-Zubayr ؓ, and he came to him. He said: I adjure you by Allah the Exalted, do you not remember that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You will indeed fight him while you are an oppressor to him'? He ؓ said: O Allah, yes; I did not remember it before this standing of mine. So he turned back. When his companion saw him, he followed him—meaning Talhah ؓ—and Marwan shot him with an arrow, and it pierced his thigh to the iron of the saddle."],[6139,"'Ali was alone with al-Zubayr ؓ on the Day of the Camel and said: I adjure you by Allah the Exalted, how did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say while you were twisting my hand in the portico of Banu so-and-so: 'You will indeed fight him while you are an oppressor to him, then he will be given victory over you'? He said: I heard it; no doubt, I will not fight you."],[6140,"Sulayman b. Surad said to al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ: Excuse me before the Commander of the Faithful. Al-Hasan said: I saw him on the Day of the Camel taking refuge with me and saying: 'I wish I had died before this by such and such years.'"],[6141,"I came to al-Hasan ؓ and said: Excuse me before the Commander of the Faithful for not being present at the battle. Al-Hasan ؓ said: What need do you have of this? I saw him taking refuge with me and saying: 'O Hasan, would that I had died twenty years before this.'"],[6142,"His mother and his maternal aunt entered upon 'A'ishah ؓ ... He mentioned the hadith. They said: Tell us about 'Ali ؓ. She said: What thing do you ask me about a man who placed his hand on a spot of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and his soul flowed into his hand, and he wiped his face with it? They said: Then why did you go out against him? She ؓ said: A matter decreed; I wish I could ransom him with all that is on the earth."],[6143,"It was said to him: What prevented you from fighting with your supporters on the Day of the Camel? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A people will come out who are doomed and will not succeed; their leader is a woman, and their leader will be in Paradise."],[6144,"'Abd al-Jabbar alone narrated it. Others said: From 'Ata', from Bilal b. Buqtur from Abu Bakrah ؓ. :, :"],[6145,"Someone who saw al-Zubayr ؓ striking down the horses told me—meaning on the Day of the Camel—and 'Ali ؓ called out to him: O Abu 'Abd Allah! He came forward until the necks of their mounts met. 'Ali ؓ said to him: I adjure you by Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, do you remember a day when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us while I was conversing privately with you, and he said: 'Are you conversing privately with him? By Allah, he will indeed fight you while he is an oppressor to you'? He said: Al-Zubayr ؓ struck the face of his mount and turned away."],[6146,"I witnessed 'Ali and al-Zubayr ؓ when they faced each other. 'Ali ؓ said to him: 'O Zubayr, I adjure you, did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: You will fight 'Ali while you are an oppressor?' He ؓ said: Yes, and I did not remember that except in this standing of mine. Then he ؓ turned away."],[6148,"Indeed, 'Ammar b. Yasir ؓ was a strong, capable man. He used to carry two stones at a time. The Prophet ﷺ heard of this, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met him and pushed him in the chest. He stood up brushing the dust from his head, and he said: 'Woe to you, O Ibn Sumayyah! The transgressing party will kill you.'"],[6149,"And al-Harith said: Al-'Abbas b. al-Fadl narrated to us: 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us with this. :, : :"],[6150,"And Abu Ya'la said: Ja'far b. Mihran narrated to us: 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, then he mentioned it in a hadith. :"],[6151,"The transgressing party will kill you."],[6152,"Indeed, the fitnah (tribulation) has occurred, so tell me what you heard the Prophet ﷺ say. He ؓ said: I heard him ﷺ say to Ibn Sumayyah ؓ: 'Woe to Ibn Sumayyah! The transgressing party will kill him.'"],[6153,"The transgressing party will kill 'Ammar ؓ."],[6154,"Two men came to 'Amr b. al-'As ؓ disputing over the blood of 'Ammar and his spoils. 'Amr ؓ said: 'Leave him alone and let him be, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Quraysh became obsessed with 'Ammar. The killer of 'Ammar and the one who takes his spoils ؓ will be in the Fire.'"],[6155,"I was walking with Mu'awiyah ؓ on his return from Siffin, between him and 'Amr b. al-'As ؓ, when 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr ؓ said: 'O my father! Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Woe to you, O Ibn Sumayyah! The transgressing party will kill you?'"],[6156,"I was sitting with Mu'awiyah ؓ when two men entered disputing over the head of 'Ammar ؓ, each of them saying: 'I killed him.' 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr ؓ said: 'Let one of you be content to give it to his companion, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The transgressing party will kill him.' Mu'awiyah ؓ said: 'Will you not spare us your madman, O 'Amr? What is the matter with him being with us?' He said: 'I am with you, but I do not fight. My father complained about me, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: Obey your father as long as he lives, and do not disobey him. So I am with you, but I do not fight.'"],[6157,"Indeed, I did not thrust with a spear, strike with a sword, or shoot an arrow. He said: It was said to him: Why? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'Obey your father,' so I obeyed him."],[6158,"I charged at 'Ammar b. Yasir ؓ on the day of Siffin, pushed him, and threw him off his horse. A man from the people of Sham got to him before me, so he severed his head. We disputed before Mu'awiyah ؓ over the head and placed it before him, each of us claiming to have killed him and each seeking the reward for his head. 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr b. al-'As ؓ was with him. 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr b. al-'As ؓ said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to 'Ammar ؓ: The transgressing party will kill you. Give glad tidings to the killer of 'Ammar of the Fire.' So I let go of it from my hand and said: 'I did not kill him.' My companion also let go of it and said: 'I did not kill him.' When Mu'awiyah ؓ saw that, he turned to 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr ؓ and said: 'What made you say this?' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say something, so I wanted to say it.'"],[6159,"When the day of Siffin ended and they turned back, 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr ؓ said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The transgressing party will kill 'Ammar.' 'Amr said to Mu'awiyah ؓ: 'Did you not hear what your nephew says?' He said: 'I seek refuge in Allah for you from doubt. Are you in doubt? Did we kill him? Only the one who brought him killed him.'"],[6160,"I returned with Muawiya ؓ from Siffin. Muawiya and Abu al-A'war al-Sulami were riding on one side, and Amr and his son were riding on another side, and I was between them, no one else but me. Sometimes I urged my mount toward these, and sometimes toward those. I heard Abdullah b. Amr ؓ say to his father: 'O my father, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to Ammar ؓ when he was building the mosque: \"You are surely keen for reward\"?' He said: 'Yes, by Allah ؓ.' And he ﷺ said: 'You are from the people of Paradise, and the transgressing party will kill you.' He said: 'Yes, I heard it.' He said: 'Then why did you kill him?' He said: 'He turned to Muawiya ؓ and said: \"O Abu Abd al-Rahman, do you not hear what this one is saying?\" He said: 'He mentioned it.' He said: 'Woe to you, you keep slipping in your speech. Did we kill him? Only those who brought him killed him.'"],[6161,"On the day of Siffin, when the heat became intense, Ammar ؓ said: 'Bring me a drink to drink.' Then he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The last drink you will drink in this world is a drink of milk.\" Then he advanced and was killed."],[6162,"And Abu Ya'la said: Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, something similar. : :"],[6163,"Ammar b. Yasir ؓ was attached to Quraysh and they were attached to him. They came upon him and beat him. Uthman ؓ came out angry, ascended the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: 'O people, what is between me and Quraysh? May Allah do such and such to Quraysh. They came upon a man and beat him. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to Ammar ؓ: \"The transgressing party will kill you.\""],[6164,"On the day of Siffin, Ammar ؓ fought but was not killed. He would come to Ali ؓ and say: 'O Commander of the Faithful, is this not the day of such and such?' He would say: 'Go away from me.' He said that several times. Then he ؓ was brought milk and drank it. Ammar ؓ said: 'This is the last drink I will drink in this world.' Then he advanced and fought until he was killed ؓ."],[6165,"Muawiya came to visit Ammar b. Yasir ؓ when he was ill. When he left him, he said: 'O Allah, do not make his death by our hands, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The transgressing party will kill Ammar.\""],[6166,"Umm Abdullah bt. Munabbih b. al-Hajjaj used to be kind to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He came to her one day and said: 'How are you, O Umm Abdullah?' She said: 'Fine. How are you, may my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Fine.' He ﷺ said: 'How is Abdullah?' She said: 'Fine.' Abdullah was a man who had renounced the world. His father said to him on the day of Siffin: 'Go out and fight.' He said: 'O my father, how can you order me to fight when you know what was in the covenant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the last thing in the covenant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was that he took your hand and placed it in mine and said: \"Obey Amr b. al-As\"?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I order you to fight.' So he went out and fought. When the battle began, Amr ؓ started reciting: 'The war blazed, and I prepared for it a horse with a high withers, well-watered in the back, connecting charge with charge, and when the horses leapt from the charge, they stirred. A sturdy one, whose chest cavity was broad, and when it leapt from the water, it splashed.' And Amr ؓ also said: 'If Jamal had witnessed my stand and my presence at Siffin, a day when its forelocks turned gray, the evening the people of Iraq came like spring clouds raised by the winds, and we came to them in ranks, as if our swords were a tide from the sea with waves piling up. When I said they had fled swiftly, battalions of them appeared to us, and battalions swayed. Our mill turned and their mill turned through the height of the day, until the shoulders turned away. They said to us: We think you should pledge allegiance to Ali. We said: Rather we think we should strike.'"],[6167,"I was standing at Siffin next to al-Ahnaf ؓ, and al-Ahnaf was next to Ammar ؓ. I heard Ammar ؓ say: 'My close friend ﷺ made a covenant with me that the last of my provisions from this world would be a drink of milk mixed with water.' He said: 'While we were like that, dust rose and they said: \"The people of Syria have come.\" The water carriers stood up to give water to the people. A slave girl came to him with a bowl of milk and handed it to Ammar ؓ. He drank it. Then Ammar ؓ handed the remainder to al-Ahnaf b. Qays ؓ. Then al-Ahnaf handed it to me. I said: 'If your companion is truthful, then it is fitting that he be killed now.' He said: 'The people surrounded us. Ammar ؓ advanced, and I heard him say: \"Paradise is under the spears today. I meet the beloved ones, Muhammad and his party.\" Then that was the last we saw of him ؓ."],[6168,"A group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ gathered, among them Ibn Mas'ud, Hudhayfa, Sa'd, Ibn Umar, and Ammar ؓ. Hudhayfa ؓ mentioned a tribulation and said: 'As for me, if I live to see it, I will know the way out of it.' Ibn Mas'ud ؓ said: 'And I, if I live to see it, will know the way out of it.' Sa'd ؓ said: 'As for me, if I live to see it and find a sword that says: \"This is a believer, leave him; this is a disbeliever, kill him,\" then I will fight; otherwise I will not fight.' Ibn Umar ؓ said: 'And I am with you.' Ammar ؓ said: 'As for me, if I live to see it, I will take my sword, place it on my shoulder, then head toward its greatest mass and strike until they disperse.'"],[6169,"A poet on the night of Siffin was reciting satire against Muawiya and Amr b. al-As, and Ammar b. Yasir ؓ was saying: 'Stick with the two wicked ones.' A man said: 'This, while you are the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ?' Ammar ؓ said: 'If you wish to sit, then sit; and if you wish to go, then go.'"],[6170,"This nation is a nation to whom mercy is shown; there is no punishment upon it except what it inflicts upon itself. She said: I said: 'How does it punish itself?' He said: 'Was not the Day of the Camel a punishment? Was not the Day of Siffin a punishment? Was not the Day of Nahrawan a punishment?'"],[6173,"If you see so-and-so delivering a sermon on my pulpit, kill him."],[6175,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ attended the day of Hunayn while distributing the spoils...... the hadith. Regarding the man's saying: \"This is a division by which the face of God is not intended.\" He said: I was present after that with Ali ؓ when he killed them at al-Nahrawan, and Ali ؓ sought—meaning al-Mukhdaj—he said: He did not find him. Then he found him after that beneath a wall, with this description. Ali ؓ said: Which of you knows this man? A man from the people said: We know him. This is Hurqus, and his mother is here. He said: Ali ؓ sent for his mother and said to her: From whom is this? She said: I do not know, O Commander of the Faithful, except that in the pre-Islamic era I was shepherding sheep of mine at al-Rabadhah, and something like darkness came over me, and I conceived from it, and gave birth to this."],[6176,"I was with my master, meaning Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, when he killed the people of al-Nahrawan, and it was as if the people had found something in themselves about his killing them. Ali ؓ said: O people, the Prophet ﷺ told me that people will go out of the religion as an arrow goes out of the game, then they will never return to it. Indeed, the sign of that is that among them is a black man with a deformed hand, one of his hands like a woman's breast, with a nipple like a woman's nipple. He said: I think he said: Around it are seven coarse hairs. So search for him, for I do not think he is other than one of them. They found him on the bank of the river, beneath the slain. He said: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. Ali ؓ was carrying an Arab bow of his, poking with it at his exit. He said: The people rejoiced when they saw him, and they were glad, and what they had been feeling left them."],[6177,"I was with my master Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, and he mentioned it. <hidden text linked=26053741 text=\"I was with my master Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ when he killed the people of al-Nahrawan, and the people had found something in themselves about his killing them. Ali ؓ said: O people, the Prophet ﷺ...\""],[6178,"I witnessed the day when the people of al-Nahrawan were killed...... and he mentioned the hadith, and in it: If a person's soul could leave from joy, the soul of Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ would have left that day. He said: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. Who..."],[6179,"The gatherings of the people were the mosques until they returned from Siffin and dissociated themselves from the arbitration. Then the people took to sitting in the streets, seeking news. While we were sitting with Ali ؓ, a man stood up and said: Permit me to speak. He was occupied with what he was doing. We said to him: What did you want to ask the Commander of the Faithful about? He said: I was in the Umrah and entered upon Aisha ؓ. She said: Who are these people who went out before you, called Harura'? She said: Did you witness their destruction? Indeed, Ali b. Abi Talib, if he wished, would tell you their story. When Ali ؓ finished what he was doing, he said: Where is the man? He related to him, and Ali ؓ proclaimed the talbiyah and said Allahu Akbar. Then he said: I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ when no one was with him but Aisha ؓ. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: How will you be, O son of Abi Talib, with a people of such-and-such? I said: God and His Messenger know best. He ﷺ said: A people who will come out from the direction of the east, reciting the Quran, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will go out of the religion as an arrow goes out of the game. Among them is a man with a deformed hand, as if his hand is the breast of an Abyssinian woman. He ؓ said: I adjure you by God, I told you that he is among them, and you said he is not among them. Then you brought him to me, dragging him? They said: O God, yes. He ؓ proclaimed the talbiyah and said Allahu Akbar."],[6180,"I was sitting with Ali ؓ while he was busy with some matter of the people, when a man came wearing travel clothes and said: O Commander of the Faithful. Ali ؓ was occupied with what he was doing in the matter of the people. My father said: I said to him: What is your affair? He said: I was on Hajj—or Umrah—and I passed by Aisha ؓ. She said to me and asked me about these people who went out among you, called al-Haruriyyah. I said: They went out at a place called Harura', so they were named al-Haruriyyah after that. She ؓ said: Blessed is the one who witnessed their destruction. She said: By God, if the son of Abi Talib wished, he would inform you of their affair. So that is why I came to ask him about that. He said: Ali ؓ finished and said: Where is the questioner? He stood up to him and related to him, and Ali ؓ proclaimed the talbiyah and said Allahu Akbar two or three times. Then he mentioned the like of it. At the end he said: You dragged him as I described to you. He said: Then he ؓ said: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth, three times."],[6182,"And from Abu Hisham, from Ibn Fudayl, something similar."],[6183,"Al-Bazzar narrated something similar."],[6184,"I came to Abu Wa'il while he was in the mosque of his tribe. We withdrew to a corner of the mosque. I said: Will you not tell me about these people whom Ali ؓ killed—why did they separate from him, and why did they respond to him when he called them, and when they separated from him, he deemed it lawful to fight them? He said: When we were at Siffin, the killing became intense among the people of Sham...... Then he mentioned a story. He said: Ali ؓ returned to Kufa, and the Khawarij said about him what they said, and they camped at Harura', and they were some ten thousand. Ali ؓ sent to them, adjuring them by God Almighty: Return to your caliph. What do you hold against him? Is it in division or judgment? They said: We fear entering into a trial. He said: Do not hasten to the error of this year for fear of the trial of next year. So they returned and said: Let him be over our region. If he accepts the arbitration, we will fight him as we fought the people of Sham at Siffin, and if he breaks it, we will fight with him. So they marched until they crossed Nahrawan. A group of them split off and began killing people. Their companions said: It was not for this that we separated from Ali. When their action reached Ali ؓ, he stood and said: Will you march against your enemy or return to those who have stayed behind in your homes? They said: Rather, we return to them. He said: Ali ؓ narrated that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: A group will come out from the direction of the east at a time of discord among the people. They will not consider your jihad with their jihad as anything, nor your prayer with their prayer as anything, nor your fasting with their fasting as anything. They will go out of the religion as an arrow goes out of the game. Their sign is a man whose upper arm is like a woman's breast. The closest of the two parties to the truth will kill them. Ali ؓ marched against them and fought them a severe fight. Ali's cavalry began to stand up to them, so he said: O people, if you are fighting them only for my sake, then by God, I have nothing to tell you. But if you are fighting for God Almighty, then let not this be your fighting. So they advanced upon them and killed them all. Then he said: Search for him. They searched but did not find him. Ali ؓ mounted his beast and came to a hollow in the ground, and there were dead bodies piled upon each other. He was extracted from beneath them, and he dragged him by his leg while the people watched. Ali ؓ said: I will not raid this year. He returned to Kufa and was killed. The people appointed al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ as caliph. Al-Hasan sent the pledge of allegiance to Muawiyah ؓ, and al-Hasan wrote about that to Qays b. Sa'd ؓ. Qays b. Sa'd stood among his companions and said: O people, two matters have come to you, and you must choose one of them: entering into a trial, or fighting without an imam. The people said: What is this? He said: Al-Hasan b. Ali has given the pledge of allegiance to Muawiyah. So the people returned and pledged allegiance to Muawiyah ؓ. Muawiyah had no concern except for those at al-Nahrawan. They began to come to him and pledge allegiance, until there remained of them three hundred and some, and they were the companions of al-Nukhaylah."],[6186,"Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us with it. The original marfu' report is in Sahih Muslim and elsewhere, and I only cited this because it contains additions over the routes that the authors of the books and Ahmad also transmitted."],[6187,"Ali ؓ refrained from fighting the people of al-Nahr until they initiated [hostilities]. They departed and came upon Abdullah b. Khabbab while he was in a village of his, having withdrawn from the fitnah. They seized him. He said: They saw a date that had fallen from the top of a palm tree, and a man among them took it and put it in his mouth. They said: 'A date from the dates of the people of the covenant, you took it without paying its price.' He said: So he spat it out. He said: Then they came upon a pig, and one of them stabbed it with his sword and killed it. They said: 'A pig belonging to the people of the covenant, you killed it.' Abdullah b. Khabbab ؓ said to them: 'Shall I not inform you—or tell you—of someone who has a greater right over you than this date and this pig?' They said: 'Who?' He said: 'I.' (I think he said): 'I have not abandoned any prayer since I reached maturity, nor the fasting of Ramadan,' and he enumerated several things. So they brought him forward and killed him. That reached Ali ؓ, and he ordered his companions to march against them. He said: 'Let them give us retribution for Abdullah b. Khabbab.' They said: 'How can we give you retribution for him when all of us killed him?' He said: 'Allah is greater.' And he said to his companions: 'Attack them, for by Allah, not ten of you will be killed and not ten of them will flee.' And so it happened. Ali ؓ said: 'Search for a man whose description is such and such.' They searched but did not find him. Then they searched again and found him. Ali ؓ said: 'Who knows this man?' No one recognized him. Then a man said: 'I saw this one at al-Najaf.' He said: 'I intend to go to this city, and there is no one there with lineage or acquaintance.' Ali ؓ said: 'You have spoken the truth; he is a man from the jinn.'"],[6188,"There was among us a young man of great worship, asceticism, and exertion. He said: We named him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but he did not recognize him. We described him by his description, but he did not recognize him. While we were thus, he approached. We said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'It is this one.' He ﷺ said: 'Indeed, I see on his face a dark mark from Satan.' He came and greeted. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Have you said within yourself that there is no one among the people better than you?' He said: 'O Allah, yes.' Then he turned away and entered the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Who will kill the man?' Abu Bakr ؓ said: 'I will.' He entered and found him standing in prayer. He said: 'Should I kill a man who is praying, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has forbidden us from striking those who pray?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Who will kill the man?' Umar ؓ said: 'I will, O Messenger of Allah.' He entered the mosque and found him prostrating. He said the same as Abu Bakr ؓ, and added: 'I will certainly return, for one better than me has already returned.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Enough, O Umar.' He mentioned it to him, and he ﷺ said: 'Who will kill the man?' Ali ؓ said: 'I will.' He ﷺ said: 'You will kill him if you find him.' He entered the mosque and found that he had already left. He ﷺ said: 'By Allah, if you had killed him, he would have been the first of them and the last of them, and no two of my Ummah would have differed.'"],[6189,"I came to al-Miqdam b. Ma'dikarib in the mosque and said: 'O Abu Yazid, the people claim that you did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'Glory be to Allah! By Allah, I saw him while I was walking with my uncle, and he took hold of this ear of mine and said to my uncle: \"Do you think this one remembers his mother or his father?\" We said to him...'"],[6190,"'Amr b. al-Dahhak b. Makhlad narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Musa narrated to us, with it. [And] Musa is weak."],[6191,"Muhammad b. al-Faraj Abu Ja'far narrated to us in Baghdad, Muhammad b. al-Zibriqan narrated to us, Musa b. Ubaydah narrated to me with it."],[6192,"There was a man at the time of the Prophet ﷺ who would go on military expeditions with us. When he returned and dismounted from his riding camel, he would head to the mosque and pray in it, prolonging the prayer, until some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ thought that he had virtue over them. One day he passed by while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting among his Companions. One of his Companions said to him ﷺ: 'That is him.' So he either sent for him or he came on his own. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him approaching, he said: 'By the One in Whose hand is my soul, indeed between his eyes there is a dark mark from Satan.' When he stood before the gathering, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Did you say within yourself when you stood: There is no one among the people better than me?' He said: 'Yes.' Then he left and went to a corner of the mosque, drew a line with his foot, then aligned his heels and stood to pray."],[6193,"We do not know it being narrated from Anas except through this route. I say: And I have learned that it has another route besides this."],[6194,"Abdullah b. Salam ؓ came to me while I had put my foot in the stirrup. He said to me: 'Where do you intend to go?' I said: 'Iraq.' He said: 'Indeed, if you go there, the sting of the sword will surely strike you there.' Ali ؓ said: 'By Allah, I had heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before him saying it.' I heard my father say: 'I was amazed at him, and I said: A warrior narrates about himself something like this.'"],[6197,"We do not know anyone who narrated it except Abdul Malik from Abu Harb, and from him only Ibn Uyaynah. Ibn Hibban and al-Hakim authenticated it."],[6198,"‘Ali ؓ fell ill with an illness that made us fear for him. Then he recovered and became well. We said: “Praise be to God who has restored you to health, O Commander of the Faithful. We had feared for you because of this illness of yours.” He said ؓ: “But I did not fear for myself.”"],[6199,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “Who was the most wretched of the ancients?” I said: “The one who hamstrung the she-camel.” He said: “You have spoken the truth. Then who is the most wretched of the latter ones?” I said: “I have no knowledge.” He said ﷺ: “The one who will strike you on this,” and he pointed to the crown of his head. And he used to say: “I wish that the most wretched of you would arise and dye this from this.”"],[6200,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ in my sleep, and I complained to him of what I had encountered from his community in the way of denial and harm. I wept, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not weep, O ‘Ali.” He turned, and I turned, and there were two men ascending, and there were boulders crushing their heads until they were split open, then they would return to how they were."],[6201,"‘Ali ؓ said: “My beloved ﷺ met me” — meaning in a dream — “the Prophet of God ﷺ.” He said: “I complained to him of what I had encountered from the people of Iraq after him, and he promised me relief from them. He ؓ did not remain except three days.”"],[6202,"When ‘Ali ؓ was killed, al-Hasan b. ‘Ali ؓ stood as a speaker. He praised God Almighty and extolled Him, then said: “To proceed: By God, you have killed a man on a night in which the Qur’an was sent down, in which Jesus son of Mary was raised up, and in which Joshua b. Nun, the servant of Moses, peace be upon them, was killed.”"],[6203,"And in it, the Children of Israel were forgiven. He added: “And no one who came before him surpassed him, and no one who came after him will catch up with him. If the Prophet ﷺ sent him in a military expedition, Gabriel ﷺ was on his right and Michael ﷺ was on his left. By God, he ؓ did not leave behind any gold or silver except eight hundred or seven hundred dirhams, which he had set aside for a servant he intended to buy.”"],[6204,"We do not know anyone who narrated this except al-Hasan, and no one related it from Ja‘far except Sukayn."],[6205,"I went out with my father to Yanbu‘ to visit ‘Ali ؓ, who was ill there. My father said to him: “What keeps you in this place? If you were to die here, none would take charge of you except the Bedouins of Juhaynah. Let yourself be carried to Madinah, for if your appointed time comes, your companions will attend to you and pray over you” — and Abu Fadalah ؓ was one of the people of Badr. ‘Ali ؓ said to him: “I will not die from this illness of mine. The Messenger of God ﷺ promised me that I would not die until I am appointed as commander, and then this” — meaning his beard — “will be dyed from the blood of this” — meaning the top of his head. Abu Fadalah ؓ was killed at Siffin."],[6206,"I witnessed ‘Ali ؓ when he stopped at Karbala’. He went and stood in one place, gestured with his hand, and said: “The place where their mounts kneel is in front of him, and the place where their saddles are is to his left.” He ؓ struck the ground with his hand, took a handful of earth and smelled it, and said: “Alas! How beloved are the bloods that will be shed in it.” Then al-Husayn ؓ came and stopped at Karbala’. Al-Dabbi said: “I was among the cavalry that Ibn Ziyad sent against al-Husayn ؓ. When I arrived, it was as if I saw the spot where ‘Ali ؓ had stood and gestured with his hand. I turned my horse around, then went to al-Husayn b. ‘Ali ؓ, greeted him, and said to him: ‘Your father ؓ was the most knowledgeable of people. I witnessed him at such and such a time say such and such. By God, you will surely be killed this very hour.’ He said: ‘What do you intend to do? Will you join us or join your family?’ I said: ‘By God, I have a debt, and I have a family, and I think I will only join my family.’ He said: ‘Then take from this wealth what you need’ — and there was wealth placed before him — ‘before it becomes forbidden to you. Then escape, for by God, no one will hear the caller, and no one will see the lightning flash, and no one will cause us hardship, but he will be cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ.’ I said: ‘By God, today I will not combine two things: taking your wealth and forsaking you.’ He turned and left him.”"],[6207,"I saw the head of al-Husayn b. ‘Ali ؓ being brought to ‘Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad, and I saw the head of ‘Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad being brought to al-Mukhtar b. Abi ‘Ubayd, and I saw the head of al-Mukhtar b. Abi ‘Ubayd being brought to Mus‘ab b. al-Zubayr, and I saw the head of Mus‘ab b. al-Zubayr being brought to ‘Abd al-Malik b. Marwan."],[6208,"When Mu‘awiyah ؓ wanted to appoint Yazid as his successor, he sent to the governor of Madinah saying: “Send to me whoever wishes.” He said: ‘Amr b. Hazm al-Ansari came to him seeking permission. The chamberlain of Mu‘awiyah ؓ came asking permission, and said: “Here is ‘Amr, he has come seeking permission.” He said: “What has brought them to me?” He said: “O Commander of the Faithful, he seeks your favor.” Mu‘awiyah ؓ said: “If he is truthful, let him write to me, and I will give him what he asks without seeing him.” The chamberlain went out to him and said: “What is your need? Write whatever you wish.” He said: “Glory be to God! I come to the door of the Commander of the Faithful and I am veiled from him? I would love to meet him and speak to him.” Mu‘awiyah ؓ said to the chamberlain: “Promise him such and such a day; when he has prayed the morning prayer, let him come.” When Mu‘awiyah ؓ had prayed the morning prayer, he ordered his bed to be placed in the hall, then the people were excluded from him. There was no one with him except a chair placed for ‘Amr. ‘Amr ؓ came and asked permission, and he was granted permission. He greeted him, then sat on the chair. Mu‘awiyah ؓ said to him: “Your need?” He said: He praised God Almighty and extolled Him, then said: “By my life, Yazid b. Mu‘awiyah ؓ has become central in lineage among Quraysh, rich in wealth, rich except in every good. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘God Almighty does not entrust a servant with a flock but that He will question him about it on the Day of Resurrection: what did he do?’ I remind you of God, O Mu‘awiyah, regarding the community of Muhammad ﷺ, whom you will appoint over it.” He said: Mu‘awiyah ؓ was seized with shortness of breath in a cold morning until he sweated, and he kept wiping the sweat from his face for a long time. Then he recovered, praised God Almighty and extolled Him, then said: “To proceed: You are a sincere man. You have spoken according to your opinion, as far as it goes. There remains none but my son and their sons, and my son is more entitled than their sons. Your need?” He said: “I have no need.” He said: “Rise.” His brother said to him: “We came from Madinah, striking its livers for the sake of some words.” He said: “You came only for the words.” So he ordered their gifts, and he ordered for ‘Amr double their amount.”"],[6209,"Al-Hakam b. Abi al-‘As asked permission to enter upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he recognized his voice. He said: “Give him permission. May God curse him and all who come from his loins except their believers — and how few they are. They will be extravagant in this world, and debased in the Hereafter. They are possessors of cunning and deception. They will be given in this world, and they will have no share in the Hereafter.”"],[6210,"I was between al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ, and Marwan was reviling al-Husayn, while al-Hasan was restraining al-Husayn ؓ. Then Marwan became angry and said: 'A cursed household!' Al-Hasan ؓ became angry and said: 'Did you say: A cursed household? By Allah, Allah cursed you while you were in the loins of your father.'"],[6211,"A man called Abu Humayd brought the Prophet ﷺ a vessel containing milk from al-Naqi' during the day. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Why did you not cover it, even by placing a stick across it?'"],[6212,"One day I was with al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ, and Marwan reviled them with a foul revilement, until he said: 'By Allah, you are indeed a cursed household.' Al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ, or one of them, said: 'By Allah, by Allah, then by Allah, Allah (Mighty and Majestic) cursed you upon the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ while you were in the loins of al-Hakam.' Marwan fell silent."],[6213,"I came to al-Miqdam b. Ma'dikarib in the mosque and said: 'O Abu Yazid, the people claim that you did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'Glory be to Allah! By Allah, I saw him while I was walking with my uncle, and he took hold of this ear of mine and said to my uncle: \"Do you think this one remembers his mother or his father?\" We said to him...'"],[6214,"Marwan was governor over us for years, and he used to revile 'Ali ؓ every Friday on the pulpit. Then Marwan was dismissed and Sa'id b. al-'As was appointed for years, and he did not revile him. Then Sa'id was dismissed and Marwan was reinstated, and he reviled him. It was said to al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ: 'Do you not hear what Marwan says? Will you not reply with anything?' He used to come on Friday and enter the room of the Prophet ﷺ and remain in it. When the sermon was finished, he would go out to the mosque and pray in it, then return to his family. Marwan was not satisfied with that, until he sent someone to him in his house. While we were sitting with him, it was said to him: 'So-and-so is at the door.' He gave him permission, and he entered and said: 'I have come to you from the ruler, and I have come to you with a firm command.' He said: 'Speak.' He said: 'Marwan sent regarding 'Ali and regarding 'Ali and regarding you and regarding you, and I found no likeness for you except the likeness of a mule. It is said to it: Who is your father? It says: My mother is a horse.' He said: 'Return to him and tell him: By Allah, I will not erase anything of what you said by reviling you, but my appointed time and your appointed time is with Allah. If you are truthful, Allah will reward you for your truthfulness, and if you are lying, then Allah is severer in retribution. Allah (Exalted is He) has honored my grandfather too much for my likeness to be the likeness of a mule.' Then he went out and met al-Husayn ؓ in the room, who asked him. He said: 'I was sent with a message, and I have delivered it.' He said: 'By Allah, you will inform me of it, or I will order that you be beaten until it is not known when the beating will finish with you.' When al-Hasan ؓ saw him, he said: 'Release him.' He said: 'I cannot.' He said: 'Why?' He said: 'I have sworn an oath.' He said: 'Marwan sent regarding 'Ali and regarding 'Ali and regarding you and regarding you, and I found no likeness for you except the likeness of a mule. It is said to it: Who is your father? It says: My mother is a horse.' Al-Husayn ؓ said: 'May you eat the clitoris of your mother if you do not convey from me what I say to him. Tell him: Regarding you, and regarding your father, and regarding your people, and the sign between me and you is that you will grasp your shoulders from the curse of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[6215,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed al-Hakam and whoever comes out of his loins."],[6216,"I heard Ibn al-Zubayr ؓ while he was leaning against the Ka'bah, and he was saying: 'By the Lord of this Ka'bah.'"],[6217,"For everything there is a blight, and the blight of this religion is Banu Umayyah."],[6218,"When Yazid b. Abi Sufyan was governor in Syria, the Muslims raided and were safe and gained booty. Among their booty was a precious slave-girl, and she fell to a man among the Muslims. Yazid sent to him and seized her from him. Abu Dharr ؓ was in Syria that day, so the man sought help from Abu Dharr ؓ against Yazid. He went with him and said to Yazid: 'Return his slave-girl to him.' He hesitated three times. Abu Dharr ؓ said: 'By Allah, if you do it, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The first to change my Sunnah will be a man from Banu Umayyah.' Then he turned away from him. Yazid caught up with him and said: 'I remind you of Allah (Exalted is He): is it I?' He said: 'O Allah, no.' And he returned the slave-girl to the man."],[6219,"Abu Dharr ؓ was in Syria during the time of Yazid b. Abi Sufyan. The Muslims raided and gained booty and obtained a precious slave-girl, and she fell to a man among the Muslims as his share."],[6220,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw in a dream as if Banu al-Hakam were leaping on his pulpit. He woke up as if enraged and said: 'Why did I see Banu al-Hakam leaping on my pulpit like monkeys leap?' He was not seen laughing after that until he died."],[6221,"When Banu Abi al-As reach thirty, the religion of Allah will be corrupted, the wealth of Allah will be traded, and the servants of Allah will be enslaved."],[6222,"The Prophet ﷺ used the toothstick while fasting."],[6223,"This matter will remain established upon justice, until a man from Banu Umayyah breaches it."],[6224,"He will be called Yazid."],[6225,"The Hour will not rise until thirty liars emerge, among them Musaylimah, al-Ansi, and al-Mukhtar; and the worst of the Arab tribes are Banu Umayyah, Banu Hanifah, and Thaqif."],[6226,"In Thaqif there is a destroyer."],[6227,"A tyrant from the tyrants of Banu Umayyah will certainly bleed from the nose on this pulpit of mine. He said: A person who saw Amr b. Sa'id b. al-As informed me that he bled from the nose on the Prophet's ﷺ pulpit until blood flowed onto the steps of the pulpit."],[6228,"He said to Abu al-A'war al-Sulami: Woe to you! Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not curse Ri'l, Dhakwan, and Amr b. Sufyan?"],[6229,"Everything has a coming and a going; indeed this religion has a coming and a going. Among the coming of this religion is what Allah sent me with, such that a tribe would gain understanding from its last members, until none remain except one or two sinners, and they are overpowered, suppressed, and humiliated. If they speak or utter, they are suppressed, overpowered, and oppressed. Then he mentioned among the going of this religion: that a whole tribe will become harsh from its last members, until none remain in it except one or two jurists, and they are overpowered, suppressed, and humiliated. If they speak or utter, they are suppressed, overpowered, and oppressed, and it is said to them: Do you transgress against us? So much so that wine will be drunk in their gathering places—the evil—and their assemblies and markets, and wine will be renamed without its name, until the last of this ummah curses its first, unless the curse befalls them, and they say: There is no harm in this drink; a man among them drinks as much as he wishes then refrains, until a woman passes by and he goes to her and lifts her garment and has intercourse with her while they watch, just as the garment of a ewe is lifted. He lifted a garment upon him of these sahuli garments, and one among them would say: If only you had avoided her on the road. That among them is like Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ. So whoever reaches that time and enjoins good and forbids evil, he will have the reward of fifty of those who accompanied me and believed in me and trusted me."],[6230,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: Allah the Exalted will grant you power in the land; you will do therein what Allah wills you to do. When you commit sins therein, your enemy will be given mastery over you and drive you back to the land of the Arabs. He said: I said then: O Messenger of Allah, how will the land of the Arabs carry us, when you have told us of the large number of Muslims? He ﷺ said: Allah will send down provision for you therein, just as He sent down for the Children of Israel when they wandered."],[6231,"Night and day will not pass until the Quran wears out in the chests of people from this ummah just as clothes wear out, and other than it becomes more pleasing to them. Their affair becomes all greed, unmixed with fear. If one falls short of the right of Allah the Exalted, his soul gives him false hopes; and if he transgresses into what Allah the Exalted forbade, he says: I hope Allah will overlook me. They wear skins of lambs over hearts of wolves. The best of them in their own eyes is the flatterer. It was said: What is the flatterer? He said: The one who neither enjoins good nor forbids evil."],[6232,"A conquest was granted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, the horses have been released, the weapons laid down, and war has laid down its burdens; they say: No fighting. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Now fighting has come. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will not cease to make the hearts of people deviate whom you will fight; Allah provides from among them until the command of Allah comes upon that. The center of the believers' abode is in Syria."],[6233,"There will not cease to be a group of my ummah fighting at the gates of Damascus and its surroundings, and at the gates of Jerusalem and its surroundings; those who abandon them will not harm them. Ibn Hamdan added: The abandonment of those who abandon them will not harm them; they will be victorious upon the truth until the Hour rises."],[6234,"A band of this affair will remain upon the truth, not harmed by the opposition of those who let them down, until the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, comes."],[6235,"A band of this affair will remain upon the truth, not harmed by the opposition of those who let them down, until the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, comes."],[6236,"A band of this affair will remain upon the truth, not harmed by the opposition of those who let them down, until the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, comes."],[6237,"A band of this affair will remain upon the truth, not harmed by the opposition of those who let them down, until the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, comes."],[6238,"I heard Abd al-Rahman al-Hadrami during the days of Ibn al-Ash'ath delivering a sermon, and he was saying: \"O people of Sham, rejoice, for so-and-so...\""],[6239,"I was with Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan ؓ when the letter of his governor came to him, informing him that he had encountered the Turks and defeated them, and of the large number of them he had killed, and the large amount of booty he had taken. Mu'awiyah ؓ became angry at that, and then ordered that it be written to him: \"I have understood what you mentioned of those you killed and the booty you took. Do not let me know that you return to any of that, nor fight them until my command comes to you.\" I said to him: \"Why, O Commander of the Faithful?\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The Turks will drive out the Arabs until they make them catch up with the places where wormwood and southernwood grow.' Thus I dislike fighting them for that reason.\""],[6240,"A man stood up to him and said: \"O Abu Sa'id, al-Hajjaj has delayed the prayer on Friday until we were near the time of 'Asr. So stand up to him and command him to fear Allah, Exalted is He.\" Al-Hasan said: \"Then he would kill me.\" The man said to him: \"Did not Allah, Mighty and Majestic, say: 'They used not to forbid one another from wrongdoing that they did' (Al-Ma'idah 5:79)?\" Al-Hasan said..."],[6241,"When Yazid b. al-Muhallab defeated the people of Basrah, I feared to sit in al-Hasan's circle, lest I be found there and recognized. So I went to al-Hasan in his house and entered upon him. I said: \"O Abu Sa'id, what about this verse?\" He said: \"Which verse?\" I said: \"The saying of Him, Mighty and Majestic: 'They used not to forbid one another from wrongdoing that they did' (Al-Ma'idah 5:79).\" He said: \"O Abdullah, the people drew the sword, and the sword intervened to prevent speech.\" I said: \"O Abu Sa'id, do you know of any virtue for one who speaks?\" He said: \"No.\" Al-Mu'alla said: Then he narrated two hadiths. He said: \"Abu Sa'id narrated to us from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: 'Let not the fear of people prevent any of you from speaking the truth when he sees it, for it does not bring death nearer nor drive provision away.'\" He said: Then al-Hasan narrated another hadith and said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It is not for a believer to humiliate himself.' It was said: 'And what is his humiliating himself?' He said: 'He exposes himself to tribulation that he cannot bear.'\" It was said: \"O Abu Sa'id, and Yazid al-Dabbi in his speech during the prayer?\" He said: \"Indeed, he did not leave prison until he regretted.\" Al-Mu'alla said: So I got up from al-Hasan's gathering and went to Yazid al-Dabbi. I said: \"O Abu Mawdud, while I and al-Hasan were discussing, you set your affair before us.\" He said: \"Enough, O Abu al-Hasan.\" I said: \"I have done so.\" He said: \"So what did he say?\" I said: \"Indeed, he did not leave prison until he regretted his statement.\" Yazid said: \"I do not regret my statement. By Allah, I stood in a position in which I risked my life.\" Yazid said: \"I came to al-Hasan and said: 'O Abu Sa'id, will we be overcome in everything, and be overcome in our prayer?' He said: 'O Abdullah, you are exposing yourself to them, and then you will accomplish nothing.'\" He said: \"Then I came to him and he said to me the same as his previous statement. So I stood up on Friday in the mosque while al-Hakam b. Ayyub was delivering the sermon, and I said: 'The prayer, may Allah have mercy on you.' When I said that, men surrounded me, seized my beard, my head, and my collar, and began striking my belly with the scabbards of their swords. They took me toward the enclosure. I entered and stood before al-Hakam while he was silent. He said: 'Are you mad? Were we not in prayer?' I said: 'May Allah set the amir right, is there any speech better than the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic?' He said: 'No.' I said: 'Have you considered if a man spread out a mushaf and read it from morning to night, would that discharge his prayer?' He said: 'By Allah, I think you are mad.' He said: 'And Anas b. Malik was sitting beneath his minbar, silent. So I said: \"O Anas! O Abu Hamzah, I adjure you by Allah, Exalted is He, for you served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and accompanied him. Did I speak with what is right or with what is wrong? With truth or with falsehood?\"' He said: 'No, by Allah, he did not answer me with a word.' So al-Hakam b. Ayyub said to him: 'O Anas.' He said: 'At your service, may Allah set you right.' He said: 'Had the time of prayer passed?' He said: 'Rather, some of it remained.' So al-Hakam said: 'Imprison him.'\" Yazid said: \"I swear to you, O Abu al-Hasan, what I met from my companions was harder on me than what I met from al-Hakam. Some of them said: 'He is a hypocrite,' and some said: 'He is mad.'\" He said: \"Al-Hakam wrote to al-Hajjaj that a man from Banu Dabbah stood up to me on Friday while I was delivering the sermon, and said: 'The prayer,' and that just witnesses have testified before me that he is mad. So al-Hajjaj wrote to him: 'If the just witnesses testify that he is mad, then release him; otherwise, cut off his hands and feet, gouge out his eyes with hot iron, and crucify him.'\" He said: \"So they testified before al-Hakam that I was mad, and he released me.\" Al-Mu'alla said, from Yazid al-Dabbi: \"Then a brother of ours died, and we followed his funeral procession and prayed over him. When he was buried, I withdrew with a group, and we remembered Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and remembered our return to Him. While we were doing that, we saw the forelocks of horses and spears. When my companions saw that, they dispersed and left me alone. Al-Hakam came and stood over me. He said: 'What were you doing?' I said: 'May Allah set the amir right, a companion of ours died, and we prayed over him, buried him, and sat remembering our Lord, remembering our return to Him, and remembering what he has come to.' He said: 'What prevented you from fleeing as they fled?' I said: 'May Allah set you right, I am innocent of that. Would I flee from the amir?' Al-Hakam was silent. Then Abdul-Malik b. al-Muhallab, who was in charge of his police, said to him: 'Do you know who this is?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'This is the one who spoke on Friday.' He said: 'Al-Hakam became angry and said: \"You are indeed bold. Seize him.\"' So I was seized, and he flogged me with four hundred lashes. I did not know when he left me because of the severity of the beating. He said: 'And he sent me to Wasit, and I remained in al-Hajjaj's dungeon until al-Hajjaj died.'\""],[6242,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ in the mosque of al-Khayf, and his companions said to me: \"Move aside, O Wathilah,\" meaning: get out of his way. He said: \"Leave him, for he has only come to ask.\" So I drew near and said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about a matter that we may take from you after you are gone.\" He ﷺ said: \"Let your own self give you a ruling.\" I said: \"How can I do that?\" He ﷺ said: \"Leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt, even if the muftis give you rulings.\" I said: \"How can I know that?\" He ﷺ said: \"Place your hand on your heart, for the heart is at rest with the lawful and is not at rest with the unlawful. And the scrupulousness of a Muslim is that he leaves the small sin for fear of falling into the great one.\" I said: \"Who is the greedy?\" He said: \"The one who seeks earnings from what is not lawful.\" I said: \"Who is the scrupulous?\" He ﷺ said: \"The one who stops at what is doubtful.\" I said: \"Who is the believer?\" He said: \"The one whom people trust with their wealth and their lives.\" I said: \"Who is the Muslim?\" He ﷺ said: \"The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.\" I said: \"Which jihad is best?\" He ﷺ said: \"A word of truth in the presence of a tyrannical ruler.\""],[6243,"The adornment of the world will be lifted in the year one hundred and twenty-five."],[6244,"Every nation has a term, and the term of my nation is one hundred years. When one hundred years pass over my nation, what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has promised it will come to it."],[6245,"By the hundredth year, Allah will send a cold, pleasant wind in which He will take the soul of every believer."],[6246,"I came to al-Miqdam b. Ma'dikarib in the mosque and said: 'O Abu Yazid, the people claim that you did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'Glory be to Allah! By Allah, I saw him while I was walking with my uncle, and he took hold of this ear of mine and said to my uncle: \"Do you think this one remembers his mother or his father?\" We said to him...'"],[6247,"5372 4483 / 3 - Sufyan b. Waki' narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Bashir b. al-Muhajir narrated to us, similarly."],[6248,"5373 4483 / 4 - And al-Ruyani said: Al-Hasan b. Ibrahim narrated to us: Ubaydullah b. Musa narrated to us: Bashir narrated it and mentioned it. A sound chain."],[6249,"Abu al-Jald narrated to him, and swore upon it: that this community will not perish until there are in it twelve caliphs, all of them acting upon guidance and the religion of truth. Among them are two men from the household of the Prophet ﷺ. One of them will live forty years and the other thirty years, and there will be caliphs after them who are not from them."],[6250,"The earth will surely be filled with oppression and injustice. When it is filled with oppression and injustice, Allah the Exalted will send a man from me whose name is my name, or the name of a prophet, who will fill it with equity and justice. The sky will not withhold any of its rain, nor the earth any of its vegetation. He will remain among them seven or eight, or if longer, nine."],[6251,"Ma'mar narrated it, from Abu Harun, from Mu'awiyah b. Qurrah, from Abu al-Siddiq, from Abu Sa'id ؓ. : :"],[6252,"The Hour will not come until a man from my household goes out against them and strikes them until they return to the truth. He said: I said: And how long will he rule? He said: Five and two. I said: What is five and two? He said: I do not know."],[6253,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the Beast and said: It has three emergences in the course of time. It will emerge in the remotest part of the desert, and its mention will not enter the town—meaning Makkah. Then it will hide for a long time. Then it will emerge another time, less than that, and its mention will become prominent in the desert and its mention will enter the town—meaning Makkah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Then while the people are in the greatest mosque, the one most sacred to Allah—best and noblest, the Sacred Mosque—they will be startled only by it braying between the Corner and the Station, shaking the dust from its head. The people will disperse from it in all directions, but a band of believers will remain steadfast, knowing that they cannot escape Allah the Exalted. It will begin with them and brand their faces until it makes them like the shining star. Then it will depart into the earth, no pursuer catching it and no fleer escaping it, to the point that a man will seek refuge from it by prayer, and it will come to him from behind and say: Now, O so-and-so, you pray? He will turn to it, and it will mark his face, then go off. People will share in wealth and accompany one another in the cities, the believer being known from the disbeliever, so that the believer will say: O disbeliever, pay me my due, and the disbeliever will say: O believer, pay me my due."],[6255,"Shall I not show you the place from which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the Beast of the earth will emerge? He struck with his staff the crack in al-Safa and said: It has feathers and down, and a third of it will emerge with the speed of a swift horse for three days and three nights. It will pass by them while they flee from it to the mosques, and it will say to them: Do you think the mosques will save you from me? It will brand them on their noses, and they will be driven into the markets, and they will say: O believer! O disbeliever!"],[6256,"The Hour will not come until two old men meet, and one of them says to his companion: When were you born? He says: On the day the sun rose from the west."],[6257,"There will come something like three nights of these nights of yours. When those who keep vigil at night recognize it, a man will stand and recite his portion, then sleep, then stand and recite his portion, then sleep, then stand and recite his portion. While they are thus, the people will stir against one another, saying: What is this? They will rush to the mosques, and behold, the sun has risen from here, from its west. It will come until when it reaches the middle of the sky, it will return. So that is: 'On the day when some signs of your Lord come, no soul will benefit from its faith'—the verse."],[6258,"Paradise has eight gates: seven are closed and one is open until the sun rises from the west."],[6260,"I asked Sa'id ؓ: What is the sign of the destruction of the people? He said: When their scholars perish."],[6261,"There will surely come upon the people a time when their hearts are the hearts of non-Arabs. It was said: And what are the hearts of non-Arabs? He said: Love of this world. Their way is the way of the Bedouins: whatever provision Allah gives them, they put it into livestock. They regard jihad as harm and charity as a fine."],[6262,"Al-Harith said: Al-Muqri' narrated to me, Sa'id b. Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Ibn Hani' narrated to me, Shufayy narrated to me, from 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr ؓ, his saying with this. I say: And this is more correct."],[6263,"The Hour will not come until some people of my Ummah return to idols that they used to worship besides Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[6264,"The Hour will not come until the Arabs worship what their forefathers used to worship for one hundred and fifty years."],[6265,"The Hour will not come until you fight your leader, and strike one another with your swords, and your worst ones inherit your worldly wealth."],[6266,"We went out with 'Abdullah ؓ from his house while the imam was bowing, so we bowed, then we walked until we joined the row. A man passed by and said: 'Peace be upon you, O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman.' He said: 'Allah is Greatest. Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.' When we finished the prayer, we said: 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, it is as if the man's greeting startled you.' He said: 'Yes, it was said that among the signs of the Hour are that mosques are taken as thoroughfares, that a man greets another only because he knows him, that a woman and a man trade together, and that women and horses become expensive together, then become cheap and never become expensive again.'"],[6267,"5390 4497 / 2 - al-Nadr informed us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Husayn, with this chain, the like of it. : :"],[6268,"Al-Tayalisi said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Husayn, something similar. : :"],[6269,"5392 4497 / 4 - Ahmad b. Mani' said: Hushaym narrated to us: Husayn narrated to us, something similar. : :"],[6270,"Ibn Mas'ud ؓ was between me and Masruq. A Bedouin passed by and said: 'Peace be upon you, O Ibn Umm 'Abd.' Ibn Mas'ud ؓ laughed, and he was asked."],[6271,"Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad b. al-Khattab narrated to us: Mu'ammal narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Husayn, something similar. Ahmad narrated it from the hadith of al-Aswad b. Yazid, from Ibn Mas'ud ؓ, with its meaning in abbreviated form, and also from the route of Tariq, from Ibn Mas'ud ؓ, with its meaning as well:"],[6272,"What Allah and His Messenger promised us we have seen all but four: the rising of the sun from the west, the Beast of the Earth, the Dajjal, and the emergence of Ya'juj and Ma'juj."],[6273,"The stars are a safeguard for the inhabitants of the sky, and the people of my House are a safeguard for my Ummah."],[6274,"I approached with Zayd b. al-Hasan and Ibn Rummana, the mawla of 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Marwan, having set up our arms for him while he was leaning on us. We entered the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and in it was Ibn Niyar, a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. He sent to Abu Bakr ؓ saying: 'Come to me.' He came to him, and he said: 'I saw you two, with Ibn Rummana between you, leaning on you and on Zayd b. al-Hasan. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The Hour will not come until the world is at the disposal of the base son of the base.'"],[6275,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the pulpit saying: O these people, when you hear of an army that has been swallowed up by the earth nearby, then the Hour has drawn near."],[6276,"A day will surely come upon this community when they will spend the evening asking one another: 'With whom was the earth swallowed tonight?' just as they ask one another: 'Who remains of the family of so-and-so?' and 'Who remains of the family of so-and-so?'"],[6277,"There will be a sinking in the east. It was said: 'A sinking in a land where there are Muslims?' He said: 'Yes, when most of their deeds are evil.'"],[6278,"The Hour will not come until you copulate in the road like donkeys copulate. I said: 'Will that really happen?' He said: 'Yes, it will surely happen.'"],[6279,"By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim ﷺ, Jesus son of Mary (peace and blessings be upon him) will surely descend... and he mentioned the hadith. In it: 'He will surely reconcile between people, remove mutual hatred, and distribute wealth. Then if he stands at my grave and says: O Muhammad, I will surely answer him.'"],[6280,"Men from my community will surely meet Jesus son of Mary (peace and blessings be upon him) and will surely witness the fighting against the Dajjal."],[6281,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas ؓ dispatched Nadlah b. 'Amr al-Ansari ؓ with three hundred men from the Muhajirun and the Ansar. They raided Hulwan and conquered it, capturing much booty and many prisoners. They came driving what was with them while they were between two mountains, until the afternoon prayer overtook them. Nadlah ؓ said to them: 'Turn toward the foot of the mountain,' and they did so. Then Nadlah ؓ stood and called the adhan, saying: 'Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar.' A voice from the mountain answered him, with no visible form: 'You have proclaimed greatness greatly, O Nadlah.' He said: 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah.' It said: 'You have been sincere, O Nadlah, with true sincerity.' He said: 'I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.' It said: 'A prophet was sent after whom there is no prophet.' He said: 'Come to prayer.' It said: 'An obligation that has been ordained.' He said: 'Come to success.' It said: 'Successful is the one who comes to it and perseveres in it.' He said: 'The prayer is about to begin.' It said: 'Endurance is for the community of Muhammad ﷺ, and upon its heads the Hour will come.' When they had prayed, Nadlah ؓ stood and said: 'O good, pleasant, beautiful speech, we have heard good speech. Are you from the angels of Allah, or a tayf (spirit), or a resident? Appear to us and speak with us, for we are a delegation of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and a delegation of His Prophet ﷺ.' Then an old man emerged from one of those mountain passes, white-haired and white-bearded, with a head like a millstone, long-bearded, in two worn white woolen garments. He said: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.' They returned his greeting. Nadlah said to him: 'Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you?' He said: 'I am Zarnab b. Tharmala, the deputy of the righteous servant Jesus son of Mary. He prayed for me to remain until his descent from heaven, and my abode is in this mountain. Convey my greetings to 'Umar b. al-Khattab, the Commander of the Faithful ؓ, and tell him: Be steadfast, aim rightly, and draw near, for the matter has drawn close. And beware, O 'Umar, if certain traits appear in the community of Muhammad ﷺ while you are among them, then flee, flee.' Nadlah ؓ said: 'O Zarnab! May Allah have mercy on you.'"],[6283,"I was sent in the breath of the Hour."],[6284,"I and the Hour were sent like these two, and I preceded it by a breath of the Hour."],[6285,"He said to 'Abdullah b. Saba' al-Saba'i: 'Woe to you! By Allah, he did not confide to me anything that he concealed from anyone of the people. By Allah, I heard him say: Before the Hour there will be thirty liars, and you are one of them.'"],[6286,"I came to al-Miqdam b. Ma'dikarib in the mosque and said: 'O Abu Yazid, the people claim that you did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'Glory be to Allah! By Allah, I saw him while I was walking with my uncle, and he took hold of this ear of mine and said to my uncle: \"Do you think this one remembers his mother or his father?\" We said to him...'"],[6287,"5409 4510 / 3 - And Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muhammad b. al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, with it:"],[6288,"The Hour will not come until seventy liars emerge before the Hour."],[6289,"Before the emergence of the Dajjal there will be seventy-some Dajjals."],[6290,"I met Ibn Sayyad one day, and with him was a man from the Jews, and his eye had been extinguished, and it was protruding like a camel's eye. When I saw it I said: \"Ibn Sayyad! I adjure you by Allah, when was your eye extinguished?\" He wiped it and said: \"I do not know, by the Most Merciful.\" I said: \"You lie, you do not know while it is in your head?\" The Jew claimed to me that I struck my hand on his chest, and I do not know that I did that. I said: \"Be off! You will never exceed your bounds.\" He said: \"Indeed, I will not exceed my bounds.\" He mentioned something I do not remember. I mentioned that to Hafsa ؓ, and she said: \"Avoid this man, for we speak that the Dajjal will emerge at a fit of anger that he becomes angry.\""],[6291,"Ibn Sayyad, his mother gave birth to him while he was one-eyed and circumcised, happy."],[6292,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard about Ibn Sayyad, he went to him with some of his companions. His mother said: \"He is playing with the boys.\" She said: \"I gave birth to him one-eyed and circumcised.\" So he called him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I believe in Allah and His messengers.\" He said: \"I have hidden something for you, what is it?\" He said: \"Dukh (smoke).\" He ﷺ said: \"Be off!\" Then he said: \"Look, what do you see?\" He said: \"I see a whirlwind and a throne on the water.\" He said: \"It has been obscured from him.\" Umar ؓ said: \"Shall I kill him, O Messenger of Allah?\" He ﷺ said: \"If he is the Dajjal, you will not be given power to kill him, and if he is not the Dajjal, it is not lawful to kill him.\""],[6293,"Indeed, with the Dajjal when he emerges there will be water and fire. As for what people see as water, it is burning fire. As for what people see as fire, it is cool water. So whoever of you reaches that, let him fall into what he sees as fire, for it is cool water. Uqba ؓ said: \"And I heard him saying that.\""],[6294,"Before the Dajjal there will be years of deception, in which rain will be abundant, vegetation will be scarce, the truthful will be belied, the liar will be believed, the treacherous will be trusted, the trustworthy will be betrayed, and the ruwaybidah will speak. It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the ruwaybidah?\" He ﷺ said: \"The one who is not paid any attention to.\""],[6295,"And what is the ruwaybidah? He said: \"The insignificant man who speaks about the affairs of the common people.\""],[6296,"The Dajjal, when he emerges, will emerge from the direction of the east. His armies and his outposts will become numerous, and no one will reach him except one who says: \"I am a delegate.\" So a man will come and say: \"I am a delegate.\" When the Dajjal sees him, he will say: \"Son of Adam, do you not know that I am your lord?\" He will say: \"No, you are the enemy of Allah, the Dajjal.\" He will say: \"Then I will kill you.\" He will say: \"Even if you kill me.\" He said: Then he will take a saw and place it between his forelock, and split him into two halves. Then he will say to those around him: \"How do you see it if I revive him?\" They will say: \"That is when we will be certain that you are our lord.\" He said: Then he will revive him. He will say to him: \"Son of Adam, you claimed that I am not your lord.\" He will say: \"I was never more certain of insight about you than now.\" He will say: \"I will slaughter you.\" He will say: \"Even if you slaughter me.\" He said: Then he will intend to slaughter him but will not be able to slaughter him. Then he will say from beneath him: \"If you are truthful, then slaughter me.\" At that point his armies will doubt him, and Ibn Maryam ﷺ will descend upon him. When he sees him and smells his scent, he will melt as lead melts."],[6297,"I entered upon Yazid b. Muawiya, and he mentioned a story. Abdullah b. Amr ؓ said: \"Is there in your land a land called Kutha, with salt marshes and palm trees?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then the Dajjal will emerge from it.\""],[6298,"I heard from some of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ a hadith about the Dajjal, and I have not heard from him a hadith nobler than it: that he will come on a donkey, and he will come to a man in the form of one of his household, and say: \"O so-and-so, I call you to the truth; my affair is true.\""],[6299,"I warn you of the Dajjal."],[6300,"He then mentioned the hadith regarding the story of the Dajjal."],[6302,"The Dajjal has eaten and walked in the markets."],[6303,"No one is given power over the Dajjal except 'Isa son of Maryam ﷺ ."],[6304,"In the story of the Dajjal, she said: And he is among you, O nation."],[6305,"In the story of Tamim al-Dari with the Dajjal, and at its beginning:"],[6306,"Tamim came to me and told me news that prevented me from the midday nap due to joy and delight of the eye."],[6307,"The Prophet ﷺ pointed with his hand toward the east about twenty times."],[6309,"Then he began to tell us: Yajuj and Majuj are from the children of Adam. If they were unleashed upon the people, they would corrupt their livelihoods. None of them dies except that he leaves from his offspring a thousand or more. Behind them are three nations: Tawil, Taris, and Mansak."],[6310,"Yajuj and Majuj dig every day."],[6311,"The Hour will not be established upon a believer. Allah Almighty will send a wind, and it will blow, and no believer will remain except that he dies."],[6312,"The Hour will not be established until Allah sends a red wind from Yemen. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will seize with it every soul that believes in Allah and the Last Day. The people will not deny it due to the few who die in it: an old man died among Banu so-and-so, an old woman died among Banu so-and-so. The Book of Allah Almighty will be taken up at night, and it will be raised to heaven, so that not a verse of it remains on earth. The earth will cast out the pieces of its liver of gold and silver, and no benefit will be taken from them after that day. A man will pass by them and strike them with his feet, saying: In these, those before us used to fight, and today they have become of no use."],[6313,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ : O Umar, how will it be for you when you die, and they measure for you three cubits and a span in a cubit and a span, then they return to you and wash you, shroud you, and perfume you, then they carry you until they place you in it, then they heap the dust upon you? When they depart from you, the two trialers of the grave will come to you: Munkar and Nakir, their voices like crashing thunder and their eyes like flashing lightning. They will shake you and interrogate you and terrify you. How will it be for you at that, O Umar? He said: O Messenger of Allah, and will I have my mind? He ﷺ said: Yes. He ؓ said: Then I shall suffice you against them."],[6314,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a boy, or a girl, and said: If anyone could be saved from the squeezing of the grave, this child would be saved."],[6315,"The straitened livelihood which Allah, Exalted is He, mentioned is the punishment of the grave."],[6316,"I witnessed Anas b. Malik ؓ when a man said to him: O Abu Hamzah, there are people who deny the intercession. He ؓ said: Do not sit with them. Then a man said to him: There are people who deny the punishment of the grave. He ؓ said: Do not sit with them."],[6317,"Seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, I have seen how they are punished in their graves."],[6318,"The punishment of the grave is true; whoever does not believe in it will be punished."],[6319,"The month is twenty-nine."],[6320,"The grave says to the dead person when he is placed in it: Woe to you, O son of Adam! What deceived you about me? Did you not know that I am the house of trial and the house of darkness? What deceived you about me when you used to pass by me with an arrogant gait? If he was righteous, a responder answers for him to the grave: Have you considered if he used to enjoin good and forbid evil? He said: Then the grave says: Then I shall return upon him as green, and his soul ascends to the Lord of the worlds. Then Ibn A'idh said to him: O Abu al-Hajjaj, what is the arrogant gait? He said: The one who advances one foot and delays the other, like your gait sometimes, O son of my brother. He said: And at that time he was wearing and adorning himself."],[6321,"The believer in his grave is in a garden, and his grave is widened for him by seventy cubits, and it is illuminated for him like the moon on the night of the full moon. Do you know about what this verse was revealed: 'Then for him is a straitened livelihood, and We will raise him on the Day of Resurrection blind'? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The punishment of the disbeliever in his grave. By the One in whose hand is my soul, ninety-nine dragons are set upon him. Do you know what the dragon is? He said: Ninety-nine serpents, each serpent has seven heads, they blow into his body, sting him, and scratch him until the Day of Resurrection."],[6322,"When people are gathered on the Day of Resurrection, they will stand for forty, with the sun above their heads, their eyes staring at the sky, awaiting the judgment, every righteous and wicked among them, none of them speaking. Then a caller will call out: Is it not justice from your Lord who created you, formed you, and provided for you, and then you worshipped other than Him, that He should assign every people to what they turned to? They will say: Yes. Then an angel will call out with that three times. Then the deities that each people used to worship will appear before them, and they will follow them until they lead them to the Fire. Then the believers and the hypocrites will remain. The believers will fall down in prostration, and the backs of the hypocrites will be fused, becoming a single bone like the horns of cattle, and they will fall on their backs. Then Allah, Exalted is He, will say to them: Raise your heads to your light, according to the measure of your deeds. So a man will raise his head and his light before him like a mountain, and a man will raise his head and his light before him like a palace, and a man will raise his head and his light before him like a house, until He mentioned like a tree. Then they will pass over the bridge like lightning and like the wind and like the running of a horse and like the hastening of a man, until the last of people remains, whose light is on the big toe of his foot like a lamp. Sometimes it shines for him and sometimes it dims, and the Fire takes branches from him. He will remain thus until he crosses. Then he will say: He does not know who has been saved from it besides me, and no one has suffered what I have suffered; its heat afflicted me and I was saved from it. He said: Then a gate of Paradise will be opened for him, and he will say: O Lord, admit me into this. He will say: My servant, perhaps if I admit you, you will ask Me for other than it. He said: Then He admits him. While he is marveling at what he is in, another gate is opened for him, and what he is in becomes insignificant in his eyes. He will say: O Lord, admit me into this. He will say: Did you not claim that you would not ask Me for other than it? He will say: By Your might and majesty, if You admit me into it, I will not ask You for other than it. He said: Then He admits him until He admits him through four gates, all of which he asks for. Then a man like light will face him. When he sees him, he will fall down and prostrate to him. He will say: What is your matter? He will say: Are you not my Lord? He will say: I am only a steward. You have in Paradise a thousand stewards over a thousand palaces, between every two palaces a journey of a thousand years, the farthest of them seen as the nearest is seen. Then a gate of green chrysolite is opened for him, containing seventy gates, in each gate spouses, couches, and attendants. He will sit with his wife, and she will hand him the cup and say: You are, since I handed you the cup, seventy times more handsome than you were before. Upon her are seventy garments of various colors, the marrow of her shin is seen, and the man wears his clothes upon her liver, and her liver is his mirror. This is a sound, connected chain whose men are trustworthy."],[6323,"The Trumpet is like a horn, blown into."],[6324,"How will people be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection? He ؓ said: They will be resurrected while the sky drizzles upon them."],[6325,"I know the last man of my nation to cross the bridge: a man who writhes on the bridge like a boy when his father brings him near; his hand slips once, and the Fire touches it, and his foot slips once, and the Fire touches it. He said: Then the angels say to him: Have you considered if Allah, Exalted is He, raises you in this place of yours and you walk upright, will you tell us of every deed you did? He said: Then he says: Yes, by His might, I will not conceal any of my deeds. He said: Then they say to him: Arise and walk upright. So he arises and walks until he crosses the bridge, then they say to him."],[6326,"I know the last of the people of Paradise to enter it: a man who used to ask Allah, Exalted, to keep him away from the Fire."],[6327,"We sat beside Ibn Umar and Abu Sa'id ؓ. One of them said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The sweat will reach the people on the Day of Resurrection.' One of them said, 'Up to the lobe of his ear,' and the other said, 'Until the sweat bridles him.' Ibn Umar ؓ said, 'Thus.' And Abu Asim described it, passing his finger from the lobe of his ear to his mouth, saying, 'This and that are alike.'"],[6328,"The Bridge (al-Sirat) is like the edge of a sword: slippery and a place of slipping, with thorns and hooks."],[6329,"Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will call the servant on the Day of Resurrection and remind him of His blessings and favors, until he says, among what he says, 'You asked Me on such-and-such a day to marry you to so-and-so' – naming her – 'and you married her.'"],[6330,"Indeed the disbeliever, the sweat will bridle him on the Day of Resurrection, and he will say, 'Give me relief, even if to the Fire.'"],[6331,"Indeed the disbeliever will be called to account on the Day of Resurrection until the sweat bridles him, until he says, 'Give me relief, even if to the Fire.'"],[6332,"The shame and disgrace that will reach the son of Adam on the Day of Resurrection in the presence of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is such that a man will wish to be ordered to the Fire."],[6333,"Indeed the sweat will cling to a man in the standing place, until he says, 'O Lord, sending me to the Fire is easier for me than what I am experiencing,' while he knows the severity of the punishment in it."],[6334,"The Trustworthy Spirit ﷺ related to him that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has decreed that the deeds of the servant will be brought on the Day of Resurrection – his good deeds and his bad deeds – and some will be set against others. If one good deed remains for him, Allah will expand for him in Paradise as He wills."],[6335,"Some of my community will come on the Day of Resurrection like a flood, and the angels will say, 'What came with Muhammad ﷺ of his community is more than what came with all the prophets.'"],[6336,"The sun and the moon are two bulls, hamstrung in the Fire."],[6337,"Regarding ablution with seawater, he said: “They are two seas; it does not harm you whichever of them you begin with.”"],[6338,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was watering a she-camel of mine in front of me, so I spat, and my sputum fell on my garment. So I began to wash my garment from the water-skin that was in front of me. He said, 'O Ammar, your sputum and the tears of your eyes are only like the water in your water-skin. Only that is washed from urine, excrement, semen from the greatest water, blood, and vomit.'"],[6339,"The people will be gathered barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised. 'A'ishah ؓ said: \"And the women, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you?\" He said: \"Yes.\" She said: \"What a disgrace!\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"And what did you find astonishing, O daughter of Abu Bakr?\" She said: \"I was astonished by your statement, that they will look at one another.\" He said: \"Then the Prophet ﷺ struck her shoulder and said: 'O daughter of Abu Quhafah, the people on that day will be preoccupied from looking, and their eyes will be raised upward for forty years. They will neither eat nor drink, staring with their eyes. Among them will be one whose sweat reaches his feet, and among them one whose sweat reaches his shins, and among them one whose sweat reaches his belly, and among them one whom sweat bridles due to the length of standing. Then after that Allah will have mercy upon the servants, and He will command the near angels, and they will carry His throne from the heavens to a white earth upon which no blood has been shed and no sin has been committed, as if it were white silver. Then the angels will stand surrounding the throne, and that is the first day on which an eye looked at Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Then He will command a caller, and he will call with a voice that the two heavy ones hear—the jinn and mankind: \"Where is so-and-so son of so-and-so?\" So they will crane their necks for that, and he will come out from the standing place, and Allah, Exalted, will make him known to the people. Then it will be said: \"His good deeds come forth with him.\" So Allah, Exalted, will make those good deeds known to the people of the standing place. When he stands before the Lord of the worlds, it will be said: \"Where are the people of grievances?\" They will come one by one, and it will be said: \"Did you wrong so-and-so in such-and-such a way?\" He will say: \"Yes, my Lord.\" That is the day when their tongues, their feet, and their hands will testify against them for what they used to earn. So his good deeds will be taken and given to the one he wronged, on a day when there is no dirham and no dinar—only taking from good deeds and returning from evil deeds. The people of grievances will continue to take from his good deeds until no good deed remains for him. Then those who remain and have not taken anything will stand and say: \"What about us? Others have taken their due and we remain.\" It will be said to them: \"Do not be hasty. It will be taken from their evil deeds and given to him, until no one remains who was wronged with any grievance.\" So Allah, Exalted, will make that known to all the people of the standing place. When his good deeds are exhausted, it will be said: \"Return to your mother, the abyss. There is no injustice today. Surely Allah is swift in reckoning.\" On that day, no angel, no sent prophet, no truthful one, no martyr, and no human being will remain except that he will think, due to the severity of the punishment he sees, that he will not be saved, except those whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, protects."],[6340,"When Allah gathers the first and the last on the Day of Resurrection, a caller will come and call with a voice that all creation hears: \"The people of the gathering will know today who is most deserving of honor.\" Then he will return and call: \"Let those stand whose sides forsake their beds [Surah al-Sajdah:16].\" They will stand, and they are few. Then he will return and call: \"Where are those whom neither trade nor sale diverts from the remembrance of Allah [Surah al-Nur:37]?\" They will stand, and they are few. Then he will return and call: \"Let those stand who used to praise Allah in prosperity and adversity.\" They will stand, and they are few. Then the rest of the people will be brought to account."],[6341,"The earth will consume everything of the human being except the coccyx bone. It was said: \"And what is it like, O Messenger of Allah?\" He ﷺ said: \"Like a mustard seed; from it they will grow.\""],[6342,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, the earth will be stretched out like leather is stretched, in its vastness such and such, and all creatures will be on one plain, their jinn and their humans. When that happens, this lowest heaven will be emptied of its inhabitants, and they will be scattered upon the face of the earth. The inhabitants of the heaven alone will be more than all the inhabitants of the earth, both jinn and humans, by double. When they are scattered upon the face of the earth, the inhabitants of the earth will be terrified of them and say: \"Is our Lord among you?\" They will be terrified by their words and say: \"Glory be to our Lord, He is not among us, and He is coming.\" Then the inhabitants of the second heaven will be emptied, and the inhabitants of the second heaven alone will be more than the inhabitants of the lowest heaven and all the inhabitants of the earth, by double. When they are scattered upon the face of the earth, the inhabitants of the earth will be terrified of them and say: \"Is our Lord among you?\" They will be terrified by their words and say: \"Glory be to our Lord, He is not among us, and He is coming.\" Then all the heavens will be emptied, one after another, and each heaven will be multiplied over the heaven below it and all the inhabitants of the earth. Whenever they are scattered upon the face of the earth, the inhabitants of the earth will be terrified of them and say to them the like of that, and they will reply to them the like of that. Then the inhabitants of the seventh heaven will be emptied, and the inhabitants of the seventh heaven are more numerous than the inhabitants of the six heavens and all the inhabitants of the earth, by double. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will come among them, and the nations will be kneeling in rows. A caller will call: \"Today you will know who are the people of honor. Let the frequent praisers of their Lord in every state stand.\" They will depart to Paradise. Then he will call a second time: \"Today they will know who are the people of honor. Let those stand whose sides forsake their beds [Surah al-Sajdah:16].\" They will stand and depart to Paradise. Then he will call a third time: \"Let those stand whom neither trade nor sale diverts from the remembrance of Allah [Surah al-Nur:37].\" They will stand and depart to Paradise. When He has taken these three groups, a neck will emerge from the Fire and look over the creatures. It has two seeing eyes and an eloquent tongue, and it will say: \"I have been appointed over three: I have been appointed over every arrogant tyrant.\" It will snatch them from the rows as a bird snatches sesame seeds, and it will settle them in Hell. Then it will emerge a second time and say: \"I have been appointed over those who harmed Allah and His Messenger.\" It will snatch them from the rows as a bird snatches sesame seeds, and it will settle them in Hell. Then it will emerge a third time—I think he said—and say: \"I have been appointed over the makers of images.\" It will snatch them from the rows as a bird snatches sesame seeds, and it will settle them in Hell. When it has taken three from these and three from those, the records will be spread out, the scales will be set up, and the creatures will be summoned to the reckoning. This is mawquf, and its chain is hasan."],[6343,"He said: \"Go to My friend and bring him to Me, for I have tested him with prosperity and adversity and found him where I love. Bring him to Me, that I may give him rest.\" He said: \"The Angel of Death will go to him, accompanied by five hundred angels. With them are shrouds and embalming perfume from Paradise, and with them are bundles of basil: the stem of each basil plant is one, and at its head are twenty colors, each color having a scent different from its companion's. With them is white silk containing pungent musk. He said: \"The Angel of Death will sit at his head, and the angels will surround him. Each of them will place his hand on a limb of his body, and that white silk and pungent musk will be spread beneath his chin. A door to Paradise will be opened for him, and his soul will be soothed at that moment by the delights of Paradise—sometimes by its spouses, sometimes by its clothing, and sometimes by its fruits—just as a child's family soothes him when he cries. His spouses will be eager for him at that moment with great eagerness.\" He said: \"The soul will emerge.\" (Al-Bursani said: he means to come out quickly because of what it sees of what it loves.) He said: \"The Angel of Death will say: 'Come out, O good soul, to lote trees with thorns removed, and clustered plantains, and extended shade, and flowing water.'\" He said: \"The Angel of Death is gentler with him than a mother with her child, knowing that this soul is beloved to its Lord, so he seeks gentleness for it, out of love for its Lord and desiring the Lord's pleasure with it. So his soul will be drawn out as a hair is drawn from dough.\" He said: \"Allah, Exalted, said: 'Those whom the angels take in a state of goodness' [Surah al-Nahl:32]. And He, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'Then if he is of those brought near, then rest and basil and a garden of bliss' [Surah al-Waqi'ah:88-89].\" He said: \"'Rest' from the hardship of death, and 'basil' with which he is received, and 'a garden of bliss' that faces him.\" He said: \"When the Angel of Death takes his soul, the soul will say to the body: 'May Allah reward you well on my behalf. You were quick in me toward obedience to Allah, Exalted, and slow in me away from disobedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic. You have been saved and you have saved.' He said: \"The body will say the like of that to the soul.\" He said: \"The places of the earth where he used to obey Allah, Exalted, will weep over him, and every gate of heaven through which his deeds ascended and his provision descended will weep for forty years.\" He said: \"When the Angel of Death takes his soul, the five hundred angels will stay by his body. No son of Adam will turn him to one side except the angels turn him before them, and they will cover him with shrouds before the shrouds of the sons of Adam, and with embalming perfume before the embalming perfume of the sons of Adam. From the door of his house to the door of his grave, two rows of angels will stand, receiving him with prayers for forgiveness.\" He said: \"At that, Iblis will cry out with a cry from which the bones of some of his body will crack, and he will say to his troops: 'Woe to you! How did this servant escape from you?' He said: \"They will say: 'This servant was protected.'\" He said: \"When the angel ascends with his soul to the heaven, Jibril ﷺ will meet him with seventy thousand angels, each bringing him a glad tiding from his Lord different from his companion's.\" He said: \"When the Angel of Death reaches the Throne with his soul, the soul will fall prostrate, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say to the Angel of Death: 'Go with the soul of this servant of Mine and place it among lote trees with thorns removed, and clustered plantains, and extended shade, and flowing water.'\" He said: \"When he is placed in his grave, prayer will come to him and be on his right, fasting will come and be on his left, the Qur'an and remembrance will come and be at his head, his walking to prayer will come and be at his feet, and patience will come and be in a corner of the grave.\" He said: \"Then Allah, Exalted, will send a punishment from the punishments, and it will approach him from his right, and prayer will say: 'Get back! By Allah, he was persistent all his life, and he has only now found rest when he was placed in his grave.' He said: \"It will approach him from his left, and fasting will say the like of that. Then it will approach him from his head, and the Qur'an and remembrance will say the like of that. Then it will approach him from his feet, and his walking to prayer will say the like of that.\" He said: \"The punishment will not approach him from any direction seeking a way except it will find the friend of Allah, Exalted, having blocked its path.\" He said: \"The punishment will then retreat and leave, and patience will say to the other deeds: 'As for me, nothing prevented me from undertaking the matter myself except that I looked at what you have. If you were unable, I would be his companion. But since you have sufficed for him, I am a reserve for him at the bridge and the scale.'\" He said: \"Allah, Exalted, will send two angels whose eyes are like flashing lightning, whose voices are like crashing thunder, whose fangs are like cattle horns, and whose breaths are like flames. They tread in their hair, and between the shoulders of each of them is a distance of such and such. Mercy and compassion have been removed from them. They are called Munkar and Nakir. In the hand of each of them is a sledgehammer; if Rabi'ah and Mudar gathered against it, they could not lift it.\" He said: \"They will say to him: 'Sit up.' He said: \"He will sit up straight, and his shrouds will fall to his waist.\" He said: \"They will say to him: 'Who is your Lord? What is your religion? Who is your Prophet?'\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, who can speak at that time when you describe the two angels as you describe?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"'Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word in this world and the Hereafter, and Allah sends astray the wrongdoers, and Allah does what He wills' [Surah Ibrahim:27].\" He said: \"He will say: 'Allah is my Lord alone, no partner has He. My religion is Islam, which the angels profess, and my Prophet is Muhammad ﷺ, the seal of the prophets.'\" He said: \"They will say: 'You have spoken the truth.'\" He said: \"They will push the grave and widen it: before him forty cubits, behind him forty cubits, on his right forty cubits, on his left forty cubits, and at his head forty cubits.\" He said: \"They will widen it forty cubits.\" (Al-Bursani said: I think he said: \"and forty cubits surrounding him.\") Then they will say to him: \"Look above you.\" He said: \"He will look above him, and there will be a door opened to Paradise. They will say to him: 'O friend of Allah, this is your abode since you obeyed Allah, Exalted.'\" He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'By Him in Whose hand is my soul, at that moment a joy will reach his heart that will never turn back.' Then it will be said to him: \"Look below you.\" He will look below him, and there will be a door opened to the Fire. They will say to him: 'O friend of Allah, this is your abode had you disobeyed Allah, but you are saved; He has deferred it for you.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, at that moment a joy will reach his heart that will never increase.\" He said: \"'A'ishah ؓ said: 'Seventy-seven doors to Paradise will be opened for him, and its breeze and coolness will come to him until Allah, Blessed and Exalted, resurrects him.'\" This chain goes to Anas b. Malik, from Tamim al-Dari, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says to the Angel of Death: 'Go to My enemy and bring him to Me, for I have expanded My provision for him and clothed him with My favor, but he insisted on disobeying Me. Bring him to Me that I may take vengeance on him.'\" He said: \"The Angel of Death will go to him in the most horrible form anyone has ever seen, with twelve eyes, and with him is an iron spit with many thorns, and with him are five hundred angels. With them are copper and coals from the coals of Hell, and with them are whips of fire, their softness the softness of whips, but they are blazing fire.\" He said: \"The Angel of Death will strike him with that spit a blow by which the base of every thorn of that spit disappears into the base of every hair, vein, and nail. Then he will twist it severely and pull his soul out from the nails of his feet and cast it into his heels.\" He said: \"The enemy of Allah will be intoxicated at that with a swoon, and the Angel of Death will give him respite, and the angels will strike his face and back with those whips. Then the angels will shake him, and his soul will be pulled from his heels and cast into his knees.\" He said: \"Then the enemy of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will be intoxicated at that with a swoon, and the Angel of Death will give him respite.\" He said: \"The angels will strike his face and back with those whips, and the Angel of Death will shake him, and his soul will be pulled from his knees and cast into his waist.\" He said: \"Then the enemy of Allah will be intoxicated at that with a swoon, and the Angel of Death will give him respite, and the angels will strike his face and back with those whips.\" He said: \"Thus it will continue until his chest and throat, then the angels will spread the copper and coals of Hell beneath his chin, and the Angel of Death will say: 'Come out, O accursed, cursed soul, to the scorching wind of Hell, and to the shade of black smoke, neither cool nor noble.'\" He said: \"When the Angel of Death takes his soul, the soul will say to the body: 'May Allah reward you with evil on my behalf. You were slow in me toward obedience to Allah, Exalted, and quick in me toward disobedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic. You have perished and caused my destruction.'\" He said: \"The body will say the like of that to the soul, and the places of the earth where he used to disobey Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will curse him.\" He said: \"The troops of Iblis will go to give him glad tidings that they have brought a servant from the children of Adam to the Fire. When he is placed in his grave, his grave will be constricted until his ribs interlace, the right entering the left and the left entering the right. Allah, Exalted, will send to him serpents like the necks of camels, which will seize him by his nose and the big toes of his feet and bite him until they meet in his middle. Allah, Exalted, will send two angels whose eyes are like flashing lightning, whose voices are like crashing thunder, whose fangs are like cattle horns, and whose breaths are like flames. They tread in their hair, and between the shoulders of each of them is a distance of such and such. Mercy and compassion have been removed from them. They are called Munkar and Nakir. In the hand of each of them is a sledgehammer; if Rabi'ah and Mudar gathered against it, they could not lift it.\" He said: \"They will say to him: 'Sit up.' He said: \"He will sit up straight, and his shrouds will fall to his waist.\" He said: \"They will say to him: 'Who is your Lord? What is your religion? Who is your Prophet?'\" He will say: \"I do not know.\" They will say to him: \"May you never know and never be guided.\" He said: \"They will strike him a blow whose sparks fly in his grave. Then they will return and say to him: 'Look above you.' He will look, and there will be a door opened from Paradise. They will say to him: 'O enemy of Allah, this is your abode had you obeyed Allah, Mighty and Majestic.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, at that moment a regret will reach his heart that will never increase.\" He said: \"They will say to him: 'Look below you.' He will look, and there will be a door opened to the Fire. They will say: 'O enemy of Allah, this is your abode since you disobeyed Allah, Mighty and Majestic.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, at that moment a regret will reach his heart, and it will never increase.\" 'A'ishah ؓ said: \"Seventy-seven doors to the Fire will be opened for him, and its heat and scorching wind will come to him until Allah, Blessed and Exalted, resurrects him to it.\" This is a hadith of astonishing context, and it is a witness to much of what is established in the long famous hadith of al-Bara' ؓ. However, this chain is strange; we know of no one who narrated from Anas, from Tamim al-Dari ؓ except through this route. Yazid al-Raqashi is very weak in memory and has many rejected narrations; he did not control the chain, so he attributed to Anas ؓ everything he heard from others. Below him also are those like him or weaker. (216) The hadith of Abu Sa'id ؓ regarding the signs of the Hour has already been mentioned. In the Dar al-Asimah edition: (he resurrects), but what is established is from Ithaf al-Busiri, which matches the context."],[6344,"When Allah, Exalted, gathers the people on one plain on the Day of Resurrection, the Fire will advance, one part of it mounting another, and its keepers will restrain it. It will say: \"By the might of my Lord, either make way between me and my spouses, or I will cover the people in one mass.\" They will say: \"Who are your spouses?\" It will say: \"Every arrogant tyrant.\" It will put out its tongue and snatch them from among the people and cast them into it. Then it will retreat, then advance again, one part of it mounting another, and its keepers will restrain it. It will say: \"By the might of my Lord, either make way between me and my spouses, or I will cover the people in one mass.\" They will say: \"Who are your spouses?\" It will say: \"Every self-conceited boaster.\" It will snatch them with its tongue and cast them into its interior. Then it will retreat, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will judge between the servants."],[6345,"Allah, Exalted, will bring out a people from the Fire after they have been charred in it and become like charcoal. They will be cast into a river at the gate of Paradise called the River of Life. They will sprout in it as a seed sprouts in the silt of a flood, or as mushrooms sprout. Then they will enter Paradise, and it will be said: \"These are the freed ones of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, from the Fire.\""],[6346,"People will certainly come out of the Fire with a foul odor, whom the Fire has charred. They will enter Paradise by the intercession of the intercessors, and they will be called therein the Jahannamiyyun."],[6347,"My intercession on the Day of Resurrection is true. Whoever does not believe in it will not be among its people."],[6348,"The most honored of Allah's creation to Him is Abu al-Qasim ﷺ. Paradise is in the heaven, and the Fire is in the earth. On the Day of Resurrection, Allah will raise the creation nation by nation and prophet by prophet until Muhammad ﷺ is the last of creation in rank. Then a bridge will be placed over Hell. Then it will be called: \"Where is Muhammad and his nation?\" He ﷺ will stand, and his nation, both righteous and wicked, will follow him."],[6349,"Allah will make Himself known to me on the Day of Resurrection, and I will prostrate with a prostration with which He will be pleased with me. Then I will praise Him with praise with which He will be pleased with me. Then I will be permitted to speak. Then my nation will pass over the Sirat, which is placed across the midst of Hell. They will pass faster than the blink of an eye and faster than an arrow, then faster than the best horses, until a man among them will come out crawling. Those are the deeds. Hell will ask for more until He places His foot in it, and parts of it will shrink back, and it will say: \"Enough, enough.\" And I will be at the Hawd. It was said: \"What is the Hawd, O Messenger of Allah?\" He ﷺ said: \"By Him in Whose hand is my soul, its drink is whiter than milk, sweeter than honey, cooler than snow, and more fragrant than musk. Its vessels are more numerous than the stars. No person drinks from it and ever thirsts, and none is turned away from it and ever quenched.\""],[6350,"A people of the Muslims who had been immersed in the Fire will surely enter Paradise, by the mercy of Allah, the Exalted, and the intercession of the intercessors."],[6351,"I have seen what my Ummah will face after me, so I have delayed my intercession to the Day of Resurrection."],[6352,"And Abu Ya'la said: Mujahid b. Musa narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, Musa b. 'Ubayda al-Rabadhi narrated to us, from Sa'id b. Abi 'Ayyash al-Zuraqi, from Anas, from Umm Salama ؓ, with this."],[6353,"5474 4566 / 3 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad b. Khazim narrated to us, then he mentioned something similar."],[6354,"I will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection between Abu Bakr and 'Umar ؓ, then I will go to the people of Baqi' al-Gharqad, and they will be resurrected with me, then I will await the people of Makkah until they come to me, and I will be resurrected between the people of the two sanctuaries."],[6355,"I hear the call, so I go out to al-Baqi', and I am gathered with them."],[6356,"The sky rains until the earth splits open over the dead, and they emerge."],[6357,"The son of Adam will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and stood between the two pans of the Balance, and an angel will be entrusted with him. If his balance is heavy, the angel will call out in a voice that the creation can hear: 'So-and-so has attained happiness after which he will never be wretched.' And if his balance is light, the angel will call out in a voice that the creation can hear: 'So-and-so has become wretched after which he will never be happy.'"],[6358,"There is none of you but that the Lord of the Worlds will ask him, with no barrier or interpreter between him and Him."],[6359,"Al-Bazzar narrated it from Safwan al-Muflis, from 'Abd al-'Aziz, and he indicated that he was alone in narrating it."],[6360,"People will be gathered on a single plain, and the caller will make them hear and their sight will penetrate. The first one called will be Muhammad ﷺ, and he will say: 'Labbaik wa sa'daik, and good is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You, and the guided one is whom You guide. Your servant is before You, I am from You and to You. There is no refuge or escape from You except to You. Blessed and exalted are You, glory be to You, Lord of the House.' This is His saying, Mighty and Majestic: 'It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praiseworthy station.'"],[6361,"Allah, the Exalted, will gather people on the Day of Resurrection on a single plain, barefoot and naked as they were created the first time. The caller will make them hear, and their sight will penetrate."],[6362,"And al-Harith said: 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Aban narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, and he mentioned the like of Shu'bah's hadith."],[6364,"Al-Bazzār said: Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. al-Junayd narrated to us, Yaḥyā b. Muḥammad b. al-Sakan narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated to us with it. Al-Ḥākim deemed it authentic. : :"],[6365,"I set out with the delegation of Thaqif, and we came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We stayed at the door, and there was no one among the people more hateful to us than a man we would enter upon. Yet when we left, there was no one among the people dearer to us than a man we would enter upon. Then one of us said, 'O Messenger of Allah, why did you not ask your Lord for a kingdom like the kingdom of Sulayman b. Dawud?' He ﷺ laughed, then said: 'Perhaps your companion has with Allah, exalted be He, something better than the kingdom of Sulayman. Allah, exalted be He, did not send any prophet except that He gave him a supplication. Some of them used it to seek worldly things and were given it, and some of them supplicated with it against their people when they disobeyed him, and they were destroyed by it. And Allah, mighty and majestic be He, has given me a supplication, and I have concealed it as intercession with my Lord for my community on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[6366,"And al-Harith said: 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Aban narrated to us, 'Abd al-Jabbar b. al-'Abbas al-Shibami narrated to us, 'Awn b. Abi Juhayfah narrated to us, something similar to it."],[6367,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"would take musk and wipe his head and beard with it.\""],[6368,"We know of no hadith for Ibn Abi 'Aqil except this one."],[6369,"They will come to Muhammad ﷺ and say to him: 'O Prophet of Allah, you are the one through whom Allah opened and sealed, and He forgave you your past and future sins. You have come on this day in safety, and you see what we are in. So arise and intercede for us with our Lord.' He ﷺ will say: 'I am your companion.' Then he will go out and gather the people until he reaches the gate of Paradise. He will take hold of a golden ring on the gate and knock on it. It will be said: 'Who is this?' It will be said: 'Muhammad.' Then it will be opened for him until he stands before Allah, mighty and majestic be He. He will ask permission to prostrate, and permission will be given to him. Then it will be called out: 'O Muhammad, raise your head, ask and you will be given, intercede and you will be granted intercession, and supplicate and you will be answered.' He said: Then a door of praise, glorification, and magnification will be opened for him such as has not been opened for anyone among creation. Then it will be called out: 'O Muhammad, raise your head, ask and you will be given, intercede and you will be granted intercession, and supplicate and you will be answered.' He will raise his head and say: 'My Lord, my community; my Lord, my community,' two or three times. Salman ؓ said: Then he will intercede for everyone who had in his heart the weight of a grain of wheat of faith, or the weight of a barley grain of faith, or the weight of a mustard seed of faith. That is the praiseworthy station."],[6370,"I will not cease interceding for my community until it is said: 'O Muhammad, bring out of the Fire anyone who has in his heart the weight of a barley grain of faith,' until he said: 'Then it will be said: O Muhammad, bring out anyone who has in his heart the amount of a mosquito's wing of faith.'"],[6371,"I will knock on the gate of Paradise, and a gate of gold will be opened, and a ring of silver, and the greatest light will receive me, and I will fall prostrate. Then I will be inspired with praise of Allah, mighty and majestic be He, such as no one before me has been inspired with. It will be said: 'Raise your head, ask and you will be given, speak and you will be heard, intercede and you will be granted intercession.' I will say: 'My community.' It will be said: 'You shall have those who have in their hearts the weight of a barley grain,' until he said: 'a mustard seed,' until he said: 'those who said: There is no god but Allah.'"],[6372,"The earth will be stretched out like the stretching of a hide, because of the greatness of Allah, mighty and majestic be He. Then no man among the children of Adam will have in it except the place of his two feet. Then I will be called as the first of the people, and I will fall prostrate. Then permission will be given to me, and I will say: 'O Lord.'"],[6373,"The first to be clothed on the Day of Resurrection will be Ibrahim ﷺ , with two Coptic garments, then the Prophet ﷺ, and he will be at the right of the Throne."],[6374,"And Abu Ya'la said: 'Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us with this. It is in a long hadith from the Musnad of Ibn Mas'ud ؓ, which Ahmad extracted."],[6375,"A believer does not wrong another believer except that Allah will exact retribution from him on the Day of Resurrection."],[6376,"Injustice is of three types: an injustice that Allah Most High will not leave, an injustice that is forgiven, and an injustice that is not forgiven. As for the injustice that is not forgiven, it is shirk; Allah will not forgive it. As for the injustice that is forgiven, it is the servant's injustice between himself and his Lord, Mighty and Majestic. As for the one that is left, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will cause some of them to be recompensed by others."],[6377,"A man will come on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds like towering mountains, and another man will keep seeking retribution from him for an injustice, taking from his good deeds until no good deed remains for him, and until [the wrongs] cause his bad deeds to return to him."],[6378,"Two men traveled through a desert. One was a devoted worshipper, and the other had a burden of sin. The worshipper became thirsty until he collapsed, and his companion looked at him as he lay prostrate. He said: 'By Allah, if this righteous servant dies of thirst while I have water, I will not attain any good from Allah; but if I give him my water, I will surely die myself.' So he trusted in Allah Most High and resolved, then he sprinkled some of his water on him and gave him the surplus. So [the worshipper] rose and they crossed the desert. He said: The one with the burden of sin will be brought to account on the Day of Resurrection and ordered to the Fire, and the angels will drive him. Then he will see the worshipper and say: 'O so-and-so, do you not recognize me?' He will say: 'Who are you?' He will say: 'I am so-and-so, the one who preferred you over myself on the day of the desert.' He will say: 'Yes, I recognize you.' Then he will say to the angels: 'Stop!' So he will be stopped, and he will come and stand, and he will call upon his Lord, saying: 'O Lord, You know the favor he did me and how he preferred me over himself. O Lord, grant him to me.' Then He, Glorified and Exalted, will say: 'He is yours.' He said: Then he will come and take him by the hand and enter him into Paradise."],[6379,"The rows of the people of the Fire will come out, and a man will pass by a man from the people of Paradise and say: 'O so-and-so, do you not recognize me?' He will say: 'Who are you?' He will say: 'I am the one who asked you for water for ablution and you granted it to me.' So he will intercede for him, and his intercession will be accepted. And a man will pass by a man and say: 'O so-and-so, do you not recognize me?' He will say: 'Who are you?' He said: 'Did you not send me on such-and-such an errand and I fulfilled it for you?' So he will intercede for him, and his intercession will be accepted."],[6380,"And Abu Ya'la said: Al-'Abbas b. al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yusuf b. Khalid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, with this. Yusuf is abandoned in hadith."],[6381,"And the confirmation of this in the Qur'an is: 'If you avoid the major sins which you are forbidden, We will remove from you your lesser sins and admit you to a noble entrance' (Qur'an 4:31) – the verse. So these are those who avoid major sins, and these are those who fall into them; the intercession of Muhammad ﷺ is established for them."],[6382,"There will enter Paradise through the intercession of one man from my nation more than the tribe of Tamim."],[6383,"When Allah gathers the creation on the Day of Resurrection, a caller will call out: 'Where are the people of excellence?' Then some people will stand, and they are few, and they will go quickly to Paradise. The angels will meet them and say: 'We saw you hurrying to Paradise. Who are you?' They will say: 'We are the people of excellence.' They will say: 'What is your excellence?' They will say: 'When we were wronged, we were patient; when evil was done to us, we forgave; and when ignorance was shown to us, we were forbearing.' Then it will be said to them: 'Enter Paradise, and excellent is the reward of the workers.' Then a caller will call out: 'Where are the people of patience?' Then some people will come forward, and they are few, and they will go quickly to Paradise. He said: The angels will meet them and say: 'We see you hurrying to Paradise. Who are you?' They will say: 'We are the people of patience.' They will say: 'What is your patience?' They will say: 'We were patient in obeying Allah Most High, and we were patient in abstaining from disobeying Allah, Mighty and Majestic.' Then it will be said to them: 'Enter Paradise, and excellent is the reward of the workers.' Then a caller will call out: 'Where are those who love one another for the sake of Allah Most High' – or he said: 'for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic' (Abu Muhammad was uncertain) – then some people will stand, and they are few, and they will go quickly to Paradise. The angels will meet them and say: 'We saw you hurrying to Paradise. Who are you?' They will say: 'We are those who love one another for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic' – or 'for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.' They will say: 'What was your mutual love?' They will say: 'We loved one another for the sake of Allah, we visited one another for the sake of Allah Most High, we were affectionate with one another for the sake of Allah Most High, and we gave to one another for the sake of Allah Most High.' Then it will be said to them: 'Enter Paradise, and excellent is the reward of the workers.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will set up the scales for the reckoning after these have entered Paradise.'"],[6384,"If you wish, I will tell you the first thing Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say to the believers on the Day of Resurrection, and the first thing they will say. They said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He ﷺ said: 'Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say to the believers on the Day of Resurrection: \"Did you love to meet Me?\" They will say: \"Yes, O our Lord.\" [Then He will say: \"Why?\" They will say: \"We hoped for Your pardon and Your forgiveness.\"] Then He will say: \"I have made My mercy obligatory for you.\""],[6385,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, we saw him laugh until his molars appeared. Umar ؓ said to him, \"What made you laugh, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom?\" He ﷺ said, \"Two men from my Ummah knelt before the Lord of Might, may His majesty be exalted. One of them said, 'O Lord, take retribution for me from my brother.' Allah, Mighty and Exalted, said, 'Give your brother his due.' He said, 'O Lord, nothing of my good deeds remains.' He said, 'O Lord, then let him bear some of my burdens.'\" He (the Prophet) said, \"The eyes of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ overflowed with tears.\" Then he said, \"Indeed that is a mighty day, in which people will need to have burdens carried for them. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said to the claimant, 'Raise your eyes and look at the gardens.' He raised his head and said, 'O Lord, I see cities of silver and palaces of gold adorned with pearls. For which prophet is this? For which truthful one is this? For which martyr is this?' He said, 'This is for the one who pays the price.' He said, 'O Lord, who can possess that?' He (Allah), Majestic and High, said, 'You possess it.' He said, 'By what, O Lord?' He said, 'By pardoning your brother.' He said, 'O Lord, I have pardoned him.' Allah, Exalted, said, 'Take your brother by the hand and enter him into Paradise.'\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about that, \"Fear Allah and make peace among yourselves, for Allah, Mighty and Exalted, will reconcile the believers on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[6386,"It has reached us that when the Day of Resurrection comes, a caller will call out, \"Where are the people of pardon?\" He said, \"Then Allah, Exalted, will reward them according to their pardoning of people.\""],[6387,"When the creatures meet on the Day of Resurrection, and the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, a caller will call out so that all creatures hear: \"O people of the gathering, abandon the wrongdoings, and your reward is upon Me.\""],[6388,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was watering a she-camel of mine in front of me, so I spat, and my sputum fell on my garment. So I began to wash my garment from the water-skin that was in front of me. He said, 'O Ammar, your sputum and the tears of your eyes are only like the water in your water-skin. Only that is washed from urine, excrement, semen from the greatest water, blood, and vomit.'"],[6389,"I entered Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants were the poor. I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants were the rich and women. I saw in it three being punished: a woman from Himyar, of Tall stature, who tied up a cat of hers, neither feeding it nor giving it water, nor letting it eat from the vermin of the earth, so it was biting her front and back. And I saw in it the brother of Banu Da'da', who used to steal from the pilgrims with his hooked staff; when it was noticed, he would say, 'It got caught on my staff.' And the one who stole the two camels of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6390,"If a stone were thrown from the edge of Hell, it would fall for seventy autumns before settling at its bottom."],[6391,"I entered upon Anas b. Malik ؓ and saw a wooden cup with him. He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to drink from it and perform ablution.'"],[6392,"And al-Bazzar said: Yusuf b. Musa narrated to us; they both said: Jarir narrated to us. Ibn Hibban deemed it authentic from the hadith of Jarir, with it."],[6393,"If there were a hundred thousand or more in this mosque, and in it a man from the people of the Fire, and he breathed, and his breath reached it, the mosque and all in it would burn."],[6394,"When Allah gathers people on one plain on the Day of Resurrection], the Fire will come, riding one upon another, and its keepers will restrain it."],[6395,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a rumbling one day and said, \"O Jibril, what is this?\" He said, \"A stone was thrown from the edge of Hell seventy autumns ago, and now it has settled at its bottom.\""],[6396,"If a stone like seven pregnant camels with their fat and their young were thrown into Hell, it would fall for seventy years without reaching its bottom."],[6397,"One day we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we saw him looking distressed. Some of us said, 'O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, why do we see you distressed?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I heard a rumble the like of which I have never heard. Jibril ﷺ came to me, so I asked him about it. He said, \"This is a rock that was thrown into the Fire seventy autumns ago, and today it reached its resting place.\"' Abu Sa'id ؓ said, 'By the One who took the soul of Muhammad, our Prophet ﷺ, we did not see him laugh after that day until we covered him with earth.'"],[6398,"The Fire complained to its Lord, Mighty and Majestic, saying, 'My Lord, parts of me are eating other parts.' So He gave it two breaths: a breath in winter and a breath in summer. The intense heat you experience is from its heat, and the intense cold you experience is from its bitter cold."],[6399,"O people! Weep, and if you cannot weep, then pretend to weep, for the people of the Fire will weep in the Fire until their tears flow down their cheeks like streams, until the tears are exhausted, and then blood will flow, causing their eyes to ulcerate."],[6400,"Concerning His saying, Exalted is He: 'And those who feared their Lord will be driven to Paradise in groups' (Q 39:73), until when they come to it, they find at the gate of Paradise a tree. (Ma'mar said:) From its trunk, (and al-Thawri said:) from its roots, there spring two springs. They betake themselves to one of them, and it is as if they were commanded to do so. (Ma'mar said:) They bathe in it, (and al-Thawri said:) they perform ablution from it, and after that their heads never become disheveled and their skins never change, as if they had anointed themselves with oil, and the radiance of bliss shines upon them. Then they betake themselves to the other spring and drink from it, and it purifies their insides, so that no impurity, harm, or evil remains in their bellies but that it comes out. The angels meet them at the gate of Paradise: 'Peace be upon you; you have become good, so enter it to abide eternally' (Q 39:73). And the youths meet them, like hidden pearls, like scattered pearls, telling them what Allah, Exalted is He, has prepared for them. They surround them as the youths of the people of this world surround a beloved one who returns from absence, saying, 'Receive good tidings: Allah has prepared for you such-and-such, and has prepared for you such-and-such.' Then one of those youths goes to a wife from among his wives and says, 'So-and-so has come,' using the name by which he was called in this world. Joy overwhelms her until she stands on the threshold of her door and says, 'Did you see him?' He said, 'Then he comes and looks at the foundation of his building, which is upon boulders of pearl, among green, yellow, and red of every color. Then he sits, and behold, carpets are spread out, cushions are arranged, and goblets are placed. Then he raises his head and looks at the ceiling of his building, and were it not that Allah, Exalted is He, (Ma'mar said:) had decreed that for him, and al-Thawri said: had subjected that for him, it would nearly take away his sight. It is but like lightning. Then he says, \"Praise be to Allah who guided us [to this]\" (Q 7:43).'"],[6401,"He mentioned the Fire and magnified its affair, then said: 'And those who feared their Lord will be driven to Paradise in groups' (Q 39:73). And he mentioned something similar, saying: 'And behold, boulders of pearl, above them a palace of red, green, and yellow.' He said: 'Then they looked at that bliss and reclined upon it and said, \"Praise be to Allah who guided us to this\" (Q 7:43).'"],[6402,"Then he reclines on one of his couches, then says, 'Praise be to Allah.'"],[6403,"He mentioned the Fire, and he mentioned of it whatever Allah willed him to mention, then he said: 'In extended columns' (Q 104:9), then he said: 'And those who feared their Lord will be driven to Paradise in groups' (Q 39:73)."],[6406,"Some Jews came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Muhammad, is there fruit in Paradise?' He ﷺ said, 'Yes, in it there is fruit, palm trees, and pomegranates.' They said, 'Will they eat as they eat in this world?' He ﷺ said, 'Yes, and many times more.' They said, 'Will they relieve themselves?' He ﷺ said, 'No, but they will sweat and then perspire, and Allah, Exalted is He, will remove whatever harm is in their bellies.'"],[6407,"He was asked: 'Do the people of Paradise have intercourse with their spouses?' He said: 'Yes, with a member that does not tire, a private part that does not become sore, and desire that does not cease.'"],[6408,"'Umara was alone in narrating it, and 'Abd al-Rahman narrated rejected reports from unknown narrators."],[6409,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about sexual intercourse in Paradise. He said: 'Yes, a pleasant midday rest, and a member that does not tire. A man will recline in it for a period of forty years without turning away from it or becoming weary of it. There will come to him in it whatever his soul desires and his eye delights in.'"],[6410,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'Do the people of Paradise engage in sexual intercourse?' He said: 'Yes, with vigorous thrusting, but there is no semen and no death.'"],[6411,"It was said: O Messenger of God, will we have intercourse with our wives in Paradise as we do in this world? He said ﷺ: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, a man will have intercourse in a single morning with a hundred virgins."],[6412,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Our clothes in Paradise—will we weave them with our hands? The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ laughed. The Bedouin said: Why do you laugh at an ignorant man asking a learned one? The Prophet ﷺ said: You have spoken the truth, O Bedouin, but they are fruits."],[6413,"If a woman of the houris with large eyes were to bring out her hand, every living being would find its fragrance. Should I leave them for you? Rather, it is fitting that I leave you for them."],[6414,"The houris with large eyes sing in Paradise, saying: We are good and beautiful, stored away for noble husbands."],[6415,"The people of Paradise say: Let us go to the market. They go to pulpits of sand dunes of musk or mountains of musk. When they return to their wives, their wives say: We find from you a fragrance we did not find when you left us—or until you left us. He said: And these say: We find from you a fragrance we did not find when we left you—or until we left you. Or as he said."],[6416,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about Paradise, how it is. He said: Whoever enters Paradise will live and not die, and will enjoy bliss without hardship. His clothes will not wear out, and his youth will not fade. It was said: O Messenger of God, how is its construction? He said ﷺ: A brick of silver and a brick of gold, its mortar is pungent musk, its pebbles are pearls and rubies, and its dust is saffron."],[6417,"Gardens of Eden are the deepest interior of Paradise. I said: What is the deepest interior of Paradise? Sulayman said: Its center."],[6418,"In Paradise there are pillars of ruby, upon which are chambers of chrysolite with open doors that shine as the shining of a brilliant star. It was said: Who will dwell in them, O Prophet of God? He said ﷺ: Those who love one another for God, those who sit together for God, and those who give generously to one another for God."],[6419,"And a servant said: Abd Allah b. Maslama narrated to us, Muhammad b. Abi Humayd narrated to us with it. Weak."],[6420,"The river Nile is the river of honey in Paradise, the river Tigris is the river of milk in Paradise, the river Euphrates is the river of wine in Paradise, and the river Sayhan is the river of water in Paradise. He said: God Almighty extinguished their light to make them in Paradise."],[6421,"Paradise was displayed to me, and I went to take a bunch from it to show you, but it was kept from me. A man said: O Messenger of God, is it like the grapes in Paradise? He said ﷺ: Like the largest bucket your mother ever filled."],[6422,"You will look at a bird in Paradise and desire it, and it will fall before you roasted."],[6423,"We do not know it except from this route, and Humayd is Ibn 'Ata', a Kufan, weak. I say: We heard it with a high chain in the part of al-Hasan b. 'Arafa."],[6425,"When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: 'Shall I give you something better than this?' They will say: 'Our Lord, what is better than this?' He, Blessed and Exalted, will say: 'My pleasure.'"],[6426,"Shall I not tell you about the lowest of the people of Paradise? They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'A man will enter from the gate of Paradise, and his servants will meet him and say: \"Welcome, our master! It is time for you to return.\"' He said: 'Then carpets will be spread for him for forty years. Then he will look to his right and to his left and see gardens, and he will say: \"For whom is what is here?\" It will be said: \"For you.\" When he finishes, a red ruby or a green emerald will be raised for him, having seventy branches, in each branch seventy rooms, in each room seventy doors. It will be said to him: \"Recite and ascend.\" He said: 'He will ascend until he reaches the couch of his kingdom and reclines on it. Its width is a mile by a mile, and it has extra space. Seventy thousand dishes of gold will be brought to him, no dish having the same color as its companion. He will find the taste of the last dish like the taste of the first. Then drinks of various kinds will be brought to him, and he will drink as much as he desires. Then the servants will say: \"Leave him and his wives.\" (Abu Shihab said: I think he said:) The servants will withdraw from him, and there will be a houri seated on the couch of her kingdom. He will see the marrow of her leg from behind the flesh and blood. He will say to her: \"Who are you?\" She will say: \"I am one of the houris with large eyes who have been hidden for you.\" He will look at her for forty years without lifting his gaze from her. Then he will raise his gaze to the rooms above him, and there will be another more beautiful than her. She will say to him: \"Is it not time that we have a share of you?\" He will ascend to her and look at her for forty years without turning his gaze away from her. When the bliss has reached its utmost with them, and they think that there is nothing better than them, the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will manifest Himself to them, and they will look at the face of the Most Merciful, and they will forget all the bliss they had witnessed when they look at the face of the Most Merciful. Then He will say: \"O people of Paradise, declare My oneness!\" They will respond with the declaration of oneness. Then He will say: \"O Dawud, glorify Me as you used to glorify Me in the world.\" Dawud will glorify his Lord, Mighty and Majestic.' Ahmad b. Yunus said: I said to Abu Shihab: 'The hadith of Khalid b. Dinar about the mention of Paradise – is it marfu'?' He said: 'Yes.' In the Dar al-'Asima edition: (umm), but what is established is from the Musnad of 'Abd b. Humayd and the Ittihaf of al-Busiri."],[6427,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah, Exalted, will separate between the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire. And when it is Monday and Thursday, pulpits of light will be placed around the Throne, and pulpits of chrysolite and ruby. The angels entrusted with them will say: 'Our Lord, for whom have You placed these pulpits?' It will be cast upon their mouths: 'For the strangers.' They will say: 'Our Lord, who are the strangers?' It will be cast upon their mouths: 'A people who loved one another for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, without having seen Him.' While they are like that, each man of them will come, knowing his seat better than one of you knows his seat in his pavilion with his wife in the abode of this world. Their nearness to the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will be according to their ranks in Paradise. When the people are complete, the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, will say: 'My servants, My creation, My visitors, and those who loved one another for My majesty without having seen Me – feed them.' They will be fed. Then He will say: 'Give them fruit.' Then they will be brought fruit containing every desire, pleasure, and fragrant scent. Then the Lord will say: 'Give them drink.' They will be brought vessels of which it is not known whether the vessel is whiter or what is in it. Then He will say: 'Clothe them.' They will be brought fruit that cleaves the ground like the breasts of virgin women; in each fruit are seventy garments, no garment resembling its sister. Then He will say: 'Perfume them.' A wind will blow and fill them with strong musk, the like of which no human has ever smelled. Then He will say: 'Remove the cover for them.' Between Allah, Exalted, and the nearest of His creation to Him are seventy thousand veils of light. The nearest of His creation to Him, from among the angels brought near, cannot raise his head to the lowest of those veils. Then those veils will be lifted, and the people will fall prostrate because of what they see of the greatness of Allah, Exalted. The Lord, Majestic and High, will say: 'Raise your heads. You are not in the abode of action; rather, you are in the abode of blessing and abiding. You will have the like of what you are in, and its like with it. Are you pleased, My servants?' They will say: 'We are pleased, our Lord, if You are pleased with us.' Then the people will return to their dwellings, having been doubled in beauty, spouses, food, drink, and everything of their affair in that manner. While they are like that, suddenly something beside them will light up his temples with beauty, and he will say: 'Who are you?' It will say: 'I am the one of whom Allah, Exalted, said: \"And with Us is more.\"' While they are like that, seventy thousand angels will come to each servant, with each angel a vessel unlike its companion, and upon his vessel something unlike its companion. They will consult among themselves as to which of them should be taken from. They will say: 'This, your Lord has sent with me to you, and He conveys peace to you.' He said: 'There are no two servants who became brothers for the sake of Allah, Exalted, but their dwellings face each other. The servant looks to the farthest part of his brother's dwelling, except that when they desire something of the pleasures of women, the veils are let down between them.'"],[6428,"I came to visit the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and 'A'ishah ؓ, and he was receiving revelation. When it was lifted from him, he ﷺ said to 'A'ishah: 'Hand me my cloak.' He went out and entered the mosque, and there was a group of people in it, no other group being in the mosque. He sat in a corner of the people until the one reminding had finished his reminder. Then he recited: 'The revelation of the prostration.' The people were unable to fit in the mosque, so 'A'ishah ؓ sent to her family: 'Attend the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for I have seen something from him I have never seen.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head, and Abu Bakr ؓ said: \"You prolonged the prostration, O Messenger of Allah.\" He ﷺ said: \"I prostrated in gratitude to my Lord for what He gave me from my nation: seventy thousand who will enter Paradise.\" Abu Bakr ؓ said: \"O Messenger of Allah, your nation is larger and better, so ask for more for them,\" until he said it twice or three times. 'Umar ؓ said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, your nation has encompassed you.\""],[6429,"Seventy thousand of my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning. 'Ukkashah ؓ said: 'O Prophet of Allah, ask Allah, Exalted, to make me one of them.' He ﷺ said: 'O Allah, make him one of them.' Another man said: 'Ask Allah, Exalted, to make me one of them.' He ﷺ said: 'O Allah, make him one of them.' Then the people were silent for a while and talked among themselves. Some of them said: 'If only we had said: O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make us one of them.' He ﷺ said: 'Ukkashah and his companion have preceded you. If you had said, I would have said, and if I had said, it would have become obligatory.'"],[6430,"Seventy thousand of my nation will enter Paradise. They said: 'Give us more, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'For every man, seventy thousand.' They said: 'Give us more, O Messenger of Allah,' and he was on a sand hill, so he scooped with his hand. They said: 'Give us more, O Messenger of Allah.' He ﷺ said: 'This,' and scooped with both hands. They said: 'O Prophet of Allah, may Allah distance from the Fire whoever enters it after this.'"],[6431,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Zayd to visit him during an illness he had. He said: 'There is no harm upon you from this illness of yours, but how will you be if you live after me and become blind?' He said: 'Then I will seek reward and be patient.' He said: 'Then you will enter Paradise without reckoning.' He said: 'He became blind after the Prophet ﷺ died, then Allah restored his sight, then he died.'"],[6432,"Whoever dies from the people of this world, young or old, they will be returned to sixty years of age, never increasing beyond it ever, in Paradise. And likewise the people of the Fire."],[6433,"I came to al-Miqdam b. Ma'dikarib in the mosque and said: 'O Abu Yazid, the people claim that you did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'Glory be to Allah! By Allah, I saw him while I was walking with my uncle, and he took hold of this ear of mine and said to my uncle: \"Do you think this one remembers his mother or his father?\" We said to him...'"],[6434,"Indeed, I know the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise: a man who kept asking Allah, the Exalted, to keep him away from the Fire, until when the people of Paradise had entered Paradise and the people of the Fire had entered the Fire, he remained between that. He said, 'O Lord, bring me near to the gate of Paradise.' It was said, 'O son of Adam, did you not ask to be kept away from the Fire?' He said, 'O Lord, who is like You? Bring me near to the gate of Paradise.' So he was brought near to it, and he looked at a tree near the gate of Paradise and said, 'O Lord, bring me near to it so that I may shade myself with its shade and eat of its fruit.' He, Majestic and Exalted, said, 'O son of Adam, did you not say [such-and-such]?' He said, 'O Lord, who is like You? Then bring me near to it.' Then he saw something better than that and said, 'O Lord, bring me near to it.' He, majestic is His majesty, said, 'O son of Adam, did you not say [such-and-such]?' He said, 'O Lord, who is like You? Then bring me near.' It was said to him, 'Run, and you shall have whatever your feet reach and your eyes see.' He said, 'So he ran until he became exhausted' – meaning he became tired – and said, 'O Lord, is this mine and this?' He will say, 'You shall have the like of it and multiples of it.' He will say, 'My Lord is pleased with me. If He permitted me to clothe the people of Paradise and feed them, I would do so generously.'"]]);
